rint_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02PRINCIPAL1/02PRINCIPAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02PRINCIPAL1/02PRINCIPAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02PRINCIPAL1/02PRINCIPAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02PRINCIPAL1/02PRINCIPAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chancellor Black: Please Consider This', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chancellor Black: Please Consider This', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Cathleen P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T00:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elissa Gootman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gootman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1993479a-5454-5ef6-8841-f7a5723a8ec2', 'word_count': 1394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1993479a-5454-5ef6-8841-f7a5723a8ec2'}, {'abstract': 'Birdwatchers turn out to take stock of what’s flying. For them, it’s the social event of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/nyregion/02critic.html', 'snippet': 'Birdwatchers turn out to take stock of what’s flying. For them, it’s the social event of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the morning after Christmas — painfully early in the morning, and a blustery morning at that. Up in the frozen tundra of the northern Bronx, some creatures were stirring, yes, but not the yellow-bellied sapsucker that Christopher Lyons was looking for.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02jpCRITIC1/02jpCRITIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02jpCRITIC1/02jpCRITIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02jpCRITIC1/02jpCRITIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Yorkers in Feathers, Counted in the Cold', 'kicker': 'City Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Yorkers In Feathers, Counted In the Cold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T00:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec6be4f9-b15b-5de3-bc92-fb00d8ef9cc2', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec6be4f9-b15b-5de3-bc92-fb00d8ef9cc2'}, {'abstract': 'Around the region, old music halls and movie houses that survived multiplexes and Netflix find a new life with a variety of entertainment offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/nyregion/02moviect.html', 'snippet': 'Around the region, old music halls and movie houses that survived multiplexes and Netflix find a new life with a variety of entertainment offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR 15 years, a plastic likeness of Humphrey Bogart has been turning heads in the lobby of the Garde Arts Center in New London. Standing in the lavishly restored faux-Moroccan interior, the statue brings to mind the classic Bogart film “Casablanca” \x97 recalling in the process a bygone era when moviegoers regularly filled the Garde’s 1,472-seat auditorium. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02THEACO6/02THEACO6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02THEACO6/02THEACO6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/02/nyregion/02THEACO6/02THEACO6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Movie Palaces, Trying on the New', 'kicker': 'Arts| Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Movie Palaces, Trying On the New', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocati