 when it appeared promptly, an infuriating no-show adolescent when it kept me waiting. Whatever its failings \x97 riders in the Rockaways were without A train service Monday after the storm \x97 I remained faithful to it, sometimes grudgingly. When I saw that blue circle with a white A inside cruising toward me on the platform, I knew I was as good as home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/nyregion/BIGCITY/BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/01/nyregion/BIGCITY/BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/nyregion/BIGCITY/BIGCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/nyregion/BIGCITY/BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/01/nyregion/BIGCITY/BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing the A Train, and Taking Not-the-Quickest Way', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missing the A Train, and Taking Not-the-Quickest Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T00:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23a556f4-d4ff-58ad-a812-b79142d911c5', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23a556f4-d4ff-58ad-a812-b79142d911c5'}, {'abstract': 'In the blogosphere, a fight over whom to find at fault  for a natural disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/12/31/a-blizzard-of-blame/', 'snippet': 'In the blogosphere, a fight over whom to find at fault  for a natural disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, John J. Doherty, like countless other New Yorkers, was stuck in the snow, and had to hire a couple of enterprising shovelers to remove his Chevy Tahoe from a drift in Brooklyn. It would have been an unremarkable moment, were Doherty not the city’s sanitation commissioner, the man responsible for unburying the rest of us. “It was,” he told The Times’s Sam Dolnick, “very embarrassing.” Well, perhaps he can take comfort in the fact that he’s not the only one red in the face on this New Year’s weekend. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Blizzard of Blame', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doherty, John J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T00:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tobin Harshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tobin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae4b348-b882-565c-9f8e-a85a83b8be82', 'word_count': 1626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae4b348-b882-565c-9f8e-a85a83b8be82'}, {'abstract': 'The state is facing a budget gap of $4 billion and proponents of privatization say selling the state-run stores could bring in $1 billion or even $2 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/us/politics/01transitionpa.html', 'snippet': 'The state is facing a budget gap of $4 billion and proponents of privatization say selling the state-run stores could bring in $1 billion or even $2 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOREST CITY, Pa. \x97 Ralph Miranda was looking for eggnog here the other day at the state liquor store, a dated and somewhat forlorn little shop with no name, just the Soviet-style designation #5801. When the store manager told him they were out, Mr. Miranda muttered, “That’s why you privatize.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION-2/TRANSITION-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION-2/TRANSITION-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION-2/TRANSITION-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION-2/TRANSITION-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION-2/TRANSITION-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Push to Privatize Pennsylvania Liquor Stores', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Push to Privatize Pennsylvania Liquor Stores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privatization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T01:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/067ca9aa-5e88-57f9-8a3e-ab5deef61a04', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/067ca9aa-5e88-57f9-8a3e-ab5deef61a04'}, {'abstract': 'Governor-elect Scott Walker has said that he hopes to force public employees’ compensation “into line” with everyone else’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/us/politics/01transitionwi.html', 'snippet': 'Governor-elect Scott Walker has said that he hopes to force public employees’ compensation “into line” with everyone else’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADISON, Wis. \x97 In preparation for Monday’s inauguration of the new governor, Scott Walker, red, white and blue bunting has been draped around the Capitol’s echoing rotunda. Lawmakers are unpacking files in their newly assigned offices. And state workers are fretting.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION1/TRANSITION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION1/TRANSITION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION1/TRANSITION1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION1/TRANSITION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/01/us/TRANSITION1/TRANSITION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin State Workers Fret, as G.O.P. Takes Over', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin State Workers Fret, as G.O.P. Takes Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T01:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byli