-3ad6-53c7-a732-361e6ad0c21d', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27a31625-3ad6-53c7-a732-361e6ad0c21d'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s see how well you followed the news in 2010. No cheating!', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/opinion/01collins.html', 'snippet': 'Let’s see how well you followed the news in 2010. No cheating!', 'lead_paragraph': 'I. Happy New Year! Besides the Times Square ball, the glorious American mosaic of things scheduled to be dropped around the nation on New Year’s Eve also included all but which one of the following:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The End-of-the-Year Quiz', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The End-of-the-Year Quiz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Bristol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risch, James E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blagojevich, Rod R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayward, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbour, Haley', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T02:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ba157f-fa82-5397-843b-dfaa8c9e7a91', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ba157f-fa82-5397-843b-dfaa8c9e7a91'}, {'abstract': 'States need to invest much more heavily in programs that prepare people for the G.E.D. The livelihoods of millions of Americans depend on it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/opinion/01sat2.html', 'snippet': 'States need to invest much more heavily in programs that prepare people for the G.E.D. The livelihoods of millions of Americans depend on it.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nearly 40 million Americans are locked into dead-end jobs because they do not have a high school diploma. A daylong exam called the General Educational Development test, or G.E.D., provides the equivalent of a high school diploma \x97 and better chances in the job market \x97 to those who pass it. Nearly 800,000 people take the exam each year, and about 500,000 pass. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Success and Failure on the G.E.D.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Success and Failure on the G.E.D.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'General Educational Development Test (GED)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Testing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T02:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/859d71a9-99e7-54b0-b1af-73ac8f4672f7', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/859d71a9-99e7-54b0-b1af-73ac8f4672f7'}, {'abstract': 'The system of oversight for the country’s intelligence agencies needs reform. Instead, Congress is continuing to reshuffle the status quo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/opinion/01sat3.html', 'snippet': 'The system of oversight for the country’s intelligence agencies needs reform. Instead, Congress is continuing to reshuffle the status quo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the recommendations by the independent 9/11 Commission in 2004, the one that Congress has had the most difficulty with is the summons to Congress to reform itself. The commission urged lawmakers to junk the hydra-headed, multicommittee system of intelligence oversight in favor of single panels in the House and the Senate combining the clout of budgeting with oversight. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Tinkering', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Tinkering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Commission on Terrorist Attacks upon the United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T02:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd37d029-ecf2-53f9-9e83-7703561deb82', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd37d029-ecf2-53f9-9e83-7703561deb82'}, {'abstract': 'Letters to the editor regarding social networking sites and the idea of community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.co