 year \x97 even the very numeral \x97 was exciting. Somehow, it is harder to place the moment when the excitement of a new year turned to wariness and then to alarm and then to futile questions about the nature of time. Are we tunneling forward into the future, or is time blowing past us like a stiff breeze? Perhaps we simply carry time within us. To be conscious at all is to be conscious of time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year Anew', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Year Anew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T02:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ced14960-b0d2-5dad-a5dc-ce1cf3a35366', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ced14960-b0d2-5dad-a5dc-ce1cf3a35366'}, {'abstract': 'The governor of Mississippi has finally freed the Scott sisters from prison. But that does not mean they have received justice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/opinion/01herbert.html', 'snippet': 'The governor of Mississippi has finally freed the Scott sisters from prison. But that does not mean they have received justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I got a call on New Year’s Eve from Gladys Scott, which was a terrific way for 2010 to end.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/