': {'original': 'By Patrick Merrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Merrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a48ed858-7dce-5fcd-8cf2-e588f4064ff8', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a48ed858-7dce-5fcd-8cf2-e588f4064ff8'}, {'abstract': 'Before leaving office as New York’s attorney general, Andrew M. Cuomo tied up a loose end from one of his signature campaigns: an investigation of the student loan industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/nyregion/01student.html', 'snippet': 'Before leaving office as New York’s attorney general, Andrew M. Cuomo tied up a loose end from one of his signature campaigns: an investigation of the student loan industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the hours before he became governor, New York’s departing attorney general, Andrew M. Cuomo, announced that he was tying up a loose end from one of his signature campaigns: an investigation of the student loan industry that uncovered kickbacks and deceptive marketing tactics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Names Developers of a Student Loan Center', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Names Developers Of a Student Loan Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Interest Research Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T03:00:50+0000', '