n': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/be629f5a-fba2-5dd2-add5-95853e485fd2', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be629f5a-fba2-5dd2-add5-95853e485fd2'}, {'abstract': 'A blind-side open-ice check in a world junior tournament game that most likely would have been allowed in North American hockey, instead drew a match penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/where-rules-are-stricter-a-hit-is-penalized/', 'snippet': 'A blind-side open-ice check in a world junior tournament game that most likely would have been allowed in North American hockey, instead drew a match penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to head-trauma safety, the difference between international and North American hockey was made clear at the world junior tournament in Buffalo last week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Rules Are Stricter, a Hit Is Penalized', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Ice Hockey Federation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T11:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/46dc615a-54b5-5d1b-8825-608a8eb5a24d', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46dc615a-54b5-5d1b-8825-608a8eb5a24d'}, {'abstract': 'Replacing a coaching staff and installing new offensive and defensive schemes demands a complete assessment of a team’s overall performance, not  some superficial, emotion-driven impulse.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/defending-the-giants-coordinators/', 'snippet': 'Replacing a coaching staff and installing new offensive and defensive schemes demands a complete assessment of a team’s overall performance, not  some superficial, emotion-driven impulse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It turns out that saying something nice about Tom Coughlin wasn’t so hard.Many readers responded to the Coughlin or Cowher post on Thursday. We’ll round up some reaction on Sunday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending the Giants’ Coordinators', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fewell, Perry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbride, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcc112ca-baab-5c02-9fa3-3eb64ea0f829', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcc112ca-baab-5c02-9fa3-3eb64ea0f829'}, {'abstract': 'It’s always someone else’s fault.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/snow-job/', 'snippet': 'It’s always someone else’s fault.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s always important to realize that someone can disagree with you politically without being a bad person. But there are bad people in politics, too. Maybe it’s just my bias that gives me the impression that there are more mean, self-centered whiners on one side of the aisle than on the other; but anyway, a spectacular performance by my governor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snow Job', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T14:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/920f8612-6ede-553d-bc77-0e5c31837bc9', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/920f8612-6ede-553d-bc77-0e5c31837bc9'}, {'abstract': 'It take a lot of growth to restore full employment.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/01/the-long-road-ahead/', 'snippet': 'It take a lot of growth to restore full employment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The figure above illustrates Okun’s Law — the relationship between growth and unemployment. (Gah — I’ve tried to remove the connecting lines, to no avail.) The horizontal axis shows annual growth rates of real GDP; the vertical axis shows the year-to-year change in the unemployment rate. Two things are clear. First, the economy has to grow around 2 1/2 percent per year just to keep unemployment from rising. Second, growth above that level leads to a less than one-for-one fall in unemployment (because hours per worker rise, more people enter the work force, etc.). Roughly, it takes two point-years of extra growth to reduce the unemployment rate by one point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Road Ahead', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T14:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2557ab79-9eb7-5105-9629-4e55b6bfbdcf', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2557ab79-9eb7-5105-9629-4e55b6bfbdcf'}, {'abstract': 'A Palestinian woman, 36, died after inhaling tear gas fired by Israeli forces a day earlier at a protest against Israel’s separation barrier in a West Bank village.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/world/middleeast/02mideast.html', 'snippet': 'A Palestinian woman, 36, died after inhaling tear gas fired by Israeli forces a day earlier at a protest against Israel’s separation barrier in a West Bank village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM \x97 A Palestinian woman died Saturday after inhaling tear gas fired by Israeli forces a day earlier at a protest against Israel’s separation barrier in a West Bank village. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/world/02mideast1-cnd/02mideast1-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tear Gas Kills a Palestinian Protester', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tear Gas Kills a Palestinian Protester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-01T15:34:59+0000'