dorsement deals, but who was the first?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serena Williams won two tennis Grand Slam singles titles in 2009, but she did not appear among the 50 top-earning American athletes ranked last summer by SI.com, whose formula included 2009 salaries or winnings and endorsements. The only woman on the earning lists was another tennis player, Maria Sharapova, who came in 20th among international athletes.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/sports/endorse2/endorse2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/sports/endorse2/endorse2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/02/sports/endorse2/endorse2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Searching for Sports’ First Female Pitchman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Back for Sports’\nFirst Female Pitchman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Elinor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ederle, Gertrude', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zaharias, Babe Didrikson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oakley, Annie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lenglen, Suzanne', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T00:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Burton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db1ec08a-ec12-589e-a7bf-109908d7fe88', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db1ec08a-ec12-589e-a7bf-109908d7fe88'}, {'abstract': 'The eruption in passing touchdowns may signal a sea change in strategy rather than a one-year statistical spike.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/sports/football/02passing.html', 'snippet': 'The eruption in passing touchdowns may signal a sea change in strategy rather than a one-year statistical spike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a staple of the New Orleans Saints’ game plan, a simple formation that puts Reggie Bush in motion and leaves tight end Jimmy Graham in a mismatch with an opposing cornerback near the goal line. But the play, which produced the Saints’ winning touchdown against the Atlanta Falcons last Monday \x97 and generated a touchdown pass in the Super Bowl last February \x97 helps explain a startling statistical leap the N.F.L. will take this season. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/sports/passing4/passing4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/02/sports/passing4/passing4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':