om it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an Op-Ed piece in The New York Times on Sunday, Jennifer George, the daughter of the producer George W. George, writes about the debacle that was her parents’ musical “Via Galactica,” one of Broadway’s most famed flops.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cautionary Tale for ‘Spider-Man’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T18:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb87df4d-7e40-5ea9-8c89-59c200d9f38f', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb87df4d-7e40-5ea9-8c89-59c200d9f38f'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans plan to make good on a campaign vow: voting to repeal President Obama’s health care overhaul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/us/politics/03repubs.html', 'snippet': 'House Republicans plan to make good on a campaign vow: voting to repeal President Obama’s health care overhaul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Soon after the 112th Congress convenes Wednesday, Republicans in the House plan to make good on a campaign promise that helped vault many new members to victory: voting to repeal President Obama’s health care overhaul.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Newcomers Set Out to Undo Obama Victories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. NEWCOMERS\nSET OUT TO UNDO\nOBAMA VICTORIES', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T19:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer and Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3d05b0b-0f6d-58b3-88cf-cb887c81a42a', 'word_count': 1633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3d05b0b-0f6d-58b3-88cf-cb887c81a42a'}, {'abstract': 'Live analysis of the Giants game against the Washington Redskins in Week 17.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/live-analysis-giants-at-redskins/', 'snippet': 'Live analysis of the Giants game against the Washington Redskins in Week 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LANDOVER, Md. — The Giants held on to beat the Redskins, 17-14, but their season was over when the Packers’ Nick Collins intercepted a Jay Cutler pass with 10 seconds left at Lambeau Field. The Bears-Packers game was closer than a lot of people expected (the betting line kept rising during the week and settled around 10 points). Lovie Smith stuck to his word and played his starters the whole way in a 10-3 loss. The Bears knew heading into the game that they had nothing to play for, but led into the third quarter as the Packers struggled to run the ball and do much of anything on offense. The Giants did their job; it wasn’t pretty, but they survived the loss of Rich Seubert to injury and finished 10-6. Now the question turns to Tom Coughlin’s future. But how can you fire a coach who won 10 games? The Giants are not known for such impatience. Toni Monkovic The live analysis of the game, by Mark Viera, is below. Pregame: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Analysis: Giants 17, Redskins 14, Final', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T19:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b79d7ea-28e7-54b0-87e0-510779646bc1', 'word_count': 2159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b79d7ea-28e7-54b0-87e0-510779646bc1'}, {'abstract': 'Texas Christian’s win over Wisconsin was the highest-rated cable program except for N.F.L. games since 2001, but it was lower than last year’s broadcast on ABC.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/rose-bowl-ratings-fall-but-are-still-good-for-espn/', 'snippet': 'Texas Christian’s win over Wisconsin was the highest-rated cable program except for N.F.L. games since 2001, but it was lower than last year’s broadcast on ABC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For ESPN, the decision to show all of the Bowl Championship Series games began to pay off when Texas Christian’s 21-19 victory over Wisconsin in the Rose Bowl on Saturday generated an 11.7 preliminary overnight Nielsen rating. While the game’s rating was the highest for any program on cable except for N.FL. games since 2001, it fell from what it had been on ABC, where it had 13.8 last year, a 12.6 in 2009 and a 12.1 in 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rose Bowl Ratings Fall, but Are Still Good for ESPN', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T20:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cac730c-89c8-5ac9-bac2-e69b34cec76d', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cac730c-89c8-5ac9-bac2-e69b34cec76d'}, {'abstract': 'Quarterback Mark Sanchez played one possession and did not throw a pass, and several other Jets starters were inactive for a rout of Buffalo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/sports/03jets.html', 'snippet': 'Quarterback Mark Sanchez played one possession and did not throw a pass, and several other Jets starters were inactive for a rout of Buffalo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. \x97 Moments after the Jets’ regular season ended, the confetti machine outside the team’s tunnel malfunctioned, shooting shiny, tiny slips of green and white paper about two feet into the air. That fit perfectly with the muted celebration.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print