itated and aggressive behavior. Certain approaches to caregiving can make life more pleasant for patients, who, research suggests, continue to feel emotions like joy or sadness even if they have no memory of the experiences that caused those emotions. And they can, in turn, make things easier for caregivers, allowing people to care for relatives with Alzheimer’s at home and delay placing them in nursing homes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caring for the Patient With Alzheimer’s', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T21:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf25850-00ec-5dac-ac12-31b5c76d7c7f', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf25850-00ec-5dac-ac12-31b5c76d7c7f'}, {'abstract': 'After problems with iPhone alarms to start the new year, Apple said the error would be fixed by Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/technology/03iphone.html', 'snippet': 'After problems with iPhone alarms to start the new year, Apple said the error would be fixed by Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pat Kiernan, a morning anchor on NY1, the New York City cable news channel, is no stranger to alarm clock problems. That’s why he usually relies on several clocks, phones and other devices to wake him in time for his early newscasts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bug Causes iPhone Alarm to Greet New Year With Silence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bug Causes iPhone Alarm to Greet New Year With Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-02T21:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9c1b49-b3f8-5b70-ad46-66d9b1494269', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9c1b49-b3f8-5b70-ad46-66d9b1494269'}, {'abstract': 'As The Stone goes on hiatus, taking stock of seven months in the virtual agora.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/stoned/', 'snippet': 'As The Stone goes on hiatus, taking stock of seven months in the virtual agora.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many stones have been thrown since we first met here in May. Some have shattered windows of received wisdom; others have bounced off walls of resistance. Some have plopped quietly into inviting ponds of assent; others have rattled down unexplored alleys of thought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stoned', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Descartes, Rene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], '