esearch looks into the murky crossroads of risk and societal status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/business/media/03drill.html', 'snippet': 'A study in the Journal of Consumer Research looks into the murky crossroads of risk and societal status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last decade, researchers have begun to study the effects of anthropomorphizing an object — finding, for example, that people cooperate better with humanlike robots. A study to be published in the Journal of Consumer Research, conducted by Sara Kim and Professor Ann L. McGill of the University of Chicago, pursues this inquiry into the murky crossroads of risk and societal status.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling Powerful and Taking Risks', 'kicker': 'Drilling Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feeling Powerful and Taking Risks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slot Machines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T03:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Mindlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mindlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce73b495-c73e-5a7d-8528-3bcde63ebd86', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce73b495-c73e-5a7d-8528-3bcde63ebd86'}, {'abstract': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/business/03ahead.html', 'snippet': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include the Institute for Supply Management manufacturing index for December and construction spending for November (Monday); factory orders for November (Tuesday); the Institute for Supply Management service index for December and ADP’s employment figures for December (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims (Thursday); and unemployment for December and consumer credit for November (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Ahead to Economic Reports This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LOOKING AHEAD', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T03:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/06458f4b-ab6a-566d-9def-a05500247234', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06458f4b-ab6a-566d-9def-a05500247234'}, {'abstract': 'The current commanding officer of the nuclear-powered U.S.S. Enterprise starred in videos that showed women showering together, referenced masturbation and bestiality and included antigay slurs and vulgarities.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/02/crude-videos-aboard-an-aircraft-carrier/', 'snippet': 'The current commanding officer of the nuclear-powered U.S.S. Enterprise starred in videos that showed women showering together, referenced masturbation and bestiality and included antigay slurs and vulgarities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The videos resemble something a college fraternity could have put together as a joke and po