, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d6745fe-2a40-5545-9281-2fed24238055', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d6745fe-2a40-5545-9281-2fed24238055'}, {'abstract': 'The KW Institute for Contemporary Art in Berlin has brought together six “cells,” created by the artist Absalon, under one roof.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/in-berlin-one-artists-unusual-vision-for-living/', 'snippet': 'The KW Institute for Contemporary Art in Berlin has brought together six “cells,” created by the artist Absalon, under one roof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israeli artist Absalon died in Paris in 1993 at age 28. But before his untimely death, he produced a large body of work, including six tiny all-white dwellings that he wanted to install in downtown Tokyo, Paris, Zurich, New York, Tel Aviv and Frankfurt. The artist designed these “Cellules” (cells), as he called them, to fit his precise dimensions in a totally scaled-down living environment so that he would, in his own words, be “obliged to live my ideas.” Now, the KW Institute for Contemporary Art (Auguststrasse 69; 49-30-243-4590; www.kw-berlin.de) has brought together all six cells under one roof. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Berlin, One Artist’s Unusual Vision for Living', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T11:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally McGrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'or