'_id': 'nyt://article/dd29b803-0e19-5f4c-8ffd-8a4b338e62ba', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd29b803-0e19-5f4c-8ffd-8a4b338e62ba'}, {'abstract': 'In pro football, there are no magicians, no miracle workers and, despite what we’re often told, no geniuses. There’s no need for the Giants to hire another outstanding coach. They already have one.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/why-keeping-coughlin-was-right-call-for-giants/', 'snippet': 'In pro football, there are no magicians, no miracle workers and, despite what we’re often told, no geniuses. There’s no need for the Giants to hire another outstanding coach. They already have one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Barall, who writes about pro football history for the Fifth Down, wrote this comment on the Coughlin or Cowher? thread.  He wrote it before the Giants won their 10th game and before John Mara said Tom Coughlin “was still the guy that we want.” I’ve updated some numbers after Sunday’s game. TM', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Keeping Coughlin Was Right Call for Giants', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T13:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/82537673-22fb-5557-ba71-dda5415d9d74', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82537673-22fb-5557-ba71-dda5415d9d74'}, {'abstract': 'A savory empada — a Portuguese stuffed pastry — that is similar to a ratatouille wrapped in puff pastry', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/the-temporary-vegetarian-a-portuguese-empada/', 'snippet': 'A savory empada — a Portuguese stuffed pastry — that is similar to a ratatouille wrapped in puff pastry', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luisa Fernandes, 56, consulting chef at the Best Chocolate Cake in the World in Brooklyn, and executive chef at Nomad in Manhattan, makes a savory empada — a Portuguese stuffed pastry — that is similar to a ratatouille wrapped in puff pastry. She sautés eggplant, tomatoes, squash, onions and garlic, and once the vegetables are cooled, she tucks them into puff pastry in muffin tins, and bakes them until they are golden. “It’s a very old Portuguese recipe that’s served for lunch with a salad,” said Ms. Fernandes, who makes it for the Best Chocolate Cake in the World. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Temporary Vegetarian: A Portuguese Empada', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T13:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/896d7f1b-6757-51eb-988b-3a4bb73d6638', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/896d7f1b-6757-51eb-988b-3a4bb73d6638'}, {'abstract': 'The best of the holiday weekend’s political commentary, from Darrell Issa, Chris Christie, Lindsey Graham and more.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/best-political-quotes-of-the-weekend/', 'snippet': 'The best of the holiday weekend’s political commentary, from Darrell Issa, Chris Christie, Lindsey Graham and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy New Year. You may have been a bit too bleary-eyed from New Year’s Eve reveling to catch the best political commentary of the weekend, but we at The Caucus weren’t. Here’s a quick roundup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Political Quotes of the Weekend', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goolsbee, Austan D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T13:16:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/476b96ff-d2d7-5828-ae02-0736fbc3cda5', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/476b96ff-d2d7-5828-ae02-0736fbc3cda5'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: the new schools chancellor’s first day on the job, new state labor rules, and the rising cost of transportation in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/morning-buzz-cuomo-forecast-calls-for-pay-freeze/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: the new schools chancellor’s first day on the job, new state labor rules, and the rising cost of transportation in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. It’s back to chilly today, with a high of only 35 and a decent chance of residential trash pickup. Alternate side parking remains suspended for the 10th day in a row. Is that some kind of modern record? Here is the news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Cuomo Forecast Calls for Pay Freeze', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T13:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5460cc70-9521-516e-8937-405ceff3672f', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5460cc70-9521-516e-8937-405ceff3672f'}, {'abstract': 'The health care law will be under the microscope of the Republican majority in the House.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/this-weeks-health-industry-news-22/', 'snippet': 'The health care law will be under the microscope of the Republican majority in the House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 112th Congress convenes on Wednesday. Republicans who took control of the House of Representatives in the midterm election are shortly expected to introduce a measure to repeal and replace the health care legislation passed in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Health Industry News', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican