lic attention to the government’s investment in Ally Financial, formerly GMAC, has been scant in comparison to the coverage of the American International Group and General Motors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valuing Ally Financial', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ally Financial Inc.', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T14:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9264daf0-583e-516c-b478-195ee436b76b', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9264daf0-583e-516c-b478-195ee436b76b'}, {'abstract': 'Comparing President Obama with Candidate Obama and finding a lot of similarity.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/obama-more-left-or-right-than-expected/', 'snippet': 'Comparing President Obama with Candidate Obama and finding a lot of similarity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have President Obama’s economic positions been more left-wing than his campaign suggested? Or more right-wing?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama: More Left or Right Than Expected?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T14:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/665eb1f6-4691-5494-b038-e84e1ea9a2b5', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/665eb1f6-4691-5494-b038-e84e1ea9a2b5'}, {'abstract': 'In Copenhagen, a Danish men’s line turned a sex shop into its storefront.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/xxx-marks-the-spot-u-s-import/', 'snippet': 'In Copenhagen, a Danish men’s line turned a sex shop into its storefront.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s an old saw, but sex sells. So it makes perfect sense for the Danish men’s line Soulland to open in a former sex shop. In deference to the space’s former incarnation, the label has kept the name and sign from the previous tenant and is trading under the U.S. Import banner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'XXX Marks the Spot | U.S. Import', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T14:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cator Sparks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cator', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sparks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae40136e-9506-5bfe-a21c-55905ed2ad0e', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae40136e-9506-5bfe-a21c-55905ed2ad0e'}, {'abstract': 'In a new book, Harvard psychologists warn of a “new grief” experienced by today’s caregivers.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/the-caregivers-bookshelf-as-the-goodbye-grows-longer/', 'snippet': 'In a new book, Harvard psychologists warn of a “new grief” experienced by today’s caregivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years ago, when Elisabeth Kübler-Ross published her landmark book “On Death and Dying,” losing a family member was typically a swifter and more sudden event. Often people literally dropped dead with heart attacks. Today’s families usually confront a different reality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caregiver’s Bookshelf: The Goodbye Grows Longer', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotions)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T14:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a85098d8-7011-5592-8522-414e6eb6ea8c', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a85098d8-7011-5592-8522-414e6eb6ea8c'}, {'abstract': 'The debut of 17 Chinese companies backed by United States venture funds bolstered the market in the fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/late-surge-in-venture-backed-i-p-o-s/', 'snippet': 'The debut of 17 Chinese companies backed by United States venture funds bolstered the market in the fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As far as venture-backed initial public offerings are concerned, 2010 ended with a bang. ', 's