d ideas from many sources” but that he would probably also be “ineffective in tackling many of America’s biggest problems.”', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/cowens-2008-obama-predictions/', 'snippet': 'In 2008, Tyler Cowen of Marginal Revolution predicted President Obama would be “an economic pragmatist who is willing to borrow good ideas from many sources” but that he would probably also be “ineffective in tackling many of America’s biggest pro...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyler Cowen of Marginal Revolution has also dug up some of his 2008 writing on then-candidate Barack Obama:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cowen’s 2008 Obama Predictions', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T15:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c6e2e5b-08f2-5b61-8939-d7c3e7c7d46f', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c6e2e5b-08f2-5b61-8939-d7c3e7c7d46f'}, {'abstract': 'In a second report, construction spending rose more than expected in November, hitting its highest level in five months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/business/economy/04econ.html', 'snippet': 'In a second report, construction spending rose more than expected in November, hitting its highest level in five months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overall manufacturing activity expanded in December for the 17th consecutive month, although the industries related to the housing sector continued to struggle, according to a report released on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manufacturing Grew in December, but Housing Sector Struggled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manufacturing Grew in December, but Housing Sector Struggled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T15:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc903be-11cb-5900-8c2f-e5858b83609f', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc903be-11cb-5900-8c2f-e5858b83609f'}, {'abstract': 'A black soap should be in every man’s dopp kit. But which bar is the best?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/vain-glorious-black-soap/', 'snippet': 'A black soap should be in every man’s dopp kit. But which bar is the best?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aside from a good straight-razor shave, grooming doesn’t offer a man many indulgences. But there’s one simple luxury that should be in every dopp kit: a great bar of soap. The latest specimens to catch my eye are black — they smell of earth and ash and their color gives them a primal ruggedness, as if you’re back in the cave, washing yourself with mud. They don’t, counterintuitively, lather black. The way this nonchemist understands the science is that the particles in these bars aren’t actually black but completely opaque, and when they’re compressed into soap, no light gets in. No light equals black. But never mind all that. Let’s suds them up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Black Soap', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T15:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffries Blackerby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffries', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blackerby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/97618fc2-17f5-5efa-9079-90753083cbd5', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97618fc2-17f5-5efa-9079-90753083cbd5'}, {'abstract': 'Stamps that always remain valid, perks from vacation rentals and other consumer-focused items from Monday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/monday-reading-more-forever-stamps/', 'snippet': 'Stamps that always remain valid, perks from vacation rentals and other consumer-focused items from Monday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: More Forever Stamps', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T15:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bae2f73-cb91-522e-9ddc-9f38f49204f1', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bae2f73-cb91-522e-9ddc-9f38f49204f1'}, {'abstract': 'A new film follows a theater troupe that travels around the United States teaching and performing classical works in communities where theater is a luxury.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/henry-in-the-hinterlands-5-questions-about-still-on-the-road/', 'snippet': 'A new film follows a theater troupe that travels around the United States teaching and performing classical works in communities where theater is a luxury.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Still on the Road,” a new film by Sara Wolkowitz, documents several months in the lives of the Acting Company, a theater troupe that travels around the United States teaching and performing classical works in communities where theater is a luxury, if it’s around at all. Ms. Wolkowitz will introduce her debut feature film, which she directed, edited and produced, when it is screened Monday night by the Film Society of Lincoln Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Henry’ in the Hinterlands: Five Questions About ‘Still on the Road’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T15:42:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4844f95-2bce-5d63-b0c7-fdc3171b1181', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4844f95-2bce-5d63-b0c7-fdc3171b1181'}, {'abstract': 'Activate your creativity with this data visualization challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/numberplay-away-hyper-pen/', 'snippet': 'Activate your creativity with this data visualization challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We puzzle solvers write a lot. Especially when solving involves correspondence. This is generally the case on Numberplay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Away, Hyper Pen!', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horne, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Many Eyes (Web Site)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T16:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/614f735a-a50c-50e9-b482-a106908d3ac8', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/614f735a-a50c-50e9-b482-a106908d3ac8'}, {'abstract': 'As one Chicago columnist put it, the Bears were “playing for the ideal of playing hard all the time.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/n-f-l-wins-as-bears-lose-with-class/', 'snippet': 'As one Chicago columnist put it, the Bears were “playing for the ideal of playing hard all the time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bears didn’t have to do it, but they competed with their best against the Packers on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Wins as Bears Lose With Class', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'ma