e cannot help everybody.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/my-resolution-the-24-burger-strategy/', 'snippet': 'The last 12 months confirmed something I’ve known about my industry — and my business — for a while now: we cannot help everybody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the season for resolutions — a time to take stock of the recent past and set goals for the coming year. As my husband and I strive to position our small-business brokerage firm as the best in class in our region, we continually try to draw on lessons learned from other professional service providers: law firms, accounting practices and wealth planners, to name a few. Next year, however, we will be looking to a rather unlikely source for business inspiration: a pub.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Resolution: The 24-Burger Strategy', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T17:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/26269625-1b91-57eb-b96e-907abfdbea48', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26269625-1b91-57eb-b96e-907abfdbea48'}, {'abstract': 'The Portuguese soprano Elisabete Matos will replace Deborah Voigt as Minnie, the gun-toting fearless saloon owner in Puccini’s “La Fanciulla del West,’’ at the Metropolitan Opera on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/elisabete-matos-to-replace-deborah-voigt-at-the-metropolitan-opera-tonight/', 'snippet': 'The Portuguese soprano Elisabete Matos will replace Deborah Voigt as Minnie, the gun-toting fearless saloon owner in Puccini’s “La Fanciulla del West,’’ at the Metropolitan Opera on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Portuguese soprano Elisabete Matos will replace Deborah Voigt as Minnie, the fearless, gun-toting saloon owner in Puccini’s “Fanciulla del West,” at the Metropolitan Opera on Monday night. Ms. Voigt, who is ill, has starred in the role since the production opened early last month. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elisabete Matos to Replace Deborah Voigt at the Metropolitan Opera Tonight', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T17:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c86ec9-af04-5ca1-ac27-f13636c9cff9', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c86ec9-af04-5ca1-ac27-f13636c9cff9'}, {'abstract': 'A large fraction of the formerly jobless who have found new work have had to switch careers, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/the-jobs-they-are-a-changin/', 'snippet': 'A large fraction of the formerly jobless who have found new work have had to switch careers, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large fraction of displaced workers who have found new jobs have had to switch careers, and most of those career-changers have downgraded to a lower-paying job, according to a new report from Rutgers’s Heldrich Center for Workforce Development.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Jobs They Are A-Changin’', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None