ter he landed on the island of Oahu.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama in Oahu: Semper Fit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T18:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b230588e-fa22-5beb-9825-953fe4068e02', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b230588e-fa22-5beb-9825-953fe4068e02'}, {'abstract': '[1] Holding on to a job rather than retiring or moving elsewhere. [2] Young workers who view employment as an entitlement, while complaining about hours and remuneration.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/job-clinging-and-slackoisie/', 'snippet': '[1] Holding on to a job rather than retiring or moving elsewhere. [2] Young workers who view employment as an entitlement, while complaining about hours and remuneration.', 'lead_paragraph': '[1] Holding on to a job rather than retiring or moving elsewhere. [2] Young workers who view employment as an entitlement, while complaining about hours and remuneration.Writing for Forbes, Victoria Pynchon spotlighted two terms associated with Generation Y and boomer workers:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Clinging and Slackoisie', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T19:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlena