es', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran May Drop Stoning Sentence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Says Change in Stoning Sentence Is Possible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashtiani, Sakineh Mohammadi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T20:51:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf6473c-8628-503e-aec1-074aaeb414db', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf6473c-8628-503e-aec1-074aaeb414db'}, {'abstract': 'Naked Angels, which develops new plays, announced on Monday that Andy Donald would succeed Geoffrey Nauffts as artistic director in July.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/naked-angels-names-new-artistic-director/', 'snippet': 'Naked Angels, which develops new plays, announced on Monday that Andy Donald would succeed Geoffrey Nauffts as artistic director in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York theater company Naked Angels, which develops new plays and had its first production on Broadway last year with the drama “Next Fall,” announced on Monday that Andy Donald would succeed Geoffrey Nauffts as artistic director in July. Mr. Donald, a theater director and producer, has been associate artistic director of Naked Angels since April 2009. Mr. Nauffts, an actor, director, and long-time company member of Naked Angels, became artistic director in September 2007 but soon found himself celebrated as a writer for “Next Fall,” his first play. The Naked Angels production of “Next Fall” had a critically acclaimed run Off Broadway in 2009, then transferred to Broadway the next year. While receiving strong reviews there as well as Tony Award nominations, including for best play, the production was not a commercial success and ran for about five months. Mr. Nauffts said in a statement that he planned to continue to write and direct for Naked Angels, and advise on artistic matters as a board member. Mr. Donald, the founding artistic director of the Charlie B. Theater Company in Los Angeles, said in the statement that he looked forward to bringing new writers and others into the company. Among the company’s offerings this season is the world premiere of the play “A Long and Happy Life,” by Bekah Brunstetter, and another world premiere, “Outside People,” by Zayd Dohrn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Naked Angels Names New Artistic Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T20:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2067e3c3-3369-5001-b05e-962a92fa2bc3', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2067e3c3-3369-5001-b05e-962a92fa2bc3'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists were trying to determine why thousands of red-winged blackbirds rained on the city about 11 on New Year’s Eve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/us/04beebe.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists were trying to determine why thousands of red-winged blackbirds rained on the city about 11 on New Year’s Eve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Square had the ball drop, and Brasstown, N.C., had its descending possum. But no place had a New Year’s Eve as unusual, or freakishly disturbing, as Beebe, Ark. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/us/04beebe_337-395/04beebe_337-395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/us/04beebe_337-395/04beebe_337-395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/04/us/04beebe_337-395/04beebe_337-395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Arkansas Blackbirds, the New Year Never Came', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Arkansas Blackbirds, The New Year Never Came', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fireworks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T20:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2ab1d65-0488-5d7c-be9e-301211862026', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c