'_id': 'nyt://article/7aa5c9ec-cbfb-5e63-84e6-7d616a165469', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aa5c9ec-cbfb-5e63-84e6-7d616a165469'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Brady finished the season with 36 touchdown passes and 4 interceptions, an astonishing 9.0 touchdown-to-interception ratio, breaking the record set by Tom Brady, in 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/bradys-spectacular-season/', 'snippet': 'Tom Brady finished the season with 36 touchdown passes and 4 interceptions, an astonishing 9.0 touchdown-to-interception ratio, breaking the record set by Tom Brady, in 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time to end the most valuable player conversation. Tom Brady finished the season with 36 touchdown passes and 4 interceptions, an astonishing 9.0 touchdown-to-interception ratio. That broke the previous record of 6.25, also set by Brady in 2007, when he threw 50 touchdowns and had eight interceptions. No other quarterback has ever topped a 6.0 ratio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brady’s Spectacular Season', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T21:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc8c5a5c-3c11-50cb-b76b-55fc9adbe029', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc8c5a5c-3c11-50cb-b76b-55fc9adbe029'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook chatter| The Citadel exodus| A.I.G.-Blackstone at odds?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/buzz-tracker/', 'snippet': 'Facebook chatter| The Citadel exodus| A.I.G.-Blackstone at odds?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sampling of what’s making the rounds in the deal-making ecosystem:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buzz Tracker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T21:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/96a2c8ea-2442-5db8-bcb9-b5476bad9780', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96a2c8ea-2442-5db8-bcb9-b5476bad9780'}, {'abstract': 'Broadway did smashing business during the week of the New Year’s holiday in spite of inconveniences related to the blizzard cleanup.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/broadway-closes-2010-with-big-ticket-sales/', 'snippet': 'Broadway did smashing business during the week of the New Year’s holiday in spite of inconveniences related to the blizzard cleanup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway did smashing business during the week of the New Year’s holiday in spite of inconveniences related to the blizzard cleanup, with 16 musicals and one play (“The Merchant of Venice”) each drawing more than $1 million and contributing to a total take of $35 million, according to the Broadway League, the theater trade group that publishes weekly grosses every Monday. That $35 million represents a sizable increase over the $28.1 million for the comparable week in 2009. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Enters 2011 With Big Ticket Sales', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T21:47:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/13f761d1-1ebc-52d7-a768-ead0d8f67fb2', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f761d1-1ebc-52d7-a768-ead0d8f67fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Steele’s rivals offered even tougher criticism of the Republican National Committee chairman after Monday’s five-way debate ended than they did during the 90-minute exchange.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/steeles-rivals-ratchet-up-criticism-after-debate/', 'snippet': 'Michael Steele’s rivals offered even tougher criticism of the Republican National Committee chairman after Monday’s five-way debate ended than they did during the 90-minute exchange.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Steele’s rivals offered even tougher criticism of the Republican National Committee chairman after Monday’s five-way debate ended than they did during the 90-minute exchange.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steele’s Rivals Ratchet Up Criticism After Debate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-03T21:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b49d8cda-c461-5420-a35c-a884b307ed5f', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b49d8cda-c461-5420-a35c-a884b307ed5f'}, {'abstract': 'Hubert Dreyfus and Sean Dorrance Kelly see the “human indecision that plagues us all” and explain how we got into this mess and how we can overcome it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/books/04book.html', 'snippet': 'Hubert Dreyfus and Sean Dorrance Kelly see the “human indecision that plagues us all” and explain how we got into this mess and how we can overcome it.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The philosopher Hubert Dreyfus and his former student Sean Dorrance Kelly have a story to tell, and it is not a pretty tale for us moderns. Ours is an age of nihilism, they say, meaning not so much that we have nothing in which to believe, but that we don’t know how to choose among the various things to which we might commit ourselves. Looking down from their perches at Berkeley and Harvard, they see the “human indecision that plagues us all.” In “All Things Shining” they offer readings of classic texts to show both how we got into this mess and how we can overcome it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/arts/book-3/book-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 990, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/arts/book-3/book-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/04/arts/book-3/book-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Classics as the Antidote to Modern Malaise', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Classics as the Antidote to Modern Malaise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and 