middlename': 'Claiborne', 'lastname': 'Ray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1faece7-80b5-524d-a97c-7c05b623b531', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1faece7-80b5-524d-a97c-7c05b623b531'}, {'abstract': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev of Russia has agreed to postpone a visit to Israel this month because of a strike by Israeli Foreign Ministry staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/world/middleeast/04webbrfs.html', 'snippet': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev of Russia has agreed to postpone a visit to Israel this month because of a strike by Israeli Foreign Ministry staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev of Russia has agreed to postpone a visit to Israel this month because of a strike by Israeli Foreign Ministry staff, a ministry spokesman said Monday. “This is not directed against Medvedev or Russia,” said the spokesman, Yigal Palmor. “But since we are on strike, we are unable to prepare for the visit. It was decided by both sides to postpone it.” Mr. Medvedev was supposed to come with a 500-strong delegation. Foreign Ministry workers are striking for more pay and better conditions. Israeli newspapers have carried reports about Israeli diplomats abroad who say they live in poverty and in some cases rely on financial support from their parents back home. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Strike Delays Russian Visit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing  | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-