alue': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T04:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8ae7b9d-4731-54a1-b78f-e5d6b842a620', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8ae7b9d-4731-54a1-b78f-e5d6b842a620'}, {'abstract': '“Spiderman” gets a news lead actress after the departure of an actress hurt during a production.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/spiderman-gets-a-new-lead-actress/', 'snippet': '“Spiderman” gets a news lead actress after the departure of an actress hurt during a production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lead role of the villainous spider-woman Arachne in the Broadway musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” will now be played by cast member T.V. Carpio, the show’s lead producer, Michael Cohl, announced in a statement on Tuesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Spider-Man’ Gets a New Lead Actress', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T04:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1595778c-34c0-5beb-8f87-fe7b029bcc8c', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1595778c-34c0-5beb-8f87-fe7b029bcc8c'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican agenda: more riches for the rich, more misery for the rest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/opinion/04herbert.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican agenda: more riches for the rich, more misery for the rest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You just can’t close the door on this crowd. The party that brought us the worst economy since the Great Depression, that led us into Iraq and the worst foreign policy disaster in American history, that would like to take a hammer to Social Security and a chisel to Medicare, is back in control of the House of Representatives with the expressed mission of undermining all things Obama.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Ready for a G.O.P. Rerun', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Ready For a G.O.P. Rerun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T04:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Herbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e2c35c-c15a-5887-9826-d384daf17eb6', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9e2c35c-c15a-5887-9826-d384daf17eb6'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama ends his Hawaii trip with a family outing.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/03/obama-wraps-up-hawaii-trip-with-family-outing/', 'snippet': 'President Obama ends his Hawaii trip with a family outing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU – After a peaceful 11-day respite that was heavy on morning workouts and afternoon golf, President Obama wrapped up his Hawaiian vacation on Monday with an action-packed afternoon of family activities. He mingled with locals at Island Snow, his favorite spot for Hawaiian shave ice – he caught a clerk off guard when he flashed a $100 bill to pay for the treats — and also took his daughters to the military cemetery where his grandfather is buried and later to the Honolulu Zoo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Wraps Up Hawaii Trip With Family Outing', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T04:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/410842db-1aa7-5d39-9ac5-a68ff5564038', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/410842db-1aa7-5d39-9ac5-a68ff5564038'}, {'abstract': 'The Republicans’ refusal to give prompt consideration to noncontroversial judicial nominees sets a terrible precedent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/opinion/04tue1.html', 'snippet': 'The Republicans’ refusal to give prompt consideration to noncontroversial judicial nominees sets a terrible precedent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual report on the federal judiciary by the chief justice of the United States is not a place you would normally go for political agitation. But that is just what Chief Justice John Roberts Jr. offered by using a portion of his year-end review to deplore the “acute difficulties” created for the justice system by the Senate’s slowness in approving President Obama’s nominees for federal judgeships.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Missing Judges', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Missing Judges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T04:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad970185-1f33-5d97-a66b-c8dfd408ef39', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad970185-1f33-5d97-a66b-c8dfd408ef39'}, {'abstract': 'A media law that took effect in Hungary this week marks a sorry step back toward political censorship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/opinion/04tue2.html', 'snippet': 'A media law that took effect in Hungary this week marks a sorry step back toward political censorship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hungarians are justly proud of the way their country stood up to Soviet tanks in 1956 and helped breach the Iron Curtain with freer emigration in 1989. But they can take no pride in a new media law that took effect this week, just as Hungary took over the rotating presidency of the European Union. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Orban Forgets', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Orban Forgets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orban, Viktor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T05:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bf6520b-9836-5fe5-9dad-0f3b872a7264', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bf6520b-9836-5fe5-9dad-0f3b872a7264'}, {'abstract': 'At this week’s Consumer Electronics Show, makers show off new computer chips that combine top-level computation and graphics functions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/technology/04chip.html', 'snippet': 'At this week’s Consumer Electronics Show, makers show off new computer chips that combine top-level computation and graphics functions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the good old days, it was all about speed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphics Ability Is the New Goal for Chip Makers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Graphics Ability Is the New Goal For Chip Makers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T05:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashlee Vance', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashlee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vance', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb4457ce-4735-55d4-869a-ad83168c22f8', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb4457ce-4735-55d4-869a-ad83168c22f8'}, {'abstract': 'The financial markets need clear and vigilantly enforced rules on what’s fairly researched information and what’s an illegal tip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/opinion/04tue3.html', 'snippet': 'The financial markets need clear and vigilantly enforced rules on what’s fairly researched information and what’s an illegal tip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As of today, seven people have been charged in an insider-trading investigation focused on investors and consultants connected to Primary Global Research, an expert-network firm. The cases, brought by Preet Bharara, the United States attorney in Manhattan, paint a disturbing picture of how some hedge funds have used this company to illegally procure information and distort the workings of a healthy financial market. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Market Tips', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Market Tips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primary Global Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T05:03:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d36e957-9cc9-5125-a58a-a9b62ac6ea4e', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d36e957-9cc9-5125-a58a-a9b62ac6ea4e'}, {'abstract': 'Where massive mounds of snow once rose, there are rising mounds of garbage and Christmas trees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/opinion/04tue4.html', 'snippet': 'Where massive mounds of snow once rose, there are rising mounds of garbage and Christmas trees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First there was the fresh snow, lying white and undisturbed all across New York. Then \x97 if you were lucky \x97 came the plowing, followed by the big melt last weekend, which turned the city into an archipelago surrounded by slush ponds. Now, where massive mounds of snow once rose, there are rising mounds of black garbage bags awaiting pickup by many of the same trucks that have been busy plowing streets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times'