New Year’s Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/world/middleeast/04egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of angry rioters broke through police lines, pelting officers with rocks and bottles in a third day of unrest set off by a bomb blast outside a church following a New Year’s Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO \x97 Thousands of angry rioters broke through police lines, pelting officers with rocks and bottles and beating them with makeshift wooden crosses in a third day of unrest set off by a bomb blast outside a church after a New Year’s Mass, which killed 21 and wounded about 100.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clashes Grow as Egyptians Remain Angry After an Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clashes Grow As Egyptians Remain Angry After an Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEXANDRIA (EGYPT)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T08:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack and Michael Slackman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slackman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c164