le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/44b649c1-ceda-5040-96d6-2f44fd5124b8', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44b649c1-ceda-5040-96d6-2f44fd5124b8'}, {'abstract': 'Grupo ACS, the Spanish construction company, says its holding in Hochtief, a smaller German rival, has surpassed 30 percent in response to a tender offer, clearing a major hurdle as it seeks full control of Hochtief.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/acs-amasses-more-than-30-of-hochtief/', 'snippet': 'Grupo ACS, the Spanish construction company, says its holding in Hochtief, a smaller German rival, has surpassed 30 percent in response to a tender offer, clearing a major hurdle as it seeks full control of Hochtief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grupo ACS, the Spanish construction company, said on Tuesday that its holding in Hochtief, a smaller German rival, had surpassed 30 percent in response to a tender offer the company made last year, clearing a major hurdle as it seeks full control of the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grupo ACS Amasses More Than 30% of Hochtief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grupo ACS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hochtief AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T10:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b8e57ef-c8e3-536e-99b7-819efdba06ad', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b8e57ef-c8e3-536e-99b7-819efdba06ad'}, {'abstract': 'Le Bal, a cultural space that opened in Paris this fall, was named for its seedy legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/putting-an-artistic-gloss-on-a-paris-cast-off/', 'snippet': 'Le Bal, a cultural space that opened in Paris this fall, was named for its seedy legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cultural space that opened this fall was named for its seedy legacy. Back in the roaring ’20s, Le Bal was a cabaret, dance club and “hôtel d’amour” (read: brothel). After World War II, the venue was converted into the largest PMU (“Pari mutuel urbain,” a bar for betting on horses) in France. Vacated and abandoned by 1992, it was re-purchased by the city in 2006 and selected as the spot for a multipurpose art space that includes galleries, a bookstore and a cafe. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting an Artistic Gloss on a Paris Cast-Off', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe532b1-b230-50e8-8b55-bc194c9cf434', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe532b1-b230-50e8-8b55-bc194c9cf434'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Moyar takes up case studies of counterinsurgency campaigns to discuss the role of leadership as a factor in conventional military performance.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/what-they-are-reading-a-question-of-command/', 'snippet': 'Mark Moyar takes up case studies of counterinsurgency campaigns to discuss the role of leadership as a factor in conventional military performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year At War will profile books, articles and other reading materials that those directly involved in the wars in Afghanistan and Iraq have found valuable in their preparations for working in the field. The first post in this series presented Abdul Salam Zaeef’s “My Life With The Taliban,” an insider’s account of the Taliban that is required reading for officers in an Army aviation task force now working in southern Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What They Are Reading: ‘A Question of Command’', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T11:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/456ed04b-6ab9-5339-b4bf-91d28b48c486', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/456ed04b-6ab9-5339-b4bf-91d28b48c486'}, {'abstract': 'A day before the 112th Congress convenes, Republicans and Demcrats are plotting ways to challenge each other, with an eye to the 2012 elections.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/the-early-word-preparing-to-fight/', 'snippet': 'A day before the 112th Congress convenes, Republicans and Demc