ght.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/fearing-another-u-s-debt-default/', 'snippet': 'Arguing for raising the debt ceiling, a White House economist said a sovereign debt default by the United States would be “unprecedented.” That’s not quite right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend, Austan Goolsbee, the chairman of the president’s Council of Economic Advisers, argued that Congress should raise the debt ceiling. In an interview with ABC’s “This Week,” he said, “If we hit the debt ceiling, that’s essentially defaulting on our obligations, which is totally unprecedented in American history. The impact on the economy would be catastrophic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fearing (Another) U.S. Debt Default', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goolsbee, Austan D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T14:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/04881ad9-ec91-57ea-a69b-17009a765171', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04881ad9-ec91-57ea-a69b-17009a765171'}, {'abstract': 's I’ve discussed often, we try to avoid colloquial or slang expressions in straight news stories. Even in features we should use them judiciously, for special effect. Chatty or colloquial language, in news stories in particular, can undercut the serious tone we strive for. Beyond that, as The Times’s stylebook often points out, many colloquial expressions are tired, h