delightful scene? By making a mistake in his travel plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe it was relief that New York was recovering from last week’s blizzard or elation that the holidays had come to an end. Whatever — Fred R. Conrad’s picture of a balloon deliverer on a subway platform in Lower Manhattan perfectly captured the sense of the moment in the city and earned itself a berth on the front page of The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong Station, Right Image', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T17:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a0b19c4-30fd-552f-a3c2-a179a24a0e35', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a0b19c4-30fd-552f-a3c2-a179a24a0e35'}, {'abstract': 'Nicholas Brooks is arraigned on a second-degree murder charge in the killing of Sylvie Cachay.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/designers-family-face-to-face-with-man-accused-in-her-death/', 'snippet': 'Nicholas Brooks is arraigned on a second-degree murder charge in the killing of Sylvie Cachay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family of a fashion designer found dead last month in the Soho House hotel in the meatpacking district saw the man accused of killing her, Nicholas Brooks, for the first time since her death when he was arraigned Tuesday on a second-degree murder charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Designer’