_id': 'nyt://article/c58fca65-4842-5b3b-9f65-f36d3bdf4acb', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58fca65-4842-5b3b-9f65-f36d3bdf4acb'}, {'abstract': 'Let the complaining begin!', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/is-technology-driving-you-up-a-tree/', 'snippet': 'Let the complaining begin!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Technology is wonderful — when it isn’t driving you up a tree screaming. What I’d like to know is, which limb of the tree are you ending up on, and what are you screaming? And which aspects of technology keep you up at night? To paraphrase, happy consumers of business information technology are all alike, but every unhappy consumer of business I.T. is unhappy in his or her own way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Technology Driving You Up a Tree?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/206ebaba-71e1-5e28-83ae-cfc2deb314ec', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206ebaba-71e1-5e28-83ae-cfc2deb314ec'}, {'abstract': 'The new editor is Lindsay Pollock, a reporter for Bloomberg.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/art-in-america-names-new-editor-in-chief/', 'snippet': 'The new editor is Lindsay Pollock, a reporter for Bloomberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lindsay Pollock, a reporter for Bloomberg and the author of “The Girl with the Gallery,” about Edith Gregor Halpert, has been named editor in chief of Art in America. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art in America Names New Editor in Chief', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollock, Lindsay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:13:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9de1ab7-6030-5f53-ad3a-c7948a3df617', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9de1ab7-6030-5f53-ad3a-c7948a3df617'}, {'abstract': 'Huffington Post puts out a help-wanted sign.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/huffpo-hangs-the-help-wanted-sign/', 'snippet': 'Huffington Post puts out a help-wanted sign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pull up to the bar at any Manhattan media watering hole and you will hear the long, low groans of journos who bemoan the sad state of the industry. But the relative health of the media employment economy really depends on where you are looking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HuffPo Hangs the ‘Help Wanted’ Sign', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huffington, Arianna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/63ef7cac-0f22-5851-9ac6-166d305f7d21', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63ef7cac-0f22-5851-9ac6-166d305f7d21'}, {'abstract': 'New discoveries in the Mush Valley in Ethiopia include 22-million-year-old fossils of mammals as well as evidence of leaf consumption by insects.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/evidence-of-mammals-and-legumes-22-million-years-old/', 'snippet': 'New discoveries in the Mush Valley in Ethiopia include 22-million-year-old fossils of mammals as well as evidence of leaf consumption by insects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bonnie F. Jacobs, a paleobotanist at Southern Methodist University, writes from Ethiopia, where she is studying fossils of ancient plant and animal life. The current field season in the Mush Valley of Ethiopia is financed by a grant to Ellen Currano of Miami University, Ohio, from the National Geographic Society Committee on Research and Exploration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evidence of Mammals and Legumes, 22 Million Years Old', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Methodist University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Miami', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bonnie F. Jacobs and Ellen Currano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bonnie', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/edc70737-d43d-5ff9-a054-495ae5dfa902', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edc70737-d43d-5ff9-a054-495ae5dfa902'}, {'abstract': 'About 300 economists have signed a letter calling on the American Economic Association to adopt a code of ethics requiring members to disclose potential conflicts of interest.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/letter-calls-on-economists-to-adopt-code-of-ethics/', 'snippet': 'About 300 economists have signed a letter calling on the American Economic Association to adopt a code of ethics requiring members to disclose potential conflicts of interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 300 economists have signed a letter calling on the American Economic Association, the world’s largest professional society for economists, to adopt a code of ethics requiring members to disclose potential conflicts of interest. As I reported last week, the association’s executive committee plans to take up the matter this week during the group’s annual meeting in Denver.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter Calls on Economists to Adopt Code of Ethics', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Robert E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ECONOMIC ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMHERST (MASS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af99f4d-feef-5add-856b-00d2924cc0cb', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af99f4d-feef-5add-856b-00d2924cc0cb'}, {'abstract': 'Wilson Jermaine Heredia will replace Robin de Jesús in the role of the sassy housekeeper Jacob.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/wilson-jermaine-heredia-returns-to-broadway-in-la-cage/', 'snippet': 'Wilson Jermaine Heredia will replace Robin de Jesús in the role of the sassy housekeeper Jacob.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Wilson Jermaine Heredia, who won a Tony for “Rent” in 1996 but hasn’t been back on Broadway since, will replace Robin de Jesús in the role of the sassy housekeeper, Jacob, in the revival of “La Cage aux Folles,” the producers announced Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilson Jermaine Heredia Returns to Broadway in ‘La Cage’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heredia, Wilson Jermaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0fd80cf-802d-5ae7-97ca-27b9be7e7134', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0fd80cf-802d-5ae7-97ca-27b9be7e7134'}, {'abstract': 'How a miscalculation in a trip to Brooklyn led to a photograph on Page 1 of The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/special-delivery/', 'snippet': 'How a miscalculation in a trip to Brooklyn led to a photograph on Page 1 of The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Fred R. Conrad wasn’t supposed to be at the Chambers Street subway station. He wasn’t even supposed to be in Manhattan. But a miscalculation in his travel itinerary left him in a spot where he could take this delightful photograph, which earned a berth on Page 1 of The Times. Our neighbors at Lens have the full story: “Wrong Station, Right Image.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Special Delivery', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T18:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4a579c-2fae-56da-b0a2-124bde44aae4', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4a579c-2fae-56da-b0a2-124bde44aae4'}, {'abstract': 'Shamsher Wadud, who used to own the restaurant Nirvana, is in tight quarters, and he hates it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/nyregion/05about.html', 'snippet': 'Shamsher Wadud, who used to own the restaurant Nirvana, is in tight quarters, and he hates it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pull back the curtain that runs down the middle of the room and look at the clutter by the window: two computer printers that double as fax machines, papers strewn on the bed. But there is also what you can’t see: the occupant’s memories of the night he opened a restaurant and George Harrison came in; the time Keith Richards showed up for dinner, unannounced, with 12 people in tow; the visit from Dan Aykroyd and his wife, Donna Dixon, both hungry. Very hungry. The bill came to $600.51.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/multimedia/author-james-barron/author-james-barron-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150