 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4975164e-ed8f-5036-8013-06d93f522433', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4975164e-ed8f-5036-8013-06d93f522433'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Affleck is nominated for “The Town,” while films like “I Love You Phillip Morris” and “Please Give” also receive some writerly love.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/writers-guild-offers-up-a-few-surprises/', 'snippet': 'Ben Affleck is nominated for “The Town,” while films like “I Love You Phillip Morris” and “Please Give” also receive some writerly love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It continues to be a good day for Ben Affleck. On top of picking up a Producers Guild nomination for “The Town,” this drama also received a nod from the Writers Guild of America on Tuesday, and Mr. Affleck stands to take home a trophy himself, as a credited screenwriter on the adaptation of the novel “Prince of Thieves” by Chuck Hogan. After being overlooked by the Golden Globes and the Screen Actors Guild, the Coen brothers also scored with an adapted screenplay nomination for “True Grit.” (The Bagger happened to be on the phone with the Coens when the nominations were announced, so we got to give them the good news. They were like, “Oh. Cool.”) The other guild nominations for that category are “127 Hours,” “The Social Network,” and another surprise, “I Love You Phillip Morris,” starring Jim Carrey and Ewan McGregor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writers Guild Offers Up a Few Surprises', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key