5a-515a-9cc3-52db3fd5d70f', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb2a75c-b35a-515a-9cc3-52db3fd5d70f'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Tierney takes to airwaves to support “Spider-Man” and says the show has been safely put together.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/four-injured-performers-is-just-not-strange-recovering-spider-man-dancer-says/', 'snippet': 'Christopher Tierney takes to airwaves to support “Spider-Man” and says the show has been safely put together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, the “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” performer Christopher Tierney was on morphine at Bellevue Hospital Center and wondering, in moments of clarity, whether it would take months or years to recover after falling more than 20 feet at the Dec. 20 performance. Only one week ago Mr. Tierney left intensive care for Manhattan’s Rusk Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine. But on Tuesday, the long-locked, muscular performer was bounding around the set of ABC’s “Good Morning, America” and smiling for photos by onlookers — the only visible evidence of his serious injuries being a torso brace covered with stencil images of Spider-Man.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Four Injured Performers Is Just Not Strange,’ Recovering ‘Spider-Man’ Dancer Says', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tierney, Christopher', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACTORS EQUITY ASSN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T20:26:38+0