eld without being sentenced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL \x97 More than 20 suspected militants, including members of an extreme Islamist organization, were released from Turkish jails on Tuesday after a Supreme Court of Appeals ruling that limits to 10 years the time detainees can be held without being sentenced.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Court Ruling, Turkey Frees 23 Suspected Militants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Court Ruling, Turkey Frees 23 Suspected Militants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:19:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6914b68d-c298-58fd-baee-64c3d9237e19', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6914b68d-c298-58fd-baee-64c3d9237e19'}, {'abstract': 'The Penfolds line of wines sold by Treasury Wine Estates is becoming the first wine brand to take part in (Red), the effort to fight AIDS in Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/wine-sales-to-benefit-product-red-aids-fight/', 'snippet': 'The Penfolds line of wines sold by Treasury Wine Estates is becoming the first wine brand to take part in (Red), the effort to fight AIDS in Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:12 p.m. | Updated (Product) Red, the effort to fight AIDS in Africa, is teaming up with its first alcoholic beverage partner, which also happens to be its first marketer partner from Australia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wine Sales to Benefit (Product) Red AIDS Fight', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Product Red', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:20:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76d8a63-30de-5a3c-9d02-22f24da6a449', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76d8a63-30de-5a3c-9d02-22f24da6a449'}, {'abstract': 'A 66-year-old man found ailing on a Manhattan subway platform died of a combination of hypothermia and natural disease, the authorities say.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/man-found-on-subway-platform-during-storm-froze-to-death/', 'snippet': 'A 66-year-old man found ailing on a Manhattan subway platform died of a combination of hypothermia and natural disease, the authorities say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 66-year-old man died of a combination of hypothermia and underlying disease after being found ailing on a Manhattan subway platform last Monday during the snowstorm, the medical examiner’s office said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Found on Subway Platform During Storm Froze to Death', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee100358-25c7-5c08-b0d4-b34afee6b8b1', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee100358-25c7-5c08-b0d4-b34afee6b8b1'}, {'abstract': 'Fill in the blanks in this column about a recent debutante ball in Manhattan. Use your own words and phrases, or choose from a scrambled list of the words or phrases that were removed.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/fill-in-debutante-ball/', 'snippet': 'Fill in the blanks in this column about a recent debutante ball in Manhattan. Use your own words and phrases, or choose from a scrambled list of the words or phrases that were removed.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fill-In | Debutante Ball', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:26:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d8b6a0-c438-509e-a482-8607b2849d94', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d8b6a0-c438-509e-a482-8607b2849d94'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Stephen Clarke played works by composers who shared a passion for dense, shifting textures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/arts/music/05stephen.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Stephen Clarke played works by composers who shared a passion for dense, shifting textures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Clarke, a Canadian pianist who revels in the challenges of difficult new music, played a concert at Le Poisson Rouge on Monday evening to celebrate the release of “Giacinto Scelsi: Piano Works 4,” his latest contribution to the Mode label’s CD series devoted to this idiosyncratic Italian composer’s music. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/STEPHENALT/STEPHENALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pianist Revels in Scores That Dare the Ear', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pianist Revels in Scores That Dare the Ear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorabji, Kaikhosru Shapurji', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scelsi, Giacinto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e76f6c08-dbe4-51c4-b814-37924480c2e4', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e76f6c08-dbe4-51c4-b814-37924480c2e4'}, {'abstract': 'The adventurous Brooklyn electronic duo Blondes pose for a photo shoot. “I’ve definitely never worn a kilt before,” says one band member.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/smart-blondes/', 'snippet': 'The adventurous Brooklyn electronic duo Blondes pose for a photo shoot. “I’ve definitely never worn a kilt before,” says one band member.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn duo Blondes makes shimmering electronic music, but the members Zach Steinman and Sam Haar used to be more interested in guitars than synths. “In college we were into Gang of Four and Television,” Steinman said, “but our tastes evolved through ’70s disco and Kraut, and eventually ’80s electronic.” It’s a trajectory that is evident in the sparse vocal samples and economical beats on their well received debut EP, “Touched.” The pair’s creative adventurousness also spilled over into a recent photo shoot for The Moment, for which Steinman and Haar were fittingly dressed in clothes by White Mountaineering, a Japanese label that mixes up American and avant-garde references with the same abandon as Blondes’ experimenting on their synths. (Yosuke Aizawa, the White Mountaineering designer, honed his chops assisting Junya Watanabe, one of the iconoclasts of Japanese fashion.) “I’ve definitely never worn a kilt before,” Haar said of his outfit. Luckily, in music as in life, Haar and his partner in crime are not afraid of change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smart Blondes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ALEXANDER FRANK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FRANK', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/026093b3-f030-5fc4-8572-a6463c679b06', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/026093b3-f030-5fc4-8572-a6463c679b06'}, {'abstract': 'Damon Winter had finished his portrait session with Fabienne Jean in Port-au-Prince when, all of a sudden, the perfect portrait presented itself.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/an-unguarded-portrait-of-haitian-spirit-2/', 'snippet': 'Damon Winter had finished his portrait session with Fabienne Jean in Port-au-Prince when, all of a sudden, the perfect portrait presented itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Damon Winter had finished his photo session with Fabienne Jean, a young dancer in Haiti whose lower right leg was amputated in the aftermath of the 2010 earthquake. Overcoming her understandable reluctance, Ms. Jean removed her prosthetic limb in the middle of the shoot and set it to the side so that Mr. Winter could photograph her legs as they are. He shot two rolls of film with his Hasselblad and wound up with a fine, eminently publishable portrait.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unguarded Portrait of Haitian Spirit', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jean, Fabienne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Damon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca6b9ee6-27d4-5a9e-99ac-ee55e239ba5b', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca6b9ee6-27d4-5a9e-99ac-ee55e239ba5b'}, {'abstract': 'The terms of every member of the House expired at noon on Monday, but the new Congress does not convene until noon on Wednesday. The result is an odd sort of limbo.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/want-to-get-rid-of-congress-its-gone-until-tomorrow-anyway/', 'snippet': 'The terms of every member of the House expired at noon on Monday, but the new Congress does not convene until noon on Wednesday. The result is an odd sort of limbo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anybody who has ever been fed up at Washington and wanted to get rid of the United States Congress, today’s the day to celebrate. It’s gone. Sort of. But better enjoy it fast, because by noon on Wednesday, Congress will be back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Get Rid of Congress? It’s Gone — Until Tomorrow, Anyway', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/786515bf-8e91-505e-944a-f056da693039', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/786515bf-8e91-505e-944a-f056da693039'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel cleared another hurdle in his bid for mayor of Chicago on Tuesday when a Cook County judge agreed with the city’s election board that his name should appear on the ballot.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/judge-rules-emanuels-name-can-appear-on-chicago-ballot/', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel cleared another hurdle in his bid for mayor of Chicago on Tuesday when a Cook County judge agreed with the city’s election board that his name should appear on the ballot.', 'lead_parag