': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c9aeb7-c843-535f-9646-994d1eabf534'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors began laying out the case that they said would show that the personal private physician for Michael Jackson caused his 2009 death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/05jackson.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors began laying out the case that they said would show that the personal private physician for Michael Jackson caused his 2009 death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES \x97 Prosecutors on Tuesday began laying out the case that they say will show the personal private doctor for the pop star Michael Jackson caused his death in 2009 by giving him a powerful anesthetic meant only for surgery and not telling the emergency doctors who eventually arrived that he had done so.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/us/JACKSON-2/JACKSON-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 665, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/us/JACKSON-2/JACKSON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/us/JACKSON-2/JACKSON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Criminal Hearing Begins for Late Pop Star’s Doctor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Criminal Hearing Begins For Late Pop Star’s Doctor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anesthesia and Anesthetics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Conrad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffa7e18d-2aad-5c8c-8673-40a5603c6e3f', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffa7e18d-2aad-5c8c-8673-40a5603c6e3f'}, {'abstract': 'New York Online: Groans from the media and about the media about coverage on Brooklyn; more lists to cap and begin the year; subway shutdowns for the Culver Viaduct project cause consternation; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/more-reasons-to-dislike-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'New York Online: Groans from the media and about the media about coverage on Brooklyn; more lists to cap and begin the year; subway shutdowns for the Culver Viaduct project cause consternation; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eat it up. Time to indulge in some online linkage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Reasons to Dislike Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/19e22e70-3251-59d1-9c16-a80fa061f582', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e22e70-3251-59d1-9c16-a80fa061f582'}, {'abstract': 'Olivier Assayas’s critically acclaimed look at the life of the international terrorist Carlos the Jackal is not just ineligible for the foreign-language film Oscar; it can’t be considered in any category because of its origins as a TV movie.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/an-oscar-shut-out-for-carlos/', 'snippet': 'Olivier Assayas’s critically acclaimed look at the life of the international terrorist Carlos the Jackal is not just ineligible for the foreign-language film Oscar; it can’t be considered in any category because of its origins as a TV movie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of film critics (including ours) pointed to the French director Olivier Assayas’s biopic “Carlos,” a five-and-a-half hour look at the life of the international terrorist Carlos the Jackal, when it came time to compile their 10 Best lists for 2010. The praise extended to the riveting performance of actor Edgar Ramirez (who played Carlos), the script (co-written by Mr. Assayas and Dan Franck) and the direction of Mr. Assayas. Some critics even maintained that “Carlos” was the best foreign film of the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Oscar Shut-Out for ‘Carlos’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assayas, Olivier', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramirez, Edgar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Ilich Ramirez', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sundance Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b05a704-c352-5911-9815-0bdc790de9b7', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b05a704-c352-5911-9815-0bdc790de9b7'}, {'abstract': 'The event, on April 12, is to be hosted by James Taylor and other celebrity guests.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/carnegie-hall-plans-120th-anniversary-gala/', 'snippet': 'The event, on April 12, is to be hosted by James Taylor and other celebrity guests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carnegie Hall announced on Tuesday that it would celebrate its 120th anniversary on April 12 with a gala event to be hosted by James Taylor, along with a sizable lineup of celebrity guests, including Bette Midler, Sting, Steve Martin and Barbara Cook. The event, to highlight “many of the extraordinary musical and cultural events that have taken place on the Hall’s legendary stages over the past 12 decades,” as the institution described it, will also feature members of the Tanglewood Festival Chorus. Proceeds will benefit Carnegie Hall’s artistic and educational programs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie Hall Plans 120th Anniversary Gala', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T21:57:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/48bb7d33-7ee3-53ba-8b2f-6355f549b7ae', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48bb7d33-7ee3-53ba-8b2f-6355f549b7ae'}, {'abstract': 'Millesime, a brasserie in the Carlton Hotel, is devoted to the pleasures of the sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/dining/reviews/05rest.html', 'sni