logs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/d-c-officials-protest-proposed-house-rule/', 'snippet': 'House Republicans plan to restrict the already-limited voting rights of delegates, including Eleanor Holmes Norton, who represents the District of Columbia.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two District of Columbia officials — Mayor Vincent C. Gray and Eleanor Holmes Norton, the district’s delegate in Congress — were on Capitol Hill on Tuesday to protest proposed changes to House rules that would strip Ms. Norton and other delegates of their already-limited voting rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'D.C. Officials Protest Proposed House Rule', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T22:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d10de4c0-ef87-5397-bbdb-fe1a2ed14a19', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d10de4c0-ef87-5397-bbdb-fe1a2ed14a19'}, {'abstract': 'Weeks after Hamas shut down an internationally-financed youth group in Gaza, eight Palestinian students, fed up with “living a nightmare inside a nightmare” in the isolated territory have posted a manifesto on Facebook expressing their rage and frustration.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/young-gazans-rage-at-hamas-and-israel/', 'snippet': 'Weeks after Hamas shut down an internationally-financed youth group in Gaza, eight Palestinian students, fed up with “living a nightmare inside a nightmare” in the isolated territory have posted a manifesto on Facebook expressing their rage and fr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weeks after Hamas shut down an internationally-financed youth group in Gaza, eight Palestinian students, fed up with “living a nightmare inside a nightmare” in the isolated territory have posted a manifesto on Facebook expressing their rage and frustration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Gazans Rage at Hamas and Israel', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T22:23:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b11234ef-d4f5-5cd4-ad36-0acfee610dd8', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b11234ef-d4f5-5cd4-ad36-0acfee610dd8'}, {'abstract': 'In “If I Want to Whistle, I Whistle,” Romania’s official submission for the best foreign language film Oscar, the protagonist is released from jail but has few prospects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/movies/05whistle.html', 'snippet': 'In “If I Want to Whistle, I Whistle,” Romania’s official submission for the best foreign language film Oscar, the protagonist is released from jail but has few prospects.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If I Want to Whistle, I Whistle,” Romania’s official submission for the best foreign-language film Oscar, is a study in confinement. Like many other recent Romanian films — Cristi Puiu’s “Stuff and Dough,” Cristian Mungiu’s “4 Months, 3 Weeks and 2 Days” or Radu Muntean’s “Boogie” — it trails after a young protagonist whose choices are drastically limited and not very promising. Silviu, an 18-year-old inmate at a juvenile prison in a drab rural area, is a few weeks from the end of a four-year sentence, but the idea that his release will bring any kind of freedom seems like a delusion or a cruel joke.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/Whistle/Whistle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/Whistle/Whistle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/Whistle/Whistle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/Whistle/Whistle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/Whistle/Whistle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Freedom Is No Guarantee for a Happily Ever After', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'If I Want to Whistle, I Whistle'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freedom Is No Guarantee for a Happily Ever After', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T22:24:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/303bf5ce-ee30-5ccf-b66a-606fe3647491', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/303bf5ce