 the University of Pennsylvania law school about the relationship between Congress and the Supreme Court.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Arlen Specter, the veteran Republican senator from Pennsylvania who switched parties and then lost in the Democratic primary, will teach law at the University of Pennsylvania, the school announced Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arlen Specter to Teach at  Law School', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T22:26:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/32689f8a-a7a8-56be-b8b5-fdc05f6adead', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32689f8a-a7a8-56be-b8b5-fdc05f6adead'}, {'abstract': 'A new report by Forrester Research predicts tablet sales will pass 24 million in the United States this year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/tablet-sales-to-spike-in-2011-forrester-says/', 'snippet': 'A new report by Forrester Research predicts tablet sales will pass 24 million in the United States this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tablets are coming! The tablets are coming!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tablet Sales to Spike in 2011, Forrester Says', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat