For most performers invited to this year’s Under the Radar festival of international alternative theater, which begins Wednesday, getting to New York is simply a matter of boarding a plane. But for the Belarus Free Theater, a politically engaged troupe used to living and working on the edge in an authoritarian state, the long trip from Minsk was a little more complicated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/jp-company-1/jp-company-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/jp-company-1/jp-company-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/jp-company-1/jp-company-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Escaped From Belarus, Actors Raise Voices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Escaped From Belarus, Actors Raise Voices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belarus Free Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T23:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b97f3158-23d7-5722-899a-a2c2609699ab', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b97f3158-23d7-5722-899a-a2c2609699ab'}, {'abstract': 'One of the keenest debates in dance right now has been about something larger: is ballet itself dead or dying?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/arts/dance/05homans.html', 'snippet': 'One of the keenest debates in dance right now has been about something larger: is ballet itself dead or dying?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each ballet dies with the fall of the curtain. Will it return to real life when next danced? Nobody can be sure. Some dances need occasional periods in cold storage; others — having forever passed their sell-by dates — carry on in some macabre afterlife onstage that feels spectral. For those of us who adored a work in its youth, which alternative is grimmer: never to see it again or to watch it acquire the lines of age and then become one of the dance dead or, worse, undead?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/hoomans/hoomans-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/hoomans/hoomans-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/hoomans/hoomans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/hoomans/hoomans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/hoomans/hoomans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Ballet Dying? Sure, It’s Died Many Times', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Ballet Dying? Sure, It’s Died Many Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Homans, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T23:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb236da-75b3-5b83-a975-a5e474760383', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb236da-75b3-5b83-a975-a5e474760383'}, {'abstract': '“Phil Ochs: There but for Fortune” is Kenneth Bowser’s documentary about that protest singer’s complicated and tragic life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/movies/05phil.html', 'snippet': '“Phil Ochs: There but for Fortune” is Kenneth Bowser’s documentary about that protest singer’s complicated and tragic life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To say that the 1960s folk singer Phil Ochs dreamed big is to understate the huge scope of his ambition. As recalled in Kenneth Bowser’s respectful, nonmaudlin documentary portrait, “Phil Ochs: There but for Fortune,” Ochs moved to New York in the early ’60s intending to be the best songwriter in the country. After meeting Bob Dylan, Ochs was forced to revise his opinion of his own potential to “second best.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/PHIL/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aspiring to Musical Power and Glory', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Phil Ochs: There but for Fortune'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aspiring to Musical Power and Glory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ochs, Phil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T23:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa751e52-b16c-5114-94b7-ded0b40094b2', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa751e52-b16c-5114-94b7-ded0b40094b2'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Lamar Alexander puts Democrats on notice that retribution is “guaranteed” if they put limits on debates.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/a-warning-on-reining-in-filibusters/', 'snippet': 'Senator Lamar Alexander puts Democrats on notice that retribution is “guaranteed” if they put limits on debates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Lamar Alexander derided Democrats’ efforts to rein in the use of filibusters in the Senate as a “brazen power grab” and warned of “guaranteed” retribution when Republicans return to the majority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warning on Reining in Filibusters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-04T23:42:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/21454c74-766e-5958-9f63-60c59393da1f', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21454c74-766e-5958-9f63-60c59393da1f'}, {'abstract': 'It’s usual for the House to tweak rules with each new session. But John Boehner has made alterations that members will vote on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/politics/05rules.html', 'snippet': 'It’s usual for the House to tweak rules with each new session. But John Boehner has made alterations that members will vote on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Here is how most people think laws get made in this town: A member of Congress introduces a bill, his colleagues express great love/outrage/urgency about the bill in front of C-Span, and members decide to pass or defeat it in a roll-call vote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress to Return With G.O.P. Vowing to Alter Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New House Speaker Enters, Bringing Rewritten Rulebook With Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value