'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Testing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707610af-f230-59f9-ab44-e5f66d2ddf90', 'word_count': 1448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707610af-f230-59f9-ab44-e5f66d2ddf90'}, {'abstract': 'The 15th edition of the dating series “The Bachelor” made its debut on Monday night, lifting ABC to second place in the prime-time ratings among the major broadcast networks', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/arts/television/05arts-THEBACHELORR_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The 15th edition of the dating series “The Bachelor” made its debut on Monday night, lifting ABC to second place in the prime-time ratings among the major broadcast networks', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 15th edition of the dating series “The Bachelor” made its debut on Monday night, lifting ABC to second place in the prime-time ratings among the major broadcast networks. According to Nielsen’s estimates, 9 million viewers tuned in to that reality show’s two-hour premiere, down slightly from the 9.5 million who watched the first installment of the series last January. CBS led the night over all with new episodes of its comedy lineup, including “Two and a Half Men” (15.3 million) and “Mike & Molly” (12.6 million) in the 9 p.m. hour, after “How I Met Your Mother” (10.4 million) and “Rules of Engagement” (9.9 million) at 8 and 8:30. CBS’s “Hawaii Five-0” won the 10 p.m. hour with 10.8 million viewers, edging ahead of ABC’s “Castle” (9.6 million). Fox was third with reruns of “House” (4.8 million) and “Lie to Me” (3.9 million), while NBC ranked fourth, earning an average of 2.8 million viewers from 9 to 11 for a “Where Are They Now?” retrospective edition of “The Biggest Loser” following a repeat of “Chuck” (2.5 million).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Bachelor’ Returns', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Bachelor’ Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1a39640-2839-5e6e-944f-90b05da9d7a8', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1a39640-2839-5e6e-944f-90b05da9d7a8'}, {'abstract': 'The morning after taping his first “Daily Show” of the new year, Jon Stewart said on Tuesday that one of his executive producers, Josh Lieb, was leaving that satiric newscast to write a sitcom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/arts/television/05arts-DAILYSHOWISL_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The morning after taping his first “Daily Show” of the new year, Jon Stewart said on Tuesday that one of his executive producers, Josh Lieb, was leaving that satiric newscast to write a sitcom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The morning after taping his first “Daily Show” of the new year, Jon Stewart said on Tuesday that one of his executive producers, Josh Lieb, was leaving that satiric newscast to write a sitcom for Warner Brothers and NBC. At the same time, Mr. Stewart, who along with Rory Albanese is also an executive producer of the show, announced a restructuring. He named three longtime staff members, Steve Bodow, Jennifer Flanz and Jim Margolis, co-executive producers; named Pam DePace a supervising producer; and promoted Tim Carvell to head writer. He did not elaborate on the reasons for the changes. Mr. Lieb had been an executive producer of “The Daily Show” for two years, and a co-executive producer for three years prior.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Daily Show’ Is Losing an Executive Producer', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Daily Show’ Is Losing An Executive Producer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieb, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce87e97-7b0d-56a8-ab50-cbd9f595877d', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce87e97-7b0d-56a8-ab50-cbd9f595877d'}, {'abstract': 'House Republican leaders are scaling back a goal to cut $100 billion from domestic spending, aides say, because the fiscal year will be nearly half over before the cuts could become law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/politics/05fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'House Republican leaders are scaling back a goal to cut $100 billion from domestic spending, aides say, because the fiscal year will be nearly half over before the cuts could become law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Many people knowledgeable about the federal budget said House Republicans could not keep their campaign promise to cut $100 billion from domestic spending in a single year. Now it appears that Republicans agree.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/us/jp-FISCAL/jp-FISCAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Lower Goal for Cuts to Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Lower Goal For Cuts To Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65507d52-68fc-57c0-b8d7-73fa9c36f930', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65507d52-68fc-57c0-b8d7-73fa9c36f930'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s ascent may prove its biggest success so far in an effort to project its heft across a region long suspicious of it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/world/middleeast/05turkey.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s ascent may prove its biggest success so far in an effort to project its heft across a region long suspicious of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZAKHO, Iraq \x97 A Turkey as resurgent as at any time since its Ottoman glory is projecting influence through a turbulent Iraq, from the boomtowns of the north to the oil fields near southernmost Basra, in a show of power that illustrates its growing heft across an Arab world long suspicious of it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/world/05turkey_337-395/JP-TURKEY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/world/05turkey_337-395/JP-TURKEY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/world/05turkey_337-395/JP-TURKEY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Resurgent Turkey Flexes Its Muscles Around Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Resurgent Turkey Builds Influence Across Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb6540a9-0076-52df-a6ab-d5c29bee4ccd', 'word_count': 1885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb6540a9-0076-52df-a6ab-d5c29bee4ccd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Simon imported and sold chateau wines from Bordeaux and estate wines from Burgundy, the Rhone and the Loire regions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/business/05simon.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Simon imported and sold chateau wines from Bordeaux and estate wines from Burgundy, the Rhone and the Loire regions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ab Simon, who as the longtime chairman of the Seagram Chateau & Estate Wines Company was a commanding figure in the American wine trade and a leading importer of fine Bordeaux to the United States, died on Saturday at his home in Manhattan. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/05simon/05simon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/05simon/05simon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/05simon/05simon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ab Simon, Chairman of Seagram Wine Unit, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ab Simon, 88, Is Dead;\nLed Seagram’s Wine Unit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T00:52:44+0000', '