al of self-glorification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/opinion/05wed1.html', 'snippet': 'Americans who hoped to observe the Republican plan to revive the economy in action will have to wait until party leaders finish their insider ritual of self-glorification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A theatrical production of unusual pomposity will open on Wednesday when Republicans assume control of the House for the 112th Congress. A rule will be passed requiring that every bill cite its basis in the Constitution. A bill will be introduced to repeal the health care law. On Thursday, the Constitution will be read aloud in the House chamber. And in one particularly self-important flourish, the new speaker, John Boehner, arranged to have his office staff “sworn in” on Tuesday by the chief justice of the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pomp, and Little Circumstance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pomp, and Little Circumstance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T02:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/52ced19b-006f-5fb7-b0ce-df3fef5375df', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52ced19b-006f-5fb7-b0ce-df3fef5375df'}, {'abstract': 'The assassination of Salman Taseer, the governor of Pakistan’s Punjab province, is a tragedy for all who understand that just and stable societies need honest debate and full respect for minorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/opinion/05wed2.html', 'snippet': 'The assassination of Salman Taseer, the governor of Pakistan’s Punjab province, is a tragedy for all who understand that just and stable societies need honest debate and full respect for minorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some twisted person has created a Facebook page in support of Malik Mumtaz Hussain Qadri, the bodyguard accused of assassinating Salman Taseer, the governor of Pakistan’s Punjab province. Mr. Taseer was a brave man who had called for the repeal of Pakistan’s outrageous anti-blasphemy law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Brave Man Killed', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Brave Man Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taseer, Salman', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T02:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ccb654-f839-5e2c-91c0-d6d0334cd8e8', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ccb654-f839-5e2c-91c0-d6d0334cd8e8'}, {'abstract': 'After an injury to her upper arm, a legal battle and bedbugs, Hortense Bermúdez says she is just getting by financially, but considers herself lucky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/nyregion/05neediest.html', 'snippet': 'After an injury to her upper arm, a legal battle and bedbugs, Hortense Bermúdez says she is just getting by financially, but considers herself lucky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The walls of Hortense Bermúdez’s apartment are lined with her own paintings, many with an autobiographical aspect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First, Accident. Then the Landlord. Finally, Bedbugs.', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First, Accident. Then the Landlord. Finally, Bedbugs.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bedbugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federation of Protestant Welfare Agencies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garment District (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T02:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret W. Ho', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Ho', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/243389e5-409b-58d7-91a7-22af974d04a5', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/243389e5-409b-58d7-91a7-22af974d04a5'}, {'abstract': 'It is dismaying to hear Justice Antonin Scalia espouse the notion that the promise of equal protection in the Constitution does not extend to protecting women against sex discrimination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/opinion/05wed3.html', 'snippet': 'It is dismaying to hear Justice Antonin Scalia espouse the notion that the promise of equal protection in the Constitution does not extend to protecting women against sex discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Justice Antonin Scalia has a knack for drawing unflattering light to himself and the Supreme Court. Recall, for example, when he refused to recuse himself from a case involving the energy task force run by Dick Cheney, his friend and duck-hunting companion, when Mr. Cheney was vice president. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There He Goes Again', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There He Goes Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T02:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d32fc1b0-b565-5444-a077-6b6d0c86c65d', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d32fc1b0-b565-5444-a077-6b6d0c86c65d'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund helped an Iraqi refugee when he fell behind on rent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/opinion/05wed4.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund helped an Iraqi refugee when he fell behind on rent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manaf Hashim did not know who was threatening to kill him in the note left on the front door of his Baghdad home or in a message left on his cellphone two days later. He suspected he was being targeted because his fiancée, Farah, was Sunni, and he was Shia. He knew only that it was best to heed such warnings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New, Safer Life', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New, Safer Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T02:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0935aea5-284c-5a91-b460-2a96e829d418', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0935aea5-284c-5a91-b460-2a96e829d418'}, {'abstract': 'A stricken 3-month-old boy whose medical treatment was delayed last week by unplowed streets in Queens died.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/queensboydeath/', 'snippet': 'A stricken 3-month-old boy whose medical treatment was delayed last week by unplowed streets in Queens died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A stricken 3-month-old boy whose medical treatment was 