permits. Protesters said the law was part of a broader crackdown on free speech in Iraq’s semiautonomous Kurdistan region. In the past six months, the government has sued at least 60 writers or media organizations for publishing work critical of the government, according to the Kurdistan Journalists’ Syndicate. Aso Karim, a lawmaker with the Kurdistan Democratic Party, said the restrictions were necessary because “Iraq is not politically stable.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Free Speech Protests in Kurdistan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Mideast', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Free Speech Protests in Kurdistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:06:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Namo Abdulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Namo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abdulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c58902-020b-51ed-ba64-29c2959a36a0', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c58902-020b-51ed-ba64-29c2959a36a0'}, {'abstract': 'Donated Christmas trees, bundled and secured to the bottom of a lake, become covered with algae, which attract aquatic insects, fish and, ultimately, fishermen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/05trees.html', 'snippet': 'Donated Christmas tre