States prison for spying for Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/world/middleeast/05briefs-spy.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Tuesday read aloud in Parliament a letter asking President Obama for clemency for Jonathan Jay Pollard, left, the American serving a life term in a United States prison for spying for Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Tuesday read aloud in Parliament a letter asking President Obama for clemency for Jonathan Jay Pollard, left, the American serving a life term in a United States prison for spying for Israel. The letter, which was sent this week, constitutes the first formal and public Israeli appeal for Mr. Pollard’s release. “Even though Israel was in no way directing its intelligence efforts against the United States,” Mr. Netanyahu wrote, “its actions were wrong and wholly unacceptable.” After 25 years in prison, he added, Mr. Pollard “has reportedly served longer in prison than any person convicted of similar crimes, and longer than the period requested by the prosecutors at the time of his plea bargain agreement.” Obama administration officials recently indicated that Mr. Pollard’s release was unlikely. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: An Appeal for a Spy’s Release', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Mideast', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: An Appeal for a Spy’s Release', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollard, Jonathan J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:27:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/92d3767d-1aa8-5426-b6c2-1f6201eddcf2', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92d3767d-1aa8-5426-b6c2-1f6201eddcf2'}, {'abstract': 'The Scottish singer was best known for his songs “Stuck in the Middle With You” and “Baker Street.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/arts/music/05rafferty.html', 'snippet': 'The Scottish singer was best known for his songs “Stuck in the Middle With You” and “Baker Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gerry Rafferty, a Scottish singer and songwriter who combined a gift for melody, a distinctive voice and a fatalistic worldview to produce 1970s hits like “Stuck in the Middle With You” and “Baker Street,” died Tuesday in Dorset, England. He was 63.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/RAFFERTY-obit/RAFFERTY-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/RAFFERTY-obit/RAFFERTY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/RAFFERTY-obit/RAFFERTY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gerry Rafferty, Songwriter, Dies at 63', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gerry Rafferty, Songwriter, Dies at 63', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/419a9c91-925a-59cf-b3b2-9e02d303eb9c', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/419a9c91-925a-59cf-b3b2-9e02d303eb9c'}, {'abstract': 'Thieves working for at least six months dug a tunnel underneath a bank in Buenos Aires and robbed 143 safety deposit boxes containing an estimated $6.5 million during the New Year’s weekend, a bank official and prosecutor said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/world/americas/05briefs-bank.html', 'snippet': 'Thieves working for at least six months dug a tunnel underneath a bank in Buenos Aires and robbed 143 safety deposit boxes containing an estimated $6.5 million during the New Year’s weekend, a bank official and prosecutor said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Thieves working for at least six months dug a tunnel underneath a bank in Buenos Aires and robbed 143 safety deposit boxes containing an estimated $6.5 million during New Year’s weekend, a bank official and prosecutor said. At least three robbers entered Banco de la Provincia in the Belgrano neighborhood on Dec. 31 and left on Jan. 3 at 7 a.m., three hours before the bank reopened after New Year, Martín Niklison, a prosecutor, said on television on Monday. The thieves rented a former dentist’s office nearly 100 feet from the bank and then dug a tunnel that ran about 16 feet underground before reaching the basement of the bank. The bank’s alarm sounded at least twice during the robbery but the police, lacking keys to the bank, left after not seeing anything from outside the bank, he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Thieves Tunneled Into Bank', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: Thieves Tunneled Into Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc2ec526-b3c7-5cb0-808c-3ffccbd39c61', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc2ec526-b3c7-5cb0-808c-3ffccbd39c61'}, {'abstract': 'A young Miami Beach arms dealer who admitted to defrauding the Pentagon in a munitions contract was sentenced on Monday to four years in federal prison, bringing a case that embarrassed the Pentagon closer to its end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/world/asia/05briefs-dealer.html', 'snippet': 'A young Miami Beach arms dealer who admitted to defrauding the Pentagon in a munitions contract was sentenced on Monday to four years in federal prison, bringing a case that embarrassed the Pentagon closer to its end.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A young Miami Beach arms dealer who admitted to defrauding the Pentagon in a munitions contract was sentenced on Monday to four years in federal prison, bringing a case that embarrassed the Pentagon closer to its end. The dealer, Efraim Diveroli, 25, was president of AEY Inc., a fledgling company that surprised industry insiders in 2007 when the United States Army awarded it a $300 million contract to supply ordnance to Afghan security forces. Mr. Diveroli pleaded guilty to plotting to ship prohibited Chinese ammunition to the war. Four men have been convicted in the scheme. Mr. Diveroli is awaiting sentencing for a separate charge of possessing a firearm while on bail. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Arms Dealer Sentenced for Scheme to Ship Prohibited Chinese Ammunition', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Arms Dealer Sentenced for Scheme To Ship Prohibited Chinese Ammunition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diveroli, Efraim E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e324b9a8-2fe5-5f63-aa0c-cd99927a6317', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e324b9a8-2fe5-5f63-aa0c-cd99927a6317'}, {'abstract': 'The British-born actress had an early start in films before being cast in the Broadway musical at 21.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/theater/05haworth.html', 'snippet': 'The British-born actress had an early start in films before being cast in the Broadway musical at 21.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jill Haworth, a British-born film ingénue in the 1960s who made her only Broadway appearance as the original Sally Bowles in “Cabaret,” died Monday at her home in Manhattan. She was 65.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/HAWORTH-obit/HAWORTH-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/HAWORTH-obit/HAWORTH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/arts/HAWORTH-obit/HAWORTH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jill Haworth, Original Sally in ‘Cabaret,’ Dies at 65', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jill Haworth, Original Sally In ‘Cabaret,’ Dies at 65', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef465675-c72a-5b88-96f3-a42e34180482', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef465675-c72a-5b88-96f3-a42e34180482'}, {'abstract': 'A three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit asked the California Supreme Court for guidance on the issue of standing in a challenge to Proposition 8.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/05brfs-JUDGESASKFOR_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit asked the California Supreme Court for guidance on the issue of standing in a challenge to Proposition 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, in San Francisco, asked the California Supreme Court for guidance on Tuesday on the issue of standing in a federal challenge to Proposition 8, the state’s voter-approved ban on same-sex marriage. The order, asking for clarification of California law, comes after former Gov. Arnold Schwarzenegger and his successor, Gov. Jerry Brown, refused to defend the proposition in court. That has left the defense primarily to conservative legal groups and proponents of the measure. In August, a federal district judge ruled Proposition 8 to be unconstitutional, but that ruling was appealed to the Ninth Circuit panel. Also Tuesday, the panel denied Imperial County, in Southern California, the right to intervene on the behalf of Proposition 8. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Judges Ask for Clarity on Same-Sex Marriage Measure', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Judges Ask for Clarity On Same-Sex Marriage Measure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a70bca-c250-5248-a8a2-c422fde89e3c', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a70bca-c250-5248-a8a2-c422fde89e3c'}, {'abstract': 'The youngest son of the former shah of Iran was found dead Tuesday in his Boston apartment, according to his brother’s Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/05brfs-SHAHSSONFOUN_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The youngest son of the former shah of Iran was found dead Tuesday in his Boston apartment, according to his brother’s Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The youngest son of the former shah of Iran was found dead Tuesday in his Boston apartment, according to his brother’s Web site. Prince Alireza Pahlavi “struggled for years to overcome his sorrow” and “in his Boston residence, took his own life, plunging his family and friends into great sorrow,” said a note on the Web site of his brother Reza Pahlavi. The prince, 44, died of a self-inflicted gunshot wound, a spokesman for the Suffolk County District Attorney’s office said. His father, Shah Mohammad Reza Pahlavi, ruled Iran from 1941 until he was overthrown in 1979; he died in Egypt in 1980. Alireza Pahlavi had studied at Harvard Divinity School.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Shah’s Son Found Dead', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Shah’s Son Found Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pahlevi, Mohammed Riza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Zezima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zezima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc80876c-7346-555f-8525-e1a9b4740b84', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc80876c-7346-555f-8525-e1a9b4740b84'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel cleared another hurdle in his bid for mayor of Chicago on Tuesday when a Cook County judge agreed with the city’s election board that his name should appear on the ballot this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/us/05brfs-ANOTHERRULIN_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel cleared another hurdle in his bid for mayor of Chicago on Tuesday when a Cook County judge agreed with the city’s election board that his name should appear on the ballot this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rahm Emanuel cleared another hurdle in his bid for mayor of Chicago on Tuesday when a Cook County judge agreed with the city’s election board that his name should appear on the ballot this year. The judge, Mark J. Ballard, upheld the board’s decision that Mr. Emanuel met the one-year residency requirement for mayoral candidates. Several objectors have said that Mr. Emanuel gave up his residency when he worked in Washington as President Obama’s chief of staff until last fall. Opponents plan to appeal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Another Ruling Favors Emanuel in Chicago Residency Dispute', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Another Ruling Favors Ex-Obama Aide in Residency Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By EMMA GRAVES FITZSIMMONS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'Graves', 'lastname': 'FITZSIMMONS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cebf34d7-50e3-52e6-8275-152629e68109', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cebf34d7-50e3-52e6-8275-152629e68109'}, {'abstract': 'In a year of higher prices, there are still plenty of ways to find bargains if you know where to look.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/travel/09pracsave.html', 'snippet': 'In a year of higher prices, there are still plenty of ways to find bargains if you know where to look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARGAIN hunters will need to be craftier when booking a trip if they want to get the best prices this year. It’s no secret that airfares are up and added fees for everything from checked bags to exit-row seats are pushing the cost of flying higher. On top of that, hotel bargains are expected to be harder to come by as business travelers begin to return, diminishing the need for hotels to discount rooms in major cities. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Practical/Practical-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Practical/Practical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Practical/Practical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '11 Tricks to Cutting Travel Costs in 2011', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Cut Travel Costs in a Year of Higher Prices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T03:55:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2886687-1535-57c1-b65f-4cb540fd1de1', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2886687-1535-57c1-b65f-4cb540fd1de1'}, {'abstract': 'The Frugal Traveler compiles a user’s guide to all of those low-cost bus lines in the Northeast.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/a-guide-to-cheap-buses-including-how-to-score-1-tickets/', 'snippet': 'The Frugal Traveler compiles a user’s guide to all of those low-cost bus lines in the Northeast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m an ideal customer for all of those low-cost bus lines that run from New York to Boston\xa0and Washington and Philadelphia: I don’t own a car. I’m cheapskate by both nature and by trade. And I have good reasons to visit two of the three cities from my home in New York — my parents live outside Boston and my brother’s family lives outside Washington. If a brain injury transformed me into a Phillies fan, I’d have the trifecta.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to Cheap Buses (Including How to Score $1 Tickets)', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greyhound Lines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T04:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d54bc6f-f0c3-5a55-82c4-6a81776ca00c', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d54bc6f-f0c3-5a55-82c4-6a81776ca00c'}, {'abstract': 'Hortense Bermúdez’s paintings are often autobiographical, like the one of a woman sleeping, unaware of the insect invaders in her apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/04/nyregion/20100105neediestA.html', 'snippet': 'Hortense Bermúdez’s paintings are often autobiographical, like the one of a woman sleeping, unaware of the insect invaders in her apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hortense Bermúdez’s paintings are often autobiographical, like the one of a woman sleeping, unaware of the insect invaders in her apartment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty