': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f465fb-2a0f-5206-897c-b3385f171779', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f465fb-2a0f-5206-897c-b3385f171779'}, {'abstract': 'Wilson Chandler had 31 points and Amar’e Stoudemire and Raymond Felton added 28 each as the Knicks improved to 20-14 at the expense of the Spurs, who have the league’s best record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/sports/basketball/05knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Wilson Chandler had 31 points and Amar’e Stoudemire and Raymond Felton added 28 each as the Knicks improved to 20-14 at the expense of the Spurs, who have the league’s best record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Duncan wiggled and launched his reliable bank shot through the net. Landry Fields shook free from Manu Ginobili and dunked off a lob from Amar’e Stoudemire. The first shots of the game began a night of rapid-fire baskets, defense forgotten and offense applauded Tuesday at Madison Square Garden. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/sports/05knicks2_337-395/05knicks2_337-395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Win a Shootout Against a Top Team', 'kicker': 'Knicks 128, Spurs 115', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks Win A Shootout Against A Top Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T04:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33fcddda-8e43-5c89-bea3-99d717edbd97', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33fcddda-8e43-5c89-bea3-99d717edbd97'}, {'abstract': 'The Indiana governor was President George W. Bush’s first budget director, and he has accepted stimulus money while lambasting the program. If he runs for president, both subjects deserve more attention.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/04/mitch-danielss-fiscal-blemishes/', 'snippet': 'The Indiana governor was President George W. Bush’s first budget director, and he has accepted stimulus money while lambasting the program. If he runs for president, both subjects deserve more attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitch Daniels‘s record as a fiscal conservative — the subject of my column this week — has at least two blemishes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitch Daniels’s Fiscal Blemishes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Mitchell E Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T04:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed3ccc4-f040-5d18-aebe-3fcadf6673ae', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed3ccc4-f040-5d18-aebe-3fcadf6673ae'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration will revise a Medicare regulation to delete references to end-of-life planning as part of the annual examinations covered under the new health care law, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/health/policy/05health.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration will revise a Medicare regulation to delete references to end-of-life planning as part of the annual examinations covered under the new health care law, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The Obama administration, reversing course, will revise a Medicare regulation to delete references to end-of-life planning as part of the annual physical examinations covered under the new health care law, administration officials said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Alters Rule on Paying for End-of-Life Planning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Reversal For Medicare On Planning For Life’s End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T04:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename