s dismissed on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two men who decided to fight charges against them for playing chess in a park have had the charges dismissed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrested Chess Players Walk Free', 'kicker': 'Gambit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'INWOOD HILL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T05:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c30240-216e-58e8-8ac7-f9ae98bc02f8', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c30240-216e-58e8-8ac7-f9ae98bc02f8'}, {'abstract': 'Shawne Merriman’s new year is off to a good start. On Saturday, Merriman, the Buffalo Bills’ star linebacker, signed a two-year contract extension.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/sports/football/05sportsbriefs-Merriman.html', 'snippet': 'Shawne Merriman’s new year is off to a good start. On Saturday, Merriman, the Buffalo Bills’ star linebacker, signed a two-year contract extension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shawne Merriman’s new year is off to a good start. On Saturday, Merriman, the Buffalo Bills’ star linebacker, signed a two-year contract extension reportedly worth up to $9 million. On Tuesday, a federal judge in Maryland awarded him $3.8 million to settle a suit he filed against the former Duke basketball players Christian Laettner and Brian Davis. Merriman was trying to recoup the $3 mil