e-d930023571f9', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b98aafb9-52b9-5327-8dae-d930023571f9'}, {'abstract': 'American International Group, the insurer selling many of its assets to pay back its government bailout, told the S.E.C. in November that it had received an unsolicited $3 billion bid for its Taiwan unit, Nan Shan — well above the division’s going price last summer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/a-i-g-received-3-billion-bid-for-taiwan-unit/', 'snippet': 'American International Group, the insurer selling many of its assets to pay back its government bailout, told the S.E.C. in November that it had received an unsolicited $3 billion bid for its Taiwan unit, Nan Shan — well above the division’s going...', 'lead_paragraph': 'American International Group, the insurance giant selling assets to pay back its government bailout, told the Securities and Exchange Commission in November that it had received an unsolicited $3 billion bid for its Taiwan unit, Nan Shan Life Insurance — an offer well above the division’s going price last summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.I.G. Received $3 Billion Bid for Taiwan Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T14:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7176fc73-47c8-5bdc-b267-bdfd1bb71f54', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7176fc73-47c8-5bdc-b267-bdfd1bb71f54'}, {'abstract': 'Last year’s best supporting actress will announce the Oscar nominations later this month, plus tidbits on the industry repercussions of “Black Swan” and the story behind Matt Damon’s abs double.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/an-early-wake-up-call-for-monique/', 'snippet': 'Last year’s best supporting actress will announce the Oscar nominations later this month, plus tidbits on the industry repercussions of “Black Swan” and the story behind Matt Damon’s abs double.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The job of announcing the Oscar nominees very, very early on the morning of Jan. 25 will fall to Mo’Nique, the Academy has announced. Last year’s best-supporting-actress winner, Mo’Nique will share the duties of naming names in 10 of 24 categories with the Academy’s president, Tom Sherak. (Maybe he’ll warm up with an appearance on her BET talk show? The Bagger would like to see him do a little something with Waka Flocka Flame.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Early Wake-Up Call for Mo’Nique', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coen, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Natalie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T14:44:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d7cfe5-d6c6-5c6e-a101-401060ec496a', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d7cfe5-d6c6-5c6e-a101-401060ec496a'}, {'abstract': 'The White House press secretary, Robert Gibbs, will leave in early February to become an outside political adviser to the president and his 2012 re-election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/gibbs-to-leave-as-white-house-press-secretary/', 'snippet': 'The White House press secretary, Robert Gibbs, will leave in early February to become an outside political adviser to the president and his 2012 re-election campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:30 a.m. | Updated Robert Gibbs, the White House press secretary and close confidante to President Obama, said Wednesday that he was stepping down to become an outside political adviser to the president and his re-election campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gibbs to Leave as White House Press Secretary', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Jay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbs, Robert L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T14:56:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f2469a-6a7d-551e-8825-2bef589e90c7', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f2469a-6a7d-551e-8825-2bef589e90c7'}, {'abstract': 'Between 2002 and 2009, 30 teams had increases of at least five wins from one season to the next. Unfortunately, for the most part, these teams were unable to carry their success into the next season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/regression-is-probable-for-chiefs-bucs-and-rams/', 'snippet': 'Between 2002 and 2009, 30 teams had increases of at least five wins from one season to the next. Unfortunately, for the most part, these teams were unable to carry their success into the next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luis DeLoureiro operates NFLStatAnalysis.net and is a contributor to the Cold Hard Football Facts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regression Is Probable for Chiefs, Bucs and Rams', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Buccaneers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T15:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luis DeLoureiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeLoureiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/284eaab2-cbae-5005-88e3-b17d3d214754', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/284eaab2-cbae-5005-88e3-b17d3d214754'}, {'abstract': 'A volatile financial market characterised by rapid price changes.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/wolf-market/', 'snippet': 'A volatile financial market characterised by rapid price changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A volatile financial market characterised by rapid price changes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolf Market', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T15:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d0befd-9bcb-5ba1-8e89-d7ab9ec654bd', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d0befd-9bcb-5ba1-8e89-d7ab9ec654bd'}, {'abstract': 'The last time there weren’t enough musical revivals to fill the four slots in the Tony Awards category was 2006.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/in-shallow-broadway-season-few-revivals/', 'snippet': 'The last time there weren’t enough musical revivals to fill the four slots in the Tony Awards category was 2006.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looks more and more likely that only two musical revivals will open on Broadway this season – “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying” and “Anything Goes” – which would leave two slots empty in the category of best revival of a musical at the 2011 Tony Awards in June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anyone Have a  Revival Handy? There Could Be a Tony in It for You', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davenport, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARENA STAGE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T15:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f5f4f1d-4cbf-52ce-8037-f6ef29a39096', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f5f4f1d-4cbf-52ce-8037-f6ef29a39096'}, {'abstract': 'Food prices are expected to remain high this year, bringing them close to the crisis levels that provoked shortages and riots in poor countries three years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/business/global/06food.html', 'snippet': 'Food prices are expected to remain high this year, bringing them close to the crisis levels that provoked shortages and riots in poor countries three years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'World food prices continued to rise sharply in December, bringing them close to the crisis levels that provoked shortages and riots in poor countries three years ago, according to newly released United Nations data. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/business/6FOOD/6FOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Data Notes Sharp Rise in World Food Prices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Notes Sharp Rise in World Food Prices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T15:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/108653c2-3632-5684-84e8-ea983fd145ef', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/108653c2-3632-5684-84e8-ea983fd145ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Internet promises a kind of immortality. What if your last tweet is the one that defines you for all time?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/magazine/09Immortality-t.html', 'snippet': 'The Internet promises a kind of immortality. What if your last tweet is the one that defines you for all time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suppose that just after you finish reading this article, you keel over, dead. Perhaps you’re ready for such an eventuality, in that you have prepared a will or made some sort of arrangement for the fate of the worldly goods you leave behind: financial assets, personal effects, belongings likely to have sentimental value to others and artifacts of your life like photographs, journals, letters. Even if you haven’t made such arrangements, all of this will get sorted one way or another, maybe in line with what you would have wanted, and maybe not.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09cyberspace_3/09cyberspace_3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09cyberspace_3/09cyberspace_3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09cyberspace_3/09cyberspace_3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyberspace When You’re Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THINGS TO\nDO IN\nCYBERSPACE\nWHEN YOU’RE\nDEAD', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T15:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecb55eba-317b-5b06-90b2-b0b8b7c744c5', 'word_count': 7897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecb55eba-317b-5b06-90b2-b0b8b7c744c5'}, {'abstract': 'Michael M. Kaiser plans to visit five cities.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/head-of-kennedy-center-to-give-management-seminars-in-africa/', 'snippet': 'Michael M. Kaiser plans to visit five cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael M. Kaiser, the president of the Kennedy Center, who doubles as an arts management guru, is taking his show on the road next month – to Africa. Over a week, he will give arts management seminars in five cities: Lagos, Nigeria; Kampala, Uganda; Nairobi, Kenya; Zanzibar, Tanzania; and Harare, Zimbabwe. The one-day sessions will be hosted by local arts leaders who have taken part in the Kennedy Center’s Summer International Fellowship program for arts managers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia