lude end-of-life planning as part of the annual physical examinations covered by Medicare under the new health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times reports today that doctors will not be reimbursed by Medicare for discussions about end-of-life care. The original proposal, included in early versions of the health care law, was criticized by conservatives who believed it would lead to the creation of “death panels.” Robert Pear writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Backs Away From End-of-Life Discussions', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T16:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4da99c9-87b2-54e5-a2f5-204de3ff0358', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4da99c9-87b2-54e5-a2f5-204de3ff0358'}, {'abstract': 'When a meeting between a coach and an athletic director follow three turmoil-ridden seasons, an N.C.A.A. probation and the worst bowl loss in team history, someone is getting fired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/sports/ncaafootball/06leading.html', 'snippet': 'When a meeting between a coach and an athletic director follow three turmoil-ridden seasons, an N.C.A.A. probation and the worst bowl loss in team history, someone is getting fired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today is one of those days when the sports news should be read while sitting down. That’s because it is necessary to pause after nearly every story and say, “Huh?” a few times before you go back and read it again. Also, it helps to have a free hand to slap your forehead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/06michigan/06michigan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/06michigan/06michigan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/06michigan/06michigan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/06michigan/06michigan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/06michigan/06michigan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mess at Michigan Drags On', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Michigan Mess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Rich (1963- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Marvin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cable, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T16:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname