'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a20b74c-d00a-591b-ad17-927f11f87f6b', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a20b74c-d00a-591b-ad17-927f11f87f6b'}, {'abstract': 'The visiting teams seem to be in an unusually strong position heading into wild-card weekend.  But things will get tougher  the following week, when the conference’s top seeds come into play.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/n-f-l-playoff-odds-and-oddities-home-and-away/', 'snippet': 'The visiting teams seem to be in an unusually strong position heading into wild-card weekend.  But things will get tougher  the following week, when the conference’s top seeds come into play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two visiting teams (the Saints and the Ravens) are favored in this weekend’s wild-card games, and it would not be stunning if the Jets (at Indianapolis) and the Packers (at Philadelphia) also won on the road in the first round. But things will get tougher for the road teams the following weekend, when the conference’s top seeds come into play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Playoff Odds and Oddities, Home and Away', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T17:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7bd72df-122a-5695-9bb9-08dba48fabe1', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7bd72df-122a-5695