e': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bb54621-71c2-5da6-b0e3-e780d79dc2e8', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bb54621-71c2-5da6-b0e3-e780d79dc2e8'}, {'abstract': 'He is to undergo a procedure to ease pain in his lower back.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/surgery-to-force-ozawa-to-miss-concerts/', 'snippet': 'He is to undergo a procedure to ease pain in his lower back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conductor Seiji Ozawa, who spent much of last year recovering from esophageal cancer and a back ailment, will miss three concerts in Japan at the end of the month because of surgery to ease pain in his lower back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surgery to Force Ozawa to Miss Concerts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ozawa, Seiji', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T17:46:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed1d3ae-0c2e-5b51-a603-d15db05e4416', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed1d3ae-0c2e-5b51-a603-d15db05e4416'}, {'abstract': 'On a recent Saturday night, employees outnumbered the patrons at this new nightspot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/fashion/06boite.html', 'snippet': 'On a recent Saturday night, employees outnumbered the patrons at this new nightspot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNDER cover of night and zebra-print miniskirts, the rowdy expanse of West 21st Street, between Broadway and the Avenue of the Americas, is Chelsea’s reigning club row. On weekends, there are endless lines of sequin-topped and high-heeled women, snaking toward thudding clubs like Crimson, Taj and Slate. At the westernmost edge is Studio XXI, a second-floor club that opened in December in the small space formerly occupied by Citrine. Those who understand roman numerals call it Studio 21. But others insist the club’s name is pronounced “Ess-Ex-Ex-Eye,” as in “sexy.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06boite_1/Z-BOITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06boite_1/Z-BOITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06boite_1/Z-BOITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Studio XXI', 'kicker': 'Boîte', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Studio XXI: Chelsea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T17:50:32+0000', 'document_type': '