r, Raj Rajaratnam.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/judge-allows-wiretaps-in-another-galleon-case/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors chalked up a second victory on the use of wiretaps, which have already been allowed in the case against the Galleon Group’s founder, Raj Rajaratnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge ruled Wednesday that federal prosecutors could use wiretapped telephone conversations as evidence against six defendants in the insider trading case involving the Galleon Group. The case has spawned a wide-ranging government investigation of suspected insider trading in the hedge fund industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Allows Wiretaps Against Defendants in Galleon Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiesi, Danielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutillo, Arthur J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goffer, Zvi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Richard J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0df09ce4-de8a-5dd8-bd31-01ff9ba685e3', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0df09ce4-de8a-5dd8-bd31-01ff9ba685e3'}, {'abstract': 'A text of Representative John A. Boehner’s first remarks as House speaker on Wednesday, as released by his office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/us/politics/06cong-text.html', 'snippet': 'A text of Representative John A. Boehner’s first remarks as House speaker on Wednesday, as released by his office.', 'lead_paragraph': "Following is a text of the speech by Representative John A. Boehner, Republican of Ohio, given after he was elected House Speaker on Wednesday, as released by Mr. Boehner's office: ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner’s First Remarks as House Speaker', 'kicker': 'Text', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce5ce137-eba6-58f6-bf32-3c7217f284bf', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5ce137-eba6-58f6-bf32-3c7217f284bf'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps it’s not surprising that business owners rarely understand why their businesses fail.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/top-10-reasons-small-businesses-fail/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps it’s not surprising that business owners rarely understand why their businesses fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the least understood aspects of entrepreneurship is why small businesses fail, and there’s a simple reason for the confusion: Most of the evidence comes from the entrepreneurs themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Reasons Small Businesses Fail', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f112e4f-b923-5ace-9e8f-d4001f7ed6e4', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f112e4f-b923-5ace-9e8f-d4001f7ed6e4'}, {'abstract': '“Duck à l’orange” deserves better treatment — and a better reputation — than it often gets.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/making-a-true-duck-a-lorange/', 'snippet': '“Duck à l’orange” deserves better treatment — and a better reputation — than it often gets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of certain commitments, it used to be difficult for my wife, Jackie, and me to travel much during the autumn, so we rarely got out of the country at the height of the game season. Now, those commitments are a thing of the past, so we were in London when restaurant menus — and shops — were rich with partridge, hare, woodcock and other wild (or semi-wild) things we rarely see in New York except when they’ve been imported from across the Atlantic. When dining out, we took advantage of this state of affairs and even remembered to chew tentatively so as not to chomp down on little balls of metal shot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making a True Duck à l’Orange', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/545260e7-e926-5bc5-ae48-dd52195df709', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/545260e7-e926-5bc5-ae48-dd52195df709'}, {'abstract': 'Part of the new federal law requires specific changes to be disclosed.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/f-d-a-orders-tobacco-industry-to-disclose-ingredients/', 'snippet': 'Part of the new federal law requires specific changes to be disclosed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal regulators informed the tobacco industry on Wednesday how to disclose, for the first time, any changes to product ingredients, a crucial regulation under the tobacco law President Obama signed in June 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Orders Tobacco Industry to Disclose Ingredients', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menthol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duff Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae295f7-1f42-555d-b518-5bf3b775d3f2', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae295f7-1f42-555d-b518-5bf3b775d3f2'}, {'abstract': 'The newly elected House Speaker John Boehner on Wednesday promised a new era of transparency while vowing to push forward the conservative agenda that swept his party into power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/us/politics/06cong.html', 'snippet': 'The newly elected House Speaker John Boehner on Wednesday promised a new era of transparency while vowing to push forward the conservative agenda that swept his party into power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jubilant Republicans took control of the House on Wednesday and installed Representative John A. Boehner of Ohio as the new speaker before pushing through an overhaul of House rules intended to expedite their drive to dismantle the new health care law, cut federal spending and provide the tax cuts they see as a way to jump-start the economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/us/06congspan5-cnd/06cong5-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/us/06congspan5-cnd/06cong5-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/us/06congspan5-cnd/06cong5-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/us/06congspan5-cnd/06cong5-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/us/06congspan5-cnd/06cong5-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Control, G.O.P. Overhauls Rules in House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TAKING CONTROL,\nG.O.P. OVERHAULS\nRULES IN HOUSE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04a0f62e-ceb3-59be-b659-4c87a40088cb', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04a0f62e-ceb3-59be-b659-4c87a40088cb'}, {'abstract': 'The newest members of Congress and their friends and families are getting their bearings.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/freshmen-and-their-children-swarm-the-hill/', 'snippet': 'The newest members of Congress and their friends and families are getting their bearings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Capitol has been flooded with 7-year-old boys in ties. Many of them struggled Wednesday to free themselves from the premature choke hold of adulthood, but were thwarted by their mothers, many of them draped in something sparkling and knee-length. The mothers swatted at the tiny hands of their sons, smoothed their wayward cowlicks and directed them to use the bathroom before heading to the House floor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freshmen and Their Children Swarm the Hill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:15:15+0000', 'documen