ations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taseer, Salman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/852b16b0-bdb7-5c25-a347-130e9c6b0348', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/852b16b0-bdb7-5c25-a347-130e9c6b0348'}, {'abstract': 'Even though the Jets had 40 sacks this season, tied for eighth in the league, they did not apply consistent pass-rushing pressure, and they will have to be able to disrupt Peyton Manning on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/can-jets-pressure-peyton-manning/', 'snippet': 'Even though the Jets had 40 sacks this season, tied for eighth in the league, they did not apply consistent pass-rushing pressure, and they will have to be able to disrupt Peyton Manning on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Chappell of The Indianapolis Star put his finger on a key matchup:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Jets Pressure Peyton Manning?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:29:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/17d73edb-f199-5569-b313-b05bfa3ca70b', 'word_count': 2488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17d73edb-f199-5569-b313-b05bfa3ca70b'}, {'abstract': 'Water use, dye impact and fair trade have all become issues in producing organic jeans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/fashion/06ORGANICJEANS.html', 'snippet': 'Water use, dye impact and fair trade have all become issues in producing organic jeans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TWO years ago, when going green was red-hot in the fashion industry, there were plenty of organic jeans to choose from. Brands including Levi’s, Banana Republic, Genetic Denim, 7 For All Mankind, Earnest Sewn, Aristocrat, Loomstate, Del Forte and J Brand offered at least one pair made with some amount of organic cotton, which is grown without environmentally threatening chemicals (according to the Sustainable Cotton Project, a nonprofit organization, conventional cotton consumes 25 percent of the world’s chemical pesticides and fertilizers).', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06jeans_span/Z-JEANS-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06jeans_span/Z-JEANS-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06jeans_span/Z-JEANS-B-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06jeans_span/Z-JEANS-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06jeans_span/Z-JEANS-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Eco-Jeans, the Green Becomes Harder to Spot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Eco-Jeans, the Green Becomes Harder to Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Zissu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zissu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f73f6a8-ae58-5fc6-a99a-3242850c6ca5', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f73f6a8-ae58-5fc6-a99a-3242850c6ca5'}, {'abstract': 'Roberto Alomar was selected in his second year on the ballot with 90 percent of the vote, Bert Blyleven in his 14th with 79.7 percent of the vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/sports/baseball/06hall.html', 'snippet': 'Roberto Alomar was selected in his second year on the ballot with 90 percent of the vote, Bert Blyleven in his 14th with 79.7 percent of the vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roberto Alomar was 9 years old in 1977 when his father, Sandy, was traded from the Yankees to the Texas Rangers. Alomar and his brother tagged along to games at old Arlington Stadium, playing ball in the parking lot with the other players’ sons, including 4-year-old Todd Blyleven.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/JPHALL1/JPHALL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/JPHALL1/JPHALL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/sports/JPHALL1/JPHALL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alomar and Blyleven Elected to Hall of Fame', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Room for 2 as Alomar and Blyleven Join Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGwire, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALOMAR, ROBERTO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T19:37:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91cf1107-3209-593d-922c-7e43750c2329', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91cf1107-3209-593d-922c-7e43750c2329'}, {'abstract': 'The News of the World, a British tabloid, has suspended a senior editor accused of authorizing the illegal interception of an actress’s voice-mail messages by reporters.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/british-tabloid-editor-suspended-over-