ers face a fresh round of claims of worker discrimination and intimidation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If some restaurants are cursed with bad locations,\xa0maybe others are cursed with bad labor relations. Two years after a federal judge awarded $4.6 million to\xa0 delivery workers at\xa0the\xa0Saigon Grill, a Manhattan noodle house, to compensate for their\xa0severe exploitation, the restaurant’s new owners face a fresh round of claims of worker discrimination and intimidation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Owners, and New Labor Complaints', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Josephine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nget, Michelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saigon Grill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T20:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb0158c8-fc04-57be-bfb7-847047310fe1', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb0158c8-fc04-57be-bfb7-847047310fe1'}, {'abstract': 'The police commissioner, Raymond W. Kelly, announced a panel to examine the department’s crime statistics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/ny