veloped in collaboration with the producer Andy LeMaster, feels very now. On the eve of a big European tour promoting the album, New Idea Society’s frontman Mike Law talks about the innovative new 3-D video for the single “Thorns.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For New Idea Society, a New Dimension', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T21:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/517adaf4-d9f5-5ebd-94c3-e5a38582d738', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/517adaf4-d9f5-5ebd-94c3-e5a38582d738'}, {'abstract': 'And could Tom Hanks be a co-star?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/streisand-in-talks-to-play-mama-rose-in-film-remake-of-gypsy/', 'snippet': 'And could Tom Hanks be a co-star?', 'lead_paragraph': '6:24 p.m. | Updated Barbra Streisand has met with Stephen Sondheim and Arthur Laurents to discuss starring as Rose, the mother of all stage mamas, in a film version of their 1959 musical “Gypsy,” the two men said in telephone interviews on Wednesday. Mr. Laurents, who wrote the book for “Gypsy” and directed its 2008 revival on Broadway starring Patti LuPone, said that Warner Brothers and Joel Silver were attached as producers, but that no director had been chosen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Streisand in Talks to Play Mama Rose in Film Remake of ‘Gypsy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 