'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea581e8b-5026-5d14-a776-2ad50a4012eb', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea581e8b-5026-5d14-a776-2ad50a4012eb'}, {'abstract': 'A bitter art-world legal battle over an allegedly fake Warhol piece might finally be going to trial after making its way through the New York courts for five years.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/an-allegedly-fake-warhol-may-get-its-day-in-court/', 'snippet': 'A bitter art-world legal battle over an allegedly fake Warhol piece might finally be going to trial after making its way through the New York courts for five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bitter art-world legal battle that has been making its way through the New York courts for five years might finally be going to trial. The poet, photographer and one-time Andy Warhol acolyte Gerard Malanga filed suit in 2005 against the artist John Chamberlain, contending that Mr. Chamberlain sold a 1967 Warhol silk-screen painting that did not belong to him and that he knew was not a real Warhol.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Allegedly Fake Warhol May Get Its Day in Court', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warhol, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b456764-c8e2-5ead-b9f4-0d9db8edda79', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b456764-c8e2-5ead-b9f4-0d9db8edda79'}, {'abstract': 'The new speaker of the House, Representative John A. Boehner of Ohio, promised a new era of transparency in lawmaking during his televised remarks to the House of Representatives on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/1248069526975/boehner-s-first-remarks-as-house-speaker.html', 'snippet': 'The new speaker of the House, Representative John A. Boehner of Ohio, promised a new era of transparency in lawmaking during his televised remarks to the House of Representatives on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new speaker of the House, Representative John A. Boehner of Ohio, promised a new era of transparency in lawmaking during his televised remarks to the House of Representatives on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/us/politics/10897_1_boehnerswornin_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/us/politics/10897_1_boehnerswornin_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "Boehner's First Remarks as House Speaker", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Bill Horn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a0267d04-7018-5bf2-9f6d-14b2b06eadff', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a0267d04-7018-5bf2-9f6d-14b2b06eadff'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers report that an 18th-century Irishman who gained wealth and fame as a 7-foot-7 freak of nature had a rare gene mutation that is probably shared by 200 to 300 people living today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/health/06giant.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers report that an 18th-century Irishman who gained wealth and fame as a 7-foot-7 freak of nature had a rare gene mutation that is probably shared by 200 to 300 people living today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He was a giant of a man, 7 feet 7 inches tall, who left his home in Ireland when he was 19 and traveled to London to make his fortune as a freak. There Charles Byrne, known as the Irish Giant, garnered wealth and fame. But, suffering from tuberculosis and an excessive love of gin, he died a few years later, in 1783. A surgeon — John Hunter — bought Mr. Byrne’s corpse, boiled it in acid to remove the flesh, and exhibited the skeleton in his museum in London.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/world/GIANT/GIANT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/world/GIANT/GIANT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/world/GIANT/GIANT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/world/GIANT/GIANT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/world/GIANT/GIANT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Giant’s Story, a New Chapter Writ by His DNA', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Giant’s Story, a New Chapter Writ by His DNA', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tumors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04db4ac6-6784-5a06-8361-d4c84858c149', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04db4ac6-6784-5a06-8361-d4c84858c149'}, {'abstract': 'One of the developing world’s great successes is Grameen Bank, run by the Nobel Peace Prize-winning Muhammad Yunus. Now he’s in trouble — and it looks as if the Bangladesh government may be after him.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/is-bangladesh-trying-to-take-over-grameen-bank/', 'snippet': 'One of the developing world’s great successes is Grameen Bank, run by the Nobel Peace Prize-winning Muhammad Yunus. Now he’s in trouble — and it looks as if the Bangladesh government may be after him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Very strange things are happening in Bangladesh these days. There seems to be a multi-pronged assault on Grameen Bank and on Muhammad Yunus, who won a Nobel Peace Prize for his role pioneering microfinance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Bangladesh Trying to Take Over Grameen Bank?', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5242cf43-2d51-5136-8454-6262b9c987a3', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5242cf43-2d51-5136-8454-6262b9c987a3'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said his outgoing press secretary had been earning “relatively modest pay.” But he falls in the top 10 percent of Americans in income distribution.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/how-modest-is-robert-gibbss-salary/', 'snippet': 'President Obama said his outgoing press secretary had been earning “relatively modest pay.” But he falls in the top 10 percent of Americans in income distribution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interview with The New York Times on Wednesday, President Obama remarked of his outgoing press secretary Robert Gibbs, “He’s had a six-year stretch now where basically he’s been going 24/7 with relatively modest pay. I think it’s natural for someone like Robert to want to step back for a second to reflect, retool, and that, as a consequence, brings about both challenges and opportunities for the White House.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How ‘Modest’ Is Robert Gibbs’s Salary?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbs, Robert L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da