oints to Errors in Gulf Spill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Ocean Energy Management, Regulation and Enforcement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transocean Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Halliburton Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a560e71-fa5b-5382-9216-06ea3252f708', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a560e71-fa5b-5382-9216-06ea3252f708'}, {'abstract': 'News reports seem to have dwindled over all since the failure of an international climate conference in Copenhagen a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/has-climate-coverage-ebbed/', 'snippet': 'News reports seem to have dwindled over all since the failure of an international climate conference in Copenhagen a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Revkin muses at his Dot Earth blog on how news media coverage of climate change leveled off in many respects last year. Among other indicators, he examines a graph on evening network news coverage generated by Robert Brulle of Drexel University. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Has Climate Coverage Ebbed?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4943ed6d-b564-5504-8d28-6f42685e327d', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4943ed6d-b564-5504-8d28-6f42685e327d'}, {'abstract': 'In “Songs My Mother Taught Me: The Judy Garland Songbook” at Feinstein’s, Lorna Luft performed tunes made famous by Garland and offered biographical tidbits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/arts/music/06luft.html', 'snippet': 'In “Songs My Mother Taught Me: The Judy Garland Songbook” at Feinstein’s, Lorna Luft performed tunes made famous by Garland and offered biographical tidbits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The terms of endearment “Mama” and “Grandma” were lavishly sprinkled through Tuesday’s opening-night performance of Lorna Luft’s warmhearted retrospective tribute “Songs My Mother Taught Me: The Judy Garland Songbook” at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency. “Mama” is, of course, the name that both Ms. Luft and her older half sister, Liza Minnelli, have always used to refer to Garland, who died in 1969. The youthful voices of Ms. Luft’s now-grown children, Jesse and Vanessa, are also heard asking questions about “Grandma.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/Luft/Luft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/Luft/Luft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/Luft/Luft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Mama’s Rainbow', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating Mama’s Rainbow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Feinstein's at the Regency", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luft, Lorna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T22:55:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebe4263-2f00-5fd4-8aca-9aa84da50793', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebe4263-2f00-5fd4-8aca-9aa84da50793'}, {'abstract': "The comedian Marc Maron's podcast is more than just jokes. His interviews often reveal unguarded moments from humorists like Robin Williams, Dane Cook and Ben Stiller.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/1248069526720/marc-maron-s-second-act.html', 'snippet': "The comedian Marc Maron's podcast is more than just jokes. His interviews often reveal unguarded moments f