rs, will become president of The Blaze, a Web site intended to curate news articles and opinion pieces for Glenn Beck’s conservative audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking to further expand his growing media presence, Glenn Beck, the conservative talk-show host, has hired a one-time chief executive of the left-leaning Huffington Post to lead his new Web site, The Blaze.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glenn Beck Hires Former Huffington Post Chief', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huffington Post', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/315a9a4a-a863-561d-8fff-eac257115d68', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315a9a4a-a863-561d-8fff-eac257115d68'}, {'abstract': 'A police officer suspected of killing a prominent secular politician on Tuesday was showered with rose petals on his way into court in Islamabad on Wednesday by Islamist lawyers.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/pakistani-lawyers-shower-murder-suspect-with-roses/', 'snippet': 'A police officer suspected of killing a prominent secular politician on Tuesday was showered with rose petals on his way into court in Islamabad on Wednesday by Islamist lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Waqar Gillani and Carlotta Gall report from Pakistan, a police officer suspected of killing a prominent secular politician on Tuesday was showered with rose petals by Islamist lawyers on his way in to court in Islamabad on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Lawyers Shower Murder Suspect With Roses', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d6e1e4-e017-57e5-a1be-8c33b1e14a13', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d6e1e4-e017-57e5-a1be-8c33b1e14a13'}, {'abstract': 'A building owner has ignored demands to remove an addition to a historic row house in Chelsea that may be the only surviving Manhattan station on the Underground Railroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/arts/design/06saved.html', 'snippet': 'A building owner has ignored demands to remove an addition to a historic row house in Chelsea that may be the only surviving Manhattan station on the Underground Railroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A building owner has ignored the city’s demands to dismantle a fifth story that was added to a landmark mid-19th-century row house in Chelsea that may be the only surviving documented Manhattan station on the Underground Railroad. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/SAVED1/SAVED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Change to Civil War-Era Building Disputed', 'kicker': None, '