2ecc'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine has named Ray Chelstowski, a former publisher at Rolling Stone and Entertainment Weekly, as publisher.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/newsweek-hires-new-publisher/', 'snippet': 'The magazine has named Ray Chelstowski, a former publisher at Rolling Stone and Entertainment Weekly, as publisher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of staff turmoil including a new owner, editor and chief executive and scores of lower-level departures, the management ranks at Newsweek are beginning to stabilize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newsweek Hires Publisher', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed320afd-6665-5b90-8d32-85ba43f9bade', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed320afd-6665-5b90-8d32-85ba43f9bade'}, {'abstract': 'Last month, food prices were at the highest level since a United Nations index originated, — partly because of crop failures associated with drought, floods and fires.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/extreme-weather-sends-food-prices-soaring/', 'snippet': 'Last month, food prices were at the highest level since a United Nations index originated, — partly because of crop failures associated with drought, floods and fires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague William Neuman reports, the United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization announced this week that food prices hit a record high last month. Its Food Price Index was 214.7 for December, the highest level since the organization created the index to measure the price of a standard basket of goods in 1990. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extreme Weather Helps Drive Up Food Prices', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wheat', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3f90a59-27f2-5d0b-bac0-0d6001c0da21', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3f90a59-27f2-5d0b-bac0-0d6001c0da21'}, {'abstract': 'For more than a decade, AndrewAndrew, a pair of D.J.’s, have dressed exactly alike as part of a radical commitment to mirroring each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/fashion/06Andrew.html', 'snippet': 'For more than a decade, AndrewAndrew, a pair of D.J.’s, have dressed exactly alike as part of a radical commitment to mirroring each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE girl in the gray cocktail dress eyed the D.J.’s, a pair of men engrossed in their matching iPads.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06andrew_span/Z-ANDREW-P1-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06andrew_span/Z-ANDREW-P1-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06andrew_span/Z-ANDREW-P1-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06andrew_span/Z-ANDREW-P1-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/fashion/06andrew_span/Z-ANDREW-P1-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mirror Images in the D.J. Booth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mirror Images In the D.J. Booth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd2b121-795d-5d41-bf1a-7261b0fc5cf2', 'word_count': 1946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd2b121-795d-5d41-bf1a-7261b0fc5cf2'}, {'abstract': 'The premiere of “Live to Dance,” CBS’s new reality competition with Paula Abdul, won its two-hour time slot in the ratings on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/arts/television/06arts-ABDULSTARTSS_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The premiere of “Live to Dance,” CBS’s new reality competition with Paula Abdul, won its two-hour time slot in the ratings on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The premiere of “Live to Dance,” CBS’s new reality competition with Paula Abdul, below, won its two-hour time slot in the ratings on Tuesday, attracting an average of 10.2 million viewers from 8 to 10 p.m., according to Nielsen’s estimates. CBS led the night over all, including the 10 o’clock hour with a rerun of “NCIS,” which also drew 10.2 million viewers and outperformed its competitors at 10, ABC’s “Detroit 1-8-7” (5.2 million) and NBC’s “Parenthood” (6 million). NBC ranked second as the premiere of the 11th edition of “The Biggest Loser” delivered 8.7 million viewers from 8 to 10, along with the night’s top ratings among viewers 18 to 49. ABC was third, garnering 6.8 million at 8 for “No Ordinary Family” and 6.6 million at 9 for the debut of the new season of “V.” Fox ranked fourth with a rerun of “Glee” (4.7 million), followed by “Million Dollar Money Drop” (3.8 million).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abdul Starts Strong', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abdul Starts Strong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/27ee8e7a-3638-5ec3-9dc9-c6b45f92b471', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27ee8e7a-3638-5ec3-9dc9-c6b45f92b471'}, {'abstract': 'Cory Stearns has been promoted to principal dancer at American Ballet Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/arts/dance/06arts-FOOTNOTE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Cory Stearns has been promoted to principal dancer at American Ballet Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cory Stearns, above, has been promoted to principal dancer at American Ballet Theater, the company said on Wednesday. Mr. Stearns, 25, joined Ballet Theater as an apprentice in 2005.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnote', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f171cdfb-27c9-52a8-9917-a700b33d6c5f', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f171cdfb-27c9-52a8-9917-a700b33d6c5f'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Thomas will star in a production of Shakespeare’s “Timon of Athens.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/theater/06arts-RICHARDTHOMA_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Thomas will star in a production of Shakespeare’s “Timon of Athens.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Thomas will star in a production of Shakespeare’s “Timon of Athens,” the opening work in an effort by the Public Theater to present scaled-down plays by Shakespeare with relatively inexpensive tickets, the theater said on Wednesday. Barry Edelstein, who runs the Public’s Shakespeare Initiative, will direct the show, which will run Feb. 15 through March 6. Single tickets, which will cost $15, go on sale on Jan. 18.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard Thomas Set for ‘Timon of Athens’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Richard Thomas Set For ‘Timon of Athens’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ec3a2ec-7eff-5fe9-8a59-7a9a3d240b6b', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec3a2ec-7eff-5fe9-8a59-7a9a3d240b6b'}, {'abstract': 'The Hotel du Golf in Abidjan is isolated in its unofficial role as the alternate seat of government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/world/africa/06ivory.html', 'snippet': 'The Hotel du Golf in Abidjan is isolated in its unofficial role as the alternate seat of government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABIDJAN, Ivory Coast \x97 Laundry hangs from balconies, beer bottles remain in the lobby, officials