n Is Set for Colts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-05T23:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e4a823f-355b-5adb-963b-345932175761', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e4a823f-355b-5adb-963b-345932175761'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hillyer was a soloist and teacher known for the warmth and expressivity of his tone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/arts/music/06hillyer.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hillyer was a soloist and teacher known for the warmth and expressivity of his tone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raphael Hillyer, the founding violist of the Juilliard String Quartet and a soloist and teacher known for the warmth and expressivity of his tone, died on Dec. 27 in Boston, where he lived. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/obituaries/06hillyer1/06hillyer1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/obituaries/06hillyer1/06hillyer1-thumbStandard-