orts', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5290662a-df5b-5d31-8e49-29b8e210af47', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5290662a-df5b-5d31-8e49-29b8e210af47'}, {'abstract': 'A new range of point-and-shoot digital cameras from Sony, shown at CES.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/an-oled-point-and-shoot-from-sony/', 'snippet': 'A new range of point-and-shoot digital cameras from Sony, shown at CES.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sony is back at the Consumer Electronics Show with a new OLED screen. But don’t plan on hanging this one on the wall; it measures three-and-a-half inches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An OLED Point-and-Shoot From Sony', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T02:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/952b347d-a292-579d-b8b2-20770bc33221', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952b347d-a292-579d-b8b2-20770bc33221'}, {'abstract': 'James Buchanan was criticized for his passivity in handling the secession crisis. But it was his single moment of activism that doomed his presidency—and the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/james-buchanans-activist-blunder/', 'snippet': 'James Buchanan was criticized for his passivity in handling the secession crisis. But it was his single moment of activism that doomed his presidency—and the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President James Buchanan’s critics rightly condemned him during the secession crisis of 1860-’61 — but they did so for exactly the wrong reason. The naysayers blasted the president for passiveness in the face of disunion, for failing promptly to reinforce endangered federal forts in the South. True, the president retreated from sending reinforcements — except for a few critical days around the New Year. At that moment, a sudden burst of irresponsible activism shrunk his record of passivity to comparative unimportance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James Buchanan’s Activist Blunder', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War and Guerrilla Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buchanan, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T02:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William W. Freehling', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Freehling', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0bdc95a-3e3d-5de4-b663-507bd993bc9b', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0bdc95a-3e3d-5de4-b663-507bd993bc9b'}, {'abstract': 'The new Republican majority has ordered that the United States Constitution be read on the floor of the House of Representatives on Thursday morning. Read along with The Caucus.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/an-annotated-guide-to-the-constitution/', 'snippet': 'The new Republican majority has ordered that the United States Constitution be read on the floor of the House of Representatives on Thursday morning. Read along with The Caucus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Republican majority has ordered that the United States Constitution be read on the floor of the House of Representatives on Thursday, the day after new lawmakers were sworn in. Congressional historians say they believe this has been done only twice before. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading Between the Battle Lines: An Annotated Guide to the Constitution', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T02:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a99630-feeb-5df7-8de2-151759a8439a', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a99630-feeb-5df7-8de2-151759a8439a'}, {'abstract': 'Philippa Raschker, 63, has set more than 200 masters track and field records and still loves competing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/sports/06master.html', 'snippet': 'Philippa Raschker, 63, has set more than 200 masters track and field records and still loves competing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARIETTA, Ga. \x97 Philippa Raschker, the most enduring female athlete you’ve never heard of, is flying solo, dashing down a track that rings a high school football field.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub