.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/live-traffic-comes-to-tomtom/', 'snippet': 'New portable GPS models from TomTom include instantaneous traffic updates and easier windshield mounting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Virtually instantaneous traffic updates come to TomTom’s line of GPS devices with the launch of its Go 2505 M LIVE model. The $349 product, which will be available by mid-2011, uses both satellite and GPRS radio signals to update traffic conditions every two minutes, compared with every 15 minutes for the company’s other models.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Traffic Comes to TomTom', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TomTom NV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T03:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric A. Taub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Taub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f428d90-50fd-51e3-8707-208eeb5d7ba2', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f428d90-50fd-51e3-8707-208eeb5d7ba2'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Nothnagel, normally a very cooperative guy, goes against the group.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/awol/', 'snippet': 'Mike Nothnagel, normally a very cooperative guy, goes against the group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — I’m surprised at you, Mike Nothnagel. You’ve always been this affable, go-with-the-flow kind of guy, and then I see that all this time there’s been a rebel inside you, screaming to get out. I will say that you announce your intent to go against the group brilliantly. It took me a bit of staring at the completed grid and the help of another pair of eyes to fully understand what you were doing, but that “aha!” moment was very satisfying. Nicely done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: Going AWOL', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T03:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/66019a51-5ce3-5685-a902-9018577d7d58', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66019a51-5ce3-5685-a902-9018577d7d58'}, {'abstract': 'The 1920s stage version of “Dracula” has been revived with Michel Altieri as the fanged one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/theater/reviews/06dracula.html', 'snippet': 'The 1920s stage version of “Dracula” has been revived with Michel Altieri as the fanged one.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Vampires are rare,” opines Dr. Van Helsing, the expert on all things undead, in the revival of the drama “Dracula” that opened Wednesday night at the Little Shubert Theater. “Nature abhors them, the forces of good combine to destroy them, but a few of these creatures have lived on for centuries.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/arts/DRACULA/DRACULA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': '