 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a1b85d81-1c03-56c7-94bd-a4ee7b6cc3bd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a1b85d81-1c03-56c7-94bd-a4ee7b6cc3bd'}, {'abstract': 'Despite 424 career saves, fourth on the career list, John Franco received only 27 votes in Hall of Fame voting.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/05/francos-hall-candidacy-is-one-shot-deal/', 'snippet': 'Despite 424 career saves, fourth on the career list, John Franco received only 27 votes in Hall of Fame voting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buried at the bottom of the Hall of Fame voting list was a revelation of sorts. Voters gave very little consideration to closer John Franco’s candidacy; so little, in fact, that he will no longer qualify for the ballot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Franco’s Hall Candidacy Is One-Shot Deal', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dca1fa5-879e-552a-9ee0-575830012cbc', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dca1fa5-879e-552a-9ee0-575830012cbc'}, {'abstract': 'How owners and lenders can solve the mortgage mess together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/opinion/06perriello.html', 'snippet': 'How owners and lenders can solve the mortgage mess together.', 'lead_paragraph': ' THREE years after the mortgage crisis began, there are still 11 million to 15 million homeowners who owe more than their home is worth, meaning that about 25 percent of all mortgage holders are underwater. As a result, foreclosures continue to mount; many homeowners can’t make their payments and are tempted to simply walk away from their debt. Meanwhile, the lenders and investors who own the loans are unwilling to work out a deal if, as is usually the case, it means losing money. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/opinion/0106oped_mclean/0106oped_mclean-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/opinion/0106oped_mclean/0106oped_mclean-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/opinion/0106oped_mclean/0106oped_mclean-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Team', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Perriello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perriello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2563eede-9f56-59e7-baf7-159f7ba24a37', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2563eede-9f56-59e7-baf7-159f7ba24a37'}, {'abstract': 'It is already clear that the House Republicans plan to serve their corporate donors, above all else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/opinion/06thu2.html', 'snippet': 'It is already clear that the House Republicans plan to serve their corporate donors, above all else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Boehner, the new speaker, promised the incoming House members of the 112th Congress on Wednesday to “give the government back to the American people.” But away from the camera, the chamber’s new Republican leadership is busy doing the opposite. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corporate House', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Corporate House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4059148e-c4e8-5f72-9308-48ca36fb26ff', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4059148e-c4e8-5f72-9308-48ca36fb26ff'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent article on the Winklevoss twins’ attempt to get a greater payout in their suit against Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/opinion/l06facebook.h