'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PCB (Polychlorinated Biphenyls)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e28c930-57a1-546e-bf50-7ba4b79da33f', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e28c930-57a1-546e-bf50-7ba4b79da33f'}, {'abstract': 'There is no way to “clean up” Twain without doing irreparable harm to the truth of his work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/opinion/06thu4.html', 'snippet': 'There is no way to “clean up” Twain without doing irreparable harm to the truth of his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next month, you will be able to buy the single- volume NewSouth Edition of Mark Twain’s “The Adventures of Tom Sawyer” and “Adventures of Huckleberry Finn,” edited by Professor Alan Gribben of Auburn University at Montgomery. It differs from other editions of those books because Mr. Gribben has turned the word “nigger” \x97 as used by Tom and Huck \x97 into “slave.” Mr. Gribben has also changed “Injun” to Indian. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That’s Not Twain', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That’s Not Twain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Samuel Langhorne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Adventures of Huckleberry Finn, The (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cb327f-6933-52ee-8b81-6273cdb26257', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cb327f-6933-52ee-8b81-6273cdb26257'}, {'abstract': 'The governments of Egypt and Iraq need to do more to provide security for their Christian citizens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/opinion/06thu3.html', 'snippet': 'The governments of Egypt and Iraq need to do more to provide security for their Christian citizens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christians are increasingly under siege in Egypt and Iraq. Over the past year, hundreds have been killed or wounded in attacks, and the violence is further raising political and sectarian tensions in the two countries. All people, regardless of their beliefs, should be outraged.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Siege', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Siege', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T04:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/196c0246-c30b-5d1f-b5