: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b3da5f-ea81-5d97-a1d2-3c7c89441d64', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b3da5f-ea81-5d97-a1d2-3c7c89441d64'}, {'abstract': 'Jacksonville’s Jack Del Rio and Houston’s Gary Kubiak will return despite not having a winning record in four of the last five years, and Peyton Manning doesn’t make their task any easier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/sports/football/06fifth.html', 'snippet': 'Jacksonville’s Jack Del Rio and Houston’s Gary Kubiak will return despite not having a winning record in four of the last five years, and Peyton Manning doesn’t make their task any easier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indianapolis Colts’ Peyton Manning set the league record for completions in a season, with 450. He also led the league in sack rate, a measure of avoiding sacks, which is often ignored when judging the talent of a quarterback. But there are many ways to rate a quarterback. Consider the news out of Jacksonville, Fla., and Houston this week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jaguars and Texans, Chasing Manning', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jaguars and Texans, Chasing Manning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Buccaneers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacksonville Jaguars', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T05:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart and Luis DeLoureiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Luis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeLoureiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/186e3430-12d4-5ab4-b0ca-9528c36ad103', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/186e3430-12d4-5ab4-b0ca-9528c36ad103'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs Capital Partners — a powerful unit at the bank that manages money for pensions, sovereign wealth funds and other prominent clients — passed on the $450 million stake in the social networking site. After that, Goldman itself made the investment.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/goldman-unit-passed-on-earlier-facebook-investment/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs Capital Partners — a powerful unit at the bank that manages money for pensions, sovereign wealth funds and other prominent clients — passed on the $450 million stake in the social networking site. After that, Goldman itself made the ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Goldman Sachs bought a stake in Facebook and started offering shares to wealthy clients, a powerful investment group within the firm turned down the chance to buy a piece of the social networking site, according to several people briefed on the internal discussions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Goldman Unit Is Said to Have Rejected Facebook', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Richard A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'va