and the Whitney Museum of American Art, among others, and he was the recipient of a Guggenheim Fellowship in 1976. His books include “Social Graces” (1984, reissued 2001), “Boxing” (1997), “Runway” (2000) and “The Vanities: Hollywood Parties 2000–2009,” which will be published this year by Schirmer/Mosel. He is a professor of photography at Bard College. This conversation, with Adriana Teresa, the co-founder of FotoVisura and the publisher of Visura Magazine, has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Moment With Larry Fink', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fink, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Teresa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Teresa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/661b7246-1ff5-5be2-b3f5-6cf6e8c1efd9', 'word_count': 2037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/661b7246-1ff5-5be2-b3f5-6cf6e8c1efd9'}, {'abstract': 'Because Goldman Sachs receives government backing against failure, its recent investment in Facebook represents a public subsidy to a company that doesn’t need one, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/why-are-taxpayers-subsidizing-facebook-and-the-next-bubble/', 'snippet': 'Because Goldman Sachs receives government backing against failure, its recent investment in Facebook represents a public subsidy to a company that doesn’t need one, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is th