n open day in Fo Tan, an industrial neighborhood near suburban Sha Tin. This year marks the 10th anniversary of the event, the Fotanian Open Studios, on Jan. 8, 9, 15 and 16. The Wah Luen Industrial Center (15-21 Wong Chuk Yeung Street) is the epicenter, with other studios in neighboring warehouse buildings. A map designed to guide visitors through the show is available.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hong Kong, Artists Open Their Studios', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T11:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Frew McMillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': 'Frew', 'lastname': 'McMillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/58d28e54-845d-544a-a1fd-5927765798ba', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58d28e54-845d-544a-a1fd-5927765798ba'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats plan a vigorous defense of President Obama’s health care legislation in the face of a repeal threat.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/democrats-plan-attack-on-republican-repeal-effort/', 'snippet': 'Democrats plan a vigorous defense of President Obama’s health care legislation in the face of a repeal threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democratic leaders in Washington plan to spend the next week doing what they all but refused to do in the 2010 midterm elections: mount a vigorous defense of President Obama’s health care legislation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Plan Attack on Republican Repeal Effort', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T11:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3861d137-4b2c-5855-b38a-3b2cdf45d784', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3861d137-4b2c-5855-b38a-3b2cdf45d784'}, {'abstract': 'Of the four wild-card games this weekend, the efficiency probability model disagrees with the general consensus on only one game, Green Bay at Philadelphia. The Packers are slightly favored by my system.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/wild-card-probabilities-packers-over-eagles/', 'snippet': 'Of the four wild-card games this weekend, the efficiency probability model disagrees with the general consensus on only one game, Green Bay at Philadelphia. The Packers are slightly favored by my system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Burke, a former Navy pilot who has taken up the less dangerous hobby of N.F.L. statistical analysis, operates Advanced NFL Stats, a blog about football, math and human behavior. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wild-Card Probabilities: Packers Over Eagles', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EAGLES, THE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T12:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d939fd8-d409-5b18-9cab-adce9af470aa', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d939fd8-d409-5b18-9cab-adce9af470aa'}, {'abstract': 'If not, there are things you can do to improve the way you communicate.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/are-your-messages-being-heard/', 'snippet': 'If not, there are things you can do to improve the way you communicate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are at the beginning of another year — that time when we turn a critical eye to what worked and what didn’t last year. So let’s give some attention to the foundation of all good marketing efforts: interpersonal communication. Think of traditional marketing as air cover but personal communications as the sales maker that wins customers and keeps clients happy and loyal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Your Messages Being Heard?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T12:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlenam