nt': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a61f9048-429b-52ae-be74-d6ea36e45b80'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs’s deal with Facebook, while it may have won praise for the bankers involved, is another example of how government backing leads to moral hazard, Simon Johnson writes at Economix.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/taxpayer-backing-for-the-facebook-bubble/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs’s deal with Facebook, while it may have won praise for the bankers involved, is another example of how government backing leads to moral hazard, Simon Johnson writes at Economix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Goldman Sachs deal with Facebook is essentially backed by taxpayers’ dollars, Simon Johnson, a former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, writes at Economix.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxpayer Backing for the Facebook Bubble', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T13:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/70d1e937-87cd-59ca-ae4e-0a6e16906ce7', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70d1e937-87cd-59ca-ae4e-0a6e16906ce7'}, {'abstract': 'The Wall Street firm is selling its 44.7 percent stake in Accordia Golf, which owns 131 golf courses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/goldman-eyes-clubhouse-in-japan-golf-deal/', 'snippet': 'The Wall Street firm is selling its 44.7 percent stake in Accordia Golf, which owns 131 golf courses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time when Goldman Sachs is making a big investment in Facebook, it is exiting from another once-prominent part of its portfolio: Accordia Golf of Japan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Eyes Clubhouse in Japan Golf Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T13:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Cane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c582d18-7b45-50c2-8367-0e49c0191575', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c582d18-7b45-50c2-8367-0e49c0191575'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: the governor’s pro-business State of the State, a team of former federal prosecutors will look into charges that the police have manipulated crime statistics, and an unpermitted addition to a landmark building persists.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/morning-buzz-e-m-s-chief-is-demoted/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: the governor’s pro-business State of the State, a team of former federal prosecutors will look into charges that the police have manipulated crime statistics, and an unpermitted addition to a landmark building persists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weather will be highly normal today, with a high in the mid-30s under partly cloudy skies. But a storm coming Friday could bring up to three inches of snow. Here is some news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | E.M.S. Chief Is Demoted', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T13:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa0f18dd-747d-5214-9f12-44489a080e10', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa0f18dd-747d-5214-9f12-44489a080e10'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of the Empire State Building have brokered a deal to buy 100 percent of the landmark tower’s energy from renewable sources. The devil, of course, is in the details.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/green-power-for-the-empire-state-building/', 'snippet': 'The owners of the Empire State Building have brokered a deal to buy 100 percent of the landmark tower’s energy from renewable sources. The devil, of course, is in the details.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid a more general makeover, the owners of the Empire State Building have spent the last couple of years burnishing the 80-year-old landmark’s green bona fides as well — chiefly though a series of efficiency upgrades and other energy retrofits. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Green Power for the Empire State Building', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '