unning game in two playoff victories last season, but a rib injury against the Colts in the A.F.C. title game was too much to overcome.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shonn Greene and Unfinished Business Against  Colts', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greene, Shonn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T14:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f842b9-a08c-57fb-9bcb-2434d043da35', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f842b9-a08c-57fb-9bcb-2434d043da35'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago’s first winery is turning out cranberry-flavored mead, made bubbly by the Methode Champenoise.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/we-made-it-ourselves-wild-blossom-meads/', 'snippet': 'Chicago’s first winery is turning out cranberry-flavored mead, made bubbly by the Methode Champenoise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While everyone else rang in the New Year with Champagne or something akin to that effervescing white, in Chicago, Greg Fischer popped open a bottle of Sparkling Cran-Nectar. It’s one of his own creations, a cranberry-flavored mead made bubbly by the Methode Champenois.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Made It Ourselves | Wild Blossom Meads', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T14:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlotte Druckman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlotte', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Druckman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c09232-f1a0-5ce6-9581-d206acc40578', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c09232-f1a0-5ce6-9581-d206acc40578'}, {'abstract': 'The Icelandic director, screenwriter, producer and occasional actor Fridrik Thor Fridriksson finds himself in the running for a second Oscar nomination, this time for “Mamma Gogo,” a film about a film whose hopes for breaking even hinge on receiving an Oscar nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/from-iceland-a-meta-comedy-about-movies-and-alzheimers/', 'snippet': 'The Icelandic director, screenwriter, producer and occasional actor Fridrik Thor Fridriksson finds himself in the running for a second Oscar nomination, this time for “Mamma Gogo,” a film about a film whose hopes for breaking even hinge on receivi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine a film that is about a film whose hopes for breaking even financially hinge on its receiving an Oscar nomination. Then imagine that the film — the real one, not the film within the film — actually ends up in contention for an Oscar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Iceland, a Meta-Comedy About Movies and Alzheimer’s', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fridriksson, Fridrik Thor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T14:01:43+