ce? In this occasional series, Anahad O’Connor, the New York Times “Really?” columnist, explores the claims and the science behind alternative remedies that you may want to consider for your family medicine cabinet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remedies: Garlic for Athlete’s Foot', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Complementary Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Athlete's Foot", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Garlic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T15:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1303c3af-e6ff-5070-b1c7-19b233099a8a', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1303c3af-e6ff-5070-b1c7-19b233099a8a'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan’s doomsday machine | Foreclosure flaws | The Facebook pitch memo', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/morning-take-out-156/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan’s doomsday machine | Foreclosure flaws | The Facebook pitch memo', 'lead_paragraph': '–The Man Who Spilled Secrets – Vanity Fair looks at Julian Assange and his relationship with The Guardian.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, Elizabeth', 'rank'