ence to prescriptions lowers hospital stays and medical costs overall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people remember to take their medicine, are they healthier because of the drugs they take or because they also go to the doctor on a regular basis and even try to exercise from time to time?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Your Medicine Pays Off', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T16:09:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/97fa7cf1-f769-5eb2-a359-d3a5034c970d', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97fa7cf1-f769-5eb2-a359-d3a5034c970d'}, {'abstract': 'The two-year term of the economic panel he heads is about to expire, but there has been no announcement about whether it will be extended.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/volckers-future-as-obama-adviser-uncertain/', 'snippet': 'The two-year term of the economic panel he heads is about to expire, but there has been no announcement about whether it will be extended.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:27 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Volcker’s Future as Obama Adviser Uncertain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volcker, Paul A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economic Recovery Advisory Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T16:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/252d1fb6-61fa-5c31-84c0-6eb3525de5e0', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/252d1fb6-61fa-5c31-84c0-6eb3525de5e0'}, {'abstract': 'Canada seemed to be cruising to the world juniors hockey title against Russia Wednesday. Then the third period happened.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/canada-stunned-by-world-juniors-collapse/', 'snippet': 'Canada seemed to be cruising to the world juniors hockey title against Russia Wednesday. Then the third period happened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Woe, Canada. Angst, hand-wringing and naked criticism are the themes of the day in the Great White North, as Canada’s junior hockey team lost in spectacular fashion to Russia in Wednesday’s world junior hockey championships in Buffalo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada Stunned by World Juniors Collapse', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T16:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/942d5799-d94e-54ec-88d5-28661a23650f', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/942d5799-d94e-54ec-88d5-28661a23650f'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Public Library is restoring a huge archive of of papers that captures the worry of families waiting for word of soldiers in battle.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/a-look-at-life-during-civil-wartime/', 'snippet': 'The New York Public Library is restoring a huge archive of of papers that captures the worry of families waiting for word of soldiers in battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Plumb’s heart broke, and she feared the worst as she set pen to paper to inquire about her husband.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at Life During (Civil) Wartime', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T16:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily B. Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf27294-87c0-5dcb-bd95-ee8118fe8132', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf27294-87c0-5dcb-bd95-ee8118fe8132'}, {'abstract': 'Saturday’s N.F.L. wild-card matchups', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/saturdays-n-f-l-wild-card-matchups/', 'snippet': 'Saturday’s N.F.L. wild-card matchups', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jets at ColtsSaturday, 8 p.m.Line: Colts by 2½', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday’s N.F.L. Wild-Card Matchups', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T16:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'new