m/2011/01/07/business/global/07engine.html', 'snippet': 'British Airways expressed confidence in the engine maker by ordering the same model that exploded midair on a Qantas plane in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON \x97 British Airways completed a contract with Rolls-Royce, the airline engine maker, on Thursday, picking the same engine model for its Airbus SAS A380 airplanes that exploded midair on a Qantas Airways plane in November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Airline Order Is Vote of Confidence in Rolls-Royce Engine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Airways Orders Disputed Engine Model From Rolls-Royce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolls-Royce PLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Airways PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T17:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d85601-c2e0-55d0-b553-1e4249c6839e', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d85601-c2e0-55d0-b553-1e4249c6839e'}, {'abstract': 'Buildings that anchored a block more than 30 years ago have fallen into disrepair since the real estate bust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/nyregion/07block.html', 'snippet': 'Buildings that anchored a block more than 30 years ago have fallen into disrepair since the real estate bust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four-story wreck that is 920 Kelly Street is a South Bronx time machine for Harry De Rienzo. Its broken windows, garbage-choked halls, mold-mottled rooms and smoky stench remind him of what much of the area looked like nearly 35 years ago, when he first arrived to work at a settlement house.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/nyregion/block-span/block-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/06/nyregion/block-span/block-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/nyregion/block-span/block-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/nyregion/block-span/block-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/nyregion/block-span/block-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the South Bronx, Blight Returns to a Rehabilitated Block', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back to the Battle Against Blight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landlords', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banana Kelly Community Improvement Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T17:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af263f69-e997-5593-94d0-2c60301f6853', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af263f69-e997-5593-94d0-2c60301f6853'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition opening today at the Yossi Milo Gallery looks at the work of the architectural photographer, who captured many of the 20th century’s Modernist masterworks on film.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/now-showing-ezra-stoller/', 'snippet': 'An exhibition opening today at the Yossi Milo Gallery looks at the work of the architectural photographer, who captured many of the 20th century’s Modernist masterworks on film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An exhibition of the work of the photographer Ezra Stoller opens today at Yossi Milo Gallery. Stoller, who died in 2004 at age 89, was the foremost chronicler of Modernist architecture, using his large-format camera to record seminal 20th-century works like Mies van der Rohe’s Seagram Building, Frank Lloyd Wright’s Fallingwater and Guggenheim Museum, and Eero Saarinen’s TWA Terminal at Idlewild Airport (now Kennedy). The exhibition of gelatin silver prints includes not just images of these buildings but also of lesser-known midcentury works like the Starkey house in Duluth, Minn., by Marcel Breuer, and the International Style, Skidmore, Owings & Merrill-designed First National City Bank (now Citibank) branch, also at Kennedy — which still stands, albeit in a less pristine landscape than when Stoller trained his deep-focus lens on it. So influential was Stoller’s approach, which captured a building’s lines in sometimes abstract, often monumental compositions, that a project wasn’t considered complete until it had been “Stollerized.” The exhibition continues through Feb. 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Ezra Stoller', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T17:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/01cb3102-26f7-559d-bad9-5cc5295a679d', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01cb3102-26f7-559d-bad9-5cc5295a679d'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian news has been dominated by Russians criticizing Americans for criticizing Russians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/world/europe/07russia.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian news has been dominated by Russians criticizing Americans for criticizing Russians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW \x97 There are few things that Russian politicians like less than being scolded about democracy and human rights, and over the last week, since the police arrested top opposition leaders at a New Year’s Eve protest, the news cycle has been dominated by Russians criticizing Americans for criticizing Russians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/world/07RUSSIA/07RUSSIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': No