e after never getting the chance to do so at her trial in Rome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial Over, Former Getty Curator Speaks Out', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'True, Marion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T18:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5ab5565-51af-5875-ad1f-056e3204e6e2', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5ab5565-51af-5875-ad1f-056e3204e6e2'}, {'abstract': 'Guido Westerwelle sought to bolster Chancellor Angela Merkel’s center-right coalition, which has been dragged down in opinion polls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/world/europe/07germany.html', 'snippet': 'Guido Westerwelle sought to bolster Chancellor Angela Merkel’s center-right coalition, which has been dragged down in opinion polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN \x97 Defying calls for his resignation, Foreign Minister Guido Westerwelle went on the offensive Thursday in a speech aimed at quashing dissent while warning of a drift leftward if supporters failed to rally around his Free Democrats party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/world/07germany_337/07germany_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702,