es for watching 3-D television.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/3-d-glasses-the-designer-version/', 'snippet': 'Marchon is making designer frame glasses for watching 3-D television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — If the goofy glasses are preventing you from buying a 3-D TV,\xa0 Marchon, which makes glasses under the Fendi, Coach and Lacoste labels, among others, wants to help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3-D Glasses, the Designer Version', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T18:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f3dc96-91f4-58e8-9d84-00c651ff03f6', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f3dc96-91f4-58e8-9d84-00c651ff03f6'}, {'abstract': 'She will create and host a show about financial problems.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/suze-orman-signs-on-to-winfreys-channel/', 'snippet': 'She will create and host a show about financial problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another one of Oprah Winfrey‘s friends is joining her new cable channel. OWN, the channel that started up last weekend, said Thursday that Suze Orman (pictured) would create a show called “Money Class,” featuring advice for people in financial straits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suze Orman Signs On to Winfrey’s Channel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orman, Suze', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oprah Winfrey Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T18:48:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a681bd2b-eec0-5f16-abba-a6c5be568202', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a681bd2b-eec0-5f16-abba-a6c5be568202'}, {'abstract': 'As lawmakers read the Constitution inside the Capitol, a group outside rallies for an amendment protecting the rights of women.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/action-urged-on-womens-rights-measure/', 'snippet': 'As lawmakers read the Constitution inside the Capitol, a group outside rallies for an amendment protecting the rights of women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As lawmakers recited the articles of the country’s founding document on the House floor Thursday, some women found themselves out in the cold – literally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Action Urged on Women’s Rights Measure', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janie Lorber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lorber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a498b3-80d8-55a9-80a2-2904ba57684d', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a498b3-80d8-55a9-80a2-2904ba57684d'}, {'abstract': '“Deadly Spin” is an evenhanded yet riveting account of the inner workings of the health care insurance industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/health/views/06chen.html', 'snippet': '“Deadly Spin” is an evenhanded yet riveting account of the inner workings of the health care insurance industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in 2007 I found myself riveted by a case playing out at the University of California, Los Angeles, the medical center where I trained and had once worked as a transplant surgeon. A 17-year-old girl named Nataline Sarkisyan was in desperate need of a transplant after receiving aggressive treatment that cured her recurrent leukemia but caused her liver to fail. Without a new organ, she would die in a matter of a days; with one, she had a 65 percent chance of surviving. Her doctors placed her on the liver transplant waiting list. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/health/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/health/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/05/health/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter/Deadly-Spin-Wendell-Potter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Insurers Put Profits Between Doctor and Patient', 'kicker': 'Doctor and Patient', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Insurers Put Profits Between Doctor and Patient', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd19f708-f353-5e4c-a9db-33b8db4735d8', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd19f708-f353-5e4c-a9db-33b8db4735d8'}, {'abstract': 'The secret to a great 36 hours on this small island off the tip of Florida is to make friends with the gregarious and outgoing locals. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/travel/1248069512636/36-hours-in-key-west.html', 'snippet': 'The secret to a great 36 hours on this small island off the tip of Florida is to make friends with the gregarious and outgoing locals. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'The secret to a great 36 hours on this small island off the tip of Florida is to make friends with the gregarious and outgoing locals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/06/travel/10740_1_36hours-keywest_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/06/travel/10740_1_36hours-keywest_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Key West', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:05:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'Shayla Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shayla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3b9875d1-38e4-5972-8be6-0a8e8110a8a3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3b9875d1-38e4-5972-8be6-0a8e8110a8a3'}, {'abstract': 'A new laptop runs cooler when it detects that it is sitting on your lap.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/hps-new-dm1-laptop-keeps-its-cool/', 'snippet': 'A new laptop runs cooler when it detects that it is sitting on your lap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — When HP set out to make a cool laptop computer, it was thinking literally. One of the standout features of the new compact sized HP Pavilion dm1 is that it is designed not to heat up while you have it sitting on your lap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HP’s New dm1 Laptop Keeps Its Cool', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laptop Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f3dc257-35b1-5e61-a4a2-36384461d9e4', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f3dc257-35b1-5e61-a4a2-36384461d9e4'}, {'abstract': 'Where to eat, shop and play on a weekend in the haven for artists and writers, chefs and hippies that is Key West, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/travel/09hours.html', 'snippet': 'Where to eat, shop and play on a weekend in the haven for artists and writers, chefs and hippies that is Key West, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KEY WEST, haven to artists and writers, chefs and hippies, is somehow more Caribbean than Floridian. The indie-minded transplants work hard to keep it that way. One-speed bicycles weave their way through colorful village streets, crammed with as many chickens as cars. Happy hour blends into dinner. And everything is oriented around the ocean, from the fish market-driven menus and the nautical-inspired art, to the sunrise worshipers who gather each dawn and the tipplers who wave goodbye at sunset. Be careful or you might just catch what islanders call “Keys disease” — a sudden desire to cut ties with home and move there.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/09HOURS3/09HOURS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/09HOURS3/09HOURS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/09HOURS3/09HOURS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/09HOURS3/09HOURS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/09HOURS3/09HOURS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Key West, Fla.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Key West, Fla.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Key West (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wildman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wildman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3b1990-dc86-58b4-9c77-a4689b98cc08', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3b1990-dc86-58b4-9c77-a4689b98cc08'}, {'abstract': 'Key West, haven to artists and writers, chefs and hippies, is somehow more Caribbean than Floridian. And the indie-minded transplants work hard to keep it that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/09/travel/20110109hours-keywest-ss.html', 'snippet': 'Key West, haven to artists and writers, chefs and hippies, is somehow more Caribbean than Floridian. And the indie-minded transplants work hard to keep it that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Key West, haven to artists and writers, chefs and hippies, is somehow more Caribbean than Floridian. And the indie-minded transplants work hard to keep it that way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/travel/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/04/travel/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/04/travel/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ/20110109HOURS-slide-CDYQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Weekend in Key West, Fla.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Key West (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:09:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4b7ab1c8-4c1c-59fa-84d4-02e43caea8fd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4b7ab1c8-4c1c-59fa-84d4-02e43caea8fd'}, {'abstract': 'In “Deadly Spin,” Wendell Potter describes the dark underbelly of the health care insurance industry.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/putting-profits-before-patients/', 'snippet': 'In “Deadly Spin,” Wendell Potter describes the dark underbelly of the health care insurance industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inherent conflict of interest in a health care system anchored by for-profit insurers lurks unspoken behind nearly every debate over reform. Few politicians dare to openly address the issue; but over the last year and a half, one unlikely individual has consistently reminded us of this moral dilemma: Wendell Potter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Profits Before Patients', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cigna Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:10:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1aed206-6eeb-5f8f-abe6-abb87e395bd0', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1aed206-6eeb-5f8f-abe6-abb87e395bd0'}, {'abstract': 'Verizon Wireless did not introduce an iPhone running on its wireless network, as many had hoped, but rather sketched out a broad vision for the future of the network and company.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/no-iphone-but-star-trek-future-from-verizon/', 'snippet': 'Verizon Wireless did not introduce an iPhone running on its wireless network, as many had hoped, but rather sketched out a broad vision for the future of the network and company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Those expecting Ivan Seidenberg, the chairman and chief executive of Verizon Communications, to pull out a gleaming iPhone from his pocket during the opening keynote of the Consumer Electronics Show can stop holding their breath.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No iPhone, but ‘Star Trek’ Future From Verizon', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c77847-61b7-5936-ab6c-17397808235e', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c77847-61b7-5936-ab6c-17397808235e'}, {'abstract': 'The new speaker says his promise of ‘a more open process’ comes with a few qualifications.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/an-open-house-or-not-boehner-explains/', 'snippet': 'The new speaker says his promise of ‘a more open process’ comes with a few qualifications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like the Democrats did before him, Speaker John A. Boehner has promised to run a much more open House and to give the Democratic minority plenty of room to offer amendments on the floor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Open House or Not? Boehner Explains', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5fef9dc-c3c9-5c19-817b-6783ea1a1628', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5fef9dc-c3c9-5c19-817b-6783ea1a1628'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets lineman D’Brickashaw Ferguson is well known for his meticulous preparation, watching as much film as his coaches and developing his own theories on how to stop opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/sports/football/07jets.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets lineman D’Brickashaw Ferguson is well known for his meticulous preparation, watching as much film as his coaches and developing his own theories on how to stop opponents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. \x97 Bill Callahan conducts meetings for the Jets’ offensive linemen because he is, after all, the team’s offensive line coach. But he invites feedback at these meetings, and one player in particular is apparently not shy about taking on Callahan as if he were a defensive end.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/07jets/07jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/07jets/07jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/07jets/07jets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/07jets/07jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/07jets/07jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jet Earns Stellar Marks as a Student of the Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jet Earns Stellar Marks as a Student of the Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value'