but at a time of skyrocketing transportation costs, drivers in the outer boroughs are getting a rare reprieve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drivers Benefit as City Holds Off on Raising Some Meter Fees', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:21:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/20f49aee-a041-5be1-92b1-4c2454e51baa', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20f49aee-a041-5be1-92b1-4c2454e51baa'}, {'abstract': 'The appearance of Joachim Levy in the “Exit Through the Gift Shop” saga raises even more questions about the authenticity of the Banksy documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/banksy-truth-and-the-third-man/', 'snippet': 'The appearance of Joachim Levy in the “Exit Through the Gift Shop” saga raises even more questions about the authenticity of the Banksy documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to get lost in a hall of art-house mirrors when thinking (or writing) about “Exit Through the Gift Shop,” better known as the Banksy documentary. The pseudonymous British street artist has emerged from the shadows a bit to promote the film – but he’s expressed surprise that people might think his work is a prank, even though, you know, that sort of comes with the territory of being an internationally known prankster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banksy, Truth and the Third Man', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':