b2e-bb1f-c583efe23ad0'}, {'abstract': 'One Police Plaza: Two suspects escaped, if only for a moment, and the Police Department was reminded of an important lesson.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/memo-keep-the-keys-from-the-prisoners/', 'snippet': 'One Police Plaza: Two suspects escaped, if only for a moment, and the Police Department was reminded of an important lesson.', 'lead_paragraph': ' There are thousands and thousands of arrests in New York City in any given year — and occasionally those taken into custody slip their shackles and flee. Sometimes they stay free for enough time for the episodes to become embarrassing black eyes for the New York Police Department. But sometimes, the moments of freedom are so fleeting that the news media never learn of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Memo: Keep the Keys From the Prisoners', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T19:51:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fdda3b9-9516-5094-a1b3-c96adfa51fff', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fdda3b9-9516-5094-a1b3-c96adfa51fff'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some of the places Marilyn Monroe spent time when she was in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/07/arts/20110107_monroe.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some of the places