ption of the Internet generation, whose knowledge is wide but shallow.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/pancake-people/', 'snippet': 'Description of the Internet generation, whose knowledge is wide but shallow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Description of the Internet generation, whose knowledge is wide but shallow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pancake People', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T20:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c843b10-0d88-5620-98be-d6e353cb632f', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c843b10-0d88-5620-98be-d6e353cb632f'}, {'abstract': 'Ellen Weiss, the senior vice president of news at National Public Radio, resigned Thursday at the conclusion of an internal investigation into the firing of senior news analyst Juan Williams.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/npr-executive-who-fired-juan-williams-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Ellen Weiss, the senior vice president of news at National Public Radio, resigned Thursday at the conclusion of an internal investigation into the firing of senior news analyst Juan Williams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ellen Weiss, the senior vice president for news at NPR whose quick firing of the senior news analyst Juan Williams last October ignited a political and public relations firestorm, resigned Thursday at the end of an internal investigation into the dismissal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 