iterature? In this lesson, students reflect on some of the reasons dystopian and post-apocalyptic stories appeal to young readers by engaging in one of six different activities. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Materials: Reflecting on Dystopian Themes in Young Adult Literature', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T20:19:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annissa Hambouz and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hambouz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb1828da-14d1-523a-83be-7691d1417bd2', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb1828da-14d1-523a-83be-7691d1417bd2'}, {'abstract': 'In a 2007 article for the journal Democracy, Gene Sperling  argued for “rising-tide economics.” He suggested that the central economic problem, at least before the financial crisis, was the disconnect between productivity and incomes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/gene-sperling-201/', 'snippet': 'In a 2007 article for the journal Democracy, Gene Sperling  argued for “rising-tide economics.” He suggested that the central economic problem, at least before the financial crisis, was the disconnect between productivity and incomes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In addition to the Gene Sperling links we provided before, Mr. Sperling — the new director of President Obama’s National Economic Council — also wrote a 2007 article for the journal Democracy in which he argued for “rising-tide economics.” He suggested that the central economic problem, at least before the financial crisis, was the disconnect between productivity and incomes. Businesses were becoming more productive, profits were rising, gross domestic product was growing — but many workers weren’t benefiting:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gene Sperling 201', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sperling, Gene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Economic Council', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T20:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/88bf8480-5a28-5a42-9b0b-60b842f08169', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88bf8480-5a28-5a42-9b0b-60b842f08169'}, {'abstract': 'The top two teams in the country, Auburn and Oregon, will play for the national title. Watch a video debate and then vote for the team you think will win.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/sports/ncaafootball/20110107-BCS-feature.html', 'snippet': 'The top two teams in the country, Auburn and Oregon, will play for the national title. Watch a video debate and then vote for the team you think will win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The top two teams in the country, Auburn and Oregon, will play for the national title. Watch a video debate an