oath of office. House leaders are trying to figure out what it will take to fix the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/two-missed-moment-to-solemnly-swear/', 'snippet': 'Two Republicans managed to miss the oath of office. House leaders are trying to figure out what it will take to fix the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Representative Pete Sessions, Republican of Texas, the man who served as chairman of the Republican Congressional Campaign Committee, and can claim a large portion of the credit for helping his party win the majority in the House, somehow managed to miss the Oath of Office on Wednesday. Apparently, so did Representative-elect Mike Fitzpatrick, a Republican from Pennsylvania. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Missed Moment to Solemnly Swear', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T20:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/081546df-6876-52a0-b1a6-2d30a565de19', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/081546df-6876-52a0-b1a6-2d30a565de19'}, {'abstract': 'Smart Kenmore appliances are coming from Sears.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/its-a-smart-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'Smart Kenmore appliances are coming from Sears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — How do you transform what is seen as a dated somewhat stodgy company into a retailer of cool?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s a Smart Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head