anks/', 'snippet': 'The latest addition to the growing Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is Holly Petraeus, the wife of Gen. David H. Petraeus, who will direct the Office of Servicemember Affairs.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:41 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Watchdog Builds Up Its Ranks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T21:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e89ef409-f8bf-5856-9aa9-53f7f938cf47', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e89ef409-f8bf-5856-9aa9-53f7f938cf47'}, {'abstract': 'Anita Rachvelishvili made her Metropolitan Opera debut in “Carmen” on Wednesday night, in a role she has already sung at La Scala.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/arts/music/07carmen.html', 'snippet': 'Anita Rachvelishvili made her Metropolitan Opera debut in “Carmen” on Wednesday night, in a role she has already sung at La Scala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the young Georgian mezzo-soprano Anita Rachvelishvili was nervous about making her Metropolitan Opera debut on Wednesday night in the title role of Bizet’s “Carmen,” she did not show it. She brought an ample, earthy voice and sensual lyricism to her performance, winning a hearty ovation. Her Don José was the tenor Roberto Alagna, who had sung the role to acclaim opposite Elina Garanca when this Richard Eyre production, effectively updated to Spain in the 1930s, was introduced on New Year’s Eve of 2009.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CARMEN/CARMEN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CARMEN/CARMEN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CARMEN/CARMEN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CARMEN/CARMEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CARMEN/CARMEN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Carmen, but Worldly Still', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Young Carmen, but Worldly Still', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Scala', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T21:02:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasi