e': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cfe5b4c-060e-5e18-9af6-65027e96f39e', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cfe5b4c-060e-5e18-9af6-65027e96f39e'}, {'abstract': 'Antigovernment protesters repulsed an attempt by the military to disperse them in fierce running battles filled with tear gas, gunfire and explosions in the worst political violence in nearly 20 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2010/04/11/world/20100411THAILAND2_index.html', 'snippet': 'Antigovernment protesters repulsed an attempt by the military to disperse them in fierce running battles filled with tear gas, gunfire and explosions in the worst political violence in nearly 20 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antigovernment protesters repulsed an attempt by the military to disperse them in fierce running battles filled with tear gas, gunfire and explosions in the worst political violence in nearly 20 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/11/world/20100411THAILAND2-S.JPG', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/11/world/20100411THAILAND2-S.JPG', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters and Police Clash in Bangkok', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T21:24:46+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d9c3a221-f9ad-519c-9601-88642f7b27e1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d9c3a221-f9ad-519c-9601-88642f7b27e1'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Gloria Cheng’s program at Le Poisson Rouge was characteristically adventurous and filled with meaningful interrelations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/arts/music/07cheng.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Gloria Cheng’s program at Le Poisson Rouge was characteristically adventurous and filled with meaningful interrelations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At home in Los Angeles the pianist Gloria Cheng is a celebrity: an invaluable new-music advocate and a preferred collaborator of composers like Pierre Boulez and Esa-Pekka Salonen. A review of a recital Ms. Cheng presented at the Colburn School of Performing Arts in September breathlessly conjured a heady, star-studded scene. But Ms. Cheng’s copious gifts are scarcely a mystery here, a point proved by the sizable, luminary-filled throng that assembled for one of her too infrequent New York appearances, at Le Poisson Rouge on Wednesday night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CHENG/CHENG-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CHENG/CHENG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/CHENG/CHENG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hues of Debussy in a Program Without Him', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head