ts/07kidrockers.html', 'snippet': 'The volume might be gentler and the show times earlier, but at Kidrockers concerts, there are no saccharine singalongs or wearying lyrics about wheels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A BRIGHT young man strode to the bar. He leaned in, pausing purposefully. “I want a Coke with 10 cherries,” he declared, slamming his fist. Leo Lorge, 7, was at the Living Room, a club on the Lower East Side, for a rock show \x97 not for a children’s concert, and certainly not for a plain old Coke. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07kidrockers_1/07kidrockers_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07kidrockers_1/07kidrockers_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07kidrockers_1/KIDROCKERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07kidrockers_1/KIDROCKERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07kidrockers_1/KIDROCKERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young and Restless, And Ready to Rock ’n’ Roll', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young and Restless, And Ready to Rock ’n’ Roll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Petrusich',