 of the iPad, 4G Vaporware and 3-D Television at the Consumer Electronics Show in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Just landed at the Consumer Electronics Show! Already, you can just feel the geekiness emitting like gamma rays from the huge convention centers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At C.E.S., the Geekiness Is Palpable', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/120939a6-ae45-5272-a55b-6248cdc9338d', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120939a6-ae45-5272-a55b-6248cdc9338d'}, {'abstract': 'Bill O’Reilly, the conservative Fox News host, will interview President Obama as part of the Fox network’s pre-game Super Bowl coverage on Feb. 6.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/bill-oreilly-to-interview-president-obama/', 'snippet': 'Bill O’Reilly, the conservative Fox News host, will interview President Obama as part of the Fox network’s pre-game Super Bowl coverage on Feb. 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s pre-Super Bowl interviewers have been Matt Lauer, in 2009, and Katie Couric, in 2010. This year he’ll add to that list — Bill O’Reilly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill O’Reilly to Interview President Obama', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Reilly, Bill", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:31:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/132eac23-8d64-570f-9649-3ff97ed1ac82', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/132eac23-8d64-570f-9649-3ff97ed1ac82'}, {'abstract': 'Tackiness beyond compare.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/the-repeal-the-senior-murdering-secret-muslim-president-act/', 'snippet': 'Tackiness beyond compare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wish I could work up some more outrage about the willingness of Republicans to simply ignore the CBO’s verdict that repealing the Affordable Care Act, aka Obamacare, aka Romneycare, would increase the budget deficit. But anyone who had been following the politics here, not just this year, but for the past 15 years at least knew this was coming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Repeal the Senior-Murdering Secret Muslim President Act', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/034c782d-6458-5cda-a2dd-63b153b59d8d', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034c782d-6458-5cda-a2dd-63b153b59d8d'}, {'abstract': 'A “soul sonic superstar” diva, part motivational speaker, takes the stage at Soho Rep, punctuating jazz-inflected grooves with strutting dance breaks and regal poses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/theater/reviews/07jomama.html', 'snippet': 'A “soul sonic superstar” diva, part motivational speaker, takes the stage at Soho Rep, punctuating jazz-inflected grooves with strutting dance breaks and regal poses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pop-cultural anthropologists have spent ample ink tracking the evolution of the American diva over the last three decades, from the coronation of the melisma queens (Whitney Houston, Mariah Carey) through the rampage of the sex kittens (Britney Spears, Christina Aguilera) to the deification of the love warrior (Beyoncé) and on to the current reign of hook-driven power-pop princesses (Lady Gaga, Rihanna, Katy Perry).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07jomama_1/jomama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07jomama_1/jomama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07jomama_1/jomama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Hiatus From the Swiss Goats', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Jomama Jones: Radiate'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea