ial': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/11e3d660-3dff-527a-9399-7a8e533d2d74', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11e3d660-3dff-527a-9399-7a8e533d2d74'}, {'abstract': 'Gwyneth Paltrow plays an alcoholic country-western star in Shana Feste’s new film, “Country Strong.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/movies/07country.html', 'snippet': 'Gwyneth Paltrow plays an alcoholic country-western star in Shana Feste’s new film, “Country Strong.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The corn is as high as a mechanical bull’s eye in “Country Strong,” a runny-mascara melodrama about a country-western superstar warbling, weeping and wailing her way back from another stint in rehab to the glare of the stage. Gwyneth Paltrow, working a deep-fried accent and a strategically conspicuous cross necklace, plays Kelly Canter, a high-profile train wreck who, in the wake of a disastrous tour and an alcohol-induced miscarriage, heads back on the road in hopes of setting her life and career straight. As they apparently like to say in Hollywood (still!), the only successful woman is a desperately unhappy woman.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07country_1/COUNTRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07country_1/COUNTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07country_1/COUNTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Am Woman. Hear Me Sob, Y’All.', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Country Strong'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Am Woman. Hear Me Sob, Y’All.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 