6'}, {'abstract': 'A pampered parakeet at the Whitney, and MoMA prepares to give de Kooning an entire floor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/arts/design/07VOGEL.html', 'snippet': 'A pampered parakeet at the Whitney, and MoMA prepares to give de Kooning an entire floor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museum curators routinely face all kinds of challenges: delicate works of art that need special attention, fragile artist egos that require careful stroking, unwilling lenders who need convincing. At the Whitney Museum of American Art right now there is a particularly unusual character, requiring attention 24/7. It’s Peetie, a blue parakeet that is having something of a star moment on the fifth floor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/JP-VOGEL-2/JP-VOGEL-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cat Is Stuffed, but the Bird Is Real', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cat Is Stuffed,\nBut the Bird Is Real', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Kooning, Willem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3b5706-11c7-5335-b536-7508b6a5a6d1', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3b5706-11c7-5335-b536-7508b6a5a6d1'}, {'abstract': 'The guitarist Marc Ribot, joined on Wednesday night by Juan Medrano Cotito and La Cumbiamba eNeYé, began his monthlong residency at Le Poisson Rouge on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/arts/07ribot.html', 'snippet': 'The guitarist Marc Ribot, joined on Wednesday night by Juan Medrano Cotito and La Cumbiamba eNeYé, began his monthlong residency at Le Poisson Rouge on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first stretch of an extended evening at Le Poisson Rouge on Wednesday, Marc Ribot sat curled around his acoustic guitar in a fog of righteous solitude. His opener, “Bateau,” came on like a cold current of air, with tremulous fingerpicking in a slow-swirling, immaterial tempo. The brittle melody that surfaced, with its classical intimations, was set against a yawning low drone on a slack-tuned open string. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07ribot_1/RIBOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07ribot_1/RIBOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07ribot_1/RIBOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Solitary Stroll Gives Way to a Full-Band Excursion', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Solitary Stroll Gives Way to a Full-Band Excursion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T22:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nat