.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global influence of blockbuster movies on the collective psyche of humanity is awesome, if not terrifying, to contemplate. Much ink has been devoted to analyzing the social effects \x97 usually viewed as pernicious \x97 of popular cinema, and that thinking has spilled over into contemporary art. Andy Warhol, Cindy Sherman, Douglas Gordon and many other artists have made the Hollywood feature an object of skeptical scrutiny.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07moffatt_1/MOFFATT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07moffatt_1/MOFFATT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07moffatt_1/MOFFATT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Made Up of Movies Tells a Story All Its Own', 'kicker': 'Last Chance | Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Made Up of Movies Tells a Story All Its Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Museum of the Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moffatt, Tracey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T23:16:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati