076ce660-60a2-5eb7-8a20-50cf11b4ed3a'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. is interested in several issues, including the structure of the Facebook deal and media reports about the offering, according to people with direct knowledge of the inquiry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/s-e-c-questions-goldman-on-offering/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. is interested in several issues, including the structure of the Facebook deal and media reports about the offering, according to people with direct knowledge of the inquiry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission has contacted Goldman Sachs about the private offering of Facebook shares to Goldman Sachs’s clients, according to a document sent to potential investors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Questions Goldman Sachs on Offering', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T23:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/91bd6618-4267-5540-88e0-4034c46f1fd2', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91bd6618-4267-5540-88e0-4034c46f1fd2'}, {'abstract': 'In its performance of “Being Harold Pinter,” the Belarus Free Theater confirms the power of a single playwright to inspire those who are addressing abuses of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/theater/reviews/07pinter.html', 'snippet': 'In its performance of “Being Harold Pinter,” the Belarus Free Theater confirms the power of a single playwright to inspire those who are addressing abuses of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A playwright’s legacy throbs with anguished, enduring life in “Being Harold Pinter,” a work of harrowing intensity and commitment from the Belarus Free Theater at La MaMa, part of the Under the Radar Festival of experimental theater that began this week. Tracing the relationship between power and violence in the works of Pinter, who died in 2008, this production out of Eastern Europe is both dismaying and extraordinarily heartening.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07pinter_1/PINTER-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07pinter_1/PINTER-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/arts/07pinter_1/PINTER-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Theater, Brought to You by the Politically Powerless', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Being Harold Pinter'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Theater, Brought to You By the Politically Powerless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belarus Free Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinter, Harold', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T23:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/52c047d5-5954-5b1a-ae17-26b18dbbb669', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52c047d5-5954-5b1a-ae17-26b18dbbb669'}, {'abstract': 'Milestones in sonic marriages over the past 104 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/01/09/magazine/mashup-timeline.html', 'snippet': 'Milestones in sonic marriages over the past 104 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milestones in sonic marriages over the past 104 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Recombinant DNA of the Mash-Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T23:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a8490736-c030-5d54-a983-c83a2becafc5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a8490736-c030-5d54-a983-c83a2becafc5'}, {'abstract': 'Gregg Gillis — a k a Girl Talk — doesn’t sing or play an instrument. On the plus side, he has 50 years of music history to plunder. And throngs of sweaty, adoring fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/magazine/09GirlTalk-t.html', 'snippet': 'Gregg Gillis — a k a Girl Talk — doesn’t sing or play an instrument. On the plus side, he has 50 years of music history to plunder. And throngs of sweaty, adoring fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine old, bald Pete Townshend shuffling gingerly onstage as a synth burbles up behind him — “Let My Love Open the Door.” Now imagine the rapper Pimp C already on that stage, in a white fur suit and hat, holding up four fingers to show off his bling. A kick line of girls in black minishorts walks it out for DJ Unk, who’s rapping about a kick line of girls, then Levon Helm appears on a drum riser to chirp out “The Weight.” Also onstage: Jay-Z, Black Sabbath, Rick Springfield, Kesha, Bruce Springsteen, Miley Cyrus, the Ramones and Tupac and Biggie Smalls (both back from the dead) and hundreds more. In the audience are a few thousand fans jammed together beneath a blinding light show, waving their arms as rolls of toilet paper and explosions of confetti fall around them. You sense they’re feeling the same freedom, daring and camaraderie that they might at a house party when someone’s parents are away. This is pretty much the state of affairs at a Girl Talk show these days.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09girltalk_span/09girltalk_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09girltalk_span/09girltalk_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09girltalk_span/09girltalk_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09girltalk_span/09girltalk_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/magazine/09girltalk_span/09girltalk_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 373-Hit Wonder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 373-Hit Wonder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girl Talk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-06T23:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Lazar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lazar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1760c8a3-23b2-5305-a27f-5956545b7050', 'word_count': 2963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1760c8a3-23b2-5305-a27f-5956545b7050'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Sifton’s article on making the Filipino national dish shot toward the top of the most-emailed list.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/how-do-you-make-adobo/', 'snippet': 'Sam Sifton’s article on making the Filipino national dish shot toward the top of the most-emailed list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday morning, nytimes.com published my article about cooking the Filipino dish chicken adobo. By Thursday night my inbox was flooded with responses, most of them offering emendations to the recipe that accompanied the column, which was based on the excellent adobo prepared at a Brooklyn restaurant, Purple Yam. You must use peppercorns! You cannot use soy sauce! Fish is best, or chicken, or pork. It’s better the next day. It’s worse the next day. You must do this to the rice. Or that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Make Adobo?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker'