/07/business/economy/07debt.html', 'snippet': 'The government could run out of cash to pay its bills as early as March if the debt limit is not increased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The Obama administration warned Congress on Thursday that the government would reach its legal borrowing limit as early as the end of March and no later than May 16 and urged House and Senate leaders to move quickly to raise the debt ceiling to avoid an unprecedented default.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geithner Asks Congress to Raise U.S. Debt Limit Quickly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Geithner Asks Congress to Raise U.S. Debt Limit Quickly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T00:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f560f0f-17bf-537a-b9c5-7c41ec350b35', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f560f0f-17bf-537a-b9c5-7c41ec350b35'}, {'abstract': 'Panasonic is showing off a prototype tablet intended to work in tandem with its Internet-connected television platform.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/a-tablet-for-panasonics-television/', 'snippet': 'Panasonic is showing off a prototype tablet intended to work in tandem with its Internet-connected television platform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — If the two prevailing themes at this year’s Consumer Electronics Show have been Internet-connected televisions and tablet computers, then Panasonic is aiming to kill both birds with one stone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tablet for Panasonic’s Television', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Panasonic Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T00:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/143f9fed-d018-5d4e-8ec1-57847f426461', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143f9fed-d018-5d4e-8ec1-57847f426461'}, {'abstract': 'A United States attorney and others debunked the argument that R. Allen Stanford is not fit to stand trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/business/07stanford.html', 'snippet': 'A United States attorney and others debunked the argument that R. Allen Stanford is not fit to stand trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON \x97 R.