ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a62e43a9-1bf4-5a50-aa3c-dad21d7763ff', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a62e43a9-1bf4-5a50-aa3c-dad21d7763ff'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates announced Thursday that he had recommended Gen. Martin E. Dempsey to be nominated as Army chief of staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/us/07brfs-GENERALRECOM_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates announced Thursday that he had recommended Gen. Martin E. Dempsey to be nominated as Army chief of staff.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates announced Thursday that he had recommended Gen. Martin E. Dempsey to be nominated as Army chief of staff. General Dempsey, now overseeing all Army training and doctrine, served two tours during the war in Iraq: as division commander in Baghdad and as senior officer for efforts to train Iraqi security forces. His past assignments include acting commander at the Central Command, which controls all American military forces in the Middle East. THOM SHANKER', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Recommended for Army Post', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'General Recommended for Army Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d498e329-c84c-5ce4-af17-687c34113a7a', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d498e329-c84c-5ce4-af17-687c34113a7a'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department announced the indictment of a former Central Intelligence Agency officer accused of giving classified information to a reporter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/us/07indict.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department announced the indictment of a former Central Intelligence Agency officer accused of giving classified information to a reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department on Thursday announced the indictment of a former Central Intelligence Agency officer who is accused of disclosing classified information to a reporter, in the latest example of a crackdown by the Obama administration on leaking to journalists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-C.I.A. Officer Named in Disclosure Indictment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-C.I.A. Officer Named In Disclosure Indictment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ffb5af0-144d-558b-b4c1-78cf5e176358', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ffb5af0-144d-558b-b4c1-78cf5e176358'}, {'abstract': 'The outdoor spectacle and a subsequent indoor game served as reminders that live hockey is a visual treat, but why must there be reminders?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/sports/hockey/07vecsey.html', 'snippet': 'The outdoor spectacle and a subsequent indoor game served as reminders that live hockey is a visual treat, but why must there be reminders?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The invigorating sight of hockey players in their gaudy outfits flitting through the wintry gloom \x97 outdoors \x97 has become an annual ritual on New Year’s Day, in only four years. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pond or Rink, Rangers Create Their Own Winter Classic', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pond or Rink, Rangers Create Their Own Winter Classic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3edc069-3104-562d-bd8d-f50e06c1e0ab', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3edc069-3104-562d-bd8d-f50e06c1e0ab'}, {'abstract': 'Diana Rutherford, 20, is living and working at Covenant House New York and increasing her mastery of cooking with an eye toward finding an apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/nyregion/07neediest.html', 'snippet': 'Diana Rutherford, 20, is living and working at Covenant House New York and increasing her mastery of cooking with an eye toward finding an apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Standing behind a long stainless-steel counter in a commercial kitchen, Diana Rutherford deftly chops a pile of carrots. Her eyes, traced with black liner and lids dusted with powdery blues and gold, are focused. Her teeth grab at a pin that pierces her lower lip as she concentrates on each cut. A tattoo on her hand is a reminder of the past: a teardrop for her deceased brother, five dots for the brothers still living, a cross for her faith, and the letters “SL” for St. Louis, the city where she made a commitment to a life outside the religious sect of her youth. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/nyregion/ALT-NEEDIEST/ALT-NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/nyregion/ALT-NEEDIEST/ALT-NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/nyregion/ALT-NEEDIEST/ALT-NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Chef in a Quest to Become Independent', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Chef In a Quest To Become Independent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Covenant House', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bruderhof', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/176d4500-18aa-52fa-93dc-48f744362881', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/176d4500-18aa-52fa-93dc-48f744362881'}, {'abstract': 'A report by a Bloomberg administration task force calls for de-emphasizing civil service exams in hiring and ending seniority as the determinant in teacher layoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/nyregion/07civil.html', 'snippet': 'A report by a Bloomberg administration task force calls for de-emphasizing civil service exams in hiring and ending seniority as the determinant in teacher layoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bloomberg administration will call on Friday for far-reaching changes to the state’s 127-year-old civil service system governing New York City’s work force, including de-emphasizing civil service exams in hiring municipal workers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City to Press for Easing of Civil Service Requirements', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City to Press for Easing of Civil Service Requirements', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Municipal Labor Committee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seniority Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00d3bd9e-8630-5e4c-9616-abb05d161238', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00d3bd9e-8630-5e4c-9616-abb05d161238'}, {'abstract': 'A company has decided that patients in some states will no longer be covered by the end of this month.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/medicare-coverage-for-breast-cancer-drug-ends-in-some-states/', 'snippet': 'A company has decided that patients in some states will no longer be covered by the end of this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breast cancer patients in some states may soon lose Medicare coverage for the expensive drug Avastin, after the Food and Drug Administration’s decision to revoke the drug’s approval for that disease. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Coverage for Breast Cancer Drug Ends in Some States', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avastin (Drug)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genentech Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T01:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/74b57b03-16c8-5a6b-a818-17056aede14d', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b57b03-16c8-5a6b-a818-17056aede14d'}, {'abstract': 'The South wasn’t the only part of the Union contemplating secession in January 1861. So was New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/first-south-carolina-then-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The South wasn’t the only part of the Union contemplating secession in January 1861. So was New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of South Carolina’s vote to secession in late December 1860, Americans both North and South anxiously wondered which state would be next to leave the Union. Little did they realize that the next call for secession would come not from a Southern state, but from a Northern city — New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First South Carolina. Then New York?', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cotton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T02:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Lockwood and Charles Lockwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lockwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lockwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c65680-3d02-54f7-adf7-a5ddcd400d3f', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c65680-3d02-54f7-adf7-a5ddcd400d3f'}, {'abstract': 'Why are we cheering Hugh Hefner’s engagement?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/06/last-call-at-the-bunny-roundup/', 'snippet': 'Why are we cheering Hugh Hefner’s engagement?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s just get this out of the way before the new year is all backed up with highly consequential events of much greater urgency: Hugh Hefner is repulsive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Call at the Bunny Roundup', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hefner, Hugh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T02:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c62723-f63d-5be2-a510-1ec44249adf6', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c62723-f63d-5be2-a510-1ec44249adf6'}, {'abstract': 'The Big Three automakers have made strides in fuel economy but still rely on light trucks and S.U.V.’s for profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/business/07green.html', 'snippet': 'The Big Three automakers have made strides in fuel economy but still rely on light trucks and S.U.V.’s for profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WAYNE, Mich. \x97 Ten years ago, the Ford Motor plant here churned out giant Expedition and Navigator sport utility vehicles that got 12 miles to the gallon \x97 and it was one of the most profitable auto factories in the world.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/business/7GREEN1/7GREEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/07/business/7GREEN1/7GREEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}},