m her job over disparaging comments she made about Jews, she can add her own name to that list.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helen Thomas Returns, With Smaller Audience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helen Thomas Returns, With Smaller Audience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Helen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T03:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9ce290f-ec7e-5c35-a5fc-fcd5f7def67b', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9ce290f-ec7e-5c35-a5fc-fcd5f7def67b'}, {'abstract': 'Defensive tackle Eric LeGrand, who was paralyzed below the neck, now has sensation throughout his body and movement of his shoulders, Rutgers said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/sports/ncaafootball/07rutgers.html', 'snippet': 'Defensive tackle Eric LeGrand, who was paralyzed below the neck, now has sensation throughout his body and movement of his shoulders, Rutgers said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the days after Rutgers defensive tackle Eric LeGrand was paralyzed below the neck from a spinal cord injury, Coach Greg Schiano and members of the program spoke hopefully about how LeGrand would one day lead the Scarlet Knights onto the field.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/07/sports/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',