chott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b4996db-5a3c-51e3-8bf0-733af0bbf2c5', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b4996db-5a3c-51e3-8bf0-733af0bbf2c5'}, {'abstract': 'Two Chinese banks said Friday that they would need to raise money to meet new capital requirements, as lenders try to buffer their balance sheets against risk.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/china-banks-seek-funds-to-pad-capital-ratio/', 'snippet': 'Two Chinese banks said Friday that they would need to raise money to meet new capital requirements, as lenders try to buffer their balance sheets against risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Chinese banks said Friday that they would need to raise money to meet new capital requirements, as the lenders look to buffer their balance sheets against risk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Banks Seek Funds to Pad Capital Ratio', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Agricultural Bank of China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T10:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b78c86e-b26e-5cf2-835b-aa586790b878', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b78c86e-b26e-5cf2-835b-aa586790b878'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Is the paranormal an appropriate field for scientific study?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/do-you-believe-in-esp/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Is the paranormal an appropriate field for scientific study?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The psychology community is engaged in a debate over the appropriateness of publishing studies that appear to show evidence for extrasensory perception in a scholarly journal. Do you think it’s possible to scientifically study what is by definition extraordinary? And, do you believe in ESP and clairvoyance? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Believe in ESP?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T10:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d1e5088-86ee-5585-84ec-f579802e5de2', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d1e5088-86ee-5585-84ec-f579802e5de2'}, {'abstract': 'Officials halted sales from thousands of farms after dioxin was found in some feed for chickens and pigs and as fears grew about how far contaminated food might have spread.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/world/europe/08dioxin.html', 'snippet': 'Officials halted sales from thousands of farms after dioxin was found in some feed for chickens and pigs and as fears grew about how far contaminated food might have spread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN \x97 German officials halted sales from 4,700 small farms on Friday and pulled millions of eggs from the shelves after dioxin was discovered in feed for chickens and pigs and the authorities announced that the contamination might have started months ago. The news set off a scramble in countries that import food from Germany, with two banning the sale of some animal products.', 'print_sectio