ct': 'Janice Shade and True Body Products turned down a request from Whole Foods — but are thriving anyway.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/more-of-everything-for-a-start-up-soap-maker/', 'snippet': 'Janice Shade and True Body Products turned down a request from Whole Foods — but are thriving anyway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last June, we published a case study that explored whether the natural soap maker True Body Products should add a scented offering. Janice Shade, True Body’s chief executive, feared that adding the line might alienate existing customers who are adamantly opposed to scented soaps, sometimes because of allergies. But the suggestion to add the scented soaps came from Ms. Shade’s North Atlantic region Whole Foods buyer, and Ms. Shade knew that a line extension would give her company the larger shelf presence it needed to increase sales, which were about $45,000 in 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Start-Up Soap Maker Starts to Get Traction', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a47cbbf-91b8-568e-8118-b05233675ee4', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a47cbbf-91b8-568e-8118-b05233675ee4'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to their achievements, Eli Manning’s far surpass those of Phil Simms at a comparable age, and it’s not even close.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.b