imedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Obama White House, Back to the Future', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Dick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Colin L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sperling, Gene', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Economic Council', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T12:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a4ed99-a838-50c3-a224-e471d845304b', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a4ed99-a838-50c3-a224-e471d845304b'}, {'abstract': 'If would be nice if people were courteous enough to leave empty the parking spaces they didn’t clear of snow.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/complaint-box-snow-code/', 'snippet': 'If would be nice if people were courteous enough to leave empty the parking spaces they didn’t clear of snow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The giant snowstorm in December rekindled the irritation that is felt by many homeowners in the New York area, who after spending hours digging their cars out of six-foot-high snowbanks and driving to pick up groceries, return home to find a strange car parked in that just-cleared curb space. This is, perhaps, a minor inconvenience compared with the plight of residents whose cars get snowed in and stay snowed in for days after a storm, but it is nonetheless frustrating on an interpersonal level.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Snow Code', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T12:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven P. Scalici', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Scalici', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2e1a31-3d38-501f-93fb-ed4d3a8ae738', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2e1a31-3d38-501f-93fb-ed4d3a8ae738'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase and Morgan Stanley won approval to form joint ventures to underwrite stock and bond offerings in China.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/jpmorgan-morgan-stanley-approved-to-form-chinese-joint-ventures/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase and Morgan Stanley won approval to form joint ventures to underwrite stock and bond offerings in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase and Morgan Stanley said on Friday that they had each won approval from Chinese regulators to form joint ventures in the country, potentially giving them a bigger role in China’s booming securities business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan and Morgan Stanley Win Approval for China Ventures', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value'