lore the qualities that make a classical composer great, maybe even the best of all time.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/top-10-composers-help-write-the-list/', 'snippet': 'In videos and posts on ArtsBeat over the next two weeks Anthony Tommasini will explore the qualities that make a classical composer great, maybe even the best of all time.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What makes great music great? There are lots of ways to answer. Here’s a playful approach: make a list of the Top 10 composers in history. A gimmick? Sure, but one worth using if you have to defend your choices. What goes into a decision to put certain composers on such a list or to keep them off? Should influence matter, or just the works themselves? What about popularity? Are there any objective criteria?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Composers: Help Write the List', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Johann Sebastian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T16:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf17717-9d8a-5aa1-8efb-13856db2b20e', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf17717-9d8a-5aa1-8efb-13856db2b20e'}, {'abstract': 'On average, Jews have higher levels of well-being than their counterparts of every other major faith in America, according to new data from the Gallup-Healthways Well-Being Index.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/american-jews-lead-the-happiest-lives/', 'snippet': 'On average, Jews have higher levels of well-being than their counterparts of every other major faith in America, according to new data from the Gallup-Healthways Well-Being Index.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On average, Jews have higher levels of well-being than their counterparts of every other major faith in America, according to new data from the Gallup-Healthways Well-Being Index.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Jews Lead the Happiest Lives', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T16:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbfd745f-362c-5c90-9fa8-c2b836f2c71b', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbfd745f-362c-5c90-9fa8-c2b836f2c71b'}, {'abstract': 'The Times Sports editor, Tom Jolly, backs the Atlanta Falcons to break through this year and earn the N.F.C. berth to Super Bowl XLV in Dallas', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/1248069532257/counterpoint-the-atlanta-falcons.html', 'snippet': 'The Times Sports editor, Tom Jolly, backs the Atlanta Falcons to break through this year and earn the N.F.C. berth to Super Bowl XLV in Dallas', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times Sports editor, Tom Jolly, backs the Atlanta Falcons to break through this year and earn the N.F.C. berth to Super Bowl XLV in Dallas', 'source'