g-for-diana-monica-ali-novel-imagines-a-future/', 'snippet': 'The author of “Brick Lane” ponders what might have been.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:17 p.m. | Updated LONDON – It might seem a curious marriage of author and subject. But the British writer Monica Ali’s coming novel tells the story of a fictional princess based on Diana, Princess of Wales, and imagines what might have happened had Diana not been killed in a car accident in Paris in 1997. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Different, Happy Ending for Diana? Monica Ali Novel Imagines a Future', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ali, Monica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diana, Princess of Wales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daily Mail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Scribner's, Charles, Sons", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T17:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f397e033-2304-5f54-abbc-232fb88bedf7', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f397e033-2304-5f54-abbc-232fb88bedf7'}, {'abstract': 'Volkswagen is mounting its first serious effort in decades to compete with the Japanese and Korean manufacturers that nearly drove it out of the U.S. market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/business/global/08volkswagen.html', 'snippet': 'Volkswagen is mounting its first seri