te index was up 2.3 percent for December, bringing the total gain for 2010 to 8.08 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'December was a big month for hedge funds, thanks in part to a sharp rally in stocks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strong Finish for Hedge Funds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jabre, Philippe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Raghavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raghavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4221cd37-04ea-5ee5-a2d2-c7d920cba36b', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4221cd37-04ea-5ee5-a2d2-c7d920cba36b'}, {'abstract': 'In a video interview, the Palestinian film director and actor goes in-depth about his particular brand of humor and the process of capturing the poetic art of comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/the-video-q-elia-suleiman-on-the-time-that-remains/', 'snippet': 'In a video interview, the Palestinian film director and actor goes in-depth about his particular brand of humor and the process of capturing the poetic art of comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It is a form of resistance to laugh, especially when you laugh in the face of oppression and authority,” said the Palestinian film director and actor Elia Suleiman in this week’s video interview. But the humor one creates “must be subtle and tender” like poetry, he explains, adding, “I’m not Borat.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Video Q | Elia Suleiman on ‘The Time That Remains’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joy Dietrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dietrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c2b81ca-77a4-5e81-b79e-fb86658b26a5', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c2b81ca-77a4-5e81-b79e-fb86658b26a5'}, {'abstract': 'A lofty perch in Upper Manhattan used to be saddled with a dangerous reputation, but today there is evidence that decades of community activism have paid off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/01/09/realestate/20110109liv_ss.html', 'snippet': 'A lofty perch in Upper Manhattan used to be saddled with a dangerous reputation, but today there is evidence that decades of community activism have paid off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lofty perch in Upper Manhattan used to be saddled with a dangerous reputation, but today there is evidence that decades of community activism have paid off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living Around | Morningside Park', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morningside Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/bcda19d1-b0d9-58ad-b817-ec6de97ed9fb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/bcda19d1-b0d9-58ad-b817-ec6de97ed9fb'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/weekend-fare-25/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New this week: Fedora, where the Montreal chef Mehdi Brunet-Benkritly takes an inventive bistro approach in the longtime Village haunt: 239 West Fourth Street (West 10th Street); (646) 449-9336. Fatty Johnson’s is Zakary Pelaccio’s temporary pop-up bar in the former Cabrito space: 50 Carmine Street (Bedford Street); (212) 929-5050.  And this weekend, Marcus Samuelsson’s recently opened Red Rooster Harlem (310 Lenox Avenue between 125th and 126th Streets) starts serving brunch from 11:30 a.m. to 3 p.m. A gospel singer will perform live at the restaurant during Sunday brunch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/789fb3b8-1157-51fa-b9b2-e44c7c46dd91', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789fb3b8-1157-51fa-b9b2-e44c7c46dd91'}, {'abstract': 'Evaluating the top clutch players in the N.B.A.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/identifying-the-n-b-a-s-top-clutch-players/', 'snippet': 'Evaluating the top clutch players in the N.B.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clutch performance in professional basketball has its own distinct mythology. The meaning of every action – each shot, foregone shot, pass and foregone pass – is dissected and analyzed to a ludicrous degree, primarily in an effort to better understand the stuff of which N.B.A. players are made. Does a certain star have “nerves of steel” or a “killer instinct?” Are they soft? Weak-minded? Descriptions such as these are thrown around disguised as absolutes, even though clutch play is often hopelessly tainted by perception bias. All it takes is one big shot to create a legend. Once a player establishes a reputation as a clutch scorer, it typically follows him to his grave, regardless of what that pesky legitimate evidence indicates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Identifying the N.B.A.’s Top Clutch Players', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd407fe-2990-552a-b9c4-630182065860', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd407fe-2990-552a-b9c4-630182065860'}, {'abstract': 'J.K. Rowling had been accused of copying from a book called “The Adventures of Willy the Wizard.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/federal-judge-makes-harry-potter-plagiarism-suit-disappear/', 'snippet': 'J.K. Rowling had been accused of copying from a book called “The Adventures of Willy the Wizard.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in New York has dismissed a lawsuit against J.K. Rowling, the author of the “Harry Potter” series, clearing Ms. Rowling of an accusation that she borrowed plotlines from a book by another British author, Adrian Jacobs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Judge Makes ‘Harry Potter’ Plagiarism Suit Disappear', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scholastic Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb01290c-6ad2-5dd1-a398-943e258f0466', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb01290c-6ad2-5dd1-a398-943e258f0466'}, {'abstract': 'After years of trailing overseas rivals, Detroit automakers are using stimulus money to develop electric cars that they hope will jump-start Michigan’s troubled economy.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/video-detroits-new-direction/', 'snippet': 'After years of trailing overseas rivals, Detroit automakers are using stimulus money to develop electric cars that they hope will jump-start Michigan’s troubled economy.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Detroit’s New Direction', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f07888d-78e8-5493-91f1-cdab3ace0b60', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f07888d-78e8-5493-91f1-cdab3ace0b60'}, {'abstract': 'James R. Doty, a former general counsel for the S.E.C., will head the agency’s oversight of corporate accounting.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/s-e-c-fills-accounting-board-vacancies/', 'snippet': 'James R. Doty, a former general counsel for the S.E.C., will head the agency’s oversight of corporate accounting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission on Friday named James R. Doty, a white-collar criminal defense attorney and former general counsel at the agency, the nation’s top accounting regulator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Appoints Head of Accounting Oversight Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b518bd5f-6fc5-5284-b779-ba98cd7f7ef8', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b518bd5f-6fc5-5284-b779-ba98cd7f7ef8'}, {'abstract': 'Afzal Hossain and Julie Nymann, new parents, bought and combined two apartments to better accommodate their live-in baby sitter, her mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/01/09/realestate/20110109habi_ss.html', 'snippet': 'Afzal Hossain and Julie Nymann, new parents, bought and combined two apartments to better accommodate their live-in baby sitter, her mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Afzal Hossain and Julie Nymann, new parents, bought and combined two apartments to better accommodate their live-in baby sitter, her mother.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Habitats | Jackson Heights, Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/6ca473f9-ac54-57c6-bbe5-531253d8cb09', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/6ca473f9-ac54-57c6-bbe5-531253d8cb09'}, {'abstract': 'Caserta, built to rival Versailles, is magnificent, breathtakingly so \x97 the swan song of Baroque architecture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/travel/09caserta.html', 'snippet': 'Caserta, built to rival Versailles, is magnificent, breathtakingly so \x97 the swan song of Baroque architecture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE is something subversively appealing about the Italian art of desecration — the use, or some would say, misuse of historic places and cultural treasures. So much of Italy is ancient, magnificent, priceless and also serviceable.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond2/Correspond2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 821, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond2/Correspond2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond2/Correspond2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Caserta, Italy', 'kicker': 'Impossible to Forget', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caserta, Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52afd0b9-76e1-576c-83b5-08e698a72a19', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52afd0b9-76e1-576c-83b5-08e698a72a19'}, {'abstract': 'Lago Todos los Santos, abutting the foothills of the Andes in southern Chile, is a place shifting colors and snow-capped volcanoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/travel/09chile.html', 'snippet': 'Lago Todos los Santos, abutting the foothills of the Andes in southern Chile, is a place shifting colors and snow-capped volcanoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN now, nearly four years after I first stood on its shores, Lago Todos los Santos, abutting the foothills of the Andes in southern Chile, sometimes invades my dreams. More than once, I have awakened with images of the lake’s constantly shifting colors and the snow-capped volcanoes and sweet-smelling forests that ring it still vivid in my head.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond1/Correspond1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond1/Correspond1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond1/Correspond1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond1/Correspond1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/travel/Correspond1/Correspond1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lago Todos los Santos, Chile', 'kicker': 'Impossible to Forget', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lago Todos los Santos, Chile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANDES MOUNTAINS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T19:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f6e7804-b3b7-5adb-ba93-854d60a237a9', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f6e7804-b3b7-5adb-ba93-854d60a237a9'}, {'abstract': 'A former Southeast Asia bureau chief recalls a visit to Phnom Penh in 1988, when the genocide was over, but Cambodia was still in mourning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/travel/09cambodia.html', 'snippet': 'A former Southeast Asia bureau chief recalls a visit to Phnom Penh in 1988, when the genocide was over, but Cambodia was still in mourning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was just a single day in Phnom Penh, one of many, but even now I can’t get it out of my head. The genocide was over \x97 Vietnam, the traditional enemy, had ended it by driving out the Khmer Rouge and setting up a collaborationist government. But in 1988, Cambodia was still mourning. So many people had died, and thousands of refugees, including those who had suffered from the Khmer Rouge and those loyal to it, lived in politicized border camps inside Thailand, waiting for a diplomatic settlement that never quite seemed to arrive.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/travel/Correspond5/Correspond5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/05/travel/Correspond5/Correspond5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi