 1978.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, this storm-tossed city will reach an impressive municipal milestone: the 17th consecutive day, stretching back to the bureaucratic observance of Christmas on Dec. 24, that alternate-side parking rules are suspended. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple of Weeks Without Parking Rules? Try a Couple Months', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T20:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f93bf7c-62ce-53e9-ab2c-2d93875a9d47', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f93bf7c-62ce-53e9-ab2c-2d93875a9d47'}, {'abstract': 'Does the white-cube environment in most museums and galleries dull the senses?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/artifacts-damn-white/', 'snippet': 'Does the white-cube environment in most museums and galleries dull the senses?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re so used to the white-cube environment of museums and galleries today that we hardly notice it. That’s the idea. Blank white walls are supposed to make it easier for viewers to focus on the artworks that hang on them. Sometimes that works, mostly for modern and contemporary art, which is often distracting enough. The general thinking seems to be that it won’t abide any competition from the institution showing it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | Damn White', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/925bc1c7-d4b6-5403-9108-cd4ccccabe4e', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/925bc1c7-d4b6-5403-9108-cd4ccccabe4e'}, {'abstract': 'The film has become a must-see for young ballet dancers, some of whom say it reflects the dark side of their art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan.html', 'snippet': 'The film has become a must-see for young ballet dancers, some of whom say it reflects the dark side of their art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARMELLA IMRIE spent six grueling hours last Wednesday mastering steps like the brisé and jeté battu for Keith Michael’s ballet “The Alice-in-Wonderland Follies.” But instead of going home to nurse her toes afterward, she and five other dancers with the New York Theater Ballet headed out to see “Black Swan.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan-span/09swan-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan-span/09swan-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan-span/SWAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan-span/09swan-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/fashion/09swan-span/09swan-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Some Dancers, ‘Black Swan’ Is a Cautionary Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Dancers, ‘Black Swan’ Is a Cautionary Tale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cf3cf61-c734-5daf-b606-f9fc14199d8b', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cf3cf61-c734-5daf-b606-f9fc14199d8b'}, {'abstract': 'Geologists preparing to leave Antarctica look ahead to a year of geochemical analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/rocks-zircon-zapping-and-a-big-shrimp/', 'snippet': 'Geologists preparing to leave Antarctica look ahead to a year of geochemical analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Goodge, left, a professor of geological sciences at the University of Minnesota-Duluth, and Jeff Vervoort, an isotope geochemist from Washington State University, are writing from their resea