reprint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit to reprint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chic in Review | Obama’s Latest Flip-Flop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Leon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e42e7d-5ba5-5c37-986f-f5b43aea98ea', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e42e7d-5ba5-5c37-986f-f5b43aea98ea'}, {'abstract': 'MTV said the “Jersey Shore” Season 3 premiere was watched by 8.45 million viewers, making it the network’s highest-rated series broadcast to date.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/jersey-shore-returns-and-mtv-rides-a-ratings-wave/', 'snippet': 'MTV said the “Jersey Shore” Season 3 premiere was watched by 8.45 million viewers, making it the network’s highest-rated series broadcast to date.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the third-season premiere of “Jersey Shore” on Thursday night, it was Deena Cortese, the newest addition to the beach house, who spent the episode repeatedly declaring herself a “blast in a glass.” But on Friday it was MTV that had cause to celebrate: it said the premiere had been watched by 8.45 million viewers, making it MTV’s highest-rated series broadcast to date. The Season 3 debut episode, in which Nicole Polizzi (alias Snooki), Mike Sorrentino (aka the Situation) and their catchphrase-coining pals returned to their abode in Seaside Heights, N.J., saw a ratings increase of 63 percent over the Season 2 premiere in July (when the orange-skinned cast traveled to Miami) and 36 percent over that season’s finale in October. The overall viewership for the latest “Jersey Shore” premiere at 10 p.m. even exceeded broadcast networks like ABC (which drew 7.8 million viewers for a “Private Practice” repeat) and NBC (which attracted just over two million for reruns of “The Office”). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jersey Shore’ Returns and MTV Rides a Ratings Wave', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polizzi, Nicole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/843a8cc8-711a-5370-a298-0b59b8a07858', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/843a8cc8-711a-5370-a298-0b59b8a07858'}, {'abstract': 'DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli talks to Scott Kessler, a research analyst at Standard & Poor’s, about whether Facebook, which just landed $450 million from Goldman Sachs, deserves its huge valuation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/is-facebook-worth-50-billion/', 'snippet': 'DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli talks to Scott Kessler, a research analyst at Standard & Poor’s, about whether Facebook, which just landed $450 million from Goldman Sachs, deserves its huge valuation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli talks to Scott Kessler, a research analyst at Standard & Poor’s, about whether Facebook, which just landed $450 millio