ac01', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d25cfd5c-0e8c-550e-aaf7-a54198a7ac01'}, {'abstract': 'Australian researchers found that breast-feeding for six months or more was associated with better performance at age 10 in math, reading, writing and spelling — but only for boys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/health/research/11childhood.html', 'snippet': 'Australian researchers found that breast-feeding for six months or more was associated with better performance at age 10 in math, reading, writing and spelling — but only for boys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yet another benefit of breast-feeding: improved academic performance later in childhood, at least for some children. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childhood: A Breast-Feeding Benefit, This One for Boys', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CHILDHOOD: A Breast-Feeding Benefit, This One for Boys', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8f4f349-f552-5678-b0f5-478b54e71522', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8f4f349-f552-5678-b0f5-478b54e71522'}, {'abstract': 'In a federal survey, 13 percent of pregnant women had high levels of cotinine, a biological indicator of tobacco exposure — and almost a quarter of them lied about it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/science/11baby.html', 'snippet': 'In a federal survey, 13 percent of pregnant women had high levels of cotinine, a biological indicator of tobacco exposure — and almost a quarter of them lied about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When pregnant women are asked if they smoke, almost a quarter of the smokers deny they have the habit.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smoking for Two, and Lying About It', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HAVING A BABY: Smoking for Two, and Lying About It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:45:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d379d0-47d7-5bfb-bbb6-6da22c4e80cf', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d379d0-47d7-5bfb-bbb6-6da22c4e80cf'}, {'abstract': 'The Compagnie Philippe Saire performed the American premiere of “Lonesome Cowboy” at the Joyce Theater on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/arts/dance/08saire.html', 'snippet': 'The Compagnie Philippe Saire performed the American premiere of “Lonesome Cowboy” at the Joyce Theater on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the five male dancers stood near the lip of the Joyce Theater’s stage after the American premiere of Philippe Saire’s “Lonesome Cowboy” on Thursday night, their bows might have been a continuation of the hourlong work’s themes about masculine group identity and behavior. Here they were, engaged in another ritualized activity, beholden to its mores and seeming at once proud, nervous and pleased.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/saire/saire-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/saire/saire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/saire/saire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Methods of Maleness, Kilts Included', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Methods Of Maleness, Kilts Included', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saire, Philippe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ac3ec2-6cd9-5c3a-9a66-9edcc19ab9ba', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ac3ec2-6cd9-5c3a-9a66-9edcc19ab9ba'}, {'abstract': 'Summers at Hedge Fund Conference | Wikileaks Readying Bank Data Release?| Jon Stewart on Facebook/Goldman', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/buzz-tracker-5/', 'snippet': 'Summers at Hedge Fund Conference | Wikileaks Readying Bank Data Release?| Jon Stewart on Facebook/Goldman', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why the Massachusetts Ruling Matters “Effectively this shows the shortcomings of the fundamental design of the securitization process, of developing a one-size-fits-all process when some states have long-standing law (real estate is very well settled) that is idiosyncratic,” says Yves Smith.Naked Capitalism', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buzz Tracker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e15c3374-1c75-58cf-8249-92bc8aef349d', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e15c3374-1c75-58cf-8249-92bc8aef349d'}, {'abstract': 'Xavier Joly and Emilie Johnson went to Harlem in search of a house like the one they had seen in the film “The Royal Tenenbaums.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/realestate/09hunt.html', 'snippet': 'Xavier Joly and Emilie Johnson went to Harlem in search of a house like the one they had seen in the film “The Royal Tenenbaums.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, as soon as Xavier Joly and Emilie Johnson returned from a three-year stay in Paris, they moved into a two-bedroom Upper West Side rental for $3,300 a month. Ms. Johnson would have been glad to remain there indefinitely, but Mr. Joly immediately began the hunt for something different.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4',