tv/', 'snippet': 'The return of “Jersey Shore” to MTV at 10 p.m. on Thursday crushed everything else on television in the audience most desired by advertisers, viewers between the ages of 18 and 49.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be unthinkable to some, but the evidence continues to suggest that the cast members of “ Jersey Shore” are among the biggest stars on television at the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jersey Shore’ Sets Ratings Record on MTV', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jersey Shore (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/221edb7b-3baa-54e3-8768-dfd2b6a33bda', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/221edb7b-3baa-54e3-8768-dfd2b6a33bda'}, {'abstract': 'New residential towers are changing the face of Downtown Brooklyn and bringing thousands of new residents to a once commercial area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/realestate/09cov.html', 'snippet': 'New residential towers are changing the face of Downtown Brooklyn and bringing thousands of new residents to a once commercial area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE view north across the East River from a high floor at Oro, a new 40-story condominium tower at 306 Gold Street in Downtown Brooklyn, is eye-popping, a panorama of clouds, bridges, water and skyscrapers in Manhattan. But gazing to the south and west from the same perch reveals a more traditional Brooklyn landscape: here a cluster of bank offices, there a line of cars at a Flatbush Avenue traffic light, set against a distant backdrop of low-rises and brownstones.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/cov-web/cov-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/cov-web/cov-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/cov-web/cov-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/cov-web/cov-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/cov-web/cov-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suddenly, a Brooklyn Skyline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suddenly, A Brooklyn Skyline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T21:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Mooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4242145-5691-5794-b648-9125084029cd', 'word_count': 1875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4242145-5691-5794-b648-9125084029cd'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, the agency charged a North Carolina money manager with defrauding investors of about $16 million, using some of the assets to buy a $4 million vacation home.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/s-e-c-claims-manager-used-funds-to-buy-vacation-home/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, the agency charged a North Carolina money manager with defrauding investors of about $16 million, using some of the assets to buy a $4 million vacation home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fund-of-funds manager Stanley Kowalewski seemed to have a penchant for real estate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Says Manager Used Funds to Buy Vacation Home', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cbfdda6-53e6-5b0b-92eb-61986669bfdd', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cbfdda6-53e6-5b0b-92eb-61986669bfdd'}, {'abstract': 'A lofty perch in Upper Manhattan used to be saddled with a dangerous reputation, but today there is evidence that decades of community activism have paid off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/realestate/09living.html', 'snippet': 'A lofty perch in Upper Manhattan used to be saddled with a dangerous reputation, but today there is evidence that decades of community activism have paid off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR decades, in spite of supporters who argued to the contrary, Morningside Park was saddled with a dangerous reputation: a haven for drug addicts, a no man’s land separating the ivy privilege of Columbia University, literally lofty on its perch, from the valley of Harlem below. Columbia students knew to avoid it. Lucy Martin-Gianino, an agent with the Corcoran Group who has sold homes along Morningside Drive, recalled crossing the park as a girl. “I thought, ‘This is the end of me,’ because it was dangerous territory.”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09livispan/09livispan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09livispan/09livispan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09livispan/09livispan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09livispan/09livispan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09livispan/09livispan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Name Evokes Dawn for a Reason', 'kicker': 'Living Around | Morningside Park', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Name Evokes Dawn for a Reason', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morningside Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'MORNINGSIDE PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Beyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74687827-26a8-53d8-9316-8dddf4833902', 'word_count': 1528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74687827-26a8-53d8-9316-8dddf4833902'}, {'abstract': 'Afzal Hossain and Julie Nymann bought and combined two apartments to accommodate their live-in baby sitter: her mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/realestate/09habi.html', 'snippet': 'Afzal Hossain and Julie Nymann bought and combined two apartments to accommodate their live-in baby sitter: her mother.', 'lead_paragraph': ' AFZAL HOSSAIN, a 34-year-old artist and architect who grew up in Bangladesh, has vivid childhood memories of women making kanthas, handmade quilts constructed of layers of fabrics from worn garments and lavishly encrusted with colorful embroidery. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09habispan/09habispan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/realestate/09habispan/09habispan-article