 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/028ee0ae-1238-5923-8109-032612a5ec10', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/028ee0ae-1238-5923-8109-032612a5ec10'}, {'abstract': 'Just because soba originally comes from Japan doesn’t mean it needs to stay there; pair the noodles with Arctic char and add some crunch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/dining/12appe.html', 'snippet': 'Just because soba originally comes from Japan doesn’t mean it needs to stay there; pair the noodles with Arctic char and add some crunch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY food rut of 2010 was soba. I was complacent, preparing it the same way every time by tossing the slender buckwheat strands with broth, scallions and sesame oil and then throwing a piece of seared salmon on top. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12appe-span/12appe-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12appe-span/12appe-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12appe-span/12appe-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12appe-span/12appe-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soba Sails From Japan', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soba Sails From Japan With an Arctic Blast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noodles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:16:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f377015a-b170-5b21-b1d2-7cab4c8fa29c', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f377015a-b170-5b21-b1d2-7cab4c8fa29c'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Adès’s “In Seven Days (Concerto for Piano With Moving Image),” performed with the Philharmonic, is a riveting, restless and kaleidoscopically colorful 30-minute orchestra piece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/arts/music/08gilbert.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Adès’s “In Seven Days (Concerto for Piano With Moving Image),” performed with the Philharmonic, is a riveting, restless and kaleidoscopically colorful 30-minute orchestra piece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Word must be getting around that when Alan Gilbert presents one of his ambitious contemporary-music projects at the New York Philharmonic, like the staged production of Ligeti’s bleakly comic opera “Le Grand Macabre” last season, these programs are not to be missed. So it was on Thursday night when Mr. Gilbert conducted the New York premiere of the British composer Thomas Adès’s “In Seven Days (Concerto for Piano With Moving Image).” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/Gilbert/Gilbert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 663, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/Gilbert/Gilbert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/arts/Gilbert/Gilbert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soundtrack for the Chaos, Light and Dark of Creation', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Soundtrack for the Chaos, Light and Dark of Creation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9926c36-7eac-5b98-81b4-0ad9431b40f1', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9926c36-7eac-5b98-81b4-0ad9431b40f1'}, {'abstract': 'In the new FX series, “Lights Out,” Holt McCallany portrays a former heavyweight champion returning to the ring and contending with his dysfunctional family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/arts/television/09lights.html', 'snippet': 'In the new FX series, “Lights Out,” Holt McCallany portrays a former heavyweight champion returning to the ring and contending with his dysfunctional family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN FX executives watched the pilot for “Lights Out,” their prospective boxing drama, they were mesmerized by the relative unknown Holt McCallany. He plays the former heavyweight champ Lights Leary as he begins a journey back into the ring while being pummeled by family strife, crushing debt, health issues and a deepening identity crisis. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/LIGHTS_span/LIGHTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/LIGHTS_span/LIGHTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/LIGHTS_span/LIGHTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/LIGHTS_span/LIGHTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/LIGHTS_span/LIGHTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Familial Discord? Enough to Back a Boxer in a Corner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Familial Discord? Enough to Back A Boxer in a Corner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leight, Warren', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T22:19:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '0', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6582708-3484-51b7-b8df-a57a1d340ba9', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6582708-3484-51b7-b8df-a57a1d340ba9'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Harbaugh, who guided Stanford to the Orange Bowl, became the coach of the San Francisco 49ers, following the career trajectory of his coaching idol, Bill Walsh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/sports/football/08harbaugh.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Harbaugh, who guided Stanford to the Orange Bowl, became the coach of the San Francisco 49ers, following the career trajectory of his coaching idol, Bill Walsh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a few days ago, Jim Harbaugh stood on the sideline at the Orange Bowl, leading the Stanford Cardinal to its first bowl victory in 14 years. His players carried Harbaugh off on their shoulders, and almost from the moment they set him down, N.F.L. owners and general managers, college presidents and boosters courted him. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-harbaugh/y-harbaugh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-harbaugh/y-harbaugh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-harbaugh/y-harbaugh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harbaugh Graduates to Coach the 49ers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harbaugh Graduates to Coach the 49