e': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4b27711-6512-5664-92b4-3d6c72d7a63b', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4b27711-6512-5664-92b4-3d6c72d7a63b'}, {'abstract': 'One of the latest photographic sensations on the Internet, Vivian Maier, did some of her best work in the 1950s.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/new-street-photography-60-years-old/', 'snippet': 'One of the latest photographic sensations on the Internet, Vivian Maier, did some of her best work in the 1950s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vivian Maier, evidently one of America’s more insightful street photographers, has at last been discovered. The release of every fresh image on the Web causes a sensation among the growing legion of her admirers. (Frankly, Lens is late to the table.) Ms. Maier’s streetscapes manage simultaneously to capture a redolent sense of place and the paradoxical moments that give the city its jazz, while elevating and dignifying the people in her frames — vulnerable, noble, defeated, proud, fragile, tender and often quite funny. Harry Callahan is just one of the masters with whom Ms. Maier is already being compared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Street Photography, 60 Years Old', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maier, Vivian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-07T23:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier