t': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b3f3ab-c34a-550b-8e47-0638485939f3'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with DealBook, Curtis Jackson, also known as 50 Cent, is bullish on social media and believes Facebook is worth $50 billion, maybe more.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/50-cent-facebook-is-worth-50-billion-maybe-more/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with DealBook, Curtis Jackson, also known as 50 Cent, is bullish on social media and believes Facebook is worth $50 billion, maybe more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Curtis Jackson, more commonly known as 50 Cent, has parlayed his career as a hip-hop artist into a multifaceted business and a tidy personal fortune. His minority investment in Glacéau turned into a windfall when Coca-Cola purchased the maker of Vitamin Water for $4.1 billion in 2007.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '50 Cent: Facebook Is Worth $50 Billion, Maybe More', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '50 CENT', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glaceau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5304bbe-c8cb-502f-9275-f3b1c25d1436', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5304bbe-c8cb-502f-9275-f3b1c25d1436'}, {'abstract': 'New desktop furniture like lamps can now incorporate wireless charging pads.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/teknions-magic-charging-lamp/', 'snippet': 'New desktop furniture like lamps can now incorporate wireless charging pads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have to admit, I haven’t been a huge fan of charging mats, those pads that recharge a phone’s batteries by just sitting it on the pad. One reason was that for them to work, you had to add some kind of clunky case to your phone or whatever you wanted to charge up. Another was, when not in use, the pad worthlessly took up a lot of desk space.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teknion’s Magic Charging Lamp', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:28:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0e20f0-95e7-5fbb-ae71-65f5f0ef55dd', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0e20f0-95e7-5fbb-ae71-65f5f0ef55dd'}, {'abstract': 'Slide Show: Subjects include New Year’s Eve, piled-up garbage, and a governor’s inauguration.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/the-week-in-pictures-for-jan-7/', 'snippet': 'Slide Show: Subjects include New Year’s Eve, piled-up garbage, and a governor’s inauguration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include New Year’s Eve, piled-up garbage, and a governor’s inauguration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for Jan. 7', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e696b51-5d21-5198-9bbc-818424c7cc59', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e696b51-5d21-5198-9bbc-818424c7cc59'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Reich, a home organizer to the rich, turned her personal neuroses into a successful business. “Some people don’t open their mail without me,” she said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09organizer.html', 'snippet': 'Barbara Reich, a home organizer to the rich, turned her personal neuroses into a successful business. “Some people don’t open their mail without me,” she said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLIDING into Susan Hitzig and Ken Yaffe’s apartment, in a doorman building off Central Park West, Barbara Reich did not waste time ogling the obvious: the sleek kitchen, the view of the American Museum of Natural History, the sophisticated living room bearing no trace of the couple’s three children. Instead, Ms. Reich peered into a closet, where she found mismatched hangers and decreed, “This is wrong.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/organize-1/organize-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/organize-1/organize-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/organize-1/organize-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/organize-1/organize-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Organize This!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Organize This!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Closets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orderliness and Clutter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elissa Gootman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gootman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f820d90-c59b-55c2-9f6a-0629d354c0fb', 'word_count': 1936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f820d90-c59b-55c2-9f6a-0629d354c0fb'}, {'abstract': 'Taking Questions: Barbara Reich, a professional organizer, will answer readers’ questions about eliminating clutter.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/ask-about-getting-organized/', 'snippet': 'Taking Questions: Barbara Reich, a professional organizer, will answer readers’ questions about eliminating clutter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the new year, often comes the resolution to toss out the old and get things in order. In this week’s Metropolitan section, Elissa Gootman of The Times writes about Barbara Reich, a professional organizer, who helped her do just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask About Getting Organized', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:38:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea74f265-a3c7-5e94-bad6-cf49d5a74f11', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea74f265-a3c7-5e94-bad6-cf49d5a74f11'}, {'abstract': 'An Egyptian blogger’s account of a vigil in Cairo to show solidarity with members of the Coptic Christian community, one week after a suicide bombing at a church.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/egyptian-bloggers-account-of-a-vigil-in-cairo/', 'snippet': 'An Egyptian blogger’s account of a vigil in Cairo to show solidarity with members of the Coptic Christian community, one week after a suicide bombing at a church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of Egyptians attended a candlelight vigil in downtown Cairo on Friday, the Coptic Christian Christmas, to show their solidarity with members of the Coptic community a week after a suicide bomber killed at least 21 people at a church in Alexandria during a New Year’s Eve Mass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Blogger’s Account of a Vigil in Cairo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/db054684-3d64-5ff9-b3e3-0c2b7313eb88', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db054684-3d64-5ff9-b3e3-0c2b7313eb88'}, {'abstract': 'Zagg, a company best known for its stick-on skins that protect phones, computers and other devices from dings and scratches, has come up with a thin lightweight Bluetooth keyboard for the iPad.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/zaggs-new-ipad-keyboard/', 'snippet': 'Zagg, a company best known for its stick-on skins that protect phones, computers and other devices from dings and scratches, has come up with a thin lightweight Bluetooth keyboard for the iPad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the chief knocks on the iPad is that while it’s great for consuming music, movies, and the Web, it’s crummy for producing anything, even simple documents. Largely that is because of the lack of a physical keyboard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zagg’s New iPad Keyboard', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:52:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6d49d3-10bb-5cb0-a347-9aa798418984', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6d49d3-10bb-5cb0-a347-9aa798418984'}, {'abstract': 'On Sundays, Henrik Lundqvist, the Swedish-born goaltender of the New York Rangers, relaxes at the movies or plays his guitar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09routine.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, Henrik Lundqvist, the Swedish-born goaltender of the New York Rangers, relaxes at the movies or plays his guitar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To be Henrik Lundqvist is to suit up. When the Swedish-born goaltender of the New York Rangers isn’t sporting Blueshirt No. 30, he may wear a dapper three-piece number. On Sundays, though, Mr. Lundqvist, 28 — who won a gold medal in the 2006 Winter Olympics blocking pucks for Sweden’s national hockey team — dresses down, relaxing at the movies or playing his guitar. He lives with his fiancée, Therese Andersson, 28, and their 4-year-old Doberman, Nova, in a two-bedroom duplex in the West 50s with a terrace and a hot tub. ELISA MALA ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE/09ROUTINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE/09ROUTINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE/09ROUTINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE/09ROUTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE/09ROUTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}]