. hoping for journalistic attention? There are just too many products announced at the show.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/07/c-e-s-a-bad-time-to-introduce-a-tech-product/', 'snippet': 'Why do companies come to C.E.S. hoping for journalistic attention? There are just too many products announced at the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I walk through the corridors of the Consumer Electronics Show, I’m frequently stopped by P.R. people hoping for a little journalistic attention. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'C.E.S.: A Bad Time to Introduce a Tech Product', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T00:55:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/51777643-71af-5800-ad82-9980ba803d6b', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51777643-71af-5800-ad82-9980ba803d6b'}, {'abstract': 'Experts say some firms are especially respectful of the work-life balance, and they are retaining valuable employees as a result.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/business/08perks.html', 'snippet': 'Experts say some firms are especially respectful of the work-life balance, and they are retaining valuable employees as a result.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the peak season for the nation’s accounting firms begins, David Leeds’s team at Ernst & Young is once again bracing for two months of 60-hour weeks auditing the books of a major bank in Atlanta.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/business/08perks/08perks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/08/business/08perks/08perks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/business/08perks/08perks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/business/08perks/08perks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/business/08perks/08perks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flex Time Flourishes in Accounting Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Retention Bonus? Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KPMG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ERNST & YOUNG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PricewaterhouseCoopers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a54de32-0987-532d-8e62-4017bf74f71c', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a54de32-0987-532d-8e62-4017bf74f71c'}, {'abstract': 'In Hispanic Muslim communities, converts keep the music and food of their roots while adopting a devotion and a new form of dress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09muslims.html', 'snippet': 'In Hispanic Muslim communities, converts keep the music and food of their roots while adopting a devotion and a new form of dress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the North Hudson Islamic Educational Center in Union City, N.J., there are Spanish-language classes on the Koran and an annual Latino Muslim Day. About 35 percent of the center’s congregation is Hispanic, and there are frequent conversions in which Puerto Ricans, Dominicans, Mexicans, Cubans and others recite the Shahadah, a declaration of belief.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09subMUSLIM5/09subMUSLIM5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09subMUSLIM5/09subMUSLIM5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09subMUSLIM5/09subMUSLIM5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im