None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5b7eed5-2626-5e07-a922-8d2247668daa', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5b7eed5-2626-5e07-a922-8d2247668daa'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant in the former Café de Bruxelles space in the West Village is an ode to the Lyonnaise bouchon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09table.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant in the former Café de Bruxelles space in the West Village is an ode to the Lyonnaise bouchon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its cozy wood paneling and focused menu, Lyon, an ode to the Lyonnaise bouchon, has become a fast favorite in the West Village since it opened last year. François Latapie, a former partner at La Goulue on the Upper East Side and a fan of French ephemera, has used his own collection to create an eclectic feel in the former Café de Bruxelles space on Greenwich Avenue at 13th Street. Old comics wallpaper the bathrooms, an illuminated Michelin man \x97 Mr. Latapie’s only New York find \x97 perches near the bar, and a peripatetic pig outfitted as a butcher (pale blue jacket, diagonally draped apron) stands in a window over a dining table, for now. On Wednesday, four friends catching up on life and art took it all in. DIANE CARDWELL ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/table/table-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width'