years of exclusivity for AT&T and is likely to upend the smartphone market in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO \x97 Verizon Wireless plans to announce on Tuesday that it will soon begin selling Apple’s iPhone 4, according to a person with direct knowledge of the plans. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Is Said to Be Planning to Announce iPhone 4 on Its Network', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Verizon Is Said to Be Planning to Announce iPhone 4 on Its Network', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4328362c-defe-52ac-a5a2-ae9e57d5cc10', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4328362c-defe-52ac-a5a2-ae9e57d5cc10'}, {'abstract': 'Prisoners are stripped of almost all individual possessions. Writing to magazines, one of the few things they can call their own, can provide comfort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/business/media/08jailmail.html', 'snippet': 'Prisoners are stripped of almost all individual possessions. Writing to magazines, one of the few things they can call their own, can provide comfort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Georgia Department of Corrections he is inmate No. 544319, in prison on a five-year sentence for drug possession. But to the editors of Maxim, he is Mike Bolick, a faithful reader and regular letter writer who has loopy penmanship and an eye for beautiful cover models.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Handwritten Letter, an Art All but Lost, Thrives in Prison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To the Editor, in an Inmate’s Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dfbe42a-e03d-5144-9b78-40bedd92c7a2', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dfbe42a-e03d-5144-9b78-40bedd92c7a2'}, {'abstract': 'East Elmhurst, Queens was among the first New York City neighborhoods where African-Americans could buy homes. So they did. And never left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/nyregion/08elmhurst.html', 'snippet': 'East Elmhurst, Queens was among the first New York City neighborhoods where African-Americans could buy homes. So they did. And never left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is a place of constant change, an ever-shifting mosaic of immigrants, ethnic groups, strivers who make their mark and move on.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/nyregion/ELMHURST/ELMHURST-articleLarge.jp