 on and initiated bills before they had been sworn in; the party leadership waffled on its promise to cut $100 billion in domestic spending this year; and Speaker of the House John Boehner was accused of breaking his own pledge to send all bills through a complete committee process. Well, at least there was no way to mess up the much-hyped symbolic measure of the day, a bipartisan reading of the Constitution, right? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Constitution, Sort Of', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:37:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tobin Harshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tobin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf11b4d-67ec-58e4-a1b7-ab9a815fbbc9', 'word_count': 2186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf11b4d-67ec-58e4-a1b7-ab9a815fbbc9'}, {'abstract': 'After the blizzard buried their homes for days, residents of a block in Bellerose, Queens, braced for Friday’s snowfall, only to find their shovels left unused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/nyregion/08block.html', 'snippet': 'After the blizzard buried their homes for days, residents of a block in Bellerose, Queens, braced for Friday’s snowfall, only to find their shovels left unused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daisy Roman dropped her sons off at school on Friday and rushed to the supermarket, just in case. Dawn Frey made sure her groceries were delivered. Five doors away, John Moore gassed up his snowblower and left handy some extra bags of road salt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/nyregion/BLOCK/BLOCK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/nyregion/BLOCK/BLOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/nyregion/BLOCK/BLOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Block Was Ready for a Storm That Barely Came', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Time, No Snowplows; This Time, Almost No Snow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T01:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afb145f8-b364-5300-9442-c469ae23a817', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afb145f8-b364-53