r Green Bay Packers coaches show film of the beefy running back John Kuhn carrying the ball \x97 often on a battering-ram run inside the 20-yard line \x97 Kuhn’s teammates chant his last name, holding the vowel for several seconds, mimicking the way fans at Lambeau Field salute their newest cult hero. Kooooon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-jp-kuhn/y-jp-kuhn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-jp-kuhn/y-jp-kuhn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/08/sports/y-jp-kuhn/y-jp-kuhn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Fit for the Packers, as Well as Their Fans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Fit for the Packers, as Well as Their Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T02:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0547608e-27a9-5437-8f1b-6f4785a673e9', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0547608e-27a9-5437-8f1b-6f4785a673e9'}, {'abstract': 'The Cocoa Chocolate Shop in Larchmont, N.Y., has developed a cult following for its hot chocolate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09qbitewe.html', 'snippet': 'The Cocoa Chocolate Shop in Larchmont, N.Y., has developed a cult following for its hot chocolate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With holiday mania behind us, we can turn to the simple joys of winter: sledding, skating, snowman-building — and sipping hot chocolate. The last comes first at the Cocoa Chocolate Shop in Larchmont, a tiny storefront boasting huge caloric possibilities in the form of truffles, bonbons, barks and — best of all — criminally smooth hot chocolate that tastes and acts like liquid chocolate pudding.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shot of Liquid Seduction', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Larchmont', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shot of Liquid Seduction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Larchmont (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T02:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c95a3b55-07b6-5942-adbc-98d924a6e0ae', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c95a3b55-07b6-5942-adbc-98d924a6e0ae'}, {'abstract': 'While open kitchens are commonplace these days, the one at Thyme really puts the chefs front and center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09dinewe.html', 'snippet': 'While open kitchens are commonplace these days, the one at Thyme really puts the chefs front and center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OPEN kitchens are commonplace these days, but even as they offer a peek into the culinary process, they usually feel separate from the dining area. Chefs and other workers are focused on their tasks, and the view is often only partial, blocked by appliances or someone’s back.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09dinewe2/09dinewe2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09dinewe2/09dinewe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/09dinewe2/09dinewe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Open Kitchen That’s Truly Open', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Yorktown Heights', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Open Kitchen That’s Truly Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T02:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily DeNitto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeNitto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c19f428-6568-598b-a4