om/2011/01/08/world/europe/08hungary.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Viktor Orban said that he would make changes if the law proved incompatible with European legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST, Hungary \x97 After a warning from the European Union that the controversy over Hungary’s broad new media law could undermine the country’s six-month presidency of the bloc, Prime Minister Viktor Orban abandoned his fiery language against the law’s European critics on Friday, emphasizing that he would make changes if the law proved incompatible with European legislation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Pressure, Hungary Softens Tone on Its Media Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Pressure, Hungary Softens Tone on Its Media Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orban, Viktor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:43:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19e33d78-0e32-585d-b66d-59cd5ba96121', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e33d78-0e32-585d-b66d-59cd5ba96121'}, {'abstract': 'Chile became the seventh country in South America to formally recognize an independent state of Palestine in the past month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/world/americas/08chile.html', 'snippet': 'Chile became the seventh country in South America to formally recognize an independent state of Palestine in the past month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO \x97 Chile formally recognized an independent state of Palestine on Friday, becoming the seventh South American country to take such a step in the past month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chile Offers Recognition for a State of Palestine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chile Offers Recognition For a State Of Palestine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinera, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92bd3b76-d72f-5672-ac6e-693b944a46e7', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92bd3b76-d72f-5672-ac6e-693b944a46e7'}, {'abstract': 'If southern Sudan votes to secede from Sudan, as expected, the United States must ensure that the transition remains peaceful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/opinion/08sat1.html', 'snippet': 'If southern Sudan votes to secede from Sudan, as expected, the United States must ensure that the transition remains peaceful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, southern Sudan is expected to vote to secede from Sudan, creating two states. The referendum is part of a 2005 agreement, which ended two decades of fighting between the Arab Muslim north and the largely Christian south that killed two million people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Southern Sudan Votes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southern Sudan Votes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e7780d5-f2a0-5254-bda0-820694428c8f', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e7780d5-f2a0-5254-bda0-820694428c8f'}, {'abstract': 'The New Jersey Supreme Court should order the state to fulfill its duty and fully finance education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/opinion/08sat2.html', 'snippet': 'The New Jersey Supreme Court should order the state to fulfill its duty and fully finance education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For almost 40 years, the New Jersey Supreme Court has tried to fulfill its duty to enforce the education clause in the state Constitution by compelling the governor and Legislature to provide equal educational opportunity for public school students. In 2009, the court decided the state had finally devised a way to do that, through a formula that would give each student, especially in poor districts, a chance at “an unhindered start in life.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Jersey Reckoning', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Jersey Reckoning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e7eba1d-f624-5cec-ac5a-53227014d9fd', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e7eba1d-f624-5cec-ac5a-53227014d9fd'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Hoiberg is back home coaching at Iowa State after 15 years in the N.B.A. as a player and executive, but his dream job comes with risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/sports/basketball/08hoiberg.html', 'snippet': 'Fred Hoiberg is back home coaching at Iowa State after 15 years in the N.B.A. as a player and executive, but his dream job comes with risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMES, Iowa \x97 In the desk of her office at City Hall, the mayor of this community, Ann Campbell, keeps a T-shirt in the cardinal and gold colors of Iowa State. A gag Christmas gift from her brother, it reads “The Other Mayor” on one side, and “32 \x97 Not Fred” on the other.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/08/spor