nt Obama was forced to sign a spending bill on Friday with a particularly harmful provision that bars spending to transfer detainees at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, to the United States for trial. As wrongheaded as this prohibition is, the president was right not to declare his intention to defy it in an accompanying statement. By doing so, he demonstrated a greater respect for the law than did President George W. Bush.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rule of Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rule of Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Signing Statements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a55116c4-d3d5-5368-a056-0fc30ffdc78a', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a55116c4-d3d5-5368-a056-0fc30ffdc78a'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s school shooting in Omaha is a horrifying reminder that politicians must stop cowering before the gun lobby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/opinion/08sat4.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s school shooting in Omaha is a horrifying reminder that politicians must stop cowering before the gun lobby.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The new year is barely a week old, but the nation has already recorded its first deadly school shooting. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Killing at Millard South', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Killing at Millard South', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Omaha (Neb)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T03:53:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0343a198-52c3-583a-8a4b-a0070ffea64a', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0343a198-52c3-583a-8a4b-a0070ffea64a'}, {'abstract': 'Tampa Bay continued its rebuilding process, shipping the 27-year-old starter to Chicago in an eight-player deal that brought the Rays five prospects in return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/sports/baseball/08base.html', 'snippet': 'Tampa Bay continued its rebuilding process, shipping the 27-year-old starter to Chicago in an eight-player deal that brought the Rays five prospects in return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 9, when Matt Garza threw his last pitch as a member of the Rays, Tampa Bay used 16 players in its playoff game against Texas. Eight of them are no longer with the organization. That is a lot of turnover for a 96-win team, but hardly unexpected for the Rays, who hold onto talent as long as their limited payroll allows.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cubs Deal for the Rays’ Garza', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'