es that he’ll walk again.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/in-espn-interview-eric-legrand-shows-positive-spirit/', 'snippet': 'Eric LeGrand of Rutgers, who is recovering from a  spinal cord injury that has left him paralyzed, believes that he’ll walk again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A powerful story by ESPN on Eric LeGrand of Rutgers, who is recovering from a spinal cord injury and believes that he’ll walk again. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In ESPN Interview, Eric LeGrand Shows Positive Spirit', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeGrand, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T06:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1d35a3-8b17-5c87-bdc8-3a74eaf777c4', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1d35a3-8b17-5c87-bdc8-3a74eaf777c4'}, {'abstract': 'An Israeli soldier was killed in a clash on the Gaza border on Friday by a mortar shell fired by his own forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/world/middleeast/08briefs-Israel.html', 'snippet': 'An Israeli soldier was killed in a clash on the Gaza border on Friday by a mortar shell fired by his own forces.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Israeli soldier was killed in a clash on the Gaza border on Friday by a mortar shell fired by his own forces, an Israeli Army spokesman said, speaking anonymously according to military regulation. Four other soldiers were wounded by the mortar. The episode occurred after Israeli forces spotted a group of Palestinians trying to plant an explosive device at the border, the army said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Soldier Killed by Friendly Fire', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Soldier Killed by Friendly Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T07:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By BLOOMBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/18824bac-d3a1-50d2-bea3-f2b54d5b82df', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18824bac-d3a1-50d2-bea3-f2b54d5b82df'}, {'abstract': 'In the their 121-96 victory over Phoenix, Amar’e Stoudemire, Mike D’Antoni and the Knicks showed that they are transforming from a work in progress to one that opponents heed with caution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sports/basketball/09knicks.html', 'snippet': 'In the their 121-96 victory over Phoenix, Amar’e Stoudemire, Mike D’Antoni and the Knicks showed that they are transforming from a work in progress to one that opponents heed with caution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX \x97 Over the past few days, Amar’e Stoudemire had expressed contentment with the Knicks’ surge, revealed his surprise about the Suns’ rigid stance in the contract negotiations that led to his departure and shared his remorse at having never reached the N.B.A. finals while playing here. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'sour