graph': 'Eirini Vourloumis is a freelance photographer who has focused on Islamic communities in the United States. She is now in Greece, where she was born, to cover the economic crisis. Ms. Vourloumis is a graduate of Parsons and the Columbia Journalism School. Her work has been published on Lens and in The New York Times, New York Magazine, FT magazine and The Village Voice. Her conversation with James Estrin has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Islam to a Latino Identity', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Union City (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T10:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/da68e43d-2417-5f18-be4e-efb95bdfb6ec', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da68e43d-2417-5f18-be4e-efb95bdfb6ec'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Atlas began running and swimming every day on Brighton Beach in Brooklyn to escape the pain of watching his mother die. Wednesday was his 1,201st consecutive day, and he said, “It’d kill me to stop.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/sweat-workout-for-a-world-of-grief/', 'snippet': 'Gary Atlas began running and swimming every day on Brighton Beach in Brooklyn to escape the pain of watching his mother die. Wednesday was his 1,201st consecutive day, and he said, “It’d kill me to stop.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a lifelong resident o