and a strange quirk in plus/minus rating as it relates to the Lakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In theory, the more minutes a team’s most productive player can play per game, the better. The Golden State Warriors seem to be embracing that spirit wholeheartedly with their use of shooting guard Monta Ellis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ellis Is the Warriors’ Warrior', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T16:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc10da23-b8bc-5bc2-b995-f8a0b9336974', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc10da23-b8bc-5bc2-b995-f8a0b9336974'}, {'abstract': 'Washington Coach Bruce Boudreau said his star, Alex Ovechkin, has become more of a team player.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/with-goal-scoring-down-ovechkin-takes-on-different-role/', 'snippet': 'Washington Coach Bruce Boudreau said his star, Alex Ovechkin, has become more of a team player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Ovechkin’s drop-off in goal scoring this season has inspired criticism, but listen to Washington Coach Bruce Boudreau, speaking after the Capitals’ Winter Classic victory over the Penguins on Jan. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Goal Scoring Down, Ovechkin Takes on Different Role', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T16:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54240f02-fffd-55f1-a826-0f288a95871e', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54240f02-fffd-55f1-a826-0f288a95871e'}, {'abstract': 'Lloyd Thacker, the founder of the Education Conservancy, who once derided the College Board for its “corporatization,” joins forces with the board in a bid to create a Web site that might help explain the admissions process to students.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/a-folk-hero-crosses-the-aisle/', 'snippet': 'Lloyd Thacker, the founder of the Education Conservancy, who once derided the College Board for its “corporatization,” joins forces with the board in a bid to create a Web site that might help explain the admissions process to students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lloyd Thacker, who has put himself forward as a proxy for parents and students frustrated by the arms-race nature of the college admissions process, has a new partner these days: the College Board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Folk Hero Crosses the Aisle', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T16:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a3f81dc-4f33-5ce4-b001-0ae07bc6ca34', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a3f81dc-4f33-5ce4-b001-0ae07bc6ca34'}, {'abstract': 'The subpoena is the first public evidence to surface of a criminal investigation of disclosures of classified information by WikiLeaks and its founder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/world/09wiki.html', 'snippet': 'The subpoena is the first public evidence to surface of a criminal investigation of disclosures of classified information by WikiLeaks and its founder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Prosecutors investigating the disclosure of thousands of classified government documents by the anti-secrecy group WikiLeaks have gone to court to demand the Twitter account activity of several people linked to the organization, including its founder, Julian Assange, according to the group and a copy of a subpoena made public late Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/JP-WIKI-2/JP-WIKI-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/JP-WIKI-2/JP-WIKI-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/us/JP-WIKI-2/JP-WIKI-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Subpoenas Twitter Over WikiLeaks Supporters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TWITTER RECORDS IN WIKILEAKS CASE ARE SUBPOENAED', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T16:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane and John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdc8d6c3-efe7-5d3f-87cd-41ac4d8f1cfe', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdc8d6c3-efe7-5d3f-87cd-41ac4d8f1cfe'}, {'abstract': 'Armed with her laptop and pluck, Khalilah El-Amin, who is unemployed, is constantly on the hunt for a steady job so that she can provide for her sons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/nyregion/09neediest.html', 'snippet': 'Armed with her laptop and pluck, Khalilah El-Amin, who is unemployed, is constantly on the hunt for a steady job so that she can provide for her sons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Khalilah El-Amin’s apartment in Brooklyn is warm and inviting and smells like butter, the result of a batch of chocolate chip cookies she baked earlier. Her sons Emmanuel, 7, and Rakim, 8, play with toy trucks while Ms. El-Amin types on her laptop.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/nyregion/SUB-09NEEDIEST/SUB-09NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju