ege dropout and world traveler who had decided that I didn’t want a job, much less a career. What I really wanted was to get paid for my hobbies: writing, gardening and politics. So I made that my goal.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/PRE/PRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/PRE/PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/business/PRE/PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m Making a Living From My Hobbies', 'kicker': 'Preoccupations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’m Making A Living From My Hobbies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hobbies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T17:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Hyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b965907c-42b2-5278-b25f-3b6f4ca5e09f', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b965907c-42b2-5278-b25f-3b6f4ca5e09f'}, {'abstract': 'Susan Axelrod talks about her husband, David, getting him to diet and their life after he leaves the White House in February.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/susan-axelrod-on-life-after-washington/', 'snippet': 'Susan Axelrod talks about her husband, David, getting him to diet and their life after he leaves the White House in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For someone who doesn’t actually live in Washington, Susan Axelrod has a pretty inside track to the White House. She is, after all, married to David Axelrod, who has been one of the president’s closest advisers since before he even declared his run. The Caucus recently caught up with Ms. Axelrod, a founding member of CURE (Citizens United for Research in Epilepsy) at Commissary, a neighborhood coffee shop a few blocks away from the apartment her husband rents — at least through early February, when he moves back to their home in Chicago. She scanned the menu for cholesterol-healthy options and weighed in on everything from the ups and downs of life in the White House, what it will be like to have her husband back at home, how they met, what she misses about Chicago when she’s not there, and her work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Susan Axelrod on Life After Washington', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T17:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/056a051b-f768-52b3-9d6d-4c099d0c7389', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/056a051b-f768-52b3-9d6d-4c099d0c7389'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Swinburn once delivered kegs of beer to pubs. Now he runs one of the world’s big brewing companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/jobs/09boss.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Swinburn once delivered kegs of beer to pubs. Now he runs one of the world’s big brewing companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I GREW up in Wales, living in the Penywaun council housing estate, or working-class housing, where my parents moved after World War II. The biggest nearby city was Cardiff.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/BOSS/BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 955, 'width': 740, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A World of Beer', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World of Beer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Molson Coors Brewing Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T17:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter S. Swinburn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Swinburn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62940cc5-2506-5686-9416-6674f50c9728', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62940cc5-2506-5686-9416-6674f50c9728'}, {'abstract': 'Being in the minority allows Democrats to assault Republicans with the same kind of attacks that Republicans so effectively used against them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/us/politics/09memo.html', 'snippet': 'Being in the minority allows Democrats to assault Republicans with the same kind of attacks that Republicans so effectively used against them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 After four years of harassment by an aggressive Republican minority, House Democrats evidently absorbed a lesson along with all those political blows: the route back to Congressional power is paved with frontal assaults on the practices and policies of the majority.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Democrats Rapidly Unleash Sharp Attacks', 'kicker': 'Congressional Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tables Turned, House Democrats Rapidly Unleash Sharp Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T18:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f92451bd-ce01-58dc-8fba-a97931b21dc7', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f92451bd-ce01-58dc-8fba-a97931b21dc7'}, {'abstract': 'As Japan and European countries are digitizing collections for national one-stop searching, efforts in the United States have been scattered.', 'web_url': 'https://ww