d_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c9a3b6-0ea4-5c4d-8c8a-6738c48631c2'}, {'abstract': 'The bond market, jolted in December, could have a bumpy road in 2011. But an analyst says that is no reason to abandon bonds as part of a long-term investment strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/business/mutfund/09bond.html', 'snippet': 'The bond market, jolted in December, could have a bumpy road in 2011. But an analyst says that is no reason to abandon bonds as part of a long-term investment strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the stock market plummeted in 2008, investors began to pour money into bond mutual funds, which generally performed quite well \x97 at least until this past December. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Long Ascent, Turbulence for Bonds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Long Ascent, Turbulence for Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T18:58:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan M. Rosen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b294b74a-e547-5776-90af-c6b35b23687f', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b294b74a-e547-5776-90af-c6b35b23687f'}, {'abstract': 'Domestic funds’ outperformance could continue in 2011 if American companies, highly profitable and flush with cash, benefit from a strengthening economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/business/mutfund/09fore.html', 'snippet': 'Domestic funds’ outperformance could continue in 2011 if American companies, highly profitable and flush with cash, benefit from a strengthening economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHN TEMPLETON may be known as the father of global investing, but the Templeton Growth fund, which he started in 1954, is finding top holdings closer to home these days.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/SUB-FORE/SUB-FORE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Long Can U.S. Stocks Keep Their Edge?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Long Can U.S. Stocks Keep Their Edge?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Duffy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duffy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03eb5447-b36a-5638-82fe-15a7ab10c8cf', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03eb5447-b36a-5638-82fe-15a7ab10c8cf'}, {'abstract': 'It’s still crucial to hang onto financial statements, but scanners and flash drives can vastly cut down on the clutter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/business/mutfund/09record.html', 'snippet': 'It’s still crucial to hang onto financial statements, but scanners and flash drives can vastly cut down on the clutter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOVING makes you face all the stuff you’ve accumulated: books, computers, clothing and, of course, reams and reams of financial documents. Before deciding whether to haul all of them to a new home, as I did a few months ago, it is worth asking what really needs to be saved and what can safely be ditched.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Save Your Financial Records, but Maybe Save a Tree', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save Your Financial Records, but Maybe Save a Tree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81157836-a9cf-5cd5-857a-d74d14a68cf0', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81157836-a9cf-5cd5-857a-d74d14a68cf0'}, {'abstract': 'Silver prices surged in 2010, helped by a new accessibility and the metal’s reputation as a safe investment in time of trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/business/mutfund/09silver.html', 'snippet': 'Silver prices surged in 2010, helped by a new accessibility and the metal’s reputation as a safe investment in time of trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR a metal deemed precious, silver has often been ignored by investors.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/SILVER/SILVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/business/SILVER/SILVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/business/SILVER/SILVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If You’ve Got the Nerve, Silver Is Easier to Buy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If You’ve Got the Nerve, Silver Is Easier to Buy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Silver', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exchange Traded Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank'