8370-b32317f4e843', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fea9983-688d-5667-8370-b32317f4e843'}, {'abstract': 'LeSean McCoy has become a versatile dynamo in the Eagles’ offense, but he has not earned as many headlines as his more celebrated teammates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sports/football/09eagles.html', 'snippet': 'LeSean McCoy has become a versatile dynamo in the Eagles’ offense, but he has not earned as many headlines as his more celebrated teammates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA \x97 When he is in the Eagles’ locker room, running back LeSean McCoy is hard to avoid and easy to hear. He bounces from stall to stall, breaking silences with one-liners and boastful statements about his hometown.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/eagles/eagles-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/eagles/eagles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/eagles/eagles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eagle Grabs a Sliver in a Crowded Spotlight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Running Back With a Running Dialogue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Eagles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1932abf3-54af-5be5-af4f-1fa94f783eac', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1932abf3-54af-5be5-af4f-1fa94f783eac'}, {'abstract': 'Jokes from TV comedy show monologues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09laugh.html', 'snippet': 'Jokes from TV comedy show monologues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAY LENO', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laugh Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laugh Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a156a6fc-49e4-5e70-ad02-274630f617f0', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a156a6fc-49e4-5e70-ad02-274630f617f0'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s one way to tackle traffic congestion. Ban car sales. That’s what China has done temporarily in its capital, Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09grist.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s one way to tackle traffic congestion. Ban car sales. That’s what China has done temporarily in its capital, Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s one way to tackle traffic congestion. Ban car sales. That’s what China has done temporarily in its capital, Beijing, where the number of cars on the roads has nearly doubled in five years, making driving a nightmare, according to The Christian Science Monitor. The government barred car sales in Beijing from Dec. 24 until later this month, when its new lottery system comes up with the names of the 20,000 lucky applicants who will have the right to buy license plates. About 100,000 people have already put their names in the drawing. New regulations have also increased parking fees in Beijing and banned cars with out-of-city plates from the roads during rush hour.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/subGRIST/subGRIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/subGRIST/subGRIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/subGRIST/subGRIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 611, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/subGRIST/subGRIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/subGRIST/subGRIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stuck in Traffic, Beijing Puts a Brake on Car Sales', 'kicker': 'Grist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stuck in Traffic, Beijing Puts a Brake On Car Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:19:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a482627-3a5c-5c6e-bd23-048cfb125bbd', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a482627-3a5c-5c6e-bd23-048cfb125bbd'}, {'abstract': '32: The percentage increase in the United Nations’ world food price index from June to December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09primeno.html', 'snippet': '32: The percentage increase in the United Nations’ world food price index from June to December.', 'lead_paragraph': '32: The percentage increase in the United Nations’ world food price index from June to December. Poor grain harvests and weather-related problems have pushed prices close to the crisis levels that provoked shortages and riots in poor countries three years ago. The index measures commodity prices on the world export market, which are generally far removed from supermarket prices in wealthy countries. (Prices in the United States are expected to rise only 2 percent to 3 percent this year.) But the situation is different in poor countries that rely on exports. “We are at a very high level,” said Abdolreza Abbassian, an economist for the United Nations’ Food and Agriculture Organization. “These levels in the previous episode led to problems and riots across the world.”', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime Number', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PRIME NUMBER', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/470f3c81-93c9-51af-b798-f6265574b75b', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/470f3c81-93c9-51af-b798-f6265574b75b'}, {'abstract': 'One of psychology’s most respected journals has agreed to publish a paper presenting what its author describes as strong evidence for extrasensory perception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09fight.html', 'snippet': 'One of psychology’s most respected journals has agreed to publish a paper presenting what its author describes as strong evidence for extrasensory perception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of psychology’s most respected journals has agreed to publish a paper presenting what its author describes as strong evidence for extrasensory perception, the ability to sense future events.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09fight-web/09fight-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09fight-web/09fight-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Words', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff164d8a-a3af-5d88-b5a0-f6932846cdff', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff164d8a-a3af-5d88-b5a0-f6932846cdff'}, {'abstract': 'The coffee chain’s decision to remove its name entirely from its logo has set off a wave of criticism from designers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09heller.html', 'snippet': 'The coffee chain’s decision to remove its name entirely from its logo has set off a wave of criticism from designers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Logomania has been in the air since the chief executive of Starbucks, Howard Schultz, announced another redesign of the Starbucks logo last week.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/books/review/Heller/Heller-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 98, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/books/review/Heller/Heller-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 98}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/books/review/Heller/Heller-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 166, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/books/review/Heller/Heller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/books/review/Heller/Heller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Makeover for the Starbucks Mermaid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DESIGN: A Makeover for a Mermaid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:50:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e7bd62a-fe49-5a5e-b73e-9fad4fd57bcb', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e7bd62a-fe49-5a5e-b73e-9fad4fd57bcb'}, {'abstract': 'As the Chiefs’ quarterback Matt Cassel prepares to start Sunday’s playoff game against the Ravens, sadness over his father’s death is mixed with the happiness of an outstanding season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sports/football/09chiefs.html', 'snippet': 'As the Chiefs’ quarterback Matt Cassel prepares to start Sunday’s playoff game against the Ravens, sadness over his father’s death is mixed with the happiness of an outstanding season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. \x97 The uplifting story of the Chiefs’ rebirth is bittersweet for their quarterback, Matt Cassel. In his sixth year as a pro, Cassel led Kansas City to 10 regular-season victories, as many as it had in the previous three seasons combined, and a date Sunday against the Baltimore Ravens in the first round of the N.F.L. playoffs. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/chiefs/chiefs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/chiefs/chiefs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/chiefs/chiefs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Chiefs’ Quarterback, Wistfulness Tempers Joy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Chiefs’ Quarterback, Wistfulness Tempers Joy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassel, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T19:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee74d5ec-e490-54c9-87e1-84a5429056cc', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee74d5ec-e490-54c9-87e1-84a5429056cc'}, {'abstract': 'After 5,000 birds died in Arkansas, the search was on for a villain — even if there was no villain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09gorman.html', 'snippet': 'After 5,000 birds died in Arkansas, the search was on for a villain — even if there was no villain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When 5,000 red-winged blackbirds fell dead on New Year’s Eve in Arkansas, and 500 more in Louisiana, many people immediately looked for a villain. There was speculation about military tests and pesticides, and a lot of wondering whether the bird deaths and other incidents, including the mass deaths of fish, were linked.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/REFEgorman/REFEgorman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/REFEgorman/REFEgorman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/REFEgorman/REFEgorman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight':