eab8'}, {'abstract': 'Across Africa, a legacy of European-drawn borders still breeds rebellion. Now southern Sudan may break the pattern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/weekinreview/09gettleman.html', 'snippet': 'Across Africa, a legacy of European-drawn borders still breeds rebellion. Now southern Sudan may break the pattern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than any other continent, Africa is wracked by separatists. There are rebels on the Atlantic and on the Red Sea. There are clearly defined liberation movements and rudderless, murderous groups known principally for their cruelty or greed. But these rebels share at least one thing: they direct their fire against weak states struggling to hold together disparate populations within boundaries drawn by 19th-century white colonialists.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/GETTLEjp/GETTLEjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/GETTLEjp/GETTLEjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/GETTLEjp/GETTLEjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/GETTLEjp/GETTLEjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/weekinreview/GETTLEjp/GETTLEjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Sudan, a Colonial Curse Comes Up for a Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': N