mes.com/2011/01/08/a-lot-of-jazz-many-more-people/', 'snippet': 'Friday night proved that a lot of people are curious about New York Winter Jazzfest.  More than were planned for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was at Winter Jazzfest Friday night. I’m returning tonight. Got to prepare myself for that. I had some good stretches, but spent a lot of time spent obstructed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lot of Jazz. Many More People.', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T22:14:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/601ace9e-dbda-51bd-8990-b1392e394bf1', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601ace9e-dbda-51bd-8990-b1392e394bf1'}, {'abstract': 'The Gridiron Heroes Spinal Cord Injury Foundation seeks to assist injured high school football players, and prompted S.M.U. Coach June Jones to establish a similar foundation for injured college athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sports/09injuries.html', 'snippet': 'The Gridiron Heroes Spinal Cord Injury Foundation seeks to assist injured high school football players, and prompted S.M.U. Coach June Jones to establish a similar foundation for injured college athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In November 2002, Chris Canales attended a high school football game for the first time since being paralyzed in one a year earlier. As Canales sat in a wheelchair next to his father, Eddie, he watched Corey Fulbright of Everman High School in Texas lie motionless on the turf, paralyzed after injuring his spinal cord.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Groups Seek to Aid Injured Players', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Groups Seek to Aid Injured Players', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, June', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Methodist University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-08T22:23:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Himmelsbach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Himmelsbach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c8db16-3391-566d-8625-27e78aead975', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c8db16-3391-566d-8625-27e78aead975'}, {'abstract': 'Worse than I thought.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/08/health-reform-and-social-security/', 'snippet': 'Worse than I thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aha: I’ve figured out what the Social Security stuff in the GOP attack on health reform is about: the excise tax on high-value plans is expected to shift some worker compensation away from health insurance toward regular pay — which is taxable, both income and payroll. And the GOP wants to assert that increased payroll tax revenue doesn’t count because, well, something about how Social Security isn’t part of the budget, and the CBO is double-counting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Reform and Social Security', 'kic