ually the endoskeleton of a populous sea animal, with 250 species worldwide. The local variety, Dendraster excentricus, is perhaps the strangest. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/09BCINTEL2/09BCINTEL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 430, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/09BCINTEL2/09BCINTEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/us/09BCINTEL2/09BCINTEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Local Intelligence | Sand Dollars', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LOCAL INTELLIGENCE: Sand Dollars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baja California (Mexico)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Golden Gate Park (San Francisco)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Burning Man Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T01:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hank Pellissier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pellissier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3cc7763-f139-5d01-85b4-32d8314bebdc', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3cc7763-f139-5d01-85b4-32d8314bebdc'}, {'abstract': 'In what he says is his final season coaching in the N.B.A., Phil Jackson is leaving no notebook unfulfilled and no topic untouched.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sports/basketball/09lakers.html', 'snippet': 'In what he says is his final season coaching in the N.B.A., Phil Jackson is leaving no notebook unfulfilled and no topic untouched.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL SEGUNDO, Calif. \x97 The question had been asked. Lakers Coach Phil Jackson saw the bait a mile away, laughed and, for one of the few times this season, punted on the opportunity to needle a rival, provoke an adversary or willingly dip himself into controversy. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/Y-LAKERS1/Y-LAKERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/Y-LAKERS1/Y-LAKERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/sports/Y-LAKERS1/Y-LAKERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking All Questions, the Lakers’ Jackson Holds Nothing Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking All Questions, The Lakers’ Jackson Holds Nothing Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T01:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne