c paintings were inspired by political conditions in his home country, Mozambique, died on Wednesday in Matosinhos, Portugal. He was 74. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/dog-NGWENYA1-obit/dog-NGWENYA1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 423, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/dog-NGWENYA1-obit/dog-NGWENYA1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/arts/dog-NGWENYA1-obit/dog-NGWENYA1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Malangatana Ngwenya, Mozambican Painter and Poet, Dies at 74', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Malangatana Ngwenya, 74, Mozambican Painter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T02:26:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0311d2fe-e889-5895-9497-798d7875ec91', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0311d2fe-e889-5895-9497-798d7875ec91'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard not to think the shooting was partly influenced by a debate that often seems to conflate disagreement with Armageddon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/us/politics/09bai.html', 'snippet': 'It’s hard not to think the shooting was partly influenced by a debate that often seems to conflate disagreement with Armageddon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Within minutes of the first reports Saturday that Representative Gabrielle Giffords, an Arizona Democrat, and a score of people with her had been shot in Tucson, pages began disappearing from the Web. One was Sarah Palin’s infamous “cross hairs” map from last year, which showed a series of contested Congressional districts, including Ms. Giffords’s, with gun targets trained on them. Another was from Daily Kos, the liberal blog, where one of the congresswoman’s apparently liberal constituents declared her “dead to me” after Ms. Giffords voted against Nancy Pelosi in House leadership elections last week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Turning Point in the Discourse, but in Which Direction?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Turning Point in the Discourse, but in Which Direction?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Angle, Sharron E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T02:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdb75074-9b4f-5675-82ef-440b08dda598', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdb75074-9b4f-5675-82ef-440b08dda598'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel has announced to labor leaders that he favors reducing pensions for all Chicago city workers, not just the new hires. Reactions are not altogether positive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/us/09cncpulse.html', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel has announced to labor leaders that he favors reducing pensions for all Chicago city workers, not just the new hires. Reactions are not altogether positive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In contrast to his main rivals in the mayor’s race, Rahm Emanuel has told labor leaders that he favors reducing pension benefits for the city’s existing work force and not just for new hires.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emanuel Says He Favors Reduced Pensions for Current Workers and New Hires', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emanuel Says He Favors Reduced Pensions for Current City Workers, Not Just New Hires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Richard M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chico, Gery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moseley-Braun, Carol', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'ra