Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da44554-b4ad-5c0f-b23f-da6e726f5bb8', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da44554-b4ad-5c0f-b23f-da6e726f5bb8'}, {'abstract': 'Scribbling a few numbers does not a deficit hawk make.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/peacockery/', 'snippet': 'Scribbling a few numbers does not a deficit hawk make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Ip is too kind in this article, in which he questions why Paul Ryan should have received an award for fiscal responsibility. Ip makes it out as if Ryan is a former good guy who has fallen astray; but there was never any reason to take his claims of being a deficit hawk seriously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peacockery', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T21:55:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f35b645-4e85-5718-bbe8-09e822849bda', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f35b645-4e85-5718-bbe8-09e822849bda'}, {'abstract': 'Both parties had concerns over the tone of discourse and wondered if a lack of civility contributed to the attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/us/politics/10capital.html', 'snippet': 'Both parties had concerns over the tone of discourse and wondered if a lack of civility contributed to the attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – With the nation’s capital reeling from Saturday’s attack on Representative Gabrielle Giffords of Arizona, in which an aide to the lawmaker and five constituents were killed both parties on Sunday began a wrenching process of soul-searching about the tone of political discourse and wondered aloud if a lack of civility had somehow contributed to the bloodshed in Tucson.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/politics/09caucus-giffords-capitol/09caucus-giffords-capitol-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/09/us/politics/09caucus-giffords-capitol/09caucus-giffords-capitol-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/politics/09caucus-giffords-capitol/09caucus-giffords-capitol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/09/us/politics/09caucus-giffords-capitol/09caucus-giffords-capitol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/09/us/politics/09caucus-giffords-capitol/09caucus-giffords-capitol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Attack, Focus in Washington on Civility and Security', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Arizona Attack, Focus in Washington is on Civility and Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, Gabriel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitol Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T21:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/625e3f4e-99d0-5944-8d23-4b610b17f732', 'word_count': 1533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/625e3f4e-99d0-5944-8d23-4b610b17f732'}, {'abstract': 'Godwin’s Law comes to the Times.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/blog-and-column-meta/', 'snippet': 'Godwin’s Law comes to the Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blog meta: I’m going to add a new rule: no Nazi references unless there’s a seriously good reason. If you’re writing about the economic policies of Hjalmar Horace Greeley Schacht, obviously it’s OK; but I’m going to try to hold down the Godwin’s Law violations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blog and Column Meta', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eab9ca92-81fb-5690-b86a-654f1f4d60ea', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eab9ca92-81fb-5690-b86a-654f1f4d60ea'}, {'abstract': 'A snapshot of readers’ responses to new and noteworthy shows, events, and people in the theater world.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/curtain-down-heads-up-readers-respond-to-small-fire-dracula-and-streisand/', 'snippet': 'A snapshot of readers’ responses to new and noteworthy shows, events, and people in the theater world.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Small Fire” sizzles. “Dracula” has no bite. Barbra Streisand as Mama Rose? Don’t get you started.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Curtain Down, Heads Up: Readers Respond to ‘Small Fire,’ ‘Dracula’ and Streisand', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b25745ac-6c96-5a65-8462-621e524456b6', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b25745ac-6c96-5a65-8462-621e524456b6'}, {'abstract': 'The author pays tribute to his mother-in-law and the odd, inspiring menagerie he found in her attic.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/life-studies/', 'snippet': 'The author pays tribute to his mother-in-law and the odd, inspiring menagerie he found in her attic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the corner of our dining room, there’s an old half-round cabinet on wheels. It has a handsomely decorated front-panel that swings around on a lazy susan to reveal a collection of whiskey glasses and decanters on the other side. It’s what’s sometimes called a hide-a-bar, though we use it now mainly as a place to charge our cellphones. We keep it prominently displayed because we like it. But it also oddly embodies the split life of my mother-in-law, from whom we inherited it. And it has lately shaped the course of my own life both as a writer and a son-in-law. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Studies', 'kicker': 'Specimens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:28:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Conniff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conniff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9a8efd5-9d37-5c55-9cdf-cb1262072598', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9a8efd5-9d37-5c55-9cdf-cb1262072598'}, {'abstract': 'Amar’e Stoudemire scored 23 tough points and finished 7-for-23 in a loss at the Staples Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/sports/basketball/10knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Amar’e Stoudemire scored 23 tough points and finished