2df7-d066-5cbc-9afb-f558c38c0d0e'}, {'abstract': 'More than 100 people crowded into a tearful healing service Sunday for Rep. Gabrielle Giffords at Congregation Chaverim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/us/10religious.html', 'snippet': 'More than 100 people crowded into a tearful healing service Sunday for Rep. Gabrielle Giffords at Congregation Chaverim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — They spilled into the aisles and the corridor, past the extra rows of folding chairs and the congregants packed into the synagogue’s corners.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/us/10religious1_span/10religious1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/10/us/10religious1_span/10religious1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/us/10religious1_span/10religious1_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/us/10religious1_span/10religious1_span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/10/us/10religious1_span/10religious1_span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Giffords’s Synagogue, Prayers for Recovery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Synagogue Has Service Of Healing For Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a56578d-446d-53c5-a98c-ed167657b33c', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a56578d-446d-53c5-a98c-ed167657b33c'}, {'abstract': '“Twin,” a memoir by Allen Shawn, describes his life and his fears after his twin sister was placed, at age 8, in an institution for the mentally disabled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/books/10book.html', 'snippet': '“Twin,” a memoir by Allen Shawn, describes his life and his fears after his twin sister was placed, at age 8, in an institution for the mentally disabled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The formative event in the composer Allen Shawn’s life happened when he was 8 years old: His twin sister, Mary, who was mentally disabled, was sent away, abruptly disappearing from his daily life. Allen not only missed her terribly, but he also became terrified of “the mental illness that Mary had exhibited, and which had led, or so it had seemed to me as a child, to her being ‘ostracized’ from the family. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twin Alone, Disconnected but Not Lost', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twin Alone, Disconnected But Not Lost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shawn, Allen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shawn, Wallace', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shawn, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f3d47f-47f7-5dbb-a286-927d1d74f823', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f3d47f-47f7-5dbb-a286-927d1d74f823'}, {'abstract': 'Akashic Books is publishing a new anthology on the Jan. 12 earthquake in Haiti as part of its “Noir” series focused on specific locales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/books/10noir.html', 'snippet': 'Akashic Books is publishing a new anthology on the Jan. 12 earthquake in Haiti as part of its “Noir” series focused on specific locales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The setup is familiar for a crime story: a kidnapping, a ransom demand, a briefcase full of money meant to be delivered on a dead-end street. But the details, specific to a section of Port-au-Prince, are what make the story called “Rosanna” fit snugly into the new anthology “Haiti Noir.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/NOIRALT/NOIRALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/NOIRALT/NOIRALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/NOIRALT/NOIRALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/NOIRALT/NOIRALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/NOIRALT/NOIRALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Tales Illuminate Haiti, Before and After Quake', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dark Tales Illuminate Haiti, Before and After Quake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danticat, Edwidge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c20ea956-b8b2-549b-8535-caeb7c66eca8', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c20ea956-b8b2-549b-8535-caeb7c66eca8'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Gosling’s powerfully played recital was a concise, cohesive overview of a post-Serialist, post-Minimalist approach to writing for the keyboard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/arts/music/10barge.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen Gosling’s powerfully played recital was a concise, cohesive overview of a post-Serialist, post-Minimalist approach to writing for the keyboard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Gosling, a British pianist who came to New York as a student in 1989, has become one of the city’s most eloquent champions of new music, both as a soloist and as a member of Ensemble Sospeso and the New York New Music Ensemble. For the most part Mr. Gosling has not been bound to a particular contemporary style, but the carefully balanced, powerfully played recital he offered at Bargemusic on Thursday evening was a concise, cohesive overview of a post-Serialist, post-Minimalist approach to writing for the keyboard. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New-Music Champion Pays a Call', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New-Music Champion Pays a Call', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0cd4d23-be27-5edb-b52b-9734f39cf998', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0cd4d23-be27-5edb-b52b-9734f39cf998'}, {'abstract': 'Tarek Halaby’s lecture-performance at Abrons Arts Center over the weekend was a political dance without any dancing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/arts/dance/10attempt.html', 'snippet': 'Tarek Halaby’s lecture-performance at Abrons Arts Center over the weekend was a political dance without any dancing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a mouthful, but the title of Tarek Halaby’s lecture-performance, which rambles along like a garrulous dissertation topic, was the first wink of the night: “An attempt to understand my socio-political disposition through artistic research on personal identity in relationship to the Palestinian-Israeli conflict, Part One.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/ATTEMPT/ATTEMPT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Man of Confliction Takes on Mideast Conflict', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man of Confliction Takes on Mideast Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T22:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb08219-9a95-5e6e-ad81-2a1199ba3fa2', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb08219-9a95-5e6e-ad81-2a1199ba3fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Bucky Pizzarelli was the guest of honor at Lyrics & Lyricists, but it was a family affair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/arts/music/10bucky.html', 'snippet': 'Bucky Pizzarelli was the guest of honor at Lyrics & Lyricists, but it was a family affair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Bucky Pizzarelli, the guest of honor at the 92Y Lyrics & Lyricists season-opening program on Saturday, didn’t amble onto the stage until the second half of the evening, his voice was heard in recorded sound bites jovially reminiscing about his life and times as a session guitarist. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/BUCKY/BUCKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/BUCKY/BUCKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/BUCKY/BUCKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Guitar Hero, Through the Years', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Real Guitar Hero, Through the Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pizzarelli, Bucky', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89b479b6-e081-5023-9e69-b0da2aa4f474', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89b479b6-e081-5023-9e69-b0da2aa4f474'}, {'abstract': 'James Tuttle asks us to keep an eye on his puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/09/sleepy/', 'snippet': 'James Tuttle asks us to keep an eye on his puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — O.K., now I get it. Now I understand how James Tuttle was able to make his debut today. Your former host, Jim Horne, recently wrote a shocking exposé of the crossword selection process (which was actually a totally false and hilarious send-up, Your Honor), but this is far more blatant. Thank goodness it’s such a cool puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: You Are Getting Sleepy …', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5661879-7919-5e6d-b8ff-ddd7d0a3e37b', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5661879-7919-5e6d-b8ff-ddd7d0a3e37b'}, {'abstract': 'Arizona has shifted from a place on the political fringe to symbol of a nation whose discourse has lost its way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/us/10arizona.html', 'snippet': 'Arizona has shifted from a place on the political fringe to symbol of a nation whose discourse has lost its way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arizona is not a world apart, but its political culture has often resided at a distance from much of the nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting Casts a Harsh Spotlight on Arizona’s Unique Politics', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Harsh Spotlight on a State&#8217;s Unique Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/660290ab-f2d0-5b8e-a983-4bd521bbbb67', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/660290ab-f2d0-5b8e-a983-4bd521bbbb67'}, {'abstract': 'The East Coast Chamber Orchestra, a conductorless string ensemble, performed at Washington Irving High School in the Peoples’ Symphony Concerts series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/arts/music/10ecco.html', 'snippet': 'The East Coast Chamber Orchestra, a conductorless string ensemble, performed at Washington Irving High School in the Peoples’ Symphony Concerts series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That the East Coast Chamber Orchestra, a conductorless string ensemble formed in 2001 and also known as ECCO, has not yet become a household name among classical music lovers is surely because it appears so infrequently. “We all have other, real jobs,” the violinist Nick Kendall said from the stage as he introduced the group at its Peoples’ Symphony Concerts debut, at Washington Irving High School on Saturday night. “This is kind of like our playground.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/ECCO/ECCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 244, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/ECCO/ECCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 244}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/ECCO/ECCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A String Ensemble at Play: Body Language and Sheer Exuberance', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A String Ensemble at Play: Body Language and Sheer Exuberance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b75f8e-cf5c-544c-8db9-795f9273448f', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b75f8e-cf5c-544c-8db9-795f9273448f'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Wally Cardona was eager for some interference in his “Intervention #4” at the Baryshnikov Arts Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/arts/dance/10intervention.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Wally Cardona was eager for some interference in his “Intervention #4” at the Baryshnikov Arts Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since an intervention is a deliberate effort to alter the course of a situation, it’s clear that the choreographer Wally Cardona is eager for some artistic interference. His “Intervention” series proposes five-day collaborations with experts in any field other than dance. According to program notes, “They enter the studio as strangers, and through their intimate encounter they generate a new work.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/10intervention/10intervention-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Picking Up Where an Artistic Stranger Left Off', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Picking Up Where an Artistic Stranger Left Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardona, Wally', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:02:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/deb96de7-cbaa-5f6e-943f-bc1d4307c004', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deb96de7-cbaa-5f6e-943f-bc1d4307c004'}, {'abstract': '“Pants on Fire’s Metamorphoses,” a witty, modern take on some of Ovid’s tales, is at the Flea Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/theater/reviews/10pants.html', 'snippet': '“Pants on Fire’s Metamorphoses,” a witty, modern take on some of Ovid’s tales, is at the Flea Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “Pants on Fire’s Metamorphoses” sounds as if it’s the kind of show that requires you to do a little homework before turning up at the theater. But it isn’t. The user-friendliness is terrific, though it also ends up being something of a limitation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/PANTS/PANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 461, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/PANTS/PANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/10/arts/PANTS/PANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing Sexes, Species and More', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Pants on Fire’s Metamorphoses'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing Sexes, Species And More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e178d9fd-d651-5663-a0f6-d9b8b30685a7', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e178d9fd-d651-5663-a0f6-d9b8b30685a7'}, {'abstract': 'The state should now take the lead in quieting the voices of intolerance and imposing sensible controls on guns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/opinion/10mon1.html', 'snippet': 'The state should now take the lead in quieting the voices of intolerance and imposing sensible controls on guns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She read the First Amendment on the House floor \x97 including the guarantee of “the right of the people peaceably to assemble” \x97 and then flew home to Arizona to put those words into practice. But when Gabrielle Giffords tried to meet with her constituents in a Tucson parking lot on Saturday, she came face to face with an environment wholly at odds with that constitutional ideal, and she nearly paid for it with her life.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloodshed and Invective in Arizona', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloodshed and Invective in Arizona', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-09T23:16:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cdc2443-4e8e-5d65-97a1-11a9d87ad93b', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cdc2443-4e8e-5d65-97a1-11a9d87ad93b'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Shuman o