nistration has been pushing China to strengthen its currency, was to meet with his Chinese counterpart, Hu Jintao.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The Chinese trade surplus shrank in 2010 as a share of gross domestic product for the third year in a row, a sign, some experts said, that its booming economy was slowly becoming less dependent on exports to drive growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "China's Trade Surplus Decline Suggests Less Reliance on Exports", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "China's Trade Surplus Decline Suggests Less Reliance on Exports", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yuan (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T04:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon LaFraniere and Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaFraniere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d65d7331-a1fe-5249-bc36-e99af691f69c', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d65d7331-a1fe-5249-bc36-e99af691f69c'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 124 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/word-of-the-day-spontaneit