ead_paragraph': 'Now that most students applying to college for next fall’s freshman class have submitted their applications, they will soon turn to the question of paying for that education. Perhaps the most important form they will fill out will be the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or Fafsa; while deadlines vary, some states require its submission by February or March, and may consider requests for financial aid on a first-come, first-serve basis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Your Questions on Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5e25cd7-50a7-5c1b-ac73-a89d52fefc8c', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5e25cd7-50a7-5c1b-ac73-a89d52fefc8c'}, {'abstract': 'Whether the unemployed can use social networking as an effective organizing tool remains to be seen, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/the-unemployed-online/', 'snippet': 'Whether the unemployed can use social networking as an effective organizing tool remains to be seen, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy Folbre is an economics professor at the University of Massachusetts Amherst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unemployed Online', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '