ed to convey a sense of energy and adventure through a blend of feminine florals like rose and jasmine with heady notes of amber and musk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What? Via Verri, a new, limited-edition fragrance from Etro.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | A New Scent From Etro', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T14:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5c07078-d5d4-5c47-bed4-65dd46ba6262', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5c07078-d5d4-5c47-bed4-65dd46ba6262'}, {'abstract': 'The TED speaker series decamped to Detroit, where Craigslist’s Craig Newmark, among other notables, envisioned technology’s role in urban renewal.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/envisioning-the-motor-city-with-or-without-the-motor/', 'snippet': 'The TED speaker series decamped to Detroit, where Craigslist’s Craig Newmark, among other notables, envisioned technology’s role in urban renewal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Ideas percolated about the role of technology in rebuilding the urban landscape at a Lincoln-sponsored TED event on Sunday evening. Guest speakers, who included scholars, entertainers and business leaders, held court on its theme, “New Tomorrows,” while following the TED guidelines that have been a hallmark of the speaker series since its founding in 1984: adhering to 18-minute time limits to say their piece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Envisioning the Motor City, With or Without the Motor', 'kicker': 'Wheels', '