1/10/follow-wheels-on-twitter/', 'snippet': 'The Wheels team is providing blanket coverage of the Detroit auto show on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We do more tweeting before 9 a.m. than most people do all day — especially if that day happens to be the first media day of the Detroit auto show, where the Wheels team is providing presser-to-presser coverage on Twitter. James G. Cobb, our party-hopping Automobiles editor, captured the tone of the morning well before sunrise:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Follow Wheels on Twitter', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T15:10:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Peele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d2a0450-0f0e-5b8a-b462-61986c9c2778', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d2a0450-0f0e-5b8a-b462-61986c9c2778'}, {'abstract': 'The body of  Carlos Castro, 65, was found on the 34th floor of the InterContinental Hotel on Friday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/charges-in-times-square-killing/', 'snippet': 'The body of  Carlos Castro, 65, was found on the 34th floor of the InterContinental Hotel on Friday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 21-year-old companion of the Portuguese celebrity journalist found murdered in his Times Square hotel room has been charged with one count of second-degree murder in his death, the police said. The body of the journalist, Carlos Castro, 65, was found on the 34th floor of the InterContinental Hotel on Friday evening. He had been sexually mutilated, an official said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2nd-Degree Murder Charge in Times Sq. Killing', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Carlos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T15:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Zraick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zraick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e459a6d-ea63-5f5b-b344-d1861232b4f1', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e459a6d-ea63-5f5b-b344-d1861232b4f1'}, {'abstract': 'Del Monte is moving forward with plans to sell itself to a buyout group led by Kohlberg Kravis Roberts after its “go shop” period expired on Saturday without any additional bids.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/del-monte-buyout-moves-forward/', 'snippet': 'Del Monte is moving forward with plans to sell itself to a buyout group led by Kohlberg Kravis Roberts after its “go shop” period expired on Saturday without any additional bids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Del Monte is moving forward with plans to sell itself to a buyout group after its “go shop” period expired on Saturday without attracting additional bids. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Del Monte Buyout Moves Forward', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T15:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/48045f37-dda4-54d3-83f9-019bb9d5a0ad', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48045f37-dda4-54d3-83f9-019bb9d5a0ad'}, {'abstract': 'An Idaho congressman says his aim is to rein in the agency’s regulatory power.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/on-our-radar-house-republican-vows-to-cut-e-p-a-budget/', 'snippet': 'An Idaho congressman says his aim is to rein in the agency’s regulatory power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The newly appointed leader of a House subcommittee that controls the Environmental Protection Agency’s budget, Representative Mike Simpson, Republican of Idaho, says he intends to slash the agency’s funding. “The E.P.A. is the scariest agency in the federal government, an agency run amok,” Mr. Simpson said in a statement on Friday. “Its bloated budget has allowed it to drastically expand its regulatory authority in a way that is hurting our economy and pushing an unwanted government further into the lives of Idahoans.” [The Hill]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: House Republican Vows to Cut E.P.A. Budget', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major