d imprisonment but offered no hint of how he would respond to the charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX \x97 Jared L. Loughner, his head shaved bare and his hands and feet in restraints, was led Monday into a federal courtroom, where he agreed not to contest his continued imprisonment but offered no hint of how he would respond to the murder and attempted murder charges linking him to the Tucson shootings that left six dead and 14 injured.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/11shooting-span/11shooting-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/11/11shooting-span/11shooting-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/11shooting-span/11shooting-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/11shooting-span/11shooting-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/11shooting-span/11shooting-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting Suspect Waives Bail and Is Ruled ‘a Danger’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Arizona Court, Suspect Waives Bail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T15:55:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7859c8ce-93e3-56f7-a806-04bf1de92859', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7859c8ce-93e3-56f7-a806-04bf1de92859'}, {'abstract': 'The German brand continues its march toward becoming a volume leader in the United States with the redesigned midsize sedan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/midsize-passat-carries-volkswagens-outsized-ambitions/', 'snippet': 'The German brand continues its march toward becoming a volume leader in the United States with the redesigned midsize sedan.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Midsize Passat Carries Volkswagen’s Outsize Ambitions', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chattanooga (Tenn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T15:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b3d0689-2d5d-5561-9039-a8f0107cefc1', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b3d0689-2d5d-5561-9039-a8f0107cefc1'}, {'abstract': 'Trent Reznor originally turned down David Fincher’s request to compose the score for “The Social Network.” Now he’s an Oscar favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/the-reluctant-film-composer/', 'snippet': 'Trent Reznor originally turned down David Fincher’s request to compose the score for “The Social Network.” Now he’s an Oscar favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bagger had a much-appreciated chance to let someone else do the heavy lifting on Friday, when we sat in the audience for our colleague Jon Pareles’s Times Talk interview with Trent Reznor. (The pairing of the Nine Inch Nails frontman with the chief pop critic of The Times drew other music luminaries: Nick Zinner of the Yeah Yeah Yeahs was sitting right behind us.) Mr. Pareles and Mr. Reznor, in a dark suit and blue tie, talked about his score with Atticus Ross for “The Social Network.” During the conversation, he showed an early clip of the title sequence from the film, originally set to Elvis Costello’s peppy “Beyond Belief,” making it seem like, as he put it, a “kids at college tomfoolery type of story.” Instead he used haunting piano set amid frayed electronica to give it a much lonelier feel. (Watch the original title sequence in this clip from the Times Talk; it begins at about the 4:40 mark.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reluctant Film Composer', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costello, Elvis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pareles, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons',