ng on the company’s plans to open its first stores in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its bid to open its first stores in New York City, Wal-Mart has begun a full-court-press publicity campaign, complete with advertisements, mailers and a New York-specific Web site that went live Monday. All this as the City Council gears up for a Wednesday hearing on Wal-Mart, which the company has decided not to attend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wal-Mart Opens Major Campaign to Take New York', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T18:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/acf5e2bb-fff9-5f4e-a6d4-0f575d4efac2', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acf5e2bb-fff9-5f4e-a6d4-0f575d4efac2'}, {'abstract': 'With the end of Monday night’s B.C.S. national championship game comes the end of the college football season, which for sports fans everywhere means a huge drop-off in their weekly sports diets.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/fantasy-non-football/', 'snippet': 'With the end of Monday night’s B.C.S. national championship game comes the end of the college football season, which for sports fans everywhere means a huge drop-off in their weekly sports diets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the end of Monday night’s B.C.S. national championship 