haracter St. Jimmy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Billie Joe Armstrong Considers Film and Theater Projects', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Broadway (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T18:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd4e7a1-d133-5f0b-bff6-fc1541dbc9f0', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd4e7a1-d133-5f0b-bff6-fc1541dbc9f0'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley’s in-house quantitative trading unit will become an independent firm, PDT Advisors, by the end of 2012 — as investment banks move to spin off such groups in the wake of Dodd-Frank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/morgan-stanley-and-proprietary-trading-group-to-part-ways/', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley’s in-house quantitative trading unit will become an independent firm, PDT Advisors, by the end of 2012 — as investment banks move to spin off such groups in the wake of Dodd-Frank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morgan Stanley announced on Monday that it would part ways with its in-house quantitative trading unit by the end of 2012. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley Moves Ahead With Quant Spinoff', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam