m Lauren Hutton and American sportswear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pre-Fall Collections, being shown in New York over the next several weeks, arrive in stores in May to fill the gap between bikinis and furs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Max Mara Pre-Fall', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:04:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8afb2c9-ab83-50a0-bf88-e5430e97c0ce', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8afb2c9-ab83-50a0-bf88-e5430e97c0ce'}, {'abstract': 'A new analysis of the best available evidence finds that many children and adults who think they have food allergies are mistaken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/health/11brody.html', 'snippet': 'A new analysis of the best available evidence finds that many children and adults who think they have food allergies are mistaken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Food allergies have generated a great deal of anxiety in recent years, with some schools going so far as to ban popular staples \x97 especially peanut butter \x97 after appeals from worried parents. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11brody/11brody-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11brody/11brody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11brody/11brody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have a Food Allergy? It’s Time to Recheck', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Have a Food Allergy? It’s Time to Recheck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:11:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/671e0608-8ced-59b5-9f3a-04e7106961cd', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/671e0608-8ced-59b5-9f3a-04e7106961cd'}, {'abstract': 'In general, in older children who do not look very distressed, fever is positive evidence of an active immune system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/health/11klass.html', 'snippet': 'In general, in older children who do not look very distressed, fever is positive evidence of an active immune system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fever is common, but fever is complicated. It brings up science and emotion, comfort and calculation. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11klass/11klass-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11klass/11klass-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/science/11klass/11klass-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lifting a Veil of Fear to See a Few Benefits of Fever', 'kicker': '18 and Under', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lifting a Veil of Fear to See a Few Benefits of Fever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fever', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immune System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Perri Klass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37742cca-30b1-5e25-b88a-2c5d48cd661e', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37742cca-30b1-5e25-b88a-2c5d48cd661e'}, {'abstract': 'Fever in a child can be scary for any parent, but knowing when and how to treat a fever can ease the stress of getting through a childhood illness.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/the-benefits-of-fever/', 'snippet': 'Fever in a child can be scary for any parent, but knowing when and how to treat a fever can ease the stress of getting through a childhood illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A child sick with fever is cause for concern for any parent. Confusion about what constitutes a “dangerous” body temperature and the proper dosing of fever medicines only adds to the anxiety. But as Dr. Perri Klass, a pediatrician, writes in this week’s “18 and Under” column:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Benefits of Fever', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fever', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:16:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Bilanow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilanow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd24fd5-67c2-5b0a-80c2-c98c57932fe9', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd24fd5-67c2-5b0a-80c2-c98c57932fe9'}, {'abstract': 'The TV ratings and consumer measurement company is expected to raise $1.5 billion — less than its previous estimate of $2 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/nielsen-lowers-expectations-for-its-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'The TV ratings and consumer measurement company is expected to raise $1.5 billion — less than its previous estimate of $2 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nielsen Holdings, the television ratings and consumer measurement company, is tempering expectations ahead of its initial public offering. According to an amended version of its prospectus, filed on Monday, Nielsen expects to price its shares at $20 to $22.\xa0At the midpoint of that range, Nielsen will raise $1.5 billion — a significant step down from its previous estimate late last year of $2 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 