 there a recent open house you attended where something slightly offbeat — or totally insane — happened?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/new-amenities-for-the-appraisal/', 'snippet': 'Was there a recent open house you attended where something slightly offbeat — or totally insane — happened?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s installment of my column, The Appraisal, may look a little different: it now features some smaller items taken fresh from the real estate pages. Each week it may also include links to recent listings, quotes from long-winded brokers and listings that mention brands of appliances most readers have never heard of. It hopes to capture some of the outrage of the already outrageous real estate world in its own words.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Amenities for The Appraisal', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41926cc1-c8c2-5698-8329-e4a8692c7bb2', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41926cc1-c8c2-5698-8329-e4a8692c7bb2'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets coach told reporters: “This week it’s Rex Ryan against Bill Belichick, it’s personal, it’s about him and myself, that’s what it’s going to come down to.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/sports/football/11vecsey.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets coach told reporters: “This week it’s Rex Ryan against Bill Belichick, it’s personal, it’s about him and myself, that’s what it’s going to come down to.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florham Park, N.J.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/sports/11vecsey-web1/11vecsey-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 821, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/sports/11vecsey-web1/11vecsey-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/sports/11vecsey-web1/11vecsey-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Coach Keeps It Personal', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subject Changes, But Ryan Talks On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:32:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4592aec0-b71f-5489-8579-8a7ff4f4f4c0', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4592aec0-b71f-5489-8579-8a7ff4f4f4c0'}, {'abstract': 'A major Canadian broadcaster reaffirmed its plans to show the criticized miniseries, which was dropped by the History channel in the U.S. but will be shown in about 30 foreign countries and markets.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/the-kennedys-will-still-receive-worldwide-broadcast-as-producers-seek-a-new-u-s-home/', 'snippet': 'A major Canadian broadcaster reaffirmed its plans to show the criticized miniseries, which was dropped by the History channel in the U.S. but will be shown in about 30 foreign countries and markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A major Canadian broadcaster on Monday reaffirmed its plans to show “The Kennedys,” a television miniseries about that political family that was dropped by the History channel, while the project’s producers continued to seek a new American broadcaster and disputed that the miniseries was historically inaccurate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Kennedys’ Will Still Receive Worldwide Broadcast As Producers Seek a New U.S. Home', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy Family', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddeb14fa-3ec7-5321-89cc-44edc452b714', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddeb14fa-3ec7-5321-89cc-44edc452b714'}, {'abstract': 'A set of puzzles about an ancient hand game called morra that provide a fine introduction to game theory.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/numberplay-finger-games/', 'snippet': 'A set of puzzles about an ancient hand game called morra that provide a fine introduction to game theory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary’s surrealist picture above is a depiction, in the spirit of Salvador Dali, of the ancient hand game of morra. Today we’ll explore various versions of this game, such as odd-even morra and guessing morra. The basic game is played in a manner similar to the well-known “rock-paper-scissors.” Two players face each other, initially concealing their hands. One of them says “One, two, three, shoot!” and then both players display a number of fingers from some preset range. The number of points or dollars at stake in each round is equal to the number of fingers displayed. In odd-even morra, one of the players (“Odd”) wins the stakes for the round if the total number of fingers displayed is odd. On the other hand (!), the other player (“Even”) wins the stakes if the total number of fingers is even.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Finger Games', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dali, Salvador', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T19:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/32825572-ffdc-5573-9615-d1d5cd8a6e5a', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32825572-ffdc-5573-9615-d1d5cd8a6e5a'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony Tommasini explores what makes a classical composer great, maybe