 two musicals — “A Little Night Music,” the revival of Stephen Sondheim‘s bittersweet romance, and “In the Heights,” which brought a host of new talents to Broadway — were especially raucous. And leave it to the crowd-pleasingly mouthy star of each show to get the last laughs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stritch and Miranda Get Last Laughs at Finales of ‘Night Music’ and ‘In the Heights’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T20:57:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e63640-8679-5415-9fd6-7120a656fe72', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e63640-8679-5415-9fd6-7120a656fe72'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Mayo, a Crédit Agricole Securities analyst, thinks that JPMorgan Chase is poised to make more acquisitions, quite possibly overseas, and that its stock price may benefit from further deals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/analyst-sees-deal/', 'snippet': 'Mike Mayo, a Crédit Agricole Securities analyst, thinks that JPMorgan Chase is poised to make more acquisitions, quite possibly overseas, and that its stock price may benefit from further deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Mayo, a banking analyst at Crédit Agricole Securities, thinks JPMorgan Chase is poised to make more acquisitions, quite possibly overseas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analyst Says It May Be Deal Time for JPMorgan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mer