d0f1a8'}, {'abstract': 'Dennis Freedman, the former creative director of W, has a new job: creative director of Barneys New York.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/an-editor-goes-to-barneys-but-not-to-shop/', 'snippet': 'Dennis Freedman, the former creative director of W, has a new job: creative director of Barneys New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis Freedman, the former creative director of W, has a new job: creative director of Barneys New York. As part of the continuing changes made by Mark Lee, the retailer’s new chief executive, Mr. Freedman will be responsible for overall creative direction of the store, including its photographic and video images, window displays, visual merchandising and store design. He will be free to engage outside window dressers and other collaborators to create Barneys’ windows, a humorous stage developed by Simon Doonan. He starts next week. Mr. Freedman, who spent 20 years at W, helped shape the look and influence of the magazine through his close contacts with photographers like Bruce Weber, Steven Klein, Juergen Teller and Philip-Lorca diCorcia. He left the magazine last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Editor Goes to Barneys, but Not to Shop', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doonan, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedman, Dennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T21:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported