nths that Apple’s iPhone would be coming to Verizon early this year, ending more than three years of exclusivity with AT&T. Still, the news on Friday that Verizon would announce an iPhone running on its CDMA network at a Tuesday news\xa0 conference in New York generated plenty of new buzz — and new enthusiasm for Apple on Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon iPhone Buzz Adds to Apple’s Shares', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T22:15:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ee1b12b-4fef-51eb-b715-962547a6f1cc', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ee1b12b-4fef-51eb-b715-962547a6f1cc'}, {'abstract': 'Dirk Meyer has resigned and will be succeeded by the chief financial officer Thomas J. Seifert while the company searches for a permanent replacement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/technology/11chip.html', 'snippet': 'Dirk Meyer has resigned and will be succeeded by the chief financial officer Thomas J. Seifert while the company searches for a permanent replacement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chip maker Advanced Micro Devices on Monday pushed out its 49-year-old chief executive, Dirk Meyer, in a move that took industry analysts by surprise.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chief Ousted in Surprise at A.M.D.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chief Ousted In Surprise At A.M.D.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Susp