erback Darrelle Revis, whom he declared the “best player in football.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone in Patriots camp waiting for bulletin-board material in advance of this week’s Round 3 showdown against the Jets got it hand-delivered on Monday. (Were you really surprised it took this long?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Who? Ryan Says Revis Is Best Player in Football', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revis, Darrelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T23:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cce31679-d623-55b8-a90e-89067a25dd0e', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cce31679-d623-55b8-a90e-89067a25dd0e'}, {'abstract': 'Asian Cup, where the Axis of Evil, in the words of the former American President George W. Bush, comes to play … soccer. Iran, Iraq and North Korea play first-round matches on Tuesday', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/ghotbi/', 'snippet': 'Asian Cup, where the Axis of Evil, in the words of the former American President George W. Bush, comes to play … soccer. Iran, Iraq and North Korea play first-round matches on Tuesday', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — Iran, Iraq and North Korea — the Axis of Evil, in the words of former President George W. Bush — all play first-round matches on Tuesday at the Asian Cup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Ghotbi Speaks … in English', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doha (Qatar)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-10T23:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Behrooz Afrakhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Behrooz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afrakhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/23212339-d854-550b-8002-3c42d44973b1', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23212339-d854-550b-8002-3c42d44973b1'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Hetherington shuttles among wildly disparate worlds. “Diary” is his impressionistic view of the sharp moments in his life and the blurred transitions among them.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/tim-hetheringtons-disquieting-diary/', 'snippet': 'Tim Hetherington shuttles among wildly disparate worlds. “Diary” is his impressionistic view of the sharp moments in his life and the blurred transitions among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The documentarian Tim Hetherington is no stranger to the readers of Lens, who have seen accounts of his book “Infidel” and his film “Restrepo,” concerning an American platoon in the Korengal Valley in Afghanistan; and the book “Long Story Bit by Bit: Liberia Retold” and the short film “Liberian Graffiti.” It’s easy to wonder how Mr. Hetherington manages to shuttle between home in a global capital like New York — where he is a contributing photographer to Vanity Fair — and outposts where the world seems forever at war with itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Hetherington’s Disquieting ‘Diary’', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biographical Information', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hetherington, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Korengal Valley (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T00:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap and Karly Domb Sadof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Karly', 'middlename': 'Domb', 'lastname': 'Sadof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/271af700-de97-5e5d-87ed-8f14687f55dd', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/271af700-de97-5e5d-87ed-8f14687f55dd'}, {'abstract': 'There isn’t much to do over on campus during winter break except eat, sleep and play basketball.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/10/living-like-the-pros-at-vanderbilt/', 'snippet': 'There isn’t much to do over on campus during winter break except eat, sleep and play basketball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I hope everyone had a wonderful holiday season. I got everything I wanted, including a nice cardigan sweater and a new cookbook. What I didn’t get however, were the new Beats by Dre headphones, which were apparently the “must-have” gift of the season, judging by the fact that every guy on the team seems to now have a pair. Who needs a radio anyway? ', 'source': 'The N