s', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T03:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton, Charlie Savage and Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bc42666-4a09-50c1-b64c-f1e323ec70bb', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bc42666-4a09-50c1-b64c-f1e323ec70bb'}, {'abstract': 'The attack in Tucson is just the latest wave in America’s endless ocean of violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/opinion/11herbert.html', 'snippet': 'The attack in Tucson is just the latest wave in America’s endless ocean of violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By all means, condemn the hateful rhetoric that has poured so much poison into our political discourse. The crazies don’t kill in a vacuum, and the vilest of our political leaders and commentators deserve to be called to account for their demagoguery and the danger that comes with it. But that’s the easy part.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Herbert_New/Herbert_New-thumbSt