come back to try to shoot them, too? And is it still safe to go to the supermarket? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/us/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/11/us/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/us/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Victim’s School, Shock, Sorrow and Nightmares', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Victim’s School, Shock, Sorrow and Nightmares', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotions)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Christina Taylor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T03:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b39aa3d-e0f5-5c70-bf80-4af5c1719b45', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b39aa3d-e0f5-5c70-bf80-4af5c1719b45'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at the work of Odette Lupis as a freelance photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST--Lupis.html', 's