Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lukashenko’s Gulag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sannikov, Andrei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0772bba0-658d-5052-a023-8a780a60f2ca', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0772bba0-658d-5052-a023-8a780a60f2ca'}, {'abstract': 'The Iron Market, a landmark in Port-au-Prince, has been rebuilt and is to be inaugurated, a rare bright spot in Haiti’s reconstruction after last January’s devastating earthquake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/world/americas/11haiti.html', 'snippet': 'The Iron Market, a landmark in Port-au-Prince, has been rebuilt and is to be inaugurated, a rare bright spot in Haiti’s reconstruction after last January’s devastating earthquake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti \x97 A year after the earthquake that devastated Haiti’s capital, just 5 percent of the rubble has been removed. The National Palace still sits in a half-demolished pile. In its shadow, on the Champs de Mars plaza, tens of thousands of Haitians live under torn or frayed tents and tarpaulins. All over the city, buildings remain pancaked, keeled over, smashed \x97 just as they were after the earthquake on Jan. 12, 2010. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/world/HAITI-1/HAITI-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/11/world/HAITI-1/HAITI-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/world/HAITI-1/HAITI-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/world/HAITI-1/HAITI-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/world/HAITI-1/HAITI-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Symbol of Hope for Haiti, a Landmark Again Stands Tall', 'kicker': 'Port-Au-Prince Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Symbol of Hope for Haiti, a Landmark Again Stands Tall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Denis", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:17:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pooja Bhatia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pooja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bhatia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1264733d-2881-5a1b-902b-76200ccd95c2', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1264733d-2881-5a1b-902b-76200ccd95c2'}, {'abstract': 'You can practically smell spring coming in the well-thumbed, dog-eared pages of seed catalogues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/opinion/11tue4.html', 'snippet': 'You can practically smell spring coming in the well-thumbed, dog-eared pages of seed catalogues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps this is the year to plant oca and yacon. Or maybe pink blueberries, a double row of kohlrabi, and a patch of Galeux d’Eysines pumpkins. Anything is possible in January, when the seed catalogues have nearly all arrived. You can practically smell spring coming in their well-thumbed, dog-eared pages, where every cabbage, every cucumber, is perfectly ripe. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Whiff of Spring', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Whiff of Spring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seeds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2793a54d-9613-5411-bdea-fef5d808b5dd', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2793a54d-9613-5411-bdea-fef5d808b5dd'}, {'abstract': 'The rankings grade more than 12,000 of the city’s 80,000 public school teachers based on the progress their students made on standardized tests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/education/11data.html', 'snippet': 'The rankings grade more than 12,000 of the city’s 80,000 public school teachers based on the progress their students made on standardized tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Manhattan judge ruled Monday that the city may release performance rankings of thousands of teachers to the public, denying a request by the teachers union