n were shot to death between 2:45 and about 6 p.m. on Monday afternoon, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/nyregion/11shoot.html', 'snippet': 'A 14-year-old boy and two men were shot to death between 2:45 and about 6 p.m. on Monday afternoon, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 14-year-old boy and two men were shot to death in three separate attacks within four hours in the city on Monday afternoon, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Fatally Shot in Separate Attacks Within 4 Hours', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Fatally Shot in Separate Attacks Within 4 Hours', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6d0f52-0d32-5cbb-9d9f-3fa0ac9da1dd', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6d0f52-0d32-5cbb-9d9f-3fa0ac9da1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Winters was the commanding officer of the Army unit whose World War II exploits were recounted in the book and miniseries “Band of Brothers.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/us/11winters.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Winters was the commanding officer of the Army unit whose World War II exploits were recounted in the book and miniseries “Band of Brothers.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Winters, the commanding officer of Easy Company, the Army unit whose gritty combat from the beaches of Normandy to the capture of Hitler’s mountain retreat was recounted in the book and television series “Band of Brothers,” died on Jan. 2 in Campbelltown, Pa. He was 92 and lived in Hershey, Pa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/us/WINTERS1-obit/WINTERS1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/us/WINTERS1-obit/WINTERS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/us/WINTERS1-obit/WINTERS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard Winters Dies at 92; Led ‘Band of Brothers’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Richard Winters, 92; Led ‘Band of Brothers’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:36:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3d5c307-3ea7-52d3-ae45-5e671d4cbbc3', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3d5c307-3ea7-52d3-ae45-5e671d4cbbc3'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers hold the Ducks’ offense in check, winning, 22-19, on a field goal in the final seconds.', 'web_url': 'https://w