nyt://slideshow/56725340-6dcf-5971-bdd4-0578a70017ec'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,440 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/us/11list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,440 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,440 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:37:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9498b393-2386-50d6-bc2f-f6fdb15b9016', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9498b393-2386-50d6-bc2f-f6fdb15b9016'}, {'abstract': 'A lobbyist for the energy industry was found dead in her sport utility vehicle early Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/us/11brfs-LOBBYISTISFO_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A lobbyist for the energy industry was found dead in her sport utility vehicle early Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lobbyist for the energy industry was found dead in her sport utility vehicle early Monday. The lobbyist, Ashley Turton, 37, a regulatory affairs analyst for Progress Energy, which is based in North Carolina, appeared to have been backing out of her garage when her car hit it and caught fire. She is the wife of Daniel Turton, White House deputy director for legislative affairs for the House of Representatives. The authorities have not yet identified Ms. Turton as the driver, but her employer issued a statement on Monday saying she had died. Ms. Turton had served as the chief of staff for Representative Rosa DeLauro, Democrat of Connecticut.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lobbyist Is Found Dead in Burned Car', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lobbyist Is Found Dead in Burned Car', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:42:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cad08eb9-ea40-5cdf-886b-18db5ae981fc', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cad08eb9-ea40-5cdf-886b-18db5ae981fc'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge on Monday ordered a former C.I.A. officer to be transferred to Virginia to face charges that he leaked classified government information to a reporter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/us/11brfs-EXCIAOFFICER_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge on Monday ordered a former C.I.A. officer to be transferred to Virginia to face charges that he leaked classified government information to a reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Monday ordered a former C.I.A. officer to be transferred to Virginia to face charges that he leaked classified government information to a reporter. The former officer, Jeffrey A. Sterling, 43, was indicted last month on charges that he shared restricted information about a secret government program meant to thwart unnamed countries’ weapons programs with a journalist, widely identified as James Risen of The New York Times. Mr. Risen wrote about a C.I.A. attempt to disrupt Iranian nuclear research in a 2006 book. That material did not appear in The Times. At a court appearance on Monday in St. Louis, not far from his home, Mr. Sterling, who worked for the C.I.A. from 1993 until he was fired in 2002, agreed to the transfer to Virginia, where the C.I.A. headquarters are located and the charges were filed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Ex-C.I.A. Officer Will Be Extradited', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | MIDWEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Ex-C.I.A. Officer Will Be Extradited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T04:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malcolm Gay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malcolm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dd65814-d9f9-5efe-8642-e76faa821357', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dd65814-d9f9-5efe-8642-e76faa821357'}, {'abstract': 'Otmar Issing, the influential former chief economist of the European Central Bank, warns that the euro’s existence could be threatened unless member countries find a way to control spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.co