acts of aggressive gamesmanship in “Too Late! antigone (contest #2),” a radical retelling of the story of Antigone by the Italian company Motus. (The show, part of the Under the Radar Festival, is performed in English with Italian subtitles.) The actors barely have time to catch their breaths to deliver their lines before another physically demanding task — swinging from a rope, for example — begins. The audience has front-row seats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under the Radar: 5 Questions About ‘Too Late! antigone (contest #2)’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T16:52:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebbce796-d6ae-5646-b1d8-5ffb4f5cc0aa', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebbce796-d6ae-5646-b1d8-5ffb4f5cc0aa'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/fafsaq-and-a/', 'snippet': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that most students applying to college for next fall’s freshman class have submitted their applications, they (and their families) will begin to tackle the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or Fafsa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Part 1: Answers to Readers’ Questions on Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T16:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kantrowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantrowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/330ddebc-e469-55c9-8a86-47e146d83372', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/330ddebc-e469-55c9-8a86-47e146d83372'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge funds, large and small, are feeling the pinch, with insurance premiums up 6 percent to 18 percent last year, according to one survey.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/hedge-funds-pinched-by-health-care-reform/', 'snippet': 'Hedge funds, large and small, are feeling the pinch, with insurance premiums up 6 percent to 18 percent last year, according to one survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Small businesses aren’t the only ones hit by the health care reform. Hedge funds, large and small, are feeling the pinch, too, at least according to one report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Funds Pinched by Health Care Reform', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T16:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '',