Donohue, president of the U.S. Chamber of Commerce, applauded “a new tone coming out of the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/chamber-praises-new-white-house-tone/', 'snippet': 'Thomas J. Donohue, president of the U.S. Chamber of Commerce, applauded “a new tone coming out of the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are further signs of thawing in the often fraught relationship between the White House and the U.S. Chamber of Commerce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Chamber of Commerce Praises New White House Tone', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donohue, Thomas J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chamber of Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5a7a9c4-40de-5fa0-821f-cd01eaa6a64f', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5a7a9c4-40de-5fa0-821f-cd01eaa6a64f'}, {'abstract': 'A gathering is scheduled for Joe’s Pub on Jan. 20.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/live-and-in-print-laphams-celebrities/', 'snippet': 'A gathering is scheduled for Joe’s Pub on Jan. 20.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you need to celebrate the publication of a highbrow journal devoted to celebrity? Highbrow celebrities, of course. Which is why Oskar Eustis, artistic director of the Public Theater, and the actors Philip Seymour Hoffman, Linda Emond and Mandy Patinkin are coming to Joe’s Pub on Jan. 20 for an evening devoted to the release of Lapham’s Quarterly’s Winter 2011 issue “Celebrity.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live and in Print: Lapham’s Celebrities', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eustis, Oskar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Philip Seymour', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapham, Lewis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patinkin, Mandy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Joe's Pub", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lapham's Quarterly", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e7f979-04b0-5e62-a98d-5378eddf65bd', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e7f979-04b0-5e62-a98d-5378eddf65bd'}, {'abstract': 'With memories of the botched response to last month’s blizzard still fresh, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the city had made significant changes to its emergency procedures that would result in a better-coordinated response.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/mayor-promises-better-storm-response/', 'snippet': 'With memories of the botched response to last month’s blizzard still fresh, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the city had made significant changes to its emergency procedures that would result in a better-coordinated response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:56 p.m. | Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Tuesday sought to reassure New Yorkers that the city would not fall short in its handling of a snowstorm expected to hit on Tuesday night. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Promises Better Storm Response', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Emergency Management (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:42:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9494bb74-3801-51e4-a55f-aa13867079a2', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9494bb74-3801-51e4-a55f-aa13867079a2'}, {'abstract': 'The American Society of Cinematographers named a mix of veterans and newcomers for its nominees, including one very humble soul.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/cinematographers-pan-across-generations/', 'snippet': 'The American Society of Cinematographers named a mix of veterans and newcomers for its nominees, including one very humble soul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Society of Cinematographers announced its nominees late on Monday, and it was a nice mix of veterans and newcomers – although still all the films you would expect. Matthew Libatique (“Black Swan”), Wally Pfister (“Inception”), Danny Cohen (“The King’s Speech”), Jeff Cronenweth (“The Social Network”) and Roger Deakins (“True Grit”) got the nod. Mr. Deakins is the old hand of the group, having been nominated nine times and won twice, for “The Shawshank Redemption” in 1995 and “The Man Who Wasn’t There” in 2002. Mr. Deakins will also receive a lifetime achievement award. Mr. Pfister has been recognized before, and Mr. Cohen, Mr. Cronenweth and Mr. Libatique are all first-timers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cinematographers Pan Across Generations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9565e388-cb3a-56b6-9f75-f0b1b9766589', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9565e388-cb3a-56b6-9f75-f0b1b9766589'}, {'abstract': 'Byron Dorgan of North Dakota and Bob Bennett of Utah left the Senate on Jan. 4. They became lobbyists one week later.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/two-former-senators-become-lobbyists-in-record-time/', 'snippet': 'Byron Dorgan of North Dakota and Bob Bennett of Utah left the Senate on Jan. 4. They became lobbyists one week later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That didn’t take long.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Former Senators Become Lobbyists — In Record Time', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c08e76c4-dd5d-5ca5-94a1-22ad26fdcac2', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c08e76c4-dd5d-5ca5-94a1-22ad26fdcac2'}, {'abstract': 'Only three months after taking over as publisher of Twelve, a small imprint of Grand Central Publishing, Susan Lehman has been abruptly replaced, Grand Central said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/at-twelve-a-brief-chapter-ends/', 'snippet': 'Only three months after taking over as publisher of Twelve, a small imprint of Grand Central Publishing, Susan Lehman has been abruptly replaced, Grand Central said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:00 p.m. | Updated Only three months after taking over as publisher of Twelve, a small imprint of Grand Central Publishing, Susan Lehman has been abruptly replaced, Grand Central said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Twelve, a Brief Chapter Ends', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehman, Susan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Central Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T17:46:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed8c9b6e-d98e-5f1f-a195-c22d7e685c84', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed8c9b6e