der\' by Axis, President Says\n</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CASABLANCA, French Morocco, Jan. 24 (Delayed) -- President Roosevelt and Prime Minister Churchill today concluded a momentous ten-day conference in which they planned Allied offensives of 1943 aimed at what the President called the "unconditional surrender of the Axis powers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ROOSEVELT, CHURCHILL MAP 1943 WAR STRATEGY AT TEN-DAY CONFERENCE HELD IN CASABLANCA; GIRAUD AND DE GAULLE, PRESENT, AGREE ON AIMS', 'kicker': 'January 15, 1943', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T19:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': '<h5>By DREW MIDDLETON </h5>\n<h5>Special Cable to The New York Times</h5>', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6edb040-db32-50f5-a44b-47cfded7ebf2', 'word_count': 1433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6edb040-db32-50f5-a44b-47cfded7ebf2'}, {'abstract': 'Stefan Jacoby, the Swedish automaker’s chief executive, framed the exercise as an experiment in battery-pack safety.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/crashed-electric-volvo-c30-displayed-at-detroit-auto-show/', 'snippet': 'Stefan Jacoby, the Swedish automaker’s chief executive, framed the exercise as an experiment in battery-pack safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — What happens when an electric car hits a wall at 40 miles an hour? For the answer, Volvo crashed one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crashed Electric Volvo C30 Displayed at Detroit Auto Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'