 {'abstract': 'Visitors hoping to wait out the expected snowstorm may find hotels booked up, a change from last month’s day-after-Christmas blizzard.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/any-hotel-room-in-a-storm-good-luck/', 'snippet': 'Visitors hoping to wait out the expected snowstorm may find hotels booked up, a change from last month’s day-after-Christmas blizzard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For people hoping to wait out the storm in a hotel room in New York City, the headaches started the moment the forecasters started talking about snow. They discovered that reservations were hard to come by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Any Hotel Room in a Storm? Good Luck', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Javits, Jacob K, Convention Center (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marriott Marquis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Retail Federation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d78c687-51bb-57d6-8096-f0647db0d1f8', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d78c687-51bb-57d6-8096-f0647db0d1f8'}, {'abstract': "the black Baptist minister who led the American Civil Rights Movement in the 1950's and '60's with his doctrine of nonviolent resistance", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0115.html', 'snippet': "the black Baptist minister who led the American Civil Rights Movement in the 1950's and '60's with his doctrine of nonviolent resistance", 'lead_paragraph': 'To many million of American Negroes, the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. was the prophet of their crusade for racial equality. He was their voice of anguish, their eloquence in humiliation, their battle cry for human dignity. He forged for them the weapons of nonviolence that withstood and blunted the ferocity of segregation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martin Luther King Jr.: Leader of Millions in Nonviolent Drive for Racial Justice', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:04:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By MURRAY SCHUMACH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Murray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SCHUMACH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/099ab380-883f-5050-b7a4-69cb6850dfa5', 'word_count': 3678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099ab380-883f-5050-b7a4-69cb6850dfa5'}, {'abstract': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">National League Champions Beat Kansas City, 35-10, in Super Bowl Game</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/big/0115.html', 'snippet': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">National League Champions Beat Kansas City, 35-10, in Super Bowl Game</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGLES, Jan. 15 -- Bryan Bartlett (Bart) Starr, the quarterback for the Green Bay Packers, led his team to a 35-10 victory over the Kansas City Chiefs today in the first professional football game between the champions of the National and American Leagues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'GREEN BAY WINS FOOTBALL TITLE', 'kicker': 'January 16, 1967', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:04:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': '<h5>By WILLIAM N. WALLACE </h5>\n<h5>Special to The New York Times </h5>', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fec0df6-c2fc-53b1-8080-1bfada45d078', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fec0df6-c2fc-53b1-8080-1bfada45d078'}, {'abstract': 'But “Running Wilde” may have reached the end of its run.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/fox-keeps-raising-hope-alive-with-order-for-second-season/', 'snippet': 'But “Running Wilde” may have reached the end of its run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of Fox’s new sitcoms this season, “Raising Hope,” will graduate to sophomore year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox Keeps ‘Raising Hope’ Alive With Order for Second Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:10:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/73e03ca2-2b23-5f7e-8783-ac272a0403a0', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73e03ca2-2b23-5f7e-8783-ac272a0403a0'}, {'abstract': 'Lesson Plan | Considering and addressing the reasons why many people do not prepare and eat home-cooked meals, and practicing the skills involved in basic food preparation.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/cook-eat-love-learning-to-prepare-nutritious-meals/', 'snippet': 'Lesson Plan | Considering and addressing the reasons why many people do not prepare and eat home-cooked meals, and practicing the skills involved in basic food preparation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | Why don’t people cook at home as often as they once did? How can home cooking help people eat more healthfully? In this lesson, students debate the merits of nutrition, economics, quality-of-life and taste when it comes to home cooking and restaurant meals. They even roll up their sleeves to make a salad, stir-fry or grain dish, recipes the Times food writer Mark Bittman claims will make a home cook out of anyone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cook, Eat … Love? Learning to Prepare Nutritious Meals', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:18:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2279ac15-2c63-5c49-8be8-b24901dd9c19', 'word_count': 1620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2279ac15-2c63-5c49-8be8-b24901dd9c19'}, {'abstract': 'Rabanne’s ubiquitous chain mail returns, in the form of a bag.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/space-capsule/', 'snippet': 'Rabanne’s ubiquitous chain mail returns, in the form of a bag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coco Chanel once dismissed Paco Rabanne as the “steelworker of fashion,” for his use of metal in his stubbornly futuristic designs. Rabanne, who is responsible for some acidic put-downs of his own, certainly lived up to the moniker with his ubiquitous chain mail dresses of the 1960s. Less known, however, is his 69 bag from a collection of that year. Celebrating the designer’s enduring vision of fashion, Comme des Garçons has teamed up with Paco Rabanne to release nine variations on the bag, including versions in clear, acrylic Perspex, pink metallic suede, and black rubber. This is one chain mail you’ll be happy to receive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Space Capsule', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b2a8091-8bf5-58b3-b738-39ed25a896cb', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b2a8091-8bf5-58b3-b738-39ed25a896cb'}, {'abstract': 'The “Tosca” created by the Swiss director Luc Bondy, revived at the Metropolitan Opera, shows some improvement over its initial run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/arts/music/12tosca.html', 'snippet': 'The “Tosca” created by the Swiss director Luc Bondy, revived at the Metropolitan Opera, shows some improvement over its initial run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If dull and uneven, with flashes of insight, is preferable to frustrating, then the Metropolitan Opera’s current production of Puccini’s “Tosca,” created last season by the Swiss director Luc Bondy and revived on Monday night, showed a marked improvement over its initial run. At its opening night in 2009, the staging was lustily booed by the audience and denounced by most critics. Revived in April 2010 with a starry new cast \x97 and without Mr. Bondy’s direct supervision \x97 the notorious production was deemed a qualified success by many audience members and critics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/arts/TOSCA/TOSCA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 898, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/arts/TOSCA/TOSCA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/arts/TOSCA/TOSCA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tosca,’ With Tinkering, Cooler Tempers and a Fill-In Tenor', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Tosca,’ With Tinkering, Cooler Tempers and a Fill-In Tenor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radvanovsky, Sondra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALAGNA, ROBERTO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bondy, Luc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:23:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cd0378-b04b-5255-aa8a-f69a195d83de', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cd0378-b04b-5255-aa8a-f69a195d83de'}, {'abstract': 'Parenting children who suffer from serious mental illnesses.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/a-killers-parents/', 'snippet': 'Parenting children who suffer from serious mental illnesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Jared Lee Loughner’s unhinged grin staring out from so many Web sites and newspapers today, parents of troubled young adults are stepping forward, giving glimpses into the pain and impotence that comes when your child has mental illness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Tucson, Parents Wonder ‘What If’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:31:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8798cc3-c820-597b-8406-00698e313009', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8798cc3-c820-597b-8406-00698e313009'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Reich, a professional organizer, responds to readers’ questions.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/answers-about-getting-organized/', 'snippet': 'Barbara Reich, a professional organizer, responds to readers’ questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barbara Reich, a professional organizer who was the subject of a recent Metropolitan article by Elissa Gootman, is taking readers’ questions this week about getting organized. You can ask a question here or find previous and subsequent installments in this Q & A here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers About Getting Organized', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a18b343-029b-5fb4-937f-2f1b303705ef', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a18b343-029b-5fb4-937f-2f1b303705ef'}, {'abstract': 'With Verizon now claiming an iPhone of its own, Apple may make some further inroads into the lucrative world of enterprise business, including major banks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/with-verizon-will-apple-take-a-bite-of-more-enterprise/', 'snippet': 'With Verizon now claiming an iPhone of its own, Apple may make some further inroads into the lucrative world of enterprise business, including major banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few companies could command as much attention for bringing an existing phone to a new telephone network as Apple, whose iPhone is coming to Verizon Wireless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Verizon, Will Apple Take a Bite of More Enterprise?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e9652d7-b699-5ebd-9180-0c513ee86c32', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e9652d7-b699-5ebd-9180-0c513ee86c32'}, {'abstract': 'Until June 23, the Tennessee men’s basketball team’s third assistant coach is the only one allowed to recruit off campus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/sports/basketball/12tennessee.html', 'snippet': 'Until June 23, the Tennessee men’s basketball team’s third assistant coach is the only one allowed to recruit off campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KNOXVILLE, Tenn. \x97 Inside Thompson-Boling Arena, Jason Shay, an assistant with the Tennessee men’s basketball team, looked down at his standardized letter jacket with the orange “T” embroidered on the front. It might not be orange enough, he thought, for his recruiting adventure over the next five and a half months.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/sports/12tennessee-web1/12tennessee-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 633, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/sports/12tennessee-web1/12tennessee-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'