value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a1483a-0743-5133-a9d5-a46ea669d014', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a1483a-0743-5133-a9d5-a46ea669d014'}, {'abstract': 'An appreciation of scientists pursuing knowledge in extreme situations, including in the belly of a blizzard.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/a-look-inside-the-belly-of-the-blizzard/', 'snippet': 'An appreciation of scientists pursuing knowledge in extreme situations, including in the belly of a blizzard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, I pushed the idea of developing a reality-TV show, “Extremities,” on science at the edge of what’s possible, sort of Mythbusters with a rotating cast that’d include biologists climbing cliffs in Greenland to study nesting falcons, the team I joined on the sea ice near the North Pole and — certainly — scientists driving around Oswego, N.Y., with portable Doppler radars to plumb the innards of storms that produce that region’s astounding lake-effect snow, one result of which is depicted in this photo (NOAA): ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A look Inside the Belly of the Blizzard', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeller, Tom Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Science Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Severe Storms Laboratory', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Everglades (Fla)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenland', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Pole', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc1176f-60d9-5c3d-9b56-ceac87f21120', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc1176f-60d9-5c3d-9b56-ceac87f21120'}, {'abstract': 'Mapping the euro crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/geography-lessons/', 'snippet': 'Mapping the euro crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Best snark about the euro crisis yet from Satyajit Das, who suggests that European leaders, as part of their educational mission, are giving us geography lessons. First they told us that Ireland wasn’t Greece; then they told us that Portugal wasn’t Ireland; now they’re telling us that Spain isn’t Greece, Ireland, or Portugal; soon the Belgians will be improving our spelling, telling us that there’s no B in PIGS.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geography Lessons', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:53:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/edcab34b-f19a-50ce-b733-d1a0fb89a4cb', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edcab34b-f19a-50ce-b733-d1a0fb89a4cb'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s restaurant review: Ciano, on East 22nd Street, in the space that Diner’s Journal readers may remember as Beppe.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/reviewing-ciano/', 'snippet': 'This week’s restaurant review: Ciano, on East 22nd Street, in the space that Diner’s Journal readers may remember as Beppe.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Ciano', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallante, Shea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatiron District (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb574317-6fc8-5268-9a41-3ed30ff876aa', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb574317-6fc8-5268-9a41-3ed30ff876aa'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Shea Gallante’s food at his new restaurant on East 22nd Street is a kind of Italian home cooking made grand and attractive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/dining/reviews/12rest.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Shea Gallante’s food at his new restaurant on East 22nd Street is a kind of Italian home cooking made grand and attractive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are two remarkable things going on at Ciano, the casual, new-style Italian restaurant that Shea Gallante opened a few months ago on East 22nd Street.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12rest-span/12rest-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12rest-span/12rest-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12rest-span/REST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12rest-span/12rest-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12rest-span/12rest-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ciano', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning by Not Trying So Hard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatiron District (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallante, Shea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bc7fbe2-b2a2-5a88-9672-d5d04e3d8a7e', 'word_count': 1357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bc7fbe2-b2a2-5a88-9672-d5d04e3d8a7e'}, {'abstract': "Doctors give the latest on Representative Gabrielle Giffords; lawmakers weigh new security measures after Saturday's shooting; and Verizon announces it will sell the iPhone. ", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/continuous/1248069551296/timescast-january-11-2011.html', 'snippet': "Doctors give the latest on Representative Gabrielle Giffords; lawmakers weigh new security measures after Saturday's shooting; and Verizon announces it will sell the iPhone. ", 'lead_paragraph': "Doctors give the latest on Representative Gabrielle Giffords; lawmakers weigh new security measures after Saturday's shooting; and Verizon announces it will sell the iPhone. ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/11/continuous/10969_1_tc-011111_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/11/continuous/10969_1_tc-011111_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | January 11, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T20:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Brent McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/fbe64b0d-14be-5c10-bf5e-96ec31327fb4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/fbe64b0d-14be-5c10-bf5e-96ec31327fb4'}, {'abstract': '“Detroit,” a new play about American dissipation with some deliciously tart roles, will be produced on Broadway in early fall of 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/detroit-on-broadway/', 'snippet': '“Detroit,” a new play about American dissipation with some deliciously tart roles, will be produced on Broadway in early fall of 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Detroit,” a new play about American dissipation with some deliciously tart roles, set in the adjacent backyards of two recovering addicts and their anxious middle-class neighbors, will be produced on Broadway in early fall of 2011 under the direction of Austin Pendleton, the producers announced on Tuesday. No casting was announced for the five-character play, which will mark the Broadway debut of the playwright Lisa D’Amour, a well-known downtown writer and artist. The Steppenwolf Theater Company in Chicago produced “Detroit” last fall, which included Laurie Metcalf (“November” on Broadway, “Roseanne” on ABC) as the middle-class wife. The lead producers will be Jeffrey Richards, Jerry Frankel and Debbie Bisno, in association with Steppenwolf; Mr. Richards and Mr. Frankel previously teamed with Steppenwolf for its transfers of “August: Osage County” and “Superior Donuts” to Broadway. Performance dates and a theater will be announced later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Detroit’ to Reside on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalf, Laurie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Steppenwolf Theatre Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dde3d1d-dea9-5c94-98a7-258819d2c450', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dde3d1d-dea9-5c94-98a7-258819d2c450'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Exchange building offers artists and entrepreneurs cheap rent and constant collaboration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/realestate/commercial/12incubate.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Exchange building offers artists and entrepreneurs cheap rent and constant collaboration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Al Attara bought a former bank on Flatbush Avenue in Brooklyn 32 years ago for under $250,000, he envisioned it as a complex in which artists, architects and furniture designers would work side by side and share ownership of the 45,000-square-foot space.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/business/Incubate2/Incubate2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/