architects and entrepreneurs, and creativity abounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A seven-story building in Flatbush is home to artists, architects and entrepreneurs, and creativity abounds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House of Ideas in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:23:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/be340424-2f8a-5d96-9f6b-ff58ad873bb4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/be340424-2f8a-5d96-9f6b-ff58ad873bb4'}, {'abstract': 'Day meets night in Alber Elbaz’s pre-fall collection for Lanvin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/just-one-look-lanvin-pre-fall-collection/', 'snippet': 'Day meets night in Alber Elbaz’s pre-fall collection for Lanvin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pre-Fall Collections, being shown in New York over the next several weeks, arrive in stores in May to fill the gap between bikinis and furs.Alber Elbaz opened his pre-fall show with an observation: more women, he says, are wearing evening clothes during the day. The collection that followed might very well be the stuff of self-fulfilling prophecy. An ivory silk floor-length skirt, for example, took on the ease of trousers when paired with a thick ribbed sweater. But the best looks swung the other way, too. Here, a blouse and tweed skirt — daytime staples — are gussied up with bronze Lurex and a dollop of fur. (The wolf is optional.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Lanvin Pre-Fall Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/034b534e-0020-5630-8f7a-ed48f5d1cedc', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034b534e-0020-5630-8f7a-ed48f5d1cedc'}, {'abstract': 'Kathryn Weatherup, the force behind the craft cocktails at her bars in Brooklyn and TriBeCa, is the rare bartender who doesn’t brook banter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/fashion/13close.html', 'snippet': 'Kathryn Weatherup, the force behind the craft cocktails at her bars in Brooklyn and TriBeCa, is the rare bartender who doesn’t brook banter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH its pyrotechnics, suspenders and tattoos, the cocktail scene in New York appears, at times, to revolve around a troupe of Barnum & Bailey escapees. But those who frequent Weather Up, a Prohibition-style cocktail lounge, need not worry. Its 34-year-old namesake and owner, Kathryn Weatherup, is tall and blond, an unbearded lady. She is what, in some circles, is called a tall drink of water. Although here, a sloe gin fizz might be more appropriate.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/13/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Anti-Banter Bartender', 'kicker': 'Up Close', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Anti-Banter Bartender', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bartenders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua David Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f9b061-fafc-5bca-a712-2584e600bdbd', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f9b061-fafc-5bca-a712-2584e600bdbd'}, {'abstract': 'When “Rock of Ages” moves to the Helen Hayes Theater in March, it will offer an unusual discount ticket program.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/a-move-and-early-bird-specials-for-rock-of-ages/', 'snippet': 'When “Rock of Ages” moves to the Helen Hayes Theater in March, it will offer an unusual discount ticket program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ’80s hair-band musical “Rock of Ages,” which closed on Sunday at the Brooks Atkinson Theater, will offer an unusual way to get discounted tickets when it resumes performances at the Helen Hayes Theater on March 24, producers announced on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Move, and Early Bird Specials, for ‘Rock of Ages’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c7c2ea1-e05a-590b-a739-3371a1bdbd16', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c7c2ea1-e05a-590b-a739-3371a1bdbd16'}, {'abstract': 'The celebrated, and threatened, Ludlow Street hangout gets one more year, which it says will allow it to find another location.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/a-reprieve-for-max-fish/', 'snippet': 'The celebrated, and threatened, Ludlow Street hangout gets one more year, which it says will allow it to find another location.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several weeks before its doors were scheduled for shuttering, Max Fish has been granted a reprieve. Monday afternoon, a lease extension was finalized giving the venerable Lower East Side bar another year at its Ludlow Street location. The extension, which maintains the terms of the current lease, is the result of an agreement between Arwen Properties and the bar’s owner, Ullie Rimkus. The lease now ends Jan. 31, 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reprieve for Max Fish', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Detrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Detrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/89cdf918-1e3d-57aa-9033-8d73de7f3a18', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89cdf918-1e3d-57aa-9033-8d73de7f3a18'}, {'abstract': 'Barbs from the New York area are just background noise to a team that does not let talking get in the way of playing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/sports/football/12patriots.html', 'snippet': 'Barbs from the New York area are just background noise to a team that does not let talking get in the way of playing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. \x97 Poor Alge Crumpler. He spent the first nine years of his career in relatively tranquil N.F.L. outposts like Atlanta and Tennessee, where opposing coaches do not heave Molotov cocktails about their next opponent’s study habits, where a playoff game is not reduced to a personal grudge match between two people who have more reason to compare their fleece separates than their 40-yard dash times, where the entertainment options preferred by the star quarterback are not scrutinized and discussed on an endless talk-radio loop. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/sports/12patriots-web3/12patriots-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/13/sports/12patriots-web3/12patriots-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/sports/12patriots-web3/12patriots-web3-jumbo.