es', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Sudan and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T21:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Merrill D. Oliver and Craig Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Merrill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/21c350a2-cdae-5691-a499-7d4117ccc88b', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21c350a2-cdae-5691-a499-7d4117ccc88b'}, {'abstract': 'Dissatisfaction over a plan to create a commission on judicial salaries was clear in responses to a recent survey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/nyregion/12judges.html', 'snippet': 'Dissatisfaction over a plan to create a commission on judicial salaries was clear in responses to a recent survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late November, the State Legislature created a commission to decide whether New York State’s 1,300 judges should get a pay raise after 12 years without one. Court officials hailed the move as the end of one of the longer standoffs in Albany, and predicted that it would calm the state’s judges, who have sometimes simmered with fury over the issue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/nyregion/JUDGES/JUDGES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 174, 'width': 155, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/nyregion/JUDGES/JUDGES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 