 of elderly, as well. Those in between form the ultimate “sandwich generation” as they increasingly find themselves caring for, or financially supporting, the helpless or ailing at both ends of life’s spectrum — both at the level of the family and the nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring Those Improving the Dying Part of Living', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hastings Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T22:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1291558-cff3-51ba-918c-0483d641d769', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1291558-cff3-51ba-918c-0483d641d769'}, {'abstract': 'The E.P.A. awards $7 million in grants to researchers to study how exposure to pollutants, and non-chemical factors like  stress, poverty and poor diet, can amplify the negative effects of a single toxic substance.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/stress-pollution-and-poverty-a-vicious-cycle/', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A. awards $7 million in grants to researchers to study how exposure to pollutants, and non-chemical factors like  stress, poverty and poor diet, can amplify the negative effects of a single toxic substance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has awarded $7 million in grants to researchers to study the cumulative health impact of pollutants like mercury and lead and social factors like stress and poor nutrition in several low-income communities, the agency said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stress, Pollution and Poverty: A Vicious Cycle?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercury (Metal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Lisa P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T22:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/19bf013d-6381-52d8-9a09-ab71684a89be', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19bf013d-6381-52d8-9a09-ab71684a89be'}, {'abstract': 'The 5.1 percent rise in Chinese consumer prices in November understated the actual inflation rate, which economists said might be twice as high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/business/global/12inflate.html', 'snippet': 'The 5.1 percent rise in Chinese consumer prices in November understated the actual inflation rate, which economists said might be twice as high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING \x97 When garment buyers from New York show up next month at Ch