ormance artist Marina Abramovic, above, may be her most ephemeral. It’s Volcano Flambé, a dessert prepared by Kevin Lasko, the chef at the seasonally changing Park Avenue Winter. “You receive this dessert in front of you and it’s kind of a mystery,” Ms. Abramovic said. Its core of dark chocolate ice cream is covered with meringue, decorated with gold leaf and a swirl of spun sugar, bedded on chocolate cookie crumbs and flambéed with rum. The artist’s booklet of off-beat recipes, “Spirit Cooking,” and an MP3 player with a talk by her accompany the dessert. It’s one of several artist collaborations the restaurant has organized with Creative Time, a nonprofit group.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-dessert/12stuff-dessert-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-dessert/12stuff-dessert-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-dessert/12stuff-dessert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-dessert/12stuff-dessert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-dessert/12stuff-dessert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marina Abramovic’s Art Doubles as Dessert', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Artist Captures The Essence Of Dessert In Latest Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creative Time', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMOVIC, MARINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T23:43:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7056a2d5-6ef0-51aa-80b6-9fbf32c6d9cf', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7056a2d5-6ef0-51aa-80b6-9fbf32c6d9cf'}, {'abstract': 'A jazz brunch for kids, a pie-baking contest, a salute to pork and talks by authors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal.html', 'snippet': 'A jazz brunch for kids, a pie-baking contest, a salute to pork and talks by authors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Cool-Cat Kids', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal-span/12fcal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal-span/12fcal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal-span/Fcal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal-span/12fcal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12fcal-span/12fcal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dining Calendar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calendar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T23:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1081e77-5116-5cb4-8ea0-6fc50cd9e460', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1081e77-5116-5cb4-8ea0-6fc50cd9e460'}, {'abstract': 'Mugolio, a thick syrup made from pine sap, can be used to drizzle on ice cream or enhance a sauce for game meats or fish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/dining/12pine.html', 'snippet': 'Mugolio, a thick syrup made from pine sap, can be used to drizzle on ice cream or enhance a sauce for game meats or fish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year in late spring, Eleonora Cunacia trudges through the foothills of the Dolomites in Northern Italy to gather wild herbs, including the buds of a kind of dwarf pine called mugo. She puts them in glass jars in the sun, where they dry and ooze sap, which she collects and cooks down with sugar and water to make Mugolio, a thick syrup fragrant with evergreen. It can be used to drizzle on ice cream, cheese or panna cotta; to enhance a sauce for game meats or fish; or in cocktails. At about a quarter of the price of the finest artisanal balsamic vinegar, it has the same uses, even over strawberries in summer.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-pine/STUFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 774, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-pine/12stuff-pine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/dining/12stuff-pine/12stuff-pine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Syrup Delivers Taste of Evergreen', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Drips and Drizzles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-11T23:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c1a22d9-604b-5680-8828-cc8a92a98d88', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c1a22d9-604b-5680-8828-cc8a92a98d88'}, {'abstract': 'Nacional, a rare and prized variety of cacao, is now being turned into pure chocolate with a floral aroma and a persistent mellow richness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/dining/12chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'Nacional, a rare and prized variety of cacao, is now being turned into pure chocolate with a floral aroma and a persistent mellow richness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAN PEARSON was working in northern Peru two years ago with his stepson Brian Horsely, supplying gear and food to mining companies, when something caught his eye.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', '