s a tour of the state’s producers.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/the-chardonnays-of-california/', 'snippet': 'Eric Asimov gives a tour of the state’s producers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I had a Kistler chardonnay was back in the mid-1980s, at the original Röckenwagner, an airy restaurant in Venice, Calif. I had never heard of Kistler at the time, but one of my companions told me the story of how these two young men, Steve Kistler and Mark Bixler, had started a winery and, virtually by themselves, were making chardonnays that were rivaling white Burgundies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chardonnays of California', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chardonnay (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T00:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/750e55ce-3150-5be9-9afb-bef689e7d818', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/750e55ce-3150-5be9-9afb-bef689e7d818'}, {'abstract': 'New Web sites are offering fewer trip options but advice from experts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/travel/16praconline.html', 'snippet': 'New Web sites are offering fewer trip options but advice from experts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN it comes to planning a vacation, travelers can either spend hours online figuring out where to go, which flights and hotels to book, and what to do when they get there, or they can call a travel agent to figure it out for them. Now, a new breed of members-only Web sites is offering something in between. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/travel/12prac/12prac-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/travel/12prac/12prac-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/travel/12prac/12prac-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Narrowing the Choices, Online', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Narrowing the Choices, Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T00:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9741dd60-3e41-5757-9312-b1d497ec5402', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9741dd60-3e41-5757-9312-b1d497ec5402'}, {'abstract': 'During his play-calling in the Bowl Championship Series, the veteran announcer goes for all the Tostitos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/sports/ncaafootball/12sandomir.html', 'snippet': 'During his play-calling in the Bowl Championship Series, the veteran announcer goes for all the Tostitos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brent Musburger: the name conjures a dramatic, if hyperbolic, voice at big events and drinking games inspired by his verbal idiosyncrasies. His analysts are “pardners.” His current pardner, Kirk Herbstreit, is Herbie, which Musburger says so often it sounds as if he’s played his cassette of “The Love Bug” to dust.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/sports/sandomir/sandomir-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/sports/sandomir/sandomir-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/sports/sandomir/sandomir-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forsaking Fact for Emotion, Musburger Keeps It Vague', 'kicker': 'Tv Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forsaking Fact for Emotion, Musburger Keeps It Vague', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T00:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ced45547-dccc-59e9-82ce-672636e6b0aa', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ced45547-dccc-59e9-82ce-672636e6b0aa'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators accused the company of misleading investors in its YieldPlus bond fund, which contained risky mortgage-backed securities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/schwab-to-pay-119-million-to-settle-bond-fund-case/', 'snippet': 'Regulators accused the company of misleading investors in its YieldPlus bond fund, which contained risky mortgage-backed securities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Charles Schwab Corporation agreed on Tuesday to pay $119 million to settle federal and state lawsuits in which regulators accused the company of misleading investors in a bond mutual fund that contained risky mortgage-backed securities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schwab to Pay $119 Million to Settle Bond Fund Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charles Schwab Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T00:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/82cb8f8c-b639-5cb2-8da5-f4a0fd27abc4', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82cb8f8c-b639-5cb2-8da5-f4a0fd27abc4'}, {'abstract': 'Accusations of discrimination rose 7.2 percent for the year ended Sept. 30, which some say is a result of layoffs during the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/business/12bias.html', 'snippet': 'Accusations of discrimination rose 7.2 percent for the year ended Sept. 30, which some say is a result of layoffs during the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a tough job market, more and more workers are accusing their employers of discrimination, a report from the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Workers Complain of Bias on the Job, a Trend Linked to Widespread Layoffs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Workers Complain of Bias on the Job, a Trend Linked to Widespread Layoffs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T00:42:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3196fb2-85c4-5ff9-9e19-b37fb9255800', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3196fb2-85c4-5ff9-9e19-b37fb9255800'}, {'abstract': 'A high school and 26 elementary schools will be shut at the end of the school year because of declining enrollment and money, according to a statement from the archdiocese.', 'web_