two years in balmy Brazil that the warmest jacket in my possession is a black leather number with a broken zipper. I didn’t even own a hat and gloves until a recent knuckle-numbing emergency led me to drop $10 on a Chinatown street corner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bargain Skiing? Yes, It’s Possible.', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Placid (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/10b9e08e-a194-5f01-b4ad-602a3cd3dbdb', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10b9e08e-a194-5f01-b4ad-602a3cd3dbdb'}, {'abstract': '“Over the past two years, the health-care reform that Obama has advocated has created a vast divide within American society and between diametrically opposed political parties, while immigration has separated the American people into two camps that cannot bear the very existence of the other,” a Chinese scholar writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/american-politics-seen-from-beijing/', 'snippet': '“Over the past two years, the health-care reform that Obama has advocated has created a vast divide within American society and between diametrically opposed political parties, while immigration has separated the American people into two camps tha...', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was struck by some recent remarks by Zhang Guoqing, a Chinese scholar, that I read in Evan Osnos’s blog and excerpted in my column today. Here are the full remarks, which originally appeared in The Beijing News:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Politics, Seen From Beijing', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a61197f-f09f-5582-8d98-a31b59b427b9', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a61197f-f09f-5582-8d98-a31b59b427b9'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas Legislature convened with Republicans in unassailable control but facing tough budget decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/us/12texas.html', 'snippet': 'The Texas Legislature convened with Republicans in unassailable control but facing tough budget decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — Two years ago, Marva Beck’s main concern was hauling feed out to cattle on her ranch and trying to avoid getting run over by hungry cows. But on Tuesday she took the oath of office in the Texas House of Representatives, one of a score of conservative neophytes who upset longtime incumbents in November.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/us/SUB-TEXAS-1/SUB-TEXAS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '