 'lead_paragraph': 'Public opprobrium played a hand in Goldman Sachs’s decision to disclose more about its trading and investments for its own account, the first fruits of which emerged in a regulatory filing on Tuesday. But the Wall Street firm’s reorganization of how it reports earnings also serves its own purposes. It makes valuing the firm a bit easier by enabling a better sum-of-the-parts analysis than was previously possible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Up Parts at Goldman Sachs', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adding Up Parts At Goldman Sachs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:39:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANTONY CURRIE and ROBERT CYRAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CURRIE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CYRAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id