'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf6b3f5-5a97-5ff7-8902-462469f5d6cc', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf6b3f5-5a97-5ff7-8902-462469f5d6cc'}, {'abstract': 'A Palestinian militant from the group Islamic Jihad was killed in Gaza on Tuesday in an Israeli airstrike, according to the Israeli military and the group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/world/middleeast/12briefs-DroneBrf.html', 'snippet': 'A Palestinian militant from the group Islamic Jihad was killed in Gaza on Tuesday in an Israeli airstrike, according to the Israeli military and the group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Palestinian militant from the group Islamic Jihad was killed in Gaza on Tuesday in an Israeli airstrike, according to the Israeli military and the group. The military said in a statement that the target of the strike, Muhammad Najar, 23, was “involved in planning a massive terror attack in the heart of Israel,” and that the pinpoint killing had disrupted those plans. Islamic Jihad threatened to avenge the Israeli attack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Airstrike in Gaza Kills a Militant', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Airstrike in Gaza Kills a Militant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Islamic Jihad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda49da7-8eb1-59df-9501-ea40309e2cf5', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda49da7-8eb1-59df-9501-ea40309e2cf5'}, {'abstract': 'A new chess program called Houdini is leading a competition that includes Rybka, the four-time defending world computer champion.', 'web_url': 'https://gambit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/11/the-new-computer-chess-bully-on-the-screen/', 'snippet': 'A new chess program called Houdini is leading a competition that includes Rybka, the four-time defending world computer champion.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Computer Chess Bully on the Screen', 'kicker': 'Gambit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:54:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b37defee-c8d7-5dfd-93b1-91fd6dd1a030', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b37defee-c8d7-5dfd-93b1-91fd6dd1a030'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that international sanctions against Iran had not affected its determination to acquire nuclear weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/world/middleeast/12netanyahubrf.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that international sanctions against Iran had not affected its determination to acquire nuclear weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Tuesday that international sanctions against Iran had not affected its determination to acquire nuclear weapons, and that to do so the sanctions needed to be “materially strengthened” and backed by “a credible military option” led by the United States. The more credible the military threat, he added, the less chance that it would have to be used. At a news conference for foreign reporters, Mr. Netanyahu would not say whether he shared the assessment of Israel’s recently retired intelligence agency chief that Iran would not be able to build a nuclear weapon before 2015. That assessment pushed back other Israeli estimates by a year or more, based on technical difficulties and other challenges faced by Iran. “Intelligence estimates are exactly that — estimates,” Mr. Netanyahu said, adding that there was quite a range.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Netanyahu Says Iran Is Undeterred', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T04:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'or