ll partly pay homage to some of historic Harlem jazz haunts, with events at Minton’s Playhouse, the Lenox Lounge, the Alhambra Ballroom and Showman’s Cafe. The Apollo Theater will host jam sessions, a jazz-themed Amateur Night and “Jazz à la Carte,” a program with the trombonist Wycliffe Gordon, above, and guests, including the tap dancer Savion Glover and the singers Carla Cook and Nikki Yanofsky. The Harlem Stage Gatehouse will present the Spanish Harlem Orchestra and two nights of tributes to the fondly remembered club Small’s Paradise, with the bassist-vocalist Meshell Ndegeocello and the pianist Jason Moran. And Jazzmobile, a community outreach, will stock the Alhambra with two nights of big bands \x97 the Jimmy Heath Big Band and the Harlem Renaissance Orchestra \x97 and hold a “cutting contest” at Minton’s, supervised by the drummer T. S. Monk. Among the other partners in the festival are Columbia University, which will host discussions with scholars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harlem Jazz Fest', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harlem Jazz Fest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T05:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c2943d9-edd2-5041-9e97-eaddd56408f9', 'word_cou