: 'New Jersey Transit', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T10:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb7524e-653a-5e2f-b340-24e70c2fee5f', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb7524e-653a-5e2f-b340-24e70c2fee5f'}, {'abstract': 'The Saturday night gathering of fire-breathers have become a fixture of Paris’s underground life and even spawned an annual party that offers anyone, if only for a night, a view into this glowing world. This year’s edition, the seventh, is on Jan. 22.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/playing-with-fire-literally-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'The Saturday night gathering of fire-breathers have become a fixture of Paris’s underground life and even spawned an annual party that offers anyone, if only for a night, a view into this glowing world. This year’s edition, the seventh, is on Jan....', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the striking and dangerous craft of fire-breathing has made something of a comeback in the last few years, it’s still a fringe activity. In Paris several years ago, the police shooed practitioners out of Paris’s parks, due to safety concerns. The fire breathers, along with flame jugglers and dancers, began meeting at a more out-of-the-way spot long favored by skateboarders: the vast (and treeless) courtyard of the Palais de Tokyo, an imposing, neo-Classical modern art museum built for the 1937 World’s Fair. Their Saturday night gatherings have become a fixture of Paris’s underground life and even spawned an annual party that offers anyone, if only for a night, a view into this glowing world. This year’s edition, the seventh, is on Jan. 22. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Playing With Fire, Literally, in Paris', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T11:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Rothbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a53010-3aad-5544-a9f3-6070e828e8b7', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a53010-3aad-5544-a9f3-6070e828e8b7'}, {'abstract': 'An early star of the A.F.L., the Bills’ Cookie Gilchrist  was a brutish running back who was colorful and combative.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/cookie-gilchrist-punishing-runner-who-took-stand-against-racism/', 'snippet': 'An early star of the A.F.L., the Bills’ Cookie Gilchrist  was a brutish running back who was colorful and combative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Barall writes about pro football history for the Fifth Down. Cookie Gilchrist died Monday at age 75.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cookie Gilchrist, Punishing Runner Who Took Stand Against Racism', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilchrist, Cookie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Bills', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'S