l-stock deal worth about $524 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henderson Global Investors, the asset manager listed in London and Sydney, said on Wednesday that it had agreed to buy the Gartmore Group in an all-stock deal worth about £335 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Henderson to Buy Gartmore for $524 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T11:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6402932-28c1-52ff-a0b9-216c3ee0cba7', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6402932-28c1-52ff-a0b9-216c3ee0cba7'}, {'abstract': 'Hezbollah cabinet ministers and their allies resigned, toppling a unity government that had brought a period of relative calm to the troubled nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/middleeast/13lebanon.html', 'snippet': 'Hezbollah cabinet ministers and their allies resigned, toppling a unity government that had brought a period of relative calm to the troubled nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon \x97 Hezbollah and its political allies withdrew from Lebanon’s cabinet on Wednesday, toppling a national unity government that had brought a measure of calm to the troubled Middle Eastern country since 2009 and deepening an emerging crisis over a United Nations-backed tribunal investigating the assassination of a former prime minister.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype'