anizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T12:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c423874f-186b-5351-b906-62ced32490c8', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c423874f-186b-5351-b906-62ced32490c8'}, {'abstract': 'A top official indicated that time was running out for a 2009 proposal for Tehran to send nuclear material abroad in return for enriched uranium for a research reactor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/middleeast/13iran.html', 'snippet': 'A top official indicated that time was running out for a 2009 proposal for Tehran to send nuclear material abroad in return for enriched uranium for a research reactor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS \x97 A week before nuclear talks resume with outside powers, a senior Iranian official was quoted on Wednesday as saying that time was running out for negotiations on some parts of his country’s nuclear program because of Tehran’s enhanced ability to enrich and manufacture atomic fuel. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Says Time Running Out for Nuclear Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warning on Iran Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T12:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dee9e813-6bb5-5099-af36-21a287a6dcd0', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dee9e813-6bb5-5099-af36-21a287a6dcd0'}, {'abstract': 'Under the plan, ITT will keep the business that makes complex technology for the aerospace, industrial and energy markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/itt-to-split-into-3-public-companies/', 'snippet': 'Under the plan, ITT will keep the business that makes complex technology for the aerospace, industrial and energy markets.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:49 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ITT to Spin Off Its Water and Military Units', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ITT Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T12:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/84910f50-6a76-5344-a932-6d64f3c0edfc', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84910f50-6a76-5344-a932-6d64f3c0edfc'}, {'abstract': 'Auto shows yield ever-increasing harvests of branded memory cards, U.S.B. fobs and CD-R’s. In this regard, the 2011 Detroit auto show did not disappoint.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/megabytes-from-the-motor-show/', 'snippet': 'Auto shows yield ever-increasing harvests of branded memory cards, U.S.B. fobs and CD-R’s. In this regard, the 2011 Detroit auto show did not disappoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Seventeen automakers held press conferences at the Cobo Center on Monday, while five warmed up the teleprompters on Tuesday. Companies, perhaps sensing that journalists’ pens can write only so legibly, or their feet carry them so quickly, have responded with an enthusiastic embrace of novelty data-storage units.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Megabytes From the Motor Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T12:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5f95148-0f05-5e58-880e-27a1261dfb53', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f95148-0f05-5e58-880e-27a1261dfb53'}, {'abstract': 'For Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, the snowfall on Wednesday was a chance to prove that the city could do better at cleaning up than it did last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow.html', 'snippet': 'For Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, the snowfall on Wednesday was a chance to prove that the city could do better at cleaning up than it did last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a city still angry about a blizzard two and a half weeks ago that left some streets unplowed for days, the storm on Wednesday seemed to be much ado about \x97 not nothing, but far less snow than many had feared. The National Weather Service recorded 9.1 inches in Central Park, less than half the total from the two-day storm in December.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow_span/13snow_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow_span/13snow_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow_span/13snow_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow_span/13snow_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/13snow_span/13snow_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Officials Greet Storm With Plows and Diplomacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Meets Snow With Plows and Diplomacy, but Storm Saves Its Punch for Farther North', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T12:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82b7ca93-e1df-52c9-8fc9-2bd6eb87233a', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82b7ca93-e1df-52c9-8fc9-2bd6eb87233a'}, {'abstract': 'Is there any way to save Europe’s democracies from sinking together in the ill-conceived currency union?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/magazine/16Europe-t.html', 'snippet': 'Is there any way to save Europe’s democracies from sinking together in the ill-conceived currency union?', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE’S SOMETHING peculiarly apt about the fact that the current European crisis began in Greece. For Europe’s woes have all the aspects of a classical Greek tragedy, in which a man of noble character is undone by the fatal flaw of hubris.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,