_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8539b70-e799-5f99-a427-64db4de40ca0'}, {'abstract': 'Though Debussy was born in 1862 and died in 1918, this path-breaker has to be considered a 20th-century giant.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/top-10-composers-which-20th-century-masters-will-make-the-cut/', 'snippet': 'Though Debussy was born in 1862 and died in 1918, this path-breaker has to be considered a 20th-century giant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the next two weeks Anthony Tommasini is exploring the qualities that make a classical composer great, maybe even the best of all time. Watch videos and vote for your own top 10 here and read previous posts here and share your thoughts in the comments field. Mr. Tommasini’s final list will be posted on Jan. 21. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Composers: Which 20th-Century Masters Will Make the Cut?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Britten, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Debussy, Claude', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stravinsky, Igor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tchaikovsky, Peter Ilyich', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T13:42:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1220d962-1ccb-5508-9bf6-1fa2b8d95289', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1220d962-1ccb-5508-9bf6-1fa2b8d95289'}, {'abstract': 'The publisher of reams of articles based on popular search-engine results disclosed a price range of $14 to $16 per share for its planned initial public offering.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/demand-media-gives-price-range-for-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'The publisher of reams of articles based on popular search-engine results disclosed a price range of $14 to $16 per share for its planned initial public offering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demand Media, the online content publisher, disclosed on Wednesday that it hoped to raise up to $138 million in its planned initial public stock offering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demand Media Gives Price Range for I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Demand Media Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T13:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8498f222-367e-5fe7-bb88-fe32334ec4ce', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8498f222-367e-5fe7-bb88-fe32334ec4ce'}, {'abstract': 'The director of “The Social Network” enjoyed the notion of a werewolf movie with a woman, but was was not so keen on the constant tabulating and handicapping of awards season.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/fincher-on-black-swan-oscar-campaigning-and-forced-vacations/', 'snippet': 'The director of “The Social Network” enjoyed the notion of a werewolf movie with a woman, but was was not so keen on the constant tabulating and handicapping of awards season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the gods of reporting – otherwise known as the Peggy Siegal planning committee – smile upon you, and you find yourself sitting next to David Fincher at a lunch at the Four Seasons. (Justin Timberlake was apparently not available.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fincher on ‘Black Swan,’ Oscar Campaigning and Forced Vacations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T14:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e5607b1-4575-5718-afca-082e275037f5', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e5607b1-4575-5718-afca-082e275037f5'}, {'abstract': 'The most amusing garden writer of all times, Nichols, who specialized in winter flowers, regularly crescendoed to the point where he could literally have you laughing out loud.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/fabulous-dead-people-beverley-nichols/', 'snippet': 'The most amusing garden writer of all times, Nichols, who specialized in winter flowers, regularly crescendoed to the point where he could literally have you laughing out loud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are any sort of gardener at all, you know that this is the time of year, when hoar frost is on the twig, that held the greatest charm for Beverley Nichols. The most amusing garden writer of all times, Nichols (1898-1985), who specialized in winter flowers, regularly crescendoed to the point where he could literally have you laughing out loud. Here he is fatally associating cyclamens, those “vulgar, obvious plants” whose seeds failed to grow for him after 10 weeks in pots, with “tiresome women who live in flats with electric stoves and indigestion and a Pekingese snoring in the scullery.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fabulous Dead People | Beverley Nichols', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Petkanas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petkanas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/47811012-1304-523c-bfb0-ec8e23ecaf79', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47811012-1304-523c-bfb0-ec8e23ecaf79'}, {'abstract': 'The Colts have to ask themselves whether they need to pair Peyton Manning with another strong leader. Not doing so could risk wasting the prime of one of the greatest players in N.F.L. history.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/peyton-manning-deserves-a-better-coach/', 'snippet': 'The Colts have to ask themselves whether they need to pair Peyton Manning with another strong leader. Not doing so could risk wasting the prime of one of the greatest players in N.F.L. history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brady/Manning debate has been raging for years. The arguments can be interesting. Peyton has the stats, the M.V.P. awards and a superior “Saturday Night Live” appearance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peyton Manning Deserves a Better Coach', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': '