9, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab669310-304f-5195-bcab-74df9721c938'}, {'abstract': 'Troops fired tear gas as the first major protest hit the capital since rioting over poverty and unemployment began three weeks ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/africa/13tunisia.html', 'snippet': 'Troops fired tear gas as the first major protest hit the capital since rioting over poverty and unemployment began three weeks ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — The government of Tunisia scrambled alternately to appease critics and to crush growing unrest on Wednesday as a three-week-old wave of violent demonstrations spread for the first time to the capital, where swarms of protesters called for the ouster of the authoritarian president, Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/world/13TUNISIA1/13TUNISIA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/world/13TUNISIA1/13TUNISIA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/world/13TUNISIA1/13TUNISIA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Spread to Tunisia’s Capital, and a Curfew Is Decreed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protests Spread to Tunisia’s Capital, and a Curfew Is Decreed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T14:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'secti