s not plowed for days after the blizzard has already been cleared. Has your street been plowed?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/same-street-different-storm-plowed/', 'snippet': 'At least one Brooklyn block that was not plowed for days after the blizzard has already been cleared. Has your street been plowed?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the block of Butler Street in Park Slope, Brooklyn, that feeds off the one-way alley called Gregory Place is any indicator, the city has been a bit more prompt in clearing the snow than it was last month. (See below.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Same Street, Different Storm: Plowed', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T15:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7310d7b-b8d2-5aa6-ad92-1f8bb6fcc0d8', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7310d7b-b8d2-5aa6-ad92-1f8bb6fcc0d8'}, {'abstract': 'After a year of almost unfathomable hardship in Haiti, more than a million displaced people still live under tents and tarpaulins, and reconstruction has barely begun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/world/americas/2010-haiti-shattered-year.html', 'snippet': 'After a year of almost unfathomable hardship in Haiti, more than a million displaced people still live under tents and tarpaulins, and reconstruction has barely begun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a year of almost unfathomable hardship in Haiti, more than a million displaced people still live under tents and tarpaulins, and reconstruction has barely begun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti: The Shattered Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T15:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3519dccc-58bf-54e8-90d8-80861abc82b1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3519dccc-58bf-54e8-90d8-80861abc82b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Turkish jeweler Sevan Bicakci was motivated by both myth and hard reality when making his one-of-a-kind pair of sterling, 24-karat gold and diamond earrings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/gift-horse/', 'snippet': 'The Turkish jeweler Sevan Bicakci was motivated by both myth and hard reality when making his one-of-a-kind pair of sterling, 24-karat gold and diamond earrings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Turkish jeweler Sevan Bicakci was motivated by both myth and hard reality when making this one-of-a-kind pair of sterling, 24-karat gold and diamond earrings. At once a representation of Poseidon’s magnificent chariot horses and a tribute to Turkey’s Mount Ida, which figures prominently in Greek mythology as the site from which the gods watched the Trojan War, the sparkly steeds are also a protest against modern-day mining on the resources-rich site. “I know this sounds odd coming from a jeweler,” Bicakci says, “but the natural treasure of Ida is much more valuable than gold.” The earrings are $16,860 at Barneys New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gift Horse', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T15:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e8126a3-f691-5e1c-8a51-b6ade69264b1', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e8126a3-f691-5e1c-8a51-b6ade69264b1'}, {'abstract': 'Bargain skiing options, answers to financial aid questions and other consumer-focused items from Wednesday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/wednesday-reading-bargain-skiing/', 'snippet': 'Bargain skiing options, answers to financial aid questions and other consumer-focused items from Wednesday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Bargain Skiing', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T15:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0b7efa-1b0f-57d3-9bbf-02d69537c8bc', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0b7efa-1b0f-57d3-9bbf-02d69537c8bc'}, {'abstract': 'Valuation is the primary reason, but vulnerability to the Volcker rule is also cited.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/jpmorgan-downgrades-goldman/', 'snippet': 'Valuation is the primary reason, but vulnerability to the Volcker rule is also cited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs is trying to put its best foot forward, with the Tuesday release of a report on ways to improve its disclosure and business practices, but analysts at a JPMorgan unit in London have lowered their rating on the firm. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Unit Downgrades Goldman', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T15:46:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8666f0e9-4bbf-5ca6-b61f-e2e56587c9e9', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8666f0e9-4bbf-5ca6-b61f-e2e56587c9e9'}, {'abstract': 'At the celebrity pile-up known as the National Board of Review gala, there was plenty of gawking at stars like Ben Affleck, Jon Hamm and Christian Bale. But Bill Murray stole the show when toasting Sofia Coppola.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/bill-murray-shows-them-how-its-done/', 'snippet': 'At the celebrity pile-up known as the National Board of Review gala, there was plenty of gawking at stars like Ben Affleck, Jon Hamm and Christian Bale. But Bill Murray stole the show when toasting Sofia Coppola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a celebrity pile-up, as usual, at the National Board of Review gala on Tuesday night: Sofia Coppola, Aaron Sorkin and Ben Affleck working the red carpet at the same time, Jon Hamm chatting with Chris Cooper, Hailee Steinfeld and Jennifer Lawrence – the 14- and 20-year-old stars and only representatives from their films, “True Grit” and “Winter’s Bone” – meeting for the first time and bonding across tables. Even among actors, there was gawking to spare: when Bill Murray took the stage, Armie Hammer, the 6’5″ blond star of “The Social Network,” took photos from his seat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Murray Shows Them How It’s Done', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coppola, Sofia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6888a99b-f826-55f6-9046-0808482483d0', 'word_count': 1507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6888a99b-f826-55f6-9046-0808482483d0'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley Investment Management on Wednesday announced it had raised $956 million for a new fund that invests in corporate mezzanine credit, a bright spot for alternative investments over the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/morgan-stanley-raises-nearly-1-billion-for-new-debt-fund/', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley Investment Management on Wednesday anno