 attack in the last few months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/asia/13bannu.html', 'snippet': 'A suicide bomber in a tribal area rammed his explosives-laden vehicle into a mosque adjacent to a police station that has come under frequent attack in the last few months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan \x97 A suicide bomber struck in a tribal area of northwestern Pakistan on Wednesday, ramming his explosives-laden vehicle into a mosque adjacent to a police station that has come under frequent attack in the last few months, a security official said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suicide Bomber Strikes in Northwest Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suicide Bomber Strikes in Northwest Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Federally Administered Tribal Areas (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehrik-e-Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/286b7d35-cf28-550d-9af5-b75bd5bd67a3', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/286b7d35-cf28-550d-9af5-b75bd5bd67a3'}, {'abstract': 'One product guaranteed to grace the red carpet this season: Clarins Instant Smooth Line Correcting Concentrate.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/vain-glorious-a-flawless-entrance/', 'snippet': 'One product guaranteed to grace the red carpet this season: Clarins Instant Smooth Line Correcting Concentrate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What: Clarins Instant Smooth Line Correcting Concentrate', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | A Flawless Entrance', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4415586-c16b-5d77-adc2-779b6c4ee420', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4415586-c16b-5d77-adc2-779b6c4ee420'}, {'abstract': 'Term for small business owners (and, presumably, others) who spend more time clasping their phones than the hands of their lover.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/phonemance/', 'snippet': 'Term for small business owners (and, presumably, others) who spend more time clasping their phones than the hands of their lover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Term for small business owners (and, presumably, others) who spend more time clasping their phones than the hands of their lover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phonemance', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:38:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dee9c58-aeeb-5046-bab7-f21154a12586', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dee9c58-aeeb-5046-bab7-f21154a12586'}, {'abstract': 'Dionne Warwick will reunite with some old singing partners next month for a live performance of “That’s What Friends Are For” to benefit AIDS research.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/live-reunion-planned-for-warwick-and-her-friends/', 'snippet': 'Dionne Warwick will reunite with some old singing partners next month for a live performance of “That’s What Friends Are For” to benefit AIDS research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stevie Wonder, Elton John, Gladys Knight and Dionne Warwick will reunite for a live performance on Feb. 9 of the song “That’s What Friends Are For” at amfAR’s New York Gala benefit at Cipriani Wall Street, the foundation has announced. The song, which was a No. 1 single in 1986, was originally written by Carole Bayer Sager and Burt Bacharach and was released by Arista as a benefit single for amfAR, the Foundation for AIDS Research. It raised $3 million for the foundation, after Ms. Warwick gathered the writers and artists, who offered to donate their portion of profits from the recording. Clive Davis, the president of Arista, also agreed to donate all profits. In addition to the special performance next month, amfAR will honor former President Bill Clinton; Diane von Furstenberg; and two of the foundation’s co-founders, Dr. Mathilde Krim and Elizabeth Taylor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Reunion Planned for Warwick and Her Friends', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John, Elton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Furstenberg, Diane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wonder, Stevie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a04029a0-30b2-512b-ab4e-fdfd0ac6fc44', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a04029a0-30b2-512b-ab4e-fdfd0ac6fc44'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/fafsaq-and-a-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that most students applying to college for next fall’s freshman class have submitted their applications, they (and their families) will begin to tackle the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or Fafsa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Part 2: Answers to Readers’ Questions on Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kantrowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantrowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffdabfc-5d9f-5b8e-9f7d-9c21beddfcbe', 'word_count': 1715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffdabfc-5d9f-5b8e-9f7d-9c21beddfcbe'}, {'abstract': 'In a speech on Wednesday, the Treasury Secretary called China “a growing source of concern,” mentioning its undervalued currency, intellectual-property theft and various forms of protectionism.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/geithners-china-concerns/', 'snippet': 'In a speech on Wednesday, the Treasury Secretary called China “a growing source of concern,” mentioning its undervalued currency, intellectual-property theft and various forms of protectionism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Timothy F. Geithner, the Treasury secretary, gave a speech on China Wednesday\xa0 morning that did not contain news but was somewhat feistier in tone than the Obama administration has been in the past. This approach — respectful yet blunt — strikes me as more promising than the deferential stance the administration has sometimes adopted before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geithner’s China Concerns', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b37092a-bf67-5b84-88cc-2b00d225883d', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b37092a-bf67-5b84-88cc-2b00d225883d'}, {'abstract': 'The street artist Shepard Fairey and The Associated Press have ended their long-running dispute surrounding the creation of the well-known campaign poster of Barack Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/fight-over-obama-hope-image-is-settled/', 'snippet': 'The street artist Shepard Fairey and The Associated Press have ended their long-running dispute surrounding the creation of the well-known campaign poster of Barack Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The street artist Shepard Fairey and The Associated Press have ended their long-running legal battle over whether Mr. Fairey violated copyright protections in using one of the news cooperative’s photographs as the basis for the well-known “Hope” campaign poster of Barack Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fight Over Obama ‘Hope’ Image Is Settled', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairey, Shepard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T16:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/317974f9-063d-5fe3-9881-b5be8fa884dc', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317974f9-063d-5fe3-9881-b5be8fa884dc'}, {'abstract': 'Home movies, now in 3D.CE', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/make-your-own-3d-videos/', 'snippet': 'Home movies, now in 3D.CE', 'lead_paragraph': 'Want to double your fun with a new camcorder? Consider a pair of 3D digicams from those dueling rivals, Sony and Panasonic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Your Own 3D Videos', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise',