Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/93981c63-4894-5156-812e-1ac4264d5865', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93981c63-4894-5156-812e-1ac4264d5865'}, {'abstract': 'The state wildlife officer who made the traffic stop had no probable cause to search Jared L. Loughner’s car.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/us/politics/13giffords.html', 'snippet': 'The state wildlife officer who made the traffic stop had no probable cause to search Jared L. Loughner’s car.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — Jared L. Loughner had repeated contact with law enforcement officers over the years, and hours before Saturday’s shootings was pulled over by a police officer for running a red light as he frenetically prepared to kill a congresswoman, the authorities said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/us/GIFFORDS/GIFFORDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/us/GIFFORDS/GIFFORDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/us/GIFFORDS/GIFFORDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Stopped Loughner’s Car on Day of Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect Ran a Red Light and Was Stopped by Police Hours Before Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey, Jo Becker and Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1541a41e-e039-5f01-84ff-18d3aff4eb7b', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1541a41e-e039-5f01-84ff-18d3aff4eb7b'}, {'abstract': 'In the hospital, doctors and nurses build walls, and maintain them, to buttress authority and prevent being challenged by staff from other floors.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/nurse-and-doctor-neighbor-and-friend/', 'snippet': 'In the hospital, doctors and nurses build walls, and maintain them, to buttress authority and prevent being challenged by staff from other floors.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Something there is that doesn’t love a wall,” begins Robert Frost’s poem “Mending Wall,” about two neighbors who meet to repair the gaps and holes in the stone wall separating their properties. They walk on either side of it, picking up and replacing fallen stones as they go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nurse and Doctor, Neighbor and Friend', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frost, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theresa Brown, R.N', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'R.', 'middlename': 'N', 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d99ed6-6635-5f2e-95a5-85a970be48a0', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d99ed6-6635-5f2e-95a5-85a970be48a0'}, {'abstract': 'As part of a whirlwind tour of New York, the newest Spider-Man takes in the Four Seasons, the “Today” show and an awards gala as part of the campaigning for “The Social Network.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/a-very-hectic-day-in-the-life-of-andrew-garfield/', 'snippet': 'As part of a whirlwind tour of New York, the newest Spider-Man takes in the Four Seasons, the “Today” show and an awards gala as part of the campaigning for “The Social Network.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accepting his award for best actor at the National Board of Review gala on Tuesday, Jesse Eisenberg revealed that he was intimidated by his co-star Andrew Garfield, who came prepared for the second day of rehearsal for “The Social Network” with a copy of “Business for Dummies.” (His character, Eduardo Saverin, was a business major; Mr. Eisenberg, who plays Facebook founder Mark Zuckerberg, added that he went out and bought a copy of “C++ for Dummies” to bone up on coding, and that neither actor read past the introductions.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A (Very Hectic) Day in the Life of Andrew Garfield', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7bda708-9a6c-5cd2-b579-433881857944', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7bda708-9a6c-5cd2-b579-433881857944'}, {'abstract': 'Beginning in April, digital versions of comics will be offered on the same day print editions arrive on newsstands.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/archie-to-go-digital/', 'snippet': 'Beginning in April, digital versions of comics will be offered on the same day print editions arrive on newsstands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Archie Andrews, the perpetual teenager from Riverdale, is taking another step into the future. Beginning in April, Archie Comics will offer digital versions of its comics on the same day that the print editions arrive on newsstands. The company will be starting with six monthly titles: Archie, Archie & Friends, Betty, Veronica, Betty and Veronica, and Jughead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Archie to Go Digital', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c75f7966-5d8e-5036-bee7-5f8aed6d781b', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c75f7966-5d8e-5036-bee7-5f8aed6d781b'}, {'abstract': 'Jennifer Saranow Schultz, the lead blogger for Bucks, shares her financial resolution for 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/resolved-be-a-smarter-negotiator/', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Saranow Schultz, the lead blogger for Bucks, shares her financial resolution for 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week on the Bucks blog, our contributors, along with some of our favorite sources, are posting about their financial resolutions for the new year. Here, Jennifer Saranow Schultz, the lead blogger for Bucks, shares her plans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resolved: Be a Smarter Negotiator', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d57cc795-81d8-51da-97b6-d494883b8940', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d57cc795-81d8-51da-97b6-d494883b8940'}, {'abstract': 'Before departing Antarctica, a geologist reflects on a month of camping on a glacier, and makes a surprise visit to the South Pole.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/on-last-field-day-a-south-pole-detour/', 'snippet': 'Before departing Antarctica, a geologist reflects on a month of camping on a glacier, and makes a surprise visit to the South Pole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Vervoort, left, an associate professor in radiogenic isotope geochemistry at Washington State University, and John Goodge, a professor of geological sciences at the University of Minnesota-Duluth, are writing from their research expedition in Antarctica.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Last Field Day, a South Pole Detour', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock and Stone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Pole', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Vervoort', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vervoort', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0c5dd6f-fe5b-5656-bdfb-9b8e6666d8ec', 'word_count': 1548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0c5dd6f-fe5b-5656-bdfb-9b8e6666d8ec'}, {'abstract': 'A few more of these successes and we’ll be doomed.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/pyrrhic-bond-auctions/', 'snippet': 'A few more of these successes and we’ll be doomed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m with Calculated Risk here: it says something about the sheer desperation of the European situation that Portugal’s ability to sell 10-year bonds at an interest rate of “only” 6.7 percent is considered a success. If you think about the debt dynamics here — the burden of growing interest payments on an economy that is likely to face years of grinding debt deflation — an interest rate that high is little short of ruinous. But it is, indeed, not as bad as people were expecting last week; hence, success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pyrrhic Bond Auctions', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8860592-ab36-588e-873e-d26b6e93fb2d', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8860592-ab36-588e-873e-d26b6e93fb2d'}, {'abstract': 'Pushing for a bill, sure. But singing for it? Councilman Oliver Koppell and a group of religious leaders and politicians are about to try doing just that.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/rallying-for-a-bill-with-sermons-and-songs/', 'snippet': 'Pushing for a bill, sure. But singing for it? Councilman Oliver Koppell and a group of religious leaders and politicians are about to try doing just that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When members of the City Council want Speaker Christine C. Quinn to call a hearing on a piece of legislation, they have a few options. They can try to cut a deal; they can issue a few dozen press releases; they can nag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rallying for a Bill, With Sermons and Songs', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': No