fficials have described as a moderate approach to regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/e-p-a-puts-off-regulating-biomass-for-now/', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A.’s announcement seems to be another signal that it is following what officials have described as a moderate approach to regulation.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Acknowledging large unknowns about the atmospheric impact of burning large amounts of plant waste and other biological materials, the Environmental Protection Agency announced on Wednesday that it would delay for three years any greenhouse gas permitting requirements for biomass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Puts Off Regulating Biomass for Now', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Lisa P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T17:35:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c665bf3a-3619-535c-9020-d00cdc674194', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c665bf3a-3619-535c-9020-d00cdc674194'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Colbert hosted a humorous, p