age chargers, but there are concerns about confusion among consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/compatability-questions-loom-for-high-voltage-e-v-charging/', 'snippet': 'Electric-vehicle engineers hope to enhance the reigning plug-port standard in the United States to accommodate high-voltage chargers, but there are concerns about confusion among consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Electric cars already on the American market, as well as those arriving soon, all use the same onboard charging port because of\xa0 SAE International, the professional organization for automotive engineers that approved the reigning J1772 standard. The standard was adopted early last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compatibility Questions for High-Voltage E.V. Charging', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Society of Automotive Engineers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T18:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0551bfd5-04d4-5b0d-95be-650f1fcafd9b', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0551bfd5-04d4-5b0d-95be-650f1fcafd9b'}, {'abstract': '“Diciembre,” at Under the Radar Festival, is a witty, sharply focused vision of a time well past celebration.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/under-the-radar-review-diciembre/', 'snippet': '“Diciembre,” at Under the Radar Festival, is a witty, sharply focused vision of a time well past celebration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even if you’re overstuffed and partied-out from last month’s Yuletide marathon, you should still try to make the acquaintance of one special ghost of Christmas future now haunting the Under the Radar Festival. In the Teatro en el Blanco’s “Diciembre” (yes, that’s Spanish for December), Guillermo Calderon envisions December 25 in Chile in 2014. And if the view ain’t pretty, it is highly picturesque — a witty, sharply focused vision of a time well past celebration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under The Radar Review: ‘Diciembre’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T18:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5139d5c-d81c-552d-9102-e11e2a02bb5b', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5139d5c-d81c-552d-9102-e11e2a02bb5b'}, {'abstract': 'Is there a lucrative market in gathering such data, from plumes of carbon dioxide to methane?  At least one company seems to think so.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/commercializing-greenhouse-gas-data/', 'snippet': 'Is there a lucrative market in gathering such data, from plumes of carbon dioxide to methane?  At least one company seems to think so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted in Wednesday’s Times, the company that brought the world WeatherBug is making what would seem a rather natural move into greenhouse gas monitoring — and pioneering a whole new market in the process. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Com