ting from @TheHammerInTheSlammer.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 10 Things to Talk About This Weekend', 'kicker': 'Crib Sheet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 10 Things To Talk About This Weekend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gossip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T20:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Alford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b58781e-fea8-5a42-8d6c-7b4ce6ea1c5d', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b58781e-fea8-5a42-8d6c-7b4ce6ea1c5d'}, {'abstract': 'Ukraine’s president said an award bestowed on one of the most divisive figures in the country’s modern history had been officially revoked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/europe/13ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'Ukraine’s president said an award bestowed on one of the most divisive figures in the country’s modern history had been officially revoked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW \x97 President Viktor F. Yanukovich of Ukraine announced Wednesday that a national award bestowed on one of the most divisive figures in the country’s modern history \x97 a leader of the Ukrainian partisans during World War II \x97 had been officially revoked.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hero of Ukraine’ Prize to Wartime Partisan Leader Is Revoked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Hero of Ukraine’ Prize to Wartime Partisan Leader Is Revoked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanukovich, Viktor F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bandera, Stepan (1909-59)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T20:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford J. Levy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Levy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/270139ba-be24-562d-a81b-930895636a69', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/270139ba-be24-562d-a81b-930895636a69'}, {'abstract': '2010 tied with 2005, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration reports, indicating that global warming continues unabated.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/a-photo-finish-for-warmest-year-on-record/', 'snippet': '2010 tied with 2005, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration reports, indicating that global warming continues unabated.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:35 p.m. | Updated NASA has just come out with its temperature numbers for 2010, and they match the NOAA analysis, showing a tie between 2010 and 2005 for hottest year on record. The NASA analysis can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photo Finish for Warmest Year on Record', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T20:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/31470091-c1d2-55cd-b68f-8193b52fa3cd', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31470091-c1d2-55cd-b68f-8193b52fa3cd'}, {'abstract': 'Lesson Plan | Exploring the implications of the Haiti disaster from the perspectives of science, engineering, health, history, arts and culture, and the media.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/one-year-later-studying-post-earthquake-haiti/', 'snippet': 'Lesson Plan | Exploring the implications of the Haiti disaster from the perspectives of science, engineering, health, history, arts and culture, and the media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview  | What can we learn from natural disasters like earthquakes, and from the quake that devastated Haiti in 2010? In this lesson, students review the Haiti earthquake, reflect on the changes that have occurred since then and develop personal responses. They engage in one or more projects in which they explore the implications of the disaster from the perspectives of science, engineering, health, history, arts and culture, and the media. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Year Later: Studying Post-Earthquake Haiti', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank':