one-man show he wrote and helped produce, now at the West End Theater. So much so, according to the production’s publicity material, that Mr. Cohen, a former high school principal who has acted in feature films, was arrested in the 1970s in Ohio, where he was mistaken for Hoffman. In visual terms, you couldn’t ask for a better meeting of subject and performer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/Abbie/Abbie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/Abbie/Abbie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/Abbie/Abbie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Life and Passions of an American Activist', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Abbie'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Life and Passions Of an American Activist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Abbie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T22:05:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e2b7745-e435-5e9d-9319-a36b62bab930', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e2b7745-e435-5e9d-9319-a36b62bab930'}, {'abstract': 'After a hiatus over the holiday season, spam is back to high levels.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/spam-is-back/', 'snippet': 'After a hiatus over the holiday season, spam is back to high levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A holiday hiatus for spammers appears to be over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spam Is Back', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spam (Electronic Mail)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symantec Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T22:06:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Riva Richmond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Riva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richmond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dff8032-43b6-5c6b-9486-07d701cd7d2a', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dff8032-43b6-5c6b-9486-07d701cd7d2a'}, {'abstract': 'The provocative design of the Broad Museum in Los Angeles came to light in a press conference last week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/artifacts-the-veil-lifts/', 'snippet': 'The provocative design of the Broad Museum in Los Angeles came to light in a press conference last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Los Angeles is a museum-proud city, and Eli Broad’s name is all over it. The doors of the Museum of Contemporary Art, which the billionaire philanthropist helped to found in 1979, might not be open today if not for him. The Los Angeles County Museum of Art has a Broad Museum of Contemporary Art within it. There’s the Broad Art Center at UCLA and a Broad Art Foundation in Venice. Even the California Department of Transportation’s building downtown has the Broad Plaza for public art. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | The Veil Lifts', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T22:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5539503-f0c5-556e-b0de-551512fab53b', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5539503-f0c5-556e-b0de-551512fab53b'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the snowstorm, most afternoon commuters should expect an unremarkable ride home on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/forecast-for-the-ride-home-unremarkable/', 'snippet': 'Despite the snowstorm, most afternoon commuters should expect an unremarkable ride home on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday proved a resilient day for the region’s mass transit network, and most afternoon commuters should expect an unremarkable ride home. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forecast for the Ride Home: Unremarkable', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T22:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/69eee594-cc9d-52b3-b398-2980906201e2', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69eee594-cc9d-52b3-b398-2980906201e2'}, {'abstract': 'Christine Ebersole’s new show at the Café Carlyle includes songs from her Broadway hit “Grey Gardens” in a larger meditation on youth and age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/arts/music/13ebersole.html', 'snippet': 'Christine Ebersole’s new show at the Café Carlyle includes songs from her Broadway hit “Grey Gardens” in a larger meditation on youth and age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sneak attack: that’s what you might call the moment in Christine Ebersole’s brilliant new show at the Café Carlyle when the merriment pauses, and she delivers a riveting dramatic performance of “Another Winter in a Summer Town.” With music by Scott Frankel and lyrics by Michael Korie, the song is a crushing moment of self-awareness and an acknowledgment of personal defeat by Little Edie Beale, whom Ms. Ebersole portrayed in the Broadway musical “Grey Gardens.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/EBERSOLE/EBERSOLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/EBERSOLE/EBERSOLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/EBERSOLE/EBERSOLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/EBERSOLE/EBERSOLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/EBERSOLE/EBERSOL