se the issue of potential danger to troops overseas if a government shutdown occurs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Preparing for a potential showdown over raising the federal debt limit, two senior House Democrats want to remind lawmakers resistant to a debt increase that they may be putting troops overseas in jeopardy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warning on Raising Federal Debt Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T22:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/544fbb1e-c9e8-5ffe-9a72-209e462fc5d0', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/544fbb1e-c9e8-5ffe-9a72-209e462fc5d0'}, {'abstract': 'The British monologist Daniel Kitson comes to know a dead man through his correspondence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/theater/reviews/13interminable.html', 'snippet': 'The British monologist Daniel Kitson comes to know a dead man through his correspondence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Kitson’s sentences are like fast-growing mutant super-vines, sending out sticky tendrils that dig into your attention and snake themselves all over it. “Burgeoning” is a word often uttered by this shaggy British monologist in “The Interminable Suicide of Gregory Church,” his one-man show at St. Ann’s Warehouse in Brooklyn. “This burgeoning delay,” he might say, as well as the more expected “burgeoning friendship.” And (though I never thought I’d use this word in writing about a theater performance), burgeoning is the perfect description for Mr. Kitson’s irresistibly overgrown style.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/INTERMINABLE/INTERMINABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/INTERMINABLE/INTERMINABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/INTERMINABLE/INTERMINABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prolific Communication From an Isolated Man', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Interminable Suicide of Gregory Church'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prolific Communication From an Isolated Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitson, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T23:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cac85a84-f387-57be-8673-04e555e4b654', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cac85a84-f387-57be-8673-04e555e4b654'}, {'abstract': 'The president and the first lady will later attend a memorial service for shooting victims.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/obama-to-visit-giffords-in-hospital/', 'snippet': 'The president and the first lady will later attend a memorial service for shooting victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama landed in Tucson on Wednesday afternoon, and immediately headed to the hospital to see Representative Gabrielle Giffords and other people injured in the shooting on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Visiting Giffords in Hospital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T23:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4dae2c6-1863-5829-bb92-0c30d901313d', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4dae2c6-1863-5829-bb92-0c30d901313d'}, {'abstract': 'A California man was arrested on Wednesday morning for threatening to kill Representative Jim McDermott, Democrat of Washington State.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/arrest-in-threat-to-kill-a-congressman/', 'snippet': 'A California man was arrested on Wednesday morning for threatening to kill Representative Jim McDermott, Democrat of Washington State.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A California man was arrested on Wednesday morning for threatening to kill Representative Jim McDermott, Democrat of Washington State, as the shootings in Tucson sparked impassioned conversation about Congressional security on Capitol Hill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrest in Threat to Kill a Congressman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T23:10:19+0000', 'docu