 of the universe from inside a classroom with a view of winter’s wonder.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/on-a-denied-snow-day-beware-the-wrath-of-schoolchildren/', 'snippet': 'A perfect day to contemplate the unfairness of the universe from inside a classroom with a view of winter’s wonder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This one hurt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Denied Snow Day, Beware the Wrath of Schoolchildren', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T23:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d1a72bf-a812-58e9-9a72-2bd675295c90', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d1a72bf-a812-58e9-9a72-2bd675295c90'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of theater as an act (and an instrument) of political defiance is a strange one these days to most Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/theater-talkback-when-political-theater-feels-truly-dangerous/', 'snippet': 'The idea of theater as an act (and an instrument) of political defiance is a strange one these days to most Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were moments throughout the Belarus Free Theater’s production of “Being Harold Pinter,” part of the Under the Radar Festival in New York, when an icy shaft of awareness would pierce my thoughts. This wasn’t so much because of the artistry and ingenuity of this troupe from Minsk, although that was not to be denied.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: When Political Theater Feels Truly Dangerous', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belarus Free Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-12T23:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4b6098b-6870-515d-8860-ddbceacb0446', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4b6098b-6870-515d-8860-ddbceacb0446'}, {'abstract': 'Rinat Aruh and Johan Liden, the founders of the design firm Aruliden, find coat racks that combine playful with practical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/garden/13shop.html', 'snippet': 'Rinat Aruh and Johan Liden, the founders of the design firm Aruliden, find coat racks that combine playful with practical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RINAT ARUH and Johan Liden, the founders of Aruliden, a product design and marketing firm in Manhattan, spend their days rethinking products that seem ripe for reinvention, and dreaming up concepts for companies like Motorola, Puma and Microsoft. A recent pet project focused on a surprisingly ordinary object — the coat hook.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/garden/13shopping/13shopping-artic