'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6b1e45-2ed5-586e-8984-eaf92e67ce09', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6b1e45-2ed5-586e-8984-eaf92e67ce09'}, {'abstract': 'After a childhood in wartime Bosnia, Ivana Bosika found her ticket to America through a volleyball scholarship. Now she sells cars in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/nyregion/13entry.html', 'snippet': 'After a childhood in wartime Bosnia, Ivana Bosika found her ticket to America through a volleyball scholarship. Now she sells cars in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a girl growing up in the Bosnian war zone, Ivana Bosika, 27, spent more time hiding with her mother in the basement of their home in bomb-battered Brcko than strategizing about her dream career. But Ms. Bosika was always determined to study business. Eventually, her volleyball skills earned her a scholarship to Long Island University, where she received an M.B.A. in 2007. A sales associate at Lexus of Queens since August 2009, she lives in Ridgewood, Queens, with her husband, George, who installs and refinishes wood floors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From War to Volleyball, Then the Lexus Lot', 'kicker': 'Entry Level', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From War to Volleyball, Then the Lexus Lot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor