ue': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T02:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee1e9596-19a2-5313-97ad-301d49ed16f5', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee1e9596-19a2-5313-97ad-301d49ed16f5'}, {'abstract': 'Roy W. Chelsen, an engine company leader who helped save lives on 9/11, died on Sunday of cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/nyregion/13chelsen.html', 'snippet': 'Roy W. Chelsen, an engine company leader who helped save lives on 9/11, died on Sunday of cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first, his firefighter colleagues were wary when Roy W. Chelsen, the physically imposing leader of Engine Company 28, told them to run for it. One of the twin towers was gone, and they were in the one still standing. Firefighter Chelsen remembered saying, “Let’s just get these people, and let’s get out of here.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/nyregion/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT/CHELSEN-SUB3-w-CREDIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Firefighter to Die Since Signing of 9/11 Health Law Is Recalled as a Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Firefighter to Die Since Signing of 9/11 Health Law Is Recalled as a Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Zadroga 9-11 Health and Compensation Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warwick (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T02:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/420857bb-8498-5bce-9dea-93cdc174de9a', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/420857bb-8498-5bce-9dea-93cdc174de9a'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Cashman clarifies a comment about Andy Pettitte and says there is nothing new to report.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/cashman-status-quo-on-pettitte/', 'snippet': 'Brian Cashman clarifies a comment about Andy Pettitte and says there is nothing new to report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say this for iconic Yankees of the championship years: they don’t fade away easily. In 2007, Bernie Williams kind of, sort of, but not officially, stopped playing baseball. Now, four years later, Andy Pettitte is in the same situation. He’s retired — kind of, sort of, but not officially.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cashman: Status Quo on Pettitte', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T02:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/55b8b439-ec17-58e9-aae1-45276e72f277', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b8b439-ec17-58e9-aae1-45276e72f277'}, {'abstract': 'After No. 4 Syracuse defeated the St. John’s men’s team, 76-59, No. 2 UConn rolled past the Red Storm women, 84-52.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/sports/ncaabasketball/13syracuse.html', 'snippet': 'After No. 4 Syracuse defeated the St. John’s men’s team, 76-59, No. 2 UConn rolled past the Red Storm women, 84-52.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a corridor inside Madison Square Garden, members of the Syracuse men’s basketball team greeted the University of Connecticut women’s players. The Orange stopped to hug and shake hands with the Huskies and to obtain their autographs. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/sports/SYRACUSE1/SYRACUSE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not St. John’s Night in 2 Losses at Garden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Not St. John’s Night In 2 Losses at Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T02:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a35995f-a5d2-52c1-94e9-c207f62420ba', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a35995f-a5d2-52c1-94e9-c207f62420ba'}, {'abstract': 'Liz Gorski puts us in the grid of fire.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/thebes/', 'snippet': 'Liz Gorski puts us in the grid of fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — It’s always great to see a puzzle by Liz Gorski. Her grids are clean, her themes are fun and her fill highlights her vast knowledge of music, among other topics. Today’s puzzle, I’m happy to say, is no different.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: Weeper of Thebes', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T03:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/00540327-b79f-5068-8fdc-b3424cca27bf', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00540327-b79f-5068-8fdc-b3424cca27bf'}, {'abstract': '“Blood From a Stone,” written by Tommy Nohilly and starring Ethan Hawke, is a worthy but wearying new play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/theater/reviews/13blood.html', 'snippet': '“Blood From a Stone,” written by Tommy Nohilly and starring Ethan Hawke, is a worthy but wearying new play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every unhappy family may be unhappy in its own way, as Tolstoy wrote, but not all of those ways are necessarily interesting. This truth is borne out by the worthy but wearying new play “Blood From a Stone” by Tommy Nohilly, a New Group production that opened Wednesday night at the Acorn Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/arts/jp-blood/jp-blood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Discord Dished Up at Every Meal', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Blood From a Stone'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Discord Dished Up At Every Meal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nohilly, Tommy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin-Vega, Daphne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapp, Gordon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLane, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Scott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawke, Ethan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Group Theater Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T03:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2a9d4a6-646b-5f53-9a1a-1cbc439e7f73', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2a9d4a6-646b-5f53-9a1a-1cbc439e7f73'}, {'abstract': 'The address used language that recalled a central part of Mr. Obama’s appeal as a presidential candidate in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/us/13assess.html', 'snippet': 'The address used language that recalled a central part of Mr. Obama’s appeal as a presidential candidate in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — When President Obama took the stage here Wednesday to address a community — and a nation — traumatized by Saturday’s killings, it invited comparisons to President George W. Bush’s speech to the nation after the attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, and the memorial service President Bill Clinton led after the bombing of a federal office building killed 168 people in Oklahoma City in 1995.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/us/13giffords_75/13giffords_75-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/us/13giffords_75/13giffords_75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thum