nts may destroy Lebanon just to quash a murder inquiry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/opinion/13cambanis.html', 'snippet': 'Why the militants may destroy Lebanon just to quash a murder inquiry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE collapse of Lebanon’s government on Tuesday signaled the final stage in Hezbollah’s rise from resistance group to ruling power. While Hezbollah technically remains the head of the political opposition in Beirut, make no mistake: the Party of God has fully consolidated its control in Lebanon, and will stop at nothing \x97 including civil war \x97 to protect its position. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hezbollah’s Latest Suicide Mission', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hezbollah&#8217;s Latest Suicide Mission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Rafik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Saad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T04:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By THANASSIS CAMBANIS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thanassis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CAMBANIS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1337cb62-a1e5-5210-9074-87721297453f', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1337cb62-a1e5-5210-9074-87721297453f'}, {'abstract': 'The new Michigan coach Brady Hoke has a reputation a