ng party at the Met for Fox Business?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greta Van Susteren of Fox News took note on Wednesday of the fancy party at Tina Brown‘s Upper East Side home to celebrate Piers Morgan‘s debut at CNN and pointed a crooked finger at the event.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'About Those ‘Fancy Launch Parties’ …', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Susteren, Greta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T04:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/50eabfa7-cb43-5ae3-a666-555a8038d37f', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50eabfa7-cb43-5ae3-a666-555a8038d37f'}, {'abstract': 'Gil Caffray, the former chief trader at the hedge fund Tiger Management, will rejoin his old firm as chief investment officer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/a-tiger-cub-returns-taking-a-top-post/', 'snippet': 'Gil Caffray, the former chief trader at the hedge fund Tiger Management, will rejoin his old firm as chief investment officer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gil Caffray, the former chief trader at the hedge fund Tiger Management, will rejoin his old firm as chief investment officer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cub Returns to Tiger, Taking a Top Post', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T04:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96930bb-99cc-57ce-8447-524f87284159', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96930bb-99cc-57ce-8447-524f87284159'}, {'abstract': 'Two Libyan citizens were sentenced in a Berlin court for spying on members of the Libyan opposition living in Europe from August 2007 until they were arrested in May 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/world/europe/13briefs-Libya.html', 'snippet': 'Two Libyan citizens were sentenced in a Berlin court for spying on members of the Libyan opposition living in Europe from August 2007 until they were arrested in May 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two Libyan citizens were sentenced in a Berlin court for spying on members of the Libyan opposition living in Europe from August 2007 until they were arrested in May 2010. A 43-year-old officer for the Libyan intelligence service, identified as Abdel A., was sentenced to two and a half years in prison while his accomplice, Adel Al., 47, was sentenced to a term of one year and 10 months. Abdel A. was convicted of overseeing a network of informal collaborators who systematically spied on Libyan opposition members living in Germany and Western Europe. Adel Al. worked as one of these informers reporting to Abdel A. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany Sentences 2 Libyan Spies', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany Sentences 2 Libyan Spies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T04:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Homola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/62fb0010-a9e2-582f-9a3a-6454c3c12c08', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62fb0010-a9e2-582f-9a3a-6454c3c12c08'}, {'abstract': 'Turns out iPad users are marking content during the day and consuming it later in the day when they can lean back and actually read.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/12/is-the-ipad-a-time-machine-for-reading/', 'snippet': 'Turns out iPad users are marking content during the day and consuming it later in the day when they can lean back and actually read.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When devices became untethered and Web content began to be consumed anywhere, it was assumed that leisure reading would take a beating as people just skipped across content while on the go. But according to Read It Later, an application that allows consumers to mark content to catch up when and where they want to, users may come across a lot of things they want to read in the middle of the day, but they actually get back to them much later in the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the iPad a Time Machine for Reading?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T04:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d22deb72-1c99-52b7-961b-effa35fad2c3', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d22deb72-1c99-52b7-961b-effa35fad2c3'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama offered the nation’s condolences to the victims of the Tucson shootings at a memorial service at the University of Arizona.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/12/us/20110113_OBAMA.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama offered the nation’s condolences to the victims of the Tucson shootings at a memorial service at the University of Arizona.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama offered the nation’s condolences to the victims of the Tucson shootings at a memorial service at the University of Arizona.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/us/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/us/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/us/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR/20110113_OBAMA-slide-PSCR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Offers Condolences in Memorial Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name