y-virus-tied-to-forest-decline/', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that the die-back of the West’s aspens is not just marring the landscape, but also helping spread a fatal strain of hantavirus transmitted by deer mice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around 2004, large numbers of aspens in the West began dying off, and with no immediately identifiable cause, scientists dubbed the phenomenon “sudden aspen decline.” Ultimately the die-back was pinned on a severe 2002 drought and heat wave that left aspens vulnerable to pests, cankers and fungi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spread of Deadly Virus Tied to Forest Decline', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southwestern States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T12:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/56586899-5feb-5e5b-9c10-4a2be8583582', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56586899-5feb-5e5b-9c10-4a2be8583582'}, {'abstract': 'The Packers-Falcons game is the one game this week where the efficiency model differs from the broad consensus, and I think it’s because the Falcons are generally overrated.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/divisional-round-probabilities-atlanta-overrated/', 'snippet': 'The Packers-Falcons game is the one game this week where the efficiency model differs from the broad consensus, and I think it’s because the Falcons are generally overrated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Burke, a former Navy pilot who has taken up the less dangerous hobby of N.F.L. statistical analysis, operates Advanced NFL Stats, a blog about football, math and human behavior. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Divisional Round Probabilities: Is Atlanta Overrated?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0d7090-9977-5431-9cb5-60f0c30a9040', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0d7090-9977-5431-9cb5-60f0c30a9040'}, {'abstract': 'Marathon Oil announced plans to spin off its downstream business, creating two independent companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/marathon-oil-to-split-into-two/', 'snippet': 'Marathon Oil announced plans to spin off its downstream business, creating two independent companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cheryl Gerber/Associated PressMarathon refinery in Garyville, La.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marathon Oil to Split in Two', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petro