ct': 'Investment professionals believe the expert network industry needs “a clear code of conduct,” according to a new report from the research firm TABB Group.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/investors-see-need-for-change-at-expert-network-firms/', 'snippet': 'Investment professionals believe the expert network industry needs “a clear code of conduct,” according to a new report from the research firm TABB Group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of a string of arrests in the federal investigation of insider trading, there is mounting pressure for change in the expert network industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investors Say Expert Networks Need to Change Their Ways', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primary Global Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T13:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/05e1c2d1-9d3c-580a-8afe-d2cfb979d854', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05e1c2d1-9d3c-580a-8afe-d2cfb979d854'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Jacobs flirted with the “Art Deco diva” for pre-fall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/just-one-look-louis-vuitton-pre-fall-collection/', 'snippet': 'Marc Jacobs flirted with the “Art Deco diva” for pre-fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pre-Fall Collections, being shown in New York over the next several weeks, arrive in stores in May to fill the gap between bikinis and furs.Marc Jacobs flirted with the “Art Deco diva” for pre-fall, evoking an era “when a woman, armed with her liberated wardrobe, could set out to conquer the world while enjoying the luxuries of her newfound freedom.” The tweed coats in particular — this one inspired by the textile designs of Louise Bourgeois — and printed flapper dresses are for a woman not afraid to wear her art on her sleeve. But lest we should forget, freedom comes with a hefty price tag. These are clothes to go for broke. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Louis Vuitton Pre-Fall Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/15bbce94-1d89-50e7-9251-499a69c6e15b', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15bbce94-1d89-50e7-9251-499a69c6e15b'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/fafsaq-and-a-part-3-2/', 'snippet': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As families of prospective college freshmen begin to tackle the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or Fafsa, Mark Kantrowitz, a financial aid expert and founder of the Web sites finaid.org and fastweb.com, is answering questions from readers of The Choice this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Part 3: Answers to Readers’ Questions on Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kantrowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantrowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e46c9d22-ce3d-5099-803b-0901af0f9f0a', 'word_count': 2138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e46c9d22-ce3d-5099-803b-0901af0f9f0a'}, {'abstract': 'While marveling at the dissonance between grassroots filmmaking and celebrity self-appreciation, Lesley Manville has learned to enjoy herself on the promotional rounds.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/a-quick-study-on-the-awards-season-circuit/', 'snippet': 'While marveling at the dissonance between grassroots filmmaking and celebrity self-appreciation, Lesley Manville has learned to enjoy herself on the promotional rounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lesley Manville had no idea what the National Board of Review was when she learned she had won its best actress award for her work in Mike Leigh’s “Another Year.” She confided this to the Bagger, and to the roomful of attendees, at the National Board of Review’s gala on Tuesday night. Though she is a veteran actress and a veteran of Mr. Leigh’s films — it is her sixth collaboration with the maverick British director, who famously drafts no scripts or characters before he begins working on his films – it is her first time at the awards slog. She’s a quick study, though. (She has to be: Mr. Leigh’s films are all improvised.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quick Study on the Awards-Season Circuit', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6f826e8-81ba-5f91-bbc9-f293c2f10458', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6f826e8-81ba-5f91-bbc9-f293c2f10458'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/morning-take-out-162/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERGERS & ACQUISITIONS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerzbank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MySpace.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sara Lee Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e304b28-509e-596c-bd2d-15fbb7f55a1e', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e304b28-509e-596c-bd2d-15fbb7f55a1e'}, {'abstract': 'The board of Exco Resources says it is considering a buyout offer made by Douglas H. Miller, the company’s chief executive, which values the oil and gas producer at $4.35 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/exco-board-is-mulling-ceos-buyout-bid/', 'snippet': 'The board of Exco Resources says it is considering a buyout offer made by Douglas H. Miller, the company’s chief executive, which values the oil and gas producer at $4.35 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board of Exco Resources, an oil and gas producer based in Dallas, said on Thursday  that it was considering a buyout offer made by Douglas H. Miller, the company’s chief executive officer, which values Exco at $4.35 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exco Board Weighs Chief’s Buyout Offer', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pickens, T Boone Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EXCO Resources Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc42c370-1540-5ed3-a358-2c2cf07e42cd', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc42c370-1540-5ed3-a358-2c2cf07e42cd'}, {'abstract': 'Antitrust investigators are asking advertisers if Google ever tied increased spending to improved visibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/technology/14google.html', 'snippet': 'Antitrust investigators are asking advertisers if Google ever tied increased spending to improved visibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS \x97 European antitrust investigators are asking advertisers whether Google suggested they increase spending with the company in return for improved visibility in its Web search results. The investigators are also examining whether Google stymied companies who had tried to move their business elsewhere.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/technology/14google-span/14google-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/technology/14google-span/14google-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/technology/14google-span/14google-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Inquiry Focuses on Google Business Practice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigators in Europe\nSurvey Google Ad Buyers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62778afa-fe88-5631-a9f4-fa25cc99579a', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62778afa-fe88-5631-a9f4-fa25cc99579a'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: The first firefighter dies since the signing of the 9/11 Zadroga health bill; a charter school kerfuffle; and more regional developments.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/morning-buzz-ghailani-prosecutors-rebut-defense-motion/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: The first firefighter dies since the signing of the 9/11 Zadroga health bill; a charter school kerfuffle; and more regional developments.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The city is getting back to its regularly scheduled program this morning. We are expecting clear skies ahead and a high in the upper 20s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Ghailani Prosecutors Rebut Defense Motion', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e8e1abc-7d40-50d8-a579-c4c5639941bf', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e8e1abc-7d40-50d8-a579-c4c5639941bf'}, {'abstract': 'Wikipedia will celebrate its 10th anniversary on Saturday with conferences and parties across the globe — organized by its users, of course.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/wikipedia-marks-10-years-of-edit-it-yourself/', 'snippet': 'Wikipedia will celebrate its 10th anniversary on Saturday with conferences and parties across the globe — organized by its users, of course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An untested idea — allowing regular people to create an online encyclopedia — went live on Jan. 15, 2001, with no fanfare. No one knew whether people would contribute to such a project, and if so, whether the information they submitted would be reliable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wikipedia Marks 10 Years of Edit-It-Yourself', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikimedia Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verne G. Kopytoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c720781-7694-5f47-8dfe-6ad93823500d', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c720781-7694-5f47-8dfe-6ad93823500d'}, {'abstract': 'Reaction to President Obama’s speech at the memorial service in Arizona on Wednesday night has been almost uniformly positive.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/praise-for-obama-from-the-right-and-left/', 'snippet': 'Reaction to President Obama’s speech at the memorial service in Arizona on Wednesday night has been almost uniformly positive.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:39 a.m. | Updated Reaction to President Obama’s speech at the memorial service in Arizona on Wednesday night has been almost uniformly positive, even from some of his sharpest critics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Praise for Obama, From the Right and Left', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2dd469-f826-5475-8f66-6b2938609f6a', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2dd469-f826-5475-8f66-6b2938609f6a'}, {'abstract': 'Attendees and honorees at two awards parties this week in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/12/movies/awardsseason/baggerawards.html', 'snippet': 'Attendees and honorees at two awards parties this week in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attendees and honorees at two awards parties this week in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/movies/awardsseason/baggerawards-slide-IJTD/baggerawards-slide-IJTD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/12/movies/awardsseason/baggerawards-slide-IJTD/baggerawards-slide-IJTD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/12/movies/awardsseason/baggerawards-slide-IJTD/baggerawards-slide-IJTD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pre-Oscar Parties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/124552b8-f2d4-5007-ba8e-70fcd4d51f53', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/124552b8-f2d4-5007-ba8e-70fcd4d51f53'}, {'abstract': 'C.J. Chivers offers a view of the Afghan countryside from the back of Black Hawk helicopters crisscrossing the region on medevac runs.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/vantage-point-the-challenges-of-small-unit-patrolling-in-afghanistan/', 'snippet': 'C.J. Chivers offers a view of the Afghan countryside from the back of Black Hawk helicopters crisscrossing the region on medevac runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carrying small digital video cameras on patrols and other military missions covered by The New York Times over the years, I have amassed a few bricks worth of footage of the Afghan war — shuras and firefights, long walks and short dashes, helicopter flights and convoys, the routines of fire base life and an accidental visual inventory of the Afghan countryside. I often keep the video camera on as a notebook, absorbing sights and sounds that I might refer to later when I write. It aids with accuracy. Many times I also find that the camera has soaked up dialogue or recorded visual details that that I didn’t hear or see in real time. It’s a priceless tool, even if it adds to the work after each assignment, when the footage must be downloaded, labeled and archived.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vantage Point: The Challenges of Small-Unit Patrolling in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marja (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0c5ba36-a7d5-5e6d-a9b1-0e7585780989', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0c5ba36-a7d5-5e6d-a9b1-0e7585780989'}, {'abstract': '“A Fire in My Belly” by David Wojnarowicz is already on display.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/museum-of-modern-art-acquires-video-withdrawn-from-smithsonian-exhibition/', 'snippet': '“A Fire in My Belly” by David Wojnarowicz is already on display.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Modern Art has acquired the David Wojnarowicz video that was removed from a show at the National Portrait Gallery in Washington after drawing criticism from a religious organization and some congressional Republicans. The museum acquired both the original 13-minute version of the video, titled “A Fire in My Belly,” and a separate 7-minute excerpt made by the artist; the two are now being shown in a loop as part of a display of contemporary art from the museum’s collection that will remain up until May 9. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Modern Art Acquires Video Withdrawn From Smithsonian Exhibition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wojnarowicz, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T14:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a14de44-97a9-55ee-a5d6-fe8ad7602ca3', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a14de44-97a9-55ee-a5d6-fe8ad7602ca3'}, {'abstract': 'With its perennially happening night life and laissez-faire attitude, the Paris of the North is usually thought of as a party city, but it does have its quieter pockets.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/northern-star-montreal/', 'snippet': 'With its perennially happening night life and laissez-faire attitude, the Paris of the North is usually thought of as a party city, but it does have its quieter pockets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its perennially happening night life and laissez-faire attitude, the Paris of the North is usually thought of as a party city, but it does have its quieter pockets. Little Burgundy, a k a \xa0La Petite Bourgogne, a working-class neighborhood that’s been slowly gentrifying over the past 10 years, isn’t as flashy as the better-known Plateau Mont-Royal, but its relaxed vibe and excellent dining options make it an ideal place for a lazy autumnal amble. More…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Star | Montreal', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T15:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2d56cf-254a-5bdb-8442-cdbd8845bcda', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2d56cf-254a-5bdb-8442-cdbd8845bcda'}, {'abstract': 'Chewing gum can in fact help alleviate the symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux disease, better known to most people as GERD or heartburn.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/remedies-chewing-gum-for-heartburn/', 'snippet': 'Chewing gum can in fact help alleviate the symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux disease, better known to most people as GERD or heartburn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a third of American adults use some form of complementary or alternative medicine, according to a government report. Natural remedies have an obvious appeal, but how do you know which ones to choose and whether the claims are backed by science? In this occasional series, Anahad O’Connor, the New York Times “Really?” columnist, explores the claims and the science behind alternative remedies that you may want to consider for your family medicine cabinet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remedies: Chewing Gum for Heartburn', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 