{'abstract': 'His movie and TV projects dominante the nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/tyler-perrys-awards-extravaganza-nominations-galore-from-n-a-a-c-p/', 'snippet': 'His movie and TV projects dominante the nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Film and television projects by Tyler Perry dominated the nominations for the N.A.A.C.P.’s 42nd annual Image Awards, announced on Wednesday, while Halle Berry, Smokey Robinson, Denzel Washington and Kanye West were among the nominees in acting and music categories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyler Perry’s Awards Extravaganza: Nominations Galore From N.A.A.C.P.', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Condoleezza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T15:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0991b888-913a-5842-b46d-47b199592f82', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0991b888-913a-5842-b46d-47b199592f82'}, {'abstract': 'The Environmental Protection Agency said on Thursday that the mountaintop-removal project would have done unacceptable damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/science/earth/14coal.html', 'snippet': 'The Environmental Protection Agency said on Thursday that the mountaintop-removal project would have done unacceptable damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The Environmental Protection Agency revoked the permit for one of the nation’s largest mountaintop-removal coal mining projects on Thursday, saying the mine would have done unacceptable damage to rivers, wildlife and communities in West Virginia. It was the first time the agency had rescinded a valid clean water permit for a coal mine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agency Revokes Permit for Major Coal Mining Project', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Revokes Permit for West Virginia Mining Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCH COAL INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T16:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a78de028-7592-533d-9de7-48080654fd85', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a78de028-7592-533d-9de7-48080654fd85'}, {'abstract': 'The agency’s action is certain to provoke an outcry from West Virginia politicians, the coal industry and other businesses that resist regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/e-p-a-revokes-controversial-mine-permit/', 'snippet': 'The agency’s action is certain to provoke an outcry from West Virginia politicians, the coal industry and other businesses that resist regulation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has revoked the permit for Arch Coal’s Spruce No. 1 mountaintop-removal coal mining project in West Virginia, saying that the operation would damage communities and wildlife. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Revokes Controversial Mine Permit', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T16:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/24623769-13ca-5bec-804f-b005371d85da', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24623769-13ca-5bec-804f-b005371d85da'}, {'abstract': 'On this week’s podcast, segments include Verizon’s iPhone, reflections on the Consumer Electronics Show,  a revamped Oxford English Dictionary and live-streaming aviation chatter.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/tech-talk-podcast-verizons-iphone/', 'snippet': 'On this week’s podcast, segments include Verizon’s iPhone, reflections on the Consumer Electronics Show,  a revamped Oxford English Dictionary and live-streaming aviation chatter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On this week’s show, J.D. Biersdorfer chats with Jenna Wortham, a New York Times technology reporter, about Verizon‘s iPhone. The Times’s personal technology editor, Sam Grobart, joins in to reflect on last week’s Consumer Electronics Show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Verizon’s iPhone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '