: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b92e8c2-8dcf-5194-b246-39a1d6fe93d7', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b92e8c2-8dcf-5194-b246-39a1d6fe93d7'}, {'abstract': 'The Cosmopolitan Las Vegas, which opened in December, offers the battery-powered sports car as a slot-machine grand prize.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/in-las-vegas-hit-the-jackpot-get-a-tesla/', 'snippet': 'The Cosmopolitan Las Vegas, which opened in December, offers the battery-powered sports car as a slot-machine grand prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The telephone’s on-hold music for the new Cosmopolitan hotel and casino came courtesy of the Talking Heads. A recent addition to the Las Vegas Strip, the Cosmopolitan projects a trendsetting image, which translates to very little Wayne Newton. It presented the rising indie-pop group Best Coast in a four-night stand in the lounge, but perhaps more telling of its ambitions to lure the young, culturally progressive and affluent, its slot machines offer a Tesla Roadster as a grand prize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Las Vegas, Hit the Jackpot, Get a Tesla', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T16:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d34cc1e5-dd40-5870-855a-e865447618a3', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d34cc1e5-dd40-5870-855a-e865447618a3'}, {'abstract': 'One thing is clear in the relationship between Nicolas Sarkozy and Angela Merkel: Ultimately, she holds the cards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/magazine/16MerkelSarkozy-t.html', 'snippet': 'One thing is clear in the relationship between Nicolas Sarkozy and Angela Merkel: Ultimately, she holds the cards.', 'lead_paragraph': ' SHE MAKES FUN, in private, of the way he walks and talks, of his rapid, jerky gestures and facial grimaces. He mocks her deliberation, her reluctance, her matronly caution. She has compared him to Mr. Bean and to the French comic Louis de Funès, with his curly hair and large nose. He sometimes calls her La Boche, the offensive French version of “Kraut,” and goes out of his way to give her an embrace and a double-cheeked kiss in the French fashion, the kind of contact that he knows very well, aides say, she cannot stand.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/magazine/16MerkelSarkozy-span/16MerkelSarkozy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/magazine/16MerkelSarkozy-span/16MerkelSarkozy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/magazine/16MerkelSarkozy-span/16MerkelSarkozy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/magazine/16MerkelSarkozy-span/16MerkelSarkozy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'