'uri': 'nyt://article/59c14e38-9f23-5556-ade4-5001bde7c915'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities accused the Belarussian Helsinki Committee of unlawfully distorting information about the situation in the country amid a continued opposition crackdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/world/europe/14belarus.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities accused the Belarussian Helsinki Committee of unlawfully distorting information about the situation in the country amid a continued opposition crackdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW \x97 The authorities in Belarus have issued a warning to a prominent human rights group, accusing it of unlawfully distorting information about the situation in the country amid a continued crackdown on opponents of President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus Issues Warning to Rights Group Amid Crackdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus Issues Warning to Rights Group Amid Crackdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T16:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2dde128-8961-5dd6-9e0d-5d0438a0ba11', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2dde128-8961-5dd6-9e0d-5d0438a0ba11'}, {'abstract': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/what-were-reading-96/', 'snippet': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T16:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/73847055-e671-5746-b791-ed22a97327b0', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73847055-e671-5746-b791-ed22a97327b0'}, {'abstract': 'Jazz forward Andrei Kirilenko just became an American citizen, but that doesn’t mean he won’t go back to Russia to play if the N.B.A. locks out its players.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/new-citizen-kirilenko-ponders-lockout-options/', 'snippet': 'Jazz forward Andrei Kirilenko just became an American citizen, but that doesn’t mean he won’t go back to Russia to play if the N.B.A. locks out its players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do svidaniya Andrei Kirilenko? (In Russian: goodbye.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Citizen Kirilenko Ponders Lockout Options', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizatio