'nyt://article/0cf62a54-0682-5187-8c77-c59d77610051'}, {'abstract': 'He gave the best speech of his presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/obama-in-arizona/', 'snippet': 'He gave the best speech of his presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t have much to add to the litany of praise that the president’s memorial service performance has earned, deservedly, from his political opponents. The peculiar atmosphere of the event notwithstanding, the speech was everything it needed to be: A moving eulogy for the dead, a sober, religiously-inflected reflection on the mystery of iniquity, and an explicit rebuke to partisan readings of this tragedy\xa0— which will close the book, one hopes, on a week’s worth of inappropriate and increasingly implausible attempts to portray Jared Lee Loughner as a Tea Partier in spirit. Everything Obama did right during his presidential campaign he did right last night: It may not have been the best speech of his life, but it was the best speech of his presidency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama in Arizona', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T17:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aa74aa9-c803-5860-b109-3578a3e3953b', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aa74aa9-c803-5860-b109-3578a3e3953b'}, {'abstract': 'The government’s request for online activity related to WikiLeaks shines a light on an out-of-date law.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/should-e-mail-and-letters-have-equal-protection/', 'snippet': 'The government’s request for online activity related to WikiLeaks shines a light on an out-of-date law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend, we reported that the government had ordered Twitter to turn over private information about users associated with WikiLeaks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should E-Mail and Letters Have Equal Legal Protection?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Communications Privacy Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Due Process', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T17:52:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee7cb8f5-7a3d-5ea8-ba7e-d895ba0c498a', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee7cb8f5-7a3d-5ea8-ba7e-d895ba0c498a'}, {'abstract': 'Does America have a cultural elite? Yes, but not the one that some worriers have in mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/movies/16scott.html', 'snippet': 'Does America have a cultural elite? Yes, but not the one that some worriers have in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME people renounce liquor or sweets. My New Year’s resolution for 2011 was to give up meta: no panels on the State or Future or Death of Criticism; no trolling the Internet looking for fights over first principles; no thumb suckers for the Sunday paper on the history or the essence of the critical profession. Enough of all that! Instead, a renewed commitment to the basics. For 12 months or more phrases like “politique des auteurs,” “Pauline Kael,” “received wisdom,” “reflexively contrarian” and “formalist hack” would not pass my lips or issue from my keyboard, no matter how much I was provoked.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/SCOTT-1/SCOTT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/SCOTT-1/SCOTT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/SCOTT-1/SCOTT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/SCOTT-1/SCOTT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/SCOTT-1/SCOTT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defy the Elite! Wait, Which Elite?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defy the Elite! Wait, Which Elite?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ebert, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kael, Pauline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T17:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '0', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'org