n’t negotiate as hard as others when their companies are on the block, a study by Cass Business School at the City University of London found.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/take-my-company-please/', 'snippet': 'Chief executives who can expect a golden handshake don’t negotiate as hard as others when their companies are on the block, a study by Cass Business School at the City University of London found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chief executives who can expect a golden handshake don’t negotiate as hard as others when their companies are on the block, a study by Cass Business School at the City University of London found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Take My Company, Please…', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T18:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5011c66-53c4-5900-8de7-1dac1038fd2b', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5011c66-53c4-5900-8de7-1dac1038fd2b'}, {'abstract': 'Photo: A ghost of snowy light shines through the trees.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/central-park-wednesday-1-a-m/', 'snippet': 'Photo: A ghost of snowy light shines through the trees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You probably think you’re sick of snow, but perhaps you’re just sick of municipal snow-clearing controversies. There was not a plow in sight when reader Adam Garelick, a lawyer for the federal Department of Labor, snapped this in Central Park in the high 70s. Thank you, Mr. Garelick. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central Park, Wednesday, 1 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T18:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a174dee-5e94-5b05-a4c9-5f3e2844b268', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a174dee-5e94-5b05-a4c9-5f3e2844b268'}, {'abstract': 'A program led by Dr. Carnell Cooper in Baltimore has produced significant drops in repeat hospitalizations for gunshot wounds and other violent injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/health/13chen.html', 'snippet': 'A program led by Dr. Carnell Cooper in Baltimore has produced significant drops in repeat hospitalizations for gunshot wounds and other violent injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of every year, in what was one of our grimmest rituals during training, the other young doctors and I would huddle over the local newspaper and read through the obituary year-in-review section. We would pick out the names and faces we recognized, recall their stories and marvel over the lives they led outside of the hospital. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/health/13well/13well-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/13/health/13well/13well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/13/health/13well/13well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking the Cycle of Violence', 'kicker': 'Doctor and Patient', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaking the Cycle of Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T18:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f47cd1-eaa9-5b34-9b18-7ac01b352f20', 'word_count': 1859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f47cd1-eaa9-5b34-9b18-7ac01b352f20'}, {'abstract': 'At the University of Maryland in Baltimore, Dr. Carnell Cooper works to break the cycle of violence in the community.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/a-doctors-mission-to-end-violence/', 'snippet': 'At the University of Maryland in Baltimore, Dr. Carnell Cooper works to break the cycle of violence in the community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we are reminded not just this week but every day in the news, violence remains a major public health issue in the United States. While advances in trauma surgery, critical care and emergency medicine have allowed doctors to save more victims of violence, these advances have done nothing to deter repeat violent crimes or the hospitalizations and death that often follow. Homicide remains the 15th leading cause of death over all and the leading cause of death among African-American males age 15 to 34.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Doctor’s Mission to End Violence', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Maryland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/11a8b5f4-8a9a-537f-a090-73a341c83155', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11a8b5f4-8a9a-537f-a090-73a341c83155'}, {'abstract': 'The Atlantic Theater Company production will be directed by David Leveaux.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/carey-mulligan-to-star-in-through-a-glass-darkly/', 'snippet': 'The Atlantic Theater Company production will be directed by David Leveaux.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Despite at least three major film projects in the works, the Academy Award nominee Carey Mulligan (“An Education”) is finding time to return to the New York stage. Ms. Mulligan is set to star in the United States premiere of “Through A Glass Darkly,” a stage adaptation of the 1961 film by Ingmar Bergman about a mentally ill young woman who, while on a tense vacation with her family, grapples with a tenuous hold on reality and with otherworldly voices, one of which may be God’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carey Mulligan to Star in ‘Through a Glass Darkly’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulligan, Carey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T18:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9456d77-8bfc-56bd-ad9c-8a9eb4077960', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9456d77-8bfc-56bd-ad9c-8a9eb4077960'}, {'abstract': 'Lesson Plan | Considering criticisms of Advanced Placement courses and exams and how the College Board plans to revamp A.P. history and biology.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/advance-notice-examining-the-focus-and-value-of-the-a-p-program/', 'snippet': 'Lesson Plan | Considering criticisms of Advanced Placement courses and exams and how the College Board plans to revamp A.P. history and biology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | Why is the College Board revamping the Advanced Placement program? What do students and teachers need to know about future A.P. tests? In this lesson, students discuss the coming changes to the Advanced Placement program as well as some of their own thoughts on what might make college preparatory learning more effective. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advance Notice: Examining the Focus and Value of the A.P. Program', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T19:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annissa Hambouz and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hambouz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/61cc83c2-2ce8-5f0e-b84b-1ae51d7d86ad', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61cc83c2-2ce8-5f0e-b84b-1ae51d7d86ad'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s where to get your New York deli fix while in Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/best-in-the-northwest-village-kornblatts-deli-portland/', 'snippet': 'Here’s where to get your New York deli fix while in Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gourmet coffee and thriving food cart cultures of Portland, Ore., are hardly starving for attention, but the city is also quietly home to Kornblatt’s Delicatessen, one of the truly great New York delis outside the five boroughs.Located in the Northwest 23rd shopping district, this displaced ode to New York deli counter culture strives for authenticity (Nova lox, pickles and meats imported from New York City), and yet it can’t help but reflect the differences between Manhattan and Portland. For starters, there are four local beers on tap, including Deschutes Black Butte Porter and Cascade I.P.A., as well as a spacious, relaxed dining room and a vegetarian Reuben option, both unheard of at, say, Katz’s or Eisenberg’s in New York. There’s even locally made organic chicken basil sausage on the brunch menu.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best in the (North)West: Kornblatt’s Deli, Portland', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T19:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Michelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce0b2771-6a35-55c5-938f-53c0a9b7b9e5', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce0b2771-6a35-55c5-938f-53c0a9b7b9e5'}, {'abstract': 'CardRatings.com’s take on the worst and best credit cards of the last year.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/the-worst-and-best-credit-cards-of-2010/', 'snippet': 'CardRatings.com’s take on the worst and best credit cards of the last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The editors of credit card comparison site CardRatings.com recently announced their\xa0 take on the worst and best credit cards of 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Worst and Best Credit Cards of 2010', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T19:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/05d24e59-62bd-51e7-9c52-9c564f9a22d9', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05d24e59-62bd-51e7-9c52-9c564f9a22d9'}, {'abstract': 'An Afghan presidential commission has determined that military operations in the Kandahar area ha