ekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2487108-1a1c-5de3-99e7-3d61927cba9e', 'word_count': 1540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2487108-1a1c-5de3-99e7-3d61927cba9e'}, {'abstract': 'Oscar pundits often say Academy winners need likable characters, which makes “The King’s Speech” a frontrunner. But Harvey Weinstein says Academy love is hard to predict.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/sympathy-for-the-academy/', 'snippet': 'Oscar pundits often say Academy winners need likable characters, which makes “The King’s Speech” a frontrunner. But Harvey Weinstein says Academy love is hard to predict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— What makes an Academy movie? (Aside from having a screener and a few dozen ‘For Your Consideration’ ads, of course.) Story, casting and directing all factor in, naturally, but Oscar pundits often point to more ephemeral measures: can you root for the characters? Do you leave the theater feeling good? As of a few weeks ago, the Bagger’s colleagues on the race beat were still hotly debating the notion of likability with respect to “The Social Network,” sometimes considered too anti-heroic but now a best picture frontrunner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sympathy for the Academy', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/95cd6d95-240e-5103-aab4-ab813e6ecc21', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95cd6d95-240e-5103-aab4-ab813e6ecc21'}, {'abstract': 'Can you recommend a place that serves such good pork and shellfish dishes that my kosher boyfriend will convert permanently? That question, and others, answered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/dining/14mrcritic.html', 'snippet': 'Can you recommend a place that serves such good pork and shellfish dishes that my kosher boyfriend will convert permanently? That question, and others, answered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mail brought, among other things, questions of religious difference and requests for reservation advice and for a place to watch television while eating well. I tried my best to answer. As ever, you can send your own questions to dinejournal@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SIFTON-span/SIFTON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SIFTON-span/SIFTON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SIFTON-span/SIFTON-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SIFTON-span/SIFTON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SIFTON-span/SIFTON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'hea