r': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2f4c962-24f1-5e3e-aa4f-67e60b06fd9c', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2f4c962-24f1-5e3e-aa4f-67e60b06fd9c'}, {'abstract': '“He was such an elusive and transient figure that for the first eight years of my life I seem to have believed my father was the product of my imagination.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/books/excerpt-cocaines-son.html', 'snippet': '“He was such an elusive and transient figure that for the first eight years of my life I seem to have believed my father was the product of my imagination.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPTER 1 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Cocaine’s Son’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b44cfe9-70c3-5e97-9612-b9c6e856b8cc', 'word_count': 2520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b44cfe9-70c3-5e97-9612-b9c6e856b8cc'}, {'abstract': 'A Times culture reporter’s memoir of his father’s drug addiction and its effects on his own life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/books/14book.html', 'snippet': 'A Times culture reporter’s memoir of his father’s drug addiction and its effects on his own life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 2005 New York magazine published “Cocaine’s Kid,” an unflinching essay by Dave Itzkoff about the addiction of his father, Gerald, a needy, hot-tempered, obsessive, yet nevertheless endearing merchant in the fur trade. The author had already discussed his dad in the ribald memoir, “Lads: A Memoir of Manhood,” which concerned his own misadventures in the magazine world, but this essay zeroed in on the effects that his father’s addiction had on his own life. It concluded with Mr. Itzkoff doubting whether he or his father, then 65 and purportedly clean, would ever truly be healed of the addiction’s impact. “This is the part of the story where I run out of events to relate,” Mr. Itzkoff writes in the last sentence of his essay, “but I don’t know that I can honestly call it the end.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Done With Drugs, But the Legacy Is Unfinished', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Done With Drugs, But the Legacy Is Unfinished', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Itzkoff, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f28c1c75-62f9-5a71-812f-1a94d978ca1d', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f28c1c75-62f9-5a71-812f-1a94d978ca1d'}, {'abstract': 'Ich bin ein Eurofriend!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/yurp-too/', 'snippet': 'Ich bin ein Eurofriend!', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comments on my euro piece are actually kind of amazing: so many Europeans convinced that any criticism must stem from American desire to see Europe fail. I guess we’re not so different after all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yurp Too', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/82a09700-fab0-532e-aa3d-bfca21c029f7', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82a09700-fab0-532e-aa3d-bfca21c029f7'}, {'abstract': 'The company reported that fourth-quarter income rose 48 percent while revenue rose 8 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/technology/14chip.html', 'snippet': 'The company reported that fourth-quarter income rose 48 percent while revenue rose 8 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intel set records for profit and revenue in its latest quarter, offering evidence that businesses were gaining confidence and investing more heavily in technology.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/business/Chip/Chip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Intel Reports Record Profit and Exudes Confidence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intel Reports Record Profit and Exudes Confidence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie J. Flynn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Flynn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ec70251-bf40-59eb-82a3-3251ce2f5b97', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ec70251-bf40-59eb-82a3-3251ce2f5b97'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion and film collide in the designer Mandy Coon’s latest project.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/13/asked-answered-mandy-coon/', 'snippet': 'Fashion and film collide in the designer Mandy Coon’s latest project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mandy Coon nabbed one of this year’s Ecco Domani fashion awards for her structural, dark, moody and much buzzed-about designs, but her talents don’t stop there. She occasionally moonlights as a D.J. and a model, and it turns out she is also something of a film buff. Her newest side project is called the Fashion in Film-Designer Inspiration movie night. First up for the private event is Ingmar Bergman’s beautifully confusing psychological thriller “Persona.” The film stars Liv Ullmann as Elisabeth, a successful actress who becomes suddenly mute, and Bibi Andersson as Alma, a young nurse who is supposed to care for Elisabeth but falls into an even more twisted and fragile mental state than her patient. The film’s costumes are more straightforward than the plot — black turtlenecks, a great pleather trench, a monochromatic suit. It’s not hard to see why Coon would be drawn to it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Mandy Coon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T21:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3951cdce-add8-5ba1-9011-c4d08c130e32', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3951cdce-add8-5ba1-9011-c4d08c130e32'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/arts/design/14art.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum and Gallery Listings for Jan. 14-20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'ra