{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udall, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T22:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/057277bd-628c-57c5-bf9b-4e586c679f21', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/057277bd-628c-57c5-bf9b-4e586c679f21'}, {'abstract': 'For many years. Jacob Wrey Mould’s sheepfold was the home of Tavern on the Green; it now awaits its next assignment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/realestate/16streetscapes.html', 'snippet': 'For many years. Jacob Wrey Mould’s sheepfold was the home of Tavern on the Green; it now awaits its next assignment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT midwinter Central Park’s old Tavern on the Green looks empty and forgotten, but this is just the time to go see it. There are no more fancy parties, no limos, just a temporary visitors’ center and a few food trucks where lights used to twinkle over one of the most popular tourist restaurants in town. Built as a shelter for sheep when they were lawn mowers, it has been cleared of the worst of the restaurant accretions by the Department of Parks and Recreation, restoring to view much of the spectacular Victorian polychromy. Now the 1871 structure is awaiting... what? ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capti