, 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/167f6e54-cc48-5cd8-948e-fcf065aaf4c6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/167f6e54-cc48-5cd8-948e-fcf065aaf4c6'}, {'abstract': 'A provincial court convicted and sentenced a truck driver to life in prison for evading more than $550,000 in road fees during eight months of highway driving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/world/asia/14china.html', 'snippet': 'A provincial court convicted and sentenced a truck driver to life in prison for evading more than $550,000 in road fees during eight months of highway driving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING \x97 Like most drivers around the world, Shi Jianfeng did not like to roll down his window at toll booths. In fact, Mr. Shi, a farmer from Henan Province in central China, was so averse to toll collectors, he evaded more than $550,000 in road fees during eight months of highway driving, according to the provincial court that convicted him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Sentence for Chinese Driver for Evading Tolls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Driver Sentenced to Life in Prison for Evading Road Tolls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-13T23:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbd24de3-bb02-5f8b-af2b-ccac3596dc09', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbd24de3-bb02-5f8b-af2b-ccac3596dc09'}, {'abstract': 'In a new film made up of true stories collected over a decade, Chinese citizens who try to fight city hall find themselves battling entrenched and unscrupulous forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/movies/14petition.html', 'snippet': 'In a new film made up of true stories collected over a decade, Chinese citizens who try to fight city hall find themselves battling entrenched and unscrupulous forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The right of the people to “petition the Government for a redress of grievances,” as the First Amendment to the United States Constitution phrases it, would seem to be a basic feature of the relationship between citizen and state. Even nondemocratic systems acknowledge the principle that the rulers should listen to the complaints of the ruled. Zhao Liang’s “Petition,” a brave and wrenching new documentary from China, takes a bottom-up view of the cruel and absurd ways that lofty ideal is put into practice on the streets of Beijing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14PETITION/PETITION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 941, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14PETITION/PETITION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14PETITION/PETITION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, You Can’t Fight City Hall', 'kicker': 'Movie Revie