s in the documentary “Breaking and Entering.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The only significantly false note in “Breaking and Entering” is its overly clever title, which doesn’t give you much of a clue that it’s a film about people obsessed with getting their names in the Guinness Book of World Records. Otherwise, Benjamin Fingerhut’s documentary is a brisk and absorbing tour of the human ego.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BREAK-span/ROUNDUP-BREAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BREAK-span/ROUNDUP-BREAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BREAK-span/ROUNDUP-BREAK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BREAK-span/ROUNDUP-BREAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14BREAK-span/ROUNDUP-BREAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Records Won’t Win Celebrity for Peculiar Elite', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Breaking and Entering'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T00:41:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 