it', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simms, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nantz, Jim', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collinsworth, Cris', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T01:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3044cbd-5688-512b-bcf1-b2cd1a5a4b23', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3044cbd-5688-512b-bcf1-b2cd1a5a4b23'}, {'abstract': 'A humane sensibility is revealed by Stellan Skarsgard as Ulrik, a reformed killer in “A Somewhat Gentle Man,” a Norwegian entry into the deadpan gangster comedy genre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/movies/14somewhat.html', 'snippet': 'A humane sensibility is revealed by Stellan Skarsgard as Ulrik, a reformed killer in “A Somewhat Gentle Man,” a Norwegian entry into the deadpan gangster comedy genre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like its glum antihero, “A Somewhat Gentle Man” takes a little time to find its feet. Until it does, you may struggle to care about Ulrik (Stellan Skarsgard), a middle-aged murderer newly released from prison. Beefy and slow-moving, quiet and ponytailed, Ulrik seems content to observe freedom rather than embrace it. His former boss (a strutting Bjorn Floberg) expects him to kill the snitch who put him away for 12 years, but Ulrik is done with violence — or so he thinks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SOME-span/ROUNDUP-SOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SOME-span/ROUNDUP-SOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SOME-span/ROUNDUP-SOME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SOME-span/ROUNDUP-SOME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/arts/14SOME-span/ROUNDUP-SOME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Humanity Under Layers of Grit and After Years of Crime', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'A Somewhat Gentle Man'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skarsgard, Stellan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moland, Hans Petter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T01:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb84e7c0-8ee2-5516-8a17-980c058cc7db', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb84e7c0-8ee2-5516-8a17-980c058cc7db'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Benedict XVI appointed an envoy to Vietnam on Thursday, a step toward normalizing diplomatic relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/world/europe/14webbrfs.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Benedict XVI appointed an envoy to Vietnam on Thursday, a step toward normalizing diplomatic relations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pope Benedict XVI appointed an envoy to Vietnam on Thursday, a step toward normalizing diplomatic relations. The Vatican has no formal diplomatic ties with Vietnam, which has about six million Roman Catholics, but relations have been improving recently. The new papal representative in Vietnam, Msgr. Leopoldo Girelli, is currently Papal Nuncio to Indonesia.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vatican: Envoy to Vietnam Appointed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BRIEFS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T01:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df947323-19d0-5639-8033-4540523c7eb9', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df947323-19d0-5639-8033-4540523c7eb9'}, {'abstract': 'Adding the beer station was a way for the drug chain to soothe concerns that it would run a local pharmacy out of business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/business/14beer.html', 'snippet': 'Adding the beer station was a way for the drug chain to soothe concerns that it would run a local pharmacy out of business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Duane Reade opened a new store a few months ago in Brooklyn, it faced opposition from residents loyal to a local pharmacy. So it decided to include something in the store that the neighborhood did not have: a bar that specializes in beer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/business/SubBeerjp1/SubBeerjp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Duane Reade in Brooklyn With a Beer Bar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drug Chain’s Beer Bar Serves a Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duane Reade Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T01:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/778b981b-3441-55dd-9e09-67ba8911685d', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/778b981b-3441-55dd-9e09-67ba8911685d'}, {'abstract': 'Pietro Polizzi, whose conviction on child pornography charges won him an unusual champion — the trial judge, Jack B. Weinstein — was sentenced to five years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/nyregion/14weinstein.html', 'snippet': 'Pietro Polizzi, whose conviction on child pornography charges won him an unusual champion — the trial judge, Jack B. Weinstein — was sentenced to five years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man whose conviction on child pornography charges won him an unusual champion \x97 the trial judge, Jack B. Weinstein \x97 was sentenced on Thursday to five years in prison, the minimum sentence required by law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Defies Prosecutors on Pornography Sentence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Defies Prosecutors On Pornography Sentence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Jack B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T01:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef60017-7ee0-509d-86da-1c0d4b12da89', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef60017-7ee0-509d-86da-1c0d4b12da89'}, {'abstract': 'A new play about a councilman who betrayed New Orleans by taking bribes stars the man himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/us/14bribes.html', 'snippet': 'A new play about a councilman who betrayed New Orleans by taking bribes stars the man himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS \x97 On Friday night, the Anthony Bean Community Theater, an 11-year-old institution on the second floor of a church office building, will be putting on a world premiere. Much of the city already knows the plot by heart, as it is based on a true story. The play concerns the downfall of a popular city councilman named Oliver Thomas who is caught taking bribes, betraying the city that supported him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/us/BRIBES--1/BRIBES--1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/14/us/BRIBES--1/BRIBES--1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/us/BRIBES--1/BRIBES--1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/14/us/BRIBES--1/BRIBES--1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/14/us/BRIBES--1/BRIBES--1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lead Plays Himself in Drama on Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lead Plays Himself in Drama on Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':