death toll for the January 2010 earthquake to 316,000, a substantial increase from the more than 250,000 deaths previously reported.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The government has raised the death toll for the January 2010 earthquake to 316,000, a substantial increase from the more than 250,000 deaths previously reported. Officials did not explain the change and did not respond to inquiries about it on Thursday. But Prime Minister Jean-Max Bellerive, at a news conference on Wednesday marking the first anniversary of the disaster, suggested it had increased at least in part because additional bodies had been pulled from the rubble. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti: Quake’s Toll Rises to 316,000', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti: Quake’s Toll Rises to 316,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3042e67-01ef-56d5-ba53-e89b94196b29', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3042e67-01ef-56d5-ba53-e89b94196b29'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Justice, already hamstrung by the difficulty of getting key nominees through the Senate confirmation process, is about to have another vacancy in a crucial position.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/us/politics/14brfs-ANOTHERJUSTI_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Justice, already hamstrung by the difficulty of getting key nominees through the Senate confirmation process, is about to have another vacancy in a crucial position.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Justice, already hamstrung by the difficulty of getting key nominees through the Senate confirmation process, is about to have another vacancy in a crucial position. David S. Kris, the assistant attorney general for the department’s national security division, announced Thursday that he is resigning, effective March 4. The division, which was created after the attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, coordinates federal law enforcement work involving matters like terrorism and espionage. Mr. Kris is taking a position with Intellectual Ventures, a Bellevue, Wash., firm that invests in inventions and patents, a department official said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Justice Department Vacancy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Justice Department Vacancy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4a38ada-88c0-5d20-aef8-9bb778044178', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4a38ada-88c0-5d20-aef8-9bb778044178'}, {'abstract': 'The National Aeronautics and Space Administration cannot develop a heavy-lift rocket by the end of 2016 within the budget provided, the space agency told Congress this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/science/space/14brfs-HEAVYLIFTROC_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The National Aeronautics and Space Administration cannot develop a heavy-lift rocket by the end of 2016 within the budget provided, the space agency told Congress this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Aeronautics and Space Administration cannot develop a heavy-lift rocket by the end of 2016 within the budget provided, the space agency told Congress this week. The blueprint specifying NASA’s mission for the next three years, which was signed into law by President Obama, called for the development of a rocket that was capable of lifting at least 70 tons into orbit and that was based on technologies from the space shuttle and the smaller, soon-to-be-canceled Ares I rocket. In response, leaders of the Senate Committee on Commerce, Science and Transportation, which oversees NASA, reiterated that they expected NASA to find a way to fit a rocket design into the specified schedule and budget. In a letter sent to NASA on Thursday, two committee members, Bill Nelson, Democrat of Florida, and Kay Bailey Hutchison, Republican of Texas, wrote that the NASA blueprint “is not an optional, advisory document: it is the law.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heavy-Lift Rocket Behind Schedule', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heavy-Lift Rocket Behind Schedule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rockets and Rocket Propulsion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce95d2af-f807-53ba-b62b-cbf0e74efeaf', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce95d2af-f807-53ba-b62b-cbf0e74efeaf'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Kay Bailey Hutchison, Republican of Texas, said Thursday that she would not seek re-election next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/us/politics/14brfs-HUTCHISONWON_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Kay Bailey Hutchison, Republican of Texas, said Thursday that she would not seek re-election next year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Senator Kay Bailey Hutchison, Republican of Texas, said Thursday that she would not seek re-election next year, a move that had been expected after her failed bid for the Republican nomination for governor last year. When her term expires, she will have served for 19 years in the Senate. Her decision gives hope to Democrats and the White House, which believes that the growth in the state’s Hispanic population is inexorably making the state more open to electing Democrats. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hutchison Won’t Seek Another Term', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hutchison Won’t Seek Another Term', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutchison, Kay Bailey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/53461ed8-842c-51c1-b6ea-e887b28d1e79', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53461ed8-842c-51c1-b6ea-e887b28d1e79'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print, January 14, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/pageoneplus/corrections.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print, January 14, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa5cd4a6-d5f8-5af9-8549-59a48d8d456f', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa5cd4a6-d5f8-5af9-8549-59a48d8d456f'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said that the United States had seen signs of a “disconnect” between China’s civilian and military leadership in episodes over the last several years', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/world/asia/14briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said that the United States had seen signs of a “disconnect” between China’s civilian and military leadership in episodes over the last several years', 'lead_paragraph': ' Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said Friday in Tokyo that the United States had seen signs of a “disconnect” between China’s civilian and military leadership in episodes over the last several years, including when President Hu Jintao appeared to be unaware this week of the test flight of a new Chinese stealth fighter. Mr. Gates said the gap was “a worry,” but held out the possibility that some incidents might have been the result of bureaucratic mistakes. Over all, he said he remained confident that Mr. Hu, who is to meet with President Obama in Washington next week, is in control of the military. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Gates Sees Disconnect Between Military Leaders', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Gates on Military Leaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T03:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8fd0461-b19c-54c5-8025-bc9a9a836e3c', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8fd0461-b19c-54c5-8025-bc9a9a836e3c'}, {'abstract': 'Amar’e Stoudemire leapfrogged Boston’s Kevin Garnett in the latest All-Star balloting returns, putting him in line to become the first Knick since Patrick Ewing in 1992 to start the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/sports/basketball/14nba.html', 'snippet': 'Amar’e Stoudemire leapfrogged Boston’s Kevin Garnett in the latest All-Star balloting returns, putting him in line to become the first Knick since Patrick Ewing in 1992 to start the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By Amar’e Stoudemire’s lofty standards, he had a below-average trip, and the bandages wrapped around his aching shoulder after Wednesday’s loss in Utah did not add much comfort. He did, however, find an encouraging development when he returned to New York on Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stoudemire on Pace to Become an All-Star', 'kicker': 'N.B.A. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stoudemire On Pace To Become An All-Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Timberwolves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Wizards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sacramento Kings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoudemire, Amare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T04:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams',