 to Saturday, and with it, plenty of opportunities to party. The overly saturated schedule of parallel events, including temporary showrooms, cocktail receptions and pop-up gourmet canteens, ensures that the fashion week fanfare goes further than the catwalk. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Party During Berlin Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T11:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emilie Trice', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emilie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trice', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b22fcae3-c5a5-5f2f-8a24-69606822aa24', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b22fcae3-c5a5-5f2f-8a24-69606822aa24'}, {'abstract': 'Unfortunately, no single measure tells us how well a charitable organization spends the money it raises or how it compares to other charities, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/how-efficient-is-private-charity/', 'snippet': 'Unfortunately, no single measure tells us how well a charitable organization spends the money it raises or how it compares to other charities, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Efficient Is Private Charity?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T11:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca158af8-e428-5fb7-a468-8dff2c6a2acf', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca158af8-e428-5fb7-a468-8dff2c6a2acf'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets’  28-14 win over the Patriots on Sept. 19 has rarely been given more than a passing notice in the last few weeks. But it changed the team’s fortunes.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/forgotten-game-jets-victory-over-patriots-in-september/', 'snippet': 'The Jets’  28-14 win over the Patriots on Sept. 19 has rarely been given more than a passing notice in the last few weeks. But it changed the team’s fortunes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jets’ ability to overcome adversity has been a central theme this season. Recovering from their 45-3 loss to the Patriots and going on to beat the Steelers in Pittsburgh two weeks later is one example. Tuning out issues related to off-the-field shenanigans – some self-inflicted – has been another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forgotten Game: Jets’ Victory Over Patriots in September', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T11:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e49816-f06d-53ea-ad7c-64085bfe2393', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e49816-f06d-53ea-ad7c-64085bfe2393'}, {'abstract': 'The agency charged with overseeing the government bailout of Citigroup said the bailout was accepted “against the advice of Citigroup insiders who considered the government’s terms too expensive.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/citis-bailout-ad-hoc-rescue-for-an-unwilling-bank/', 'snippet': 'The agency charged with overseeing the government bailout of Citigroup said the bailout was accepted “against the advice of Citigroup insiders who considered the government’s terms too expensive.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The agency charged with overseeing the government bailout of Citigroup said in a report published Thursday that the Bush administration’s decision to save the financial behemoth was “strikingly ad hoc,” and that its offer was accepted “against the advice of Citigroup insiders who considered the government’s terms too expensive.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citi’s Bailout: Ad Hoc Rescue for an Unwilling Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T11:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9958c186-ce40-54f4-844b-90bb184f6abc', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9958c186-ce40-54f4-844b-90bb184f6abc'}, {'abstract': 'No one ever said it would be easy.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/business-owners-discuss-their-technology-issues/', 'snippet': 'No one ever said it would be easy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I invited you to put in your two cents about the dark side of information technology, along with any praise that came to mind. Thanks much to the many of you who did so. There were a lot of great comments — too many, unfortunately, for me to be able to single them all out or otherwise address them here. Though I’m going to dedicate this post to selectively recapping the comments and seeing what perspective we can wring out of them, it won’t be my last word on the subject. And some of the comments I neglect here will influence future posts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Owners Talk Technology', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T12:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa5e621a-63fc-5964-b2a2-f73f7e8d04d4', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa5e621a-63fc-5964-b2a2-f73f7e8d04d4'}, {'abstract': 'Scent Sciences wants you to wake up and smell the turkey dinner—or any of 20 other smells.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/discovered-while-nosing-around-c-e-s/', 'snippet': 'Scent Sciences wants you to wake up and smell the turkey dinner—or any of 20 other smells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m a big fan of Yankee Candle–my favorites include Christmas Cupcake and Fluffy Towels—but ScentScape might be a smell too far for me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Discovered While Nosing Around CES….', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T12:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/db5b9525-c77a-5ec7-a1d6-0ae01b1025bd', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db5b9525-c77a-5ec7-a1d6-0ae01b1025bd'}, {'abstract': 'The 48 percent increase in the bank’s annual earnings provides signs that consumers and businesses are slowly regaining their balance in the aftermath of the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/jpmorgans-fourth-quarter-profits-rise-47-to-4-8-billion/', 'snippet': 'The 48 percent increase in the bank’s annual earnings provides signs that consumers and businesses are slowly regaining their balance in the aftermath of the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:19 p.m. | Up