'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T16:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7d0a650-4ee0-542d-8f68-bda5c6c28e2b', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7d0a650-4ee0-542d-8f68-bda5c6c28e2b'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever position one takes in these perennial quarrels, this much would seem inarguable: The few ounces of protection from ballistic eye wear are a wise investment for soldiers.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/vantage-point-protecting-ones-eyes-in-explosions/', 'snippet': 'Whatever position one takes in these perennial quarrels, this much would seem inarguable: The few ounces of protection from ballistic eye wear are a wise investment for soldiers.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Late in the afternoon on May 27, 2010, a Marine and Afghan foot patrol working in the scrub and dunes along the Helmand River in Afghanistan unknowingly walked up to a hidden bomb. The description of what happened next will be familiar to anyone who has closely followed the war, or walked Afghanistan’s rural provinces with Western troops for any length of time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vantage Point: Protecting the Eyes That Face Explosions', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyeglasses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine C