iebus of Wisconsin survived seven rounds of balloting to succeed Michael Steele as party officials demanded new leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OXON HILL, Md. \x97 The Republican National Committee selected a new leader on Friday, with its choice, Reince Priebus of Wisconsin, surviving seven contentious rounds of balloting to overtake Michael Steele, the embattled chairman, as party officials demanded new leadership to fortify the party for the 2012 presidential race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/us/15repubs2/15repubs2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/us/15repubs2/15repubs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/15/us/15repubs2/15repubs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Elects a New Chairman as Steele Drops Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Elects a New Chairman As Steele Drops Out of the Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steele, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T18:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zelen