yt://article/24239d44-104f-53c4-80ab-72f6818d8b54', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24239d44-104f-53c4-80ab-72f6818d8b54'}, {'abstract': 'Island Creek Oyster Bar is an extension of the Island Creek Oysters farm in nearby Duxbury, Mass. So it’s no surprise that oysters take pride of place on a long and varied menu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/travel/16bites-oyster.html', 'snippet': 'Island Creek Oyster Bar is an extension of the Island Creek Oysters farm in nearby Duxbury, Mass. So it’s no surprise that oysters take pride of place on a long and varied menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Island Creek Oyster Bar brings a special twist to the trend of farm-to-table restaurants: the small farms carefully listed next to each dish on Oyster Creek’s menu specialize in aquaculture, the raising of seafood and shellfish. But that’s not all: the restaurant itself is an extension of Island Creek Oysters, a farm founded in 1992 in nearby Duxbury, Mass. So it’s no surprise that though the menu is long and varied, at Island Creek, which opened in October, oysters take pride of place.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/travel/16bites/16BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/travel/16bites/16bites-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/travel/16bites/16bites-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Island Creek Oyster Bar, in Boston', 'kicker': 'Bites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Island Creek Oyster Bar: Boston', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's