f State program shows United States documentaries in foreign countries to teach people about American values and issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/movies/16docs.html', 'snippet': 'A Department of State program shows United States documentaries in foreign countries to teach people about American values and issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIM A. SNYDER’S “Welcome to Shelbyville” is a melting-pot movie, asimmer with social issues: immigration, racism, unemployment, intolerance. Its examination of the clash between Somali Muslims and rural Tennesseeans does not sugarcoat the kinds of conflicts that have bedeviled the country for centuries; it questions, in its way, what America means. And it’s been shown around the world by the United States State Department.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/DOCS-2/DOCS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/DOCS-2/DOCS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/DOCS-2/DOCS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/DOCS-2/DOCS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/arts/DOCS-2/DOCS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Conducting Documentary Diplomacy', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conducting Documentary Diplomacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 