: [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc5fff8-40ec-55bd-ae7c-f667e365237e', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc5fff8-40ec-55bd-ae7c-f667e365237e'}, {'abstract': 'Slide Show: Subjects include Coptic Christmas in Brooklyn, more snow, what remains of the Deutsche Bank building downtown and more.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/the-week-in-pictures-for-jan-14/', 'snippet': 'Slide Show: Subjects include Coptic Christmas in Brooklyn, more snow, what remains of the Deutsche Bank building downtown and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include Coptic Christmas in Brooklyn, more snow, what remains of the Deutsche Bank building downtown and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for Jan. 14', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T22:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a224e20-4cc0-59f6-8bf2-54df6db9b886', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a224e20-4cc0-59f6-8bf2-54df6db9b886'}, {'abstract': 'The former restaurant critic for The New York Times presents some of the restaurants he considers New York’s best of all time.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/new-yorks-all-time-best-an-alternate-take/', 'snippet': 'The former restaurant critic for The New York Times presents some of the restaurants he considers New York’s best of all time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be easy enough to start a fight by proposing the 10 best New York restaurants of the past decade. Robert Sietsema is just begging for a brawl by daring to name the 10 best of the past two centuries. Point number one (the obvious): we have no idea what the food tasted like at Delmonico’s in 1858, or even what the raw ingredients tasted like, for that matter. Try naming the 10 greatest tenors before the era of recorded sound. We know who the most famous ones were, and we have written descriptions of something that cannot, in the final analysis, be put into words. But that’s it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s All-Time Best Restaurants: An Alternate Take', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T22:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec9ce386-da45-5f1c-8427-dfd5173c6bd2', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec9ce386-da45-5f1c-8427-dfd5173c6bd2'}, {'abstract': 'Intuit, the maker of TurboTax software, has an application called SnapTax that allows taxpayers to file federal taxes by iPhone or Android using the 1040EZ form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/technology/personaltech/15phone.html', 'snippet': 'Intuit, the maker of TurboTax software, has an application called SnapTax that allows taxpayers to file federal taxes by iPhone or Android using the 1040EZ form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO \x97 Few chores are as unpleasant as doing taxes. But filers can avoid some of the drudgery by turning it over to their mobile phones.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/technology/15phone-web/15phone-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/technology/15phone-web/15phone-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/15/technology/15phone-web/15phone-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Task for Phone: File Taxes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Task For Phone: File Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intuit Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T22:48:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verne G. Kopytoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fda3a16-2843-5d3f-b135-b5c7dc78141e', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fda3a16-2843-5d3f-b135-b5c7dc78141e'}, {'abstract': 'The problem with dropped calls on the iPhone may no longer be blamed on the network now that Apple has signed a deal with Verizon Wireless.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/business/15nocera.html', 'snippet': 'The problem with dropped calls on the iPhone may no longer be blamed on the network now that Apple has signed a deal with Verizon Wireless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With this week’s announcement that Verizon Wireless is going to begin selling the iPhone \x97 something its customers have been panting for ever since AT&T got that first, exclusive iPhone contract four years ago \x97 it’s time for me to face the music. Nobody really cares that the iPhone is flawed. After this column, I’m going to stop caring too. I swear it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/10/16/business/nocera-75/nocera-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/10/16/business/nocera-75/nocera-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Deal May Expose iPhone Flaws', 'kicker': 'Talking Business', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Verizon Deal May Expose IPhone Flaws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T22:53:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/552e97b3-f8fa-58da-9153-a68777324aed', 'word_count': 1652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/552e97b3-f8fa-58da-9153-a68777324aed'}, {'abstract': 'In the face of the crisis, locals here have banded together in cooperation, in an effort to rebuild from one of Australia’s worst natural disasters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/world/asia/15australia.html', 'snippet': 'In the face of the crisis, locals here have banded together in cooperation, in an effort to rebuild from one of Australia’s worst natural disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRANTHAM, Australia \x97 For Allan Marshall, this tiny Australian town has always been a tightly knit place, never more so than in days since a surging, flotsam-filled torrent hit the town, smashing apart homes and sweeping neighbors to their deaths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/world/15australia1_span/16australia1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/world/15australia1_span/16australia1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/world/15australia1_span/16australia1_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu