esolutions are still ringing in one’s ears, is a good time to visit Miraj Healthy Grill in Williston Park. As the name suggests, this nine-month-old spot serves the kind of food we are supposed to be eating. It features Persian and Mediterranean cuisines, which translate to grilled meats, big salads and vegetable-laden appetizers.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16dineli2/16dineli2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16dineli2/16dineli2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Food Leans Toward the Healthful', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Williston Park', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Food Leans Toward the Healthful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-14T23:29:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8a66aad-a746-55d6-bb40-e432f7a76e38', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8a66aad-a746-55d6-bb40-e432f7a76e38'}, {'abstract': 'Eggs encased in savory Italian sausage meat, then shallow-fried until crisp and golden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/dining/19appe.html', 'snippet': 'Egg