ew York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16MAX1/16MAX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16MAX1/16MAX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16MAX1/16MAX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16MAX1/16MAX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Max Fish Magic: Will It Travel Well?', 'kicker': 'New York Story', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Max Fish Magic: Will It Travel Well?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MAX FISH', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T01:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0261f3c-8bee-5a33-a263-6eca73a2158e', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0261f3c-8bee-5a33-a263-6eca73a2158e'}, {'abstract': 'While serving as city director of public health and safety for $10,000 a year, Bobby Valentine will continue working as a baseball analyst for ESPN.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/nyregion/15valentine.html', 'snippet': 'While serving as city director of public health and safety for $10,000 a year, Bobby Valentine will continue working as a baseball analyst for ESPN.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While it is hardly unusual for someone to enter public service from the sports world (think Bill Bradley) or from show business (Ronald Reagan, Arnold Schwarzenegger, Al Franken et al.), it is uncommon for celebrities to hold office and work at another job at the same time. Clint Eastwood is that rare example of an actual moonlighting politician, having gotten himself elected mayor of Carmel-by-the-Sea, Calif., in 1986 even as “Heartbreak Ridge,” his shoot-’em-up about the invasion of Grenada, was in theaters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/nyregion/VALENTINE/VALENTINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/nyregion/VALENTINE/VALENTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/15/nyregion/VALENTINE/VALENTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skills Honed in Mets Dugout to Be Used in a City Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Skills Honed in Mets Dugout to Be Used in a City Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stamford (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valentine, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d