Goodheart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodheart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffd37d8f-6c9a-54c9-8999-34bf192b5dd9', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffd37d8f-6c9a-54c9-8999-34bf192b5dd9'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s thirst is quenched by a network of water tunnels whose origins span three centuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/nyregion/16tunnel.html', 'snippet': 'The city’s thirst is quenched by a network of water tunnels whose origins span three centuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT took seven years for workers to build the 8,558-foot Holland Tunnel in the 1920s. Bernard Daly and a team of 150 have spent the last four years digging three tunnels that together span 8,881 feet in the northern Bronx. And while the Holland Tunnel was built for cars, Mr. Daly’s tunnels are for something more basic: water.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16TUNNEL2/16TUNNEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16TUNNEL2/16TUNNEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Water Tunnels, Age Is Just a Number', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Water Tunnels, Age Is Just a Number', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T02:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'sectio