0-13b6-58ef-8d7f-f2a8f13af2cf', 'word_count': 3530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fefed70-13b6-58ef-8d7f-f2a8f13af2cf'}, {'abstract': '“After the Fall,” at the Hudson Valley Center for Contemporary Art in Peekskill, features 18 artists from six countries in Eastern and Central Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/nyregion/16artwe.html', 'snippet': '“After the Fall,” at the Hudson Valley Center for Contemporary Art in Peekskill, features 18 artists from six countries in Eastern and Central Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art can be very good at illuminating history, showing how shifting geographies, ideologies and violent upheavals have real but often hidden effects on individuals. That, in a sense, is what the exhibition “After the Fall,” at the Hudson Valley Center for Contemporary Art in Peekskill, sets out to do. The show features 18 artists from six countries in Eastern and Central Europe, most of whom were born under Communist rule but came of age “after the fall.” It’s a great premise, but in the end a very academic show. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16ART2WE/16ART2WE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/16ART2WE/16ART2WE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '18 Journeys Forged in Communism', 'kicker': 'Art  Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '18 Journeys Forged In Communism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hudson Valley Center for Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'