York, Repeating His Call for Action', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Crisscrosses New York, Repeating His Call for Action', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T02:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7daf8aeb-4866-5d3a-bce1-a98c3200d452', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7daf8aeb-4866-5d3a-bce1-a98c3200d452'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of action from the Asian Cup tournament in Qatar.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/asian-cup-australia-and-south-korea-in-a-stalemate/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of action from the Asian Cup tournament in Qatar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — South Korea’s young team (average age 24) got the better of Australia’s older and more experienced Socceroos (average age nearly 30) for much of Friday’s Group C first-round match of the Asian Cup. But a goal by Mile Jedinak in the 62nd minute canceled out Koo Ja Cheol’s goal in the first half of the 1-1 tie. The teams are tied on points at the top of the group with one match to play. Australia faces Bahrain, which defeated India, 5-2, while the South Koreans have an easier route with a game against winless India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Cup: Australia and South Korea in a Stalemate', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahill, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T02:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Behrooz Afrakhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Behrooz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afrakhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7db2559-a72f-53e9-a857-524c77e85b7b', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7db2559-a72f-53e9-a857-524c77e85b7b'}, {'abstract': 'Silky on the outside, crunchy in the middle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/14/middle-2/', 'snippet': 'Silky on the outside, crunchy in the middle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — I don’t know about you, but this was a clockwise solve for me. I started in the northwest, barreled right around the outside of the puzzle, finished up in the southwest. Then I got completely stumped in the middle. WUPATKI, Barry? Really?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: Stuck in the Middle With You', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T03:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0d39d54-8fea-5e99-845a-cc06e90267f5', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0d39d54-8fea-5e99-845a-cc06e90267f5'}, {'abstract': 'Sexual assault accusations against Steelers quarterback Ben Roethlisberger have caused some fans to have a difficult time rooting for him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/sports/football/15steelers.html', 'snippet': 'Sexual assault accusations against Steelers quarterback Ben Roethlisberger have caused some fans to have a difficult time rooting for him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH \x97 Between sales of goat Cheddar, David Sunseri gave his seal of approval to another big cheese this week. Sunseri, an owner of the Pennsylvania Macaroni Company, which is as much a local institution as the Steelers, named quarterback Ben Roethlisberger as his favorite player. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/sports/15steelers_395/15steelers_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/sports/15steelers_395/15steelers_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/15/sports/15steelers_395/15steelers_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pittsburgh, a Quarterback Split', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NFL PLAYOFFS | DIVIS