ting, an appellate court in Manhattan ruled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court has ruled that Joe Berlinger, a filmmaker who was ordered to hand over footage from his 2009 documentary “Crude” to the Chevron Corporation, cannot invoke a journalist’s privilege in refusing to do so because his work does not constitute an act of independent reporting.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentary Filmmaker Doesn’t Qualify for a Journalist’s Privilege, a Court Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documentary Filmmaker Doesn’t Qualify for a Journalist’s Privilege, a Court Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlinger, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T03:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c904c7-cb06-58ba-ba8e-28998cda22fe', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c904c7-cb06-58ba-ba8e-28998cda22fe'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Serwer, left, of The American Prospect and Michael C. Moynihan of Reason debate Glenn Beck and responsibility for political acts of violence.\n', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/1248069565504/bloggingheads-