felt called to ministry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Almost Ambassador Encounters a Congressional Dead End', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Almost Ambassador Encounters a Congressional Dead End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Faith-Based Initiatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Suzan Johnson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T03:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e11635-eaf3-5067-b9d4-739cb09ddc88', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e11635-eaf3-5067-b9d4-739cb09ddc88'}, {'abstract': 'Two men said to be members of the 18th Street gang were charged Thursday with trying to extort taco truck owners in South Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/us/15brfs-CHARGESINTAC_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Two men said to be members of the 18th Street gang were charged Thursday with trying to extort taco truck owners in South Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two men said to be members of the 18th Street gang were charged Thursday with trying to extort taco truck owners in South Los Angeles. The police say that the practice of charging “rent” to owners of the growing fleet of the trucks so they can do business has become widespread, and that the 18th Street gang, one of the largest in Los Angeles, has singled out small Hispanic businesses. “The extortions fixate on the Hispanic community because people fear being deported or having to testify, so they don’t want to report anything,” Sgt. Alma Burke of the police said. Erin Glenn, executive director of a union that represents truck owners, said extortion had been a problem for years, but she had started to hear more complaints recently. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Charges in Taco Truck Extortion', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Charges in Taco Truck Extortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extortion and Blackmail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vendors, Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T03:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef5330a-a6fa-5051-bf80-c06b7ed431aa', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef5330a-a6fa-5051-bf80-c06b7ed431aa'}, {'abstract': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. said Friday that his new chief of staff would be Bruce Reed, who worked for former President Bill Clinton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/us/politics/15brfs-BIDENCHOOSES_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. said Friday that his new chief of staff would be Bruce Reed, who worked for former President Bill Clinton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. said Friday that his new chief of staff would be Bruce Reed, who worked for former President Bill Clinton, first as his assistant for domestic policy planning, then as deputy domestic policy adviser and finally as chief domestic policy adviser. Mr. Reed, who has led the moderate Democratic Leadership Council, will succeed Ron Klain, who will run Case Holdings, the parent company of the investment company of the former AOL chief Steve Case. Most recently, he was executive director of the National Commission on Fiscal Responsibility and Reform. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Chooses a Chief of Staff', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biden Chooses a Chief of Staff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Bruce N', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T03:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7424fd6e-d2f7-5b82-baeb-861aa0a77be7', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7424fd6e-d2f7-5b82-baeb-861aa0a77be7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s time to start reviewing the latest books from the Republican presidential hopefuls. First up is the new one from Tim Pawlenty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/opinion/15collins.html', 'snippet': 'It’s time to start reviewing the latest books from the Republican presidential hopefuls. First up is the new one from Tim Pawlenty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the time when presidential candidates start poking their little noses up through the snow, and making soft, trilling noises. I know you think it’s too soon, even though Mitt Romney made his intentions clear on the family Christmas card. But as a public service, I am going to start providing summaries of the latest books from the potential Republican nominees so we’ll all be well educated by the time the debates begin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'hei