l District Court in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Embassy Bombing Suspect Was Told of Plot, Filing Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Terror Suspect in 1998 Bombings Was Told of Plot a Week in Advance, a Filing Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dar es Salaam (Tanzania)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Lewis A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghailani, Ahmed Khalfan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T04:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a50e6a0b-deb6-5a87-97c7-e27136beee89', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a50e6a0b-deb6-5a87-97c7-e27136beee89'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of a chain of jewelry stores lost about $50 million worth of paintings, diamonds and antiques in one of the more brazen recent thefts at country homes of the wealthy outside of Moscow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/world/europe/15briefs-Russia.html', 'snippet': 'The owner of a chain of jewelry stores lost about $50 million worth of paintings, diamonds and antiques in one of the more brazen recent thefts at country homes of the wealthy outside of Moscow.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The owner of a chain of jewelry stores lost about $50 million worth of paintings, diamonds and antiques in one of the more brazen recent thefts at country homes of the wealthy outside of Moscow. The burglars tied up security guards, retrieved keys from a caretaker’s house and made off with paintings by the 19th-century Russian masters Ilya Repin, Ivan Shishkin and Ivan Aivazovsky, Russian television news reported. Their owner, Aleksandr Tarantsev, said the paintings were insured. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: $50 Million Art and Gem Theft', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: $50 Million Art and Gem Theft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T04:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/66944baf-5099-547b-96bc-7c7d758e54b2', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66944baf-5099-547b-96bc-7c7d758e54b2'}, {'abstract': 'A truck driver sentenced to life in prison for evading $550,000 in road tolls will be offered another trial, a court ruled Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/world/asia/15briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'A truck driver sentenced to life in prison for evading $550,000 in road tolls will be offered another trial, a court ruled Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A truck driver sentenced to life in prison for evading $550,000 in road tolls will be offered another trial, a court ruled Friday. The Pingdingshan Intermediate Court in Henan Province said it would retry the man, Shi Jianfeng, citing what it described as new evidence of an accomplice who helped him defraud toll collectors over an eight-month period. In a posting on its Web site on Friday, the court said intense media attention to the case persuaded it to question the defendant again, revealing that he had not acted alone. Mr. Shi, a farmer who had turned to hauling construction material, evaded the tolls on his two trucks during more than 2,300 trips. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Toll Evader to Get New Trial', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Toll Evader to Get New Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T04:40:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/57fcb3e3-5dc2-5828-808a-c431002dbd6d', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57fcb3e3-5dc2-5828-808a-c431002dbd6d'}, {'abstract': 'Police officers have detained 96 people on suspicion of illegally using tainted milk powder that should have been destroyed after a food scandal that angered and frightened parents across China in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/world/asia/15briefs-Milk.html', 'snippet': 'Police officers have detained 96 people on suspicion of illegally using tainted milk powder that should have been destroyed after a food scandal that angered and frightened parents across China in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Police officers have detained 96 people on suspicion of illegally using tainted milk powder that should have been destroyed after a food scandal that angered and frightened parents across China in 2008, state news organizations reported Friday. That year at least 22 dairy companies were found to have sold products tainted with melamine, an industrial chemical that can be toxic to infants; at least six babies died of kidney problems and 300,000 children fell ill. Among the 96 people detained, 17 have been convicted on criminal charges and 2 have been sentenced to life in prison. Thirty-eight others are awaiting trial and 41 are being investigated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Inquiry on Tainted Milk Powder', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Inquiry on Tainted Milk Powder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Melamine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T04:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8deb079-193b-53d5-ae1e-8a285854d0e0', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8deb079-