 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de0731b0-e0e3-5c10-a33a-139f98352401', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de0731b0-e0e3-5c10-a33a-139f98352401'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Bebeshko, a former refugee, overcame the challenges of immigrant life to graduate from Fordham University. He now wants to work with the Russian-speaking Jewish community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/nyregion/16neediest.html', 'snippet': 'Alex Bebeshko, a former refugee, overcame the challenges of immigrant life to graduate from Fordham University. He now wants to work with the Russian-speaking Jewish community.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Alex Bebeshko’s early life was not easy. He said his mother was a drug addict, and other addicts would come to their apartment in Odessa, Ukraine, to buy a hit of “rastvor,” an opium derivative, and shoot it up, sometimes in front of him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/BULL-NEEDIEST/BULL-NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/BULL-NEEDIEST/BULL-NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/nyregion/BULL-NEEDIEST/BULL-NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Ukrainian Immigrant Reconnects With His Roots', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Ukrainian Immigrant Reconnects With His Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UJA-Federation of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T17:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ewa Kern-Jedrychowska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ewa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kern-Jedrychowska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8257818b-2389-5108-a622-a2cd2cd93d06', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8257818b-2389-5108-a622-a2cd2cd93d06'}, {'abstract': 'Abyei is worrisome because so many of the ingredients of the wider north-south war — the oil, the proxy forces, the historic rivalries — are distilled there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/world/africa/16sudan.html', 'snippet': 'Abyei is worrisome because so many of the ingredients of the wider north-south war — the oil, the proxy forces, the historic rivalries — are distilled there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABYEI, Sudan — There is a place in Sudan where Africa and the Arab world meet, where one thatched roof hut carries a roughly-hewn cross at the top and next door an identical hut flaunts a crescent moon, where heavily armed nomads sweep in for raids and heavily armed villagers fight back.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/world/16sudan2/16sudan2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/world/16sudan2/16sudan2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/world/16sudan2/16sudan2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/world/16sudan2/16sudan2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/world/16sudan2/16sudan2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roots of Bitterness in a Region Threaten Sudan’s Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roots of Bitterness in a Disputed Land Threaten Sudan’s Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T17:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6619107-231b-5330-a610-7ee325c29761', 'word_count': 1317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6619107-231b-5330-a610-7ee325c29761'}, {'abstract': 'In the past, the nation has been jolted into civility. But it’s unclear whether this will happen after the killings in Tucson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/weekinreview/16bai.html', 'snippet': 'In the past, the nation has been jolted into civility. But it’s unclear whether this will happen after the killings in Tucson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For anyone who hoped that the tragedy in Tucson might jolt the political class into some new period of civility and reflection, suddenly subduing all the radio ranters and acid bloggers, the days that followed brought a cold reality.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/weekinreview/JPBAI1/JPBAI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Tucson, Is the Anger Gone?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is the Anger Gone?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T17:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9a2197b-146d-5c7a-be5c-5953c152418d', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9a2197b-146d-5c7a-be5c-5953c152418d'}, {'abstract': 'While Mark Sanchez shares with Tom Brady rugged good looks and heartthrob status, he does not yet match Brady in on-the-field success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/sports/football/16quarterbacks.html', 'snippet': 'While Mark Sanchez shares with Tom Brady rugged good looks and heartthrob status, he does not yet match Brady in on-the-field success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Nic Screws, the fashion market editor at Esquire magazine, analyzed Tom Brady and Mark Sanchez, she saw more than two quarterbacks who will meet Sunday in the N.F.L. playoffs. From two men as at ease in suits as in shoulder pads, she saw comfort urban style (Brady) compared with fancy sunglasses and shiny ties (Sanchez), along with good hair (both).', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/quarterbacks1/quarterbacks1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/quarterbacks1/quarterbacks1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/quarterbacks1/quarterbacks1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Sanchez and Tom Brady: Peers in Style, Not in Results', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Master and the Apprentice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T17:39:40+0000', 'docume