/f5edc447-feb8-5559-b7c8-8ff4c37b39e3'}, {'abstract': 'Michel Balthazard, a top official of the electric car program, and Bertrand Rochette were both dismissed. The company remains vague about accusing a foreign power of involvement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16renault.html', 'snippet': 'Michel Balthazard, a top official of the electric car program, and Bertrand Rochette were both dismissed. The company remains vague about accusing a foreign power of involvement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS \x97 Renault has formally fired two of the men it has accused of espionage, their lawyers said Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renault Fires 2 Men Accused of Selling Corporate Secrets About Electric Vehicles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Renault Fires 2 Men Accused of Selling Corporate Secrets About Electric Vehicles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Industrial Espionage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renault SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:34:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/435b3b49-a99c-55cf-850c-f8eb4302ae64', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/435b3b49-a99c-55cf-850c-f8eb4302ae64'}, {'abstract': 'We’re not as gray as expected.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/early-social-security-projections/', 'snippet': 'We’re not as gray as expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This post by Bruce Webb sent me looking briefly at some early Social Security Trustees’ reports, to firm up my answer to something that has been bugging me for years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Social Security Projections', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/361b7d54-34e3-5047-9774-7d6b81f5cb41', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361b7d54-34e3-5047-9774-7d6b81f5cb41'}, {'abstract': '“I love the electricity, but there’s a lot of tension that week, too,” says Scott Lipps of One Management, on his experiences with Fashion Week. “No amount of schooling can ever prepare you for this.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/jobs/16boss.html', 'snippet': '“I love the electricity, but there’s a lot of tension that week, too,” says Scott Lipps of One Management, on his experiences with Fashion Week. “No amount of schooling can ever prepare you for this.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS born in my parents’ car on their way from their home in Long Island to the hospital. They were passing through a town called Gibson at the time, so they chose that as my middle name. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/BOSS/BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 971, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Road to the Runway', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Road to the Runway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Lipps', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a108ce8f-fb70-5297-83dc-f24862aea4bb', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a108ce8f-fb70-5297-83dc-f24862aea4bb'}, {'abstract': 'The trust of Helen Cohen, who lost $700,000 on a real estate investment, was already in arbitration with its former broker when the company opened a court case as well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16gret.html', 'snippet': 'The trust of Helen Cohen, who lost $700,000 on a real estate investment, was already in arbitration with its former broker when the company opened a court case as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN investors file complaints against their brokers, the matters are almost always heard by an arbitration panel rather than by a judge or jury. Arbitration forums like those run by the Financial Industry Regulatory Authority typically adjudicate cases more quickly than the courts and less expensively, because costs associated with discovery and extensive legal filings are minimized if not eliminated.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arbitration, Litigation, Aggravation', 'kicker': 'Fair Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arbitration, Litigation, Aggravation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:42:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eab9a36-8573-5893-8f21-153f86ecbe75', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eab9a36-8573-5893-8f21-153f86ecbe75'}, {'abstract': 'Smaller American architectural firms are receiving more commissions from China, and finding that Chinese clients are, in some ways, easier to work for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16build.html', 'snippet': 'Smaller American architectural firms are receiving more commissions from China, and finding that Chinese clients are, in some ways, easier to work for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was an unusual commission, unlike anything that Stuart Silk, a Seattle architect, had been offered in his quarter-century of practice: design three high-end custom homes for clients he would never meet. Although there were some specifications for functions and dimensions \x97 total square feet, for example, and the number of bedrooms and baths \x97 there wasn’t a clue as to style or a construction budget.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/BUILD/BUILD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/business/BUILD/BUILD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 6