://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16corner.html', 'snippet': 'Robin Domeniconi of the Elle Group encourages her team to remember the art of “M.R.I.,” or the “most respectful interpretation” of what someone is saying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This interview with Robin Domeniconi, senior vice president and chief brand officer for the Elle Group,  was conducted and condensed by Adam Bryant.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/CORNER/CORNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/CORNER/CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/business/CORNER/CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Say Anything, but Phrase It the Right Way', 'kicker': 'Corner Office', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Say Anything,\nBut Phrase It\nThe Right Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Bryant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/27ed6d3a-b758-538b-a79b-5610afb4251c', 'word_count': 1902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27ed6d3a-b758-538b-a79b-5610afb4251c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s easy to use a smartphone’s camera as a hand-held copier. But some people say it may bear some resemblance to unauthorized file sharing of music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16ping.html', 'snippet': 'It’s easy to use a smartphone’s camera as a hand-held copier. But some people say it may bear some resemblance to unauthorized file sharing of music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY wife and I sat cross-legged on the floor of a local Barnes & Noble store recently, surrounded by several large piles of books. We were searching for interior design ideas for a new home that we are planning to buy.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/16ping-span/16ping-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/business/16ping-span/16ping-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/16ping-span/16ping-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Your Camera Phone Turn You Into a Pirate?', 'kicker': 'Ping', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Your Camera Phone Turn You Into a Pirate?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d9a891-f82e-5dd1-867a-818e6b11621c', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d9a891-f82e-5dd1-867a-818e6b11621c'}, {'abstract': '“Practical Wisdom,” a new book by Barry Schwartz and Kenneth Sharpe, offers ways to enact wise decisions for the greater good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16shelf.html', 'snippet': '“Practical Wisdom,” a new book by Barry Schwartz and Kenneth Sharpe, offers ways to enact wise decisions for the greater good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT is it about businesspeople and self-help books? Is there any other field where so many people read so many books about how to do better, manage better, lead better, sell better, speak better, tan better and turn somersaults better? O.K., I made those last two up, but you see the point. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/SHELF/SHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 634, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Spirit of the Mensch', 'kicker': 'Off the Shelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Spirit Of the Mensch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpe, Kenneth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T19:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burrough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeba8f7c-dbcb-5091-ad87-befddbc7a64a', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeba8f7c-dbcb-5091-ad87-befddbc7a64a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should list concrete proposals — ones he is prepared to fight for — to reduce the long-term deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/business/16view.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama should list concrete proposals — ones he is prepared to fight for — to reduce the long-term deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BY the time President Obama gave his State of the Union address last year, the speech felt like an old friend. It had been part of my life \x97 from the brainstorming sessions in late November 2009 to the last minute fact-checking. I knew when all of my favorite lines were coming. That led to an awkward moment during the address when I sprang to my feet, applauding the president’s tacit endorsement of the free-trade agreement with South Korea, before noticing that the only other person cheering seemed to be Ron Kirk, the special trade representative.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/VIEW/VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 912, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/business/VIEW/VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/business/VIEW/VIEW-thumbStandard.