ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfdcca85-554a-5412-928b-e7b3b18cb44c', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfdcca85-554a-5412-928b-e7b3b18cb44c'}, {'abstract': 'Despite low incomes, health coverage and high school graduation, Hidalgo County residents live two years longer than the United States or Texas averages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/us/16ttexpectancy.html', 'snippet': 'Despite low incomes, health coverage and high school graduation, Hidalgo County residents live two years longer than the United States or Texas averages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDINBURG \x97 Many of the longest lives in Texas are lived in an unlikely place: along the state’s impoverished border with Mexico. Despite conditions that often have the opposite consequences \x97 desperately low incomes, a widespread lack of health insurance and poor rates of high school graduation \x97 the predominantly Hispanic residents of Hidalgo County live on average to be 80, two years longer than the United States or Texas averages. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/us/16ttexpectancy/16TTEXPECTANCY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/us/16ttexpectancy/16ttexpectancy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/us/16ttexpectancy/16ttexpectancy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Border, Long Lives Despite Dismal Statistics', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LIFE EXPECTANCY; On the Border, Long Lives Despite Dismal Statistics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-15T23:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Ramshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cf2a58d-7f28-584a-aac8-daf6e9fcc0a8', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cf2a58d-7f28-584a-aac8-daf6e9fcc0a8'}, {'abstract': 'In March 2010, few of our leaders wanted to see what Giffords saw — that the vandalism and the death threats were part of a tide of insurrectionism that had been rising since the final weeks of the 2008 campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/opinion/16rich.html', 'snippet': 'In March 2010, few of our leaders wanted to see what Giffords saw — that the vandalism and the death threats were part of a tide of insurrectionism that had been rising since the final weeks of the 2008 campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OF the many truths in President Obama’s powerful Tucson speech, none was more indisputable than his statement that no one can know what is in a killer’s mind. So why have we spent so much time debating exactly that?', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 