5a96-a327-4d8ad493081a'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Clippers started the season with one victory in their first 14 games. After a 105-91 loss to Philadelphia on Dec. 15, the Clippers were 5-21 and among the worst teams in the league. The rookie forward Blake Griffin’s ferocious dunks were the lone highlights.  But after that loss, the Clippers began to turn their season around.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/15/clippers-show-some-life/', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Clippers started the season with one victory in their first 14 games. After a 105-91 loss to Philadelphia on Dec. 15, the Clippers were 5-21 and among the worst teams in the league. The rookie forward Blake Griffin’s ferocious dunk...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Clippers started the season with one victory in their first 14 games. After a 105-91 loss to Philadelphia on Dec. 15, the Clippers were 5-21 and among the worst teams in the league. The rookie forward Blake Griffin’s ferocious dunks (usually coming in losses) were the lone highlights for a team that seemed to be going nowhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clippers Show Some Life', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Blake', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T04:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Bierman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bierman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_i