e musical-comedy star whose belting voice and brassy style entertained Broadway and movie audiences for 50 years', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ethel Merman, the musical-comedy star whose belting voice and brassy style entertained Broadway and movie audiences for 50 years, was found dead in her Manhattan apartment yesterday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethel Merman, Queen of Musicals, Dies at 76', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By MURRAY SCHUMACH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Murray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SCHUMACH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ec6650a-247f-5407-a0de-adc5969dfd77', 'word_count': 2210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ec6650a-247f-5407-a0de-adc5969dfd77'}, {'abstract': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">No Ground Fighting Yet; Call to Arms by Hussein</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/big/0116.html', 'snippet': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">No Ground Fighting Yet; Call to Arms by Hussein</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'lead_paragraph': "WASHINGTON, Thursday, Jan. 17 -- The United States and allied forces Wednesday night opened the long threatened war to drive President Saddam Hussein's army from Kuwait, striking Baghdad and other targets in Iraq and Kuwait with waves of bombers and cruise missiles launched from naval vessels.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "U.S. AND ALLIES OPEN AIR WAR ON\nIRAQ; BOMB BAGHDAD AND KUWAITI\nTARGETS; 'NO CHOICE' BUT FORCE,\nBUSH DECLARES ", 'kicker': 'January 17, 1991', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': '<h5> By ANDREW ROSENTHAL </h5>\n<h5>Special to The New York Times </h5>', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bde9ed5d-64d4-572a-a33c-b8b4c876bc12', 'word_count': 2437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bde9ed5d-64d4-572a-a33c-b8b4c876bc12'}, {'abstract': 'Green Bay used five straight touchdowns in the second and third quarters to break open the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/15/sports/NFCDivisionalPlayoffs.html', 'snippet': 'Green Bay used five straight touchdowns in the second and third quarters to break open the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Green Bay used five straight touchdowns in the second and third quarters to break open the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/15/sports/NFCDivisionalPlayoffs-slide-B6L8/NFCDivisionalPlayoffs-slide-B6L8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.C. Divisional Replay: Packers 48, Falcons 21', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falcons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T05:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/688b7331-4f67-5c01-8ad7-471b256b4169', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/688b7331-4f67-5c01-8ad7-471b256b4169'}, {'abstract': 'Shootout attempts are increasingly incorporating spin moves and other flashy maneuvers, and controversy has increased right alongside. But, these moves are not new.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/rule-book-allows-shootout-showiness/', 'snippet': 'Shootout attempts are increasingly incorporating spin moves and other flashy maneuvers, and controversy has increased right alongside. But, these moves are not new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Edmonton’s Linus Omark, in his first N.H.L. game last month, pulled a spin move just after picking up the puck at center ice, skated over the blue line, pump-faked, then slapped the puck past Tampa Bay goalie Dan Ellis, the hockey world went nuts.The Lightning players were furious, criticizing Omark for what they considered a showboat move that disrespected the game. But others said that the Lightning had been merely sore losers and that the shootout — a skills contest tacked onto what was otherwise a tie game — was meant to entertain fans. Omark’s move, they argued, was entertaining. And besides, it worked.Since then, more shootout attempts have incorporated spin moves, most right in front of the goalie, and the controversy has not subsided.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rule Book Allows Shootout Showiness', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasek, Dominik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T05:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 's