 {'main': 'Photo Replay: Jan. 16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T21:38:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ce55f50f-1f9b-5c62-9903-1cc33c423d45', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ce55f50f-1f9b-5c62-9903-1cc33c423d45'}, {'abstract': 'West could take two quick tricks, but in this case the smarter play is to pass the lead off to partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/crosswords/bridge/17card.html', 'snippet': 'West could take two quick tricks, but in this case the smarter play is to pass the lead off to partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are certain plays that we make almost without thinking \x97 then soon realize that we have made a mistake. This is an example (see Diagram 1):', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Quick Choice May Not Be the Right Choice', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Quick Choice May Not Be the Right Choice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T21:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fa37a85-f16d-562b-89e1-6ed84798605f', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fa37a85-f16d-562b-89e1-6ed84798605f'}, {'abstract': 'On a snowy day in Chicago, the Bears dominated and set up a matchup with their rival, Green Bay, in the N.F.C. championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/sports/football/17bears.html', 'snippet': 'On a snowy day in Chicago, the Bears dominated and set up a matchup with their rival, Green Bay, in the N.F.C. championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO \x97 By the time the Bears bolted to a quick and insurmountable lead against the Seattle Seahawks in Sunday’s N.F.C. divisional playoff game, snow was sticking to Soldier Field’s frozen grass. During timeouts, workers used brooms and leaf blowers to clear the yardage lines, making more progress than the Seahawks’ offense for most of the game. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/YJPBEARS/YJPBEARS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/YJPBEARS/YJPBEARS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/YJPBEARS/YJPBEARS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bears Sweep Aside Seahawks and Gain Duel With Packers', 'kicker': 'Bears 35, Seahawks 24', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bears Cast Aside Seahawks and Gain Duel With Packers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T21:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a582868e-802a-5b37-882f-20c30f249660', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a582868e-802a-5b37-882f-20c30f249660'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago jumped in front quickly and won the N.F.C. divisional game, 35-24.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/16/sports/SPTSBEARS0116.html', 'snippet': 'Chicago jumped in front quickly and won the N.F.C. divisional game, 35-24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chicago jumped in front quickly and won the N.F.C. divisional game, 35-24.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 861, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/sports/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5/SPTSBEARS0116-slide-1OK5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.C. Divisional Replay: Bears Eliminate Seahawks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-16T22:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/198e4156-7f03-555b-88ca-feabda4eb21c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/198e4156-7f03-555b-88ca-feabda4eb21c'}, {'abstract': 'Baroque reeds carried the day at a Boston Early Music Festival at the Morgan Library & Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/arts/music/17early.html', 'snippet': 'Baroque reeds carried the day at a Boston Early Music Festival at the Morgan Library & Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is a marching band to do this time of year if it doesn’t have a bowl game to accompany? An eccentric variant, the Symphonie des Dragons, playing mostly Baroque oboes and bassoons, set up shop on Thursday evening at the Morgan Library & Museum for a concert in the series presented by the Boston Early Music Festival, “From the Court to the Stage: The Rise of the French Oboe Band.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/arts/EARLY/EARLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/17/arts/EARLY/EARLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/arts/EARLY/EARLY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Band No