best dramatic actor for “The King’s Speech” and Natalie Portman danced away with the award for best actress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/movies/awardsseason/17globes.html', 'snippet': '“The Social Network” took the prize for best drama, Colin Firth was named best dramatic actor for “The King’s Speech” and Natalie Portman danced away with the award for best actress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. \x97 What can be the silliness of the Golden Globes matched up with the seriousness of the critics on Sunday night as “The Social Network” took the prize for best drama, Colin Firth was named best dramatic actor for “The King’s Speech” and Natalie Portman danced away with the award for best actress in a drama at the entertainment industry’s second-favorite awards show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/movies/awardsseason/17globes-socialnetwork/17globes-socialnetwork-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/16/movies/awardsseason/17globes-socialnetwork/17globes-socialnetwork-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/movies/awardsseason/17globes-socialnetwork/17globes-socialnetwork-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/16/movies/awardsseason/17globes-socialnetwork/17globes-socialnetwork-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/16/movies/awardsseason/17globes-socialnetwork/17globes-social