 quarterbacks. But in their first two stops along the way, in Indianapolis and New England, the Jets have rendered their opponents pedestrian.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/GREEN/GREEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/GREEN/GREEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/GREEN/GREEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/GREEN/GREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/17/sports/GREEN/GREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Second Week, the Jets Make an Elite Quarterback Look Ordinary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Second Week, the Jets Make an Elite Quarterback Look Ordinary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T04:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27b9ccc1-13f6-51b8-8350-8fbf79f85e10', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27b9ccc1-13f6-51b8-8350-8fbf79f85e10'}, {'abstract': 'The Hollywood Foreign Press Association is not always a great predictor of future statuettes for the hopefuls that populate the accolades circuit. But this year, the winners hewed closely to expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/16/a-globes-full-of-conventional-wisdom/', 'snippet': 'The Hollywood Foreign Press Association is not always a great predictor of future statuettes for the hopefuls that populate the accolades circuit. But this year, the winners hewed closely to expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif.— The Golden Globes has weathered its share of scandals and ridicule, from bribery charges to the suggestion that “The Tourist” is a comedy. (The show’s host, Ricky Gervais, not to mention some of the honored, didn’t shy away from poking fun.) And the Hollywood Foreign Press Association is not always a great predictor of future statuettes for the hopefuls that populate the accolades circuit. (See: “Avatar” last year.) But this year, the winners hewed closely to the conventional wisdom of awards-watchers, honoring the same performers, writers and directors who have been marching up red carpets and fine-tuning their thank-you speeches for weeks. (“I’m trying to mix it up,” Lee Unkrich, the director of “Toy Story 3,” said.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Globes Full of Conventional Wisdom', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cholodenko, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood Foreign Press Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T04:56:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/483f4ea9-f89d-54a8-b7fc-b04cce0af027', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/483f4ea9-f89d-54a8-b7fc-b04cce0af027'}, {'abstract': 'the American gangster and prohibition era crime\nleader', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0117.html', 'snippet': 'the American gangster and prohibition era crime\nleader', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI BEACH, FLA., Jan. 25 --Al Capone, ex-Chicago gangster and prohibition era crime leader, died in his home here tonight. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capone Dead At 48; Dry Era Gang Chief', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3cbd441-7cee-5ce1-bb69-31cbbf6f91a1', 'word_count': 1672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3cbd441-7cee-5ce1-bb69-31cbbf6f91a1'}, {'abstract': 'Ricky Gervais, host of the Golden Globe ceremony, was merciless from the start, mocking