-9b94-5e92-b717-7bf3bc3cce98'}, {'abstract': 'Tucked away on a quiet street in Paris’s 10th Arrondissement, Le Pompon, a bar and concert venue housed that opened in a former synagogue in October, is anything but timid.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/in-paris-a-bar-and-music-venue-with-style-to-spare/', 'snippet': 'Tucked away on a quiet street in Paris’s 10th Arrondissement, Le Pompon, a bar and concert venue housed that opened in a former synagogue in October, is anything but timid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked away on a quiet street in the 10th Arrondissement, Le Pompon is anything but timid. A former synagogue, the space has been converted into a speakeasy-style bar, a secret smoking salon and a concert venue. Since opening in October, the spot (39, rue des Petites Écuries; 33-1-53-34-60-85; www.lepompon.fr) has steadily been attracting crowds of trans-European hipsters, French fashionistas and just about anyone who enjoys dancing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, a Bar and Music Venue With Style to Spare', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T11:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Pfeiffer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfeiffer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0be9d4d-14a2-5a33-a9f6-6b2e59683b69', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0be9d4d-14a2-5a33-a9f6-6b2e59683b69'}, {'abstract': 'The needs of American w