rive that spanned nearly eight minutes  helped seal a stunning Jets victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Patriots were Patriots, winning titles and making other teams look foolish, Donovan McNabb and Andy Reid and the Eagles were faulted for time-wasting and inefficiency during the fourth quarter of a Super Bowl defeat.On Sunday, New England left itself open to the same criticism:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Was Patriots’ Urgency in Fourth-Quarter Drive?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T12:55:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d46b2841-ba5b-515d-a3f8-ff9adb281a18', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d46b2841-ba5b-515d-a3f8-ff9adb281a18'}, {'abstract': 'A vegetable tempura without eggs in the batter.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/the-temporary-vegetarian-vegan-vegetable-tempura/', 'snippet': 'A vegetable tempura without eggs in the batter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Masato Nishihara, the executive chef of Kajitsu, an elegant vegan Japanese restaurant in the East Village, created a vegan vegetable tempura, one without eggs in the batter. “He believes that tempura batter, originally, was just flour and water, and that when you go back in history, at some point someone added eggs,” said Chiaki Takada, who interpreted for Mr. Nishihara. The chef said that the differences between the two tempuras — one with eggs, the other without — are not big.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Temporary Vegetarian: Vegan Vegetable Tempura', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ed2e12-3e0d-5554-890a-df6cd8b01745', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ed2e12-3e0d-5554-890a-df6cd8b01745'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of readers’ reviews of Jon Robin Baitz’s new play “Other Desert Cities” and the Roundabout’s revival of “The Importance of Being Earnest” by Oscar Wilde.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/curtain-down-heads-up-readers-respond-to-other-desert-cities-and-earnest/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of readers’ reviews of Jon Robin Baitz’s new play “Other Desert Cities” and the Roundabout’s revival of “The Importance of Being Earnest” by Oscar Wilde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manners, secrets and family relationships collide in two vastly different ways — one dramatically timely, the other timelessly funny — in the plays “Other Desert Cities” and “The Importance of Being Earnest,” which opened last week in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Curtain D