r': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T14:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya and Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d7ccf29-8d4d-5c65-a633-a9429400c9a0', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d7ccf29-8d4d-5c65-a633-a9429400c9a0'}, {'abstract': 'Check out a sneak peek at Gang Gang’s coming album via a new video by Jules Marquis, set inside a Macy’s department store.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/video-exclusive-gang-gang-dance-and-jules-marquis/', 'snippet': 'Check out a sneak peek at Gang Gang’s coming album via a new video by Jules Marquis, set inside a Macy’s department store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York favorites Gang Gang Dance will release their highly anticipated (at least by the art-rock set) fifth album this spring on the 4AD label. As the band gears up for the big date, it is planning a slew of shows, among them tonight’s private after-party for Capsule, a hip-enough fashion trade show held regularly in New York. Curated by Sean Hanratty, the night’s bill includes Light Asylum as an opening act and a video installation by the artists Daniel Turner and Colin Snapp. The two recently began collaborating under the name Jules Marquis; this past December they debuted their joint work with a well-received show at the Martos Gallery in Chelsea. (And for those traveling to Milan in the next few days for men’s fashion week, Turner has a solo show titled “Britannica” opening January 19 at the Pianissimo gallery on Via Ventura 6.)'