ecutive was taking a medical leave. Apple shares tumbled 6.2 percent in Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/business/global/18markets.html', 'snippet': 'United States stock futures declined abroad after Apple said that its chief executive was taking a medical leave. Apple shares tumbled 6.2 percent in Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The euro fell on Monday, ending a five-day rally against the dollar, and Spanish bonds dropped as the region’s ministers debated a bailout plan. United States stock futures declined abroad after Apple said that its chief executive, Steve Jobs, was taking a medical leave of absence.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Slips Against Dollar, and Futures Lose Ground', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Euro Slips Against Dollar, And Futures Lose Ground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T15:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5194074d-11e7-5713-ae99-1d9cab1fa804', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5194074d-11e7-5713-ae99-1d9cab1fa804'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the Golden Globe winners Sunday night are talented, but they’re also very glamorous.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/fashion-has-a-moment-at-the-golden-globes/', 'snippet': 'Many of the Golden Globe winners Sunday night are talented, but they’re also very glamorous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the Golden Globe winners Sunday night are talented, but they’re also very glamorous. Most of the female nominees and presenters are regularly among the top fashion vote-getters — Angelina Jolie, Anne Hathaway, Nicole Kidman, Scarlett Johansson, Amy Adams — and some of them have had contracts with major fashion houses, as Natalie Portman, who won for “Black Swan,” does with Dior. And I expect to see all their Globes pictures splashed across European gossip magazines next week during the Paris couture shows. That’s the payoff that the Hollywood Foreign Press Association expects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Has a Moment at the Golden Globes', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T15:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2159b1ea-102d-55c5-8ff7-223058e66ff4', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2159b1ea-102d-55c5-8ff7-223058e66ff4'}, {'abstract': 'Riccardo Tisci’s trophy look was this three-piece suit in a computer-generated armadillo print.', 'web_url': 'http