, 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/133df8e0-ae49-59d1-a8fd-e0e2996a8767'}, {'abstract': 'Haiti’s former dictator, Jean-Claude Duvalier, huddled with his advisers at a Port-au-Prince hotel a day after his stunning return to the country, but canceled plans to speak to reporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/world/americas/18haiti.html', 'snippet': 'Haiti’s former dictator, Jean-Claude Duvalier, huddled with his advisers at a Port-au-Prince hotel a day after his stunning return to the country, but canceled plans to speak to reporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti \x97 One year after Haiti was hit by a devastating earthquake that killed more than 200,000 people, the country grappled on Monday to absorb yet another potentially destabilizing blow: the surprising return of the former dictator Jean-Claude Duvalier, whose emergence from nearly a quarter-century in exile prompted condemnations from around the world and ignited new fears of conflict. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/world/18haiti-span3/18haiti-span3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/world/18haiti-span3/18haiti-span3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/world/18haiti-span3/18haiti-span3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Duvalier Meets With Advisers as Haiti Holds Its Breath', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Duvalier Meets With Advisers As Haiti Holds Its Breath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T16:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginger Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c022fe8d-5c98-5e81-9409-9bcf5759ec37', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c022fe8d-5c98-5e81-9409-9bcf5759ec37'}, {'abstract': 'Ginger, a member of the same plant family as turmeric, contains anti-inflammatory compounds and volatile oils \x97 gingerols \x97 that show analgesic effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/health/18really.html', 'snippet': 'Ginger, a member of the same plant family as turmeric, contains anti-inflammatory compounds and volatile oils \x97 gingerols \x97 that show analgesic effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Claim: Eating Ginger Helps Reduce Muscle Pain and Soreness', 'kicker': 'Really?'