imes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Well, at Least I Got One Right', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T16:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/48827ab5-0acc-55ad-8c7c-6d6f695abbd1', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48827ab5-0acc-55ad-8c7c-6d6f695abbd1'}, {'abstract': 'Tips on how to capture steam or fire in a cooking shot.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/food-photography-shooting-smoke-steam-and-flames/', 'snippet': 'Tips on how to capture steam or fire in a cooking shot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Scrivani (@Andrew Scrivani) is a freelance photographer who contributes to The New York Times. He writes the blog Making Sunday Sauce. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Photography: Shooting Smoke, Steam and Flames', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T16:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Scrivani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scrivani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f9f7656-15c9-579f-8f33-87811f6016b5', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f9f7656-15c9-579f-8f33-87811f6016b5'}, {'abstract': 'The co-author of a new book on China’s economy and financial system says the country’s growth model is flawed and its reforms have fallen short.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/a-conversation-with-carl-walter/', 'snippet': 'The co-author of a new book on China’s economy and financial system says the country’s growth model is flawed and its reforms have fallen short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their new book, “Red Capitalism: The Fragile Financial Foundation of China’s Extraordinary Rise” (John Wiley & Sons), Carl E. Walter and Fraser J.T. Howie paint a troubling portrait of China’s economy and its financial system. Despite the nation’s mind-boggling growth and images of gleaming skyscrapers and luxury cars, the authors say China’s growth model is flawed and fragile, and they warn about substantial risks accumulating in its banking system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Carl Walter', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/29368f14-62f3-5ae0-8707-d564624dd610', 'word_count': 1169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29368f14-62f3-5ae0-8707-d564624dd610'}, {'abstract': 'It’s Scorecard season again! Here’s our pick of the best quotes from day 1 of the fall 2011 men’s-wear shows.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/scorecard-jil-sander-wins-4/', 'snippet': 'It’s Scorecard season again! Here’s our pick of the best quotes from day 1 of the fall 2011 men’s-wear shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s Scorecard season again! The fall 2011 men’s-wear shows kicked off in Milan on Saturday, so as ever we’re here reading the deluge of reviews so you don’t have to. Early observations: January showers may bring February flowers, because critics are feeling that defining and refining your signature is totally cool.\xa0(Just see Raf Simons’s masterful play across the gender line of couture volumes and Technicolor from his last women’s collection at Jil Sander.) But be wary not to get stuck in a disco groove.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Jil Sander Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/73e25057-2af6-5950-838e-5b75db947f83', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73e25057-2af6-5950-838e-5b75db947f83'}, {'abstract': 'The truth about vacation club giveaways, a new way to buy glasses and other consumer-focused items from The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/monday-reading-vacation-club-giveaways/', 'snippet': 'The truth about vacation club giveaways, a new way to buy glasses and other consumer-focused items from The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Vacation Club Giveaways', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/999e6f70-2caa-5c64-b154-4bd4c67fce5f', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/999e6f70-2caa-5c64-b154-4bd4c67fce5f'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s Department of Consumer Affairs and the city’s public advocate both said that the Web site for “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” more clearly indicated the preview period for the show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/officials-say-theyre-satisfied-with-updated-spider-man-promotion/', 'snippet': 'New York City’s Department of Consumer Affairs and the city’s public advocate both said that the Web site for “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” more clearly indicated the preview period for the show.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:40 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Say They’re Satisfied With Updated ‘Spider-Man’ Promotion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadway League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a1fb0f7-3f1b-5fef-86f6-9d27be3d4041', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a1fb0f7-3f1b-5fef-86f6-9d27be3d4041'}, {'abstract': 'Publishers have been given until Feb. 1 to decide whether to turn overdue payments into a loan to Borders, according to Media Decoder.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/deadline-draws-nearer-in-borders-talks-with-publishers/', 'snippet': 'Publishers have been given until Feb. 1 to decide whether to turn overdue payments into a loan to Borders, according to Media Decoder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Publishers have been given until Feb. 1 to decide whether they are willing to accept a proposal from the Borders Group to turn overdue payments into a loan, several people briefed on the situation said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Borders Gives Publishers a Deadline', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALVAREZ & MARSAL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borders Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a45181-2d3d-51d9-8088-a17e2331e373', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a45181-2d3d-51d9-8088-a17e2331e373'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever you think about the ways of Rex Ryan’s Jets, they did take the knees out from under a rather enduring model franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/sports/football/18leading.html', 'snippet': 'Whatever you think about the ways of Rex Ryan’s Jets, they did take the knees out from under a rather enduring model franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can almost hear that noise in the background: the N.F.L. copy machine shutting down. For years it has been churning out copies of the Patriots franchise game plan and mimeos of the sour genius head coach in clearance-rack clothing (although a pure reproduction of the charisma vacuum that is Bill Belichick has proved elusive), but sometime in the middle of the Jets’ dismantling of New England on Sunday, someone hit the off button. And there will be a significant pause before a restart because, as much as the N.F.L. loves its copy machine, is it really possible to create another Rex Ryan? And if you could, would all that hot air evaporate the oceans?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Singular Approach and an Exceptional Victory', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Singular Approach and an Exceptional Victory for the Jets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:09:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b5578b-6c65-5519-b5b1-62661542a0c5', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b5578b-6c65-5519-b5b1-62661542a0c5'}, {'abstract': 'How it works.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/health-care-basics/', 'snippet': 'How it works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: The pie chart only shows that part of health care paid for by insurance. The rest is out-of-pocket spending, which happens even in single-payer systems, public health spending, and a grab-bag of other stuff. Source is here (pdf).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Basics', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b285c4a0-ac21-5ac5-aed1-56bf465c378e', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b285c4a0-ac21-5ac5-aed1-56bf465c378e'}, {'abstract': 'When we last left the family, Bill Henrickson had just won a Utah State Senate seat and took the opportunity of his victory speech to reveal his complicated marriage to his constituents. It did not go over well.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/big-love-watch-the-consequences-of-honesty/', 'snippet': 'When we last left the family, Bill Henrickson had just won a Utah State Senate seat and took the opportunity of his victory speech to reveal his complicated marriage to his constituents. It did not go over well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fifth and final season of “Big Love” began on Sunday night on HBO. We’ll be following the wind-down here each week and hope you’ll join us for a continuing conversation about the Henricksons’ polygamous household. A broad-scope review of the series appeared last week, but here we’ll get down to the nitty gritty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Big Love’ Watch: The Consequences of Honesty', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Show, Grant', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tripplehorn, Jeanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1467610-de31-58d4-af55-d40c113507f5', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1467610-de31-58d4-af55-d40c113507f5'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman said it was restricting participation in its new Facebook investment fund to foreign clients, after receiving intense public scrutiny over the creation of the fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/goldman-limits-facebook-investment-to-foreign-clients/', 'snippet': 'Goldman said it was restricting participation in its new Facebook investment fund to foreign clients, after receiving intense public scrutiny over the creation of the fund.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:55 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Limits Facebook Investment to Foreign Clients', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fed6022-7515-5961-8530-c844decb1399', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fed6022-7515-5961-8530-c844decb1399'}, {'abstract': 'Ricky Gervais’s barbed performance was the talk of the Golden Globes afterparties, and his writing partner dismissed chatter that the host was momentarily silenced by the Hollywood Foreign Press Association.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/all-the-cutting-jokes-on-schedule/', 'snippet': 'Ricky Gervais’s barbed performance was the talk of the Golden Globes afterparties, and his writing partner dismissed chatter that the host was momentarily silenced by the Hollywood Foreign Press Association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The talk of the parties at the Beverly Hilton Hotel after the Golden Globes was the barbed performance of the host, Ricky Gervais. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cutting Jokes, on Schedule', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood Foreign Press Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c46aaa04-f178-5e2f-bcee-0f1c7f351797', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c46aaa04-f178-5e2f-bcee-0f1c7f351797'}, {'abstract': 'The man who has ruled Libya with an iron fist for more than four decades says that sinister Western intelligence organization was behind the fall of his ally in Tunisia: WikiLeaks.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/qaddafi-sees-wikileaks-plot-in-tunisia/', 'snippet': 'The man who has ruled Libya with an iron fist for more than four decades says that sinister Western intelligence organization was behind the fall of his ally in Tunisia: WikiLeaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 2:58 p.m. As Tunisians struggle to create order from the chaos that has followed the fall of a dictator, the country’s neighbors are engaged in a different kind of fight: over how to interpret and even what to call the events that led to the flight of Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, after weeks of street protests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaddafi Sees WikiLeaks Plot in Tunisia', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d78de7-5a65-56f0-8cd6-df8fc72fae04', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d78de7-5a65-56f0-8cd6-df8fc72fae04'}, {'abstract': 'With aggressive sales targets for China, Porsche’s chief executive said he would not rule out producing the brand’s next S.U.V. there.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/porsche-cajun-s-u-v-could-be-built-in-china/', 'snippet': 'With aggressive sales targets for China, Porsche’s chief executive said he would not rule out producing the brand’s next S.U.V. there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a Monday edition of the German magazine Focus, Porsche chief executive Matthias Mueller said that the automaker’s current production capacity at its Stuttgart-Zuffenhausen factory was insufficient to meet worldwide sales targets, particularly in emerging markets like China. But as Porsche integrates more fully with its parent company, the Volkswagen Group, the brand might locate production of future models — among them an S.U.V., the Cajun, which will be smaller and less expensive than the Cayenne — in either China or North America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Porsche Cajun S.U.V. Could Be Built in China', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winterkorn, Martin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porsche AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:31:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fed6504-b057-5d94-899d-ea96eddf01cd', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fed6504-b057-5d94-899d-ea96eddf01cd'}, {'abstract': 'Rashida Jones, Aziz Ansari and Alexa Chung were just some of the boldface names at our pre-Golden Globes dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/fete-accompli-t-party-in-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'Rashida Jones, Aziz Ansari and Alexa Chung were just some of the boldface names at our pre-Golden Globes dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#108", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fete Accompli | T Party in Los Angeles', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d66a552e-9101-5822-abba-d8c705d5bcc1', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d66a552e-9101-5822-abba-d8c705d5bcc1'}, {'abstract': 'Can a dose of ginger help you recover after a workout?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/soothing-sore-muscles-with-ginger/', 'snippet': 'Can a dose of ginger help you recover after a workout?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a dose of ginger help you recover after a workout?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soothing Sore Muscles With Ginger', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ginger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Barrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5953fb79-6ddf-5aeb-a454-66de88ce98a0', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5953fb79-6ddf-5aeb-a454-66de88ce98a0'}, {'abstract': 'Buying because everyone else is buying is not an investment strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/investing-with-the-herd/', 'snippet': 'Buying because everyone else is buying is not an investment strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog, and other drawings are available on his personal Web site, BehaviorGap.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investing With the Herd', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbedc824-6e96-5556-94b4-8d04053d972e', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbedc824-6e96-5556-94b4-8d04053d972e'}, {'abstract': 'A set of numerical puzzles honoring two great American heroes, Martin Luther King Jr. and Benjamin Franklin.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/numberplay-honoring-martin-and-ben/', 'snippet': 'A set of numerical puzzles honoring two great American heroes, Martin Luther King Jr. and Benjamin Franklin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today is Martin Luther King day, a federal holiday. Martin Luther King Jr. was actually born on Jan. 15, 1929, but we celebrate his birthday today, guided by the great American principle that states, “No holiday shall be wasted by falling on a weekend!” Coincidentally, Jan. 17 is the birthday of another great American hero, Benjamin Franklin, who was born on this date in 1706 by the modern Gregorian calendar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Honoring Martin and Ben', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calendars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:54:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik with Aziz Inan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aziz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Inan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/14fb33be-a5e1-543c-8bdd-d0f604089ce9', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14fb33be-a5e1-543c-8bdd-d0f604089ce9'}, {'abstract': 'Former Cavaliers small forward Bob “Bingo” Smith is recovering from a major stroke, and finds comfort and support by attending the team’s home games.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/bingo-smith-the-cavaliers-loyal-superstar-perseveres/', 'snippet': 'Former Cavaliers small forward Bob “Bingo” Smith is recovering from a major stroke, and finds comfort and support by attending the team’s home games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard for younger basketball fans to imagine, but the Cleveland Cavaliers had flashy scorers long before some guy named LeBron James played there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bingo Smith, the Cavaliers’ Loyal Superstar, Perseveres', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Robert Bingo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/447056c4-4c26-575d-97ef-4095bbb94239', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447056c4-4c26-575d-97ef-4095bbb94239'}, {'abstract': 'The grueling off-road race, now in its third year in South America, concluded this past weekend outside Buenos Aires.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/high-peaks-high-drama-in-2011-dakar-rally/', 'snippet': 'The grueling off-road race, now in its third year in South America, concluded this past weekend outside Buenos Aires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After driving nearly 6,000 miles over frigid high Andean plains and coastal dunes, up rock-gorged gullies and across boundless grasslands, a hearty cadre of truckers, four-wheel A.T.V. drivers, motorcyclists and car pilots were fêted with confetti and champagne on Sunday in Buenos Aires, having wrapped the 2011 Dakar Rally‘s 15th and final stage on Saturday, just outside the Argentinian capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Peaks, High Drama in 2011 Dakar Rally', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dakar Rally', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sainz, Carlos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dakar (Senegal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d64c08a0-1408-5f39-9379-a8ce1931b665', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d64c08a0-1408-5f39-9379-a8ce1931b665'}, {'abstract': 'The company has been forced to address publishers’ concerns about content and advertising revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/technology/18iht-google18.html', 'snippet': 'The company has been forced to address publishers’ concerns about content and advertising revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian antitrust authority said Monday that it had ended an investigation into Google’s Internet news service after the company took steps to ease newspaper publishers’ concerns about control over their content and the sharing of advertising revenue. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Google Worry Recedes, for Now, as Italy Ends Investigation Into News Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Google Worry Recedes, for Now, as Italy Ends Investigation Into News Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T17:57:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52694945-df56-5208-a67a-f4aac69062d9', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52694945-df56-5208-a67a-f4aac69062d9'}, {'abstract': 'For more than a decade, TripAdvisor.com has been a popular Web site for users to rate hotels, restaurants and activities. Now it has added airlines to the roster of rateable items.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/tripadvisor-debuts-airline-rating-system/', 'snippet': 'For more than a decade, TripAdvisor.com has been a popular Web site for users to rate hotels, restaurants and activities. Now it has added airlines to the roster of rateable items.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than a decade, TripAdvisor.com has been a popular Web site for users to rate hotels, restaurants and activities. Now it has added airlines to the roster of ratable items. The new feature, which debuted last week as part of TripAdvisor Flights, the site’s online flight search tool, allows travelers to add feedback on airlines in eight categories, as part of their booking process. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TripAdvisor Debuts Airline Rating System', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Saltzstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltzstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/25db5067-057d-5072-85f4-21437349b055', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25db5067-057d-5072-85f4-21437349b055'}, {'abstract': 'It is now time for Corey Hertzog, the former Penn State striker and future Red Bulls player, to relax and enjoy the next couple of days. Just do not expect to find Hertzog rooted to h