an-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Ordeal of Landing a Short-Term Rental', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Long Ordeal of Landing a Short-Term Rental', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T18:16:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5a17c61-20b6-5f17-93b7-82637a03a929', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5a17c61-20b6-5f17-93b7-82637a03a929'}, {'abstract': 'Thinkers explore whether there are workarounds for cognitive traits that may be holding back human progress.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/whats-missing-from-our-cognitive-toolkit/', 'snippet': 'Thinkers explore whether there are workarounds for cognitive traits that may be holding back human progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is your brain on words. It’s clearly a pretty hard-wired system. But can we find ways to use what’s locked in our skulls to better effect? I’ll be writing more soon on that broad question, with a hint of my thoughts provided in a recent Tweet. Some variant on noosphere is clearly nigh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Missing From Our ‘Cognitive Toolkit’?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brockman, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryson, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Helen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gell-Mann, Murray', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahneman, Daniel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcus, Gary', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinker, Steven', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, Jay', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T18:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/96ade0e2-cc7f-576a-b6ef-0ff8bae886cc', 'word_count': 1872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96ade0e2-cc7f-576a-b6ef-0ff8bae886cc'}, {'abstract': 'The Packers and the Jets are still alive in the N.F.L. playoffs while the top-seeded Falcons and Patriots are out, once again illustrating the league’s parity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/sports/football/18fastforward.html', 'snippet': 'The Packers and the Jets are still alive in the N.F.L. playoffs while the top-seeded Falcons and Patriots are out, once again illustrating the league’s parity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2010 N.F.L. season was played with a fun-house mirror effect: down was up, up was down, parity was alive and so was a 7-9 division champion. But in a season of anomalies \x97 19 overtime games, the Detroit Lions winning \x97 none stood out quite like this: one year after both No. 1 playoff seeds advanced to the Super Bowl, the top seeds were eliminated in their first game, and both sixth-seeded teams advanced to the conference championship games Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/18fastfroward-span2/18fastfroward-span2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/18fastfroward-span2/18fastfroward-span2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/18fastfroward-span2/18fastfroward-span2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/18fastfroward-span2/18fastfroward-span2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/18fastfroward-span2/18fastfroward-span2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No. 1s Out as Sixth Seeds Celebrate', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Fast Forward', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where No. 6 Is Better Than No. 1', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], '