ost recent subject in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still feeling sluggish on this holiday Monday? These pictures might help you wake up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Coffeehouses, 2 Weeks, 50 Cups', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfc84c28-352e-56fb-9056-4a5ee9a1db7c', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfc84c28-352e-56fb-9056-4a5ee9a1db7c'}, {'abstract': 'It is a Groundhog-Day-be-damned prediction: When the city gets at least eight inches of snow in December, it will get more by the end of that same winter. Brace yourself for the statistical argument.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/a-weather-hobbyist-predicts-more-snow-much-more/', 'snippet': 'It is a Groundhog-Day-be-damned prediction: When the city gets at least eight inches of snow in December, it will get more by the end of that same winter. Brace yourself for the statistical argument.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Jan. 21 | Stephen Fybish is worried that you might think he thought this up after the December snowstorm that caught the city by surprise, or the smaller ones last week and the week before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Weather Hobbyist Predicts More Snow — Much More', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:28:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ca794d8-2ea4-53a7-85f0-523827c38c46', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ca794d8-2ea4-53a7-85f0-523827c38c46'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/fafsaq-and-a-part-7-2/', 'snippet': 'Mark Kantrowitz, a financial-aid guru, is answering reader questions on the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, and other topics of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As families of prospective college freshmen begin to tackle the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or Fafsa, Mark Kantrowitz, a financial aid expert and founder of the Web sites finaid.org and fastweb.com, has been answering questions from readers of The Choice over the last week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last of 7 Parts: Answers to Readers’ Questions on Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kantrowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantrowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa019b3-f242-577f-bbc9-0760b888e5ad', 'word_count': 2395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa019b3-f242-577f-bbc9-0760b888e5ad'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets’ Brook Lopez has recovered his scoring touch but adequate rebounding continues to elude him.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/lopez-scoring-but-fighting-rebounding-woes/', 'snippet': 'The Nets’ Brook Lopez has recovered his scoring touch but adequate rebounding continues to elude him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a rough start to the new year, the Nets’ Brook Lopez seems to be back on track. January hadn’t been kind to Lopez; in each of the month’s first five games, he scored at a below-average rate by his season’s standards, and Lopez even scored in single digits twice during that stretch. The Nets’ two latest games have been a different story though, as Lopez dropped a pair of incredibly efficient, high-scoring performances against the Lakers and the Blazers. The momentary snag in Lopez’s per-game scoring didn’t provide any real cause for alarm, but it’s nice to see him reverse course with such prolific efforts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lopez Scoring, but Fighting Rebounding Woes', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Brook', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/620249ff-01f0-5787-90ae-19432324cd7a', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/620249ff-01f0-5787-90ae-19432324cd7a'}, {'abstract': 'The decision by President Michel Suleiman appears to signal the difficulties that Lebanon’s politicians will face in negotiations to choose a new prime minister.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/world/middleeast/18lebanon.html', 'snippet': 'The decision by President Michel Suleiman appears to signal the difficulties that Lebanon’s politicians will face in negotiations to choose a new prime minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon \x97 The Lebanese president on Monday postponed talks to form a new government as regional leaders convened in Syria to find a way out of one of Lebanon’s worst crises in years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lebanon Delays Talks on New Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lebanese Leader Delays Talks on New Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Rafik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Saad', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasrallah, Hassan', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri and Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce93204d-faf9-5444-8d9e-e3c4ede13642', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce93204d-faf9-5444-8d9e-e3c4ede13642'}, {'abstract': 'A study of studies showed that nearly half of clinical trials cite none or only one of previous trials addressing the same question.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/health/research/18cite.html', 'snippet': 'A study of studies showed that nearly half of clinical trials cite none or only one of previous trials addressing the same question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Science, so the story goes, is a meticulously built edifice. Discoveries balance on ones that preceded them. Research is stimulated by studies that went on before.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial in a Vacuum: Study of Studies Shows Few Citations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial in a Vacuum: Study of Studies Shows Few Citations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa43d45a-15f3-5caa-9778-180da0fc6021', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa43d45a-15f3-5caa-9778-180da0fc6021'}, {'abstract': 'All of a sudden you find yourself being a focal point of your own people, and yesterday’s monsters are your only merciful protection.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/17/embedistan-monsters-everywhere/', 'snippet': 'All of a sudden you find yourself being a focal point of your own people, and yesterday’s monsters are your only merciful protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doing an embed puts you in such a weird situation as an Iraqi. It creates this contradiction inside you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Embedistan: Monsters Everywhere', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T19:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Hamdani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamdani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6008499-0f9a-524e-8b13-9579b5b433d4', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6008499-0f9a-524e-8b13-9579b5b433d4'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers say it’s not clear how to make effective shoe inserts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/health/nutrition/18best.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers say it’s not clear how to make effective shoe inserts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Benno M. Nigg has become a leading researcher on orthotics \x97 those shoe inserts that many athletes use to try to prevent injuri