ion to date takes a lighter hand to his now signature staples, most notably a deconstructed suede biker jacket, a tough leather shirtdress with a sheer back, great slouchy trousers (we like this wide, slightly cropped version with the slit at the knee) and a variety of cool knits. And they all come in your favorite shade of black.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Alexander Wang Pre-Fall', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T21:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/074283b2-26ff-53b9-be56-1b50df2a3f68', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074283b2-26ff-53b9-be56-1b50df2a3f68'}, {'abstract': 'A border collie knows 1,022 nouns, a record that displays the unexpected depths of the canine mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/science/18dog.html', 'snippet': 'A border collie knows 1,022 nouns, a record that displays the unexpected depths of the canine mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chaser, a border collie who lives in Spartanburg, S.C., has the largest vocabulary of any known dog. She knows 1,022 nouns, a record that displays unexpected depths of the canine mind and may help explain how children acquire language.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/science/18dog/18dog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': 