sse is putting 15 immigrant women from this poor Paris suburb through a professional cooking course, and guaranteeing a job for those who complete their certificates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/world/europe/18sarcelles.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Alain Ducasse is putting 15 immigrant women from this poor Paris suburb through a professional cooking course, and guaranteeing a job for those who complete their certificates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARCELLES, France \x97 In some ways, it is just a drop of costly olive oil in a turbid lake, but for 15 women from this poor Paris suburb, it is a chance for a stable and nourishing, if difficult, career. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/world/SARCELLES-1/SARCELLES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/18/world/SARCELLES-1/SARCELLES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/world/SARCELLES-1/SARCELLES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/world/SARCELLES-1/SARCELLES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/world/SARCELLES-1/SARCELLES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Door Into Top Kitchens for French North Africans', 'kicker': 'Sarcelles Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North African Seasoning For Top French Kitchens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ducasse, Alain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T23:47:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bbdce8c-b7cb-5ffa-80f6-786046baff47', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bbdce8c-b7cb-5ffa-80f6-786046baff47'}, {'abstract': 'Apple would have been better served by explicitly naming Tim Cook acting chief executive, leaving Steven P. Jobs as chairman during his medical leave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/business/18views.html', 'snippet': 'Apple would have been better served by explicitly naming Tim Cook acting chief executive, leaving Steven P. Jobs as chairman during his medical leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple needs to delegate Steve Jobs’s power more formally to someone else. Mr. Jobs, Apple’s chief executive, is handing day-to-day control to the company’s chief operating officer, Tim Cook, because of health issues. Yet he retains his chief executive title. This is the third such move, and this time the handover is indefinite. However painful, a more formal transfer to an acting chief executive would have been better.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Needs a Stronger Transfer of Power', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stronger Transfer Needed at Apple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yuan (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Timothy D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-17T23:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and John Foley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/840b1280-73b2-5592-afd1-1bdedc9dbc06', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840b1280-73b2-5592-afd1-1bdedc9dbc06'}, {'abstract': 'Toshiba is a rare example of a company tapping what some economists call Japan’s least used resource: women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/business/global/18screen.html', 'snippet': 'Toshiba is a rare example of a company tapping what some economists call Japan’s least used resource: women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO \x97 It is the Achilles’ heel of 3-D television: the clunky glasses that viewers must wear to see images pop out in 3-D. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/business/Screen/