pet': 'When Bart Scott had his interview/tirade with the ESPN reporter Sal Paolantonio on Sunday night, his teammates noticed. His coaches noticed. And, yes, his mother noticed, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. – When Bart Scott went all WWE, with an anger-non-management tirade exchange with the ESPN reporter Sal Paolantonio on Sunday night, his teammates noticed. His coaches noticed. His mother noticed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bart Scott’s Mother Reacts to His Rant', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Bart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T00:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6615883-0a5e-5dc8-85ca-1336fc2772a5', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6615883-0a5e-5dc8-85ca-1336fc2772a5'}, {'abstract': 'The $14 million Go Fish Georgia Educational Center has become a cautionary tale about the long-term ramifications of prerecession decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/us/18fishing.html', 'snippet': 'The $14 million Go Fish Georgia Educational Center has become a cautionary tale about the long-term ramifications of prerecession decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PERRY, Ga. \x97 Every weekend, Michael Morris and his 2-year-old son, Jacob, visit this small town’s enormous new $14 million fishing museum. They watch bream and bass swim in aquarium-size tanks. They play with an interactive model of a fishing boat and try to catch fish on a computer simulation using a rod and reel connected to a video screen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/us/FISHING-2/FISHING-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/18/us/FISHING-2/FISHING-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/us/FISHING-2/FISHING-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/us/FISHING-2/FISHING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/us/FISHING-2/FISHING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fishing Museum Is Symbol of Waste in Georgia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Fishing Museum Becomes a Symbol Of Waste in Georgia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T00:00:59+0000', 'document_typ