gs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/morning-buzz-cuomos-kind-of-committee/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: an increase in violence in housing projects, Martin Luther King’s Birthday observances, and a lawsuit over renovations on West 34th Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday will be sodden but a little warmer, with rain virtually certain and highs nearing 40.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Cuomo’s Kind of Committee', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:32:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd807af-ae68-521d-bca7-8acd79c18e40', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd807af-ae68-521d-bca7-8acd79c18e40'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans in the House plan to introduce a bill on Wednesday to repeal the health care overhaul.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/democrats-make-a-case-for-the-health-care-law/', 'snippet': 'Republicans in the House plan to introduce a bill on Wednesday to repeal the health care overhaul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With House Republicans planning to approve a bill on Wednesday that would repeal the big health care overhaul, Democrats on Tuesday ramped up their efforts to defend the law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Make a Case for the Health Care Law', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:32:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/56dab699-ad1f-583c-95d7-53b3c1f2dd10', 'word_count': 1707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56dab699-ad1f-583c-95d7-53b3c1f2dd10'}, {'abstract': 'The former chef of Persimmon will offer a Korean-inflected fusion menu.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/off-the-menu-on-the-road-kimchi-taco/', 'snippet': 'The former chef of Persimmon will offer a Korean-inflected fusion menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Youngsun Lee, who briefly owned Persimmon, the tiny set-menu restaurant in the East Village, and Phillip Lee, with whom he worked at BR Guest restaurants, will open the Kimchi Taco truck, with a mash-up of Korean and other cuisines, on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu, On the Road: Kimchi Taco', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e1537d-c21c-5c09-888c-3bd5a2bb4963', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e1537d-c21c-5c09-888c-3bd5a2bb4963'}, {'abstract': 'The savings are real.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/medicare-and-health-reform/', 'snippet': 'The savings are real.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many attacks on health reform involve assertions that the law’s proposed Medicare savings can’t possibly materialize, that the Democrats just made stuff up. So it’s worth looking at where those savings are supposed to come from. The Center on Budget and Policy Priorities has a nice summary of the law’s financing; here’s the Medicare table:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare and Health Reform', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fc2fed9-2db5-54e8-b33c-4edd2e410990', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fc2fed9-2db5-54e8-b33c-4edd2e410990'}, {'abstract': 'The third-quarter delivery date reflected the impact of the November fire and the time required to install new software and new electrical panels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/19boeing.html', 'snippet': 'The third-quarter delivery date reflected the impact of the November fire and the time required to install new software and new electrical panels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boeing Company on Tuesday pushed back the first delivery of its 787 Dreamliner to the third quarter, hoping that the delay will give it enough time to finish a jetliner that is more than three years behind schedule.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/Boeing/Boeing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/Boeing/Boeing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/business/Boeing/Boeing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing Again Delays Delivery of Dreamliner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Again Delays Delivery of Dreamliner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/507f21a9-ed81-5a4f-9f6d-94466a5fb6fd', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/507f21a9-ed81-5a4f-9f6d-94466a5fb6fd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McIntyre discusses the difficult burden of replacing Andy Whitfield, the actor who created the title character on the hit Starz series about a Roman gladiator who will lead a slave revolt.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/he-is-spartacus-liam-mcintyre-talks-about-taking-over-in-season-2-of-blood-and-sand/', 'snippet': 'Mr. McIntyre discusses the difficult burden of replacing Andy Whitfield, the actor who created the title character on the hit Starz series about a Roman gladiator who will lead a slave revolt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday Liam McIntyre received some of the most exciting news of his career, and some of the most difficult: he learned that he had just been cast in the title role in a cable series — but as the replacement for Andy Whitfield in “Spartacus: Blood and Sand.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Is Spartacus: Liam McIntyre Talks About Taking Over in Season 2 of ‘Blood and Sand’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitfield, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T13:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2324ad8-b3ad-5ebd-a836-d02b848ad7e3', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2324ad8-b3ad-5ebd-a836-d02b848ad7e3'}, {'abstract': 'Another reason to visit: Juergen Teller has not one but two exhibitions in the German capital these days.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/now-showing-juergen-teller-in-berlin/', 'snippet': 'Another reason to visit: Juergen Teller has not one but two exhibitions in the German capital these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Juergen Teller has not one but two exhibitions in the German capital these days. “Paradis,” at Johann König Galerie in Berlin Kreuzberg, shows large-format prints of a naked Charlotte Rampling with an equally naked Raquel Zimmermann, rambling about the Louvre and posing alongside the Mona Lisa and a marble Napoleon. Originally published in the French magazine Paradis in 2009 and shown at Lehmann Maupin in New York the same year, the images have lost none of their beauty or inherent shock factor. Teller’s other, much smaller, show in Berlin is equally revealing. Located in an ingeniously designed third-floor space run by the Berlin-based 032c Magazine, the exhibition comprises new work that Teller has simply called “Men and Women.” An image of a naked Vivienne Westwood, broadly grinning and with her legs splayed, presides over the show like a regal cross between Annie Sprinkle and Marie Antoinette, while next to her the photographer William Eggleston, photographed at home in Memphis, and Teller’s own 9-year-old son, Ed, photographed in the gym of a hotel in the Maldives, seem goofily adrift. “It’s really a show about impotence,” remarked a guest at the opening on Saturday night. “In the middle you have Vivienne, all powerful and sexual, and to the left and to the right you have an old man who can’t really do it anymore, and a young man who can’t do it yet.” No word from Teller himself whether he subscribes to the same interpretation — when pressed for a quote during dinner after the opening, Teller simply pointed to a David Hamilton photograph on the wall and said, “I like those breasts.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Juergen Teller in Berlin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felix Burrichter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrichter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aaee5d0-d860-52a3-a406-ad6f3a8f4ab9', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aaee5d0-d860-52a3-a406-ad6f3a8f4ab9'}, {'abstract': 'My colleague Pat Lyons pointed out a device that’s been popping up a lot lately in the leads of feature stories. Call it the “call it” lead.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/a-phrase-we-love-too-much/', 'snippet': 'My colleague Pat Lyons pointed out a device that’s been popping up a lot lately in the leads of feature stories. Call it the “call it” lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Phrase We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c912d820-4ab3-5472-ad4f-487b2bbcbf52', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c912d820-4ab3-5472-ad4f-487b2bbcbf52'}, {'abstract': 'My colleague Pat Lyons pointed out a device that’s been popping up a lot lately in the leads of feature stories. Call it the “call it” lead.', 'web_url': 'https://topics.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/a-phrase-we-love-too-much/', 'snippet': 'My colleague Pat Lyons pointed out a device that’s been popping up a lot lately in the leads of feature stories. Call it the “call it” lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Phrase We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d633a421-8594-546d-aaa0-69453f0b086a', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d633a421-8594-546d-aaa0-69453f0b086a'}, {'abstract': 'A former chef from Sushi Yasuda will be preparing sushi at this much-anticipated SoHo restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/off-the-menu-niko/', 'snippet': 'A former chef from Sushi Yasuda will be preparing sushi at this much-anticipated SoHo restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given its location — in the former Honmura An — and the chef at its eight-seat sushi bar — Hiro Sawatari formerly of the highly esteemed Sushi Yasuda — Niko has generated a lot of interest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu: Niko', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sushi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Cobi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e15d750-e038-5e36-afb1-30a44729866e', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e15d750-e038-5e36-afb1-30a44729866e'}, {'abstract': 'Moelis & Company, the investment bank, is already an established player in Dubai, having advised Dubai World on its $23.5 billion debt restructuring.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/moelis-opens-dubai-office/', 'snippet': 'Moelis & Company, the investment bank, is already an established player in Dubai, having advised Dubai World on its $23.5 billion debt restructuring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moelis & Company said on Tuesday that it had opened an office in Dubai, its seventh office worldwide. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moelis Opens Dubai Office', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moelis & Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf07c95b-49cd-55b1-bc61-19839db93048', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf07c95b-49cd-55b1-bc61-19839db93048'}, {'abstract': 'Small change, by historical standards.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-recent-history-of-the-dollar/', 'snippet': 'Small change, by historical standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some commenters seem to believe that there has been a massive depreciation of the dollar since Ben Bernanke began QE2, or more broadly since he began rapidly increasing the monetary base. But nooooo! [/end Belushi] The dollar briefly surged during the oh-God-we’re-all-gonna-die period of the financial crisis, then fell more or less back to where it was at the start of the recession. And all of these movements were small compared with the long dollar slide during the Bush years — a slide, by the way, which was never part of my critique of that era.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Recent History of the Dollar', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/743269fa-7d11-5a89-afee-109f9e8733cf', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/743269fa-7d11-5a89-afee-109f9e8733cf'}, {'abstract': 'The retailer announced that it will continue to solicit higher takeover offers until Feb. 15 as part of a settlement with a group of shareholders.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/j-crew-settlement-talks-stumble-on-go-shop/', 'snippet': 'The retailer announced that it will continue to solicit higher takeover offers until Feb. 15 as part of a settlement with a group of shareholders.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:21 p.m. | Updated J. Crew announced its settlement with the plaintiff shareholders and set a meeting to vote on the TPG leveraged buyout for March 1. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'J. Crew Settles Lawsuit Over $3 Billion Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drexler, Millard S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'J Crew Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leonard Green & Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:24:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '