A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/world/JP-TUNISIA/JP-TUNISIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/JP-TUNISIA/JP-TUNISIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/JP-TUNISIA/JP-TUNISIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/world/JP-TUNISIA/JP-TUNISIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Officials Quit in Tunisia Amid Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MORE OFFICIALS QUIT IN TUNISIA AMID PROTESTS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghannouchi, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77e204a8-464c-5cc9-b099-5c84d397ee09', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77e204a8-464c-5cc9-b099-5c84d397ee09'}, {'abstract': 'In a rare accolades season setback for “The Social Network,” it earned only six nominations;“The King’s Speech” got 14, including best picture, best actor, best director, best supporting actress and actor, best cinematography, best screenplay, best score and best British film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/british-academy-swoons-for-the-kings-speech/', 'snippet': 'In a rare accolades season setback for “The Social Network,” it earned only six nominations;“The King’s Speech” got 14, including best picture, best actor, best director, best supporting actress and actor, best cinematography, best screenplay, bes...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The British Academy of Film and Television Arts, the Old Country version of the Academy, announced its nominees for the Orange British Academy Film Awards on Tuesday morning, and “The Fighter” swept. Nope, not at all. The highest honors went, of course, to “The King’s Speech,” the most British of films. In a rare accolades-season setback for “The Social Network,” it earned only six nominations; “The King’s Speech” got 14, including best picture, best actor, best director, best supporting actress and actor, best cinematography, best screenplay, best score and best British film. “Black Swan” also did well, earning 12 nods, and “Inception” received 9. The Bafta winners have coincided with the Oscar best-picture winner four times over the last decade. For the full list of hopefuls, look here. The winners will be announced on Feb. 13 in London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Academy Swoons for ‘The King’s Speech’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Academy of Film and Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80a21dc-4dc7-5d12-9826-ba75c10554fb', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80a21dc-4dc7-5d12-9826-ba75c10554fb'}, {'abstract': 'Bike traffic is up 70 percent on London’s streets.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/on-our-radar-londons-bike-lane-superhighways/', 'snippet': 'Bike traffic is up 70 percent on London’s streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The London transit authority reports that rush-hour cycling traffic has doubled on two downtown thoroughfares since the creation of bike-lane “superhighways” on the streets last year. Over all, bike traffic on the streets is up 70 percent. The two-way lanes, which radiate out from the city center, are painted bright blue and feature safety mirrors, signals at intersections and bicycle parking spaces. [Road.cc]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Cyclists Flock to London’s Bike-Lane ‘Superhighways’', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ventura County (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fedbadb2-ef6d-51bf-89c2-0ade2f680735', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fedbadb2-ef6d-51bf-89c2-0ade2f680735'}, {'abstract': 'It may be yuckety outside, but on City Room, we’ll be blasting summer all day long.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/summer-fun-day-its-a-scorcher-out-there/', 'snippet': 'It may be yuckety outside, but on City Room, we’ll be blasting summer all day long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Out there in the City Room alternate universe, that is. As an antidote to the faceful of raw sleet you got when you stuck your head out the front door this morning, we will be recreating an actual city summer all day long, with the hottest hits from our archives. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Fun Day | It’s a Scorcher Out There', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T14:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb052d5-d6ea-51f0-8deb-a32f7c9f84c0', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb052d5-d6ea-51f0-8deb-a32f7c9f84c0'}, {'abstract': 'But still sounding reasonable.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/old-dollar-thoughts/', 'snippet': 'But still sounding reasonable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aha. A not-too-technical paper I wrote about the dollar’s international role back in 1984 — one that still holds up pretty well, as far as I can tell — is available online (pdf).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Dollar Thoughts', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:11:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e3af3a-c483-5e70-82fd-7ddc40199094', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e3af3a-c483-5e70-82fd-7ddc40199094'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared James Bond film titles, villains, henchmen, Bond girls and groan-worthy puns.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-social-network-is-not-enough/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared James Bond film titles, villains, henchmen, Bond girls and groan-worthy puns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared James Bond film titles, villains, henchmen, Bond girls and groan-worthy puns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Social Network is Not Enough', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aef000f0-7b4e-5d55-ad03-8f2e434bdbea', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aef000f0-7b4e-5d55-ad03-8f2e434bdbea'}, {'abstract': 'The order to review all business regulations is signed on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/obama-orders-review-of-business-regulations/', 'snippet': 'The order to review all business regulations is signed on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama, intensifying his courtship of the business community, announced Tuesday that he is issuing an executive order that aims to free companies of unnecessary regulatory burdens and promote economic growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Orders Review of Business Regulations', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef10a362-5e02-5bd4-bd9b-5ee513c5d489', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef10a362-5e02-5bd4-bd9b-5ee513c5d489'}, {'abstract': 'Regis Philbin told viewers Tuesday morning that he will step down as co-host of “Live with Regis and Kelly”  sometime later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/regis-philbin-to-leave-live-with-regis-and-kelly/', 'snippet': 'Regis Philbin told viewers Tuesday morning that he will step down as co-host of “Live with Regis and Kelly”  sometime later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regis Philbin, a star of morning television for a generation, made a surprise announcement at the start of “Live with Regis and Kelly” Tuesday morning, telling viewers that he intended to step down sometime later this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regis Philbin to Leave ‘Live with Regis and Kelly’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philbin, Regis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/067b50e0-8793-5476-98a8-dca1d02a871b', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/067b50e0-8793-5476-98a8-dca1d02a871b'}, {'abstract': 'Host country Qatar, runner up in Group A, will play Japan, winner of Group B in 20,000 seat Al Garafa Stadium instead of 40,000 seat Khalifa Stadium, used for the opening ceremony, when the two teams meet this Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/asian-cup-big-game-small-stadium/', 'snippet': 'Host country Qatar, runner up in Group A, will play Japan, winner of Group B in 20,000 seat Al Garafa Stadium instead of 40,000 seat Khalifa Stadium, used for the opening ceremony, when the two teams meet this Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — Host Qatar, runner-up in Group A, will play Japan, winner of Group B, in 20,000-seat Al Garafa Stadium instead of 40,000-seat Khalifa Stadium, used for the opening ceremony, when the two teams meet in an Asian Cup quarterfinal match on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Cup: Big Game, Small Stadium', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Behrooz Afrakhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Behrooz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afrakhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc5f4821-e54e-5114-8de2-c90951d0d20c', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc5f4821-e54e-5114-8de2-c90951d0d20c'}, {'abstract': 'Finding short-term rentals in New York, an airline rating system from TripAdvisor and other consumer-focused items from Tuesday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/tuesday-reading-new-york-short-term-rentals/', 'snippet': 'Finding short-term rentals in New York, an airline rating system from TripAdvisor and other consumer-focused items from Tuesday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: New York Short-Term Rentals', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:48:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/95339877-840a-529a-8e55-6efb56c551dd', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95339877-840a-529a-8e55-6efb56c551dd'}, {'abstract': 'He also calls on the New Jersey governor to reconsider his decision to scrap the Trans-Hudson project.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/schumer-criticizes-christies-plan-to-divert-tunnel-funds/', 'snippet': 'He also calls on the New Jersey governor to reconsider his decision to scrap the Trans-Hudson project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:44 p.m. | New York’s senior senator, Charles E. Schumer, sharply criticized New Jersey’s governor, Chris Christie, for his decision to halt the construction of a commuter rail tunnel under the Hudson River and to try to divert some of the money for that project to fix roads and bridges in New Jersey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schumer Criticizes Christie’s Plan to Divert Tunnel Funds', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Hudson Passenger Rail Tunnel (ARC Tunnel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'P