 where they grabbed the other Senate seat and lone Congressional seat last November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kent Conrad Will Retire From Senate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T15:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2d5ca1-0034-54f2-bfea-eec493750f50', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2d5ca1-0034-54f2-bfea-eec493750f50'}, {'abstract': 'Gordon Murray, a former investment banker who came to believe in a different form of investing and wrote a book about it, has died. He was was the subject of a Your Money column in November.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/gordon-murray-former-investment-banker-dies-at-60/', 'snippet': 'Gordon Murray, a former investment banker who came to believe in a different form of investing and wrote a book about it, has died. He was was the subject of a Your Money column in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordon Murray, the investment banker whose conversion to passive investing was the subject of my Your Money column last Nov. 26, died on Saturday at his home in Burlingame, Calif. He was 60 years old and had suffered from glioblastoma, an aggressive form of brain cancer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gordon Murray, Former Investment Banker, Dies at 60', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a482957-e179-5cf2-9a3c-88aa3187f197', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a482957-e179-5cf2-9a3c-88aa3187f197'}, {'abstract': 'A leading Tunisian blogger and activist has gone from prison to cabinet minister in less than a week.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/tunisian-blogger-joins-government/', 'snippet': 'A leading Tunisian blogger and activist has gone from prison to cabinet minister in less than a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 3:26 p.m. Less than two weeks ago, Slim Amamou, a Tunisian blogger and activist, was using his @slim404 Twitter feed to let friends know that the police had been to his house. Later the same day, after he was arrested, the 33-year-old computer programmer managed to turn his phone on and log on to Google Latitude to broadcast his location: inside the country’s feared ministry of the interior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisian Blogger Joins Government', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/47593e57-baa3-543b-a8b3-13d838dc3c32', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47593e57-baa3-543b-a8b3-13d838dc3c32'}, {'abstract': 'Judd Apatow, searching for material for his hosting gig this Saturday at the Producers Guild of America, asks his Twitter followers for jokes better than Ricky Gervais’s.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/joke-seeking-apatow-takes-to-twitter/', 'snippet': 'Judd Apatow, searching for material for his hosting gig this Saturday at the Producers Guild of America, asks his Twitter followers for jokes better than Ricky Gervais’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The comedy impresario Judd Apatow (“Knocked Up,” “40-Year-Old Virgin”), who is hosting the Producers Guild Awards on Saturday, has spent a lot of his time since the Golden Globes Sunday night soliciting material on Twitter that would be better than Ricky Gervais’s. “If anyone has any jokes that they think are better than Ricky Gervais’s, post here, and I will read the winners and say your name at P.G.A. awards,” he wrote. He then apparently stayed up until 3 a.m. on Tuesday collecting replies, including gems like “The P.G.A. Awards are so cheap even the host had to crowd-source material” and “‘Inception’ is really about Hollywood. everyone’s constantly trying to ruin your dreams so they can make a buck.” Finally: “@CreepyCreeper: @JuddApatow is the Ricky Gervais of comedy.” We have a winner. Good night.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joke-Seeking Apatow Takes to Twitter', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APATOW, JUDD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Producers Guild of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c592471e-ebe8-5daf-b4a6-a187c8b24b49', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c592471e-ebe8-5daf-b4a6-a187c8b24b49'}, {'abstract': 'As winter settles in, a peek back at a toasty day in August 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/summer-fun-day-its-finally-too-darn-hot/', 'snippet': 'As winter settles in, a peek back at a toasty day in August 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This article first appeared on Aug. 17, 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Fun Day | It’s (Finally) Too Darn Hot', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan and Jonathan Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3315e40-425c-5921-b366-11a142ce86a5', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3315e40-425c-5921-b366-11a142ce86a5'}, {'abstract': 'Detroit Red Wings forward Mike Modano is making a quicker recovery from hand and wrist surgery than expected.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/modano-eyes-quicker-return-than-expected/', 'snippet': 'Detroit Red Wings forward Mike Modano is making a quicker recovery from hand and wrist surgery than expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Veteran Detroit Red Wings center Mike Modano fully understands how lucky he is right now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Modano Eyes Quicker Return Than Expected', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modano, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/99eadf58-d7ab-5180-abb9-5de4ba8d33c9', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99eadf58-d7ab-5180-abb9-5de4ba8d33c9'}, {'abstract': 'Seen as nearing the end of his tenure, President Hu Jintao will emphasize common interests during his visit to the United States but may have little to offer on issues that most concern the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/asia/19hu.html', 'snippet': 'Seen as nearing the end of his tenure, President Hu Jintao will emphasize common interests during his visit to the United States but may have little to offer on issues that most concern the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — For the Obama administration, the four-day visit by President Hu Jintao of China may offer a platform to try to make progress on issues troubling their countries: currency, the trade imbalance, human rights and China’s military stance. But Mr. Hu arrives with a comparatively low-key message, intoning his favorite idea: harmony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/19hu-cnd2/19hu-cnd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/world/19hu-cnd2/19hu-cnd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/19hu-cnd2/19hu-cnd2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/19hu-cnd2/19hu-cnd2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/world/19hu-cnd2/19hu-cnd2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Leader Has Message of Harmony, but Limited Agenda', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s President Takes Message of Harmony to U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:32:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fe33eb7-a95b-5de2-adc3-088f94300288', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fe33eb7-a95b-5de2-adc3-088f94300288'}, {'abstract': 'Brett Favre, who filed retirement papers with the N.F.L. and threw a conciliatory rose to his former team, will leave the game with a complicated legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/sports/football/19leading.html', 'snippet': 'Brett Favre, who filed retirement papers with the N.F.L. and threw a conciliatory rose to his former team, will leave the game with a complicated legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might have noticed that the N.F.L. playoffs so far have been dusted with a little green and gold glitter. It’s the pixie dust that has seemed to follow the Green Bay Packers. Yes, cheese headwear is definitely fashionable again. The team is riding high after two impressive playoff victories and heads into the National Football Conference championship game in Chicago knowing the Bears really wanted to knock them out of the playoffs in the final regular-season game and couldn’t. Aaron Rodgers might be the best quarterback in the playoffs (O.K., so he really only has to beat out Ben Roethlisberger for that distinction) and for the first time in the history of Brett Favre retirements, they really don’t have to care. Nirvana! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/sports/19leading-web1/19leading-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/sports/19leading-web1/19leading-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/sports/19leading-web1/19leading-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Retiring Favre Backs the Packers', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retiring Favre Backs the Packers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Favre, Brett', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roethlisberger, Ben', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbef9e03-3859-5c30-bba6-3ca16591b11d', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbef9e03-3859-5c30-bba6-3ca16591b11d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kirshner, who guided the course of Brill Building and bubblegum pop in the 1950s and ’60s as a music publisher and promoter, and later served as an Ed Sullivan for Kiss and the Ramones as the producer and host of “Don Kirshner’s Rock Concert” on television, died on Monday in Boca Raton, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/don-kirshner-bubblegum-music-promoter-dies-at-77/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kirshner, who guided the course of Brill Building and bubblegum pop in the 1950s and ’60s as a music publisher and promoter, and later served as an Ed Sullivan for Kiss and the Ramones as the producer and host of “Don Kirshner’s Rock Concert” ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don Kirshner, who guided the course of Brill Building and bubblegum pop in the 1950s and ’60s as a music publisher and promoter, and later served as an Ed Sullivan for 1970s artists like Bruce Springsteen, Pink Floyd, Kiss and the Ramones with his weekly program “Don Kirshner’s Rock Concert” on television, died on Monday in Boca Raton, Fla. He was 76. The cause was heart failure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don Kirshner, Rock Producer and Promoter, Dies at 76', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brill Building', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/417171ba-f4f9-587a-bd65-ad771503f950', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/417171ba-f4f9-587a-bd65-ad771503f950'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Richard G. Lugar of Indiana reaffirmed his commitment Tuesday to seek re-election to a seventh term, even though he conceded that he could face “a competitive situation” in a Republican primary.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/senator-lugar-will-seek-re-election/', 'snippet': 'Senator Richard G. Lugar of Indiana reaffirmed his commitment Tuesday to seek re-election to a seventh term, even though he conceded that he could face “a competitive situation” in a Republican primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Richard G. Lugar of Indiana reaffirmed his commitment Tuesday to seek re-election to a seventh term, saying that he will not be deterred by a frustrated electorate that is intent on trying to defeat well-established Republican incumbents in their primary elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Lugar Will Seek Re-election', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/16c49d71-5d53-5cfe-8a5c-76bbfd16b4b7', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16c49d71-5d53-5cfe-8a5c-76bbfd16b4b7'}, {'abstract': 'On the second day of the fall 2011 season, critics were more feeling Tomas Maier’s conceptual use of prismatic color than the usual Italiante swagger.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/scorecard-bottega-veneta-wins/', 'snippet': 'On the second day of the fall 2011 season, critics were more feeling Tomas Maier’s conceptual use of prismatic color than the usual Italiante swagger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lime green trousers and tangerine jackets as a statement on modern man — is\xa0Scorecard in Milan or Paris? On the second day of the fall 2011 season, critics were more feeling Tomas Maier’s conceptual use of prismatic color than the usual Italiante swagger. Meanwhile, the jury’s still out on just how perverse were Miuccia Prada’s boys who sparkle in the sun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Bottega Veneta Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/def50fcc-75e2-50ff-a78d-d6ba5704c0ed', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def50fcc-75e2-50ff-a78d-d6ba5704c0ed'}, {'abstract': 'The airline reported a profit for the fourth quarter, but earnings fell short of analysts’ expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/19air.html', 'snippet': 'The airline reported a profit for the fourth quarter, but earnings fell short of analysts’ expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Delta Air Lines, the nation’s largest carrier, said Tuesday that it had a profit in the fourth quarter but warned that rising fuel prices could erase its narrow gains this year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/air/air-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delta Warns That Higher Fuel Costs Could Erase Gains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delta Warns Fuel Costs Could Erase Gains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delta Air Lines Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb1ffa5-8edb-53a9-9c1b-a96d0e58ac1e', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb1ffa5-8edb-53a9-9c1b-a96d0e58ac1e'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Joseph I. Lieberman, independent of Connecticut, is facing a challenge from the  state’s former Democratic secretary of state, Susan Bysiewicz.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/lieberman-gets-a-challenger-for-senate/', 'snippet': 'Senator Joseph I. Lieberman, independent of Connecticut, is facing a challenge from the  state’s former Democratic secretary of state, Susan Bysiewicz.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:45 p.m. | Updated Senator Joseph I. Lieberman, independent of Connecticut, will be challenged next year by the state’s former Democratic secretary of state, Susan Bysiewicz, she announced on her Facebook page on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lieberman Gets a Democratic Challenger', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b2e4a70-f697-5d3b-9983-515e5842e35a', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b2e4a70-f697-5d3b-9983-515e5842e35a'}, {'abstract': 'A play-by-play of one commuter’s journey to Times Square from Brooklyn on the F line, which has begun its new schedule for the next few months.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/notes-from-a-delayed-commute/', 'snippet': 'A play-by-play of one commuter’s journey to Times Square from Brooklyn on the F line, which has begun its new schedule for the next few months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A play-by play of one commuter’s journey to Midtown from Brooklyn on the F line, which began its newly altered weekday route to accommodate construction on the Culver Viaduct. By her estimates, she will have to budget an extra 10 to 12 minutes (weather-depending) to get to work on time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The F Line: Notes From a Delayed Commute', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justine Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/04767abb-0a28-513c-bc06-0c0fdad82cb9', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04767abb-0a28-513c-bc06-0c0fdad82cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Essex County, N.J., executive, has cultivated great influence in Trenton with a traditional political machine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/nyregion/19divincenzo.html', 'snippet': 'Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Essex County, N.J., executive, has cultivated great influence in Trenton with a traditional political machine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK \x97 Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Essex County executive, flips open his ringing cellphone and says “Hey, Gov,” raising a finger to pause an interview as he steps from the room. “We talk a lot,” he says later, grinning broadly, when asked about Chris Christie. “A lot.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/Divincenzo/Divincenzo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/Divincenzo/Divincenzo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/Divincenzo/Divincenzo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/Divincenzo/Divincenzo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/Divincenzo/Divincenzo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democratic Power Broker in New Jersey Has Governor’s Ear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democratic Power Broker in New Jersey Has Governor’s Ear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiVincenzo, Joseph N Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Essex County (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T16:48:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fda4d4c4-e866-571a-af5d-5b7e0ef5f5c9', 'word_count': 1295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fda4d4c4-e866-571a-af5d-5b7e0ef5f5c9'}, {'abstract': 'An account of what happens to a massive Detroit auto plant the year after it shuts down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/books/19book.html', 'snippet': 'An account of what happens to a massive Detroit auto plant the year after it shuts down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title and subtitle of Paul Clemens’s new book, “Punching Out: One Year in a Closing Auto Plant,” are so misleading that they nearly constitute literary fraud. If I’d paid $25.95 for it \x97 book critics get free advance copies \x97 I’d consider calling, or inventing, the Better Nonfiction Bureau. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19book/19book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19book/19book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19book/19book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Touchstone of Detroit Is Dismantled', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A