011-01-18T17:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcdbf3c9-3f5a-54b2-be90-d674243cd0ce', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcdbf3c9-3f5a-54b2-be90-d674243cd0ce'}, {'abstract': 'Root vegetables lend additional heft to this ginger-scented soup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/health/nutrition/18recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Root vegetables lend additional heft to this ginger-scented soup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Living in France, I was always impressed by the bags of mixed vegetables, called soupe, sold in farmers’ markets and supermarkets alike. The bags usually included an onion, carrots and celery, a leek, a turnip or two and a bouquet garni consisting of a bay leaf, a sprig of thyme and another of parsley. I’ve added root vegetables to this ginger-scented soup, which is inspired by the many simple suppers I enjoyed in the homes of French friends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i