rted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slackman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f275e2c9-2ae1-5eff-82b0-1cf74e3db01f', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f275e2c9-2ae1-5eff-82b0-1cf74e3db01f'}, {'abstract': '“My husband has a major birthday coming up in March. To celebrate, I would like to take him for a long weekend within about four hours’ drive from New York City.”', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/qa-romantic-inn-about-4-hours-from-new-york/', 'snippet': '“My husband has a major birthday coming up in March. To celebrate, I would like to take him for a long weekend within about four hours’ drive from New York City.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband has a major birthday coming up in March. To celebrate, I would like to take him for a long weekend within about four hours’ drive from New York City. I am looking for a romantic inn with a comfortable lounge and fireplace and good food at a rate of less than $300 a night. We prefer small places rather than large resorts. We don’t ski but would like to be close to some good hiking (providing there is not too much snow) or some interesting place to visit. Do you have any suggestions?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Romantic Inn About 4 Hours From New York', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rusha Haljuci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haljuci', 'quali