ief executive, Steven P. Jobs, announced he was taking a medical leave of absence just ahead of the release of the company’s quarterly earnings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs’s Departure Overshadows Apple Earnings Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ahead of Earnings, Apple Faces Questions About Chief’s Health', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:11:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67f5b376-cd66-5949-9447-0672000f67cd', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67f5b376-cd66-5949-9447-0672000f67cd'}, {'abstract': 'A nightclub dancer said she asked Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy for $6.7 million to keep quiet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/europe/19italy.html', 'snippet': 'A nightclub dancer said she asked Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy for $6.7 million to keep quiet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME \x97 A tabloid tidal wave washed over Italy on Tuesday as newspapers published eye-popping wiretapped conversations from a nightclub dancer who said she had dallied with Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi as a minor, but whether it would sweep the wily prime minister out to sea was still anyone’s guess. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/09/world/19italyspan-cnd/9italy-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/02/09/world/19italyspan-cnd/9italy-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/09/world/19italyspan-cnd/9italy-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/09/world/19italyspan-cnd/9italy-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/09/world/19italyspan-cnd/9italy-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wiretaps of Berlusconi’s Teenage Friend Emerge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wiretaps Fan Flames of the Berlusconi Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbbca091-e11f-548c-b1bb-bcd9fee4f2d4', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbbca091-e11f-548c-b1bb-bcd9fee4f2d4'}, {'abstract': 'The fast food purveyor, which has been increasing its focus on China and other fast-growing foreign countries, is selling the pair of domestic-focused businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/yum-puts-long-john-silvers-and-aw-on-the-block/', 'snippet': 'The fast food purveyor, which has been increasing its focus on China and other fast-growing foreign countries, is selling the pair of domestic-focused businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yum Brands, which has been prospering abroad, announced on Monday that it planned to sell a pair of domestic-focused businesses, Long John Silver’s and A&W All-American Food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yum Puts Long John Silver’s and A&W on the Block', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yum Brands Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ef98bfd-7468-5d4e-b412-9dfdb9973cb1', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ef98bfd-7468-5d4e-b412-9dfdb9973cb1'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Asimov discusses some of the wines from his tasting panel of 2008 Oregon pinot noirs.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-coming-of-age-of-oregon-pinot-noirs/', 'snippet': 'Eric Asimov discusses some of the wines from his tasting panel of 2008 Oregon pinot noirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wine panel’s tasting of 2008 pinot noirs from the Willamette Valley in Oregon was exciting. The wines were delicious, and we were all pleased to find so many of them in a lovely, restrained style that invited rather than overpowered. These, I would like to think, are the sorts of wines that inspired those far-sighted pioneers back in the late 1960s and 1970s who imagined that Willamette would be a great place to grow pinot noir.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Coming of Age of Oregon Pinot Noirs', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pinot Noir (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:26:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba79f5b-8d03-5069-b51b-8635ccea6368', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba79f5b-8d03-5069-b51b-8635ccea6368'}, {'abstract': 'A thin waif of a sandwich at the John Dory made with bottarga and butter has exercised its power of seduction on my palate.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/now-nibbling-music-to-your-mouth/', 'snippet': 'A thin waif of a sandwich at the John Dory made with bottarga and butter has exercised its power of seduction on my palate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the beginning of December, I checked out the John Dory’s new digs. It was 10 p.m. and I was meeting a good friend, who happens to be a chef, for a celebratory dinner — a three-year-long project had finally come to fruition. We were hungry, and we weren’t going to settle for anything less than excellence. We pulled up to the actual oyster bar in the back of the boisterous seafood saloon, ordered some champers and perused the menu. Under the “Snacks” heading, I read Carte da Musica. What was that? I asked my pal the chef. She didn’t know. So we interrogated one of the able shuckers manning the bivalve station in front of us. The term, he said, refers to an Italian cracker that is named for its resemblance to sheet music (i.e., carte da musica) — it’s that thin and delicate. At the John Dory, he followed up, these crackers provide the foundation for a sandwich of butter and bottarga.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Nibbling | Music to Your Mouth', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlotte Druckman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlotte', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Druckman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bc190a7-1bfd-5022-96ed-02585cb9c3e6', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bc190a7-1bfd-5022-96ed-02585cb9c3e6'}, {'abstract': 'Confederate general during the American Civil War', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0119.html', 'snippet': 'Confederate general during the American Civil War', 'lead_paragraph': "Intelligence was received last evening of the death at Lexington, Va., Of Gen. Robert E. Lee, the most famous of the officers whose celebrity was gained in the service of the Southern Confederacy during the late terrible rebellion. A report was received some days ago that he had been smitten with paralysis, but this was denied, and though it was admitted that he was seriously ill, hopes of his speedy recovery seem to have been entertained by his friends. Within the last two or three days his symptoms had taken an unfavorable turn, and he expired at 91/2 o'clock yesterday morning of congestion of the brain, at the age of sixty-three years, eight months and twenty-three days. ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gen. Robert E. Lee', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e32a589f-92ff-5972-a79a-46f35920bd94', 'word_count': 1442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e32a589f-92ff-5972-a79a-46f35920bd94'}, {'abstract': 'Oprah Winfrey proved to be ratings draw on Monday for Piers Morgan’s debut on CNN.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/strong-ratings-for-piers-morgans-debut/', 'snippet': 'Oprah Winfrey proved to be ratings draw on Monday for Piers Morgan’s debut on CNN.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CNN’s “Piers Morgan Tonight” premiered to 2.1 million viewers on Monday, according to preliminary ratings from the Nielsen Company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Ratings for Piers Morgan’s Debut', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Piers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cable News Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:38:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0deb391-ef80-5023-9735-80333e3d59d7', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0deb391-ef80-5023-9735-80333e3d59d7'}, {'abstract': 'the Italian film director', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0120.html', 'snippet': 'the Italian film director', 'lead_paragraph': ' Federico Fellini, whose deeply personal films were vivid, sometimes bizarre portraits of the human condition, died yesterday at the Umberto I Hospital in Rome. He was 73.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federico Fellini, Film Visionary, Is Dead at 73', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By PETER B. FLINT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2552a547-dea5-5203-a081-06e613b1be31', 'word_count': 2631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2552a547-dea5-5203-a081-06e613b1be31'}, {'abstract': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">FREEZE SET ON HIRING</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\nCalifornian Stresses Need To Restrict Government and Buoy Economy\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/big/0120.html', 'snippet': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">FREEZE SET ON HIRING</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\nCalifornian Stresses Need To Restrict Government and Buoy Economy\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington, Jan. 20 -- Ronald Wilson Reagan of California, promising "an era of national renewal," became the 40th President of the United States today as 52 Americans held hostage in Iran were heading toward freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Reagan Takes Oath As 40th President;\nPromises An 'Era Of National Renewal' ", 'kicker': 'January 21, 1981', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': '<h5>By Steven R. Weisman </h5>\n<h5>Special to The New York Times </h5>', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/779aada2-862f-53fa-9cbc-5a9401d99bf9', 'word_count': 1512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/779aada2-862f-53fa-9cbc-5a9401d99bf9'}, {'abstract': 'More than 54 percent of investors in a new study plan to increase their contributions to hedge funds in the next 12 months, reflecting a growing confidence in money managers among public pensions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/despite-so-so-year-hedge-funds-gain-favor/', 'snippet': 'More than 54 percent of investors in a new study plan to increase their contributions to hedge funds in the next 12 months, reflecting a growing confidence in money managers among public pensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hardly chastened by a year of modest gains by hedge funds, the majority of institutional investors are planning to increase the money they allocate to them, according to a new study.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite So-So Year, Hedge Funds Gain Favor', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/013226a4-1ff3-58ea-b4aa-b7b658df9b85', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/013226a4-1ff3-58ea-b4aa-b7b658df9b85'}, {'abstract': "California's public health department introduces a new antismoking ad campaign.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/1248069571572/california-tobacco-free-campaign.html', 'snippet': "California's public health department introduces a new antismoking ad campaign.", 'lead_paragraph': "California's public health department introduces a new antismoking ad campaign.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/business/11037_1_18adnewsletter1_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/business/11037_1_18adnewsletter1_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California Tobacco-Free Campaign', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:41:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e8091e21-5233-5ef0-9f89-c6e43a1df47d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e8091e21-5233-5ef0-9f89-c6e43a1df47d'}, {'abstract': 'How polarized are we, really?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-roots-of-overheated-rhetoric/', 'snippet': 'How polarized are we, really?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along with a host of pointless arguments about Sarah Palin, the aftermath of the Arizona shootings has inspired an interesting intra-liberal debate about how polarized America really is. Noam Scheiber, of instance, watched the president’s speech last\xa0week and came away thinking that Obama underplayed the reality of Americans’ ideological divisions. “After all,” he writes, “the reason the country is so polarized is that we disagree pretty strongly about what would strengthen our democracy (say, a richer social safety net versus greater reliance on the free market and individual responsibility).”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Roots of Overheated Rhetoric', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mate