ytimes.com/2011/01/18/business/media/18adnewsletter3.html', 'snippet': 'Amp Agency, part of Alloy Media and Marketing, completed the sale of its offices in Los Angeles and New Jersey to the Bright Media Group, which will operate under the name of Bright Promotions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amp Agency, part of Alloy Media and Marketing, completed the sale of its offices in Los Angeles and New Jersey, which specialize in experiential marketing, to the Bright Media Group, which will operate under the name of Bright Promotions. Financial terms were not disclosed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebd26773-3d65-50eb-ac6a-7d8bf08f545a', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebd26773-3d65-50eb-ac6a-7d8bf08f545a'}, {'abstract': 'White Collar Watch examines the possible direction of the Securities and Exchange Commission’s inquiry into Wall Street’s dealings with sovereign wealth funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/for-wall-street-antibribery-inquiry-is-cause-for-concern/', 'snippet': 'White Collar Watch examines the possible direction of the Securities and Exchange Commission’s inquiry into Wall Street’s dealings with sovereign wealth funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission‘s inquiry into Wall Street’s dealings with sovereign wealth funds for possible violations of the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act is another expansion in the use of the antibribery law. Over the past few years, the act has been used more frequently against multinational companies, and there is no reason why financial firms should avoid scrutiny.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Wall Street, Antibribery Inquiry Is Cause for Concern', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (1977)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bab4f2bd-f7e8-5383-93a0-39f51e6805de', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bab4f2bd-f7e8-5383-93a0-39f51e6805de'}, {'abstract': 'In the Schools: For some teachers, a blog is an analyst’s divan; for others, it is the new water cooler, or the new bullhorn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/what-teachers-reveal-when-they-blog/', 'snippet': 'In the Schools: For some teachers, a blog is an analyst’s divan; for others, it is the new water cooler, or the new bullhorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she started a blog, she saw it as a venue to chronicle her daily dealings as a teacher, a kind of diary with no lock and key. She settled on a pseudonym, Miss Brave, “because when I tell people I teach in a New York City public elementary schools, many of them say, ‘Whoa, you’re brave,’ ” she explains on her site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Teachers Reveal When They Blog', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1859b13-2a09-5ee3-80f4-634f221fd23d', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1859b13-2a09-5ee3-80f4-634f221fd23d'}, {'abstract': 'Directors, writers and actors are honored.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/theater-hall-of-fame-names-new-members/', 'snippet': 'Directors, writers and actors are honored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Theater Hall of Fame, which this year is celebrating its 40th anniversary honoring lifetime achievement in American theater, has announced its new inductees. They are the directors Michael Blakemore, musical director Paul Gemignani, the playwright Caryl Churchill, the actors Linda Lavin, Brian Dennehy and Fritz Weaver, the director and librettist James Lapine and, posthumously, the director and writer Joseph Chaikin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Hall of Fame Names New Members', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaikin, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Churchill, Caryl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dennehy, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gemignani, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapine, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavin, Linda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindstrom, Pia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weaver, Fritz', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gershwin Theater', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater Hall of Fame', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T18:57:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d2d8ea-ebad-5a1a-b8e1-31e8cec33c6b', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d2d8ea-ebad-5a1a-b8e1-31e8cec33c6b'}, {'abstract': 'The buyout giant led by Stephen Schwarzman has signed up for the 140-character-limit messaging service.  But will its gregarious leader will make an appearance?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/blackstone-joins-the-twitter-age/', 'snippet': 'The buyout giant led by Stephen Schwarzman has signed up for the 140-character-limit messaging service.  But will its gregarious leader will make an appearance?', 'lead_para