ne}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5a7512de-d705-50c1-adca-f59af0a732b6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5a7512de-d705-50c1-adca-f59af0a732b6'}, {'abstract': 'This season, Karl Lagerfeld was inspired by Mademoiselle Chanel’s Gripox jewelry, making its way to fifth-century Byzantium by way of swinging London.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/just-one-look-chanel-metier-darts-collection/', 'snippet': 'This season, Karl Lagerfeld was inspired by Mademoiselle Chanel’s Gripox jewelry, making its way to fifth-century Byzantium by way of swinging London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pre-Fall Collections, being shown in New York over the next several weeks, arrive in stores in May to fill the gap between bikinis and furs.For some years now, Karl Lagerfeld has taken pre-fall as an opportunity to keep all of the petits mains of Paris busy. His Métier d’Arts Collection showcases the talents of embroiderers and makers of feathers and lace and buttons and bows and trims — occasionally all in a single look. This season took, as its leaping-off point, Mademoiselle Chanel’s Gripox jewelry, making its way to fifth-century Byzantium by way of swinging London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Chanel Métier d’Arts Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e8e16b7-3ad3-5f64-87b6-73ed335cdebc', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e8e16b7-3ad3-5f64-87b6-73ed335cdebc'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity owned bank ramped up its plans for an initial public offering, saying it could raise $630 million — more than double what the bank expected when it first filed to go public last year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/bankunited-boosts-i-p-o-plans/', 'snippet': 'The private equity owned bank ramped up its plans for an initial public offering, saying it could raise $630 million — more than double what the bank expected when it first filed to go public last year.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:14 p.m. | Updated BankUnited on Tuesday ramped up its plans for an initial public offering, saying it could raise $630 million – more than double what the bank expected when it first filed for an I.P.O. last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BankUnited Increases Plans for I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Wilbur L Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BankUnited', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackstone Group, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f8783cd-1c8c-570c-a325-510c4825df5d', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f8783cd-1c8c-570c-a325-510c4825df5d'}, {'abstract': 'A critique of new White House efforts to foster the integrity and communication of science.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/a-look-at-white-house-views-on-scientific-integrity/', 'snippet': 'A critique of new White House efforts to foster the integrity and communication of science.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph A. Davis, a freelance writer who among many things edits the Society of Environmental Journalists daily roundup of environmental stories, has completed a detailed four-part examination of White House Scientific Integrity Guidelines issued by President Obama’s science adviser, John Holdren, in December.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at White House Views on Scientific Integrity', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Management and Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/910aed79-dca4-5688-b4f2-9759f4e8ed6e', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/910aed79-dca4-5688-b4f2-9759f4e8ed6e'}, {'abstract': 'Slide show: A series of reader-submitted photos taken during July’s heat wave.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/summer-fun-day-from-one-extreme-to-the-other/', 'snippet': 'Slide show: A series of reader-submitted photos taken during July’s heat wave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While you’re dodging foot-deep slush puddles and running from the gray icy spray of buses and cars, we bring you reader-submitted images from July, when normally sane New Yorkers and their pets were lulled into submission by the heat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Fun Day | From One Extreme to the Other', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/994a5c36-1838-50b2-a373-d6bfdca81715', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/994a5c36-1838-50b2-a373-d6bfdca81715'}, {'abstract': 'Down Goes Brown has tips for the N.H.L. All-Star captains as they prepare to draft their teams.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/tips-for-drafting-your-all-star-team/', 'snippet': 'Down Goes Brown has tips for the N.H.L. All-Star captains as they prepare to draft their teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. All-Stars have been announced, and the team captains will be named this week. That means we’re closing in on the first ever All-Star Fantasy Draft, in which the 42 players will be divided up with a school-yard style draft.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips for Drafting Your All-Star Team', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hoc