europe/19russia.html', 'snippet': 'A top official for the Russian Orthodox Church lashed out at women who leave the house “painted like a clown” and “confuse the street with striptease.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW \x97 A top official for the Russian Orthodox Church on Tuesday proposed creating an “all-Russian dress code,” lashing out at women who leave the house “painted like a clown” and “confuse the street with striptease.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dress Code For Russians? Priest Chides Skimpiness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dress Code For Russians? Priest Chides Skimpiness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Orthodox Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:32:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50f8f889-ab13-57eb-975d-8a0d00ce53ce', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50f8f889-ab13-57eb-975d-8a0d00ce53ce'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Etheridge will take over the role from Feb. 1-6, in between Billie Joe Armstrong’s appearances Jan. 18-30 and Feb. 10-27.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/her-name-is-jimmy-melissa-etheridge-will-join-american-idiot-cast-for-one-week/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Etheridge will take over the role from Feb. 1-6, in between Billie Joe Armstrong’s appearances Jan. 18-30 and Feb. 10-27.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Broadway musical “American Idiot,” the character of St. Jimmy is a wild force of nature who thrashes around the stage like an adrenaline-charged rock star — which is partly why the role has suited Billie Joe Armstrong, the front man of the punk rock band Green Day, who is playing the part off and on this winter (and whose band’s music provides the show’s score). Now the producers are going to give another rocker a try at St. Jimmy: Melissa Etheridge will take over the role for one week, Feb. 1 to 6, in between Mr. Armstrong’s appearances Tuesday to Jan. 30 and Feb. 10 to 27.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Name Is Jimmy: Melissa Etheridge Will Join ‘American Idiot’ Cast For One Week', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Etheridge, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5ad6a8d-0186-5c4c-a6d4-1e3c88682e41', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5ad6a8d-0186-5c4c-a6d4-1e3c88682e41'}, {'abstract': 'Bad for the periphery.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/european-inflation-targets/', 'snippet': 'Bad for the periphery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jean-Claude Trichet is sounding hawkish about inflation again — and this is very bad news for the European periphery. Let me offer a stylized example to explain why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Inflation Targets', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1758fb6a-f620-56c2-bb9d-8968155fee3e', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1758fb6a-f620-56c2-bb9d-8968155fee3e'}, {'abstract': 'The Absolut vodka brand returns as a presenting sponsor for the third season of “RuPaul’s Drag Race,” as advertisers increasingly customize content for shows on individual cable channels.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/sponsorship-of-this-series-is-no-drag/', 'snippet': 'The Absolut vodka brand returns as a presenting sponsor for the third season of “RuPaul’s Drag Race,” as advertisers increasingly customize content for shows on individual cable channels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the television audience continues to fragment, more cable channels are being created. Or is it that as more cable channels are introduced, the viewing audience continues to fragment? Either way, it is a trend that Madison Avenue is taking part in more frequently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sponsorship of This Series Is No ‘Drag’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RuPaul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABSOLUT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2