ogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/first-trade-center-officers-will-be-in-place-soon/', 'snippet': 'In a State of the N.Y.P.D. speech, Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly discussed the department’s plans to secure the World Trade Center area with a command that will eventually grow to 673 officers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first wave of officers from a new World Trade Center command will be in place by the opening of the site’s memorial on Sept. 11, 2011, Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly said on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Trade Center Officers Will Be in Place Soon', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Police Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0394d145-e285-5c46-9a5a-2220f2f32ff7', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0394d145-e285-5c46-9a5a-2220f2f32ff7'}, {'abstract': 'The company argues that regulators incorrectly interpreted data on use of the drug to treat breast cancer, and it wants the F.D.A. to rescind its decision to revoke approval.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/genentech-appeals-avastin-decision/', 'snippet': 'The company argues that regulators incorrectly interpreted data on use of the drug to treat breast cancer, and it wants the F.D.A. to rescind its decision to revoke approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Genentech on Tuesday formally asked the Food and Drug Administration to overturn last month’s decision revoking the approval of the drug Avastin as a treatment for breast cancer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genentech Appeals Avastin Decision', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avastin (Drug)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genentech Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T19:58:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/26b04b82-f289-5b09-b15a-e781cd8afc60', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26b04b82-f289-5b09-b15a-e781cd8afc60'}, {'abstract': 'Alexandre Desplat recorded the score for “The King’s Speech” at the famed studio used by the Beatles, where a special microphone was found.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-king-at-abbey-road/', 'snippet': 'Alexandre Desplat recorded the score for “The King’s Speech” at the famed studio used by the Beatles, where a special microphone was found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— Among the many Britishisms honored with a Bafta nod today was the score for “The King’s Speech.” Of course, the composer, Alexandre Desplat, is French, but let’s not dwell on that. Mr. Desplat -– a veteran of creating music for award-season movies, including “The Curious Case of Benjamin Button,” “The Ghost Writer,” “Fantastic Mr. Fox,” “Julie & Julia,” and many others –- recorded the score for the Colin Firth vehicle at Abbey Road studios in London, he told the Bagger the other day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘King’ at Abbey Road', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Firth, Colin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eb238e6-b885-5fb6-be8b-f9d21c13b531', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eb238e6-b885-5fb6-be8b-f9d21c13b531'}, {'abstract': 'Term for anti-government protests in Tunisia; Jasmine is the country’s national flower.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/jasmine-revolt/', 'snippet': 'Term for anti-government protests in Tunisia; Jasmine is the country’s national flower.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Term for anti-government protests in Tunisia; Jasmine is the country’s national flower. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jasmine Revolt', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c05f348-2c28-5dc1-a777-e0dd6000f387', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c05f348-2c28-5dc1-a777-e0dd6000f387'}, {'abstract': '“Wicked” regains number one at Broadway box office in otherwise slow week', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/the-witch-is-alive-wicked-regains-top-spot-as-broadway-box-office-sputters/', 'snippet': '“Wicked” regains number one at Broadway box office in otherwise slow week', 'lead_paragraph': 'The winter doldrums have arrived at most of Broadway’s box offices, as they usually do this time of year. Many musicals and plays had swaths of empty seats last week, and 19 of the theater district’s 40 houses were dark because of shows closing or being on hiatus. Broadway productions grossed a total of $14.9 million last week, compared with $20.8 million the week before and $17.6 million for the comparable week in January 2010. The slowdown in ticket sales traditionally sets in mid-January, with the end of holiday vacations and the resumption of school, and often lasts until the advent of spring vacations and new productions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Witch Is Alive! ‘Wicked’ Regains Top Spot As Broadway Box Office Sputters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc123827-b0d8-59ae-8269-05f56ec2bbf6', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc123827-b0d8-59ae-8269-05f56ec2bbf6'}, {'abstract': 'Tips for safeguarding sensitive year-end and tax-related mail.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/protecting-mail-from-identity-thieves/', 'snippet': 'Tips for safeguarding sensitive year-end and tax-related mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As employers and banks mail out your year-end and tax documents this month, you shouldn’t just be thinking about preparing your taxes. You should also be thinking about how to protect your mail from identity thieves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protecting Mail From Identity Thieves', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Fraud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/be875d3b-db88-5a51-8721-c4476bedec08', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be875d3b-db88-5a51-8721-c4476bedec08'}, {'abstract': 'A photo shoot with Kwong, the sometime fashion blogger and Elite model, by Elle Muliarchyk is fittingly baroque.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/girl-on-bear-rug-lily-kwong-c-2011/', 'snippet': 'A photo shoot with Kwong, the sometime fashion blogger and Elite model, by Elle Muliarchyk is fittingly baroque.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#371", 592, 490, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Girl on Bear Rug,’ (Lily Kwong, c. 2011)', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Horacio Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Horacio', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc173f5-5a76-5876-a94f-7916982f89c8', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc173f5-5a76-5876-a94f-7916982f89c8'}, {'abstract': 'The twisted skeleton of an old pier on the Hudson River, around 64th Street, was removed over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/remnants-of-an-industrial-past-now-gone/', 'snippet': 'The twisted skeleton of an old pier on the Hudson River, around 64th Street, was removed over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:44 p.m. | Updated Many New Yorkers are attached to their city’s gritty industrial past, especially when it is juxtaposed with newer gleaming luxury structures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remnant of an Industrial Past, Now Gone', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3230dc9-dff6-575d-9168-b0dc3fd98c2f', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3230dc9-dff6-575d-9168-b0dc3fd98c2f'}, {'abstract': 'The first game of the match between David Nalbandian and Lleyton Hewitt foreshadowed what would unfold over the next 4 hours 48 minutes of this gorgeous, gutsy first-round match.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/analysis-nalbandian-survives-hewitt/', 'snippet': 'The first game of the match between David Nalbandian and Lleyton Hewitt foreshadowed what would unfold over the next 4 hours 48 minutes of this gorgeous, gutsy first-round match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first game of the match between David Nalbandian and Lleyton Hewitt foreshadowed what would unfold over the next 4 hours 48 minutes of this gorgeous, gutsy first-round match. With Nalbandian serving, Hewitt played with brio to gain four break points. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: Nalbandian Survives Hewitt', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hewitt, Lleyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nalbandian, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/778584bd-23a0-5193-9af8-fe5a626801c1', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/778584bd-23a0-5193-9af8-fe5a626801c1'}, {'abstract': 'In 1985, only seven known Maguire daisy plants were still living; today, biologists estimate that there are 163,000 in southeastern Utah.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/tiny-flower-saved-from-extinction/', 'snippet': 'In 1985, only seven known Maguire daisy plants were still living; today, biologists estimate that there are 163,000 in southeastern Utah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Maguire daisy, a dime-size wildflower found in sandstone canyons and atop mesas in Utah, was removed from the endangered species list this week after a 25-year effort to rescue it from extinction, the Interior Department said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Flower Saved from Extinction', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strickland, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/88ffb2c0-b03e-50ec-8e70-5210dc34441a', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88ffb2c0-b03e-50ec-8e70-5210dc34441a'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Department creates unit to decide how to discipline career prosecutors if they are found guilty of intentionally violating rules.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/a-step-to-deal-with-prosecutors-misconduct/', 'snippet': 'Justice Department creates unit to decide how to discipline career prosecutors if they are found guilty of intentionally violating rules.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Justice Department on Tuesday announced the creation of a unit that will decide how to discipline career officials who commit acts of prosecutorial misconduct, including whether to refer them to state bar associations for punishment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Step to Deal With Prosecutors’ Misconduct', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:32:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b60388-9818-58f2-af28-c1563bed4cbe', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b60388-9818-58f2-af28-c1563bed4cbe'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street pay is front and center again, with big banks reporting earnings. Will there be a quiet reformation of compensation? CNBC talks to Brad Hintz, a senior analyst at Sanford Bernstein.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/will-wall-street-pay-rise/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street pay is front and center again, with big banks reporting earnings. Will there be a quiet reformation of compensation? CNBC talks to Brad Hintz, a senior analyst at Sanford Bernstein.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street pay is front and center again, with big banks reporting earnings this week. Will there be a quiet reformation of compensation? The pool at Goldman Sachs, which reports results on Wednesday, is likely to be up, although pay per employee could be down. CNBC talks to Brad Hintz, a senior analyst at Sanford Bernstein.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Pay May Rise, by One Measure', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Sanford', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNBC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:33:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeaa0c85-9fa4-51d8-be34-788f377f721b', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeaa0c85-9fa4-51d8-be34-788f377f721b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rogovin took up photography as a way to champion the underprivileged and went on to become one of America’s leading social documentarians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/arts/design/19rogovin.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rogovin took up photography as a way to champion the underprivileged and went on to become one of America’s leading social documentarians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milton Rogovin, an optometrist and persecuted leftist who took up photography as a way to champion the underprivileged and went on to become one of America’s most dedicated social documentarians, died on Tuesday at his home in Buffalo. He was 101.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19rogovin/19rogovin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19rogovin/19rogovin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/19rogovin/19ro