'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/247257b5-728e-536c-adee-386426ba1361', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247257b5-728e-536c-adee-386426ba1361'}, {'abstract': 'Dinara Safina’s 44-minute loss to Kim Clijsters was another sad chapter in the decline of her career.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/safina-in-free-fall-shows-little-fight-in-loss/', 'snippet': 'Dinara Safina’s 44-minute loss to Kim Clijsters was another sad chapter in the decline of her career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not getting a single game in a match is called a “bicicleta” in Spain, and a “double bagel” in English-speaking countries. Whatever you want to call it, Dinara Safina’s 44-minute loss to Kim Clijsters was another sad chapter in her decline. Her brother Marat (they are the first brother and sister to be ranked No. 1 in the world) also failed to live up to his potential. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safina, in Free Fall, Shows Little Fight in Loss', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/138728e7-6ec0-5619-9fd6-24d579529993', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/138728e7-6ec0-5619-9fd6-24d579529993'}, {'abstract': 'A new online tool pits dealers against each other to compete for a customer’s business, but as the author learned, the deal might still require old-fashioned haggling.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/carwoo-demystifying-the-art-of-the-deal/', 'snippet': 'A new online tool pits dealers against each other to compete for a customer’s business, but as the author learned, the deal might still require old-fashioned haggling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those starting the new year looking for a new car, an online service proposes to remove hassles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CarWoo: Demystifying the Art of the Deal', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:52:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/be4590a2-61ae-5902-9cbf-6cdc55ffd761', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be4590a2-61ae-5902-9cbf-6cdc55ffd761'}, {'abstract': 'The sad truth is that until relatively recent decades, women have had severely limited opportunities within all the arts, especially music and, even more, composition.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/top-10-composers-the-female-factor/', 'snippet': 'The sad truth is that until relatively recent decades, women have had severely limited opportunities within all the arts, especially music and, even more, composition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Tommasini has been exploring the qualities that make a classical composer great, maybe even the best of all time. Watch videos and vote for your own top 10 here and read previous posts here and share your thoughts in the comments field. Mr. Tommasini’s final list will be posted on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Composers: The Female Factor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T20:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c39aba5-12a4-5a86-b765-5e429c6dcd65', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c39aba5-12a4-5a86-b765-5e429c6dcd65'}, {'abstract': 'Arias brought his remarkably feminine, deftly honed vocals to a lineup of covers that spanned several decades at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/notes-from-the-underground-joey-arias-in-concert/', 'snippet': 'Arias brought his remarkably feminine, deftly honed vocals to a lineup of covers that spanned several decades at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last October, “Joey Arias in Concert” played to sold-out audiences at the Abrons Arts Center. This past week, Arias gave a one-night-only repeat performance at Le Poisson Rouge. The downtown legend glided across the stage in impossibly high heels, opening with his now infamous Billie Holiday number, followed by a lineup of covers that spanned several decades. In between songs, Arias’s mix of remarkably feminine, deftly honed vocals and raspy trash talk set the tone for two costume changes — one involving full lingerie. An adoring crowd fueled him with vodka shots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Joey Arias in Concert', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T21:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e519157-8198-5c27-a746-fd1ed35109c2', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e519157-8198-5c27-a746-fd1ed35109c2'}, {'abstract': 'For $250,000, a British vintage-motorcycle enthusiast would craft an exacting copy of the bike famously favored by Lawrence of Arabia.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/replicating-the-brough-superior/', 'snippet': 'For $250,000, a British vintage-motorcycle enthusiast would craft an exacting copy of the bike famously favored by Lawrence of Arabia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was “a miracle that all this docile strength waits behind one tiny lever for the pleasure of my hand,” wrote T.E. Lawrence, better known as Lawrence of Arabia, in praise of his Brough Superior motorcycle in the mid-1920s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Replicating the Brough Superior', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, T E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T21:02:24+0000'