, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/regulatory/regulatory-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/regulatory/regulatory-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/business/regulatory/regulatory-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Asks for Review of Rules Stifling Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Asks For Review Of Rules Stifling Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T21:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bae5b893-970f-5c30-bb05-f348277af21e', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bae5b893-970f-5c30-bb05-f348277af21e'}, {'abstract': 'State of the Nation, State of the State, State of the City and now… State of the Block: yours.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/tell-us-the-state-of-your-block/', 'snippet': 'State of the Nation, State of the State, State of the City and now… State of the Block: yours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president gives the State of the Union, the governor the State of the State and, on Wednesday, the mayor will deliver the State of the City. These addresses tend to follow a similar outline. The official in question lists recent accomplishments, outlines future challenges, and implores everyone — invariably, and often with brow furrowed — to do more with less. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us the State of Your Block', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the City Message (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T21:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/92520b63-05bf-5cda-959d-2c95cfe52497', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92520b63-05bf-5cda-959d-2c95cfe52497'}, {'abstract': 'Heading toward bankruptcy, First Quality Music of Louisville, Ky., shakes things up by spending money it wasn’t sure it had.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/deciding-to-hire-a-170000-consultant/', 'snippet': 'Heading toward bankruptcy, First Quality Music of Louisville, Ky., shakes things up by spending money it wasn’t sure it had.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, we published a case study about the challenges facing First Quality Music, a family-owned supplier of stringed musical instruments, including guitars and mandolins, along with parts and accessories. Founded in 1970 in Louisville, Ky., the nine-employee company also makes its own banjos as well as game calls for hunters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'