nytimes.com/2011/01/19/health/research/19pfizer.html', 'snippet': 'The deal, worth up to $632 million, is part of Pfizer’s effort to keep up with rivals that are increasingly relying on biotechnology for products and profits.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Pfizer, the world’s largest drug company, has agreed to pay up to $632 million to Theraclone Sciences in a research collaboration on antibody drugs for cancer and infectious disease, the companies said Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pfizer in Deal With Theraclone for Antibody Drug Research', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pfizer in Deal With Theraclone for Antibody Drug Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pfizer Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T22:09:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duff Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f43363a6-c642-565b-8e82-029047f06595', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f43363a6-c642-565b-8e82-029047f06595'}, {'abstract': 'The Association of American Physicians and Surgeons has been vocal in the country’s health care debate, and other groups assert that its positions are outside the mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/19physicians.html', 'snippet': 'The Association of American Physicians and Surgeons has been vocal in the country’s health care debate, and other groups assert that its positions are outside the mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A small professional group of doctors involved in the effort to repeal the new health care law has a history of opposing government involvement in medicine, including challenging President Bill Clinton’s attempts to overhaul health care in the 1990s. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/sub-Physicians-Refer/sub-Physicians-Refer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/business/sub-Physicians-Refer/sub-Physicians-Refer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/sub-Physicians-Refer/sub-Physicians-Refer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vocal Physicians Group Renews Health Law Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vocal Physicians Group Renews Health Law Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T22:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9002be2f-6d8e-564d-bcc2-5ef824c8a8ae', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9002be2f-6d8e-564d-bcc2-5ef824c8a8ae'}, {'abstract': 'The design team at Mulberry trotted out to the English countryside for inspiration and returned to breathe some fresh air into ’70s-era classics.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/just-one-look-mulberry-pre-fall-collection/', 'snippet': 'The design team at Mulberry trotted out to the English countryside for inspiration and returned to breathe some fresh air into ’70s-era classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pre-Fall Collections, being shown in New York over the next several weeks, arrive in stores in May to fill the gap between bikinis and furs.The design team at Mulberry trotted out to the English countryside for inspiration and returned to breathe some fresh air into ’70s-era classics. The showroom, which was decked out for the occasion as an enchanted forest, provided a lively backdrop for snug jackets and kicky skirts in indigo denim and Prince of Wales check as well as blouses and dresses in new prints like “rumpled roses” and “feathered friends.” The total look was polished off, natch, with a new lineup of bags, including Taylor (shown here).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Mulberry Pre-Fall Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T22:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3e7321-288e-5323-9c9d-4b9fded9f65e', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3e7321-288e-5323-9c9d-4b9fded9f65e'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Carolyn McCarthy of New York said Tuesday she would introduce a bill next week that would ban high-capacity ammunition magazines.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/mccarthy-will-introduce-bill-to-limit-ammunition-clips/', 'snippet': 'Representative Carolyn McCarthy of New York said Tuesday she would introduce a bill next week that would ban high-capacity ammunition magazines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seizing on the shooting in Arizona that killed six and critically injured Representative Gabrielle Giffords, Representative Carolyn McCarthy of New York, a long-time gun control advocate, said Tuesday she would introduce a bill next week that would ban high-capacity ammunition magazines. The bill would be carried in the Senate by Senator Frank Lautenberg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McCarthy Will Introduce Bill to Limit Ammunition Clips', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T22:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/335ac789-4b50-56a0-9118-95c6ec3b7b80', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/335ac789-4b50-56a0-9118-95c6ec3b7b80'}, {'abstract': 'Flavio Mendez Santiago helped start one of Mexico’s most notorious criminal organizations, Los Zetas, which acted as an enforcer for the Gulf Cartel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/americas/19mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Flavio Mendez Santiago helped start one of Mexico’s most notorious criminal organizations, Los Zetas, which acted as an enforcer for the Gulf Cartel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY \x97 A man who helped start one of Mexico’s most notorious criminal organizations has been arrested, adding to the list of high-profile kingpins the police and the military have arrested or killed in the past year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexican Gang Kingpin Arrested', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexican Gang Kingpin Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zetas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T22:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/383bbff7-33dc-5c28-9514-d4b153db4645', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/383bbff7-33dc-5c28-9514-d4b153db4645'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Joseph I. Lieberman, who is deeply unpopular among Democrats in Connecticut, has decided not to run for a fifth term.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/lieberman-will-not-run-for-re-election/', 'snippet': 'Senator Joseph I. Lieberman, who is deeply unpopular among Democrats in Connecticut, has decided not to run for a fifth term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Joseph I. Lieberman will announce on Wednesday that he will not seek a fifth term, accordi