 Jets?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/stop-the-jets/', 'snippet': 'The stock market has always gone up after the Steelers, Packers or Bears won the Super Bowl. But it fell after the Jets won in 1969. Why would any investor root for the Jets?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of New York is going crazy over the New York Jets. (If you haven’t followed football, they have scored two playoff upsets and will go to the Super Bowl if they come up with another one in Pittsburgh this Sunday.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop the Jets', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T23:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ee00711-b6ea-53af-8431-3920f0a9ffd6', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ee00711-b6ea-53af-8431-3920f0a9ffd6'}, {'abstract': 'The stock market has always gone up after the Steelers, Packers or Bears won the Super Bowl. But it fell after the Jets won in 1969. Why would any investor root for the Jets?', 'web_url': 'https://norris.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/stop-the-jets/', 'snippet': 'The stock market has always gone up after the Steelers, Packers or Bears won the Super Bowl. But it fell after the Jets won in 1969. Why would any investor root for the Jets?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of New York is going crazy over the New York Jets. (If you haven’t followed f