 “Zenith,” a self-described “retro-futuristic steampunk thriller,” can make you feel like the confused hero of “Memento” — that is, someone unable to form new memories. Skittering back and forth between two time periods and a small group of nut cases, this bewildering collision of noir narration and purple paranoia may be long on atmosphere but is woefully short on sense.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/sub-zenith/sub-zenith-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/sub-zenith/sub-zenith-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/sub-zenith/sub-zenith-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/sub-zenith/sub-zenith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/arts/sub-zenith/sub-zenith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Dad Left a Conspiracy; You’re Invited to the Hunt', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Zenith'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Dad Left a Conspiracy; You’re Invited to the Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-18T23:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, '