aken over the former Honmura An space. The sushi chef, Hiro Sawatari, above, an alumnus of the much-esteemed Sushi Yasuda, will name the source for each seafood species on the menu. In the interest of conservation, he will not serve bluefin tuna, but will offer a sustainable omakase menu. James London and Marina Schulze are in the kitchen preparing more-substantial fare that depends on Japanese ingredients but sometimes takes a Western approach, like short ribs braised with a mustard glaze in a beef jerky dashi, and octopus seared on a plancha with watermelon radish. Cobi Levy is an owner along with, among other partners, the chef Josh DeChellis. (Opens Monday): 170 Mercer Street (Houston Street), (212) 991-5650.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/OFF-1/OFF-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/OFF-1/OFF-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/OFF-1/SUBOFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/OFF-1/SUBOFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/OFF-1/SUBOFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'OFF THE MENU', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T00:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 