essed to where someone is now selling a gourmet version of the Chia Pet? ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/PETSALAD/PETSALAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 613, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/PETSALAD/PETSALAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/dining/PETSALAD/PETSALAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pet Salad With That Mouse?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Salad With That Mouse?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T00:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce295799-487e-57bd-bb95-8770b2be16e6', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce295799-487e-57bd-bb95-8770b2be16e6'}, {'abstract': 'Artists and admirers share their memories of Ellen Stewart, founder of La MaMa Experimental Theater Club and pioneer of Off Off Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/theater/23stewart.html', 'snippet': 'Artists and admirers share their memories of Ellen Stewart, founder of La MaMa Experimental Theater Club and pioneer of Off Off Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ELLEN STEWART, who died on Jan. 13, was in her early 40s when she founded La MaMa Experimental Theater Club in 1962. At an age when some people settle into complacency, she built one of New York’s most influential cultural institutions. Half a century and more than 3,000 productions later, she leaves behind a legacy that includes pioneering the Off Off Broadway movement, importing international theater work before it was popular, and providing a home in the East Village for experimentation. While an era has ended, her theater and its vast population of artists and admirers carry on. A few of them were asked by Jason Zinoman to recall the woman known as Mama. Here are excerpts from their responses. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/STEWART-1/STEWART-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/STEWART-1/STEWART-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/STEWART-1/STEWART-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/STEWART-1/STEWART-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/STEWART-1/STEWART-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Downtown’s Pioneering Stage Mama', 'kicker': None, 'content_ki