sponse to the deadly landslides in the state of Rio de Janeiro last week that killed at least 710 people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil to Step Up Plans for Disaster Preparedness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil to Step Up Plans For Disaster Preparedness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T00:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55f9a2a3-1ccb-592e-9422-32365cc45ac0', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55f9a2a3-1ccb-592e-9422-32365cc45ac0'}, {'abstract': 'The sixth version of the firm’s plan for a public stock offering contains signs buried in its 1,000-plus pages that should encourage prospective investors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/19views.html', 'snippet': 'The sixth version of the firm’s plan for a public stock offering contains signs buried in its 1,000-plus pages that should encourage prospective investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apollo Global Management’s I.P.O. plans have aged well. Last week, Apollo, Leon D. Black’s buyout shop, filed the sixth iteration of its prospectus, three years after the first. The latest version contains signs buried in its 1,000-plus pages that should encourage prospective investors. Apollo looks ready to move from the dark corners of a private Goldman Sachs exchange, where it trades at a steep discount, to the public market’s bright lights.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Promise for Apollo in New Prospectus', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Promise for Apollo in New Prospectus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackstone Group, The', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPRAISALS AND VALUATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T00:58:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By LISA LEE, JEFFREY GOLDFARB and ANTONY CURRIE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LEE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GOLDFARB', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CURRIE', 'qualifier': No