/hockey-as-you-have-never-seen-it/', 'snippet': 'To mark the 40th anniversary of the Buffalo Sabres, the club and the Albright-Knox Art Gallery in Buffalo mounted “Forty: The Sabres in the N.H.L.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To mark the 40th anniversary of the Buffalo Sabres, the club and the Albright-Knox Art Gallery in Buffalo mounted “Forty: The Sabres in the N.H.L.,” a special exhibition that ran from Nov. 7 to Jan. 9.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hockey as You Have Never Seen It', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Sabres', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T01:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/267d72d8-923b-5383-aab9-3049fe56ecb1', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/267d72d8-923b-5383-aab9-3049fe56ecb1'}, {'abstract': 'The Lebanese crisis is another episode in which the United States has watched as events unfold beyond its control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/middleeast/19lebanon.html', 'snippet': 'The Lebanese crisis is another episode in which the United States has watched as events unfold beyond its control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon \x97 In Lebanon’s worst crisis in years, whose resolution may determine whether Hezbollah controls a government allied with the United States, American diplomacy has become the butt of jokes here. Once a decisive player here, Saudi Arabia has all but given up. In their stead is Turkey, which has sought to mediate a crisis that, given events on Tuesday in Beirut’s streets, threatens to turn violent before it is resolved.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lebanon Shows Shift of Influence in Mideast', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crisis in Lebanon Exemplifies Waning Influence of U.S. and Its Allies in Mideast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T01:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/8375baed-1276-53fe-8cf6-acf6920b8c67', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8375baed-1276-53fe-8cf6-acf6920b8c67'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,425 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,425 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Department of Defense has identified 4,425 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '