': 'nyt://article/aacec007-5d21-5328-8aed-b22d656a4b39'}, {'abstract': 'Video from a store security camera shows the attack on Representative Gabrielle Giffords and Judge John M. Roll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19giffords.html', 'snippet': 'Video from a store security camera shows the attack on Representative Gabrielle Giffords and Judge John M. Roll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — The chief investigator for the sheriff’s department here has for the first time publicly described the brief and gory video clip from a store security camera that shows a gunman not only shooting Representative Gabrielle Giffords just above the eyebrow at a range of three feet, but then using his 9-millimeter pistol to gun down others near her at a similarly close range.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Captured ‘Calculated’ Gunman in Tucson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '5 Seconds of Horror: Video Captured ‘Calculated’ Gunman in Tucson Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roll, John M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cffa17b5-e45c-5fce-8145-41251c86164d', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cffa17b5-e45c-5fce-8145-41251c86164d'}, {'abstract': 'After his wife took her life, Jose Ventura brought his young sons to New York from the Dominican Republic. He provides for them while working as a building superintendent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/nyregion/19neediest.html', 'snippet': 'After his wife took her life, Jose Ventura brought his young sons to New York from the Dominican Republic. He provides for them while working as a building superintendent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the time, Jose Ventura, 53, is unflappable. A building superintendent who presides over 86 apartments in Inwood, he fields calls from tenants day and night and battles for turf with gangs that sometimes leave their drugs and guns behind. Mr. Ventura also looks after his two young sons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Losing Wife, Man Becomes Cook and Caretaker to His Sons', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Losing Wife, He Becomes Cook and Caretaker to Sons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Aid Society", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11057b39-8aae-5f04-974b-f33c4e9c6a91', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11057b39-8aae-5f04-974b-f33c4e9c6a91'}, {'abstract': 'The Industrial and Commercial Bank of China celebrates an expansion in Europe and finds a willing host in France.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/frances-fetes-chinas-bank-giant/', 'snippet': 'The Industrial and Commercial Bank of China celebrates an expansion in Europe and finds a willing host in France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — As President Hu Jintao kicked off a four-day visit to Washington on Tuesday highlighting China’s rising economic might, the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China was busy flexing its muscle on the other side of the Atlantic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Fetes China’s Bank Giant', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Industrial and Commercial Bank of China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd153f54-3ea0-549e-be10-b15c2115f073', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd153f54-3ea0-549e-be10-b15c2115f073'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should consider that a safety net, fortified by stimulus, saved millions of Americans from poverty before it commits to any more slashing and burning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/opinion/19wed1.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should consider that a safety net, fortified by stimulus, saved millions of Americans from poverty before it commits to any more slashing and burning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, the first year of the Great Recession, the number of Americans living in poverty rose by 1.7 million to nearly 47.5 million. While hugely painful, that rise wasn’t surprising given the unraveling economy. What is surprising is that recent census data show that those poverty numbers held steady in 2009, even though job loss worsened significantly that year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poverty and Recovery', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poverty and Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (2009)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value':