arguing cases before the Supreme Court. The court must be careful to not give them an unfair advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/opinion/19wed2.html', 'snippet': 'Former solicitors general are increasingly going into private practice and arguing cases before the Supreme Court. The court must be careful to not give them an unfair advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Roberts court is hearing a larger share of cases about economic activities that matter to big business than the Rehnquist court before it. A recent study done by scholars for The Times documents that, compared with other Supreme Courts since 1953, this one is “significantly more likely to produce a conservative decision” in those cases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends of the Court?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends of the Court?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solicitors General', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Theodore B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/53c2fc42-9725-560e-9d9a-3de4b78e6c21', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53c2fc42-9725-560e-9d9a-3de4b78e6c21'}, {'abstract': 'With riders dressed for an arctic chill, the subway trains seemed to be carrying their own fog with them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/opinion/19wed4.html', 'snippet': 'With riders dressed for an arctic chill, the subway trains seemed to be carrying their own fog with them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been an atmospheric 24 hours in New York City. The subway trains have been running fine. But when they tunneled into their stations on Tuesday, they seemed to be carrying their own fog with them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riders in the Mist', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riders in the Mist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/777d1080-32a6-543f-97d2-a21b9b8dd55e', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/777d1080-32a6-543f-97d2-a21b9b8dd55e'}, {'abstract': 'More than 2,000 wealthy investors or companies named in Swiss banking papers released by WikiLeaks could face prosecution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/global/19tax.html', 'snippet': 'More than 2,000 wealthy investors or companies named in Swiss banking papers released by WikiLeaks could face prosecution.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The individuals and companies whose offshore account information may be detailed in Swiss banking documents disclosed to WikiLeaks could face American prosecutors \x97 or go untouched, senior tax lawyers said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Leak Consequences Depend on Details', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Leak Consequences Depend on Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations',