ctic of Russia Draw Opposition From Partners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BP’s Exploration Plans in the Arctic of Russia Draw Opposition From Partners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosneft', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer and Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f6f6d1c-ca65-52a6-9ba9-44ec8d0892f8', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f6f6d1c-ca65-52a6-9ba9-44ec8d0892f8'}, {'abstract': 'As travelers spent the night stuck in traffic in Guizhou Province, residents were happy to sell them instant noodles and other staples — at a 500 percent markup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/asia/19traffic.html', 'snippet': 'As travelers spent the night stuck in traffic in Guizhou Province, residents were happy to sell them instant noodles and other staples — at a 500 percent markup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HETAOCUN, China \x97 Compared with some of the more spectacular recent traffic jams in China, among them a 60-mile snarl last summer that paralyzed a major artery outside Beijing for two weeks, the thousands of travelers who spent the night trapped on a snow-coated highway in southwest Guizhou Province on Monday did not even warrant a mention in the local news media. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/TRAFFIC-2/TRAFFIC-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/world/TRAFFIC-2/TRAFFIC-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/TRAFFIC-2/TRAFFIC-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/TRAFFIC-2/TRAFFIC-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/world/TRAFFIC-2/TRAFFIC-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, Traffic Jam Benefits Enterprising Villagers', 'kicker': 'Hetaocun Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Traffic\nBacks Up,\nVillagers See\nOpportunity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd986f4c-29b2-5d43-8ad1-571292f5e709', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd986f4c-29b2-5d43-8ad1-571292f5e709'}, {'abstract': 'As host of the formal affair for President Hu Jintao of China, President Obama confronts tricky protocol issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/asia/19dinner.html', 'snippet': 'As host of the formal affair for President Hu Jintao of China, President Obama confronts tricky protocol issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 It has been more than 13 years since a Chinese president has been the guest of honor at the most lavish party any White House can give, a state dinner. As host of such an affair Wednesday night for his Chinese counterpart, Hu Jintao, President Obama is walking into a danger zone of protocol and international diplomacy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/world/asia/19dinner/19dinner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diplomatic Dangers Lurk in the State Dinner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diplomatic Dangers Lurk in State Dinner for Chinese Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39358740-9a3f-50f0-88a1-ffa31eab0070', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39358740-9a3f-50f0-88a1-ffa31eab0070'}, {'abstract': 'As employees become more mobile and less tied to their desks, the average amount of space per employee has been dropping, and what remains is being made more flexible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/realestate/commercial/19space.html', 'snippet': 'As employees become more mobile and less tied to their desks, the average amount of space per employee has been dropping, and what remains is being made more flexible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HILLSBORO, Ore. \x97 Intel was never one of those technology companies where employees had beanbag chairs, designer desks and pinball machines. Its offices were known for their endless rows of gray cubicles, low ceilings and fluorescent lighting. For decades it resisted any changes to its office environment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/SubSpace1/SubSpace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/19/business/SubSpace1/SubSpace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/SubSpace1/SubSpace1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/SubSpace1/SubSpace1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/business/SubSpace1/SubSpace1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Office Work Space Is Shrinking, but That’s Not All Bad', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Office Work Space Is Shrinking, but That’s Not All Bad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristina Shevory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shevory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7599310-cf68-580b-95d7-b275e21f9468', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7599310-cf68-580b-95d7-b275e21f9468'}, {'abstract': 'As President Hu Jintao visits the United States this week, China is running a 60-second video on a series of billboard-size screens on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/chinas-publicity-ads-arrive-in-times-square/', 'snippet': 'As President Hu Jintao visits the United States this week, China is running a 60-second video on a series of billboard-size screens on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China has established an extra large, extra red beachhead in Times Square. In an advertising push the state news agency Xinhua described as a “public diplomacy campaign” that coincides with President Hu Jintao’s visit to the United States this week, China is running a 60-second video on a series of billboard-size screens on Broadway. Some of the screens stay red — with Chinese characters in white — while the video is playing on the other screens with images of Chinese celebrities like the martial-arts movie star Jackie Chan; the basketball player Yao Ming; the astronaut Yang Liwei; and the pianists Lang Lang and Yundi. Xinhua said the video would be shown 15 times an hour, 20 hours a day, through Feb. 14, and on CNN through Feb. 13.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Publicity Ads Arrive in Times Square', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outdoor Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a00101e3-fd73-500f-a75f-bf79393d7414', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a00101e3-fd73-500f-a75f-bf79393d7414'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees G.M. Brian Cashman is sure to be asked why the Yankees did exactly what he said they wouldn’t by signing a free agent like Rafael Soriano.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/cashman-has-some-explaining-to-do/', 'snippet': 'Yankees G.M. Brian Cashman is sure to be asked why the Yankees did exactly what he said they wouldn’t by signing a free agent like Rafael Soriano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael Soriano will be introduced on Wednesday at Yankee Stadium as the newest member of the team and as the most expensive setup man in baseball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cashman Has Some Explaining to Do', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T02:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a3f4cdf-5b90-59d4-b58c-42af54a41945', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a3f4cdf-5b90-59d4-b58c-42af54a41945'}, {'abstract': 'Kristian House garnishes his grid generously.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/gimmick/', 'snippet': 'Kristian House garnishes his grid generously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — Good news. The theme of today’s puzzle is great, and the gimmick made me grin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Getting the Gimmick', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T03:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d21d5a-837e-5a31-a1e1-ff9b8c8c2101', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8d21d5a-837e-5a31-a1e1-ff9b8c8c2101'}, {'abstract': 'Those in a position to help often struggle with how to distinguish ominous behavior from the merely odd, the red flags from the red herrings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19mental.html', 'snippet': 'Those in a position to help often struggle with how to distinguish ominous behavior from the merely odd, the red flags from the red herrings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON —What are you supposed to do with someone like Jared L. Loughner?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/us/jp-MENTAL/jp-MENTAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Someone to Psychiatric Treatment Can Be Difficult and Inconclusive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Someone to Psychiatric Treatment Can Be Difficult and Inconclusive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murd