James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36142e95-8cfc-5036-840f-05166fe366b5', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36142e95-8cfc-5036-840f-05166fe366b5'}, {'abstract': 'The discovery in Spokane prompted law enforcement to ask march officials to change their route and several businesses to evacuate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19bomb.html', 'snippet': 'The discovery in Spokane prompted law enforcement to ask march officials to change their route and several businesses to evacuate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE \x97 A suspicious backpack found Monday along the route of a march honoring the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., in Spokane, Wash., contained a live bomb that was “likely capable of inflicting multiple casualties,” federal investigators said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Is Found in Backpack Before March Honoring King', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bomb Is Found in Backpack Before March Honoring King', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spokane (Wash)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T03:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7ef4a2-eb5b-53e4-a6ae-79a6e08594e7', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7ef4a2-eb5b-53e4-a6ae-79a6e08594e7'}, {'abstract': 'In a dispute between the government and military contractors, the Supreme Court did not seem inclined to offer guidance to lower courts about cases that invoke national security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19scotus.html', 'snippet': 'In a dispute between the government and military contractors, the Supreme Court did not seem inclined to offer guidance to lower courts about cases that invoke national security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 It has been almost 60 years since the Supreme Court last had a hard look at the state secrets privilege, which can allow the government to shut down litigation by invoking national security. In the years since the attacks on Sept. 11, 2001, the government has invoked the privilege frequently to scuttle cases, saying they would frustrate its efforts to combat terrorism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Knotty State Secrets Case, Justices Ponder Telling Litigants to ‘Go Away’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Knotty State Secrets Case, Justices Ponder Telling Litigants to ‘Go Away’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense Contracts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Dynamics Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T03:44:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fefe9e3b-856e-52f5-be7f-fb8740977d56', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fefe9e3b-856e-52f5-be7f-fb8740977d56'}, {'abstract': 'Anwar al-Awlaki, an American-born Muslim cleric believed to be hiding in Yemen, was sentenced to 10 years in prison in connection with the killing of a French citizen last October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/world/middleeast/19awlaki.html', 'snippet': 'Anwar al-Awlaki, an American-born Muslim cleric believed to be hiding in Yemen, was sentenced to 10 years in prison in connection with the killing of a French citizen last October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 A judge in Yemen sentenced the radical American-born Muslim cleric Anwar al-Awlaki in absentia on Monday to 10 years in prison on charges of incitement to murder and belonging to a terrorist group. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen Sentences American-Born Cleric in Absentia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'WORLD BRIEFING | MIDDLE EAST; Yemen: U.S.-Born Cleric Is Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T03:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '