/19/nyregion/19stevens.html', 'snippet': 'Stevens Institute of Technology, which last year settled a lawsuit brought by the state, has hired a University of Maryland official as its president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year after settling a lawsuit brought by the State of New Jersey, Stevens Institute of Technology announced Tuesday that it had named Nariman Farvardin, the provost at the University of Maryland, to be its seventh president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/STEVENS/STEVENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/STEVENS/STEVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/nyregion/STEVENS/STEVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Scrutiny by New Jersey, College Names a New Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Scrutiny by New Jersey, College Names a New Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stevens Institute of Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raveche, Harold J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T04:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2d1b167-2a6e-5ca5-9fb0-a203696a5cc7', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2d1b167-2a6e-5ca5-9fb0-a203696a5cc7'}, {'abstract': 'Can MTV, dangling a prize of a $100,000 development budget, coax students to improve the process of seeking and securing financial aid?', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/18/mtv-college-board/', 'snippet': 'Can MTV, dangling a prize of a $100,000 development budget, coax students to improve the process of seeking and securing financial aid?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One is an interactive game in which students seeking scholarships would be represented by avatars that would guide them through each step of the financial aid process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Help With Financial Aid as Reimagined by the MTV Generation', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T04:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1473bfb-98c9-516e-831f-3e0247f67838', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1473bfb-98c9-516e-831f-3e0247f67838'}, {'abstract': 'His hearing and vision compromised, Martin Greenberg learned to feel the beat of New York, as illustrated by Béatrice de Géa.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/feeling-new-york-citys-restless-pulse/', 'snippet': 'His hearing and vision compromised, Martin Greenberg learned to feel the beat of New York, as illustrated by Béatrice de Géa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he leaves home to make his way around the city, Martin Greeenberg wears a badge. It’s the simplest way to let other pedestrians know he is both deaf and blind. Mr. Greenberg, 58, is an accountant who now teaches American Sign Language classes. He was born and raised in New York City, and has fond childhood memories of the subway — rush hour and the underground lights. In his mind, the trains represented freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling New York City’s Restless Pulse', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handicapped', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald and Béatrice de Géa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Béatrice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Géa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/94656069-ed97-5e4c-ba8c-9c470cc476ae', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94656069-ed97-5e4c-ba8c-9c470cc476ae'}, {'abstract': 'The jobless rate is higher in the United States than in Britain, Germany, Japan or Russia, a new study found, pointing to American employers’ unusual degree of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/economy/19leonhardt.html', 'snippet': 'The jobless rate is higher in the United States than in Britain, Germany, Japan or Russia, a new study found, pointing to American employers’ unusual degree of power.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Alone among the world’s economic powers, the United States is suffering through a deep jobs slump that can’t be explained by the rest of the economy’s performance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/business/jp-leonhardt/jp-leonhardt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Wreckage of Lost Jobs, Lost Power', 'kicker': 'Economic Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Wreckage Of Lost Jobs, Lost Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2eca754-91cb-5684-af05-bcbf5c56d1c6', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2eca754-91cb-5684-af05-bcbf5c56d1c6'}, {'abstract': 'Conducted by the nonprofit Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, the study underlined the symbiotic role of side air bags and sound vehicle structure.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/crash-study-highlights-need-for-better-side-impact-protections/', 'snippet': 'Conducted by the nonprofit Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, the study underlined the symbiotic role of side air bags and sound vehicle structure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, in a new analysis of side-impact crashes, on Wednesday said its crash simulations showed that drivers of vehicles that received the consumer group’s Poor rating would be three times as likely to die in a similar real-world crash as drivers of vehicles that received a Good rating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crash Study Highlights Need for Better Side-Impact Protections', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a38baa0-f247-5068-a730-6000f1a56524', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a38baa0-f247-5068-a730-6000f1a56524'}, {'abstract': 'Does weight lifting make you smarter?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/phys-ed-brains-and-brawn/', 'snippet': 'Does weight lifting make you smarter?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has long been a cliché that muscle bulk doesn’t equate to intelligence. In fact, most of the science to date about activity and brain health has focused on the role of endurance exercise in improving our brain functioning. Aerobic exercise causes a steep spike in blood movement to the brain, an action that some researchers have speculated might be necessary for the creation of new brain cells, or neurogenesis. Running and other forms of aerobic exercise have been shown, in mice and men, to lead to neurogenesis in those portions of the brain associated with memory and thinking, providing another compelling reason to get out at lunchtime and run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phys Ed: Brains and Brawn', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight Lifting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7519f1a-3388-5399-a284-d1cdcc2328c6', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7519f1a-3388-5399-a284-d1cdcc2328c6'}, {'abstract': 'Somewhere in my journal, “2011” is written big and bold across an entire page. The same thing is hanging on a piece of paper on the wall of my room in New Jersey. I wrote them two years ago, signifying my goal — to represent my country in the FIFA Women’s World Cup in Germany. Also in my journal is written “2008,” the year of the last Olympics. I did not achieve that goal.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/code-words-for-2011-play-happy/', 'snippet': 'Somewhere in my journal, “2011” is written big and bold across an entire page. The same thing is hanging on a piece of paper on the wall of my room in New Jersey. I wrote them two years ago, signifying my goal — to represent my country in the FIFA...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midfielder Yael Averbuch, a Montclair, N.J., native by way of the University of North Carolina, will be contributing to the Goal blog in the runup to the third season of Women’s Professional Soccer and as the United States women’s national team prepares to the FIFA Women’s World Cup in Germany later this year. Now, she checks in from China, where the U.S. is getting ready to face Sweden on Friday in the Four Nations Tournament.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Code Words for 2011: Play Happy', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Averbuch, Yael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sundhage, Pia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael Averbuch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Averbuch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6856ee9e-116c-5fec-9816-51c4902bc42b', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6856ee9e-116c-5fec-9816-51c4902bc42b'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 72 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/word-of-the-day-diffident/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 72 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'diffident •\\ˈdi-fə-dənt, -ˌdent\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | diffident', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:03:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/33580897-487c-513c-b274-3be16007db62', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33580897-487c-513c-b274-3be16007db62'}, {'abstract': 'Is today’s unemployment structural or cyclical? Yes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/arguing-over-the-jobs-slump/', 'snippet': 'Is today’s unemployment structural or cyclical? Yes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debate in the blogosphere over the the American jobs slump — the subject of my column this week — is a disagreement about causes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arguing Over the Jobs Slump', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/da13c5d8-1752-5b4e-b51c-f97cfc7ce529', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da13c5d8-1752-5b4e-b51c-f97cfc7ce529'}, {'abstract': 'The assent carried a list of conditions, the most important aimed at preventing the new media conglomerate from thwarting competition in online video.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/business/media/19comcast.html', 'snippet': 'The assent carried a list of conditions, the most important aimed at preventing the new media conglomerate from thwarting competition in online video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comcast received government approval Tuesday to acquire NBC Universal, emerging from a lengthy review with a list of conditions, the most important aimed at preventing the new media conglomerate from thwarting competition in online video.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comcast Receives Approval for NBC Universal Merger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comcast Receives Approval For NBC Universal Merger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f558685b-6ec8-5137-a6f0-09aaf6280c0e', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f558685b-6ec8-5137-a6f0-09aaf6280c0e'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Kent Conrad of North Dakota became the first Democrat to announce he would not seek another term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/politics/19conrad.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Kent Conrad of North Dakota became the first Democrat to announce he would not seek another term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Senator Kent Conrad of North Dakota on Tuesday became the first Democrat to announce he would not run for re-election in 2012, handing Republicans an early opportunity to gain a seat in a conservative-leaning state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/us/CONRAD/CONRAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/19/us/CONRAD/CONRAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/19/us/CONRAD/CONRAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Midwest Democrat Rules Out Senate Re-election Bid in ’12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Midwest Democrat Rules Out Senate Re-election Bid in ’12', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conrad, Kent', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fd836dc-b11b-5f1d-8ef7-a2e1c711cad2', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fd836dc-b11b-5f1d-8ef7-a2e1c711cad2'}, {'abstract': 'The husband of a wounded congressman describes the confusion after her shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/giffordss-husband-heard-his-wife-had-died-in-tucson/', 'snippet': 'The husband of a wounded congressman describes the confusion after her shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While racing to his wife’s side, Mark Kelly, the husband of Rep. Gabrielle Giffords, heard from erroneous television news reports that his wife had been killed when she was shot outside of a Safeway supermarket in Tucson on Jan. 8, he said in a televised interview on Tuesday evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giffords’s Husband Heard His Wife Had Died in Tucson', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec15e641-dc46-5b33-95c9-35dc33781b5c', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec15e641-dc46-5b33-95c9-35dc33781b5c'}, {'abstract': 'Atlanta’s public school system was warned on Tuesday that it could lose accreditation this year if feuding school board members do not resolve their differences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/education/19brfs-ATLANTASCHOO_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Atlanta’s public school system was warned on Tuesday that it could lose accreditation this year if feuding school board members do not resolve their differences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Atlanta’s public school system was warned on Tuesday that it could lose accreditation this year if feuding school board members do not resolve their differences. An independent accreditation group, AdvancED, announced that it was placing the high schools in the 49,000-student school system on probation, giving the board nine months to make improvements or face further punishments. Losing accreditation affects students’ ability to apply to college or receive scholarships. The announcement followed months of public power struggles between two groups of board members for control of the board. Atlanta is the second largest school system that the accreditation group has ever placed on probation, according to its spokeswoman, Jennifer H. Oliver.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Atlanta Schools Are Placed on Probation', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Atlanta Schools Are Placed on Probation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCREDITATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/19f8241b-2259-573b-a92a-f7aa9cdcd0fd', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19f8241b-2259-573b-a92a-f7aa9cdcd0fd'}, {'abstract': 'Whether or not ethnic Somali children in Minneapolis have unusually high rates of autism will be investigated by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention and the National Institutes of Health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19brfs-AUTISMINSOMA_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Whether or not ethnic Somali children in Minneapolis have unusually high rates of autism will be investigated by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention and the National Institutes of Health.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Whether or not ethnic Somali children in Minneapolis have unusually high rates of autism will be investigated by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention and the National Institutes of Health in conjunction with Autism Speaks, an autism research organization, the centers and Autism speaks announced Tuesday. Somali parents in Minneapolis have complained for years that many of their children, regardless of where they were born, are autistic, and want an explanation. “I’m so happy to be in a country where one voice can make a difference,” said Idil Abdull, who has an autistic son and has for years asked for an investigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Autism in Somali Children Will Be Investigated', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | HEALTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Autism in Somali Children Will Be Investigated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Autism Speaks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/815d077f-25b2-5515-95f8-792ca28ebd69', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/815d077f-25b2-5515-95f8-792ca28ebd69'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department announced on Tuesday the creation of a unit that will decide how to discipline career officials who commit prosecutorial misconduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/us/19brfs-NEWJUSTICEDE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department announced on Tuesday the creation of a unit that will decide how to discipline career officials who commit prosecutorial misconduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department announced on Tuesday the creation of a unit that will decide how to discipline career officials who commit prosecutorial misconduct, including whether to refer them to state bar associations for punishment. The unit will review cases whenever the department’s internal ethics watchdog, the Office of Professional Responsibility, finds that a prosecutor intentionally or recklessly violated the rules to which he is subject. Cases in which office investigators conclude that prosecutors merely made a mistake or had poor judgment would, however, still be handled by their supervisors. Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. appointed Kevin Ohlson, who until recently was his chief of staff, to be chief of the new unit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Justice Department Office Will Discipline Prosecutors', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Justice Department Office Will Discipline Prosecutors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T05:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f3a50ad-47cf-598f-b1e4-f0645b145a6d', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f3a50ad-47cf-598f-b1e4-f0645b145a6d'}, {'abstract': 'Images from some of the films appearing at the 2011 Sundance Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/18/movies/sundance.html', 'snippet': 'Images from some of the films appearing at the 2011 Sundance Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images from some of the films appearing at the 2011 Sundance Film Festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '