], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8d9fe75-d7e3-5526-8cb9-356a36bac8f3', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8d9fe75-d7e3-5526-8cb9-356a36bac8f3'}, {'abstract': 'New research gives climate scientists optimism that they can make a more accurate determination of the sun’s role in global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/a-better-yardstick-for-solar-cycles/', 'snippet': 'New research gives climate scientists optimism that they can make a more accurate determination of the sun’s role in global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With 2010 tying 2005 for the warmest year on record, and 10 of the last 13 years ranking as the 10 warmest ever, it becomes ever more difficult to sustain an argument that global warming is not occurring. So the question becomes more of a whodunit. Is it man, or nature, or both, and in what measure? In making their argument for natural causes, many climate skeptics tend to focus attention on the sun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Yardstick for Solar Cycles', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Naval Research Laboratory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Colorado', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T16:06:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb030be-47ac-523c-8bed-4fc6cab82a0f', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb030be-47ac-523c-8bed-4fc6cab82a0f'}, {'abstract': 'Finding humor, via Twitter, in news that a possible life-friendly planet may not exist.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/vanishing-planet-in-140-amusing-characters/', 'snippet': 'Finding humor, via Twitter, in news that a possible life-friendly planet may not exist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s another reason I engage on Twitter: Laughter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vanishing Planet in 140 Amusing Characters', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astronomy and Astrophysics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T16:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db97d3f-15c4-53c8-b550-e505edf8c07d', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db97d3f-15c4-53c8-b550-e505edf8c07d'}, {'abstract': 'Orlando executive Lucas Boyce discusses his rise from growing up in a foster home to working in the White House and now in the N.B.A.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/orlando-executive-boyce-discusses-beating-lifes-odds/', 'snippet': 'Orlando executive Lucas Boyce discusses his rise from growing up in a foster home to working in the White House and now in the N.B.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 31, Lucas Boyce is one of the N.B.A.’s youngest executives. His role as the OrlandoMagic’s director of multicultural insights, cause marketing and government affairs comes after he served in the White House during George W. Bush’s administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orlando Executive Boyce Discusses Beating Life’s Odds', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orlando (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T16:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/189ccdd3-d911-55da-b57a-a26b96e0fd21', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/189ccdd3-d911-55da-b57a-a26b96e0fd21'}, {'abstract': 'The Raiders owner turned the formal introduction of Hue Jackson as coach into a two-hour evisceration of his former coach, Tom Cable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/football/20leading.html', 'snippet': 'The Raiders owner turned the formal introduction of Hue Jackson as coach into a two-hour evisceration of his former coach, Tom Cable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what team you root for, in whatever sport, you may 