imedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Divorce and the Stay-at-Home-Mom', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T17:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/868ca174-51ac-578c-b448-191b453b137e', 'word_count': 1539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/868ca174-51ac-578c-b448-191b453b137e'}, {'abstract': 'What the latest additions and promotions in the administration say about the president’s political style and policy initiatives.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/obamas-clinton-white-house/', 'snippet': 'What the latest additions and promotions in the administration say about the president’s political style and policy initiatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Brooks: Gail, are you aware that what goes up, must come down, the spinning wheel gotta spin round, and, according to an authoritative Congressional Budget Office study, it is, therefore, best to ride a painted pony and let the spinning wheel spin?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Clinton White House', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, William M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed , Bruce N', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sperling, Gene', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T17:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff0a0a62-72e7-5627-9f0f-7f152d9c3715', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff0a0a62-72e7-5627-9f0f-7f152d9c3715'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Hathaway will play Selina Kyle and Mr. Hardy will play a villain named Bane in the next Batman movie from the “Inception” director Christopher Nolan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/roles-of-anne-hathaway-and-tom-hardy-revealed-in-dark-knight-rises/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Hathaway will play Selina Kyle and Mr. Hardy will play a villain named Bane in the next Batman movie from the “Inception” director Christopher Nolan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Batman has found a nemesis for his next cinematic adventure – and, it appears, a love interest, too. On Wednesday, Warner Brothers Pictures announced a new cast member and the role of another in “The Dark Knight Rises,” the third Batman movie to be directed by Christopher Nolan, the “Inception” and “Memento” filmmaker. Joining Christian Bale, who returns as Batman and his daytime alter ego, Bruce Wayne, is Anne Hathaway (of “Love and Other Drugs”) who will play Selina Kyle; the film will also feature Tom Hardy, a co-star of “Inception,” as the villain Bane.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roles of Anne Hathaway and Tom Hardy Revealed in ‘Dark Knight Rises’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nolan, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T17:51:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef2ac3b-b9bf-5608-9d06-79bb5425ed9c', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef2ac3b-b9bf-5608-9d06-79bb5425ed9c'}, {'abstract': 'The federation has offered to organize the European Women’s Chess Championship, an event it walked away from several weeks ago. The offer follows a protest by participants in the Women’s World Championship, which was held in Turkey last month.', 'web_url': 'https://gambit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/about-face-turkish-federation-offers-to-organize-event-it-spurned/', 'snippet': 'The federation has offered to organize the European Women’s Chess Championship, an event it walked away from several weeks ago. The offer follows a protest by participants in the Women’s World Championship, which was held in Turkey last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late last month, the Turkish Chess Federation withdrew as host of the 2011 European Women’s Championship. The reason given by Ali Nihat Yazici, the federation’s president, was that he and the federation had been treated badly by the European Chess Union, the governing body of the game in Europe. ', 'source': 'The New Y