bestiary-of-malthusian-miserabilists/', 'snippet': 'After an attack on those seeking population stability, a more subtle discussion of human numbers and choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I received a promotional e-mail from spiked, the often-biting British publication fond of puncturing all manner of ideological balloons, touting a broadside against warnings about overpopulation. The piece, The definitive guide to modern-day Malthusians, by Brendan O’Neill, had a predictably provocative summary: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deconstructing a Bestiary of Malthusian ‘Miserabilists’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condoms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ridley, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1474e4b5-d9e5-5e16-9bb1-4374c3eadccb', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1474e4b5-d9e5-5e16-9bb1-4374c3eadccb'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers at Rice University say that agricultural tendencies occur in about a third of Dictyostelium discoideum amoebas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/science/25obamoeba.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers at Rice University say that agricultural tendencies occur in about a third of Dictyostelium discoideum amoebas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Humans are not the only farmers. Other animals, like ants and termites, grow food, and now a new study reports that a species of amoeba, one of the simplest of organisms, also farms. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25obamoeba1/25obamoeba1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25obamoeba1/25obamoeba1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25obamoeba1/25obamoeba1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crops of Bacteria, Farmed by Amoebas', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crops of Bacteria, Farmed by Amoebas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/167ad9b0-8813-509f-9fa1-d780a538999d', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/167ad9b0-8813-509f-9fa1-d780a538999d'}, {'abstract': 'As Senator Joseph I. Lieberman of Connecticut has felt the lash of some liberals angry about his middle-of-the-road politics, so, too, have voters acutely sensed his withdrawal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/nyregion/20lieberman.html', 'snippet': 'As Senator Joseph I. Lieberman of Connecticut has felt the lash of some liberals angry about his middle-of-the-road politics, so, too, have voters acutely sensed his withdrawal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps no one could claim credit for Senator Joseph I. Lieberman’s decision not to seek a fifth term more than Markos Moulitsas, the founder of the liberal blog Daily Kos. In 2006, Mr. Moulitsas mobilized like-minded Democrats to try to unseat Mr. Lieberman as punishment for supporting the Iraq war and for being too accommodating to President George W. Bush.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/nyregion/LIEBERMAN/LIEBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/nyregion/LIEBERMAN/LIEBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/nyregion/LIEBERMAN/LIEBERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/nyregion/LIEBERMAN/LIEBERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/nyregion/LIEBERMAN/LIEBERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75