Edwards’s most productive season yet, the Jets receiver has found his happy place, but for one night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/football/20edwards.html', 'snippet': 'In Braylon Edwards’s most productive season yet, the Jets receiver has found his happy place, but for one night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. \x97 The more Braylon Edwards talked, the more he sounded humbled, sounded changed. He called 2010 his best season and said he traded statistics for team unity in hope of shifting the perceptions that have shadowed him.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/EDWARDS3/EDWARDS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 632, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/EDWARDS3/EDWARDS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/EDWARDS3/EDWARDS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Edwards, Productivity and Patience Take Hold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Edwards, Productivity And Patience Take Hold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, Braylon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/769f8684-13f5-53e1-8564-2fcbd89f06dc', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/769f8684-13f5-53e1-8564-2fcbd89f06dc'}, {'abstract': 'The No. 4 seed had to leave the court after the last point of the first set to deal with a hip flexor strain, but she returned to dispatch Sandra Zahlavova.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/tennis/20iht-TENNIS20.html', 'snippet': 'The No. 4 seed had to leave the court after the last point of the first set to deal with a hip flexor strain, but she returned to dispatch Sandra Zahlavova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia \x97 It could have been another day at the Australian Open of frivolous themes, with the focus on Venus Williams’s latest risqué tennis dress. But then Williams screamed in pain as she lost the last point of the first set, limped to her chair and hobbled off the court for treatment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/20tennis-web1/20tennis-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/20tennis-web1/20tennis-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/20tennis-web1/20tennis-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/20tennis-web1/20tennis-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/20tennis-web1/20tennis-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venus Williams Hobbles Off, Then Roars Back', 'kicker': 'Australian Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venus Williams Hobbles Off, Then Roars Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b09d514-8bae-50d2-b063-75e84585d720', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b09d514-8bae-50d2-b063-75e84585d720'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy winnowed down the foreign-language Oscar race to nine from 65, and France’s entry, the much-praised “Of Gods and Men,” did not make the cut.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/a-shortlist-and-the-usual-snubs/', 'snippet': 'The Academy winnowed down the foreign-language Oscar race to nine from 65, and France’s entry, the much-praised “Of Gods and Men,” did not make the cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nine films that will move on to the next stage of competition for the Oscar for best foreign-language film were revealed on Wednesday, and as is typical, there were surprises – and snubs. The highly regarded French submission, “Of Gods and Men,” about Christian monks trying to keep their monastery going amid Islamist conflict in Algeria, was left off the list, but an Algerian film about that country’s struggle to break free from French rule, “Outside the Law,” was included. So were two other films that address cultural conflicts between the West and Islam: Canada’s “Incendies” and Denmark’s “In a Better World,” which won the Golden Globe for best foreign-language film last weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shortlist, and the Usual Snubs', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c724c53c-7167-5b4b-8550-0ff09e7b1b89', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c724c53c-7167-5b4b-8550-0ff09e7b1b89'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists and engineers who work on government space programs must submit to intrusive background checks, the Supreme Court ruled on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/us/20scotus.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists and engineers who work on government space programs must submit to intrusive background checks, the Supreme Court ruled on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Employees of government contractors, including scientists and engineers who work on government space programs, must submit to intrusive background checks if they want to keep their jobs, the Supreme Court ruled unanimously on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Uphold Background Checks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Uphold Background Checks for Government Contractors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c439cb9-55f6-5ea0-9acb-b7338f85334d', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c439cb9-55f6-5ea0-9acb-b7338f85334d'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago’s Derrick Rose has improved across the board this season, but his biggest steps forward have come on the defensive end.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/rose-dwarfs-other-improvements-with-defense/', 'snippet': 'Chicago’s Derrick Rose has improved across the board this season, but his biggest steps forward have come on the defensive end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derrick Rose’s ongoing most valuable player campaign is often unfairly boiled down to his superior shooting this season, but Rose’s increased range is far from his most compelling improvement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rose Dwarfs Other Improvements With Defense', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Derrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:47:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a7a83ef-8b1d-5b66-b0d7-8e39065f9887', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a7a83ef-8b1d-5b66-b0d7-8e39065f9887'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch designer creates fanciful objects in Venetian glass out of everyday items in her latest collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/heart-of-glass-kiki-van-eijk/', 'snippet': 'The Dutch designer creates fanciful objects in Venetian glass out of everyday items in her latest collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month at Design Miami, the Dutch designer Kiki van Eijk showed a collection of seven objects for Venice Projects, an Italian gallery that commissions contemporary artists to work with traditional Venetian glass techniques. The collection is now available at veniceprojects.com. Van Eijk’s fanciful, craft-intensive and extravagant objects (“Love,” shown here, is $19,200) invest everyday items like a cooking pot or a watering can with emotional resonance by virtue of juxtapositions (a stack of glass pillows topped by an hourglass in “Rest”) and color (red for passion in “Love”). Van Eijk and her partner, the designer Joost van Bleiswijk, will also be part of the exhibition “Glasstress 2011,” which opens June 3 to coincide with the Venice Biennale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heart of Glass | Kiki van Eijk', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T18:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c5e5d3-65c6-5f22-9ee8-763f65840049', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c5e5d3-65c6-5f22-9ee8-763f65840049'}, {'abstract': 'Suzanne Malveaux will anchor the 11 a.m. and noon hours of “CNN Newsroom,” replacing Tony Harris, who exited the channel at the end of last year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/suzanne-malveaux-to-anchor-cnn-newsroom/', 'snippet': 'Suzanne Malveaux will anchor the 11 a.m. and noon hours of “CNN Newsroom,” replacing Tony Harris, who exited the channel at the end of last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CNN continues to tweak its weekday lineup, this time by naming a new lunchtime anchor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suzanne Malveaux to Anchor ‘CNN Newsroom’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cable News Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T19:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5640d38b-0a2a-5468-a057-c36392a60d3d', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5640d38b-0a2a-5468-a057-c36392a60d3d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Sheed drew upon his Anglo-American background to write bittersweet essays, criticism, memoirs and fiction about cultural life on both sides of the Atlantic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/books/20sheed.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Sheed drew upon his Anglo-American background to write bittersweet essays, criticism, memoirs and fiction about cultural life on both sides of the Atlantic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wilfrid Sheed, the wittily satirical man of letters who drew upon his Anglo-American background to write bittersweet essays, criticism, memoirs and fiction about cultural life on both sides of the Atlantic, died early Wednesday in Great Barrington, Mass. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SHEED-obit/SHEED-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SHEED-obit/SHEED-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SHEED-obit/SHEED-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilfrid Sheed, Writer of Gentle Wit, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wilfrid Sheed, a Man of Letters With a Gentle Wit, Is Dead at 80', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheed, Wilfrid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T19:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Lehmann-Haupt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lehmann-Haupt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3104f7b9-3d86-5c73-86c1-50a4a673ad11', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3104f7b9-3d86-5c73-86c1-50a4a673ad11'}, {'abstract': 'In “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother,” Amy Chua offers a highly readable screed on the art of obsessive parenting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/books/20book.html', 'snippet': 'In “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother,” Amy Chua offers a highly readable screed on the art of obsessive parenting.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There are all these new books out there portraying Asian mothers as scheming, callous, overdriven people indifferent to their kids’ true interests,” Amy Chua writes. She ought to know, because hers is the big one: “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother,” a diabolically well-packaged, highly readable screed ostensibly about the art of obsessive parenting. In truth, Ms. Chua’s memoir is about one little narcissist’s book-length search for happiness. And for all its quotable outbursts from Mama Grisly (the nickname was inevitable), it will gratify the same people who made a hit out of the granola-hearted “Eat, Pray, Love.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'But Will It All Make ‘Tiger Mom’ Happy?', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'But Will It All Make Mommy Happy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chua, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T19:18:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e87df71-d509-5748-81ad-4ab861820233', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e87df71-d509-5748-81ad-4ab861820233'}, {'abstract': 'No penalties would be charged if a restaurant earns an A.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/mayor-promises-a-plan-for-fewer-restaurant-fines/', 'snippet': 'No penalties would be charged if a restaurant earns an A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced a reduction in the fines that restaurateurs are likely to encounter while navigating the city’s new letter-grade sanitary inspection system. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Promises a Plan for Fewer Restaurant Fines', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T19:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization