Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6691fe16-8597-5a46-bc01-e93cdfdbe3a8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6691fe16-8597-5a46-bc01-e93cdfdbe3a8'}, {'abstract': 'A father loses custody because of his rigid homework standards.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/a-court-rules-dad-is-too-strict/', 'snippet': 'A father loses custody because of his rigid homework standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I promise (well, I hope . . .) this will be the last mention of Amy Chua and “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother,” at least for a while. But in light of the debate the book has caused over “how strict is too strict,” a bit of news out of Australia. A father of three has been told by the Federal Magistrates’ Court in Melbourne that he was “too rigid and obsessive” in his parenting, according to The Herald Sun newspaper. Among his methods: requiring them to write reports on their daily activities, do extra homework above their grade level and read to him nightly over the phone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Court Rules Dad Is Too Strict', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Custody and Support', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T21:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ea1d4f7-fe15-54d4-8cd6-59bf08a7208d', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ea1d4f7-fe15-54d4-8cd6-59bf08a7208d'}, {'abstract': 'Merely a metaphor for a multitasking society? If only it were.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/14klass-ess.html', 'snippet': 'Merely a metaphor for a multitasking society? If only it were.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As recently as 2002, an international group of leading neuroscientists found it necessary to publish a statement arguing passionately that attention deficit hyperactivity disorder was a real condition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/14/health/14KLASS/14KLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/12/14/health/14KLASS/14KLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/14/health/14KLASS/14KLASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/14/health/14KLASS/14KLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/14/health/14KLASS/14KLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Untangling the Myths About Attention Disorder', 'kicker': '18 and Under', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T21:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': 'By PERRI KLASS, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KLASS', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22055c85-3e38-51ea-b6a9-d0c80231add6', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22055c85-3e38-51ea-b6a9-d0c80231add6'}, {'abstract': 'News of Belarus Free Theater includes NY rally, Public Theater benefit, and plans to do show in Chicago', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/support-for-belarus-theater-troupe-includes-rally-benefit-and-a-chicago-engagement/', 'snippet': 'News of Belarus Free Theater includes NY rally, Public Theater benefit, and plans to do show in Chicago', 'lead_paragraph': 'On December 19, a presidential election in Belarus that international observers said was fraudulent sent protesters into the streets, including members of the Belarus Free Theater. The troupe managed to evade the official repression that put down the protests and leave their country, and after a widely-praised two-week run at the Under the Radar alternative theater festival, they have remained in New York, where on Wednesday, to mark one month since the questionable vote and crackdown, they led another protest, this one outside the Belarussian mission to the United Nations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Support for Belarus Theater Troupe Includes Rally, Benefits and a Chicago Engagement', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T21:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea6d73c-0ea0-58c3-b869-5ddb896ce563', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea6d73c-0ea0-58c3-b869-5ddb896ce563'}, {'abstract': 'New novels by Alice Hofmann, Bradford Morrow, Thelma Adams, Howard Gordon, Suzanne Corso and Adam Schwartz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/books/20newly.html', 'snippet': 'New novels by Alice Hofmann, Bradford Morrow, Thelma Adams, Howard Gordon, Suzanne Corso and Adam Schwartz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The publishing industry has had its share of woes, but writing books, apparently, has not lost its allure. This month a television producer, a short-story writer, a film critic and a screenwriter whose first draft was her journal all deliver their debut novels. Bradford Morrow has been at it longer, writing both fiction and poetry. And then there’s Alice Hoffman, who clocks in with her 28th (!) work of fiction.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newly Released Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newly Released', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Alice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Thelma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrow, Bradford', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Howard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T21:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah Meadows', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meadows', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf0a26cd-dd25-5cae-bff5-8fd47e7bc198', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf0a26cd-dd25-5cae-bff5-8fd47e7bc198'}, {'abstract': 'Specialized social networks have grown in popularity among users who prefer a more focused way to share information and photos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics.html', 'snippet': 'Specialized social networks have grown in popularity among users who prefer a more focused way to share information and photos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Facebook’s membership approaching 600 million, and more features and apps continually being added to the site, it sometimes seems as if it’s the only social network around. But it’s not the only one, even if it’s dominant. Specialized networks are catching on with users who prefer a more focused way to share photos, videos or music, or who simply don’t want everyone on Facebook looking at their pictures. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics-span/20basics-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics-span/20basics-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics-span/20basics-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics-span/20basics-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/technology/personaltech/20basics-span/20basics-s