, 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/us/jp-CONG/jp-CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/us/jp-CONG/jp-CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes for Repeal of Health Law in Symbolic Act', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'AS VOWED, HOUSE VOTES TO REPEAL HEALTH CARE LAW', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn and Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7b134d5-47cd-5653-ac90-e03ef361ddfe', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7b134d5-47cd-5653-ac90-e03ef361ddfe'}, {'abstract': 'Six hearts was bid. How could it be made?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/crosswords/bridge/20card.html', 'snippet': 'Six hearts was bid. How could it be made?', 'lead_paragraph': ' All the top British players hope to be invited to the Lederer Memorial Trophy, named for Richard and Tony Lederer, father and son. Over the final weekend of October eight teams competed in the event. The main difference from previous years was the lack of foreign teams.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Lederer Memorial, a Look at a Long-Card Oddity', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Lederer Memorial, A Look at a Long-Card Oddity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ea5ee3e-d087-5d96-b685-09014f8b435c', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ea5ee3e-d087-5d96-b685-09014f8b435c'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet opened its winter season on Tuesday with an all-Balanchine program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/arts/dance/20ballet.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet opened its winter season on Tuesday with an all-Balanchine program.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Life in New York just is more complete when New York City Ballet is in residence and dancing Balanchine. Let me add a few immediate qualifications to that. Like any of the company’s followers, I have my grumbles: I certainly don’t mean to imply that the company should dance nothing but Balanchine; yes, I sometimes see \x97 mainly outside New York \x97 other companies that dance Balanchine as well or better; and there are many other forms of dance and art that I crave. But in its wealth of Balanchine repertory City Ballet has an unmatchable asset, and to renew acquaintance with these ballets can be among the great and regular joys of living in New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/BALLET/BALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/BALLET/BALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/BALLET/BALLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/BALLET/BALLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/BALLET/BALLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reintroductions on a Winter’s Eve', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Reintroductions on a Winter's Eve", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairchild, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouder, Ashley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/658e35b1-0487-5f5a-8d55-b9a594bb3754', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/658e35b1-0487-5f5a-8d55-b9a594bb3754'}, {'abstract': 'ABC’s interview with the astronaut Capt. Mark E. Kelly, the husband of Representative Gabrielle Giffords, generated only modest interest in prime time on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/arts/television/20arts-KELLYINTERVI_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'ABC’s interview with the astronaut Capt. Mark E. Kelly, the husband of Representative Gabrielle Giffords, generated only modest interest in prime time on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC’s interview with the astronaut Capt. Mark E. Kelly, the husband of Representative Gabrielle Giffords, generated only modest interest in prime time on Tuesday: according to Nielsen’s estimates 6.2 million viewers tuned in to the special edition of “20/20” at 10 p.m. In contrast, “The Good Wife” on CBS led the hour with 11.3 million viewers, and CBS’s “NCIS” won the night with 21 million at 8. Earlier, excerpts from the interview did provide a boost to ABC’s “World News With Diane Sawyer,” which attracted an average of 9.1 million viewers, the newscast’s largest audience in almost a year. CBS led the night over all, also garnering 17.3 million at 9 for “NCIS: Los Angeles.” NBC placed second with “The Biggest Loser,” from 8 to 10 (8.2 million), followed by “Parenthood” (5.6 million). ABC, in third, averaged 5.7 million at 8 and 9 with “No Ordinary Family” and “V,” while Fox ranked fourth with a rerun of “Glee” at 8 (4.4 million) and “Million Dollar Money Drop” at 9 (5.3 million).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kelly Interview Ratings', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kelly Interview Ratings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:29:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc74918f-766d-5d12-b321-d6124c89f490', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc74918f-766d-5d12-b321-d6124c89f490'}, {'abstract': 'Western women who order Japanese makeup online say they are drawn in by the products’ superior quality and innovation compared with American or European brands — even when it comes to the cheapest drugstore finds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/fashion/20SKIN.html', 'snippet': 'Western women who order Japanese makeup online say they are drawn in by the products’ superior quality and innovation compared with American or European brands — even when it comes to the cheapest drugstore finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOUNG women in Japan have long used makeup to transform themselves into plastic dolls or anime princesses come to life. Brands homegrown there, like Mellish and Dolly Wink, make the spidery fake eyelashes, doe-eyed contact lenses and eyelid tape that help them with this metamorphosis.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-SKIN-A/Z-SKIN-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-SKIN-A/Z-SKIN-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-SKIN-A/Z-SKIN-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 883, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-SKIN-A/Z-SKIN-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-SKIN-A/Z-SKIN-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Makeup From Japan to Your Mailbox', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Makeup From Japan to Your Mailbox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kayleen Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kayleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d46af3d8-7986-5fea-9d02-68f296b4e30b', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d46af3d8-7986-5fea-9d02-68f296b4e30b'}, {'abstract': 'Artificial tanning options without the sun damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/fashion/20SPOTS.html', 'snippet': 'Artificial tanning options without the sun damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S mid-January and for some of us, pastiness is starting to seem like a permanent condition. Fortunately there are some affordable self-tanning options. They might not rival the experience of sitting on a Caribbean beach, but they do avoid the unpleasant side effects of sun exposure.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/BeautySpots-inline/BeautySpots-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty Spots', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beauty Spots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suntan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Howard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Howard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f2cf67e-855f-567b-b10a-28380c7f5667', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f2cf67e-855f-567b-b10a-28380c7f5667'}, {'abstract': 'A noise band hides inside the sound of Smith Westerns, which played at the Glasslands Gallery in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/arts/music/20smith.html', 'snippet': 'A noise band hides inside the sound of Smith Westerns, which played at the Glasslands Gallery in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was Cullen Omori \x97 in a shapeless sweater, possibly in need of a sandwich, hair swallowing his face \x97 holding his guitar tenderly onstage Tuesday night at the Glasslands Gallery in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Behind him his band, Smith Westerns, was playing with a straight face, possibly a bit tentatively. All of the emotion fell to Mr. Omori, then, who was happy to be a ham, dreaming about love that won’t ever end, holding notes until they decayed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/smith/smith-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet, Dreamy Nibbles From Band With Teeth', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweet, Dreamy Nibbles From Band With Teeth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6b5508b-2a7e-5806-8a2d-00559ebf140e', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6b5508b-2a7e-5806-8a2d-00559ebf140e'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Koons, who is known for appropriating pop-culture imagery, says that bookends sold by a San Francisco gallery violate his intellectual property rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/arts/design/20suit.html', 'snippet': 'Jeff Koons, who is known for appropriating pop-culture imagery, says that bookends sold by a San Francisco gallery violate his intellectual property rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Jeff Koons has developed a distinctive style, and made a lot of money, by appropriating pop-culture imagery and mass-produced objects, from inflatable toys to vacuum cleaners and kitschy greeting cards. Over his three-decade career that approach, while helping to make him famous, has also brought accusations of exploiting other people’s copyrighted images. He has been sued for copyright violation four times, losing three of the cases.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SUIT/SUIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SUIT/SUIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/arts/SUIT/SUIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Twist, Jeff Koons Claims Rights to ‘Balloon Dogs’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Twist, Jeff Koons Claims Rights to ‘Balloon Dogs’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf46cd8-59e0-5d55-9c86-4b7be4d4d98f', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf46cd8-59e0-5d55-9c86-4b7be4d4d98f'}, {'abstract': 'Kris Jenkins’s brother Cullen plays for the Packers, but Kris is still hoping to be the Jets’ biggest cheerleader in the Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/kris-jenkins-dreaming-of-jets-packers-super-bowl/', 'snippet': 'Kris Jenkins’s brother Cullen plays for the Packers, but Kris is still hoping to be the Jets’ biggest cheerleader in the Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. – Kris Jenkins spent all but one game this season on injured reserve. He will not play in the A.F.C. championship game Sunday against Pittsburgh. Nor will he play in the Super Bowl should the Jets advance that far for the second time in franchise history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kris Jenkins Dreaming of Jets-Packers Super Bowl', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Kris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:43:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b10960-f451-593d-9a8b-a59ffab18e14', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b10960-f451-593d-9a8b-a59ffab18e14'}, {'abstract': 'Where to buy tools for a set of forgotten skills, tastes and virtues referred to as “the household arts.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/fashion/20CRITIC.html', 'snippet': 'Where to buy tools for a set of forgotten skills, tastes and virtues referred to as “the household arts.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALKING down a residential street in Poughkeepsie, N.Y., several years ago, I was stopped in my tracks by the beauty of a backyard clothesline hung with well-made, well-loved cotton things: embroidered pillowcases, hand-sewn aprons, cloth napkins and unstained tablecloths, secured on a white rope with wooden clothespins, waving before a wall of pine trees. It actually brought tears to my eyes; it was like stumbling on a time capsule full of lost femininity \x97 all that stuff that was abandoned in the 1970s for being too contaminated by patriarchal social engineering. But there was something so careful, patient, constructive and good about that beautiful laundry. It was a genuine example of homemaking as a verb \x97 a creative act that reifies the idea of “home.” ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-CRITIC-C/Z-CRITIC-C-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-CRITIC-C/Z-CRITIC-C-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/fashion/Z-CRITIC-C/Z-CRITIC-C-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Primer for the Wholesome, Happy Home', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Primer for the Wholesome, Happy Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T23:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cintra Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cintra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e0de09f-f833-53c8-8e7a-2a0f621727ea', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e0de09f-f833-53c8-8e7a-2a0f621727ea'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets’ owner, Mikhail D. Prokhorov, abruptly canceled a meeting with Carmelo Anthony and his agent, saying he had decided to end the pursuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/basketball/20nets.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets’ owner, Mikhail D. Prokhorov, abruptly canceled a meeting with Carmelo Anthony and his agent, saying he had decided to end the pursuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK \x97 The Nets spent months tying up phone lines from here to Russia, discussing possibilities with the team’s majority owner, Mikhail D. Prokhorov, by which they could obtain the Denver Nuggets’ Carmelo Anthony.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/NETS1/NETS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/NETS1/NETS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/NETS1/NETS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets End Their Bid to Obtain Anthony', 'kicker': 'Nets 103, Jazz 95', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets End Their Bid To Obtain Anthony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-19T2