ltimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e41b3c75-53cb-55db-bd90-ab2886b94d1b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e41b3c75-53cb-55db-bd90-ab2886b94d1b'}, {'abstract': 'A show at Julius Lowy Frame and Restoring Company presents picture frames once considered as important as the art they contained.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/garden/20shows.html', 'snippet': 'A show at Julius Lowy Frame and Restoring Company presents picture frames once considered as important as the art they contained.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred years ago, frames were considered as important as the artwork they contained. “Frame makers of the Arts and Crafts period became interested in frames as an art form, even signing them,” said Lisa Wyer.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20shows/20shows-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 880, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20shows/20shows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20shows/20shows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Antique Frames on Exhibit', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frames in Focus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donna Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7c81df8-2224-5e99-a8c1-bd60d248deb8', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c81df8-2224-5e99-a8c1-bd60d248deb8'}, {'abstract': 'Finding refuge from the outside world, and from parents, in a tree, under the earth, in a tomb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/garden/20Domestic.html', 'snippet': 'Finding refuge from the outside world, and from parents, in a tree, under the earth, in a tomb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS 9, my brother, Jeb, was 8, and maybe if we’d been born in a city we would not have started building treehouses and forts, igloos and tepees, even digging a hole in the ground that we covered with thick branches of pine, oak and maple. Or maybe if our mother and father did not fight most every night, their yelling rising up the stairwell like some poisonous vapor to us and our two sisters, Jeb and I would not have gone looking for the scrap lumber we found under the closed summer camps near our rented house in southern New Hampshire \x97 two-by-fours and two-by-sixes, warped plywood and long planks of rough spruce. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20domestic/Domestic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20domestic/20domestic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20domestic/20domestic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnai