of black walnut and other woods, inlaid with Lucite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many parents, Athena Calderone thought a growth chart would make a nice decorative addition to her son’s room. But Ms. Calderone, an interior designer based in Brooklyn, also wanted a piece that would work in her Dumbo loft, a modern space made less austere with organic wood. “Jivan’s room is visible from the entire space,” she said, referring to her son. “I wanted what was happening in the living room to flow throughout, not get dumbed down in his room.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20kids/CURRENTS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20kids/20kids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/garden/20kids/20kids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Growth Chart With a Decorative Touch', 'kicker': 'Currents | Kids', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charting Growth With a Decorative Touch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_