 pay $300 million over 20 years, plans to show 200 sports events a year, including at least one football game and eight men’s basketball games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The University of Texas announced Wednesday the creation of a statewide sports network that will carry games plus academic, cultural and arts programming. The unnamed channel will focus on the Longhorns, unlike the Big Ten Network, which has a broader, conference-wide focus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'University of Texas Will Create Its Own Sports Network With ESPN', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/987a0cdf-2608-5624-992f-f288afe7bc54', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/987a0cdf-2608-5624-992f-f288afe7bc54'}, {'abstract': 'Nicola Formichetti’s  template seemed to be the things we know about Mugler’s style—the strong silhouette, the mixture of tailoring and metals or plastic, a hard sex appeal.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/rethinking-the-mugler-man/', 'snippet': 'Nicola Formichetti’s  template seemed to be the things we know about Mugler’s style—the strong silhouette, the mixture of tailoring and metals or plastic, a hard sex appeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been more than 20 years since I squeezed my way into a Thierry Mugler show, enduring the high-handed manner of the house publicists, and tonight I suppose I was a little wistful for the groupies and the attitude when I arrived for the debut showing of Nicola Formichetti, the new creative director of Mugler. There was a small throng of young people at the door, but not much greater than you’d find outside most shows in Paris, and the PR handlers moved the guests along and offered them glasses of Champagne. Everything is professional now. Shows start on time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking the Mugler Man', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2dd7bb5-be6b-513f-bfc6-d989a70bd043', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2dd7bb5-be6b-513f-bfc6-d989a70bd043'}, {'abstract': 'According to a congressional aide who spoke to Reuters, State Department officials concluded late last year that the publication of leaked U.S. diplomatic cables obtained by WikiLeaks “was embarrassing but not damaging.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/u-s-officials-reportedly-said-wikileaks-revelations-were-not-damaging/', 'snippet': 'According to a congressional aide who spoke to Reuters, State Department officials concluded late last year that the publication of leaked U.S. diplomatic cables obtained by WikiLeaks “was embarrassing but not damaging.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to a Congressional aide who spoke to Reuters, State Department officials concluded late last year that the publication of leaked United States diplomatic cables obtained by WikiLeaks “was embarrassing but not damaging.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Officials Reportedly Said WikiLeaks Revelations Were ‘Not Damaging’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c671cc-ea49-5554-af5a-00600238720f', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c671cc-ea49-5554-af5a-00600238720f'}, {'abstract': 'Eight players from the 2008 Olympic team said they would play in the National Pro Fastpitch League, citing scheduling conflicts and softball’s elimination from the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/20softball.html', 'snippet': 'Eight players from the 2008 Olympic team said they would play in the National Pro Fastpitch League, citing scheduling conflicts and softball’s elimination from the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a member of the United States softball team, Jessica Mendoza has competed against the best players in the world, winning a gold medal at the Athens Olympics in 2004 and a silver medal in Beijing in 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/SOFTBALL1/SOFTBALL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/SOFTBALL1/SOFTBALL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heigh