. 24, 1991, Saddam Hussein directed his frustration at an unlikely target: the Soviet leader Mikhail S. Gorbachev. Mr. Hussein had dispatched his foreign minister to Moscow in an 11th-hour bid to head off a ground war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hussein Wanted Soviets to Head Off U.S. in 1991', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hussein Wanted Soviets\nTo Head Off U.S. in 1991', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:49:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d0b743c-02c6-5712-944a-c6c26a043f73', 'word_count': 1566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d0b743c-02c6-5712-944a-c6c26a043f73'}, {'abstract': 'The following is a list of guests expected at the president’s State Dinner honoring President Hu Jintao of China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/world/asia/20dinner-list.html', 'snippet': 'The following is a list of guests expected at the president’s State Dinner honoring President Hu Jintao of China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is a list of guests expected at the president’s State Dinner honoring President Hu Jintao of China, as provided by the White House:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Dinner Guests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Dinner Guests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce70959-77a1-501f-bac4-cb950006824e', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce70959-77a1-501f-bac4-cb950006824e'}, {'abstract': 'An extraordinary Iraqi archive, captured in 2003 and kept classified until this week, reveals how Saddam Hussein attempted to win Soviet support before the first United States war with Iraq in 1991.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/saddam-hussein-sought-soviet-support-before-91-gulf-war/', 'snippet': 'An extraordinary Iraqi archive, captured in 2003 and kept classified until this week, reveals how Saddam Hussein attempted to win Soviet support before the first United States war with Iraq in 1991.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael R. Gordon reports on the release of three extraordinarily candid transcripts of conversations that Saddam Hussein had with his advisers in the early days of the 1991 Persian Gulf war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saddam Hussein Sought Soviet Support Before ’91 Gulf War', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T00:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a88f4e8b-8927-5868-b3ee-11e28941c335', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a88f4e8b-8927-5868-b3ee-11e28941c335'}, {'abstract': 'A plan made at the request of the American Federation of Teachers calls for resolving misconduct within 100 days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/education/20teachers.html', 'snippet': 'A plan made at the request of the American Federation of Teachers calls for resolving misconduct within 100 days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teachers accused of misconduct should have their cases decided within a speedy 100 days by a special examiner and not be cast into an interminable limbo of waiting, said Kenneth R. Feinberg, the arbitration expert, who investigated teacher discipline at the request of the American Federation of Teachers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan Offered to Overhaul Discipline of Teachers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan Offered To Overhaul Discipline Of Teachers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weingarten, Randi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TEACHERS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T01:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 