llage on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/nyregion/20josephine.html', 'snippet': 'Firefighters who rescued Josephine B. Harris on Sept. 11 called her their guardian angel. They will hoist her coffin at a funeral Mass in Greenwich Village on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cloth interior of her blue steel coffin will be custom-embroidered with the image of a firefighter in full gear, walking hand in hand with an angel. Her prayer cards will display her smiling face on one side and the words of the Fireman’s Prayer on the other.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '9/11 Firefighters to Attend Funeral of Woman They Once Saved', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Funeral of a 9/11 Survivor Will Bring Out Firefighters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T01:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39cf26bf-c8bc-5d66-add4-c48910209fdf', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39cf26bf-c8bc-5d66-add4-c48910209fdf'}, {'abstract': 'Fired by the Vikings with his team in turmoil, Mike Tice is focusing on the little things with the Bears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/football/20tice.html', 'snippet': 'Fired b