', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for former Gov. Don E. Siegelman asked a federal appeals court to overturn his 2006 bribery conviction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSONVILLE, Fla. \x97 Three federal appeals court judges seemed ready on Wednesday to see the convictions of former Gov. Don E. Siegelman of Alabama and the man accused of bribing him in a new light.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/us/SIEGELMAN/SIEGELMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/us/SIEGELMAN/SIEGELMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/us/SIEGELMAN/SIEGELMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judges Take Another Look at Ex-Alabama Governor’s Conviction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judges Take Another Look at Ex-Alabama Governor’s Conviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siegelman, Donald E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scrushy, Richard M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T03:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4475bdaa-a73d-5606-9412-64a4750cc238', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4475bdaa-a73d-5606-9412-64a4750cc238'}, {'abstract': 'Why can’t those who face foreclosure get the same sorts of help as bankrupt companies?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/19/whats-good-for-g-m-is-good-for-homeowners/', 'snippet': 'Why can’t those who face foreclosure get the same sorts of help as bankrupt companies?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have been fully conditioned by now to expect that the rich and powerful will get the biggest slice of whatever pie is being served, while those less fortunate — and less well connected — will get the crumbs. But it still rankles when we witness time and time again how big corporations get deals the little guy can only dream about, especially when a little creative thinking could alter the status quo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Good for G.M. Is Good For Homeowners', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeowner Affordability and Stability Plan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T03:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William D. Cohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c36079-5801-5497-9f8c-aee89d29d637', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c36079-5801-5497-9f8c-aee89d29d637'}, {'abstract': 'With the Nets surprisingly withdrawing from the Carmelo Anthony sweepstakes, the Knicks will instantly leap to the forefront of the discussion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/sports/basketball/20garden.html', 'snippet': 'With the Nets surprisingly withdrawing from the Carmelo Anthony sweepstakes, the Knicks will instantly leap to the forefront of the discussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON \x97 The name had escaped Mike D’Antoni’s lips before he even realized it, and he immediately regretted the subconscious slip. If there is one player who should not be mentioned in casual conversation, it is Carmelo Anthony.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/GARDEN/GARDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 952, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/GARDEN/GARDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/sports/GARDEN/GARDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Spotlight Now Turns to Knicks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anthony Spotlight Now Turns To Knicks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 1, 'majo