'nyt://article/bf7cb346-7502-5270-8a82-ac1ca78e4934'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,426 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,447 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/us/20list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,426 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,447 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,426 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,447 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T04:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/493ee800-6c82-5dc6-b432-6e586f7c74d9', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/493ee800-6c82-5dc6-b432-6e586f7c74d9'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations Security Council unanimously approved sending an additional 2,000 peacekeepers to the Ivory Coast, citing the lack of security facing the more than 9,000 troops and police officers already there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/world/africa/20briefs-UNTOSENDMORE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations Security Council unanimously approved sending an additional 2,000 peacekeepers to the Ivory Coast, citing the lack of security facing the more than 9,000 troops and police officers already there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations Security Council unanimously approved sending an additional 2,000 peacekeepers to the Ivory Coast, citing the lack of security facing the more than 9,000 troops and police officers already there. So many soldiers are required to protect the Golf Hotel, home to Alassane Ouattara, the recognized president, as well as senior United Nations officials, that there are none to spare elsewhere in the country. The new troops are expected to deploy by June. Raila Odinga, Kenya’s prime minister, announced after two days of meetings that the latest African attempt to resolve the crisis had failed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivory Coast: U.N. to Send More Peacekeepers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ivory Coast: U.N. to Send More Peacekeepers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ivory Coast', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T04:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dba1495-e485-59ed-a115-2a6066a46348', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dba1495-e485-59ed-a115-2a6066a46348'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Benedict XVI appointed the president and the governing board of a new financial watchdog aimed at overseeing the Vatican’s finances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/world/europe/20briefs-Vatican.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Benedict XVI appointed the president and the governing board of a new financial watchdog aimed at overseeing the Vatican’s finances.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Pope Benedict XVI on Wednesday appointed the president and the governing board of a new financial watchdog aimed at overseeing the Vatican’s finances and helping it comply with international policies against money laundering and the financing of terrorists. Benedict announced the new agency in December and on Wednesday appointed Cardinal Attilio Nicora, left, already the Holy See’s de-facto finance minister, as its president. The four board members, all laymen, have backgrounds in accounting, law and finance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Vatican: Pope Names Leaders of Financial Monitor', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Vatican: Pope Names Leaders of Financial Monitor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T04:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/54a493da-e2e6-5f0c-9727-0748b0102124', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54a493da-e2e6-5f0c-9727-0748b0102124'}, {'abstract': 'Thirteen civilians crammed into a motorized rickshaw were killed by a roadside bomb in eastern Paktika Province on Wednesday, according to the provincial governor, Muhibullah Samim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/world/asia/20briefs-18AREKILLEDB_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Thirteen civilians crammed into a motorized rickshaw were killed by a roadside bomb in eastern Paktika Province on Wednesday, according to the provincial governor, Muhibullah Samim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirteen civilians crammed into a motorized rickshaw were killed by a roadside bomb in eastern Paktika Province on Wednesday, according to the provincial governor, Muhibullah Samim. The rickshaw was taking the group to visit a clinic in Khoshamand District when it set off the bomb. Also on Wednesday, five border policemen were killed in the Shemolzo District of Zabul Province, close to the Pakistan border, when their vehicle struck a roadside bomb. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: 18 Are Killed by Roadside Bombs', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: 18 Are Killed by Roadside Bombs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T04:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By FAROOQ JAN MANGAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farooq', 'middlename': 'Jan', 'lastname': 'MANGAL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d17d3f6a-28cd-5ab6-ba44-22a557413143', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d17d3f6a-28cd-5ab6-ba44-22a557413143'}, {'abstract': 'The Panel for Educational Policy vote