b957-2b5910f94804'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Langham led a formidable roster of leading men and women through the rigors of Shakespeare, Shaw, Molière, Chekhov and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/theater/20langham.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Langham led a formidable roster of leading men and women through the rigors of Shakespeare, Shaw, Molière, Chekhov and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Langham, a classical theater director who honed his craft in a Nazi prisoner-of-war camp and went on to become the artistic head of the Stratford Shakespeare Festival in Ontario, Canada, and the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis and to direct Shakespeare and Molière on Broadway, died on Saturday at his home in Kent, England. He was 91. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/theater/20langham_art/20langham_art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/20/theater/20langham_art/20langham_art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/20/theater/20langham_art/20langham_art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Langham, Classical Theater Director, Dies at 91', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stratford Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'T