ype_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f8b9503-9731-5b9c-8433-11e9f4ad0067', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f8b9503-9731-5b9c-8433-11e9f4ad0067'}, {'abstract': 'Struggling to placate protesters, Tunisia’s interim government announced steps toward an amnesty for political exiles, including Islamists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/world/africa/21tunis.html', 'snippet': 'Struggling to placate protesters, Tunisia’s interim government announced steps toward an amnesty for political exiles, including Islamists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS \x97 Tunisia’s interim government struggled Thursday to placate protesters demanding the eradication of the country’s former ruling party. The government announced steps toward an amnesty for political exiles, including Islamists. Several cabinet ministers said they were resigning from the old ruling party. And demonstrators outside the party headquarters were met by soldiers who said the building now belonged to the people and who eventually helped pull down the party’s name from the facade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21tunis2/21tunis2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21tunis2/21tunis2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21tunis2/21tunis2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia Takes Step Toward Allowing Exiles to Return', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisian Protesters Demand Break With the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T12:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbe61777-0974-5e1a-8f0b-541b18c8d079', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbe61777-0974-5e1a-8f0b-541b18c8d079'}, {'abstract': 'The bank’s executives say that improvement in its major businesses is a sign that its revamping is starting to take hold.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/morgan-stanleys-quarterly-profits-rise-60-to-600-million/', 'snippet': 'The bank’s executives say that improvement in its major businesses is a sign that its revamping is starting to take hold.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:44 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley’s Quarterly Earnings Increase 60%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Gregory J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T12:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1fa68e2-6c72-5555-a119-facd6c43739f', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1fa68e2-6c72-5555-a119-facd6c43739f'}, {'abstract': 'Sir Elton John headlined a fund-raiser in Beverly Hills — extravagant even when measured against Hollywood events — to aid the legal challenge to Proposition 8.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/elton-john-headlines-glittery-prop-8-fund-raiser/', 'snippet': 'Sir Elton John headlined a fund-raiser in Beverly Hills — extravagant even when measured against Hollywood events — to aid the legal challenge to Proposition 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. – He walked on stage in sunglasses, an earring glittering in one ear. The days of jumping on piano benches were presumably behind him. Still, in 16 songs that lasted over 90 minutes on Wednesday evening, Sir Elton John offered a robust private concert to a relatively intimate audience gathered under a tent in an estate in the Hollywood Hills on a cool California evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elton John Headlines Glittery Prop. 8 Fund-Raiser', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkle, Ronald W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John, Elton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reiner, Rob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beverly Hills (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T12:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be4d51c-fcf7-5db6-83bd-4206e5d21e7f', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be4d51c-fcf7-5db6-83bd-4206e5d21e7f'}, {'abstract': 'Wide receiver Santonio Holmes said if the Jets won the Super Bowl, it would be sweet revenge against the Steelers, who traded him:  “That’s a slap back in those guys’ face for trading me.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/santonio-holmes-revenge-would-be-sweeter-in-super-bowl/', 'snippet': 'Wide receiver Santonio Holmes said if the Jets won the Super Bowl, it would be sweet revenge against the Steelers, who traded him:  “That’s a slap back in those guys’ face for trading me.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A transcript of Santonio Holmes’s conference call with reporters Wednesday, as provided by the N.F.L. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santonio Holmes: Revenge Would Be Sweeter in Super Bowl', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T13:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f7ac79-da14-5366-88ca-ae2c74ff8ff6', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f7ac79-da14-5366-88ca-ae2c74ff8ff