636bc4', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/158d5eae-47c4-5eb2-b43c-d7ca19636bc4'}, {'abstract': 'Y=E, S=I. So?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/barbarous-economics/', 'snippet': 'Y=E, S=I. So?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So I see a number of people saying things along the lines of, “If income always equals spending, then real income can’t possibly change” — and imagining that they’re being wise! More evidence of our descent into a Dark Age of macroeconomics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbarous Economics', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:08:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/758cf888-8cf0-56e1-a2fb-b574dd0cb857', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/758cf888-8cf0-56e1-a2fb-b574dd0cb857'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: A woman who was kidnapped more than 20 years ago is reunited with her family, an investigation opens into how grades were awarded at a highly ranked school; and other regional developments.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/morning-buzz-2/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: A woman who was kidnapped more than 20 years ago is reunited with her family, an investigation opens into how grades were awarded at a highly ranked school; and other regional developments.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It may be sunny now, but snow is on the way again overnight; high temperatures Thursday will be in the 30s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Cuomo Ponders Big Cuts in Work Force', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccbede12-cc0a-5e6c-9ed1-d6ba13a39f65', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccbede12-cc0a-5e6c-9ed1-d6ba13a39f65'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/morning-take-out-166/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERGERS & ACQUISITIONS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/40be278c-ef48-5fbd-bdae-a86f2ad73004', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40be278c-ef48-5fbd-bdae-a86f2ad73004'}, {'abstract': 'Natalie Portman and Ashton Kutcher star in a brisk romantic comedy distinguished by a dose of semi-cynical sexual candor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/movies/21nostringsattached.html', 'snippet': 'Natalie Portman and Ashton Kutcher star in a brisk romantic comedy distinguished by a dose of semi-cynical sexual candor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having recently endured starvation and battered toes in the service of her art, Natalie Portman now encounters another of the ordeals laid out for ambitious young actresses who want to be movie stars. Less than a week after gracing the Golden Globes broadcast in a rose-bedecked gown and collecting an award for her work in “Black Swan,” Ms. Portman pops up on Friday on the big screen in a pre-Valentine’s Day romantic comedy with an instantly forgettable title.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/movies/21string-span/21string-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/21/movies/21string-span/21string-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/movies/21string-span/21string-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/movies/21string-span/21string-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/movies/21string-span/21string-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Firm Commitment to Casual', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'No Strings Attached'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Firm Commitment to Casual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Natalie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kutcher, Ashton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reitman, Ivan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:18:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/798f5109-6162-52b9-ba99-a116dc34415c', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/798f5109-6162-52b9-ba99-a116dc34415c'}, {'abstract': 'Hot toddies and bonfires at an outdoor showing of a movie about Antarctica.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/nocturnalist-a-snowbound-screening/', 'snippet': 'Hot toddies and bonfires at an outdoor showing of a movie about Antarctica.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nocturnalist | A Snowbound Screening', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenpoint (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b78edf2-9774-594e-86a0-628f471c9cf9', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b78edf2-9774-594e-86a0-628f471c9cf9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cooper, the CNN host and “60 Minutes” correspondent, discusses his role as the Book Voice in “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying,” and the efforts of his mother, Gloria Vanderbilt, to expose him to theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/anchor-away-anderson-cooper-on-how-he-landed-in-how-to-succeed-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cooper, the CNN host and “60 Minutes” correspondent, discusses his role as the Book Voice in “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying,” and the efforts of his mother, Gloria Vanderbilt, to expose him to theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anderson Cooper knows it’s been a good, long while since he’s seen a Broadway show – possibly as long ago as the late 1970s, when he was 11 and his mother, Gloria Vanderbilt, took him to see the original Broadway run of “Evita.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anchor Away! Anderson Cooper on How He Landed in ‘How to Succeed’ on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Anderson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a910074c-dcde-515c-b3f4-f92fae0aa31a', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a910074c-dcde-515c-b3f4-f92fae0aa31a'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Eisman, the hedge fund manager who bet against the subprime mortgage market, is considering leaving FrontPoint Partners to start his own shop, another potential blow to a firm dogged by insider trading scandals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/frontpoints-eisman-said-to-start-own-firm/', 'snippet': 'Steve Eisman, the hedge fund manager who bet against the subprime mortgage market, is considering leaving FrontPoint Partners to start his own shop, another potential blow to a firm dogged by insider trading scandals.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:21 p.m. | Updated Steve Eisman, the prominent hedge fund manager who successfully bet against the subprime mortgage market, is considering leaving FrontPoint Partners to open his own shop, another potential blow to a firm dogged by the insider trading scandals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FrontPoint’s Eisman Is Said to Weigh Starting His Own Firm', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/57604865-b744-58b8-901f-b0a8ee21e0a3', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57604865-b744-58b8-901f-b0a8ee21e0a3'}, {'abstract': 'Members of both political parties will mark the anniversary of the J.F.K. presidential inauguration from Jan. 20, 1961, at events in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/john-f-kennedy-inaugurals-50th-anniversary-is-noted/', 'snippet': 'Members of both political parties will mark the anniversary of the J.F.K. presidential inauguration from Jan. 20, 1961, at events in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and lawmakers from both parties on Thursday will celebrate the 50th anniversary of John F. Kennedy’s inauguration as president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John F. Kennedy Inaugural’s 50th Anniversary Is Noted', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d616af41-1259-546b-a7cf-57dbc7a3ca11', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d616af41-1259-546b-a7cf-57dbc7a3ca11'}, {'abstract': 'With a new phone, the Atrix, the once-mighty Motorola makes an impressive bid for the spotlight.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/its-a-phone-its-a-laptop-its-an-atrix/', 'snippet': 'With a new phone, the Atrix, the once-mighty Motorola makes an impressive bid for the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there has been a muted response to what is arguably the most powerful mobile phone currently made – the Atrix – it may be due to its parentage. The phone comes from Motorola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s a Phone, It’s a Laptop, It’s an Atrix', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motorola Mobility Hldg Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T14:46:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiz