0a17a831'}, {'abstract': 'To avoid turf battles, chaotic communications and duplicated efforts, aides said, a significant realignment is under way in the West Wing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/us/politics/21obama.html', 'snippet': 'To avoid turf battles, chaotic communications and duplicated efforts, aides said, a significant realignment is under way in the West Wing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 President Obama will close the office of political affairs at the White House in preparation for the establishment of his re-election headquarters, which will open its doors in Chicago by late March to concentrate on building a national fund-raising and grass-roots operation to rival his first campaign, aides said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/SUB-OBAMA/SUB-OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Will Move Political Operations to Chicago', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Will Move Political Operations to Chicago', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plouffe, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smoot, Julianna', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T16:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42672018-8aa2-54d9-8f54-f7856f74b838', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42672018-8aa2-54d9-8f54-f7856f74b838'}, {'abstract': 'Ronald Barber recalls images of a pool of blood, the sound of a gun, the bullet casings on the ground. But he doesn’t remember Judge John M. Roll trying to save him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/us/21survivor.html', 'snippet': 'Ronald Barber recalls images of a pool of blood, the sound of a gun, the bullet casings on the ground. But he doesn’t remember Judge John M. Roll trying to save him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON \x97 Since the shooting, Ronald Barber has retold his memory of the scene over and over \x97 to his family, to a psychologist friend and to investigators. The vivid images of a pool of blood on the ground, the “pop-pop-pop” sound of a gun and seeing bullet casings on the ground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21survivor2/21survivor2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21survivor2/21survivor2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21survivor2/21survivor2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tucson Survivor Describes Chaos of Rampage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Shooting Survivor, Recurring Images Continue to Haunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject',