little light onto the more mundane corners of deployed life in Afghanistan, “A Year at War,” offers some visual answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Year at War', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year at War: Updates and Questions', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T19:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/81b7ea33-61e6-535f-b05b-9869218034ec', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81b7ea33-61e6-535f-b05b-9869218034ec'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Laurel Nakadate has her first major museum show, featuring photographs and video, at MoMA P.S. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/arts/design/23nakadate.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Laurel Nakadate has her first major museum show, featuring photographs and video, at MoMA P.S. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': '“IT’S a little like sneaking around your old school,” Laurel Nakadate said, flashing a conspiratorial grin as she led a visitor up a staircase to the second floor of the repurposed school building that houses MoMA P.S. 1 in Long Island City, Queens. Closed and quiet on a mid-December day, that exhibition complex would soon display Ms. Nakadate’s first major museum show \x97 “Only the Lonely,” opening Sunday \x97 and she had just moved into a temporary studio there, across the hall from the galleries where t