ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/23f943d5-076c-5c7d-8b86-a98d2d55e7b8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/23f943d5-076c-5c7d-8b86-a98d2d55e7b8'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo would not say whether he planned a major reduction in the state work force but warned that painful choices would have to be made.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/cuomo-warns-of-pain-but-does-not-detail-scale-of-cuts/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo would not say whether he planned a major reduction in the state work force but warned that painful choices would have to be made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POUGHKEEPSIE, N.Y. – Following news reports that he is considering cutting thousands of state jobs, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo repeated on Thursday his warning that the budget he will unveil at the start of February will cause great pain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Warns of Pain but Doesn’t Detail Scale of Cuts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Public Employees Federation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T19:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0ab773c-40e9-5968-9d33-d363e63c63e4', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0ab773c-40e9-5968-9d33-d363e63c63e4'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln Center Theater will have to wait until the fall of 2011 to transfer the play, rather than this spring, because the 40 Broadway houses are all booked', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/for-this-season-the-broadway-landscape-is-dry-for-other-desert-cities/', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Center Theater will have to wait until the fall of 2011 to transfer the play, rather than this spring, because the 40 Broadway houses are all booked', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is how Broadway works nowadays: Lincoln Center Theater producers have a new critically acclaimed play, “Other Desert Cities,” in their Off Broadway space, the Mitzi E. Newhouse Theater. The producers want to capitalize on the strong reviews and transfer the play this spring to a Broadway house, where visibility will be far greater, more money stands be made, and Tony Awards are a possibility. (Off Broadway shows don’t qualify for Tonys.) But at this point Lincoln Center Theater will have to wait until the fall of 2011 to transfer the play, rather than this spring, because the 40 Broadway houses are all booked, according to executives involved with the transfer discussions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For This Season, The Broadway Landscape Is Dry For ‘Other Desert Cities’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T19:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf358753-3b8c-5da6-9493-678b3f13e5d5', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf358753-3b8c-5da6-9493-678b3f13e5d5'}, {'abstract': 'Shares in the insurer tumbled more than 14 percent on Thursday, but only because of a technical reason involving warrants for the company’s stock.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/about-a-i-g-s-stock-price/', 'snippet': 'Shares in the insurer tumbled more than 14 percent on Thursday, but only because of a technical reason involving warrants for the company’s stock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shares in the American International Group plunged more than 14 percent on Thursday, hitting $43.80 in midafternoon trading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'About A.I.G.’s Stock Price …', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T19:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f54786a-b208-5dd8-8dcb-5afcb16895f1', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f54786a-b208-5dd8-8dcb-5afcb16895f1'}, {'abstract': 'The fashions shown during the recently concluded Milan fall/winter 2011 collections were, in a word, manly.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/milan-fashion-week-post-mortem/', 'snippet': 'The fashions shown during the recently concluded Milan fall/winter 2011 collections were, in a word, manly.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#507", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week | Post Mortem', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T19:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/734ed71b-4222-50e5-9c85-0fc9de01349b', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/734ed71b-4222-50e5-9c85-0fc9de01349b'}, {'abstract': 'Radio waves are used to entangle 10 billion pairs of particles in a silicon crystal, making qubits that will linger as long as several seconds \x97 a lifetime in quantum computing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/science/25spin.html', 'snippet': 'Radio waves are used to entangle 10 billion pairs of particles in a silicon crystal, making qubits that will linger as long as several seconds \x97 a lifetime in quantum computing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a step toward a generation of ultrafast computers, physicists have used bursts of radio waves to briefly create 10 billion quantum-entangled pairs of subatomic particles in silicon. The research offers a glimpse of a future computing world in which individual atomic nuclei store and retrieve data and single electrons shuttle it back and forth.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Billions of Entangled Particles Advance Quantum Computing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Billions of Entangled Particles Advance Quantum Computing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morton, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '