int_headline': 'NFL PLAYOFFS | CONFERENCE CHAMPIONSHIPS; Pump, Pump and Pass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roethlisberger, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c19889ec-c244-539b-adf0-5c0a3464ad30', 'word_count': 1365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c19889ec-c244-539b-adf0-5c0a3464ad30'}, {'abstract': 'What to do when your boyfriend comes from a family of noisy eaters, and other problems.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/dear-flofab-they-slurp-they-slouch-they-shovel-they-smack/', 'snippet': 'What to do when your boyfriend comes from a family of noisy eaters, and other problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Florence Fabricant gives advice on the fine points of entertaining at home and eating in restaurants. Have a dining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: They Slurp! They Slouch! They Shovel! They Smack!', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c49ac055-f788-5885-9b4a-347f6c128a3b', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c49ac055-f788-5885-9b4a-347f6c128a3b'}, {'abstract': 'Developed in the federal agency’s Ann Arbor, Mich., lab, the hydraulic hybrid system will be put in duty on the Chrysler Town & Country minivan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/e-p-a-and-chrysler-link-up-for-hybrid-technology-test/', 'snippet': 'Developed in the federal agency’s Ann Arbor, Mich., lab, the hydraulic hybrid system will be put in duty on the Chrysler Town & Country minivan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency and the Chrysler Group announced on Wednesday that they would work together to develop a light-duty hydraulic hybrid vehicle. Current plans call for the system to be installed in the Chrysler Town & Country minivan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. and Chrysler Link Up for Hybrid Technology Test', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANN ARBOR (MICH)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:06:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f37edb25-5fb0-521c-a0f4-0c86ca7dc7e4', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f37edb25-5fb0-521c-a0f4-0c86ca7dc7e4'}, {'abstract': 'Stanford Makishi will step down next month after three years in the post.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/executive-director-of-baryshnikov-arts-center-is-leaving/', 'snippet': 'Stanford Makishi will step down next month after three years in the post.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Stanford Makishi will step down as executive director of the Baryshnikov Arts Center on Feb. 28, the center said on Thursday. Mr. Makishi, 45, a Harvard-educated former dancer, has held the post for three years, serving as the right-hand man of Mikhail Baryshnikov, the founder and artistic director. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Director of Baryshnikov Arts Center Is Leaving', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baryshnikov, Mikhail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Makishi, Stanford', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/becf4637-cfa9-5b93-ad64-c0ed2adc90eb', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/becf4637-cfa9-5b93-ad64-c0ed2adc90eb'}, {'abstract': 'Paprika Steen stars as an alcoholic actress in “Applause,” by Martin Pieter Zandvliet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/movies/21applause.html', 'snippet': 'Paprika Steen stars as an alcoholic actress in “Applause,” by Martin Pieter Zandvliet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art imitates life in “Applause,” though usually it just imitates incomparably greater art. A Danish movie unwisely under the influence, it turns on an alcoholic actress, Thea Barfoed (Paprika Steen), struggling with her boozing ways, estranged children, former husband, fleshy neck and apparently brilliant career. I was great, she says after one performance. I’ll have to take her word for it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/APPLAUSE/APPLAUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/APPLAUSE/APPLAUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/APPLAUSE/APPLAUSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/APPLAUSE/APPLAUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/APPLAUSE/APPLAUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Even on the Wagon, Not Ready for a Close-Up', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Applause'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even on the Wagon, Not Ready for a Close-Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steen, Paprika', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b00e22-35a4-5778-aa47-c39f1c2cf218', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b00e22-35a4-5778-aa47-c39f1c2cf218'}, {'abstract': 'The prize is Israel’s highest literary award for foreigners.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/mcewan-wins-jerusalem-prize/', 'snippet': 'The prize is Israel’s highest literary award for foreigners.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ian McEwan, the author of “Amsterdam,” “Atonement” and “Saturday,” among other books, is the 2011 winner of the Jerusalem Prize, Israel’s highest literary award for foreigners. The award, $10,000, is granted every other year during the Jerusalem International Book Fair, and will be given to him on Feb. 20th. The prize has gone to authors including Bertrand Russell, Susan Sontag, Milan Kundera, Mario Vargas Llosa and Haruki Murakami. It honors writers whose work “promotes the idea of freedom of the individual in society.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McEwan Wins Jerusalem Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEwan, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 