': 'HIBERNATORS BALL', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times: For Children, for Jan. 21-27', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times: For Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puppets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3d003a-d5ee-5196-a560-835ccf7cf2de', 'word_count': 3416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3d003a-d5ee-5196-a560-835ccf7cf2de'}, {'abstract': 'In “Spartacus: Gods of the Arena” we are at a Roman gladiatorial campus where dorm life leaves the shenanigans at the Big Ten looking fairly pathetic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/television/21spartacus.html', 'snippet': 'In “Spartacus: Gods of the Arena” we are at a Roman gladiatorial campus where dorm life leaves the shenanigans at the Big Ten looking fairly pathetic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like AMC’s “Mad Men” the latest series on Starz is a period drama in which the patriarchy dominates, the class system is rigidly delineated, and the cultural attitude toward drinking has yet to fall under the punishing heels of recovery and restraint. As its name suggests, “Spartacus: Gods of the Arena” (beginning on Friday) is set well before the advent of Alcoholics Anonymous but right during the high moment of extreme sports. Specifically we are in the late 70s B.C. in the ancient city of Capua at a Roman gladiatorial campus where dorm life leaves the shenanigans at the Big Ten looking fairly pathetic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/SPARTACUS/SPARTACUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/SPARTACUS/SPARTACUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/SPARTACUS/SPARTACUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/SPARTACUS/SPARTACUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/SPARTACUS/SPARTACUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Adventures of Spartacus Sixpack', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Adventures of Spartacus Sixpack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T21:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk':