 Newtown residents voted to buy the former state psychiatric institution at the center of town, their primary aim was to head off housing developers eying its 185-acre campus. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/wczo/wczo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 212, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/wczo/wczo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 212}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/wczo/wczo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/wczo/wczo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/wczo/wczo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Warily, Newtown Weighs New Housing', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warily, Town Weighs New Housing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0f2a6e-0a1e-5864-9f01-84cbf9d7fc6f', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0f2a6e-0a1e-5864-9f01-84cbf9d7fc6f'}, {'abstract': 'In “Room 17B,” by Parallel Exit, the antics are the thing, and the officemates are in the business of humor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/theater/reviews/21room.html', 'snippet': 'In “Room 17B,” by Parallel Exit, the antics are the thing, and the officemates are in the business of humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tempting to say that Room 17B is like a lot of offices in Manhattan, especially the ones in the financial district: whatever work is being done in there is mysterious and produces no tangible product or benefit. But that’s only partly true. While it’s not clear what line of work the four inhabitants of Room 17B are in, they do generate something of value: laughter. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/ROOM/ROOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/ROOM/ROOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/ROOM/ROOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In This Cubicle World, Actions Speak Loudest', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Room 17B'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In This Cubicle World, Actions Speak Loudest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parallel Exit', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 