epeats itself, the price goes up. Well, not so with this week’s events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been said that each time history repeats itself, the price goes up. Well, not so with this week’s events. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/MISER/MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f101d44c-e462-5c83-92e4-39028d977409', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f101d44c-e462-5c83-92e4-39028d977409'}, {'abstract': 'Gallim Dance is sharing a bill through Saturday with Sidra Bell Dance New York at Dance Theater Workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/dance/21bell.html', 'snippet': 'Gallim Dance is sharing a bill through Saturday with Sidra Bell Dance New York at Dance Theater Workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance Theater Workshop’s Dance Docents program, in which employees are available to answer questions from the audience about the work being performed, has prompted no small amount of eye rolling among the organization’s generally sophisticated fan base. But on Tuesday night I had my first inquiry appropriate for the docent: Why on earth was the workshop presenting Sidra Bell Dance New York and Andrea Miller’s Gallim Dance? And was this a sign of things to come at New York Live Arts, the entity created by the recent merger of the Dance Theater Workshop and the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/BELL/BELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Experiments in the Aggressive and Supernatural', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experiments in the Aggressive and Supernatural', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gallim Dance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c3b1a7-af44-5ecf-ae5b-9285c3524758', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c3b1a7-af44-5ecf-ae5b-9285c3524758'}, {'abstract': 'The Chiara String Quartet performs in the Ecstatic Music Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/music/21chiara.html', 'snippet': 'The Chiara String Quartet performs in the Ecstatic Music Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After kicking off with an exciting eight-hour marathon on Monday, the Ecstatic Music Festival, devoted to collaborations by young artists working on the increasingly permeable border between classical music and pop, began in earnest on Wednesday evening with a concert by the Chiara String Quartet at Merkin Concert Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/CHIARA/CHIARA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical-Pop Border, No Guards in Sight', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical-Pop Border, No Guards in Sight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muhly, Nico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chiara String Quartet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2b7b22-b14b-5e52-a2a5-0e119e244bbc', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2b7b22-b14b-5e52-a2a5-0e119e244bbc'}, {'abstract': 'Children’s paintings created in the 1930s are on display, alongside recent works by New York City students, at the Children’s Museum of the Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/design/21antiques.html', 'snippet': 'Children’s paintings created in the 1930s are on display, alongside recent works by New York City students, at the Children’s Museum of the Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Works Progress Administration kept artists employed during the Great Depression, teaching the masses. In New York City about 50,000 people a week, mostly children, took free painting and drawing classes at community centers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1930s Children’s Art on Display in SoHo', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1930s Children’s Art\nOn Display in SoHo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Museum of the Arts", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e60b85ac-772a-5514-822a-4fe5408267e0', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e60b85ac-772a-5514-822a-4fe5408267e0'}, {'abstract': 'A 60th anniversary exhibition at Tibor de Nagy Gallery celebrates a golden New York moment in which art and poetry mingled and collaborated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/design/21tibor.html', 'snippet': 'A 60th anniversary exhibition at Tibor de Nagy Gallery celebrates a golden New York moment in which art and poetry mingled and collaborated.', 'lead_paragraph': ' I don’t believe in golden ages, but I do believe in golden moments. Culturally speaking, New York City has had its share, and one began at the end of 1950 when Tibor de Nagy Gallery opened on 53rd Street near Third Avenue in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/TIBOR/TIBOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/TIBOR/TIBOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/TIBOR/TIBOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Art Dallied With Poetry on 53rd Street', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Art Dallied With Poetry on 53rd Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tibor de Nagy Gallery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9899fd92-dbb0-59e1-baff-8f423ffc9de6', 'word_count': 1327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9899fd92-dbb0-59e1-baff-8f423ffc9de6'}, {'abstract': 'Dries Van Noten presented his fall collection on Thursday night in a sculpture museum, where the figures were suitably larger than life.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/paris-mens-local-heroes/', 'snippet': 'Dries Van Noten presented his fall collection on Thursday night in a sculpture museum, where the figures were suitably larger than life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men’s fashion owes a lot to uniforms, military and civilian, and contemporary designers seem to love both the traditions as well as the sense of heroism. Dries Van Noten presented his fall collection on Thursday night in a sculpture museum, where the figures were suitably larger than life. White cotton trousers, peacoats with rough fur-trimmed lapels, and chunky fisherman sweaters alluded to the sea, while wide-leg flannel suits and top coats pointed to an elegant urban uniform. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Men’s: Local Heroes', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T22:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/15baed00-8f0e-5d32-9daf-fce959b04a0f', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15baed00-8f0e-5d32-9daf-fce959b04a0f'}, {'abstract': 'Andre Agassi was selected to the International Tennis Hall of Fame and will be inducted on July 9.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/agassi-selected-to-hall-of-fame/', 'snippet': 'Andre Agassi was selected to the International Tennis Hall of Fame and will be inducted on July 9.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When his wife, Stefanie Graf, was inducted into the International Hall of Fame in 2004, Andre Agassi gave a memorable, emotional speech introducing her, giving himself a tough act to follow now that he has been inducted himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agassi Selected to Hall of Fame', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AGASSI, ANDRE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be4dd2a-4cb2-5f44-92fb-5a69aae382ab', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be4dd2a-4cb2-5f44-92fb-5a69aae382ab'}, {'abstract': 'Verizon filed an appeal in Washington, arguing that the F.C.C. overreached last month when it set up enforceable regulations for Internet service providers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/verizon-challenges-new-net-rules/', 'snippet': 'Verizon filed an appeal in Washington, arguing that the F.C.C. overreached last month when it set up enforceable regulations for Internet service providers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The legal challenges to the Federal Communication Commission’s net neutrality order have begun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Challenges New Net Rules', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0cd3bdc-974f-5e31-b958-b1d9c0830c94', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0cd3bdc-974f-5e31-b958-b1d9c0830c94'}, {'abstract': 'Art, fashion and ghosts collide in fordProject, a new gallery in Midtown.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/artifacts-the-curse-of-57th-street/', 'snippet': 'Art, fashion and ghosts collide in fordProject, a new gallery in Midtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening this week of a new gallery in Midtown has generated unusual confusion in the worlds of art and fashion. Because the gallery’s name is fordProject, it has been promoted as a division of Ford Models, and many of us who have seen fashion climb on the back of art — and vice versa – to broaden its audience naturally assumed that the gallery was an offshoot of the agency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | The Curse of 57th Street', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4512801b-f382-5968-94b3-fc1d26ead4d8', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4512801b-f382-5968-94b3-fc1d26ead4d8'}, {'abstract': 'Models backstage at Rick Owens with their hair slicked into little wings.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/hot-licks/', 'snippet': 'Models backstage at Rick Owens with their hair slicked into little wings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Models backstage at Rick Owens with their hair slicked into little wings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot Licks', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/66d1212a-9837-5519-add9-dfc89577dcd1', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66d1212a-9837-5519-add9-dfc89577dcd1'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama persuaded China to take a harder line toward North Korea, which opened the door to new talks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/world/asia/21diplo.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama persuaded China to take a harder line toward North Korea, which opened the door to new talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 President Obama warned President Hu Jintao that if China did not step up its pressure on North Korea, the United States would have to redeploy its forces in Asia to protect itself from a potential North Korean strike on American soil, a senior administration official said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21DIPLO/21DIPLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21DIPLO/21DIPLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/world/21DIPLO/21DIPLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Warning to China Sends Ripples to the Koreas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An American Warning to China Causes a Ripple Effect on the Korean Peninsula', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/172f6ac5-f474-5331-ba27-e14529a74d24', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/172f6ac5-f474-5331-ba27-e14529a74d24'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Way Back,” the new Peter Weir film, escapees from a Siberian gulag attempt a bleak, demoralizing 4,000-mile trek to freedom in India during the early 1940s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/movies/21way.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Way Back,” the new Peter Weir film, escapees from a Siberian gulag attempt a bleak, demoralizing 4,000-mile trek to freedom in India during the early 1940s.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Way Back,” a heroically minded survival story from Peter Weir, tells the possibly true tale of a group of prisoners who fled a Soviet gulag in 1940 and walked, wandered and all but crawled to freedom. For months a veritable league of national types, united by desperation and the English language, push through the cold and the heat, slipping through forests and across mountains and deserts. Surviving on moldering provisions and precious scraps of protein, dodging predators, two-legged and four-, the travelers embody a besieged humanity that might have been more stirring if their torment were in a rather less exquisite frame.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/WAY/WAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/WAY/WAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/WAY/WAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/WAY/WAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/WAY/WAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pushing the Limits of Endurance', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Way Back'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pushing the Limits of Endurance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weir, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a854a55-b28f-57c5-87a9-f5f3e59bd59f', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a854a55-b28f-57c5-87a9-f5f3e59bd59f'}, {'abstract': 'A film called “Romeo and Juliet in Yiddish” combines elements of the play with plot points from the actors’ real lives.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/20/a-familiar-story-of-boy-meets-girl-but-in-yiddish/', 'snippet': 'A film called “Romeo and Juliet in Yiddish” combines elements of the play with plot points from the actors’ real lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Shakespeare’s tragedy, Romeo is so steeped in love poetry that Juliet accuses him of kissing “by the book.” By contrast, Lazer Weiss, who plays the lead role in the new film “Romeo and Juliet in Yiddish,” didn’t understand the concept of romantic love until he was in his 20s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Familiar Story of Boy Meets Girl, but in Yiddish', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hasidism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yiddish Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-20T23:17:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jed Lipinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24d20e3-6fc4-5abb-a0ed-f38893b9679d', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24d20e3-6fc4-5abb-a0ed-f38893b9679d'}, {'abstract': 'Manhattan is awash in antiques fairs this weekend, including the Winter Antiques Show, the American Antiques Show and the New York Ceramics Fair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/arts/design/21fairs.html', 'snippet': 'Manhattan is awash in antiques fairs this weekend, including the Winter Antiques Show, the American Antiques Show and the New York Ceramics Fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is Everything Old Is New Again Week in New York, with antiques fairs and exhibitions popping up all over Manhattan. This weekend, three of the most lavishly expansive are displaying collectibles of almost every conceivable kind, from ancient Egyptian sculpture to midcentury modern décor. Each has a distinctly different appeal.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/FAIRS-3/FAIRS-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/FAIRS-3/FAIRS-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/FAIRS-3/FAIRS-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Smorgasbord of Fine Art, the Strange and the Old', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Smorgasbord of Fine Art, the Strange and the Old', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject