ng through their property.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21TTTRANSMISSION/21TTTRANSMISSION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21TTTRANSMISSION/21TTTRANSMISSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/us/21TTTRANSMISSION/21TTTRANSMISSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lack of Transmission Lines Is Restricting Wind Power', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lack of Transmission Lines Is Restricting Wind Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:25:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Galbraith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galbraith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b792359-8630-5ebe-a6d1-c88ce76da61b', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b792359-8630-5ebe-a6d1-c88ce76da61b'}, {'abstract': 'Holiday shoppers relied on the its search tools, helping to increase revenue, and a research firm said Google’s share of display ad revenue had grown significantly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/technology/21google.html', 'snippet': 'Holiday shoppers relied on the its search tools, helping to increase revenue, and a research firm said Google’s share of display ad revenue had grown significantly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google’s strong fourth-quarter earnings proved that it is now firmly ensconced in e-commerce, and also showed that, with its Android operating system and related apps, it is smoothly transitioning to the mobile world.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Google, a Boost From E-Commerce', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Google, a Boost From E-Commerce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/698876c5-f77d-52d5-bd76-7143a669a798', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/698876c5-f77d-52d5-bd76-7143a669a798'}, {'abstract': 'Both Gov. Rick Perry and Lt. Gov. David Dewhurst are positioning themselves for runs for higher office, and their moves would set off an avalanche of others by Texas Republican officehol