ttee voted that the agency approve the first test that can show Alzheimer’s in the brain of a living person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An advisory committee to the Food and Drug Administration recommended unanimously Thursday that the agency approve the first test \x97 a brain scan \x97 that can show the characteristic plaques of Alzheimer’s disease in the brain of a living person. The approval was contingent on radiologists agreeing on what the scans say and doctors being trained in how to read the scans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Sees Promise in Alzheimer’s Imaging Drug', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alzheimer’s Test For Live Patients Clears a Hurdle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avid Radiopharmaceuticals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Testing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lilly, Eli, & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6476ccba-10eb-5364-a96b-76acc0378ceb', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6476ccba-10eb-5364-a96b-76acc0378ceb'}, {'abstract': 'Atlanta has moved from having the third-worst congestion in the nation to having the 10th worst, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/us/21atlanta.html', 'snippet': 'Atlanta has moved from having the third-worst congestion in the nation to having the 10th worst, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA \x97 Traffic is Atlanta’s Godzilla, a monster of gigantic proportions that seems too big to defeat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/ATLANTA/ATLANTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/us/ATLANTA/ATLANTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/us/ATLANTA/ATLANTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Traffic Survey Shows Movement in Rankings, if Not on Roads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traffic Survey Shows Movement in Rankings, if Not on Roads; For Atlanta, Better, But Still Short of Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiz