 torrential rains caused mudslides in mountain towns north of Rio de Janeiro, the death toll has risen to at least 747 people, with over 300 missing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/world/americas/21briefs-Brazil.html', 'snippet': 'More than a week after torrential rains caused mudslides in mountain towns north of Rio de Janeiro, the death toll has risen to at least 747 people, with over 300 missing.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More than a week after torrential rains caused mudslides in mountain towns north of Rio de Janeiro, the death toll has risen to at least 747 people, while rescue workers struggle to locate an additional 333 people who are still missing. A Red Cross helicopter involved in the rescue effort crashed in strong winds in Nova Friburgo, where the bodies of eight family members were found and carried out, above, on Thursday. A military spokesman said the crew and passengers suffered only light injuries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Toll Rises Again in Mudslides', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: Toll Rises Again in Mudslides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:36:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Myrna Domit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Myrna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Domit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'orga