ns, were killed in an insurgent attack in the Bala Murghab district of Badghis Province on Tuesday. On Thursday, the coalition amended the report, saying the two soldiers were cleaning their weapons when an Afghan soldier approached them with an M-16 rifle and asked to use their equipment to clean his weapon. The Italians noticed that the Afghan soldier’s rifle was loaded and asked him to unload it. The Afghan soldier reacted by shooting the Italians and then fleeing the outpost, NATO said. One soldier was killed and the other wounded. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Soldier Killed by Afghan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Soldier Killed by Afghan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T01:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Rivera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rivera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4e8f97d-3212-5c06-9dcd-6f73d8826e15', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4e8f97d-3212-5c06-9dcd-6f73d8826e15'}, {'abstract': 'Defenders of the fading Fairgrounds Speedway, which sits on city-owned land, made their case against calls for development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/2