.html', 'snippet': 'The grass field, on which the N.F.C. championship game will be played Sunday, can be scuffed, squishy or rock hard — even all three at once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE FOREST, Ill. \x97 It has been called Chicago’s Soldier Field since the 1920s as a memorial to World War I armed forces, which may surprise some recent opposing football teams who thought it was so named because an army marched across it \x97 with tanks in tow.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Bears Players Are Wary of Soldier Field’s Slippery Turf', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Bears Players Are Wary Of Soldier Field’s Slippery Turf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T02:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76540049-390d-548f-9e2b-c5d2f92fceec', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76540049-390d-548f-9e2b-c5d2f92fceec'}, {'abstract': 'Katawba Battersbee was facing eviction from her apartment in Harlem, but with a $1,849 grant from the Community Service Society of New York, she was able to her pay back what she owed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/nyregion/21neediest.html', 'snippet': 'Katawba Battersbee was facing eviction from her apartment in Harlem, but with a $1,849 grant from the Community Service Society of New York, she was able to her pay back what she owed.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When a woman responsible for hiring at Amtrak asked her what sort of work she could do, Katawba Battersbee had an answer ready. “Well,” she said, “I’m personable.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/nyregion/21NEEDIEST/21NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/nyregion/21NEEDIEST/21NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/nyregion/21NEEDIEST/21NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting a Winding Job Path, With a Smile', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charting a Winding Job Path, With a Smile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Service Society of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T02:06:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e4efdfd-48ae-53cf-be39-46e2ca3bb723', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt