dgets: let corporations lend their names to schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Chicago’s financially ailing public school system struggling to improve academic performance at its 675 public schools, education has emerged as a central issue in the municipal election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pulse: Name that School, Trim That Deficit', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pulse: Name That School,\nTrim That Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T03:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By LORRAINE FORTE (CATALYST CHICAGO)', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lorraine', 'middlename': 'Forte', 'lastname': 'CATALYST', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7981acc8-1ffb-5cb2-8250-d528ea60f98e', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7981acc8-1ffb-5cb2-8250-d528ea60f98e'}, {'abstract': 'A response to an article about the repeal of the Health Care law in the House of Representatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/opinion/l21health.html', 'snippet': 'A response to an article about the repeal of the Health Care law in the House of Representatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Repeal Vote', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None,