 to his life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordon S. Murray, a former Wall Street executive who chose not to go quietly into the night, writing and publishing himself a popular paperback guide for ordinary investors while he was struggling with terminal cancer, died Saturday at his home in Burlingame, Calif., days before his book was scheduled to come out in hardcover. He was 60.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/books/21murrayimg/21murrayimg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/books/21murrayimg/21murrayimg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/books/21murrayimg/21murrayimg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gordon Murray, Retired Wall St. Executive, Dies at 60; Wrote Investment Guide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gordon Murray, Wall Street Retiree and Author, Dies at 60', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse First Boston Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T03:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/503aaa60-8479-5340-8a8d-0ff8c7d0338a', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/503aaa60-8479-5340-8a8d-0ff8c7d0338a'}, {'abstract': 'The Afghanistan leader’s order to postpone the opening of Parliament will only make the fight against the Taliban harder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/opinion/21fri1.html', 'snippet': 'The Afghanistan leader’s order to postpone the opening of Parliament will only make the fight against the Taliban harder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took particular audacity for President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan to order Parliament to delay this weekend’s opening session while an unconstitutional court he appointed re-investigates charges of fraud in last fall’s parliamentary vote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Karzai’s Latest', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Karzai&#8217;s Latest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pashtun (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T03:37:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/37032134-821c-5b09-a9e6-6a9821e0f1c7', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37032134-821c-5b09-a9e6-6a9821e0f1c7'}, {'abstract': 'The first President Bush and others who led the Persian Gulf war of 1991 gathered to say that “we got this one right.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/us/politics/21bush.html', 'snippet': 'The first President Bush and others who led the Persian Gulf war of 1991 gathered to say that “we got this one right.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLLEGE STATION, Tex. \x97 The first President Bush, now 86, walked unsteadily to his seat on the stage. Former Vice President Dick Cheney, who was Mr. Bush’s defense secretary, spoke as a mechanical device pumped his failing heart. The others were grayer, balder or bearers of the scars of fresher wars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Band of Brothers’ Mark Gulf War Anniversary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;Band of Brothers&#8217; Mark Gulf War Anniversary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Dick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Colin L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Persian Gulf War', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T03:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7a8d3ff-8334-56a4-8a5a-b9a8ecd142ca', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7a8d3ff-8334-56a4-8a5a-b9a8ecd142ca'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Long’s perfect ride in the Quiksilver in Memory of Eddie Aikau in Hawaii in 2009 helped pull the focus away from tow surfing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/22surfing.html', 'snippet': 'Greg Long’s perfect ride in the Quiksilver in Memory of Eddie Aikau in Hawaii in 2009 helped pull the focus away from tow surfing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Long plans his life and surfing adventures from a spartan garage apartment in San Clemente, Calif., about a mile from his boyhood home. On a recent afternoon, Long, a fit and wiry 27-year-old, tracked a major storm on his laptop in order to time a trip to Hawaii. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YSURFING1/YSURFING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YSURFING1/YSURFING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YSURFING1/YSURFING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YSURFING1/YSURFING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YSURFING1/YSURFING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'King of Big Waves Puts Attention Back on Paddle Surfing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King of the Big Waves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T04:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Dixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe585751-58eb-5200-be0d-aa300dc3ffc5', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe585751-58eb-5200-be0d-aa300dc3ffc5'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican is watching the sex scandal engulfing the Italian prime minister, Silvio Berlusconi, “with concern,” its secretary of state, Cardinal Tarcisio Bertone, said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/world/europe/21briefs-Vatican.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican is watching the sex scandal engulfing the Italian prime minister, Silvio Berlusconi, “with concern,” its secretary of state, Cardinal Tarcisio Bertone, said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Vatican is watching the sex scandal engulfing the Italian prime minister, Silvio Berlusconi, “with concern,” its secretary of state, Cardinal Tarcisio Bertone, said Thursday, the news agency ANSA reported. The cardinal’s remarks are a sign of Mr. Berlusconi’s growing political weakness a week after prosecutors began investigating whether he compensated “a significant number” of women, including a minor, for sex. The prime minister denies all wrongdoing. According to ANSA, Cardinal Bertone said the Roman Catholic Church urged greater “morality” and “legality” in public life, especially from those holding public office. His remarks were seen as lending support to centrist politicians who seek to oust Mr. Berlusconi. In a television interview on Wednesday, the minor, Karima el-Mahroug, denied that she had sex with Mr. Berlusconi or asked for money in exchange for her silence, as wiretapped phone conversations published in the Italian news media this week suggested. ', 'print_section':