y Hecate. (2) A hobgoblin, spectre, phantom.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/daily-lexeme-empusa/', 'snippet': '(1) In classical sense: A hobgoblin or spectre supposed to be sent by Hecate. (2) A hobgoblin, spectre, phantom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s word, in association with the scholarly Oxford English Dictionary, is', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Lexeme: Empusa', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T09:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c796e5-fd4f-57ff-8f3a-0fe5ee10bea4', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c796e5-fd4f-57ff-8f3a-0fe5ee10bea4'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Whether it was a local, national or international story about politics, sports, science, technology, music, fashion, food or someone famous, let us know what’s caught your attention in the news in the last month, and why.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/what-news-stories-have-surprised-you-recently/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Whether it was a local, national or international story about politics, sports, science, technology, music, fashion, food or someone famous, let us know what’s caught your attention in the news in the last month, and why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the New York Region section of The Times this week, there was a story headlined “Woman Abducted as Infant in 1987 Meets Family.” In the Science section there was a story about a dog who knows 1,022 nouns. In 