ips, the Bears and the Packers have rarely been good at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Bears and the Green Bay Packers are two of the storied franchises in the N.F.L., with 21 championships between them and a rivalry that dates to the early 1920s. So how have they gone 70 years without meeting in the playoffs?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bears and Packers in Postseason: A History of Missing Each Other', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T10:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Coffin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coffin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/33f939f6-aacd-55d0-88ce-9726d3d50254', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33f939f6-aacd-55d0-88ce-9726d3d50254'}, {'abstract': 'From Jan. 24 to Feb. 6, Gastrofestival celebrates all aspects of the culinary landscape of Madrid, including food and wine’s relationship to art, cinema, theater, fashion and literature, in venues around the city.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/surveying-madrids-culinary-landscape/', 'snippet': 'From Jan. 24 to Feb. 6, Gastrofestival celebrates all aspects of the culinary landscape of Madrid, including food and wine’s relationship to art, cinema, theater, fashion and literature, in venues around the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though Madrid Fusion, which runs Jan. 25 to 27, is the more established and exclusive event, this year, for the second time, there’s an accompanying event intended to examine the relationship between food and wine and the rest of the cultural spectrum. From Jan. 24 to Feb. 6, Gastrofestival celebrates all aspects of the culinary landscape of Madrid, including food and wine’s relationship to art, cinema, theater, fashion and literature, in venues around the city. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surveying Madrid’s Culinary Landscape', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T11:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/495ad60b-9105-5d6c-9773-ec4f24138be0', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/495ad60b-9105-5d6c-9773-ec4f24138be0'}, {'abstract': 'Everybody wants to bring the federal deficit under control, but a poll finds lots of contradictions in  people’s ideas about how this might be done. The Republican Study Group has offered up its own blueprint.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/the-early-word-facing-the-music/', 'snippet': 'Everybody wants to bring the federal deficit under control, but a poll finds lots of contradictions in  people’s ideas about how this might be done. The Republican Study Group has offered up its own blueprint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline'