-8fce111b6a2d'}, {'abstract': '“Burma Soldier” traces the life of a soldier from the battlefield to the opposition and eventually to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/world/asia/22myanmar.html', 'snippet': '“Burma Soldier” traces the life of a soldier from the battlefield to the opposition and eventually to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — It is the most vilified army in Southeast Asia, known for crushing pro-democracy demonstrations in Myanmar and for its brutal suppression of ethnic groups seeking self-rule in the region’s longest-running civil war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22myanmar-span/22myanmar-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22myanmar-span/22myanmar-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22myanmar-span/22myanmar-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22myanmar-span/22myanmar-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22myanmar-span/22myanmar-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentary Shows Rare Look at Dissent in Myanmar Military', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind the Facade\nOf Myanmar’s Army', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi, Daw', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T14:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Mydans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mydans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f90afe82-26ac-546c-8940-a5fdb61e19ac', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f90afe82-26ac-546c-8940-a5fdb61e19ac'}, {'abstract': 'Help with finding shared rides, F.D.I.C. overdraft rules and other consumer-focused items from Friday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/friday-reading-ride-sharing-apps/', 'snippet': 'Help with finding shared rides, F.D.I.C. overdraft rules and other consumer-focused items from Friday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Ride-Sharing Apps', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T14:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d8cd78-e1ea-560c-a71d-081942189773', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d8cd78-e1ea-560c-a71d-081942189773'}, {'abstract': 'Figuring out if your company qualifies for the tax credit isn’t as simple as it sounds.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/looking-to-the-affordable-care-act-for-help/', 'snippet': 'Figuring out if your company qualifies for the tax credit isn’t as simple as it sounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that 2010 is complete, I can see what kind of help Obamacare — sorry, the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act — will give me with my health insurance bills. I mentioned in a previous post that my insurance rates for 2011 were a little lower than they had been in 2010 (although I expect them to resume their regular upward march next year). I own a small, struggling manufacturing company that has been providing health care to my people even though it’s a stretch. Surely the Affordable Care Act will come to my rescue! But the devil is always in the details, particularly when Congress decides to “help.” So the first thing to check: Am I eligible for the tax credit? Here’s what I found in the guidelines issued by the Internal Revenue Service:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking to the Affordable Care Act For Help', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T14:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entr