-season sports contests involving their local teams are accompanied by what are now wagering rituals.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The playoff ritual has become a political staple: Days before a big game, mayors or governors feel compelled to make wagers distinctive of their cities or states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/nyregion/22wagesimg/22wagesimg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 562, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Politicians, Big Games Mean Odd Bets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Politicians, Big Games Mean Odd Bets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rendell, Edward G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravenstahl, Luke', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T15:34:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b0bf656-705e-5217-8f1a-a30a3389020c', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b0bf656-705e-5217-8f1a-a30a3389020c'}, {'abstract': 'The Costume Designers Guild announced its nominees and contemporary fare dominated, including “Black Swan.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/hoodies-corsets-and-avian-transformations/', 'snippet': 'The Costume Designers Guild announced its nominees and contemporary fare dominated, including “Black Swan.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Hoodies and corsets, sweats and power suits are all being celebrated as the year’s best cinematic outfits by the Costume Designers Guild. The group announced its nominees on Friday and there were more nominees in the contemporary film category than either period or fantasy. The Academy usually favors period fare, so maybe it will take a page from the guild – the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees, Local 892 – and nominate “The Fighter,” “The King’s Speech” or “True Grit.” The contemporary hopefuls are “Black Swan,” the not-at-all campy “Burlesque,” “Inception,” “The Social Network” (go hoodies!) and “Wall Street: Money Never Sleeps.” The fantasy films are “Alice in Wonderland,” “Tron: Legacy” and “The Tempest.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoodies, Corsets and Avian Transformations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARONOFSKY, DARREN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Designers Guild', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rodarte', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T15:44:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cc5acda-