pet': 'This perplexing turn of phrase is extremely common, even among careful writers and speakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Allen Pinsky e-mails: “Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo used the phrase ‘cannot be underestimated’ twice in his inaugural address. My interpretation of this is the reader/listener couldn’t possibly think lower of the situation or person. As he was referring to the degree of economic suffering, shouldn’t he have said either ‘cannot be overestimated’ or ‘should not be underestimated’ in this context?”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Cannot Be Underestimated’', 'kicker': 'On Language', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Language: &#8220;Cannot Be Underestimated&#8221;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T15:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c1f5cc-fcc6-54ac-a933-ab9ce5b33b63', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c1f5cc-fcc6-54ac-a933-ab9ce5b33b63'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s effort to weed out needless rules will probably find that regulations reviled by some are cherished by others, analysts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/business/22regulate.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s effort to weed out needless rules will probably find that regulations reviled by some are cherished by others, analysts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 There is a federal regulation that dictates that place names on new hig