paris-fashion-week-an-old-lapel-is-new-again/', 'snippet': 'At Dries Van Noten, plenty swirled beneath the opaque surface of the designer’s intent, from Bowie glam to aristocratic refinement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Dries Van Noten, plenty swirled beneath the opaque surface of the designer’s intent, from Bowie glam to aristocratic refinement. But clear understanding could be found in the left lapel of the collection’s jackets. These were doubled: a white, navy or fur second layer buttoned to the inside of the jacket and folded around on top, duplicating the true left lapel. Graphically, the effect was a contrasting sweep across the chest, almost a sash, reminiscent of military regalia. According to Van Noten, this sort of construction has its origins in the military uniforms for which lapels were first invented. Often one would be buttoned across the neck for extra warmth, but because that interrupted the shape (particularly a problem if any battle medals happened to be hanging there), a second lapel was needed to cover the chest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Fashion Week | An Old Lapel Is New Again', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9e6246b-62a9-5f86-a2c2-2a5fac803e4a', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9e6246b-62a9-5f86-a2c2-2a5fac803e4a'}, {'abstract': 'Jerricho Cotchery’s teammates said they probably would not have made it to the championship game without the receiver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/football/22cotchery.html', 'snippet': 'Jerricho Cotchery’s teammates said they probably would not have made it to the championship game without the receiver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — Jerricho Cotchery has played football for 21 years, since he was 7 in Birmingham, Ala., and to do something for that long, especially at a high level, requires a lot of emotion. Still, he loves football.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/22cotchery-web1/22cotchery-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/22cotchery-web1/22cotchery-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/22cotchery-web1/22cotchery-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/22cotchery-web1/22cotchery-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/22cotchery-web1/22cotchery-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cotchery Provides Calm in Jets’ Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among a Boisterous Bunch of Jets, Cotchery Remains Calm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotchery, Jerricho', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f8b2502-72fb-5785-bfb2-7b62622a9f73', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f8b2502-72fb-5785-bfb2-7b62622a9f73'}, {'abstract': 'Green Bay’s Tramon Williams has emerged as one of the biggest stars of the N.F.L. postseason. So why wasn’t he drafted?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/football/22packers.html', 'snippet': 'Green Bay’s Tramon Williams has emerged as one of the biggest stars of the N.F.L. postseason. So why wasn’t he drafted?', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. \x97 There is no longer doubt that Tramon Williams, the dynamic cornerback of the Green Bay Packers, has the skills to succeed in the N.F.L.: athletic ability, great instincts, smarts and a willingness to work. Williams demonstrated those attributes in the last two weeks, intercepting three passes, one for a touchdown, to help the Packers reach the N.F.C. championship game against the Chicago Bears on Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/packers/packers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/packers/packers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/packers/packers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':