 We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/defbedea-65b6-56b9-8302-a5025c47bced', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/defbedea-65b6-56b9-8302-a5025c47bced'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan, chairman of the House budget committee, will give his party’s response to President Obama’s State of the Union address next week.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/paul-ryan-to-deliver-state-of-the-union-response/', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan, chairman of the House budget committee, will give his party’s response to President Obama’s State of the Union address next week.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:36 p.m. | Updated Representative Paul Ryan of Wisconsin, chairman of the House budget committee and the point person for the Republican efforts to cut spending, will give his party’s official response to President Obama’s State of the Union address next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Ryan to Deliver State of the Union Response', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/576c80a8-c7ff-5f98-aba3-7fdb4b300f94', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/576c80a8-c7ff-5f98-aba3-7fdb4b300f94'}, {'abstract': 'We have finished our work in Ethiopia, having collected a vast array of fossils that is noteworthy for its lack of palm specimens.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/a-last-look-at-mush-valley/', 'snippet': 'We have finished our work in Ethiopia, having collected a vast array of fossils that is noteworthy for its lack of palm specimens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bonnie F. Jacobs, a paleobotanist at Southern Methodist University, writes from Ethiopia, where she is studying fossils of ancient plant and animal life. The current field season in the Mush Valley of Ethiopia is financed by a grant to Ellen Currano of Miami University, Ohio, from the National Geographic Society’s Committee for Research and Exploration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Look at Mush Valley', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bonnie F. Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bonnie', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae1cc925-992c-56da-afdf-e0c952d30952', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae1cc925-992c-56da-afdf-e0c952d30952'}, {'abstract': 'Nicholas Delbanco asks why some artists mature early and run out of steam, while others gain momentum in old age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/books/review/Allen-t.html', 'snippet': 'Nicholas Delbanco asks why some artists mature early and run out of steam, while others gain momentum in old age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question of “old-age art” is mysterious and perennially fascinating. Creative artists who continue to work late in life so often seem to undergo a sea change: a distillation, a new intensity, a sloughing off of excess and ornament in favor of deep essentials. W. B. Yeats, himself a notable example of the phenomenon, provided an image for it: “Though leaves are many, the root is one; / Through all the lying days of my youth / I swayed my leaves and flowers in the sun; / Now I may wither into the truth.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/allen/allen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 691, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/allen/allen-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/arts/allen/allen-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Late Style', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Late Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delbanco, Nicholas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/757d1489-04da-55ee-80b4-9d2af84e27e6', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757d1489-04da-55ee-80b4-9d2af84e27e6'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly two weeks after a gunshot passed through her brain, Representative Gabrielle Giffords headed to a rehabilitation center in Houston to continue her recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/us/22giffords.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly two weeks after a gunshot passed through her brain, Representative Gabrielle Giffords headed to a rehabilitation center in Houston to continue her recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON \x97 Nearly two weeks after a gunman shot her in the head at an outdoor meeting with voters, Representative Gabrielle Giffords was transferred by air Friday to Memorial Hermann hospital here to begin what is likely to be a long and arduous rehabilitation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/us/GIFFORDS-1/GIFFORDS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/us/GIFFORDS-1/GIFFORDS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/us/GIFFORDS-1/GIFFORDS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/us/GIFFORDS-1/GIFFORDS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/us/GIFFORDS-1/GIFFORDS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giffords Arrives at Rehabilitation Facility in Houston', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Giffords, Houston Marks Start of Rehabilitation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c8bbda1-9eca-5103-8c59-e4e975559858', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c8bbda1-9eca-5103-8c59-e4e975559858'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets are at once the most riveting team in the N.F.L. playoffs and the most maddening. Luckily, any Super Bowl combination this year should be compelling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/football/22leading.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets are at once the most riveting team in the N.F.L. playoffs and the most maddening. Luckily, any Super Bowl combination this year should be compelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It being Friday, almost everyone has run out of things to say about the teams in the N.F.L. conference championship games on Sunday. Yes, the buildup between games is part of the N.F.L.’s charms, but, by Friday, charm is showing some signs of fatigue. Can you read another article about how Pittsburgh is slowly embracing Ben Roethlisberger? Have you had it up to here with how much Bears and Packers fans hate each other?', 'source': 'The New York Times'