as in many cases the “biggest source of profits in their global operations.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 American corporate leaders took away from China’s president this week a partly comforting, partly maddening view on which both sides could agree: like it or not, they will increasingly depend on each other.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China and U.S. Businesses See Gains in Deeper Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China and U.S. Businesses See Gains in Deeper Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d58fe9-79ce-5dab-9283-e20e491d0ef7', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d58fe9-79ce-5dab-9283-e20e491d0ef7'}, {'abstract': 'This memoir recalls the heady, scary times of an 11-year-old Cuban’s introduction to America in the early 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/books/review/Mishan-t.html', 'snippet': 'This memoir recalls the heady, scary times of an 11-year-old Cuban’s introduction to America in the early 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1962, Carlos Eire found himself, at age 11, in a refugee camp for Cuban children on the edge of the Florida Ever\xadglades, staring at a chicken sandwich. It was a pallid, perfectly bisected square. “Where are the feathers?” he wondered. “Where are the feet, or the beak, or the blood and offal? Who dismembered this lumpy, clucking creature and turned it into a geometry lesson?”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost Boy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost Boy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eire, Carlos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/27a43d2d-a425-56eb-9ef1-4c2ec53ab839', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27a43d2d-a425-56eb-9ef1-4c2ec53ab839'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Roddick used a combination of big serves and overall consistency to beat Robin Haase, 2-6, 7-6 (2), 6-2, 6-2.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/roddick-grinds-on-to-the-fourth-round/', 'snippet': 'Andy Roddick used a combination of big serves and overall consistency to beat Robin Haase, 2-6, 7-6 (2), 6-2, 6-2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For two sets on Friday, Robin Haase of the Netherlands overpowered the No. 8 seed Andy Roddick. Taking advantage of Roddick’s tentative, defensive play, a fearless Haase was rewarded for his aggression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roddick Grinds On to the Fourth Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T16:51:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Lin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f61ef82-5487-5307-a542-e133f9982c5d', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f61ef82-5487-5307-a542-e133f9982c5d'}, {'abstract': 'George Ranalli combined two apartments on West 15th Street into a place almost entirely of his own space-saving design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/realestate/23habi.html', 'snippet': 'George Ranalli combined two apartments on West 15th Street into a place almost entirely of his own space-saving design.', 'lead_paragraph': ' IN 1895, a handsome brick and limestone building with soaring oak-framed windows was erected on the corner of 15th Street and Sixth Avenue. The five-story structure, one of dozens of stately cast-iron concoctions that lined the Ladies’ Mile, spent much of its life as a furniture factory, with a showroom on the ground floor.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/habi-3/habi-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/realestate/habi-3/habi-3-articleLarge.jpg', 