askan winter take their toll on a marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening passages of David Vann’s swift and beautifully written first novel, “Caribou Island,” introduce Gary and Irene, a long-married couple who have decided (well, Gary has decided) to build a cabin on an island in the middle of a remote Alaskan lake. The mood grows uneasy as they encounter a progression of small mishaps: a threatening storm, an overloaded hull, an accident near the start of the trip that sends a steady stream of water into the struggling boat. Gary pushes on nevertheless, and the boat lunges through the water farther and farther from shore.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/books/review/Canty-t_CA0/Canty-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/books/review/Canty-t_CA0/Canty-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/books/review/Canty-t_CA0/Canty-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/books/review/Canty-t_CA0/Canty-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/books/review/Canty-t_CA0/Canty-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Only Bitterness Remains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Only Bitterness Remains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vann, David', 'rank': 1, 'majo