nce of the painful condition among people 60 and older who had been inoculated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The herpes zoster vaccine, which has already proved effective for preventing shingles in a large clinical trial, may be even more effective in broad clinical practice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aging: Shingles Vaccine Shows Promise for Older Adults', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aging: Shingles Vaccine Shows Promise for Many', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shingles (Disease)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814372b2-9896-5c94-8aab-1b1fd17fd7eb', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814372b2-9896-5c94-8aab-1b1fd17fd7eb'}, {'abstract': 'Kohlrabi, rutabagas, turnips and celery root are among the winter vegetables showcased in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/giving-root-vegetables-their-due/', 'snippet': 'Kohlrabi, rutabagas, turnips and celery root are among the winter vegetables showcased in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Food writers tend to be exuberant about spring and summer vegetables, but a bit muted about cold-weather produce,” writes Martha Rose Shulman in this week’s Recipes for Health. “That’s too bad: There are plenty of delicious, comforting dishes to be made with vegetables like kohlrabi, rutabaga, celeriac, carrots and turnips.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Root Vegetables Their Due', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Bilanow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilanow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/13576f98-2f08-50f2-8112-6f1874c3aebc', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13576f98-2f08-50f2-8112-6f1874c3aebc'}, {'abstract': 'Blast from the Past: A defense of not treating stock option costs as an expense.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/stock-option-accounting-again/', 'snippet': 'Blast from the Past: A defense of not treating stock option costs as an expense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I wrote the preceding post criticizing Senator Joe Lieberman for his efforts to block stock option accounting, I had no idea that there are still people who deem it bad accounting to expense the value of stock options. (As opposed to those who quarrel with how we estimate the value, which is a subject where there is plenty of room for argument.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stock Option Accounting, Again', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stock Options and Purchase Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:04:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_de