[{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ec68780-9afe-50b9-9e9c-17794e658800', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ec68780-9afe-50b9-9e9c-17794e658800'}, {'abstract': 'Menopausal women taking escitalopram, sold as Lexapro, averaged 1.41 fewer hot flashes per day than in those who took a placebo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/health/research/25regimens.html', 'snippet': 'Menopausal women taking escitalopram, sold as Lexapro, averaged 1.41 fewer hot flashes per day than in those who took a placebo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study suggests that a widely prescribed antidepressant may provide at least some relief for women with hot flashes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regimens: Antidepressant May Help Quench Hot Flashes', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regimens: Antidepressant May Ease Hot Flashes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menopause', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261b64da-f51c-55ec-b572-b6414cebdbd2', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261b64da-f51c-55ec-b572-b6414cebdbd2'}, {'abstract': 'The student bodies of Holy Cross School, on West 43rd Street, and Sacred Heart of Jesus School, on West 52nd Street, will be combined.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/two-catholic-schools-on-west-side-will-merge/', 'snippet': 'The student bodies of Holy Cross School, on West 43rd Street, and Sacred Heart of Jesus School, on West 52nd Street, will be combined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Roman Catholic grade schools on the West Side of Manhattan will merge in September as part of a broad reorganization plan that calls for the closing of 27 schools at the end of the current academic year, the Archdiocese of New York announced Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Catholic Schools on West Side Will Merge', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/953197db-aed0-546c-8cf2-1afa0a9747f4', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953197db-aed0-546c-8cf2-1afa0a9747f4'}, {'abstract': 'For those with abdominal pain and bloating caused by I.B.S., peppermint oil may be an effective natural remedy.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/remedies-peppermint-oil-for-irritable-bowel/', 'snippet': 'For those with abdominal pain and bloating caused by I.B.S., peppermint oil may be an effective natural remedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a third of American adults use some form of complementary or alternative medicine, according to a government report. Natural remedies have an obvious appeal, but how do you know which ones to choose and whether the claims are backed by science? In this occasional series, Anahad O’Connor, the New York Times “Really?” columnist, explores the claims and the science behind alternative remedies that you may want to consider for your family medicine cabinet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remedies: Peppermint Oil for Irritable Bowel', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0c0749c-aea6-5e82-9ae7-350eca553f50', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0c0749c-aea6-5e82-9ae7-350eca553f50'}, {'abstract': 'Where architects lunch in Berlin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/courtyard-canteen/', 'snippet': 'Where architects lunch in Berlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few contemporary architects have earned more prestigious and prominent commissions in Berlin than the British-born David Chipperfield. His office in Mitte is currently working on at least three projects in the German capital, in addition to another dozen or so in different parts of Germany, Austria and Switzerland. With so much on their plate, Chipperfield and his team barely have time for lunch every day, let alone for deciding where to eat. Which is why Chipperfield has leased out part of his Berlin office’s courtyard space to a restaurant aptly called Kantine (canteen).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Courtyard Canteen', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:17:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felix Burrichter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrichter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d69314d9-f49d-57db-a00b-e1c284489e97', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d69314d9-f49d-57db-a00b-e1c284489e97'}, {'abstract': 'Commissioner Rafael E. Cestero is taking a job with a private-sector developer.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/housing-preservation-commissioner-leaving-post/', 'snippet': 'Commissioner Rafael E. Cestero is taking a job with a private-sector developer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael E. Cestero, commissioner of the city Department of Housing Preservation and Development, is leaving his job for a private-sector post. Mr. Cestero, who has served two stints in city government but spent most of his career in the private sector, will become managing director at L+M Development Partners, a developer of affordable and market-rate housing nationwide. Mr. Cestero will be involved only in projects outside of New York City, the housing preservation department said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Housing Preservation Commissioner Leaving Post', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf1922e-29de-5a0e-b56e-e61cfa19c159', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf1922e-29de-5a0e-b56e-e61cfa19c159'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from the operation led by South Korean to free the crew of a freighter hijacked in the Arabian Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/21/world/middleeast/20110122-PIRATES.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from the operation led by South Korean to free the crew of a freighter hijacked in the Arabian Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from the operation led by South Korean to free the crew of a freighter hijacked in the Arabian Sea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/middleeast/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/21/world/middleeast/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/21/world/middleeast/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6/20110122_PIRATES-slide-2YL6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Daring Rescue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:21:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle