rial Practice in Performance at Wesleyan University has created a new professional certificate program in curating performance art, the first of its kind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Institute for Curatorial Practice in Performance at Wesleyan University says, performance art “is first and foremost a social experience that happens on a person-to-person level.” That has not stopped the institute from creating a new professional certificate program in curating performance art that primarily occurs off-campus. The nine-month program, the first of its kind, is scheduled to begin this summer and is targeted at professionals with one to five years of experience. The course involves three short residencies. Danspace Project in New York City collaborated on the design and implementation of the program. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Wesleyan, a Program for Performance Art Curators', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wesleyan University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6330b25c-5a7a-589f-bb2e-bed3b62db854', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6330b25c-5a7a-589f-bb2e-bed3b62db854'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists are invited to compose aphorisms – short, pithy sentences that encapsulate some general truth.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/weekend-competition-aphorisms-hint-at-the-possibility-of-certainty/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists are invited to compose aphorisms – short, pithy sentences that encapsulate some general truth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists are invited to compose aphorisms – short, pithy sentences that encapsulate some general truth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Competition: Aphorisms Hint at the Possibility of Certainty', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e21a368-9272-5b37-9fe0-0ba7f34da86e', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e21a368-9272-5b37-9fe0-0ba7f34da86e'}, {'abstract': 'The E.P.A.’s decision expands the pool of vehicles that can use the higher ethanol blend to about 62 percent of the total on the roads. But the new blend is still a long way from the market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/business/energy-environment/22ethanol.html', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A.’s decision expands the pool of vehicles that can use the higher ethanol blend to about 62 percent of the total on the roads. But the new blend is still a long way from the market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The Environmental Protection Agency said on Friday that cars and light trucks from the 2001 model year onward can safely use a blend of 15 percent ethanol mixed with gasoline, up from the 10 percent standard now in effect in much of the country. The decision expands the pool of vehicles that could use such a fuel to about 62 percent of the total on the roads. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Approves Use of More Ethanol in Gasoline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.P.A. Approves Use of More Ethanol in Gasoline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:36:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cfd2d55-e529-5de9-b2aa-d44c0b936276', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cfd2d55-e529-5de9-b2aa-d44c0b936276'}, {'abstract': 'SecondMarket, the leading exchange for trading shares of private companies, completed $157.8 million of transactions in the fourth quarter of 2010, more than double its third-quarter volume.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/shares-of-facebook-and-other-private-companies-still-on-fire/', 'snippet': 'SecondMarket, the leading exchange for trading shares of private companies, completed $157.8 million of transactions in the fourth quarter of 2010, more than double its third-quarter volume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SecondMarket, the leading exchange for trading shares of private companies, released a report this morning that makes clear what DealBook has told you over the last month: The market for private shares, while still small, is on fire. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shares of Facebook and Other Private Companies Still on Fire', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SecondMarket Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1788b78f-45d5-594e-be1b-47bf2a1114ce', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1788b78f-45d5-594e-be1b-47bf2a1114ce'}, {'abstract': 'As the Google Android platform closes in on the iPhone, will Apple decide to offer its successful phone  on multiple carriers?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/will-apple-put-the-iphone-on-other-carriers/', 'snippet': 'As the Google Android platform closes in on the iPhone, will Apple decide to offer its successful phone  on multiple carriers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nick Bilton/The New York TimesAmong the several impressive numbers that Apple shared in its latest quarterly earnings report on Tuesday was the sale of more than 16 million iPhones over the quarter. Next month sales will surely continue to rise as Apple starts selling the iPhone on the Verizon network. But if Apple wants to fend off the iPhone’s rivals, will it have to sell its signature mobile device on other networks as well? Some analysts say yes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Apple Put the iPhone on Other Carriers?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Google Phone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'comScore Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', '