ted clothes that required sunglasses. I don’t mean as an accessory for those who wore them; I mean for the people looking at them. (A slide show of costumes designed by Ms. Aldredge is here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surface Thrills: Remembering the Costumes of Theoni V. Aldredge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T18:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a897ec6-c28b-5064-99f7-411678bd601c', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a897ec6-c28b-5064-99f7-411678bd601c'}, {'abstract': 'With about a month to go until the election, Rahm Emanuel holds a two-to-one advantage over his closest competitor, Carol Moseley Braun, according to a new poll.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/poll-shows-rahm-far-ahead-in-chicago-mayors-race/', 'snippet': 'With about a month to go until the election, Rahm Emanuel holds a two-to-one advantage over his closest competitor, Carol Moseley Braun, according to a new poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With just over a month to go until the mayoral election in Chicago, Rahm Emanuel , the former White House chief of staff, holds a two-to-one advantage over his closest competitor in the race, former Senator Carol Moseley Braun, according to a citywide Chicago Tribune/WGN poll. But the poll did not find Mr. Emanuel capturing the 50 percent threshold needed to avoid a runoff election in April.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Shows Emanuel Ahead in Chicago Mayor’s Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': No