t', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:19:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca25545f-cbae-5373-8eac-867023e4a07a', 'word_count': 1478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca25545f-cbae-5373-8eac-867023e4a07a'}, {'abstract': 'Baby sitters will be available at three matinee performances of “Kin” at Playwrights Horizons.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/no-need-to-call-a-sitter-playwrights-horizons-has-done-it/', 'snippet': 'Baby sitters will be available at three matinee performances of “Kin” at Playwrights Horizons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any parent of small children knows that the cost of hiring a baby sitter is often higher than the cost of tickets to a play. So now Playwrights Horizons is offering affordable, professional child care during three of its Sunday matinees. “The combined cost of theater tickets and child care is the factor most often cited by people with young children as the reason they rarely attend the theater,” Leslie Marcus, the managing director, said in a statement. “Our hope is that this program will become a model for other performing arts organizations in New York.” The program, called Playtime!, will be available on Feb. 27, March 20 and April 2 during the afternoon performance of “Kin,” a new play by Bathsheba Doran. While parents are watching the show, their children (4 to 12) will be upstairs in a rehearsal space and watched by Sitters Studio, a baby-sitting company made up of working artists. The service is free for members and $15 for non-members. The Theater Subdistrict Council, a nonprofit corporation, is helping to finance the project.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Need to Call a Sitter, Playwrights Horizons Has Done It', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doran, Bathsheba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6731f852-7baf-5540-b99b-3128cc439fee', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6731f852-7baf-5540-b99b-3128cc439fee'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. men’s national team plays its first match of 2011 Saturday night against Chile in Carson, Calif. But the game, which is scheduled to kick off about 10 p.m. Eastern, will only be available on a Spanish language network and on ESPN’s broadband service.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/u-s-men-set-for-2011-debut/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. men’s national team plays its first match of 2011 Saturday night against Chile in Carson, Calif. But the game, which is scheduled to kick off about 10 p.m. Eastern, will only be available on a Spanish language network and on ESPN’s broadb...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Habla TeleFutura?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Men Set for 2011 Debut', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo':