}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/travel/0123-KUCHING-slideshow-slide-LAVD/0123-KUCHING-slideshow-slide-LAVD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/travel/0123-KUCHING-slideshow-slide-LAVD/0123-KUCHING-slideshow-slide-LAVD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Borneo’s City Streets and Jungle Trails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Borneo (Indonesia);Borneo (Malaysia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f6cd8455-44c0-547e-8633-b38cfd6b48ae', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f6cd8455-44c0-547e-8633-b38cfd6b48ae'}, {'abstract': 'Kuching, Malaysia, has a cosmopolitan blend of cultures and is a starting point for other excursions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/travel/23borneo.html', 'snippet': 'Kuching, Malaysia, has a cosmopolitan blend of cultures and is a starting point for other excursions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SNOW-WHITE fortress in the style of the English Renaissance, garnished with crenellations, pepper pot turrets and an octagonal keep, is not quite what you’d expect to find on a steamy bluff overlooking an equatorial river in Malaysian Borneo. But Fort Margherita, built in 1879 by Charles Brooke, the second White Rajah of Sarawak, is just one of the many charms of Kuching, a gracious and kaleidoscopically diverse city of about 600,000 just an hour and a half by air from Singapore.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Kuching-1/Kuching-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Kuching-1/Kuching-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Kuching-1/Kuching-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Kuching-1/Kuching-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Kuching-1/Kuching-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Borneo, City Pleasures and Jungle Adventure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Borneo Bound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sarawak (Malaysia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Borneo (Malaysia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4219f8e5-9a39-5cea-82fd-a6a25c3e804e', 'word_count': 3195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4219f8e5-9a39-5cea-82fd-a6a25c3e804e'}, {'abstract': 'Saturne, in Paris’s Bourse district, is dedicated to elevating wild and rigorously sourced artisanal ingredients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/travel/23bites-saturne.html', 'snippet': 'Saturne, in Paris’s Bourse district, is dedicated to elevating wild and rigorously sourced artisanal ingredients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Paris, a cave à manger is generally a place to get a glass of wine and a plate of saucisson sec. But in some cases, it’s also where you go for some of the most satisfying food in the city: the profound braises at Le Baratin, the perfect clams at Le Verre Volé, the vegetables at Racines, plucked from the garden of Alain Passard, the chef at the three-star L’Arpège.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/sub-BITES/sub-BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/sub-BITES/sub-BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/sub-BITES/sub-BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Saturne, in Paris', 'kicker': 'Bites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paris', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Muhlke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Muhlke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/706fa067-e31c-5397-a0f5-1997f00c294a', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/706fa067-e31c-5397-a0f5-1997f00c294a'}, {'abstract': 'A new tour company brings high tea and high thread counts to a rugged corner of Northern India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/travel/23ladakh-journeys.html', 'snippet': 'A new tour company brings high tea and high thread counts to a rugged corner of Northern India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE little boy in the maroon robe had me at “Julé.” As his friends flitted about pouring yak-butter tea into tourists’ bowls, he limped toward the back of the windowless Thiksey monastery’s prayer hall, heavy copper pot trailing behind him. He offered a small serving of the creamy broth, a flash of Chiclet-like baby teeth and that Ladakhi greeting. Then he slipped back into his row and began to sway to the rhythm of the surrounding chants. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Journeys-span/Journeys-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Journeys-span/Journeys-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Journeys-span/Journeys-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Journeys-span/Journeys-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Journeys-span/Journeys-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In India, Luxury Arrives in a Himalayan Haven', 'kicker': 'Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing Luxury To a Rugged Himalayan Haven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By HEIDI MITCHELL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heidi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MITCHELL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47b8aef2-faee-5d9b-9a48-38aa8bc44140', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47b8aef2-faee-5d9b-9a48-38aa8bc44140'}, {'abstract': 'As name-brand chefs lay down roots in the city, a new cuisine emerges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/travel/23choice-philadelphia.html', 'snippet': 'As name-brand chefs lay down roots in the city, a new cuisine emerges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUGH tourists still mob Philadelphia’s famous cheese-', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Choice-1/Choice-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Choice-1/Choice-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred