 is a character actor in these joint efforts, a sensual diversion from a performance, but at Zagreus Projekt, a gallery space and restaurant in Mitte, it plays a starring role.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/23HEADS-span/23HEADS-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/23HEADS-span/23HEADS-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/23HEADS-span/23HEADS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/23HEADS-span/23HEADS-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/23HEADS-span/23HEADS-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Meets Food in Berlin', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Meets Cuisine in Berlin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gisela Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gisela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce2adbc1-a580-5eba-8cda-11a2891847a2', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce2adbc1-a580-5eba-8cda-11a2891847a2'}, {'abstract': 'Two hours from London, medieval Norwich is a reader’s town, with a university that hosts literary festivals and plentiful bookstores and cafes whose author readings draw crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/travel/23overnighter-norwich.html', 'snippet': 'Two hours from London, medieval Norwich is a reader’s town, with a university that hosts literary festivals and plentiful bookstores and cafes whose author readings draw crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a rainy night in September, all the shop fronts in the city center of Norwich, England, were dark and shuttered except for one. With each swing of the door, an expectant hum escaped from the Book Hive, an independent bookstore that opened in October 2009, as patrons eagerly awaited the arrival of the British-born Australian author Alex Miller.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Overnighter-span/Overnighter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Overnighter-span/Overnighter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Overnighter-span/Overnighter1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Overnighter-span/Overnighter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/travel/Overnighter-span/Overnighter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Norwich, England — a Getaway for Book Lovers', 'kicker': 'Overnighter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Writers, and Readers, Feel at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel B. Doyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea486dce-194b-5040-8b57-7ababbaba41c', 'word_count': 1448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea486dce-194b-5040-8b57-7ababbaba41c'}, {'abstract': 'Wealth managers’ clients are shying away from complicated hedge fund investments in favor of simple bets on blue-chip stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/your-money/asset-allocation/22wealth.html', 'snippet': 'Wealth managers’ clients are shying away from complicated hedge fund investments in favor of simple bets on blue-chip stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALL STREET is about to be flush with bonus money. And while there will certainly be the highfliers who blow it on fast cars and other flashy toys, the reality is that most bankers will put their bonuses into rather mundane investments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/your-money/asset-allocation/22wealth-