rds': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T19:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean McIndoe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McIndoe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c55d75-aa12-5d40-9546-a9fd626ff4fd', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c55d75-aa12-5d40-9546-a9fd626ff4fd'}, {'abstract': 'The reconstructed theater is planning a Cultural Olympiad in which all of the plays will be performed in 38 different languages.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/shakespeares-globe-theater-to-present-the-bards-canon-in-38-languages/', 'snippet': 'The reconstructed theater is planning a Cultural Olympiad in which all of the plays will be performed in 38 different languages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shakespeare’s Globe Theater will present a familiar array of the writer’s plays in 2012 but in some unfamiliar languages. The reconstructed theater, in the Southwark section of London, announced what it calls a “Cultural Olympiad,” in which all of the plays will be performed, each in a different language. The idea is to present a theatrical counterpart to the Olympic games which are scheduled to take place in London that year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shakespeare’s Globe Theater to Present the Writer’s Canon in 38 Languages', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Globe Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/268d7730-682a-59da-896e-44fc6281a9df', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268d7730-682a-59da-896e-44fc6281a9df'}, {'abstract': 'Knicks Coach Mike D’Antoni has put Ronny Turiaf back in the starting lineup, hoping to change course in a four-game losing streak.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/turiaf-returns-to-knicks-starting-lineup/', 'snippet': 'Knicks Coach Mike D’Antoni has put Ronny Turiaf back in the starting lineup, hoping to change course in a four-game losing streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike D’Antoni’s search for answers -– to a losing streak, a defensive slump and a punchless bench — has led him back to Ronny Turiaf, and a lineup change that he hopes will be permanent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turiaf Returns to Knicks’ Starting Lineup', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felton, Raymond', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turiaf, Ronny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': Non