etting off a flurry of other moves.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/more-executives-move-from-sony-to-universal/', 'snippet': 'Universal Music has lured away a top Sony executive, potentially setting off a flurry of other moves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A month after Universal Music Group hired away a top executive from Sony Music Entertainment, its chief rival, the company is making several changes in senior management positions and cutting about 60 lower-level jobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Executives Move From Sony to Universal', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Clive', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iovine, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Doug', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Antonio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interscope', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Music Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac1fe6ed-5451-58dd-9ff3-2b88f8eee196', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac1fe6ed-5451-58dd-9ff3-2b88f8eee196'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at how much of the conventional advice for retirement savings is heavily dependent on the markets performing well in the decade before retirement.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/the-one-big-catch-with-retirement-investing/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at how much of the conventional advice for retirement savings is heavily dependent on the markets performing well in the decade before retirement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at the frightening realities of investing for retirement. The conventional advice usually goes something like this: Save a respectable amount of your income, invest in a diversified portfolio, and you should be able to comfortably retire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The One Big Catch With Retirement Investing', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e3ef303-1a3a-5d23-ad1c-c345b538dade', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e3ef303-1a3a-5d23-ad1c-c345b538dade'}, {'abstract': 'While Fox’s “American Idol” remained the dominant ratings force in its second night on Thursday, competitors on CBS, ABC and NBC all had some positive ratings news.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/a-strong-night-for-idol-and-its-rivals/', 'snippet': 'While Fox’s “American Idol” remained the dominant ratings force in its second night on Thursday, competitors on CBS, ABC and NBC all had some positive ratings news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the competition, the best news from the first week of “American Idol” is that the juggernaut is no longer plowing under everything in its path.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strong Night for ‘Idol’ — and its Rivals', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dafd7ae-aa8f-5583-a54b-fb0ca570e329', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dafd7ae-aa8f-5583-a54b-fb0ca570e329'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers adopted a bill that would exempt “artistic or cultural works” from a 1991 law that prevents the presence of tobacco in advertisements for goods of any kind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/world/europe/22france.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers adopted a bill that would exempt “artistic or cultural works” from a 1991 law that prevents the presence of tobacco in advertisements for goods of any kind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS \x97 France may count more than its share of iconic chain-smokers \x97 from Jean-Paul Sartre to Alain Delon \x97 but for two decades the country has been systematically removing cigarettes from their fingertips or lips in any advertisements that use their likenesses. This week, though, a parliamentary committee approved a bill that would give back the tobacco products those celebrities held so dear, and by which they came to be known.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Seeks to Let Icons Light Up Once More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Seeks To Let Ico