es', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Considine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Considine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9dd76f-f9e2-57bf-9d40-052d7c84daa1', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9dd76f-f9e2-57bf-9d40-052d7c84daa1'}, {'abstract': 'The market for yachts is still depressed long after the recession has ended, discouraging would-be buyers and leaving owners unable to sell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/business/22yachts.html', 'snippet': 'The market for yachts is still depressed long after the recession has ended, discouraging would-be buyers and leaving owners unable to sell.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What is tougher than having one sleek mega-yacht for sale in a glutted market? The answer, for the moment at least, is having two mega-yachts on the market. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/22yachts/22yachts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/business/22yachts/22yachts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/22yachts/22yachts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/business/22yachts/22yachts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/business/22yachts/22ya