ract': 'Cars and light trucks in the 2001 model year and later can safely use a fuel with up to 15 percent ethanol, rather than the 10 percent that is now the standard, the agency said.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/e-p-a-approves-increased-ethanol-in-auto-fuel/', 'snippet': 'Cars and light trucks in the 2001 model year and later can safely use a fuel with up to 15 percent ethanol, rather than the 10 percent that is now the standard, the agency said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Matthew L. Wald reported Friday in The New York Times, the Environmental Protection Agency has approved ethanol formulations of 15 percent in unleaded gasoline, up from the 10 percent standard that is used in most of the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Approves Increased Ethanol in Auto Fuel', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b9154c-c33b-506c-9790-c8536c463ff3', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b9154c-c33b-506c-9790-c8536c463ff3'}, {'abstract': 'For “Modern Family,” self-analysis is part of the sitcom’s storyline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/fashion/23THISLIFE.html', 'snippet': 'For “Modern Family,” self-analysis is part of the sitcom’s storyline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capt