 battle over automotive innovations and product designs is often over computer code and is sometimes the target of industrial spies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/automobiles/23SPIES.html', 'snippet': 'The battle over automotive innovations and product designs is often over computer code and is sometimes the target of industrial spies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BATTLES over the ownership of innovations and product designs have raged in the auto industry since the first horseless carriages sputtered out of inventors’ garages. In 1911, Henry Ford won a highly publicized eight-year court battle with George Selden, who tried to patent the automobile even though he had never sold one. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/automobiles/SPIE/SPIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Computer Code an Increasingly Precious E.V. Commodity', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Computer Code an Increasingly Precious E.V. Commodity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renault SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T20:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Brooke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organ