8-29f561278b3b', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72184f04-252f-5d05-ba78-29f561278b3b'}, {'abstract': 'The Film Forum series “Fritz Lang in Hollywood,” starting Jan. 28, features 22 films from Lang, the Austrian genius who didn’t always get his way in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/movies/23dargis.html', 'snippet': 'The Film Forum series “Fritz Lang in Hollywood,” starting Jan. 28, features 22 films from Lang, the Austrian genius who didn’t always get his way in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAKING movies in Hollywood has never been easy, though maybe it should have been for the Austrian genius with a monocle screwed into his right eye and a dark, forbidding Weltanschauung lodged deep in his head. But life is cruel and filmmaking can be nearly as brutal, and so it was for Fritz Lang (1890-1976). “I always fought very hard in Hollywood,” he said in 1970, sounding like the embattled veteran he became. Late in life he said that the main theme in all his movies was the “fight against destiny, against fate,” and it’s hard not to wonder if he was thinking about his own fortunes as a Hollywood director. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/DARGIS/DARGIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/DARGIS/DARGIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/DARGIS/DARGIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/arts/DARGIS/DARGIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su