 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7406edc-441f-578b-a801-19428208d178', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7406edc-441f-578b-a801-19428208d178'}, {'abstract': 'The former British prime minister Tony Blair appeared, for a second time, before Britain’s official inquiry into the invasion of Iraq. This time, he offered something that he hadn’t the first time: regret.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/blair-sits-before-iraq-inquiry-this-time-with-regrets/', 'snippet': 'The former British prime minister Tony Blair appeared, for a second time, before Britain’s official inquiry into the invasion of Iraq. This time, he offered something that he hadn’t the first time: regret.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former British prime minister Tony Blair appeared, for a second time, before Britain’s official inquiry into the invasion of Iraq on Friday. During four hours of testimony, Mr. Blair tried to shift the debate from Iraq to Iran — the former, a subject on which he was taken to task for during his appearance in January 2010. On Friday, he accused Tehran of supporting terrorist groups in the region and seeking to block Middle East peace efforts, even saying that they “facilitate a situation in which that region cannot embark on the process of modernization it urgently needs.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blair Sits Before Iraq Inquiry, This Time With Regrets', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraq Inquiry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq'