ke Shimabukuro might have seemed like an exotic and fleeting talent. He was a ukulele virtuoso. He was a YouTube star. He was big in Japan. All of which is still true, and a lot less inherently intriguing now. Durability is the bane of novelty, and Mr. Shimabukuro has been nothing if not durable in recent years, steadily refining his craft, trusting that his fan base, and his media profile, will keep up.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/shima/shima-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/shima/shima-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/shima/shima-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Carefully Honed Image as a Master of the Ukulele', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Carefully Honed Image As a Master of the Ukulele', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T22:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecb11b13-d234-5d5c-84fc-135de0c7264b', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecb11b13-d234-5d5c-84fc-135de0c7264b'}, {'abstract': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit to r