598c-8959-7cb0e7f873ea'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday night the artist Jan Fabre and his dance and theater company presented the premiere of his “Prometheus — Landscape II” at Montclair State University in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/arts/dance/22prometheus.html', 'snippet': 'On Thursday night the artist Jan Fabre and his dance and theater company presented the premiere of his “Prometheus — Landscape II” at Montclair State University in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan Fabre is a monumental artistic personality, a distinctly European type that hardly seems to exist in America. He had an exhibition of his drawings, sculptures and installations at the Louvre; he covered the Hall of Mirrors in the Royal Palace in Brussels with the wing cases of nearly a million beetles; and he was an artistic adviser to the Avignon Festival. He has toured the Continent in the various guises of theater director, opera director, choreographer, performance artist and playwright.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/prometheus/prometheus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/prometheus/prometheus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/prometheus/prometheus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/prometheus/prometheus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/arts/prometheus/prometheus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Visit From Europe’s Do-It-All Artist', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Visit From Europe’s Do-It-All Artist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabre, Jan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montclair State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T23:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/55bcab93-90f2-543e-a0fb-b1e3a7227075', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55bcab93-90f2-543e-a0fb-b1e3a7227075'}, {'abstract': 'A stabbing, allegedly by her husband, almost cost Ms. Martin her life. Now, it may have given the boxer her career back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/fashion/23Christy.html', 'snippet': 'A stabbing, allegedly by her husband, almost cost Ms. Martin her life. Now, it may have given the boxer her career back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS a boxer, Christy Martin’s signature color was pink: pink shorts, pink robe, sometimes even pink boots. Pink was her color when she fought on the undercard of a Mike Tyson fight in Las Vegas in 1996, the blood dripping onto her shorts; pink was her color when she became the only woman boxer to make the cover of Sports Illustrated the following month; pink was her color after her career and women’s boxing had both fizzled, when she fought her last fight a year and a half ago, at a New York State fair. The guys in her corner hadn’t liked the pink at first, she said, but after that Sports Illustrated cover, they were all asking if they could wear the pink.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/fashion/23christy/CHRISTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/fashion/23christy/23christy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/fashion/23christy/23christy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christy Martin, Boxer, Takes Another Shot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Shot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Christy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-21T23:28:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3ac8265-0059-54fc-b36b-7055e1f7d3bc', 'word_count': 2911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3ac8265-0059-54fc-b36b-7055e1f7d3bc'}, {'abstract': 'A video from Anthony Di Fiore, a primate biologist at New York University who is studying spider monkeys in Ecuador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/1248069580153/white-lipped-peccaries-in-ecuador.html', 'snippet': 'A video from An