stretch of games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/ncaabasketball/22storm.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Lavin, fired at U.C.L.A. in 2003, has St. John’s improving, just in time for a rugged stretch of games.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Steve Lavin is no longer the manic 30-something coach who 10 years ago gave as good as he got to his critics. Then, he was the besieged wunderkind at U.C.L.A. who led a roster of underclassman blue chips known as the Baby Bruins. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/storm/storm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Second Run as Coach, Lavin Finds Better Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Second Run as Coach, Lavin Finds Better Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavin, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T00:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ab2502f-a8be-59a8-9930-c2b583f721eb', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ab2502f-a8be-59a8-9930-c2b583f721eb'}, {'abstract': 'A space-age looking food court in Chelsea provides customers an opportunity to build and pay for a meal using a touch-screen kiosk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/nyregion/23table.html', 'snippet': 'A space-age looking food court in Chelsea provides customers an opportunity to build and pay for a meal using a touch-screen kiosk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a space-age look courtesy of Syd Mead \x97 who was a designer on “Blade Runner,” “Aliens” and the original “Tron” \x97 this food court at the Eventi Hotel in Chelsea offers a dining experience not unlike, if a cut or two above, say, Chick-fil-A’s and Master Wok’s at the Paramus Park Mall. One of several such smorgasbords that have recently popped up, the spot has four counters \x97 The Press (coffee), 3Bs (bacon, burgers and beer), Fornetti (Italian) and RedFarm Stand (Asian) \x97 from which customers can build and pay for a meal using a single touch-screen kiosk. Sitting on Avenue of the Americas between 29th and 30th Streets, it has been pulling in a mix of office workers and passers-by since opening in October. On Wednesday, a couple and their young sons grabbed a bite after a potentially career-making appointment. DIANE CARDWELL ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/nyregion/23table/23table-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/nyregion/23table/23table-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/nyregion/23table/23table-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main':