 restraint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/nyregion/23dinenj.html', 'snippet': 'Mo C Mo C Japanese Cuisine serves sushi and fresh seafood with a sense of restraint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE’S plenty to like at happy little Mo C Mo C Japanese Cuisine, tucked into a storefront along a side street in Princeton. There’s the cozy atmosphere that fosters conversation between the closely spaced, cheerful laminate tables. There’s the friendly and responsive service. There’s the intensely floral and aromatic jasmine tea. And there’s the restraint on the plate that allows the simple green of snow peas and the dusky orange of salmon to star.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/nyregion/23DINENJ1/23DINENJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/nyregion/23DINENJ1/23DINENJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cozy Spot for Sushi Done Simply', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Princeton', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cozy Spot For Sushi Done Simply', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T02:12:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbaa8d6c-e495-5a8e-83a6-3183beda3260', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbaa8d6c-e495-5a8e-83a6-3183beda3260'}, {'abstract': 'The particulars of the violent death of Tajeme Sylvester, 31, are mysterious, and to his many friends in the Brooklyn arts scene, shockingly sad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/nyregion/22metjournal.html', 'snippet': 'The particulars of the violent death of Tajeme Sylvester, 31, are mysterious, and to his many friends in the Brooklyn arts scene, shockingly sad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tajeme Sylvester was a carpenter, a handyman and a poet. He was known as an impressive craftsman, whether renovating a brownstone or constructing a set for an Off Broadway theater. After hours, he was a fixture on the party circuit, dancing to house music, hip-hop and whatever else moved him. On Jan. 10, he became a statistic: the seventh homicide victim of 2011. His murder, which remains unsolved, stunned a community that saw him as a vibrant force on the Brooklyn arts scene.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vibrant Force Lost, While an Arts Scene Mourns', 'kicker': 'Red Hook Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vibrant Force Lost, While an Arts Scene Mourns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Red Hook (NYC)', 'ra