bfb7-99b45b9cce89'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bloomberg wants Albany to return control of New York City to the city. Given the city’s clear progress, and Albany’s clear failings, that makes good sense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/opinion/22sat2.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bloomberg wants Albany to return control of New York City to the city. Given the city’s clear progress, and Albany’s clear failings, that makes good sense.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In the mid-1970s, New York City was in such deep financial trouble that the state basically took charge. Albany’s lawmakers mandated important reforms, including modernizing the city budget system so that it is clear, transparent and professional. They decided against such changes for their own operations, which helps explain why the state is now the one in big trouble.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Give Back New York City', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Give Back New York City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the City Message (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T02:51:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/807b49ba-497f-51bd-a44c-d77ca6bcebbd', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80