d chilis to dry. By the time Mr. Bouazizi was 26, his work as a fruit vendor had earned him just enough money to feed his mother, uncle and five brothers and sisters at home. He dreamed about owning a van.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22SIDI1_span/SIDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22SIDI1_span/SIDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22SIDI1_span/SIDI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22SIDI1_span/SIDI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/world/22SIDI1_span/SIDI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slap to a Man’s Pride Set Off Tumult in Tunisia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slap to a Man’s Pride Set Off Tumult in Tunisia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouazizi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T02:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_nam