son': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/149353bc-4b3a-59e0-9985-a634cd6e2c85', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/149353bc-4b3a-59e0-9985-a634cd6e2c85'}, {'abstract': 'China is suddenly talking up cooperation on North Korea, the economy and a host of other issues. We hope the change in tone will mean a change in substance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/opinion/22sat1.html', 'snippet': 'China is suddenly talking up cooperation on North Korea, the economy and a host of other issues. We hope the change in tone will mean a change in substance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of rancor, China is suddenly talking up cooperation on North Korea, the economy, and other difficult issues. There are several possible explanations for the change in tone \x97 and, we hope \x97 substance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Newly Cooperative China', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Newly Cooperative China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/038342b2-29bc-5238-abe1-0c2a249901d4', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/038342b2-29bc-5238-abe1-0c2a249901d4'}, {'abstract': 'The final report from the presidential commission investigating the gulf oil spill rightly warns that government regulation alone can’t prevent another such disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/opinion/22sat3.html', 'snippet': 'The final report from the presidential commission investigating the gulf oil spill rightly warns that government regulation alone can’t prevent another such disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final report from the presidential commission investigating the gulf oil spill rightly warns that government regulation alone can’t prevent another such disaster. The blowout reflected industrywide weaknesses, not just BP’s, it said. And what is needed is a “fundamental transformation” of industry practices putting a far higher premium on safety.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Sign They Get It', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Sign They Get It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Bob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/817e6d98-d04e-5999-a01e-0198662519bc', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/817e6d98-d04e-5999-a01e-0198662519bc'}, {'abstract': 'We lament the end of an era of high-energy particle experiments in America that defined the threshold of our understanding of matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/opinion/22sat4.html', 'snippet': 'We lament the end of an era of high-energy particle experiments in America that defined the threshold of our understanding of matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Batavia, Ill. \x97 just west of Chicago \x97 you can walk along trails through a thousand-acre restored prairie filled with rare species like compass plant and rattlesnake master. From the edge of the prairie, you can see, as well, a four-mile ring of concrete and steel. That is the berm above the Tevatron, a high-energy subterranean racetrack for particle beams and the heart of the Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory, or Fermilab. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tevatron', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Tevatron', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Large Hadron Collider', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba8b4945-94a9-50e0-b248-0a190afa03aa', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba8b4945-94a9-50e0-b248-0a190afa03aa'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors will also ask a judge to decide whether Roger Clemens’s lawyer should be prevented from cross-examining Andy Pettitte, a former client.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/baseball/22base.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors will also ask a judge to decide whether Roger Clemens’s lawyer should be prevented from cross-examining Andy Pettitte, a former client.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prosecutors in Roger Clemens’s federal perjury case notified a court Friday that they intended to use bank, telephone, hospital and other business records as evidence against him. The prosecutors also asked a judge to hold a hearing on whether Clemens’s lawyer, Rusty Hardin, should be prevented from cross-examining a key witness, Yankees pitcher Andy Pettitte, because Hardin briefly represented both men. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank and Telephone Records Are Planned in Clemens Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank and Telephone Records Are Planned in Clemens Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perjury', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:26:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/264f4cdd-4061-5d79-8cc2-a1886a932c92', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/264f4cdd-4061-5d79-8cc2-a1886a932c92'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks coach’s search for answers — to a skid, a defensive slump and a punchless bench — has led him back to Ronny Turiaf, and a lineup change that he hopes will be permanent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/22garden.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks coach’s search for answers — to a skid, a defensive slump and a punchless bench — has led him back to Ronny Turiaf, and a lineup change that he hopes will be permanent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO \x97 Mike D’Antoni’s search for answers \x97 to a losing streak, a defensive slump and a punchless bench \x97 has led him back to Ronny Turiaf, and a lineup change that he hopes will be permanent.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'D’Antoni Shuffles Lineup in Hope of Stabilizing Knicks', 'kicker': 'Spurs 101, Knicks 92', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lineup Is Shuffled, but Result Is Same', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Antoni, Mike", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turiaf, Ronny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:31:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18130007-e8ae-50b8-9daf-b63ebb46d27e', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18130007-e8ae-50b8-9daf-b63ebb46d27e'}, {'abstract': 'Two franchises that were once powers in the Eastern Conference have drifted to the bottom of the pack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/basketball/22nets.html', 'snippet': 'Two franchises that were once powers in the Eastern Conference have drifted to the bottom of the pack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK \x97 The Nets and the Detroit Pistons exchanged Eastern Conference supremacy in the first half of the last decade, appearing in the N.B.A. finals twice each. Through ownership changes, coaching changes and the cyclical nature of professional basketball, the teams have now sunk to the bottom of the conference and are currently trying to emerge from Carmelo Anthony-induced stupors. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/nets/nets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/22/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pistons Can Be Example, Not Trade Partner, for Nets', 'kicker': 'On Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pistons Can Be Example, Not Trade Partner, for Nets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Pistons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T03:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e60375-8224-5ad9-95c3-b65901d3bad6', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e60375-8224-5ad9-95c3-b65901d3bad6'}, {'abstract': 'After the premiere of “The Green Wave,” a brutal depiction of repression and government-sanctioned violence in Iran, Ali Samadi Ahadi said the outrage over the imprisonment of Jafar Panahi could have an effect on the regime.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/21/sundance-gets-a-taste-of-iranian-politics/', 'snippet': 'After the premiere of “The Green Wave,” a brutal depiction of repression and government-sanctioned violence in Iran, Ali Samadi Ahadi said the outrage over the imprisonment of Jafar Panahi could have an effect on the regime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— After the Sundance premiere Friday of “The Green Wave,” a brutal depiction of repression and government-sanctioned violence in Iran, the Iranian filmmaker behind the documentary, Ali Samadi Ahadi, struck a surprisingly hopeful chord. Not about human-rights violations in his homeland — the soft-spoken Mr. Ahadi, who lives in Germany, thinks those will continue. But he was upbeat about whether Iran was listening to the outrage that followed its jailing last month of the celebrated director Jafar Panahi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance Gets a Taste of Iranian Politics', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu