our and a half years in prison for obstruction of justice and lying about torturing murder suspects. The man, Jon Burge, 63, was found guilty in June of lying under oath in a 2003 civil court case about the torture of suspects in custody during the 1970s and 1980s. More than 100 black men accused Mr. Burge and other officers under his command of subjecting them to electrocution, beatings and other acts of torture to gain confessions in murder cases. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Ex-Police Commander Sentenced', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | MIDWEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Ex-Police Commander Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burge, Jon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T04:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By KARI LYDERSEN, CHICAGO NEWS COOPERATIVE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LYDERSEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chicago', 'middlename': 'News', 'lastname': 'COOPERATIVE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd563829-1ba5-58b4-bee0-5a8cf50ee60f', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd563829-1ba5-58b4-bee0-5a8cf50ee60f'}, {'abstract': 'The lawyer for Pfc. Bradley Manning, the Army intelligence analyst detained on charges of leaking classified information to WikiLeaks, accused the military of placing him unnecessarily on suicide watch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/us/22brfs-LAWYERPROTES_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The lawyer for Pfc. Bradley Manning, the Army intelligence analyst detained on charges of leaking classified information to WikiLeaks, accused the military of placing him unnecessarily on suicide watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lawyer for Pfc. Bradley Manning, the Army intelligence analyst detained on charges of leaking classified information to WikiLeaks, accused the military on Friday of abusing Private Manning by placing him unnecessarily on suicide watch. The lawyer, David E. Coombs, said psychiatric reviews had determined that Private Manning was not a suicide risk and should even be taken off the less restrictive “prevention of injury watch” and put on normal status at the jail at the Marine Corps base at Quantico, Va. Instead, on Tuesday and Wednesday, Private Manning was placed on the stricter suicide watch, eliminating his daily hour of exercise and stripping him of all clothing except underwear. After Mr. Coombs protested, Private Manning was returned to prevention-of-injury status. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyer Protests Status of Soldier in Leaks Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyer Protests Status of Soldier in Leaks Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T04:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National'