r the film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Previously Unseen Portraits of Bobby Fischer by Harry Benson', 'kicker': 'Gambit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Bobby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garbus, Liz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Life (Magazine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T05:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f6e03d2-50b6-5a57-bd95-eaee7df135ab', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f6e03d2-50b6-5a57-bd95-eaee7df135ab'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Angels acquired the All-Star center fielder Vernon Wells from Toronto in exchange for catcher Mike Napoli and outfielder Juan Rivera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/sports/baseball/22sportsbriefs-mets.html', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Angels acquired the All-Star center fielder Vernon Wells from Toronto in exchange for catcher Mike Napoli and outfielder Juan Rivera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Angels acquired the All-Star center fielder Vernon Wells from Toronto in exchange for catcher Mike Napoli and outfielder Juan Rivera. Wells has four years and $86 million left on his seven-year, $126 million contract. Neither team would say if any money was included to offset Wells’s salary. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blue Jays Ship Wells to Angels', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blue Jays Ship Wells to Angels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Vernon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T05:57:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f98c1dc-3d6f-5989-8397-591d75fb18ca', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f98c1dc-3d6f-5989-8397-591d75fb18ca'}, {'abstract': 'Iran stuck to its insistence that it has the right to enrich uranium, but Western officials said their proposals for a fuel swap remained on the table.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/world/middleeast/23nuke.html', 'snippet': 'Iran stuck to its insistence that it has the right to enrich uranium, but Western officials said their proposals for a fuel swap remained on the table.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL \x97 Two days of talks between Iran and six world powers ended in failure on Saturday, with Iran refusing to engage on any concrete proposals to build confidence that its nuclear program is only for peaceful purposes and with no date set for another meeting.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi