and some underground spaces currently off-limits to the public—could begin by the end of the year and is expected to last between two and three years. The Colosseum will remain open during the restoration, which will be monitored by the Culture Ministry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tod’s to Help Fund Colosseum Restoration', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T15:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba5edc36-62dc-54ad-aacd-a419bfae155c', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba5edc36-62dc-54ad-aacd-a419bfae155c'}, {'abstract': 'John Goodge, a professor of geological sciences at the University of Minnesota-Duluth, answers readers’ questions about his expedition to Antarctica.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/answering-questions-about-antarctica/', 'snippet': 'John Goodge, a professor of geological sciences at the University of Minnesota-Duluth, answers readers’ questions about his expedition to Antarctica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Goodge, left, a professor of geological sciences at the University of Minnesota-Duluth, and Jeff Vervoort, an isotope geochemist from Washington State University, recently returned from their research expedition in Antarctica.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answering Questions About Antarctica', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': Non