h, depression, inflation.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/has-the-world-run-out-of-spare-capacity/', 'snippet': 'North, South, depression, inflation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samuel Brittan points us to John Kemp suggesting that global growth is hitting supply-side limits. The argument is that while high unemployment and low inflation may prevail in advanced economies, the rest of the world is facing accelerating inflation, together with rising commodity prices. And that is, indeed, a fair picture of what’s going on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Has the World Run Out of Spare Capacity?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T16:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fea42d2-701d-5dff-99a4-8efa57c246e9', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fea42d2-701d-5dff-99a4-8efa57c246e9'}, {'abstract': 'Europe does OK on job creation.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/eurosclerosis-then-and-now/', 'snippet': 'Europe does OK on job creation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated with an additional figure at end', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurosclerosis, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T16:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/684035af-fa85-5568-864f-3151e93f6385', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/684035af-fa85-5568-864f-3151e93f6385'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s cryptic crossword is a bit shocking, but it made me laugh.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/22/cryptic-treasure-hunt/', 'snippet': 'Today’s cryptic crossword is a bit shocking, but it made me laugh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — If you were born and raised in the United States, odds are good that you have not had a lot of exposure to cryptic crosswords. I fall into that group, but I’ve resolved to fix that. American-style crosswords are wonderful, but just look at the variety of puzzles we have available to us every Sunday in The New York Times. Sometimes the brain needs a little something different on which to nosh, no?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Cryptic Treasure Hunt', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T17:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/81fd8261-3e16-5167-a6f7-0543e6623b11', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81fd8261-3e16-5167-a6f7-0543e6623b11'}, {'abstract': 'As players and employees come and go with the Jets, one thing has stayed the same: no Super Bowl title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/sports/football/23jets.html', 'snippet': 'As players and employees come and go with the Jets, one thing has stayed the same: no Super Bowl title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. \x97 For 11 seasons, Shaun Ellis made Jets history, felt Jets history, lived Jets history. He played home games at a stadium named after another team. He practiced in a place that symbolized the franchise, underwhelming and outdated. He knows something about Jets heartache.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyy-jets/yyy-jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyy-jets/yyy-jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyy-jets/yyy-jets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyy-jets/yyy-jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyy-jets/yyy-jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bleeding Green', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bleeding Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-22T17:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_na