nyt://article/da8b39b4-342b-55c8-b0b4-8cf536a4ec70'}, {'abstract': 'As Aaron Rodgers prepares for the N.F.C. title game, people who know him say the fame of being the Packers’ quarterback hasn’t changed him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/sports/football/23packers.html', 'snippet': 'As Aaron Rodgers prepares for the N.F.C. title game, people who know him say the fame of being the Packers’ quarterback hasn’t changed him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. \x97 Once a week or so, Packers quarterback Aaron Rodgers strolls into Cheese Cake Heaven, a delicatessen and bakery near Lambeau Field popular with Packers players and their wives. Deb Katers, who works the register at lunchtime, said Rodgers often chose the build-your-own sandwich option \x97 “a turkey avocado kind of thing,” she said \x97 and exchanged playful banter with the counter staff.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyypackers/yyypackers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyypackers/yyypackers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/sports/yyypackers/yyypackers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Packers’ Rodgers Handles Pressure With Ease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just a Guy in Titletown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'm