k', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df49cf7-75b6-5417-9eb8-a3bef4a45a2b', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df49cf7-75b6-5417-9eb8-a3bef4a45a2b'}, {'abstract': 'Give average Americans a better economic deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23reich.html', 'snippet': 'Give average Americans a better economic deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'P RESIDENT OBAMA will have to devote a big part of his State of the Union address to the economy, but which economy?', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recover Our Spending Power', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; Recover Our Spending Power", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROBERT B. REICH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/66b7e140-bc0c-575c-8a74-a92140459346', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66b7e140-bc0c-575c-8a74-a92140459346'}, {'abstract': 'An approach aimed at potential buyers, not the gun, has a real chance of winning bipartisan support.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23kessler.html', 'snippet': 'An approach aimed at potential buyers, not the gun, has a real chance of winning bipartisan support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH the Tucson shootings still in the news, there’s a good chance President Obama will discuss gun control in his speech. How he does it could mean progress or stalemate on the issue.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun Control Without a Ban', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE PRESIDENTS SPEECH; Gun Control Without a Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:03:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Cowan and Jim Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee367b0d-861e-5b8d-adfe-6f3fe4326326', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee367b0d-861e-5b8d-adfe-6f3fe4326326'}, {'abstract': 'States need to help parents ascertain whether their children are getting high-quality instruction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23rhee.html', 'snippet': 'States need to help parents ascertain whether their children are getting high-quality instruction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE past year was a sobering one for American educators, as we learned that the United States is falling farther behind in international student rankings. To his credit, President Obama put forward a plan for change that hit the mark, a brilliant stroke that even the “abolish the Department of Education” crowd had to admire. Race to the Top, the competitive grant program that harnesses stimulus dollars to drive reform, convinced a surprising number of governors and legislators from both parties to pay the entrance fee by proving they could strengthen their education laws.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep All the Top Teachers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; Keep All the Top Teachers", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Rhee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rhee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/71a19096-938b-51e0-b4a4-8f38a5466420', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71a19096-938b-51e0-b4a4-8f38a5466420'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama must commit accelerating job growth and controlling the federal deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23rivlin.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama must commit accelerating job growth and controlling the federal deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA must use his State of the Union speech to make clear his commitment to two economic imperatives: accelerating job growth and controlling the federal deficit. He must persuade Americans that we do not have a choice between the two. We have to do both, and we have to get the timing right.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Create Jobs Not Deficits', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; Create Jobs Not Deficits", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice M. Rivlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e334d343-5a23-5fc6-9c65-496b8d3b20aa', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e334d343-5a23-5fc6-9c65-496b8d3b20aa'}, {'abstract': 'By expanding our nonpolluting energy choices, we can ameliorate a variety of risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23revkin.html', 'snippet': 'By expanding our nonpolluting energy choices, we can ameliorate a variety of risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FACING a public focused on economic revival, a hostile House and the lowest level of voter concern in a long while on human-driven climate change, President Obama could easily punt on energy this Tuesday. But this would actually be the ideal time for him to introduce an energy quest as a keystone 21st-century American imperative. Only by expanding our menu of nonpolluting energy choices can we hope to ameliorate a variety of social, geopolitical, climatic and economic risks facing the country and the world.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy for the Economy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; Energy for the Economy", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/140b0ee4-2496-550a-9f33-9e58367983d9', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/140b0ee4-2496-550a-9f33-9e58367983d9'}, {'abstract': 'The key to success is working together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23daschle.html', 'snippet': 'The key to success is working together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'G IVEN the deep divide on health care reform in the courts, the Congress and the country, the long-term viability of this historic achievement depends in part on President Obama’s ability to reduce the tension and seek common ground. In his State of the Union message, he should say something like this:', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Final Health Care Debate', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; The Final Health Care Debate", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Daschle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daschle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e32d86-1958-5fc0-85e0-ae85bd19833d', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e32d86-1958-5fc0-85e0-ae85bd19833d'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should say that in Tunisia, and everywhere else, that we will side with those working to build democracies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/opinion/23abrams.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama should say that in Tunisia, and everywhere else, that we will side with those working to build democracies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE revolt in Tunisia has thrown both that nation’s dictator, Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, and the Obama administration’s democracy-promotion policy onto the ash heap of history. The revolt undermined — indeed, destroyed — two years of effort in Washington to move toward a policy of “engagement” with hostile and repressive regimes.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Less ‘Engagement,’ More Democracy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "THE PRESIDENT'S SPEECH; Less ‘Engagement,’ More Democracy", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiaobo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elliott Abrams', 'perso