ard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Banned in Beijing!', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banned In Beijing!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:12:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4fd3c98-42a4-5034-865f-267ce7842799', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4fd3c98-42a4-5034-865f-267ce7842799'}, {'abstract': 'In 1933, Arkansas went “plain, flat broke.” The fallout — on roads, spending and image — lasted for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23davey.html', 'snippet': 'In 1933, Arkansas went “plain, flat broke.” The fallout — on roads, spending and image — lasted for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the states dream up budget plans for a new year, some find themselves staring at deficits in the billions of dollars, vanishing federal stimulus funds, mounting health care costs, their own struggling cities and a canyon of underfunded pension liabilities ahead.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/DAVEY/DAVEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/DAVEY/DAVEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/DAVEY/DAVEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The State That Went Bust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The State That Went Bust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/465b6c9a-96d7-5cc4-8cfa-db5ad440d411', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/465b6c9a-96d7-5cc4-8cfa-db5ad440d411'}, {'abstract': '11.9: The percentage of U.S. workers in unions last year, the lowest proportion in 70 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23prime.html', 'snippet': '11.9: The percentage of U.S. workers in unions last year, the lowest proportion in 70 years.', 'lead_paragraph': '11.9: The percentage of American workers in unions last year, the lowest proportion in more than 70 years, according to the government’s Bureau of Labor Statistics. The number of workers in unions fell by 612,000 last year, to 14.7 million. About 20 percent of workers were in unions in 1983; the figure was 35 percent during the mid-1950s, according to labor historians. Last year “was a very tough year for unionized workers,” said John Schmitt, a senior economist with the Center for Economic and Policy Research in Washington. “We’re seeing declines in the private sector, and we’re seeing declines in the public sector.”', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime Number', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prime Number', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b95a42cf-064c-5fab-a71e-a6b8bcb012a7', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b95a42cf-064c-5fab-a71e-a6b8bcb012a7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will strike a theme of national unity and renewal in his State of the Union address Tuesday as he stresses the need for both government spending in key areas and an attack on the budget deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/us/politics/23obama.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama will strike a theme of national unity and renewal in his State of the Union address Tuesday as he stresses the need for both government spending in key areas and an attack on the budget deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 President Obama will outline an agenda for “winning the future” in his State of the Union address on Tuesday night, striking a theme of national unity and renewal as he stresses the need for government spending in key areas and an attack on the budget deficit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Press Centrist Agenda in His Address', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'OBAMA TO PRESS CENTRIST AGENDA IN HIS ADDRESS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/858949b1-985e-5dd6-b9c7-fbc240bb0993', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/858949b1-985e-5dd6-b9c7-fbc240bb0993'}, {'abstract': 'Haiti’s former dictator, Jean-Claude Duvalier, returned to the country unexpectedly last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23backthen.html', 'snippet': 'Haiti’s former dictator, Jean-Claude Duvalier, returned to the country unexpectedly last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Haiti’s former dictator, Jean-Claude Duvalier, returned unexpectedly last week for the first time after being forced to flee in 1986. He was quickly arrested on charges of embezzlement and corruption. Following Mr. Duvalier’s overthrow in 1986, mobs ransacked his estates. One of them was an Alpine-style retreat visited by The Times’s James Brooke shortly after it was looted.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Then: 1986', 'kicker': 'Back Then', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1986', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efcd3573-9628-51ca-8a85-179ed642a351', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efcd3573-9628-51ca-8a85-179ed642a351'}, {'abstract': 'Smog is erasing the skyline in Hong Kong.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23grist.html', 'snippet': 'Smog is erasing the skyline in Hong Kong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hong Kong’s most striking feature — the skyline of skyscrapers silhouetted against Victoria Peak — is getting harder and harder to see, reports Bettina Wassener on The Times’s Green blog. Over the last few decades, as the city’s economy and that of neighboring mainland China has expanded, air pollution in the region has worsened and so has visibility. And the obscured view is not the only concern. A study released last week by the University of Hong Kong Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine reported that the air pollution was linked to 1,200 deaths in the city annually from 2007 to 2010.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/Grist/Grist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 952, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/Grist/Grist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/weekinreview/Grist/Grist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Grist', 'kicker': 'Grist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smog Is Erasing The Skyline In Hong Kong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31ff6eb4-0175-556b-aecd-438554517df9', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31ff6eb4-0175-556b-aecd-438554517df9'}, {'abstract': 'Jokes from TV comedy show monologues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23laugh.html', 'snippet': 'Jokes from TV comedy show monologues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAY LENO', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laugh Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laugh Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letterman, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmel, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Conan", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7521480-84ab-575c-bfe5-8d221d816a96', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7521480-84ab-575c-bfe5-8d221d816a96'}, {'abstract': 'Glenn Beck has taken to criticizing a liberal sociologist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/weekinreview/23fighting.html', 'snippet': 'Glenn Beck has taken to criticizing a liberal sociologist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glenn Beck has taken to criticizing Frances Fox Piven, the liberal sociologist, for her radical plan, published 45 years ago, to help poor people. Some liberals have come to her defense, saying she has received death threats. Fox News said Mr. Beck had quoted her accurately and never threatened her.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'FIGHTING WORDS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piven, Frances Fox', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T00:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organiza