ide what to do with unused buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/us/23ttfacilities.html', 'snippet': 'If the Texas Legislature makes big cuts in money for public schools, districts may find themselves having to decide what to do with unused buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Texas public schools are facing what could be $10 billion less in state financing \x97 a stark prospect that could empty school buildings across the state as districts consolidate campuses to reduce costs. One proposal under consideration by the Austin Independent School District, the state’s fourth largest, suggests closing eight elementary schools and one middle school. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/us/23TTFACILITIES/23TTFACILITIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 887, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/us/23TTFACILITIES/23TTFACILITIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/us/23TTFACILITIES/23TTFACILITIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Budget Cuts Are Made, Districts May Have to Decide on Fate of Unused Schools', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Budget Cuts Are Made, Districts May Have to Decide on Fate of Unused Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate'