well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/us/23ttcanceled.html', 'snippet': 'At the beginning of the television season, four new series produced in Texas had their premieres. Three have already been canceled, and the fourth one isn’t looking well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was supposed to be a watershed season for television production in Texas. While the Austin-based NBC drama “Friday Night Lights” was wrapping production on its final season, four new series set in the Lone Star State got network green lights, including three whose productions would be based in the Dallas-Fort Worth area. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/us/sub23TTCANCELLED1/sub23TTCANCELLED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/23/us/sub23TTCANCELLED1/sub23TTCANCELLED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/23/us/sub23TTCANCELLED1/sub23TTCANCELLED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Great TV Series Set in Texas? Sorry, You’re Canceled', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Great TV Series Set in Texas? Sorry, You’re Canceled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T01:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Kelly