r couch  watching the games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not hard to see Troy Polamalu’s importance to the Steelers, whether you’re poring over advanced statistics or reclining on your couch watching the games. (In the videos above and below, Polamalu does a fair impression of Jimmy Superfly Snuka — without the benefit of jumping off the top rope.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Troy Polamalu Factor', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polamalu, Troy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T12:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f98a77-13eb-52fd-8e71-0f9834626e00', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f98a77-13eb-52fd-8e71-0f9834626e00'}, {'abstract': 'It took four hours and 44 minutes, setting a Grand Slam record for women, but Francesca Schiavone was finally able to beat Svetlana Kuznetsova, 6-4, 1-6, 16-14 on Sunday at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sports/tennis/24iht-open24.html', 'snippet': 'It took four hours and 44 minutes, setting a Grand Slam record for women, but Francesca Schiavone was finally able to beat Svetlana Kuznetsova, 6-4, 1-6, 16-14 on Sunday at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia \x97 It was not the emotional summit of Francesca Schiavone’s career. That came last June when Schiavone kissed the red clay at the French Open in Paris after becoming the first Italian woman to a Grand Slam singles title.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YTENNIS-ALT/YTENNIS-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YTENNIS-ALT/YTENNIS-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/YTENNIS-ALT/YTENNIS-ALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 535, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Nearly 5 Hours, Italian Wins Epic Match', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Final Kick, Italian Wins Marathon Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuznetsova, Svetlana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T12:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a40d7893-a29e-5058-86e1-e5c844215775', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a40d7893-a29e-5058-86e1-e5c844215775'}, {'abstract': 'Whether the Jets like it or not, a lot of the burden of returning to the Super Bowl after a four-decade drought is on Mark Sanchez’s shoulders.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/do-you-have-confidence-in-mark-sanchez/', 'snippet': 'Whether the Jets like it or not, a lot of the burden of returning to the Super Bowl after a four-decade drought is on Mark Sanchez’s shoulders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH – Whether the Jets like it or not, a lot of the burden of returning to the Super Bowl after a four-decade drought is on Mark Sanchez’s shoulders. Sanchez is a victory away from the most playoff road wins by an N.F.L. quarterback. But he evokes strong emotions from Jets fans, some of whom see the promise but are unsettled by his uneven performance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Have Confidence in Mark Sanchez?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristian R. Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristian', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9978004b-a36c-59bf-87c0-1ade306ffc90', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9978004b-a36c-59bf-87c0-1ade306ffc90'}, {'abstract': 'A Jan. 23, 1911, shooting stirred one man to mount a successful campaign for a gun-control law.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/100-years-ago-the-shot-that-spurred-new-yorks-gun-control-law/', 'snippet': 'A Jan. 23, 1911, shooting stirred one man to mount a successful campaign for a gun-control law.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nothing spurs talk of gun-control legislation quite like a highly publicized crime committed with the aid of a handgun. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '100 Years Ago, the Shot That Spurred New York’s Gun-Control Law', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldsborough, Fitzhugh Coyle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tammany Hall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T16:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Duffy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duffy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb29ced1-6246-5956-8fb0-17e72ec7e75b', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb29ced1-6246-5956-8fb0-17e72ec7e75b'}, {'abstract': 'Following a succession plan laid out years ago, President Hu Jintao will pass the baton to his presumed successor, Xi Jinping, now China’s vice president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/asia/24leader.html', 'snippet': 'Following a succession plan laid out years ago, President Hu Jintao will pass the baton to his presumed successor, Xi Jinping, now China’s vice president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING \x97 President Hu Jintao of China returned home this weekend after a trip intended to repair relations with the United States. But the next time the White House marches out the honor guard and polishes the crystal for a Chinese leader, it is unlikely to be for Mr. Hu.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/SUB-LEADERS/SUB-LEADERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/24/world/SUB-LEADERS/SUB-LEADERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/SUB-LEADERS/SUB-LEADERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/SUB-LEADERS/SUB-LEADERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/world/SUB-LEADERS/SUB-LEADERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Grooming Deft Politician as Next Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Grooms a New Leader, Politically Deft, if Little Known', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T16:21:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'F