 and the founder of Blackwater are said to be involved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/africa/24somalia.html', 'snippet': 'Somalia said that it would most likely sever its relationship with a security company in which South African mercenaries and the founder of Blackwater are said to be involved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia \x97 The minister of information for the transitional federal government here said Sunday that Somalia was likely to end its relationship with Saracen International, a private security company in which South African mercenaries and the founder of Blackwater Worldwide are said to be involved.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia Is Likely to Cut Ties to Mercenaries, Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia Is Likely to Cut Ties To Mercenaries, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xe Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercenaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T18:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3123997e-a168-560f-a447-05587d6d5d81', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3123997e-a168-560f-a447-05587d6d5d81'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/photos-of-the-moment-damir-doma/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#514", 592, 490, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Damir Doma', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cc64c06-0b34-5b07-830c-5781c4a4a7ab', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cc64c06-0b34-5b07-830c-5781c4a4a7ab'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/photos-of-the-moment-hermes-2/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#158", 592, 490, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Hermès', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/322ce795-db7b-5dcf-8d73-85cb2a5f139b', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/322ce795-db7b-5dcf-8d73-85cb2a5f139b'}, {'abstract': 'Live analysis of the N.F.C. championship game between the Green Bay Packers and the Chicago Bears.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/live-analysis-n-f-c-championship-game/', 'snippet': 'Live analysis of the N.F.C. championship game between the Green Bay Packers and the Chicago Bears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Green Bay Packers are headed back to the Super Bowl after beating the Chicago Bears, 21-14, in the N.F.C. championship game at Soldier Field. But before their trip to Dallas was sealed, they had to withstand a rally attempt led by perhaps the most unlikely figure in championship game history. Caleb Hanie, the Bears’ third-string quarterback, was forced into action after Jay Cutler and Todd Collins were both knocked out with injuries. Hanie threw a 35-yard touchdown to Earl Bennett with 4:43 remaining that pulled the Bears within 7 points, but his inexperience showed. He threw one interception that was returned B.J. Raji 18 yards for a score and he was picked off by Sam Shields with about 40 seconds left, a play that sealed the Packers’ victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Final: Packers 21, Bears 14', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/24bd2512-e7a7-527a-8e2e-3ab55c4d09c0', 'word_count': 2296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24bd2512-e7a7-527a-8e2e-3ab55c4d09c0'}, {'abstract': 'At Lanvin, Hermès and Yves Saint Laurent, the jacket is getting roughed up this season—nipped, shortened, tweaked.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/paris-mens-nip-it-bud/', 'snippet': 'At Lanvin, Hermès and Yves Saint Laurent, the jacket is getting roughed up this season—nipped, shortened, tweaked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jacket is getting roughed up this season—nipped, shortened, tweaked. At Lanvin on Sunday morning, the jackets looked leaner for fall; some were pilled with black puffer jackets, and the collection included wide trousers, the narrow ones looked more in step with the rest of the urban line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Men’s: Nip It, Bud', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lanvin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By By CATHY HORYN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HORYN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/02509a03-3f7f-5521-a65d-afada2c3b788', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02509a03-3f7f-5521-a65d-afada2c3b788'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt charged that a Palestinian extremist group with links to Al Qaeda was behind the New Year’s Eve bombing that killed 21 people and set off days of sectarian rioting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/middleeast/24egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt charged that a Palestinian extremist group with links to Al Qaeda was behind the New Year’s Eve bombing that killed 21 people and set off days of sectarian rioting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO \x97 Egypt’s interior minister charged Sunday that a Palestinian extremist group with links to Al Qaeda was behind the Dec. 31 bombing outside a church in Alexandria that killed 21 people and set off days of sectarian rioting around the nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Links Palestinians to Attack at Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Links Palestinians To Attack At Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Slackman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slackman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98725254-44ed-570b-b3d6-e8b3b0d2ebc2', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98725254-44ed-570b-b3d6-e8b3b0d2ebc2'}, {'abstract': 'Miranda July’s second feature, “The Future,” opens with a talking cat, and gets cuter, weirder and darker from there.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/a-whimsical-end-to-writers-block/', 'snippet': 'Miranda July’s second feature, “The Future,” opens with a talking cat, and gets cuter, weirder and darker from there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— Miranda July’s second feature, “The Future,” opens with a talking cat, and gets cuter, weirder and darker from there. Ms. July, the artist, writer and performer, had a Sundance hit in 2005 with “Me and You and Everyone We Know,” which went on to win a Camera d’Or at Cannes for best first feature, and her next film was eagerly awaited. But in a director’s statement, Ms. July wrote that she so dreaded making a follow-up that she was nearly paralyzed with writer’s block. That turned out to be her inspiration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Whimsical End to Writer’s Block', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkes, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'July, Miranda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linklater, Hamish', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T19:31:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd24b7b0-d225-5042-86d6-3ec5eaecffa8', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd24b7b0-d225-5042-86d6-3ec5eaecffa8'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of Frank Gehry’s design of the New World Center in Miami Beach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/24/arts/design/20110124-gehry.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of Frank Gehry’s design of the New World Center in Miami Beach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of Frank Gehry’s design of the New World Center in Miami Beach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24