-max/', 'snippet': 'The United States opened its 2011 schedule Saturday night with a 1-1 draw against Chile at the Home Depot Center in Carson, Calif.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States opened its 2011 schedule Saturday night with a 1-1 draw against Chile at the Home Depot Center in Carson, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For U.S., Mixx and Dax to the Max', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T21:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a8c96a1-6e3f-5609-a5ff-30c9a7d3b6dc', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8c96a1-6e3f-5609-a5ff-30c9a7d3b6dc'}, {'abstract': 'A nonprofit group announced the winner of a competition to design a crossing to help migratory wildlife cross a section of Interstate 70 in Colorado.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/science/earth/24overpass.html', 'snippet': 'A nonprofit group announced the winner of a competition to design a crossing to help migratory wildlife cross a section of Interstate 70 in Colorado.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 At a picturesque spot in the mountains near the ski resorts of Vail and Breckenridge, Colo., two streams of traffic converge: people driving east and west on Interstate 70, and animals \x97 black bears, cougars, bobcats, elk and deer \x97 headed north and south to feed and mate. When they collide, the animal is almost always killed and the vehicle badly damaged, even if the driver is lucky enough to escape injury. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/us/OVERPASS/OVERPASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/us/OVERPASS/OVERPASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/us/OVERPASS/OVERPASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Design Picked for Wildlife Crossing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where a Highway Crosses Wildlife’s Path, Designers Compete to Avert Collisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roadkill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T21:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa23001d-159d-5fa1-80d3-a6755c5447ef', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa23001d-159d-5fa1-80d3-a6755c5447ef'}, {'abstract': 'Raf Simons has announced that he has severed his dealings with his manufacturing partner, leaving open the question of when he will be able to sell the fall 2011 collection to store buyers. His clothes deserve a wider audience.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/the-guide-raf-simons/', 'snippet': 'Raf Simons has announced that he has severed his dealings with his manufacturing partner, leaving open the question of when he will be able to sell the fall 2011 collection to store buyers. His clothes deserve a wider audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly six years ago, in a review of a Raf Simons show, I wrote that the Belgian designer deserved a Swiss bank. The reference was to the Swiss Textile Award that Mr. Simons had won that year and the difference the prize money made in his future-minded collection. Since then, many people have said I favor Mr. Simons, both in his men’s line and the women’s collections he does for Jil Sander. Look, I just think Mr. Simons consistently turns out interesting collections, and in 2005, I looked at videos and photographs of all his shows and presentations going back to the mid-’90s, to see what I had missed — which was a lot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Guide: Raf Simons', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sander, Jil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T21:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5578c071-ddc1-5cef-a507-4860b8374045', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5578c071-ddc1-5cef-a507-4860b8374045'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Gabrielle Giffords is likely to remain in an intensive care unit until the end of the week because of a slight buildup of spinal fluid in her brain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/us/24giffords.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Gabrielle Giffords is likely to remain in an intensive care unit until the end of the week because of a slight buildup of spinal fluid in her brain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON —Representative Gabrielle Giffords is likely to remain in an intensive care unit until the end of the week because of a slight buildup of spinal fluid in her brain after her transfer by air from Tucson to Memorial Hermann hospital here, hospital officials say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giffords Remains in Intensive Care', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giffords Remains in Intensive Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T21:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9814c722-b4fc-51e7-acad-f8cd6982cc36', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9814c722-b4fc-51e7-acad-f8cd6982cc36'}, {'abstract': 'The maker of Jimmy Dean sausages has received a preliminary bid from a group of buyout firms led by Apollo Global Management, and is expected to receive one from JBS of Brazil and the Blackstone Group.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/sara-lee-weighs-future-after-receiving-takeover-interest/', 'snippet': 'The maker of Jimmy Dean sausages has received a preliminary bid from a group of buyout firms led by Apollo Global Management, and is expected to receive one from JBS of Brazil and the Blackstone Group.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:56 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sara Lee Weighs Future After Receiving Takeover Interest', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JBS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sara Lee Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/50a03771-081c-5093-9e89-c02255b5fde5', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50a03771-081c-5093-9e89-c02255b5fde5'}, {'abstract': 'The image of early naturalists as exploitative hunters ignores their contributions to science and humanity.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/heroic-naturalists-or-imperialist-dogs/', 'snippet': 'The image of early naturalists as exploitative hunters ignores their contributions to science and humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it mean to discover a species? Who should get the credit for it? Why did early naturalists think it worth risking their lives, and often losing them, to ship home the first specimens of a previously unknown butterfly or bat? These turn out to be tangled questions, and it is easy to get stuck on the thorns. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heroic Naturalists or Imperialist Dogs?', 'kicker': 'Specimens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Conniff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conniff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd06f3ba-5cbe-56b2-bbf5-fcfba200301f', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd06f3ba-5cbe-56b2-bbf5-fcfba200301f'}, {'abstract': 'The region of southern Sudan, which recently carried out a referendum on seceding from the north, will be named the Republic of South Sudan upon independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/africa/24sudan.html', 'snippet': 'The region of southern Sudan, which recently carried out a referendum on seceding from the north, will be named the Republic of South Sudan upon independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, Sudan \x97 Southern Sudan, which recently carried out a referendum on seceding from the north, will be named the Republic of South Sudan upon independence, officials here in the regional capital said Sunday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Southern Sudan Nears a Decision on One Matter: Its New Name', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southern Sudan Nears a Decision on One Matter: Its New Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f3b1bd0-724e-55de-b3a1-281b18b0dde2', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f3b1bd0-724e-55de-b3a1-281b18b0dde2'}, {'abstract': 'More remembrances of Ellen Stewart of La MaMa.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/more-words-about-ellen-stewart/', 'snippet': 'More remembrances of Ellen Stewart of La MaMa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Space and deadline constraints kept some voices out of Sunday’s Arts and Leisure piece on Ellen Stewart, the guiding force behind the East Village performance space La MaMa and an Off Off Broadway pioneer who died on Jan. 13. Here, a few more theater-world figures remember Ms. Stewart as a figure of contradictions — at once easygoing and hard-nosed, opinionated and indulgent. Jason Zinoman, a critic for The New York Times, collected the recollections:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Words About Ellen Stewart', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Ellen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La MaMa ETC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd6c174c-9e76-509a-89ec-1c0fb0b3e9f0', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd6c174c-9e76-509a-89ec-1c0fb0b3e9f0'}, {'abstract': 'The defection of the Green Party raises questions about Prime Minister Brian Cowen’s hold on his office and the nation’s commitments under an international bailout plan for the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/europe/24ireland.html', 'snippet': 'The defection of the Green Party raises questions about Prime Minister Brian Cowen’s hold on his office and the nation’s commitments under an international bailout plan for the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON \x97 Ireland’s political turmoil deepened on Sunday when the Green Party abandoned the governing coalition with the Fianna Fail party of Prime Minister Brian Cowen, raising fresh doubts about Mr. Cowen’s ability to cling to office beyond the next few days and prompting new questions about Ireland’s commitments under the $114 billion bailout plan for its economy negotiated with international lenders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/IRELAND/IRELAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/IRELAND/IRELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/world/IRELAND/IRELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Green Party Quits Irish Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greens Quit Ireland Coalition, Imperiling Prime Minister', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowen, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GREEN PARTY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fianna Fail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae94c4cd-aac2-5fc0-a8dd-08d4a8c238aa', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae94c4cd-aac2-5fc0-a8dd-08d4a8c238aa'}, {'abstract': 'Live coverage and analysis of the A.F.C. championship game between the Jets and the Steelers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/coming-soon-jets-at-steelers/', 'snippet': 'Live coverage and analysis of the A.F.C. championship game between the Jets and the Steelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jets battled back from a 24-0 second quarter deficit, but it wasn’t enough. The Steelers held off their comeback to win the A.F.C. championship game by 24-19.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Analysis: Final: Steelers 24, Jets 19', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d51884c-7f4c-53d2-b57e-cb67d603b522', 'word_count': 3185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d51884c-7f4c-53d2-b57e-cb67d603b522'}, {'abstract': 'Repertorio Español performs Federico García Lorca’s mysterious, intimate play “Así Que Pasen Cinco Años” in Spanish with a live English translation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/theater/reviews/24once.html', 'snippet': 'Repertorio Español performs Federico García Lorca’s mysterious, intimate play “Así Que Pasen Cinco Años” in Spanish with a live English translation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beggars can’t be choosers. This was the cliché with which I tried to comfort myself Thursday night at the Gramercy Theater, at the opening of Repertorio Español’s production of Federico García Lorca’s “Así Que Pasen Cinco Años” (“Once Five Years Pass”). This mysterious, intimate play, which depicts a young man’s lengthy engagement, its traumatic end and out-of-time aftermath, is rarely performed and is here presented in the original Spanish. If you’re not proficient in that language, your experience of what seems to be a vibrant and muscular rendering by this company and its artistic director, René Buch, will be filtered through a live English translation (courtesy of headphones). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/ONCE/ONCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/ONCE/ONCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/ONCE/ONCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/ONCE/ONCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/ONCE/ONCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiancé, Tied in Poetic Knots', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Así Que Pasen Cinco Años'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fiancé, Tied in Poetic Knots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Repertorio Espanol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Lorca, Federico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7d53fc5-15e0-571c-9407-8d1aa3bab82f', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7d53fc5-15e0-571c-9407-8d1aa3bab82f'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of costumes designed by Theoni V. Aldredge, who died Jan. 21.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/24/theater/20110124-aldredge.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of costumes designed by Theoni V. Aldredge, who died Jan. 21.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of costumes designed by Theoni V. Aldredge, who died Jan. 21.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/theater/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/theater/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/theater/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM/20110124-aldredge-slide-47GM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life of Design', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aldredge, Theoni V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cf7f0420-49ce-5e04-a4e6-51a7df6ea024', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cf7f0420-49ce-5e04-a4e6-51a7df6ea024'}, {'abstract': 'Chick Corea joined the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra in a retrospective of his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/music/24corea.html', 'snippet': 'Chick Corea joined the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra in a retrospective of his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What should a Chick Corea retrospective concert sound like? There’s so much there, so many different causes and curiosities: cooled-out electric funk with singers, nearly classical solo-piano études, blizzarding jazz-rock, Afro-Cuban rhythms, straightforward extensions of Bud Powell and the jazz mainstream. Beyond Mr. Corea’s own keyboard touch, springy and clear with controlled flourish and just about perfect time, it’s hard to find a clean aesthetic line through what he does. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/COREA/COREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jazz Man Returns to His Past', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jazz Man Returns To His Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corea, Chick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2dd59bf-4bb6-5dd2-a064-631982e9e665', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2dd59bf-4bb6-5dd2-a064-631982e9e665'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Biss, a familiar presence at the piano in performances with orchestras, gets his solo recital at a legendary hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/music/24biss.html', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Biss, a familiar presence at the piano in performances with orchestras, gets his solo recital at a legendary hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thoughtful American pianist Jonathan Biss has played on the main stage at Carnegie Hall as a soloist with several orchestras. His vibrant account of Schumann’s Piano Concerto with James Levine and the Met Orchestra in 2008 comes to mind. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/BISS/BISS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 647, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pianist at Last Has Carnegie All to Himself', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pianist at Last Has Carnegie All to Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biss, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/32831e79-3367-55c8-92d1-424f1690fbb7', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32831e79-3367-55c8-92d1-424f1690fbb7'}, {'abstract': '“The Bright Stream,” choreographed by Alexei Ratmansky and performed by American Ballet Theater at the Kennedy Center, shows the comedy in life on a collective Soviet farm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/dance/24stream.html', 'snippet': '“The Bright Stream,” choreographed by Alexei Ratmansky and performed by American Ballet Theater at the Kennedy Center, shows the comedy in life on a collective Soviet farm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 It was a surprise to enter the Kennedy Center, which is currently presenting an exhibition commemorating the presidency of John F. Kennedy, and find, across the Opera House proscenium arch, the hammer and sickle insignia of Soviet Russia. In June the same hammer and sickle will hang in the Metropolitan Opera House in New York. We’ve come a long way since the cold war \x97 but how?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/STREAM/STREAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/STREAM/STREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/STREAM/STREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Down on the Dacha, Farmers Showing Off Expressive Footwork', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Down on the Dacha, Farmers Showing Off Expressive Footwork', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shostakovich, Dmitri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e27d813b-f6d6-5b5a-9c95-723818249f09', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e27d813b-f6d6-5b5a-9c95-723818249f09'}, {'abstract': 'Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker dances as part of the Museum of Modern Art’s Performance Exhibition Series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/dance/24moma.html', 'snippet': 'Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker dances as part of the Museum of Modern Art’s Performance Exhibition Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1981 Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker, a young Belgian student at New York University’s Tisch School of the Arts, presented her first professional work of choreography at a festival in Westchester County in New York. It was a solo, set to Steve Reich’s “Violin Phase,” in which Ms. De Keersmaeker moved in circular patterns with strict repetitions of a single turning, twisting phrase that brilliantly played off the music’s formalism and drama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/MOMA/MOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/MOMA/MOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/MOMA/MOMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/MOMA/MOMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/MOMA/MOMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dancer’s Line and the Artist’s Line Intersect in the Sand', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dancer’s Line and the Artist’s Line Intersect in the Sand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Keersmaeker, Anne Teresa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:47:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/284669ba-419d-555d-90f6-95a8bb068d46', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/284669ba-419d-555d-90f6-95a8bb068d46'}, {'abstract': 'This year the Juilliard School’s annual Focus! Festival surveys Polish music since 1945. The opening concert was on Saturday at Alice Tully Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/music/24focus.html', 'snippet': 'This year the Juilliard School’s annual Focus! Festival surveys Polish music since 1945. The opening concert was on Saturday at Alice Tully Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Juilliard School’s annual Focus! Festival provides a significant service for New York concertgoers by shining a light, sustained and searching, on a tightly defined subject. Usually the themes are geographical, and Joel Sachs, the festival’s director, has made a point of assembling programs that balance familiar names with composers most Americans will not have encountered. You invariably come away from these free concerts with a sense of having discovered something. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/FOCUS/FOCUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 489, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Embracing the Modern With Tone Clusters, Not Dissonance', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Embracing the Modern With Tone Clusters, Not Dissonance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Juilliard Ensemble', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd7193fb-2e58-53b9-98a9-a0324b911c1a', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd7193fb-2e58-53b9-98a9-a0324b911c1a'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Radu Lupu and the conductor Christoph von Dohnanyi apply their talents to Brahms’s Piano Concerto No. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/music/24lupu.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Radu Lupu and the conductor Christoph von Dohnanyi apply their talents to Brahms’s Piano Concerto No. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many classical and operatic works that are now repertory standards were glumly received at their premieres because of substandard performances, bafflement at audacious musical gestures or simply the audience’s inability to appreciate the worth of a new piece immediately. During one of its first performances, Brahms’s Piano Concerto No. 1 in D minor, now popular, was greeted with widespread hissing from puzzled listeners. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/LUPU/LUPU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Chair, Not a Bench, Exploring Brahms’s Poetry', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From a Chair, Not a Bench, Exploring Brahms’s Poetry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lupu, Radu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dohnanyi, Christoph von', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d872e73-7e97-55aa-acb6-a8b594d4e5db', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d872e73-7e97-55aa-acb6-a8b594d4e5db'}, {'abstract': 'Emanuel Ax headlines a Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center program of Schubert and new music inspired by him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/arts/music/24ax.html', 'snippet': 'Emanuel Ax headlines a Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center program of Schubert and new music inspired by him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing about Schubert inevitably begins with how hard it is to understand him. His biography is ambiguous, his musical style unclassifiable: no longer Classical but not yet Romantic, and looking ahead toward decidedly modern harmonies and rhythms.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/arts/AX/AX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relishing and Playing With Reverberations of Schubert', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relishing and Playing With Reverberations of Schubert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ax, Emanuel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65a3cc7e-ed72-553b-82f6-16da7b5cfbf0', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65a3cc7e-ed72-553b-82f6-16da7b5cfbf0'}, {'abstract': 'Practicing what he preached at the premiere of his product placement documentary “The Greatest Story Ever Sold,” Morgan Spurlock sold one a naming right to one audience member.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/buying-your-way-into-the-credits/', 'snippet': 'Practicing what he preached at the premiere of his product placement documentary “The Greatest Story Ever Sold,” Morgan Spurlock sold one a naming right to one audience member.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— “Docbuster” is what Morgan Spurlock calls his product placement documentary “The Greatest Movie Ever Sold” – excuse us, “Pom Wonderful Presents: The Greatest Movie Ever Sold” (as our colleague Brooks Barnes told us yesterday). In the film, Mr. Spurlock, the stunt documentarian behind “Supersize Me,” doesn’t address whether (or how well) marketing sponsorships and tie-ins work on consumers, but at the premiere of the film on Saturday, it was kind of clear. Appearing at the Q&A wearing a suit adorned with the logos of the corporations that funded his movie – Pom pomegranate juice, JetBlue Airways, Ban deodorant, etc. – Mr. Spurlock brought the company executives, a k a his cast, up front with him for a resounding round of applause. He began drinking a bottle of Pom. “I’m 40 percent happier, suddenly,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buying Your Way Into the Credits', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Product Placement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spurlock, Morgan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-23T22:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e48712ab-9df3-5262-ab17-b5b1c1cddbcb', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e48712ab-9df3-5262-ab17-b5b1c1cddbcb'}, {'abstract': 'Even as pressure built on him and his Jets, Coach Rex Ryan did not back away from his bombastic personality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sports/football/24araton.html', 'snippet': 'Even as pressure built on him and his Jets, Coach Rex Ryan did not back away from his bombastic personality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pittsburgh', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/YJETS/YJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/YJETS/YJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/18/sports/YJETS/YJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Season Comes to an End, but Ryan Is Unbowed', 'kicker': 'On Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets’ Season Comes to an End, But Ryan Is Unbowed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '