on by more than 30,000 people in Brussels was the first clear sign of popular frustration at Belgium’s protracted political crisis and its worrying effect on financial markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/world/europe/24belgium.html', 'snippet': 'A demonstration by more than 30,000 people in Brussels was the first clear sign of popular frustration at Belgium’s protracted political crisis and its worrying effect on financial markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS \x97 Defying the normal conventions of protest politics, more than 30,000 Belgians rallied here on Sunday not to try to get rid of a government, but to press their squabbling politicians to form one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/BELGIUM/BELGIUM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 957, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belgians Press Politicians to Form Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belgians Take to the Streets to Protest the Government (a Lack of One, That Is)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T00:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Ne