'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mindlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a690e60d-451c-590e-b13d-f380c21fd692', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a690e60d-451c-590e-b13d-f380c21fd692'}, {'abstract': 'In his State of the Union address, President Obama must fully delineate his own plans in the face of a newly strengthened and shrill Republican Party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/opinion/24mon1.html', 'snippet': 'In his State of the Union address, President Obama must fully delineate his own plans in the face of a newly strengthened and shrill Republican Party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama unveiled a promising new theme on Friday when he toured a factory in Schenectady, N.Y., and began talking about the desperate need to foster competitiveness and innovation in the pursuit of American jobs. The real test of his commitment to that cause in the second half of his term will come on Tuesday in his State of the Union address. He will have to make his case in the face of a newly strengthened and shrill Republican Party, determined to dismantle government’s most fundamental role in fighting the recession.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Chance for Mr. Obama', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Chance for Mr. Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T02:17:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc7e