': 'nyt://article/1f0c41d0-ccc7-5daa-bea0-10eedc23a33d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. LaLanne found recognition through his obsession with grueling workouts and nutrition, complemented by a salesman’s gift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sports/24lalanne.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. LaLanne found recognition through his obsession with grueling workouts and nutrition, complemented by a salesman’s gift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack LaLanne, whose obsession with grueling workouts and good nutrition, complemented by a salesman’s gift, brought him recognition as the founder of the modern physical fitness movement, died Sunday afternoon at his home in Morro Bay, Calif. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/sports/LALANNE-obit/LALANNE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/sports/LALANNE-obit/LALANNE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/sports/LALANNE-obit/LALANNE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jack LaLanne, Founder of Modern Fitness Movement, Dies at 96', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jack LaLanne, 96, Fitness’s Father, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaLanne, Jack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T03:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/23f28ab0-23d5-5338-9572-ccf7ce8f083a', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23f28ab0-23d5-5338-9572-ccf7ce8f083a'}, {'abstract': 'After a rough start last year, the “Next” films are turning into Exhibit A of how cheap digital technology is level the filmmaker playing field.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/23/the-search-for-the-next-little-thing/', 'snippet': 'After a rough start last year, the “Next” films are turning into Exhibit A of how cheap digital technology is level the filmmaker playing field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— Last year, Sundance decided to start a new section of the festival called “Next,” dedicated to “low- and no-budget films.” It didn’t go so well. Filmmakers placed in the section hated being called out for their shoestring shoots and the films turned out to be, well, not that great.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Search for the ‘Next’ Little Thing', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T03:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b367af-9c86-54f9-80be-a0e4a7466dc9', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b367af-9c86-54f9-80be-a0e4a7466dc9'}, {'abstract': 'Though the two chambers of Congress always have their own rhythms, they have started the year with an unusually stark contrast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/us/politics/24senate.html', 'snippet': 'Though the two chambers of Congress always have their own rhythms, they have started the year with an unusually stark contrast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In its first few weeks of official business this year, the House of Representatives voted to undo President Obama’s health care overhaul, pondered cuts to large swaths of the government and stood silently beneath flags flying at half-staff to honor a fallen Congressional aide and his critically wounded boss.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/us/SENATE/SENATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'While House Is Abuzz, Senate Hits Snooze Button', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While House Is Abuzz, Senate Hits Snooze Button', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T03:28:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126be160-8236-5e18-99e8-7c2921ffc705', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126be160-8236-5e18-99e8-7c2921ffc705'}, {'abstract': 'It has not taken Mark Sanchez long to reach rarefied air, but against the Steelers, he couldn’t replicate the late-game heroics he displayed in games against the Colts and Patriots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sports/football/24green.html', 'snippet': 'It has not taken Mark Sanchez long to reach rarefied air, but against the Steelers, he couldn’t replicate the late-game heroics he displayed in games against the Colts and Patriots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH \x97 The education of Mark Sanchez has featured questions of development alongside flashes of brilliance. But each of his first two seasons ended in the same place: the A.F.C. title game.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/subGREEN/subGREEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/subGREEN/subGREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/subGREEN/subGREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanchez Grows Again, but It’s Not Enough', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sanchez Grows Again, But It’s Not Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh S