lion defending the mortgage finance companies and their former top executives in civil lawsuits accusing them of fraud. The cost was a closely guarded secret until last week, when the companies and their regulator produced an accounting at the request of Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fannie and Freddie Leave Legal Bills to Taxpayers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T07:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b77d28-43d2-5dba-aae4-02803f51b69e', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b77d28-43d2-5dba-aae4-02803f51b69e'}, {'abstract': 'Commissioners did not vote on the recommendation that a higher standard of fiduciary duty be applied.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/s-e-c-study-recommends-more-oversight-of-brokers/', 'snippet': 'Commissioners did not vote on the recommendation that a higher standard of fiduciary duty be applied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investment advisers and stockbrokers should be subject to the same fiduciary standard of conduct — putting a customer’s interests above their own — rather than the different governance regimes that currently apply to the two groups, the Securities and Exchange Commission recommended on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Study Recommends More Oversight of Brokers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T07:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d