web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/pereira-agrees-that-sanchez-fumbled/', 'snippet': 'The CBS announcer Jim Nantz thought it was a pass by Mark Sanchez. The officials ruled that it was a fumble. What did you think?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The CBS announcer Jim Nantz thought it was a pass. The officials ruled that it was a fumble. What did you think?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pereira Agrees That Sanchez Fumbled', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pereira, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T10:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4ddb717-304e-580a-9a19-2219330e2953', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4ddb717-304e-580a-9a19-2219330e2953'}, {'abstract': 'Sanofi-Aventis has extended its $69-a-share tender offer for all outstanding Genzyme common stock to Feb. 15.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sanofi-extends-tender-offer-as-talks-drag-on/', 'snippet': 'Sanofi-Aventis has extended its $69-a-share tender offer for all outstanding Genzyme common stock to Feb. 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sanofi-Aventis, the French drug giant, said on Monday that its $69-a-share tender offer for all outstanding Genzyme common stock, which was to have expired on Friday, had been extended to Feb. 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanofi Extends Genzyme Tender Offer as Talks Drag On', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genzyme Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanofi-Aventis S.A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T10:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9679a98-c300-5427-ae13-92773c9ddec7', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9679a98-c300-5427-ae13-92773c9ddec7'}, {'abstract': 'The Kala Ghoda Arts Festival is Mumbai’s most important annual cultural event. This year’s version will take place Feb. 5 to 13, spread over several streets in Mumbai’s tiny but beautiful colonial-era art district.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/in-the-streets-mumbai-celebrates-the-arts/', 'snippet': 'The Kala Ghoda Arts Festival is Mumbai’s most important annual cultural event. This year’s version will take place Feb. 5 to 13, spread over several streets in Mumbai’s tiny but beautiful colonial-era art district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the general absence of parks and open spaces, the street is the nucleus of communal life in Mumbai. It’s where meals are sold and eaten, where groceries are purchased on the commute home and where neighbors gather every evening for a chat. But until recent years, art and culture remained off the city’s streets, strictly confined to galleries and theaters frequented by the elite. The debut of the Kala Ghoda Arts Festival (KGAF) in 1999 changed that. This year’s version will take place Feb. 5 to 13, spread over several streets in Mumbai’s tiny but beautiful colonial-era art district. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Streets, Mumbai Celebrates the Arts', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Riddhi Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Riddhi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e72ff7bf-c7fc-5a59-bac8-6f89be696d9c', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e72ff7bf-c7fc-5a59-bac8-6f89be696d9c'}, {'abstract': 'Polygamy carries a social stigma, for good reason, an economist writes, but some in her field are finding it a rich vein of research.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/the-economics-of-big-love/', 'snippet': 'Polygamy carries a social stigma, for good reason, an economist writes, but some in her field are finding it a rich vein of research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy Folbre is an economics professor at the University of Massachusetts Amherst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Economics of Big Love', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polygamy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T11:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Folbre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Folbre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a6b3b29-596c-5014-b9b0-e2557c07c017', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a6b3b29-596c-5014-b9b0-e2557c07c017'}, {'abstract': 'Rex Ryan will undoubtedly declare that the Jets will win the Super Bowl before next season. But should he?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/has-rex-ryan-set-the-bar-too-high/', 'snippet': 'Rex Ryan will undoubtedly declare that the Jets will win the Super Bowl before next season. But should he?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only a cynic would argue that a loss in the A.F.C. championship game, even if it was the second straight stumble at the playoffs’ penultimate step, means the Jets had a bad year. But Coach Rex Ryan had vowed a season of Super Bowl or bust, and now he has the latter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Has Rex Ryan Set the Bar Too High?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T11:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materia