rtation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T12:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f65a9fb1-44e5-54f2-9093-c61c2fac8c00', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f65a9fb1-44e5-54f2-9093-c61c2fac8c00'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s resident political statistical guru looks to see if the best-reviewed film of the year might be hurt by the Academy’s preferential voting system.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/critics-love-the-social-network-will-the-academy-defriend-it/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s resident political statistical guru looks to see if the best-reviewed film of the year might be hurt by the Academy’s preferential voting system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nate Silver will be providing awards-season insight for Carpetbagger leading up to the 83rd Academy Awards on Feb. 27. Mr. Silver is the author of the Times’ FiveThirtyEight blog, which is devoted to the analysis of statistics and data in politics and other areas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics Love ‘Social Network.’ Will The Academy Defriend It?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T12:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e0e8035-df96-5864-919a-6c82b617f88e', 'word_count': 2245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e0e8035-df96-5864-919a-6c82b617f88e'}, {'abstract': 'A Hungarian layered casserole of potatoes and eggs, with sour cream and paprika.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/the-temporary-vegetarian-hungarian-potato-and-egg-casserole/', 'snippet': 'A Hungarian layered casserole of potatoes and eggs, with sour cream and paprika.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarabeth Levine, the baker, restaurateur and cookbook author, gave me the recipe for rakott krumpli, a Hungarian layered casserole of potatoes and eggs, with sour cream and paprika, at a party. I was so excited by the simple and tasty sound of it, that the moment I got home, I made it with one potato, one egg – and a tweak. I added a layer of sautéed onions to moisten and sweeten the dish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Temporary Vegetarian: Hungarian Potato and Egg Casserole', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T13:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f65923-deae-53a7-b968-8763a32f3b75', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f65923-deae-53a7-b968-8763a32f3b75'}, {'abstract': 'General Assembly, a new space in Manhattan with services for entrepreneurs, aims to provide a hub for the blossoming New York technology scene.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/a-place-for-techies-to-gather/', 'snippet': 'General Assembly, a new space in Manhattan with services for entrepreneurs, aims to provide a hub for the blossoming New York technology scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new business in the Flatiron district of Manhattan called General Assembly is not a university, but its founders hope it will seem like one. The 20,000-square-foot space offers desks, Internet access, classes and other services for entrepreneurs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Assembly Aims to Gather New York Techies', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Office Space, And More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T13:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/42cbe838-6757-5a57-b9f3-eba0b0df8048', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42cbe838-6757-5a57-b9f3-eba0b0df8048'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets’ primary headset went out early, and the backup  stopped working during a key sequence in the fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/sanchez-says-headset-malfunctioned/', 'snippet': 'The Jets’ primary headset went out early, and the backup  stopped working during a key sequence in the fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quarterback Mark Sanchez said a malfunctioning headset made things that much more difficult for the Jets in the