ing to see whether he will be chosen to serve on a jury.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:34 p.m. | Updated Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. has traded in the White House Situation Room for a courthouse in Wilmington, Del., where he is waiting to see whether he will be chosen to serve on a jury.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Reports for Jury Duty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2be43ba6-713b-565a-9c10-ac7ad6dbd955', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2be43ba6-713b-565a-9c10-ac7ad6dbd955'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker, which has lagged behind most major brands in developing hybrid or electric-vehicle powertrains, announced it would begin leasing an E.V. in its home market next year.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/in-japan-mazda-steps-up-e-v-intent/', 'snippet': 'The automaker, which has lagged behind most major brands in developing hybrid or electric-vehicle powertrains, announced it would begin leasing an E.V. in its home market next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Monday, Mazda could not muster even a wan embrace of hybrid or electric-vehicle technology, ceding that buzzing high ground to fellow Japanese bran