terial': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54bff0e1-5625-5ab1-8717-b79073bcaf80', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54bff0e1-5625-5ab1-8717-b79073bcaf80'}, {'abstract': 'Archie Gottesman, who leads Edison Properties, which owns the building called the Ludlow, made it a rule that new renters there have their pets spayed or neutered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/nyregion/25appraisal.html', 'snippet': 'Archie Gottesman, who leads Edison Properties, which owns the building called the Ludlow, made it a rule that new renters there have their pets spayed or neutered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Archie Gottesman is a pet lover and the chairwoman of Animal Haven, a shelter for cats and dogs. She spends her spare time looking for homes for pets, to save them from being euthanized. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving New Meaning to the Term ‘a Fixer-Upper’', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker'