ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1629cb2-bc3b-594a-bef3-245fb6b93313', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1629cb2-bc3b-594a-bef3-245fb6b93313'}, {'abstract': 'The term gets thrown around a lot, but what does it really mean? And is it demeaning? Or a dream-come-true?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/is-the-term-lifestyle-business-an-insult/', 'snippet': 'The term gets thrown around a lot, but what does it really mean? And is it demeaning? Or a dream-come-true?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The week of January 10 offered something of a theme here at You’re the Boss. Both Paul Downs and I wrote posts (here’s Paul’s post, here’s mine) addressing various aspects of owning what is commonly referred to as a “lifestyle business.” After more than 50 comments combined, Ted in Tacoma Park finally asked for a definition of the term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Term ‘Lifestyle Business’ an Insult?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:49:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4d57407-0217-59d2-a6a9-2fc24c29aeed', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4d57407-0217-59d2-a6a9-2fc24c29aeed'}, {'abstract': 'Mozilla and Google said Monday that they plan to provide browser features that will allow users to opt-out of being tracked by third-party advertisers online.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/google-and-mozilla-announce-new-privacy-features/', 'snippet': 'Mozilla and Google said Monday that they plan to provide browser features that will allow users to opt-out of being tracked by third-party advertisers online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Add two more Internet browser makers to the list of companies planning to offer Web users new ways to control how their personal data is collected online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google and Mozilla Announce New Privacy Features', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mozilla Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c15ef7e-8447-57c5-b3a8-4e7463d435be', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c15ef7e-8447-57c5-b3a8-4e7463d435be'}, {'abstract': 'Vanisha Mittal Bhatia — the only daughter of the world’s fifth-richest man, Lakshmi Mittal — and her husband, Amit Bhatia, purchased a sizable stake in the quantitative hedge fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/mittal-heiress-buys-stake-in-roc-capital/', 'snippet': 'Vanisha Mittal Bhatia — the only daughter of the world’s fifth-richest man, Lakshmi Mittal — and her husband, Amit Bhatia, purchased a sizable stake in the quantitative hedge fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vanisha Mittal Bhatia, the only daughter of the world’s fifth-richest man, Lakshmi N. Mittal, ArcelorMittal’s chief executive, recently purchased a sizable stake in the quantitative hedge fund Roc Capital, according to a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mittal Heiress Buys Stake in Roc Capital', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ArcelorMittal S.A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f045737-c345-5a46-b7ec-c61961448372', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f045737-c345-5a46-b7ec-c61961448372'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s mayor, together with family members and friends of shooting victims, urged a better background check system for gun buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/nyregion/25bloomberg.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s mayor, together with family members and friends of shooting victims, urged a better background check system for gun buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man whose son was among the students killed at Columbine High School stepped up to the microphone at City Hall on Monday wearing the boy’s sneakers. A pastor recalled a former congregant who was one of the people shot this month outside a supermarket in Tucson. And a woman told the story of her son, who died in 2007 in East Harlem. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/ybloomberg/ybloomberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/ybloomberg/ybloomberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/ybloomberg/ybloomberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/ybloomberg/ybloomberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/ybloomberg/ybloomberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg and Relatives of Shooting Victims Push for Stricter Gun Control', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg Pushes for Stricter Gun Control Measures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mayors Against Illegal Guns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5ca2b4-60c1-5ea1-934f-1fb9369516c7', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5ca2b4-60c1-5ea1-934f-1fb9369516c7'}, {'abstract': 'The Appraisal: Is a landlord’s requirement that prospective tenants get their pets spayed or neutered reasonable?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/a-pets-fair-price-for-a-home/', 'snippet': 'The Appraisal: Is a landlord’s requirement that prospective tenants get their pets spayed or neutered reasonable?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Appraisal column, we tell of one downtown landlord who also runs an animal shelter and requires cat and dog owners to get their pets spayed or neutered if they want to live in her apartment building, the Ludlow, on the Lower East Side. The policy, a reflection of the owner’s concerns about all the unwanted cats and dogs put to sleep each year, doesn’t seem to have upset many of her tenants, who largely share her sentiments. But that doesn’t mean it wouldn’t bother other pet owners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pet’s Fair Price for a Home?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T17:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By