ries of problems using chess pieces on a four-by-four grid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ThinkFun, a maker of puzzle and game software, has developed a chess application for the iPhone, iPad and iTouch. Called Solitaire Chess, the application presents a series of problems with chess pieces on a four-by-four grid. The challenge is to eliminate all but one piece through a series of captures. The problems vary in difficulty from easy to expert. There is a demonstration Web site for people to test out the application. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Solitaire Chess Anyone?', 'kicker': 'Gambit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T19:42:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6e7bf00-36e7-517d-8c2d-89886d861baf', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6e7bf00-36e7-517d-8c2d-89886d861baf'}, {'abstract': 'A veteran climate scientist who, as a grandfather, has become a climate campaigner, presses the president to abandon special interests.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/nasas-hansen-presses-obama-for-a-carbon-cost-and-nuclear-push/', 'snippet': 'A veteran climate scientist who, as a grandfather, has become a climate campaigner, presses the president to abandon special interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 26, 10:35 p.m. | Updated below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NASA’s Hansen Presses Obama for a Carbon Cost and Nuclear Push', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, James E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T19:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d10d1c8e-5a07-51f2-b04e-fe988f87ba71', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d10d1c8e-5a07-51f2-b04e-fe988f87ba71'}, {'abstract': 'For seven seasons, first on NBC and then on CBS, “Medium” offered a blend of outlandish story lines and a believable marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/medium-ends-with-emotional-farewell/', 'snippet': 'For seven seasons, first on NBC and then on CBS, “Medium” offered a blend of outlandish story lines and a believable marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For seven seasons, first on NBC and then on CBS, “Medium” put across some of prime time’s most outlandish story lines by grounding them in one of television’s most believable marriages. So it was fitting that the series, a combination of paranormal murder mystery and domestic dramedy, crossed over to the TV hereafter on Friday night with a series finale that was narratively challenged but emotionally satisfying. It didn’t take a medium to predict that there would be tears.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Medium’ Ends With Emotional Farewell', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARQUETTE, PATRICIA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T19:44:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2276b35c-23bc-57cf-ac33-0d05a64f5e39', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2276b35c-23bc-57cf-ac33-0d05a64f5e39'}, {'abstract': 'By circumcising an infant according to Jewish tradition moments after his death, a doctor who also is a mohel provided a moment of normality to a family confronting immense loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/health/views/25cases.html', 'snippet': 'By circumcising an infant according to Jewish tradition moments after his death, a doctor who also is a mohel provided a moment of normality to a family confronting immense loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My hands trembled as I grasped the tiny sleeve of skin with my forceps and separated it from his pale, still penis. He lay weirdly motionless on a utility table, which I had draped with a slate-blue operating-room towel. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/health/25cases/25cases-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/health/25cases/25cases-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/health/25cases/25cases-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Life Passes, and a Ritual of Birth Begins', 'kicker': 'Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Young Life Passes, and a Ritual of Birth Begins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotions)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T19:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark S. Litwin, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Litwin', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c6e8394-886e-59fc-9d8a-1d9a40f83314', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c6e8394-886e-59fc-9d8a-1d9a40f83314'}, {'abstract': 'the British novelist', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0125.html', 'snippet': 'the British novelist', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON, April 2--Mrs. Virginia Woolf, novelist and essayist, who has been missing from her home since last Friday, is believed to have been drowned at Rodwell, near Lewes, where she and her husband, Leonard Sidney Woolf, had a country residence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia Woolf Believed Dead', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T19:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Special Cable to The New York Times', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9833a962-f6b8-5940-8ed9-85bae9484500', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9833a962-f6b8-5940-8ed9-85bae9484500'}, {'abstract': 'In very rare cases, overdoses of caffeine have been fatal. But it would be very hard to ingest enough ordinary coffee \x97 at least 42 cups at a sitting \x97 to kill yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/science/25qna.html', 'snippet': 'In very rare cases, overdoses of caffeine have been fatal. But it would be very hard to ingest enough ordinary coffee \x97 at least 42 cups at a sitting \x97 to kill yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Can too much caffeine kill you?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25qna/25qna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 867, 'subTyp