'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b44995-e13e-5fcc-91f9-3c0b4c952bb7', 'word_count': 3548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b44995-e13e-5fcc-91f9-3c0b4c952bb7'}, {'abstract': 'A hint: It has less to do with price-to-earnings ratios and more to do with goals and plans that are much more qualitative.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/when-to-sell-your-stocks/', 'snippet': 'A hint: It has less to do with price-to-earnings ratios and more to do with goals and plans that are much more qualitative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog, and other drawings are available on his personal Web site, BehaviorGap.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When to Sell Your Stocks', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ebffc27-18ba-5ff3-b3dd-a362520c5fd8', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ebffc27-18ba-5ff3-b3dd-a362520c5fd8'}, {'abstract': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">Proclamation and Induction Implement Sovereignty and Sever Ties With British\n</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\nTwo-Day National Holiday\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/big/0126.html', 'snippet': '<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\n<font size="+1">Proclamation and Induction Implement Sovereignty and Sever Ties With British\n</font>\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>\nTwo-Day National Holiday\n<HR align="LEFT" size="1" width="50"/>', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Delhi, Jan. 25 -- The proclamation of the Republic of India and the induction of the first President, Dr. Rajendra Prasad, will be marked by a two-day national holiday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India a Republic, Prasad President ', 'kicker': 'January 27, 1950', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': '<h5>By Robert Trumbull </h5>\n<h5>Special to The New York Times </h5>', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e730114e-4ce6-5074-b0cd-0fa1b8285eef', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e730114e-4ce6-5074-b0cd-0fa1b8285eef'}, {'abstract': 'the American general who achieved acclaim as a grand strategist in World War II and in Korea', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0126.html', 'snippet': 'the American general who achieved acclaim as a grand strategist in World War II and in Korea', 'lead_paragraph': ' General of the Army Douglas MacArthur served his country as a soldier for more than 60 years. He achieved the highest acclaim for his exploits as a grand strategist in World War II and in Korea and then held the center stage in one of the bitterest civil versus military controversies in the history of the nation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commander of Armies That Turned Back Japan Led a Brigade in World War I', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c3d8902-bcf0-54b9-9663-dcbd331d7fc5', 'word_count': 6396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c3d8902-bcf0-54b9-9663-dcbd331d7fc5'}, {'abstract': 'Wild enthusiasm in seeking and treating tiny abnormalities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/health/views/25zuger.html', 'snippet': 'Wild enthusiasm in seeking and treating tiny abnormalities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Make no mistake about it: modern medicine is a religion. For all the complicated science, the bottom line is that either you believe in the science or you don’t. If you are an average citizen and have your doubts, then you can just go about your business. But suppose you are a doctor and have your doubts. Then what?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25zuge/25zuge-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25zuge/25zuge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/science/25zuge/25zuge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pound of Prevention Is Worth a Closer Look', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pound of Prevention Is Worth a Closer Look', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welch, H Gilbert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c940edcf-63b8-555e-927d-eddea977bffc', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c940edcf-63b8-555e-927d-eddea977bffc'}, {'abstract': 'The ever-combative former leader of The New Republic helped toughen up modern liberalism. So he’s not about to let some lily-livered lefties take him down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Peretz-t.html', 'snippet': 'The ever-combative former leader of The New Republic helped toughen up modern liberalism. So he’s not about to let some lily-livered lefties take him down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE WINTER LIGHT was fading to gold near the Western Wall when a young Orthodox Jew with curls the color of Jerusalem stone approached an elderly pilgrim clad in suede boots and a Gucci leather jacket. The boy tried to tie a teffilin\xad — a black leather box with Torah verses inside — around the American’s arm. The gesture was not necessarily altruistic; he was hoping for a donation in return. The man resisted. The boy tried another approach.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/magazine/30peretz-1/30peretz-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 685, 