roups “that have an interest in and actively protect our nation’s waters and wetlands resources.” But it’s a lobbying group for farming, mining and manufacturing interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, the Waters Advocacy Coalition could be mistaken for a typical environmental group. The home page of its Web site, protectmywater.org, features a banner reading “Protect the Clean Water Act” across a photo slide show of flowing streams and clear mountain lakes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Industry Group’s Self-Depiction Raises Eyebrows', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FARM BUREAU FEDERATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Manufacturers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Cattlemen's Beef Assn", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc437c24-a5de-51e8-ae74-17a3a09c1b6c', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc437c24-a5de-51e8-ae74-17a3a09c1b6c'}, {'abstract': 'The areas where the women were assigned to work had 21 percent fewer stillbirths and 15 percent fewer newborn deaths than in other areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/