confused about whether they are getting enough — or maybe too much — calcium and vitamin D through their diets and supplements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people are confused about whether they are getting enough — or maybe too much — calcium and vitamin D through their diets and supplements, writes Jane Brody in this week’s Personal Health column.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Getting Enough Calcium and Vitamin D?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calcium', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamin D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Bilanow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilanow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1810644-48cd-5fce-b2ca-d5be687d979b', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1810644-48cd-5fce-b2ca-d5be687d979b'}, {'abstract': 'Dining suggestions from Sam Sifton, restaurant critic for The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/hey-mr-critic-20/', 'snippet': 'Dining suggestions from Sam Sifton, restaurant critic for The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mailman brought in a devilish question about breakfast bagels, and a sweet one about marriage and birthdays. Someone wanted to know where to get a drink and a bite after seeing “The Merchant of Venice” on Broadway. I tried to answer these queries and more. As always, you can send questions about where to go or what to eat in New York to dinejournal@nytimes.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hey, Mr. Critic!', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fc5ca2f-cb2e-581d-bb86-7a3db0c480d8', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fc5ca2f-cb2e-581d-bb86-7a3db0c480d8'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/photos-of-the-moment-paul-smith-2/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#380", 592, 490, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Paul Smith', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaee8391-fc59-5ebe-8b2f-0dfa64291e17', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaee8391-fc59-5ebe-8b2f-0dfa64291e17'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Rachid Ammar told protesters the military would keep stability until the interim government had elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/world/africa/25tunis.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Rachid Ammar told protesters the military would keep stability until the interim government had elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS \x97 The general who may be both the most powerful and the most popular figure in Tunisia spoke publicly Monday for the first time since the ouster of the former dictator, Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, pledging to uphold “the revolution” and urging patience until the interim government can hold new elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/world/25tunis_337/TUNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/world/25tunis_337/TUNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/world/25tunis_337/TUNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chief of Tunisian Army Pledges His Support for ‘the Revolution’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chief of Tunisian Army Pledges His Support for ‘the Revolution’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ammar, Rachid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:18:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d48c53e-66fa-541d-aa5b-4614650b043c', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d48c53e-66fa-541d-aa5b-4614650b043c'}, {'abstract': 'The carmaker will call back workers from a pool of about 3,000 nationwide and add a shift to build versions of the GMC Sierra and Chevrolet Silverado.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/business/25gm.html', 'snippet': 'The carmaker will call back workers from a pool of about 3,000 nationwide and add a shift to build versions of the GMC Sierra and Chevrolet Silverado.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLINT, Mich. \x97 General Motors said on Monday that it would add 750 jobs so that it can increase production of pickup trucks, welcome news in this economically depressed city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Plans to Add 750 Jobs at Pickup Truck Plant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Plans to Add 750 Jobs at Pickup Truck Plant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flint (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff58cad-d0e8-52f3-867e-5b5f37abdfa7', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff58cad-d0e8-52f3-867e-5b5f37abdfa7'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas Berdych and Novak Kjokovic meet in a quarterfinal match at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/quarterfinals-preview-berdych-vs-djokovic/', 'snippet': 'Tomas Berdych and Novak Kjokovic meet in a quarterfinal match at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomas Berdych overpowered Novak Djokovic in their Wimbledon semifinal last July. The tall Czech served well and outhit Djokovic in a match that was surprisingly one-sided. Time and again, Berdych turned a point his way with a huge inside-out forehand, generating tremendous force with seemingly little effort. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quarterfinals Preview: Berdych vs. Djokovic', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc783d96-c9a0-506c-b346-1a54cd19f2b1', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc783d96-c9a0-506c-b346-1a54cd19f2b1'}, {'abstract': 'The final season of this HBO series appears headed toward exploring the effects of an insidious strain of patriarchy on the lives of the women featured.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/big-love-watch-women-under-pressure/', 'snippet': 'The final season of this HBO series appears headed toward exploring the effects of an insidious strain of patriarchy on the lives of the women featured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seemed deliciously timely that Sunday night’s episode of “Big Love” turned Nicki Grant into a kind of fundamentalist Mormon Tiger Mom. The final season is distinctly headed toward exploring the effects of an insidious strain of patriarchy on the lives of the women featured.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Big Love’ Watch: Women Under Pressure', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paxton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad50bf70-51d2-5ba0-adfb-beb759e6e56e', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad50bf70-51d2-5ba0-adfb-beb759e6e56e'}, {'abstract': 'Financial Crisis Rashomon|The S.E.C. and the Sick C.E.O.|Floyd Norris on CoCo’s', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/buzz-tracker-15/', 'snippet': 'Financial Crisis Rashomon|The S.E.C. and the Sick C.E.O.|Floyd Norris on CoCo’s', 'lead_paragraph': '3 Crisis Reports Coming Heidi N. Moore, during her DealBook stint, once likened a paper by some Republican members of the Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission to “a game of political Rashomon.” But as Jeremy Irons, playing Claus von Bulow, drawled in “Reversal of Fortune,” “You have no idea.” For come Thursday, we will be getting not just two views of the financial crisis, but three. Kevin Drawbaugh and Dave Clarke of Reuters say that the six Democrats will release a report focusing on “the greed and power of Wall Street” Republican commission member Peter Wallison will offer his dissent, while three other Republicans will offer an account that focuses on global factors. Reuters', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buzz Tracker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d82715d-65cf-58cd-8063-899c5b9c5d45', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d82715d-65cf-58cd-8063-899c5b9c5d45'}, {'abstract': 'The day in sports included handball in Sweden and ice dancing in Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/24/sports/SPTSREPLAY0124.html', 'snippet': 'The day in sports included handball in Sweden and ice dancing in Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day in sports included handball in Sweden and ice dancing in Switzerland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/sports/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU/SPTSREPLAY0124-slide-HRZU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Jan. 24', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/eed952ab-53ec-5ddc-9ba5-5c1528df908e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/eed952ab-53ec-5ddc-9ba5-5c1528df908e'}, {'abstract': 'American boutique banks like Compass Advisers are gaining traction in China, using well-placed associates, serendipitous connections and specialized knowledge to strengthen their ties.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/boutique-investment-banks-gain-traction-in-china/', 'snippet': 'American boutique banks like Compass Advisers are gaining traction in China, using well-placed associates, serendipitous connections and specialized knowledge to strengthen their ties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last September in a restaurant on Israel’s Mediterranean coast, Ze’ev Goldberg, a partner at the boutique investment bank Compass Advisers, listened to Ren Jianxin, the chairman of China National Chemical, explain how he turned a paltry 10,000 renminbi loan (about $1,500) into a $24 billion company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Competing With Big Banks, Smaller Can Be Better', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Stephen M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organ