'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c99d2bfd-80e4-5929-bdca-215c76a19668', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c99d2bfd-80e4-5929-bdca-215c76a19668'}, {'abstract': 'Online eyewitnesses give accounts of the Moscow attack; Mahmoud Abbas fires back at documents revealing Palestinian concessions; the office of the artist Al Hirschfeld moves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/1248069584821/timescast-january-24-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Online eyewitnesses give accounts of the Moscow attack; Mahmoud Abbas fires back at documents revealing Palestinian concessions; the office of the artist Al Hirschfeld moves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Online eyewitnesses give accounts of the Moscow attack; Mahmoud Abbas fires back at documents revealing Palestinian concessions; the office of the artist Al Hirschfeld moves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/24/world/11085_1_tc-012411_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/24/world/11085_1_tc-012411_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | January 24, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirschfeld, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/39b9b06a-efbe-52a3-8387-ac4b1dc1e821', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/39b9b06a-efbe-52a3-8387-ac4b1dc1e821'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Olsen, star of two movies at Sundance, is in such demand that she didn’t even get to watch all of “Martha Marcy May Marlene” at the premiere.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/that-other-olsen-girl/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Olsen, star of two movies at Sundance, is in such demand that she didn’t even get to watch all of “Martha Marcy May Marlene” at the premiere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— Elizabeth Olsen has an ear infection. The perils of being a Sundance It girl – or at least trumpeted as one by agents, managers and publicists – is such that Ms. Olsen, the 21-year-old star of two films here, “Silent House,” and “Martha Marcy May Marlene,” has suffered through a whirlwind schedule of promotion; after a trip to nearby Salt Lake City for a screening, she wound up feeling sick enough to visit a doctor, who diagnosed her. But that didn’t stop the whirlwind. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That (Other) Olsen Girl', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Ashley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Mary-Kate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef1e3ce9-9ee3-5ec3-9261-0b741cf5bd1c', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef1e3ce9-9ee3-5ec3-9261-0b741cf5bd1c'}, {'abstract': 'Moscow is hoping to attract foreign investors to buy billions in bonds and stakes of state-owned companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/business/global/25rusecon.html', 'snippet': 'Moscow is hoping to attract foreign investors to buy billions in bonds and stakes of state-owned companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW \x97 A few years ago, Vladimir V. Putin, as president, compared the energy riches of Siberia to a piece of candy held tightly by Russia, as if in a “sweaty fist.” However much investors might want it, it was off limits. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Rusecon1/Rusecon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Rusecon1/Rusecon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Rusecon1/Rusecon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Rusecon1/Rusecon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Rusecon1/Rusecon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Seeks Foreign Investment to Fill Budget Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia, Facing Big Budget Gap, Warms to Foreign Investors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privatization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:48:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1b0e98d-f196-53e0-8fbb-3ff68880218b', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1b0e98d-f196-53e0-8fbb-3ff68880218b'}, {'abstract': 'More than any other wine, rosés start to be discarded near the end of summer, but they can offer year-round pleasure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/dining/26pour.html', 'snippet': 'More than any other wine, rosés start to be discarded near the end of summer, but they can offer year-round pleasure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you look really hard, you will find them condemned to a dusty back shelf underneath a few cobwebs, or perhaps looking forlorn on the half-price rack, their once brilliant colors dulled by neglect. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/POUR/POUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/POUR/POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/POUR/POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rosé Can Bloom in Winter, Too', 'kicker': 'The Pour', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rosé Can Bloom in Winter, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/460b9c15-9f10-5881-9ba0-8db17ceeb959', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/460b9c15-9f10-5881-9ba0-8db17ceeb959'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama has decided to nominate Donald Verrilli, a White House lawyer, to become solicitor general, succeeding Elena Kagan.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/obama-selects-donald-verrilli-as-solicitor-general/', 'snippet': 'President Obama has decided to nominate Donald Verrilli, a White House lawyer, to become solicitor general, succeeding Elena Kagan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is preparing to nominate a White House deputy counsel and prominent litigator, Donald B. Verrilli Jr., to be solicitor general of the United States, the White House confirmed on Monday. The position has been vacant since Elena Kagan became a Supreme Court associate justice last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Selects Donald Verrilli as Solicitor General', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T20:55:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3feed09-4e21-52d6-ace2-b7de0bf55a16', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3feed09-4e21-52d6-ace2-b7de0bf55a16'}, {'abstract': 'James Levine led the Met Orchestra in two demanding works at Carnegie Hall on Sunday afternoon: Mozart’s “Posthorn” Serenade and Mahler’s “Lied von der Erde.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/arts/music/25met.html', 'snippet': 'James Levine led the Met Orchestra in two demanding works at Carnegie Hall on Sunday afternoon: Mozart’s “Posthorn” Serenade and Mahler’s “Lied von der Erde.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Levine devoted the Met Orchestra’s concert at Carnegie Hall on Sunday afternoon to two works, but they were big, demanding ones. Mozart’s “Posthorn” Serenade (K. 320), despite a title that suggests a light entertainment, is as grand as most of his symphonies and, at 45 minutes, twice as long as most of them. And “Das Lied von der Erde,” Mahler’s monumental setting of ancient Chinese poetry, is a symphony disguised as a song cycle. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/arts/MET1/MET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/arts/MET1/MET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_na