find out what American women are doing about birth control these days, the National Center for Health Statistics conducted some painstaking research: 80-minute interviews with each of 7,356 women ages 15 to 44. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Birth Control Update, in Thousands of Interviews', 'kicker': 'Vital Statistics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Birth Control Update, in Thousands of Interviews', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sterilization (Biological)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f407d86f-1d5b-5029-a32b-917fd2756804', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f407d86f-1d5b-5029-a32b-917fd2756804'}, {'abstract': 'Nonprofits based in New York are turning to other states for help in issuing tax-exempt bonds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/business/25charity.html', 'snippet': 'Nonprofits based in New York are turning to other states for help in issuing tax-exempt bonds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nonprofits based in New York are turning to other states for help in issuing tax-exempt bonds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nonprofits Turn to Out-of-State Options for Bonds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Nonprofits Turn to Out-of-State Options for Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0c9be79-f51a-5741-b92b-1ecab334e243', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0c9be79-f51a-5741-b92b-1ecab334e243'}, {'abstract': 'Rejecting Keynes, and much more.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/the-war-on-demand/', 'snippet': 'Rejecting Keynes, and much more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something really strange has happened to the debate over economic policy in the face of the Great Recession and its aftermath — or maybe the real point is that events have revealed the true nature of the debate, stripping away some of the illusions. It’s a bigger story than any one point of dispute — say, over the size of the multiplier, or the effects of quantitative easing — might suggest. Basically, in the face of what I would have said is obviously a massive shortfall of aggregate demand, we’re seeing on all-out attack on the very notion that the demand side matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The War on Demand', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/992553bd-9d48-58b9-8316-4a1f05d107d5', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/992553bd-9d48-58b9-8316-4a1f05d107d5'}, {'abstract': 'DJ Skee, a k a Scott Keeney, a radio show host, goes to greater lengths than most fliers to plan ahead for stormy weather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/business/25flier.html', 'snippet': 'DJ Skee, a k a Scott Keeney, a radio show host, goes to greater lengths than most fliers to plan ahead for stormy weather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M usually mellow, but I’ve become a bit of a travel diva. I use a ton of different Web sites and frequent-flier upgrades and even choose to fly out of specific airports if I can \x97 all to make the travel experience less of a hassle. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/25flier/25flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/25flier/25flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/business/25flier/25flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A D.J. Has a Play List in Case of Turbulence', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A D.J. Has a Play List In Case of Turbulence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f38717-31ed-5a1d-9778-6096d835f29e', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f38717-31ed-5a1d-9778-6096d835f29e'}, {'abstract': 'A judge delayed a pretrial hearing for a political consultant accused of stealing $1.1 million from Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/hearing-delayed-for-consultant-charged-with-defrauding-bloomberg/', 'snippet': 'A judge delayed a pretrial hearing for a political consultant accused of stealing $1.1 million from Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state judge on Monday postponed by two weeks oral arguments in the case against John F. Haggerty Jr., a Republican political consultant who is accused of stealing $1.1 million from Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg during the 2009 campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hearing Delayed for Consultant Charged With Defrauding Bloomberg', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aba9ef98-7da2-5851-a3ac-4af19e32bbb0', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aba9ef98-7da2-5851-a3ac-4af19e32bbb0'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Lockyer, California’s state treasurer, calls the notion “a cynical proposal, intended to incite a panic in response to a phony crisis.”', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/state-bankruptcies-ludicrous-he-says/', 'snippet': 'Bill Lockyer, California’s state treasurer, calls the notion “a cynical proposal, intended to incite a panic in response to a phony crisis.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'California’s state treasurer, Bill Lockyer, denounced on Monday continuing efforts to establish a new framework for states to restructure their debts, saying no state wanted or needed to declare bankruptcy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Bankruptcies? ‘Ludicrous,’ He Says', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lockyer, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f914032-b16c-5fce-b505-7bfc669e77ef', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f914032-b16c-5fce-b505-7bfc669e77ef'}, {'abstract': 'An update on the mom who doesn’t sleep because her toddler doesn’t sleep.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/finally-getting-some-sleep/', 'snippet': 'An update on the mom who doesn’t sleep because her toddler doesn’t sleep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Vander Schaaff has been sleeping. And reading. And worrying a bit about her husband, who has been taking the night shifts for a week and now “looks like a bedraggled lumberjack — unshaven and tired,” she reports in an e-mail, adding, “I’ll give him a break soon.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '(Finally) Getting Some Sleep', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7675f230-0e12-56d9-9d6a-f6b011c78c31', 'word_count': 1382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7675f230-0e12-56d9-9d6a-f6b011c78c31'}, {'abstract': 'Many aging doctors are under increasing financial pressures that make them reluctant to retire; some experts warn that there are too few safeguards to protect patients against those who should no longer be practicing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/health/25doctors.html', 'snippet': 'Many aging doctors are under increasing financial pressures that make them reluctant to retire; some experts warn that there are too few safeguards to protect patients against those who should no longer be practicing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About eight years ago, at the age of 78, a vascular surgeon in California operated on a woman who then developed a pulmonary embolism. The surgeon did not respond to urgent calls from the nurses, and the woman died.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Doctors Age, Worries About Their Ability Grow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Doctors Age, Worries About Their Ability Grow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-24T21:19:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Tarkan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tarkan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88475776-4242-5f4c-9862-f4a2bfa1d62d', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88475776-4242-5f4c-9862-f4a2bfa1d62d'}, {'abstract': 'The previous Lebanese government didn’t do anything to rein in the Shiite movement, analysts say, so for many Israelis the change is simply “a semantic change.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/world/middleeast/25israel.html', 'snippet': 'The previous Lebanese government didn’t do anything to rein in the Shiite movement, analysts say, so for many Israelis the change is simply “a semantic change.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM \x97 For Israel, the prospect of a government in Lebanon backed by Hezbollah, one of Israel’s worst enemies, seemed to be the realization of a nightmare. Yet some analysts here said it was not necessarily an immediate cause for alarm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hezbollah-Run Lebanon, but 