idarity with President Felipe Calderón and to rebut public doubts about persistent violence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Voices U.S. Support of Mexico in Trip', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Voices U.S. Support of Mexico in Trip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calderon, Felipe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T01:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5674c748-0460-58ac-8a70-3da5ba7548a0', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5674c748-0460-58ac-8a70-3da5ba7548a0'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court justice Clarence Thomas said that a misunderstanding led to an omission over six years on federal disclosure forms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/us/politics/25thomas.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court justice Clarence Thomas said that a misunderstanding led to an omission over six years on federal disclosure forms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Under pressure from liberal critics, Justice Clarence Thomas of the Supreme Court acknowledged in filings released on Monday that he erred by not disclosing his wife’s past employment as required by federal law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/us/THOMAS/THOMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/us/THOMAS/THOMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/us/THOMAS/THOMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Cites Failure to Disclose Wife’s Job', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thomas Cites Failure To Disclose Wife’s Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Virginia Lamp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Clarence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hillsdale College', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heritage Foundation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T