f days, doesn’t come cheap.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/a-hefty-price-for-entry-to-davos/', 'snippet': 'For corporate executives, the cost of being a Davos Man, or a Davos Woman, even for just a couple of days, doesn’t come cheap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Harrer/Bloomberg NewsThe town of Davos, Switzerland, an expensive place to go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hefty Price for Entry to Davos', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions and Conferences', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bono', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Case, Stephen M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papandreou, George A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwab, Klaus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T02:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d585648-6265-5908-8527-c7ef6ee79e2d', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d585648-6265-5908-8527-c7ef6ee79e2d'}, {'abstract': 'The non-profit program Year Up is getting low-income young people into jobs by training them in the culture of work.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/an-education-in-the-ways-of-the-workplace/', 'snippet': 'The non-profit program Year Up is getting low-income young people into jobs by training them in the culture of work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most frustrating economic news of 2010 wasn’t that the recession had worsened — it was that things had improved markedly for corporations, but not for the labor force. Even Alan Greenspan expressed concern that the U.S. is evincing “fundamentally two separate types of economy” — one in which big companies and high earners thrive, the other in which millions struggle to find jobs and make ends meet. One group that has been particularly hard hit by the recession is youth. Among workers aged 16 to 24, the unemployment rate is almost 20 percent. For young Latinos, it’s over 24 percent, and for young African Americans, it’s over 32 percent. Some 4.4 million youths are currently unemployed.This is of serious concern to a country with a rapidly aging population. And while today’s best jobs require post-secondary schooling, 30 percent of U.S. public school students fail to graduate from high school (pdf), and more than half of those who enroll in higher education fail to earn a degree or credential within eight years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Training Youths in the Ways of the Workplace', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T02:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5edd156b-bd2d-50af-87a3-92912881cb44', 'word_count': 1615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5edd156b-bd2d-50af-87a3-92912881cb44'}, {'abstract': 'The food industry said it created a plan at the urging of Michelle Obama, but she gave it only tepid approval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/business/25label.html', 'snippet': 'The food industry said it created a plan at the urging of Michelle Obama, but she gave it only tepid approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting in the next few months, the front of many food packages will prominently display important nutrition information, including calorie, fat and sugar content. The industrywide program was announced Monday by food makers and grocers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Label1/Label1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Label1/Label1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Label1/Label1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Label1/Label1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Label1/Label1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Makers Devise Own Label Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Makers Devise Own Label Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T02:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ead9475b-75fa-508e-8f62-ff78fccc4b9c', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ead9475b-75fa-508e-8f62-ff78fccc4b9c'}, {'abstract': 'The Bush White House, particularly before the 2006 midterm elections, routinely violated a federal law that prohibits use of federal tax dollars to pay for political activities, a report issued Monday by an independent federal agency concludes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/us/politics/25ethics.html', 'snippet': 'The Bush White House, particularly before the 2006 midterm elections, routinely violated a federal law that prohibits use of federal tax dollars to pay for political activities, a report issued Monday by an independent federal agency concludes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The Bush White House, particularly before the 2006 midterm elections, routinely violated a federal law that prohibits use of federal tax dollars to pay for political activities by creating a “political boiler room” that coordinated Republican campaign activities nationwide, a report issued Monday by an independent federal agency concludes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/us/ETHICS/ETHICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 499, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bush White House Broke Elections Law, Report Says'