ever experienced a Burns supper in Scotland, where the traditional entree, haggis \x97 a sheep sausage encased in a sheep’s stomach \x97 is a delicacy. In America, when the haggis makes its entrance, guests reach for the whiskey, which is also traditional at Burns suppers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night of Food and Song', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Night of Food and Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T02:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eead716-3489-518f-ae70-1651e4848902', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eead716-3489-518f-ae70-1651e4848902'}, {'abstract': 'Rex Ryan will remain the Jets’ coach as long as he keeps leading them to the playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/sports/football/25vecsey.html', 'snippet': 'Rex Ryan will remain the Jets’ coach as long as he keeps leading them to the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/25/sports/VECSEY/VECSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 210}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/