he exploration and production business with refining and other activities. This model worked for decades but today accords a conglomerate discount to the likes of Exxon Mobil, Shell and BP. Splitting up, as the smaller Marathon is doing, could add tens of billions of dollars to shareholders’ portfolios.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Split Up Oil Companies to Unlock Their Value', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oil Giants Need\nA Reorganization', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPRAISALS AND VALUATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T02:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Swann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/98425eb4-0815-5eda-a1f7-e61ebd802270', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98425eb4-0815-5eda-a1f7-e61ebd802270'}, {'abstract': 'There will be no Broadway parade for the Jets, along with no need for trash-talking over whether the team belongs to New York or, as reality would suggest, New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/nyregion/25nyc.html', 'snippet': 'There will be no Broadway parade for the Jets, along with no need for trash-talking over whether the team belongs to New York or, as reality would suggest, New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s look on the bright side. Yes, it is a shame that the Jets will not be headed to the Super Bowl. That is the price they pay for failing to internalize the concept of football as a game to be played in all four quarters, not just the final two. But at least we will be spared more weeks of trans-Hudson nyah-nyahing over whether the team belongs to New York or, as reality would suggest, New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Defeat, No Super Bowl for New Jersey', 'kicker': 'NYC', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Defeat, No Super Bowl For New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T03:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79026bb3-5b39-5766-8d9f-2410e99e4692', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79026bb3-5b39-5766-8d9f-2410e99e4692'}, {'abstract': 'Right from the start, Randall J. Hartman commands us to attack his puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/24/doberman/', 'snippet': 'Right from the start, Randall J. Hartman commands us to attack his puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — Wow. I can’t say too much about this theme without giving it away, but let’s just say that for what it is, it sure is fresh. And it couldn’t have been an easy task to be that fresh four times in an international setting. Very nicely done, Mr. Hartman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Command to a Doberman', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T03:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed5fa4bb-8927-5d1e-b7fb-b69e61683d23', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed5fa4bb-8927-5d1e-b7fb-b69e61683d23'}, {'abstract': 'Sandra Perez was paying for her own degree while trying to help her sons, but she also needed to get out of her brother’s apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/nyregion/25neediest.html', 'snippet': 'Sandra Perez was paying for her own degree while trying to help her sons, but she also needed to get out of her brother’s apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chaos reigns at Sandra Perez’s apartment on Staten Island. Visitors are expected, including one loaded with cameras, and the family is rushing to get ready.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/nyregion/neediest/neediest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo