potential misconduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The panel appointed by Congress to investigate the causes of the financial crisis referred a handful of cases involving potential wrongdoing to the Justice Department, a person close to the investigation said Monday evening.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel Investigating Financial Crisis Is Said to Refer Cases to Justice Dept.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Investigating Financial Crisis Is Said to Refer Cases to Justice Dept.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T04:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfee43c3-8a6a-507b-a9e9-c4177791e5e7', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfee43c3-8a6a-507b-a9e9-c4177791e5e7'}, {'abstract': 'The concert promoter George Wein is to announce on Tuesday that this year he will stage the Newport Jazz Festival, set for Aug. 5-7, and the Newport Folk Festival, July 29-31, as nonprofit events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/arts/music/25arts-ANONPROFITNE_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The concert promoter George Wein is to announce on Tuesday that this year he will stage the Newport Jazz Festival, set for Aug. 5-7, and the Newport Folk Festival, July 29-31, as nonprofit events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The concert promoter George Wein is to announce on Tuesday that this year he will stage the Newport Jazz Festival, set for Aug. 5-7, and the Newport Folk Festival, July 29-31, as nonprofit events, under the direction of the new Newport Festivals Foundation. “The point of going nonprofit is to perpetuate what we’ve created there since 1954,” Mr. Wein said. The festivals he helped create in Newport, R.I. \x97 both started more than 60 years ago \x97 suffered a major setback after Mr. Wein sold his concert-production business to Festival Network, a company that had financial troubles in 2009. Subsequently, Mr. Wein took back the festivals. After the last two editions of the Newport Jazz Festivals, which he deemed artistic and popular successes, he described his main focus as perpetuating the legacy of the festivals. He has built a new board to carry out that task, and he will continue to seek corporate sponsors, he said. The festivals will announce their full schedules in the coming weeks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nonprofit Newport', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nonprofit Newport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T05:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca83d1f-c61e-5f2c-91ac-1da4a6a120d4', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca83d1f-c61e-5f2c-91ac-1da4a6a120d4'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 39 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/word-of-the-day-tranquility/', 'snip