te of the Union, or Not?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T11:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1a0d645-6e80-54e4-b295-df2d9939386f', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1a0d645-6e80-54e4-b295-df2d9939386f'}, {'abstract': 'The Fantastic Four will lose one of its team members to the Grim Reaper in an issue that is to be released Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/fantastic-four-no-more/', 'snippet': 'The Fantastic Four will lose one of its team members to the Grim Reaper in an issue that is to be released Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first family of Marvel Comics – the Fantastic Four – will lose one of its team members to the Grim Reaper in an issue that is to be released Tuesday. Fantastic Four no. 587, written by Jonathan Hickman and illustrated by Steve Epting, is part five of a storyline whose title, “Three,” tipped off an impending change in status for the famous quartet. Fans of the series have been endlessly speculating which of the heroes would go. Stop reading now if you do not want to know. Ready? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantastic Four No More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T12:00:02+0000', 'document_