mage', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/movies/awardsseason/25oscar-nominations-slide-9DNW/25oscar-nominations-slide-9DNW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/movies/awardsseason/25oscar-nominations-slide-9DNW/25oscar-nominations-slide-9DNW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 83rd Annual Oscar Nominations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6bcea06d-e819-5780-8b41-6a43139e1cab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6bcea06d-e819-5780-8b41-6a43139e1cab'}, {'abstract': 'In the aftermath of Monday’s deadly suicide bombing at a Moscow airport, a Russian television channel suggested that the makers of an American video game might be partly to blame.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/russian-media-points-to-moscow-airport-attack-in-u-s-video-game/', 'snippet': 'In the aftermath of Monday’s deadly suicide bombing at a Moscow airport, a Russian television channel suggested that the makers of an American video game might be partly to blame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 10:23 a.m. As Russia’s president, Dmitri Medvedev, criticized airport officials for allowing a suicide bomber to enter the Domdedovo airport in Moscow on Monday, a Russian television report suggested that an American video game might also be to blame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Media Points to Moscow Airport Attack in U.S. Video Game', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f7ee39e-94fb-55d1-b944-58826068dae5', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f7ee39e-94fb-55d1-b944-58826068dae5'}, {'abstract': 'The predicted double-dip in housing has begun, and analysts say declines are likely to continue, though not as intensely as in 2007 and 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/business/economy/26econ.html', 'snippet': 'The predicted double-dip in housing has begun, and analysts say declines are likely to continue, though not as intensely as in 2007 and 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A new slide in housing prices has begun in earnest, with averages in major cities across the country falling to their lowest point in many years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26ECON/26ECON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26ECON/26ECON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26ECON/26ECON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26ECON/26ECON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26ECON/26ECON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Home Prices Slump Again, Hitting New Lows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Housing Prices, Already Down, Fall Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Case-Shiller Home Price Index", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/763d78be-9e0a-544f-a643-255a304b7a0e', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/763d78be-9e0a-544f-a643-255a304b7a0e'}, {'abstract': 'The nominees for best foreign-language film come from all over the world this year, with only two finalists from usually dominant Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-show-of-diversity/', 'snippet': 'The nominees for best foreign-language film come from all over the world this year, with only two finalists from usually dominant Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interesting show of geographic diversity, the nominees for best foreign-language film come from all over the world this year. Only two of the five finalists, Denmark’s “In a Better World” and Greece’s “Dogtooth,” hail from Europe, which traditionally dominates the category.Two of the other finalists are from North America (though obviously not the United States): Mexico’s “Biutiful” and Canada’s “Incendies.” And the remaining slot goes to an African film, Algeria’s “Outside the Law.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Show of Diversity', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardem, Javier', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bier, Susanne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:40:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d872196-4c7a-5f1c-8817-56b566145157', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d872196-4c7a-5f1c-8817-56b566145157'}, {'abstract': 'Four Dow components reported results. In addition, a monthly housing index showed a decline in prices in November.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/business/26markets.html', 'snippet': 'Four Dow components reported results. In addition, a monthly housing index showed a decline in prices in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shares on Wall Street ended the day little changed on Tuesday as investors held back in anticipation of economic and policy developments. Earnings results were also mixed, adding to the lack of direction.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', '