'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5942231b-727f-525e-8fe1-a7788aec637e', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5942231b-727f-525e-8fe1-a7788aec637e'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Cholodenko, very upfront about her Oscar desires, didn’t pretend she wasn’t watching the announcements live.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-bittersweet-moment-for-the-mother-of-the-kids/', 'snippet': 'Lisa Cholodenko, very upfront about her Oscar desires, didn’t pretend she wasn’t watching the announcements live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — “Did I have a gut feeling? Or a stomach ache?” said Lisa Cholodenko, who predicted early in the awards season that her film “The Kids Are All Right” would earn some statuary. Whatever her bodily reaction, she was right; the film received a spot on the best picture list, as well as nods for best actress, best supporting actor and best original screenplay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bittersweet Moment for the Mother of ‘The Kids’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kids Are All Right, The (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bening, Annette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cholodenko, Lisa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c5b703-87a7-53d4-a026-59be7b2dc518', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c5b703-87a7-53d4-a026-59be7b2dc518'}, {'abstract': 'What Happens When will last only until its building is demolished.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/off-the-menu-john-frasers-popup/', 'snippet': 'What Happens When will last only until its building is demolished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What Happens When', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu: John Fraser’s Popup', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T14:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/98c2b24e-9f1d-5610-92e3-2f7082971668', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98c2b24e-9f1d-5610-92e3-2f7082971668'}, {'abstract': 'In a bizarre twist of rock and roll history,  one of New York’s favorite underground bands performed in the basement of what used to be the legendary venue CBGB’s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/notes-from-the-underground-light-asylum/', 'snippet': 'In a bizarre twist of rock and roll history,  one of New York’s favorite underground bands performed in the basement of what used to be the legendary venue CBGB’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a bizarre twist of rock and roll history, one of New York’s favorite underground (read: unsigned) bands, Light Asylum, performed in the basement of what used to be the legendary venue CBGB’s. The two man act, made up of the keyboardist Bruno Coviello, and the vocalist Shannon Funchess, knocked out an hour-long set laden with heavy rhythms, new wave-ish synth and Funchess’s impossibly deep bravado. Complete with a fog machine and colored lights, the show was a voyage into the depths of Funchess’s tortured visions — and the future of New York dance music. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes from the Underground | Light Asylum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T15:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7231466-649f-59a6-9c2b-a567ffd0ad38', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7231466-649f-59a6-9c2b-a567ffd0ad38'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota, releases a new video promoting his book — and his love of America.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/in-new-video-images-of-pawlenty-the-patriot/', 'snippet': 'Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota, releases a new video promoting his book — and his love of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest Web video for Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota and a likely Republican candidate for president in 2012, there is not a single awe-inspiring, patriotic image that is left out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Video, Images of Pawlenty the Patriot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': '