t.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/state-of-the-union-watch-the-strategy-not-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'For all the pomp and promises and the media attention it attracts, the big annual speech rarely moves any president’s approval rating very much either way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The State of the Union this year once again coincides with what I call “Hype Week,” the period between the N.F.L. conference championships and the Super Bowl (now 13 days long) in which absolutely nothing of interest seems to take place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State of the Union: Watch the Strategy, Not the Polls', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T15:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cd61557-ce66-576d-b660-5061130d4bf6', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cd61557-ce66-576d-b660-5061130d4bf6'}, {'abstract': 'As a pregame warm-up, DealBook takes a closer look at The Economist, The Atlantic and the profound Twitter post of Daniel Gross to see what could be learned about Davos.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/getting-ready-for-davos/', 'snippet': 'As a pregame warm-up, DealBook takes a closer look at The Economist, The Atlantic and the profound Twitter post of Daniel Gross to see what could be learned about Davos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johannes Eisele/Agence France-Presse — Getty ImagesPreparing for the World Economic Forum annual meeting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Descending on Davos', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T15:21:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcef1f48-26c9-51c6-a2ca-4f918505778e', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcef1f48-26c9-51c6-a2ca-4f918505778e'}, {'abstract': 'Only one or two out of 100 displayed a mastery of science on nationwide tests, the Department of Education said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/education/26test.html', 'snippet': 'Only one or two out of 100 displayed a mastery of science on nationwide tests, the Department of Education said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the most recent nationwide science test, about a third of fourth graders and a fifth of high school seniors scored at or above the proficiency level, according to results released Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Few Students Show Proficiency in Science, Tests Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Few Students Show Proficiency In Science, Federal Tests Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Testing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T15:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'fir