e Coen brothers are waking up a little more canonized this morning. “True Grit,” snubbed by many other awards groups, had a great showing with the Academy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Those unlikely box office champs and self-declared outsiders the Coen brothers are waking up a little more canonized this morning. “True Grit,” snubbed by many other awards groups, had a great showing with the Academy, earning 10 nominations over all – second only to “The King’s Speech” – and placing in key categories like best adapted screenplay and best director. Does that advance its cause for best picture? The film didn’t earn a best editing nomination, traditionally a bellwether for the eventual top winner, but that didn’t stop experts like Roger Ebert from banking on it for a surprise win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘True Grit’ Triumph and Other Surprises', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T15:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a464cfa7-4e95-56f5-9340-59c165cada24', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a464cfa7-4e95-56f5-9340-59c165cada24'}, {'abstract': 'He certainly does not have the pedigree or press notices of goal scorers like Cristiano Ronaldo, Lionel Messi or Carlos Tévez, and if you have not heard the name Marc Janko, scouts for some of the top European club teams certainly have.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011