mentioned as possibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/why-dont-americans-live-longer/', 'snippet': 'A new National Academy of Sciences report names smoking and lack of universal health insurance. Obesity and inequality are also mentioned as possibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Academy of Sciences has just released a fascinating report on life expectancy in rich countries around the world. The researchers who wrote the report — public-health experts, demographers, economists and others, from around the world — have tried to figure out why Americans don’t live as long as people in many other countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Don’t Americans Live Longer?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/05db53e5-6e3c-56a4-8c0b-5f8cab8563b6', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05db53e5-6e3c-56a4-8c0b-5f8cab8563b6'}, {'abstract': 'Harvard may be the alma mater of Conan O’Brien, but its Hasty Pudding Club is giving its Man of the Year honors to Jay Leno.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/award-for-jay-leno-opens-old-wounds-mostly-ours/', 'snippet': 'Harvard may be the alma mater of Conan O’Brien, but its Hasty Pudding Club is giving its Man of the Year honors to Jay Leno.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:42 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Award for Jay Leno Opens Old Wounds (Mostly Ours)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Julianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Conan", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivy League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af1b974-ffb2-5efb-82a5-440002fe7af8', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af1b974-ffb2-5efb-82a5-440002fe7af8'}, {'abstract': 'The long-in-the-making “Fighter” gets seven Oscar nominations, but the producers are disappointed that Mark Wahlberg didn’t make the cut.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-roar-of-the-underdog/', 'snippet': 'The long-in-the-making “Fighter” gets seven Oscar nominations, but the producers are disappointed that Mark Wahlberg didn’t make the cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — “The Fighter” has been an underdog from the get-go, initially rejected by Paramount and then reluctantly taken back in. So David Hoberman and Todd Lieberman, two of the film’s producers, were having a hard time processing the love. First they thought they had five nominations. No, wait — six. Seven?!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Roar of the Underdog', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoberman, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf0e240e-8453-5ec7-b9b8-375f2c1bfe67', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf0e240e-8453-5ec7-b9b8-375f2c1bfe67'}, {'abstract': 'In his State of the State address on Monday, Gov. Jerry Brown is expected to press plans to help close California’s massive budget gap.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/brown-to-deliver-state-of-the-state-monday/', 'snippet': 'In his State of the State address on Monday, Gov. Jerry Brown is expected to press plans to help close California’s massive budget gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO – Since his election in November, Gov. Jerry Brown has made few public appearances: among them, the release of his budget, his inauguration and some chance encounters with reporters as he moved through the halls of the state Capitol. Mr. Brown’s aides say he has been consumed with coming up with a plan to close the state’s $25 billion budget shortfall; whatever the case, the contrast with his predecessor, Arnold Schwarzenegger, has been notable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown to Deliver State of the State on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/600ff16a-e638-5b2d-aff8-4ff5504c6cd4', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/600ff16a-e638-5b2d-aff8-4ff5504c6cd4'}, {'abstract': 'An angry mob that attempted to storm the office of Al Jazeera in the West Bank city of Ramallah on Monday included Palestinian police officers in civilian clothes, a local journalist said.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/palestinian-police-are-said-to-have-participated-in-protest-at-al-jazeera/', 'snippet': 'An angry mob that attempted to storm the office of Al Jazeera in the West Bank city of Ramallah on Monday included Palestinian police officers in civilian clothes, a local journalist said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An angry mob that attempted to storm the office of Al Jazeera in the West Bank city of Ramallah on Monday, following the publication of leaked Palestinian documents by the Arab news network, included Palestinian police officers in civilian clothes, according to a local journalist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Police Are Said to Have Participated in Protest Against Al Jazeera', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d73270b-91dc-50ab-972f-1bb384a942d1', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d73270b-91dc-50ab-972f-1bb384a942d1'}, {'abstract': 'Why isn’t it stronger?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-demand-side-temptation/', 'snippet': 'Why isn’t it stronger?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nick Rowe makes a good point: most of the time, in market economies, sellers feel constrained while buyers don’t. I’m somewhat surprised that he doesn’t mention why: it’s because perfect competition is actually rare, because oligopoly or monopolistic competition — in which prices exceed marginal cost — is actually the norm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Demand-Side Temptation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/237044ec-5126-5fa4-9980-566c7dfba11f', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/237044ec-5126-5fa4-9980-566c7dfba11f'}, {'abstract': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/what-were-reading-104/', 'snippet': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/926041ed-b17e-5bfe-802d-50690ff8c396', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/926041ed-b17e-5bfe-802d-50690ff8c396'}, {'abstract': 'An annual report on human rights has faulted Ban Ki-moon, the secretary general, among other major leaders, for acting timidly in the face of rights abuses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/26nations.html', 'snippet': 'An annual report on human rights has faulted Ban Ki-moon, the secretary general, among other major leaders, for acting timidly in the face of rights abuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS \x97 Republican members of Congress on Tuesday used their newly won control of the House to advocate that the United States hinge its hefty support for the United Nations budget to more tangible efforts by the organization to root out corruption and advance American foreign policy goals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Renews Call to Tie U.N. Funding to U.S. Goals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Renews Call to Tie U.N. Funding to U.S. Goals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Kenneth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'},