ippet': 'Scientists track fisher behavior in urban and wild settings to better understand the success of weasel populations in the northeast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roland Kays, curator of mammals at the New York State Museum and author of Mammals of North America, writes from Albany,\xa0 where he is comparing the behavior of fishers in urban and wild settings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albany’s Urban Weasels', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANY (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roland Kays', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kays', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c44a597-9f27-5f7d-9b81-ecbaa5d9d208', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c44a597-9f27-5f7d-9b81-ecbaa5d9d208'}, {'abstract': 'Jacki Weaver and Melissa Leo both received nominations in the best supporting actress category, for “Animal Kingdom” and “The Fighter,” respectively.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-steely-matriarchs-speak/', 'snippet': 'Jacki Weaver and Melissa Leo both received nominations in the best supporting actress category, for “Animal Kingdom” and “The Fighter,” respectively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacki Weaver has ridden what the Carpetbagger called her “little wave of critical love” right into a best supporting actress nomination for her work as a bleached-blond bad mama in “Animal Kingdom.” But she slept right through the news this morning, learning of her nod when her ex-husband, in Australia, sent her a text message.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Steely Matriarchs Speak', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leo, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc4095ba-9eab-5847-b125-f917a584afe2', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc4095ba-9eab-5847-b125-f917a584afe2'}, {'abstract': 'A good job by the Academy in a good year for movies.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/notes-on-the-oscar-nominations/', 'snippet': 'A good job by the Academy in a good year for movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They’re out! And I’d like to thank the Academy for doing a bang-up job this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes on the Oscar Nominations', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:34:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7a4d923-fa5b-5a68-9649-fd63461db3c1', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7a4d923-fa5b-5a68-9649-fd63461db3c1'}, {'abstract': 'A teenage boy blew up himself near a Shiite procession in Lahore, and a second bomber struck a similar procession in Karachi, killing a total of at least a dozen people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/asia/26pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'A teenage boy blew up himself near a Shiite procession in Lahore, and a second bomber struck a similar procession in Karachi, killing a total of at least a dozen people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAHORE, Pakistan \x97 A teenage boy blew himself up on Tuesday evening while trying to break through heavy security for a Shiite procession here, killing at least 10 people and wounding 79, the police said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/world/Pakistan/Pakistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombers Hit Processions of Shiites in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombers Hit Processions Of Shiites In Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/324a5dde-3df9-581c-8a30-556344cb4160', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/324a5dde-3df9-581c-8a30-556344cb4160'}, {'abstract': 'The one-day festival at the Empire Polo Club in Indio, Calif., will bring together the the high-volume bands Metallica, Slayer, Megadeth and Anthrax.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/bang-your-head-and-protect-your-ears-the-big-four-are-coming-to-california/', 'snippet': 'The one-day festival at the Empire Polo Club in Indio, Calif., will bring together the the high-volume bands Metallica, Slayer, Megadeth and Anthrax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Empire Polo Club in Indio, Calif., isn’t completely resodded and picked clean of trash immediately after this year’s Coachella festival wraps up on April 17, we’re guessing the field’s next major occupants won’t mind too much. The following Saturday, April 23, those same fairgrounds will be home to the one-day festival the Big 4, which apparently aspires to be the heaviest heavy-metal show that ever tested the mettle of metalheads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bang Your Head and Protect Your Ears: The Big Four Are Coming to California', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metallica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T16:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a569e702-c890-526d-8b93-a5764685660a', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a569e702-c890-526d-8b93-a5764685660a'}, {'abstract': 'Fans may hear Ben Roethlisberger and “redemption” in the same sentence now that the Steelers are in the Super Bowl, as if athletic success can magically paper over all manner of sin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/sports/26leading.html', 'snippet': 'Fans may hear Ben Roethlisberger and “redemption” in the same sentence now that the Steelers are in the Super Bowl, as if athletic success can magically paper over all manner of sin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know those national debt counters, the neon things on the sides of buildings that display a huge number that’s rising really quickly? We would like to see a Ben Roethlisberger redemption counter, representing every time the word “redemption” is mentioned in the same sentence as the Pittsburgh quarterback, and watch a huge number quickly rise. The bulbs may even short out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/football/26leading1/26leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/football/26leading1/26leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/football/26leading1/26leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/football/26leading1/26leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/football/26leading1/26leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Is Not Redemption', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': Non