rtini/', 'snippet': 'A drink that fuses childhood comfort food and molecular mixology can be found at Clive’s, a popular craft cocktails joint in Victoria, British Columbia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Clive’s, a popular craft cocktails joint in Victoria, British Columbia, the scene is pure hotel lounge kitsch: swirling dark carpets, white leather panels on the walls, fantasia lamps, high-backed banquettes and an unavoidable marble bar. The décor may be stuck in the 1970s, but Shawn Soole, a crack bartender from Brisbane, Australia, transcends these trappings with a dedication to innovation and craft, most notably with his Cold Night In, an original creation that fuses childhood comfort food and molecular mixology. The result is what he calls a grown-up cocktail equivalent of a “toastie” (an Australianism for a grilled sandwich) and tomato soup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Drinking | The Grilled Cheese and Tomato Soup Martini', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T17:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Michelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f93220-c704-55f5-9a77-c547336fe948', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f93220-c704-55f5-9a77-c547336fe948'}, {'abstract': 'The former House energy committee chairman asks whether Patrick Michaels submitted accurate information to Congress on funds he received from the energy industry.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/waxman-presses-climate-skeptic-on-industry-funds/', 'snippet': 'The former House energy committee chairman asks whether Patrick Michaels submitted accurate information to Congress on funds he received from the energy industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February 2009, Patrick Michaels, a former climatologist at the University of Virginia who is now a senior fellow at the Cato Institute, a conservative think tank, appeared before a House subcommittee to testify on the issue of climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waxman Presses Climate Skeptic on Industry Funds', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Upton, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waxman, Henry A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zakaria, Fareed', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cato Institute', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politico, The', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T17:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/191c29fc-9caa-556e-bd1b-ae96b6e593a7', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191c29fc-9caa-556e-bd1b-ae96b6e593a7'}, {'abstract': '“From New York City, where should I go on vacation for the first week of March? I would like to relax on this vacation.”', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/qa-march-getaway-for-three-generations/', 'snippet': '“From New York City, where should I go on vacation for the first week of March? I would like to relax on this vacation.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I will be taking the bar exam in February. After the exam, I have one week to go on a trip before I start working at a law firm. From New York City, where should I go on vacation for the first week of March? I would like to relax on this vacation. Is the Caribbean my only option? I will be traveling with my husband and 18-month-old son (my 57-year-old parents and 27-year-old sister may join us).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: March Getaway for Three Generations', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Key West (Fla)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T18:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rusha Haljuci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haljuci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/367e3850-c6cc-59b9-a273-1c10dea2c8f0', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/367e3850-c6cc-59b9-a273-1c10dea2c8f0'}, {'abstract': 'A simulated arcade machine houses an iPad for Atari game-play.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-arcade-ipad-style/', 'snippet': 'A simulated arcade machine houses an iPad for Atari game-play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Push buttons and joysticks, flashing lights and roaring sound effects, and at the heart of this sight-and-sound sensation, a box that ate quarters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Arcade, iPad-Style', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T18:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed6b196-67b6-5fa2-a7c2-7583f3ba82a6', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed6b196-67b6-5fa2-a7c2-7583f3ba82a6'}, {'abstract': 'Evan R. Goldstein, an editor at the Chronicle of Higher Education, was officially appointed editor of the intellectual and literary Web site Arts & Letters Daily.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/new-editor-named-for-arts-letters-daily/', 'snippet': 'Evan R. Goldstein, an editor at the Chronicle of Higher Education, was officially appointed editor of the intellectual and literary Web site Arts & Letters Daily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evan R. Goldstein, an editor at the Chronicle of Higher Education, was officially appointed editor of the intellectual and literary Web site Arts & Letters Daily on Tuesday. The site, now owned by the Chronicle, was started in 1998 by Denis Dutton, a distinguished philosopher who died a few weeks ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arts & Letters Daily Names New Editor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'