ive/f1789198-c41f-595a-9c6f-b73adad0923a'}, {'abstract': 'A nomination for best supporting actress helps Helena Bonham Carter, co-star of “The King’s Speech,” cope with a cold.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-queen-gets-a-feel-good-shot-for-her-cold/', 'snippet': 'A nomination for best supporting actress helps Helena Bonham Carter, co-star of “The King’s Speech,” cope with a cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Helena Bonham Carter, nominated for her role in “The King’s Speech” as the pitch-perfect would-be Queen of England to the stuttering would-be King, was in London with her two young children watching the nominations on television. “I have a cold,” she said. “An Oscar nomination makes you feel a lot better.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Queen Gets a Feel-Good Shot for Her Cold', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonham Carter, Helena', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T18:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b5a01c9-3d5f-582e-8b98-d97e968d0081', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b5a01c9-3d5f-582e-8b98-d97e968d0081'}, {'abstract': 'To earn a coveted place on Page 1, Earl Wilson had only to take his customary subway ride from Brooklyn to Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-page-1-picture-met-him-at-the-station/', 'snippet': 'To earn a coveted place on Page 1, Earl Wilson had only to take his customary subway ride from Brooklyn to Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earl Wilson has been at The New York Time