ound an apartment to rent in London — great location, great price. All he had to do was wire payment up front. Guess what? No apartment. He’s not alone in being scammed in vacation rentals. Advice on how not to join him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was stressed, rushing to make last-minute lodging arrangements for a three-stop writing trip to Europe, when it appeared on Craigslist: the perfect apartment for my first stop in London. A tiny studio in Notting Hill for just £45, or $73, a night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burned! A London Vacation Rental Scam', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Craigslist', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Crime Complaint Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6955c18d-6886-56bd-9eca-08c3636a4bcb', 'word_count': 1738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6955c18d-6886-56bd-9eca-08c3636a4bcb'}, {'abstract': 'Petra Kvitova faces Vera Zvonareva in an intriguing quarterfinal match Wednesday in Melbourne.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/quarterfinals-preview-kvitova-vs-zvonareva/', 'snippet': 'Petra Kvitova faces Vera Zvonareva in an intriguing quarterfinal match Wednesday in Melbourne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Petra Kvitova faces Vera Zvonareva in an intriguing quarterfinal match Wednesday in Melbourne. While Zvonareva, the second seed, has worked her way through her part of the draw with little fanfare, Kvitova has advanced with two big upsets over veteran players. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quarterfinals Preview: Kvitova vs. Zvonareva', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:24:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db9c1bc-54b0-581b-9935-ec31731bd337', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db9c1bc-54b0-581b-9935-ec31731bd337'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: Why plunge your feet into an icy lake when you can hitch a ride on the back of a swan?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/prospect-park-lake-820-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: Why plunge your feet into an icy lake when you can hitch a ride on the back of a swan?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the going gets cold, the birds huddle together and even, in the case of one enterprising American coot and an accommodating mute swan, atop one another. “Some coots really enjoy the swan boats in this weather,” reports Anne-Katrin Titze, the park-watcher who snapped this picture. Her lakefront census today logged 648 waterfowl, including 17 coots, 6 mute swans, 215 mallards and a hooded merganser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prospect Park Lake, 8:20 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdd697aa-97ef-51a3-b083-cf3636f5acb2', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdd697aa-97ef-51a3-b083-cf3636f5acb2'}, {'abstract': 'Standing on the soccer field while “The Star-Spangled Banner” plays never, ever gets old.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/in-china-an-encore-with-meaning/', 'snippet': 'Standing on the soccer field while “The Star-Spangled Banner” plays never, ever gets old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midfielder Yael Averbuch, a Montclair, N.J., native by way of the University of North Carolina, will be contributing to the Goal blog in the runup to the third season of Women’s Professional Soccer and as the United States women’s national team prepares to the FIFA Women’s World Cup in Germany later this year. This is here final posting from the Four Nations tournament in China, which the United States won on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, an Encore With Meaning', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael Averbuch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Averbuch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8271ce64-05ec-597f-998d-a8a13ba33990', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8271ce64-05ec-597f-998d-a8a13ba33990'}, {'abstract': 'A Congressional inquiry said bankers and regulators could have seen the 2008 crisis coming and stopped it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/business/economy/26inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'A Congressional inquiry said bankers and regulators could have seen the 2008 crisis coming and stopped it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The 2008 financial crisis was an “avoidable” disaster caused by widespread failures in government regulation, corporate mismanagement and heedless risk-taking by Wall Street, according to the conclusions of a federal inquiry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26inquiry/26inquiry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26inquiry/26inquiry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26inquiry/26inquiry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26inquiry/26inquiry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/business/26inquiry/26inquiry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Crisis Was Avoidable, Inquiry Finds', 'ki