edia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murderer Is Executed in Georgia After Losing Stay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murderer Is Executed in Georgia After Losing Stay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson and Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc5426e-5112-5957-8d65-ed2a99f29024', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc5426e-5112-5957-8d65-ed2a99f29024'}, {'abstract': 'Amy Adams has not lost any of her wonder about the movies or the Academy Awards, but upon news of her nomination for playing the tough girlfriend in “The Fighter” her first words were to praise the man who got the film made.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/big-hair-strong-will-and-oscar-nomination/', 'snippet': 'Amy Adams has not lost any of her wonder about the movies or the Academy Awards, but upon news of her nomination for playing the tough girlfriend in “The Fighter” her first words were to praise the man who got the film made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Adams’s supporting actress nomination for her role as the tough girlfriend in “The Fighter” is her third Oscar nod, but Ms. Adams said Tuesday she has not lost any of her wonder about the movies or the Academy Awards. But her first words were to praise the man who got the film made, roping in a wary Paramount, and watching major stars drop out of the project along the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Hair, Strong Will and an Oscar Nomination', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T21:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/775c43a1-d8a7-54e9-8ec4-620727d9f1c0', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/775c43a1-d8a7-54e9-8ec4-620727d9f1c0'}, {'abstract': 'Alber Elbaz and Lucas Ossendrijver of Lanvin take the win for the best in the final Paris men’s-wear shows.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/scorecard-lanvin-wins-5/', 'snippet': 'Alber Elbaz and Lucas Ossendrijver of Lanvin take the win for the best in the final Paris men’s-wear shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be the middle of couture fashion week, but as somehow always seems to happen with these things, this morning critics were still filing their reviews from the weekend’s final Paris men’s-wear shows, so today Scorecard doubles your fun with one more recap for the gents. At the end of a season of polarizing dichotomies — wide-legged trousers or jeggings? top hat or Stetson? heteronormative or not-so? lime green or tangerine?\xa0— Alber Elbaz and Lucas Ossendrijver offered a playfully performative suggestion: Why not just pile it all on in a “choose your own adventure” kind of way?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Lanvin Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c177f36a-f1b6-5089-8266-7e90c51a116a', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c177f36a-f1b6-5089-8266-7e90c51a116a'}, {'abstract': 'Each issue will explore a dish or ingredient in depth, starting with ramen.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/david-changs-latest-an-ipad-app-and-a-journal/', 'snippet': 'Each issue will explore a dish or ingredient in depth, starting with ramen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can’t get enough of the Momofuku chef, David Chang? Soon you’ll be able to carry him around with you. In late April, he plans to release Lucky Peach, a quarterly iPad app and print journal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Chang’s Latest: An iPad App and a Journal', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, David (Chef)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meehan, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MOMOFUKU NOODLE BAR', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e364e24-2867-59e5-9ecd-fec185424f66', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e364e24-2867-59e5-9ecd-fec185424f66'}, {'abstract': 'The latest survey on consumer confidence shows those with higher incomes are much more inclined to see the economy on the rebound.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/better-spirits-especially-for-the-better-off/', 'snippet': 'The latest survey on consumer confidence shows those with higher incomes are much more inclined to see the economy on the rebound.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 8:14 p.m. | Updated  to clarify index benchmark and income groupings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Better Spirits,’ Especially for the Better-Off', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conference Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e6c181e-4e5c-53b2-8a74-aac4716222a3', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e6c181e-4e5c-53b2-8a74-aac4716222a3'}, {'abstract': 'The railroad’s chairman was responding to years of litigation over the company’s role in the deportation of Jews who ended up at Nazi death camps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/europe/26france.html', 'snippet': 'The railroad’s chairman was responding to years of litigation over the company’s role in the deportation of Jews who ended up at Nazi death camps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS \x97 The head of France’s national railway company, known as the S.N.C.F., on Tuesday made the company’s first formal public apology directly to Holocaust victims. The regrets came just a few months after American lawmakers, survivors and their descendants moved to block the company from winning contracts in the United States if it did not acknowledge its role in the shipping of thousands of Jews to Nazi death camps and make amends.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Railway Formally Apologizes to Holocaust Victims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Survivors Of Holocaust Hear Apology In France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concentration Camps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:09:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d62a93d-1088-5839-b491-f04f86e1e709', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d62a93d-1088-5839-b491-f04f86e1e709'}, {'abstract': 'Two F1 teams use the Lotus name, and fight over it in court.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/two-lotus-teames-race-it-out-in-court-and-in-the-media/', 'snippet': 'Two F1 teams use the Lotus name, and fight over it in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Formula One season competition has already begun for two of the teams, both of which have the name “Lotus” in their title. Team Lotus and\xa0Lotus Renault GP were in London High Court on Monday in a battle over the right to use the Lotus name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Lotus Teams Race It Out in Court and in the Media', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8f33277-5e85-5f43-a258-97ea32ee8628', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8f33277-5e85-5f43-a258-97ea32ee8628'}, {'abstract': 'Two F1 teams use the Lotus name, and fight over it in court.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/two-lotus-teames-race-it-out-in-court-and-in-the-media/', 'snippet': 'Two F1 teams use the Lotus name, and fight over it in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Formula One season competition has already begun for two of the teams, both of which have the name “Lotus” in their title. Team Lotus and\xa0Lotus Renault GP were in London High Court on Monday in a battle over the right to use the Lotus name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Lotus Teams Race It Out in Court and in the Media', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', '