://article/770596e3-bede-5467-accc-a5d1c18487d4', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/770596e3-bede-5467-accc-a5d1c18487d4'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Riesch has a commanding lead in the overall World Cup Alpine standings, but Lindsey Vonn, the three-time defending champion, said she had not given up the chase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/sports/skiing/26vonn.html', 'snippet': 'Maria Riesch has a commanding lead in the overall World Cup Alpine standings, but Lindsey Vonn, the three-time defending champion, said she had not given up the chase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite Maria Riesch’s commanding 145-point lead in the overall World Cup Alpine standings, Lindsey Vonn said Tuesday that she had not given up the chase for a title she has won the last three years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/Y-VONN/Y-VONN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/Y-VONN/Y-VONN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/sports/Y-VONN/Y-VONN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vonn’s Role in Chase for Title Is Reversed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vonn’s Role In Chase For Title Is Reversed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vonn, Lindsey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Skiing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riesch, Maria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Skiing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1308ece8-bda9-5ce4-be21-2ac65785e4f7', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1308ece8-bda9-5ce4-be21-2ac65785e4f7'}, {'abstract': '“I had already put the key into the door of my building on Lenox Avenue when the question came at my back.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/books/excerpt-harlem-is-nowhere.html', 'snippet': '“I had already put the key into the door of my building on Lenox Avenue when the question came at my back.”', 'lead_paragraph': '1: A Colony of Their Own', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Harlem Is Nowhere’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharifa Rhodes-Pitts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharifa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rhodes-Pitts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed6924f7-8394-54aa-a7a6-2e06583116ae', 'word_count': 5337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed6924f7-8394-54aa-a7a6-2e06583116ae'}, {'abstract': 'With CBS broadcasting comedy reruns on Monday, ABC and Fox finished in a virtual tie for first place in the night’s ratings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/arts/television/26arts-ABCANDFOXSPL_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'With CBS broadcasting comedy reruns on Monday, ABC and Fox finished in a virtual tie for first place in the night’s ratings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With CBS broadcasting comedy reruns on Monday, ABC and Fox finished in a virtual tie for first place in the night’s ratings, according to Nielsen’s estimates. Lifting ABC for the night, “The Bachelor” delivered 9.2 million viewers from 8 to 10 p.m. while Fox earned comparable ratings if slightly fewer viewers on average over that time period with new episodes of “House” at 8 (10.4 million) and “Lie to Me” at 9 (7.7 million). CBS ranked third with repeats but still managed to attract the night’s largest audience with a rerun of “Two and Half Men” at 9 (11.4 million). NBC finished fourth but won the 10 p.m. time slot with its new series “Harry’s Law” (10.4 million), which outperformed ABC’s “Castle” (9.1 million) and CBS’s rerun of “Hawaii Five-0” (6.5 million). Earlier, NBC drew 6.2 million at 8 for “Chuck” and 5.9 million at 9 for “Chase.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC and Fox Split Night', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ABC and Fox Split Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d1693d4-1822-5561-a41e-fe36cb2fa673', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d1693d4-1822-5561-a41e-fe36cb2fa673'}, {'abstract': 'Michele Bachmann says that her unofficial response to the State of the Union address is “not a competition” with the official one by Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/bachmanns-speech-will-push-tea-party-goals/', 'snippet': 'Michele Bachmann says that her unofficial response to the State of the Union address is “not a competition” with the official one by Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a Washington tradition that on the night the president gives his annual address to Congress, a member of the opposition gives a formal response. Tonight, there will be a response to the response. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann’s Speech Will Push Tea Party Goals', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:38:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/514ea604-fc7b-51ec-8244-5445bcb58e22', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514ea604-fc7b-51ec-8244-5445bcb58e22'}, {'abstract': 'While the makers of “Gasland” were thrilled with their nomination, the natural gas industry was not so happy.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-thumbs-down-for-gasland/', 'snippet': 'While the makers of “Gasland” were thrilled with their nomination, the natural gas industry was not so happy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nomination for best documentary truly thrilled the makers of “Gasland” — the producer Trish Adlesic was crying so hard when she called the film’s director, Josh Fox, with the news, that he had trouble understanding her. But there was one constituency that was not so happy. As Green, our sister blog, writes, the natural gas industry gave a thumbs down to the documentary about the perils of natural gas drilling, or fracking. “While it’s unfortunate there isn’t an Oscar category for propaganda, this nomination is fitting, as the Oscars are aimed at praising pure entertainment among Hollywood’s elite,” said Lee Fuller, executive director of Energy In Depth, a pro-drilling group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Thumbs Down for ‘Gasland’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd2300d6-42d9-5fa9-aaef-a10de1bf31a9', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd2300d6-42d9-5fa9-aaef-a10de1bf31a9'}, {'abstract': 'In a letter to troops, Gen. David H. Petraeus offered an assessment that was noticeably more upbeat than a White House assessment issued last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/asia/26petraeus.html', 'snippet': 'In a letter to troops, Gen. David H. Petraeus offered an assessment that was noticeably more upbeat than a White House assessment issued last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan \x97 Just hours before President Obama gave his State of the Union address, his commander in Afghanistan, Gen. David H. Petraeus, offered what amounted to his own “state of the war” address, one noticeably more upbeat than a White House assessment issued late last year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Is Gaining in Afghanistan, General Writes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Is Gaining\nIn Afghanistan,\nGeneral Writes\nIn Upbeat Letter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 