cellor Cathleen P. Black did not stray from her message as she presided over her first public meeting, and never mind that the audience was made up primarily of the people her words would focus on: veteran teachers, whom she wants to b...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schools Chancellor Cathleen P. Black skipped the pleasantries, ignored the boos and did not stray from the message as she presided over her first public meeting last week. Never mind that the audience was made up primarily of the same people her words would focus on: veteran teachers, whom she wants to be made easier to fire, and union loyalists, who oppose the move.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Face in an Old Fight', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seniority Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Cathleen P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/de615e6f-e1e8-5adc-bba0-518c855dc4da', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de615e6f-e1e8-5adc-bba0-518c855dc4da'}, {'abstract': 'There is a place for the inner hipster at the World Economic Forum.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/davos-one-crazy-exciting-circus/', 'snippet': 'There is a place for the inner hipster at the World Economic Forum.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Davos ‘One Crazy, Exciting Circus’', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e94a429-81dc-535f-815e-4c5366b6c53b', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e94a429-81dc-535f-815e-4c5366b6c53b'}, {'abstract': 'The new Jungle City recording studios marry new technology with a New York-glamour vibe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/arts/music/26studio.html', 'snippet': 'The new Jungle City recording studios marry new technology with a New York-glamour vibe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jungle City Studios, a new recording studio perched above the High Line in Chelsea, seems to be a vision out of New York’s glorious musical past. Packed with the kind of gear that makes sound engineers salivate, like an extremely rare 1960s recording console by EMI side-by-side with the latest gleaming digital equipment, it is not the kind of place you would expect for an era of pirated music and GarageBand. And that’s before you notice the Louis Vuitton-patterned fabric on the walls.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/STUDIO-1/STUDIO-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/STUDIO-1/STUDIO-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/STUDIO-1/STUDIO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/STUDIO-1/STUDIO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/STUDIO-1/STUDIO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Studio Harks Back to a Musical Golden Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Studio Harks Back To a Musical Golden Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd46134-b2a6-523f-9657-9a6941419675', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd46134-b2a6-523f-9657-9a6941419675'}, {'abstract': 'After learning of his film’s many nominations, Danny Boyle, the director and co-screenwriter of “127 Hours,” treated himself with a cab ride home.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/a-cab-ride-celebration/', 'snippet': 'After learning of his film’s many nominations, Danny Boyle, the director and co-screenwriter of “127 Hours,” treated himself with a cab ride home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah— Danny Boyle, the Oscar-winning director of “Slumdog Millionaire” and newly minted multiple nominee for “127 Hours,” is currently in the midst of directing an adaptation of “Frankenstein” at the National Theater in London. So when he got word of his Academy honors, he decided to treat himself to a cab after rehearsal. “I normally get the Tube home,” Mr. Boyle said, from the back of the cab. “But I can’t do any phone calls on the Tube. And it’s a pretty exciting day, I thought I’d get a taxi home to celebrate.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cab-Ride Celebration', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaufoy, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T22:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64bc076-2db2-5ed1-9bda-6104fdf34b19', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64bc076-2db2-5ed1-9bda-6104fdf34b19'}, {'abstract': 'A video from Anthony Di Fiore showing three female spider monkeys, a mom and two daughters, hanging out in the trees over a mineral lick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/1248069587716/female-spider-monkeys.html', 'snippet': 'A video from Anthony Di Fiore showing three female spider monkeys, a mom and two daughters, hanging out in the trees over a mineral lick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A video from Anthony Di Fiore showing three female spider monkeys, a mom and two daughters, hanging out in the trees over a mineral lick.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/25/science/11096_1_25sawmonkeys_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/25/science/11096_1_25sawmonkeys_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Female Spider Monkeys', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T23:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/225ce919-c6c3-56e8-9523-3ebfedfe24ac', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/225ce919-c6c3-56e8-9523-3ebfedfe24ac'}, {'abstract': 'Volkswagen and Mercedes-Benz will feature models not yet available, and movie studios will also preview films coming later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/business/media/26adco.html', 'snippet': 'Volkswagen and Mercedes-Benz will feature models not yet available, and movie studios will also preview films coming later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REMEMBER when movie theaters called the trailers they showed “previews of coming attractions”? Many of the glitzy, big-budget commercials that are scheduled to run during Super Bowl XLV on Feb. 6 will offer previews of coming products and services.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'During Super Bowl, Whetting Appetites for Products to Come', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'During Super Bowl, Whetting Appetites for Products to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T23:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f50e5d35-e703-5e2b-90d6-4b12ea480fb3', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50e5d35-e703-5e2b-90d6-4b12ea480fb3'}, {'abstract': 'Before, during and after the State of the Union address, The Thread scans commentary from across the Web and hosts responses from guest contributors.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/thread-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'Before, during and after the State of the Union address, The Thread scans commentary from across the Web and hosts responses from guest contributors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Thread has lined up a number of Opinionator columnists and guest experts to weigh in over the course of the State of the Union message this evening, with breaking updates throughout. And, as always on the Thread, we’ll be rounding up the most interesting opinions to be found around the blogosphere before, during and after the speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thread of the Union', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T23:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tobin Harshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tobin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a9a107-0b02-5312-8da9-9db9f4c62eaf', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a9a107-0b02-5312-8da9-9db9f4c62eaf'}, {'abstract': 'The band’s new album, “The King Is Dead,” and three-night stand at the Beacon Theater highlight a turn to shorter songs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/arts/music/26decem.html', 'snippet': 'The band’s new album, “The King Is Dead,” and three-night stand at the Beacon Theater highlight a turn to shorter songs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “We do short songs now,” Colin Meloy of the Decemberists said during his band’s concert on Monday night at the Beacon Theater, starting a three-night stand there to open its United States tour. That statement sums up the latest turn in his songwriting for the band. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/DECEMBERISTS/DECEMBERISTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/DECEMBERISTS/DECEMBERISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/DECEMBERISTS/DECEMBERISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Decemberists, a Time to Shift Gears', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Decemberists, a Time to Shift Gears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beacon Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Decemberists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-25T23:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d01e16d-8e06-5eb3-a683-33f580827522', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d01e16d-8e06-5eb3-a683-33f580827522'}, {'abstract': 'As banks retreat, corporations like Google and Verizon are stepping up to buy tax credits from developers of low-income housing and get the projects moving again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/realestate/commercial/26credits.html', 'snippet': 'As banks retreat, corporations like Google and Verizon are stepping up to buy tax credits from developers of low-income housing and get the projects moving again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melbourne Apartments is a new 84-unit building in Des Moines, where a three-bedroom apartment rents for $775 a month but comes with restrictions \x97 a family of five, for example, can earn no more than $47,460 a year. What is remarkable about this otherwise modest project is that the equity came from the search-engine giant Google, whose Mountain View, Calif., headquarters are more than 1,500 miles away. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Credits1/Credits1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Credits1/Credits1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/business/Credits1/Credits1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Invests in Low-Income Housing? Google, for One', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Invests in Low-Income Housing? Google, for One', 'name': None, 