section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TODAY marks the exit of The Minimalist from the pages of the Dining section, as a weekly column at least. There may be return appearances, but the unbroken string of more than 13 years and nearly 700 columns ends here. (I’m not leaving the Times family; more about that in a minute.) ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26MINI-span/26MINI-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26MINI-span/26MINI-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26MINI-span/26MINI-span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26MINI-span/26MINI-span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26MINI-span/26MINI-span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimalist Makes His Exit', 'kicker': 'The Minimalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Goodbye, Over A Cocktail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T00:04:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f8f88b5-fd5e-5231-9344-debf7de3635c', 'word_count': 1616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f8f88b5-fd5e-5231-9344-debf7de3635c'}, {'abstract': 'Gabe Johnson, a video journalist with The New York Times who shoots cooking videos with Mark Bittman, recalls his favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-best-minimalist-video-just-ask-the-guy-who-shot-them/', 'snippet': 'Gabe Johnson, a video journalist with The New York Times who shoots cooking videos with Mark Bittman, recalls his favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week marks the last weekly appearance of the Minimalist column by Mark Bittman. Since 2006, Gabe Johnson, a video journalist with The New York Times, has shot and produced all the videos that accompany the column — more than 200 of them. (The Times has compiled some of the most watched.) He also sampled each and every recipe Mr. Bittman cooked on camera. There will be more Minimalist videos in the future, drawing on recipes from the Times archives, but Diner’s Journal asked Mr. Johnson to talk about the best thing he’s tasted so far. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Minimalist Video? Just Ask the Guy Who Shot Them', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T00:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cc972a7-be91-57b0-b07f-ce5b7078a982', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cc972a7-be91-57b0-b07f-ce5b7078a982'}, {'abstract': 'With the end of The Minimalist, Mark Bittman picks 25 favorites out of more than 1,000 recipes that appeared with his column.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-minimalist-chooses-25-of-his-favorites/', 'snippet': 'With the end of The Minimalist, Mark Bittman picks 25 favorites out of more than 1,000 recipes that appeared with his column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Picking 25 favorites out of more than 1,000\xa0 recipes from The Minimalist — the last weekly column appears this week — is an awesome task. But each of these, listed in order of appearance, represents something special either to me or to regular readers of The Minimalist, or in a couple of cases — most notably Jim Lahey’s bread — to a wider audience. It’s a list that will make you want to cook, I think. What are your favorites?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimalist Chooses 25 of His Favorites', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T00:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c7e7452-2325-5c32-95cd-f03a1ae9d57d', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c7e7452-2325-5c32-95cd-f03a1ae9d57d'}, {'abstract': 'Vladimir Nabokov studied butterflies, and he came up with a sweeping hypothesis that, 65 years later, DNA analysis has proven correct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly.html', 'snippet': 'Vladimir Nabokov studied butterflies, and he came up with a sweeping hypothesis that, 65 years later, DNA analysis has proven correct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vladimir Nabokov may be known to most people as the author of classic novels like “Lolita” and “Pale Fire.” But even as he was writing those books, Nabokov had a parallel existence as a self-taught expert on butterflies.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly1/01butterfly1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly1/01butterfly1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly1/01butterfly1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly1/01butterfly1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01butterfly1/01butterfly1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nonfiction: Nabokov Theory on Butterfly Evolution Is Vindicated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Truth of Butterfly Evolution That It Took a Novelist to Reveal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Butterflies and Moths', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nabokov, Vladimir', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T00:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b875bc4-1cf6-5f8e-bba9-40522a8e1809', 'word_count': 1544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b875bc4-1cf6-5f8e-bba9-40522a8e1809'}, {'abstract': 'A retrospective of the films of Hiroyuki Tanaka, or Sabu, at Japan Society includes “Non-Stop,” “Monday” and “Postman Blues.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/movies/26sabu.html', 'snippet': 'A retrospective of the films of Hiroyuki Tanaka, or Sabu, at Japan Society includes “Non-Stop,” “Monday” and “Postman Blues.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan Society is holding what it says is the first major retrospective of the movies of Hiroyuki Tanaka, who goes by the nom de film Sabu, and you can picture the people responsible for Japan’s image overseas quietly gritting their teeth. They would probably like to keep under the radar Sabu’s distinctive take on the modern Japanese man: paralyzed by feelings of inadequacy, in thrall to cartoonish yakuza fantasies and only coming alive when he’s drunk beyond the point of memory or volition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SABU1/SABU1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SABU1/SABU1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSta