ea stop from the Catskills to Asbury Park, NJ.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When All Tomorrow’s Parties, a British alternative music festival known for its connoisseur taste and noncorporate, mom-and-pop leadership style, came to the New York area in 2008, its organizers chose an unusual spot: Kutsher’s Country Club in Monticello, N.Y., one of the last old Catskills resorts, whose aging facilities brought some charm and kitsch to louder-than-loud shows by bands like My Bloody Valentine and Sunn O))).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SUBATP/SUBATP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SUBATP/SUBATP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SUBATP/SUBATP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SUBATP/SUBATP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/SUBATP/SUBATP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alternative Rock Festival Is Moving to Jersey Shore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alternative Rock Festival Is Moving to Jersey Shore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "All Tomorrow's Parties (Music Festival)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'n