retch cotton or embroidered.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/chanel-eat-fast-walk-fast/', 'snippet': 'Karl Lagerfeld’s collection had the wispy, vague, slightly deliberated quality of the Laurencin portrait of Chanel, with the graphic element supplied by narrow black jeans that were in plain stretch cotton or embroidered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime in the early 1920s, Marie Laurencin, a painter and illustrator in Paris, was asked by Coco Chanel to paint her portrait. According to one Internet site, Chanel rejected the portrait, saying it didn’t look like her. I’m inclined to agree with her, but there’s something very pretty about the soft, watery pastels with a graphic element of black.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chanel: Eat Fast, Walk Fast', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e46f8e1-7b31-5bdd-9e85-f41d3a4b6465', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e46f8e1-7b31-5bdd-9e85-f41d3a4b6465'}, {'abstract': 'The Lower Manhattan Development Corporation is seeking to recover money it advanced to the construction manager it hired for the long-stalled demolition of the tower near ground zero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/nyregion/26deutsche.html', 'snippet': 'The Lower Manhattan Development Corporation is seeking to recover money it advanced to the construction manager it hired for the long-stalled demolition of the tower near ground zero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last chapter in the tortured tale of the former Deutsche Bank building near ground zero will play out in court now that the 41-story office tower has finally been dismantled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$100 Million Suit Planned Over Former Deutsche Bank Building', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Development Agency Plans Suit Over Former Deutsche Building', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank Building (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lower Manhattan Development Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bovis Lend Lease', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:14:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74342292-53c7-5896-86ba-5cfc4269fae1', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74342292-53c7-5896-86ba-5cfc4269fae1'}, {'abstract': 'The economic forum should address the “too big to fail” bank problem, destabilizing capital flows, improving governance and liberalization to free markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/business/26views.html', 'snippet': 'The economic forum should address the “too big to fail” bank problem, destabilizing capital flows, improving governance and liberalization to free markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global economy is not as healthy as it looks. The International Monetary Fund now predicts 4.4 percent growth for 2011. But inflation has reared its ugly head across the globe, suggesting that many economies are growing faster than can be sustained without structural changes. Spurring on reform should be the main focus of the annual World Economic Forum gathering this week in Davos, Switzerland.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Growth Agenda for World Economic Forum', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth Agenda\nFor Davos Forum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Dixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/83322071-a55b-544c-a0c4-8b24acc99e04', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83322071-a55b-544c-a0c4-8b24acc99e04'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Becker, the Nobel laureate economist, and Richard Posner, the federal judge and author, argue that tuition at public colleges should increase. They compare a tuition increase to a tax on the affluent. Are they onto something?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/is-college-tuition-too-low/', 'snippet': 'Gary Becker, the Nobel laureate economist, and Richard Posner, the federal judge and author, argue that tuition at public colleges should increase. They compare a tuition increase to a tax on the affluent. Are they onto something?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column this week looks at ways to cut wasteful spending on higher education and redirect the money more productively. Another way to keep colleges in decent financial shape during tough economic times, of course, is to raise tuition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is College Tuition Too Low?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posner, Richard A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c3c586-34bd-52f8-97b0-7ac1375f37f4', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c3c586-34bd-52f8-97b0-7ac1375f37f4'}, {'abstract': 'A response to an article about Alzheimer’s disease in China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/opinion/lweb26alzheimers.html', 'snippet': 'A response to an article about Alzheimer’s disease in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Alzheimer’s Disaster', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Alzheimer’s Disaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:16:25+0000', 'doc