e': 'Buying Wine in New York State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd03db4-7d86-57d8-aa21-011b5b3439d1', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd03db4-7d86-57d8-aa21-011b5b3439d1'}, {'abstract': 'Jack Kimball rose swiftly from being a private citizen with strong opinions to being the leader of the New Hampshire Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/us/politics/26kimball.html', 'snippet': 'Jack Kimball rose swiftly from being a private citizen with strong opinions to being the leader of the New Hampshire Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DERRY, N.H. \x97 Until last weekend, one of Jack Kimball’s biggest claims to political fame was the eye-catching conservative messages he would post on a sign outside his office-cleaning company. “Let’s All Stop Paying Our Mortgages,” read one as the subprime crisis raged. “Obama Hands Off Our Healthcare,” barked another as the contentious federal health care law was being debated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/us/KIMBALL/KIMBALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/us/KIMBALL/KIMBALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/us/KIMBALL/KIMBALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yesterday’s Gadfly, Today’s Political Boss', 'kicker': 'Man in the News | John W. Kimball Jr.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yesterday’s Gadfly, Today’s Political Boss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimball, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f03dafb-7b94-5f88-8353-f03d455d788c', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f03dafb-7b94-5f88-8353-f03d455d788c'}, {'abstract': 'After days of protests, dozens of Tunisians marched in the capital on Tuesday to demonstrate their patience with the interim government that replaced the ousted dictator Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/africa/26tunis.html', 'snippet': 'After days of protests, dozens of Tunisians marched in the capital on Tuesday to demonstrate their patience with the interim government that replaced the ousted dictator Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS \x97 After days of antigovernment protests, dozens of Tunisians marched in the capital on Tuesday to demonstrate their patience with the interim government that replaced the ousted dictator Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, pleading with their fellow citizens to give the temporary leadership time to hold elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Call for Calm in Tunis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Call for Calm in Tunis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T01:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810f35b3-5c28-55d7-88b8-d5ffaf675681', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810f35b3-5c28-55d7-88b8-d5ffaf675681'}, {'abstract': 'Anna Mashutina was on her way to accept an award when she was killed along with dozens of other people in a terrorist attack at Domodedovo Airport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/europe/26ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'Anna Mashutina was on her way to accept an award when she was killed along with dozens of other people in a terrorist attack at Domodedovo Airport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Anna Mashutina hated compliments. When praised for her plays, she would look down in embarrassment, or respond by listing their shortcomings. She was so bashful about her success that she sometimes seemed to be apologizing for it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Playwright’s Voice, Silenced in a Flash of Terrorism in Moscow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kic