id': 'nyt://article/c6a24557-a6e7-5842-819f-aea5a21ee224', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a24557-a6e7-5842-819f-aea5a21ee224'}, {'abstract': 'Thin slices of La Quercia’s new version of coppa piccante make a handsome addition to an appetizer platter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/dining/26coppa.html', 'snippet': 'Thin slices of La Quercia’s new version of coppa piccante make a handsome addition to an appetizer platter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At La Quercia, an American producer of cured pork from heritage breeds, Herb Eckhouse keeps coming up with new temptations. He has just introduced his version of coppa piccante, a well-marbled, deep mahogany hunk of pork shoulder with a brash swagger thanks to cumin and smoky Spanish paprika. Thin slices make a handsome addition to an appetizer platter, and dicings can go into a salad or provide the underpinning of a stew.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26STUFF-2/26STUFF-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26STUFF-2/26STUFF-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26STUFF-2/STUFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26STUFF-2/STUFF2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/dining/26STUFF-2/STUFF2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coppa Piccante With a