ce Is Elusive on Charge Of a Blizzard Work Slowdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halloran, Daniel J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4928ea4-9215-5a26-b1e5-3621756abb40', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4928ea4-9215-5a26-b1e5-3621756abb40'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | What did you think of the president’s speech to Congress, his cabinet, the Supreme Court and the nation?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/what-is-your-reaction-to-obamas-second-state-of-the-union-address/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | What did you think of the president’s speech to Congress, his cabinet, the Supreme Court and the nation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his second State of the Union speech, President Obama focused his remarks on the economy and innovation with a “plan to win the future,” declaring that it is imperative that the United States rise to meet the challenges of the world. What did you think of Mr. Obama’s speech?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Your Reaction to Obama’s Second State of the Union Address?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:13:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dffc0980-ee29-5fd3-963d-3fc1179ae267', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dffc0980-ee29-5fd3-963d-3fc1179ae267'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gordon, a chiseled character actor, played tough guys, most memorably the mob boss Frank Nitti on the television series “The Untouchables.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/arts/television/26gordon.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gordon, a chiseled character actor, played tough guys, most memorably the mob boss Frank Nitti on the television series “The Untouchables.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Gordon, a granite-faced, gravel-voiced character actor famous for playing heavies, most memorably the mob boss Frank Nitti on the classic television series “The Untouchables,” died on Thursday. He was 94 and lived in Santa Fe, N.M.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/arts/GORDON-obit/GORDON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 