ated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for David Leonhardt on the State of the Union', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonhardt, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:33:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By ECONOMIX EDITORS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Economix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'EDITORS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/715e2325-f350-59f0-b238-a99f131d0e32', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/715e2325-f350-59f0-b238-a99f131d0e32'}, {'abstract': 'The slowdown prompted some economists to warn that the country was at increased risk of a “double dip” recession', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/europe/26britain.html', 'snippet': 'The slowdown prompted some economists to warn that the country was at increased risk of a “double dip” recession', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON \x97 Prime Minister David Cameron’s coalition government received a sharp political jolt on Tuesday with the release of official figures showing that Britain’s economy contracted slightly in the last three months of 2010, prompting some economists to warn that the country was at increased risk of a “double dip” recession after four consecutive quarters of modest growth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/world/BRITAIN/BRITAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Economy Stalls, in Setback for Cameron', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain’s Economy Stalls, Prompting Attacks on Cameron’s Strict Austerity Cure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns and Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7312c43-43ce-5d7c-b1dd-977b52a66996', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7312c43-43ce-5d7c-b1dd-977b52a66996'}, {'abstract': 'Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, the inventors of the Unix operating system and the C programming language, have been awarded the Japan Prize. Thompson also created the first master-level chess computer.', 'web_url': 'https://gambit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/computer-chess-pioneer-wins-prestigious-japan-prize/', 'snippet': 'Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, the inventors of the Unix operating system and the C programming language, have been awarded the Japan Prize. Thompson also created the first master-level chess computer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, the inventors of the Unix operating system and C programming language more than 40 years ago, have been awarded the Japan Prize, according to the San Francisco Chronicle. The prize goes each year to people whose work “aims to promote the advancement of science and technology for the peace and prosperity of mankind.” The award is for $600,000. Ten previous recipients have also won Nobel Prizes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Computer (Chess) Pioneer Wins Prestigious Japan Prize', 'kicker': 'Gambit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unix (Operating System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bell Laboratories', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5713ffa7-c8e9-529a-a000-b9f1c5c2f4a6', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5713ffa7-c8e9-529a-a000-b9f1c5c2f4a6'}, {'abstract': 'With a call for a two-year extension of a domestic spending freeze, the president sought to respond to critics demanding cuts to reduce budget deficits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/us/politics/26fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'With a call for a two-year extension of a domestic spending freeze, the president sought to respond to critics demanding cuts to reduce budget deficits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 By proposing a two-year extension to the three-year domestic spending freeze he called for a year ago, President Obama sought to quickly counter Republican demands for deeper cuts to shrink government and reduce annual budget deficits.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/us/STATE-FLOATER-4/STATE-FLOATER-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Counters G.O.P. With Plan to Extend Spending Freeze', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Counters G.O.P. With Plan to Extend Spending Freeze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7897fc0-e4b2-5e9c-874d-ea58ce266a2e', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7897fc0-e4b2-5e9c-874d-ea58ce266a2e'}, {'abstract': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy said Tuesday that France had concluded a deal with Russia to sell it four Mistral assault ships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/europe/26briefs-Francebrf2.html', 'snippet': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy said Tuesday that France had concluded a deal with Russia to sell it four Mistral assault ships.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Nicolas Sarkozy said Tuesday that France had concluded a deal with Russia to sell it four Mistral assault ships. The deal, which has now been signed, according to a joint French-Russian statement on Tuesday, was criticized by the United States and NATO allies in the Baltics for providing Russia with a modern carrier for helicopters or tanks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Sells Assault Ships to Russia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Sells Assault Ships to Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/36140ee8-850c-5afa-ad1b-f3fcbce71cd6', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36140ee8-850c-5afa-ad1b-f3fcbce71cd6'}, {'abstract': 'He Depu, a prominent Chinese democracy advocate who had been jailed for eight years, was beaten by police officers on Monday, just after he was released from jail, according to a report by Human Rights in China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/asia/26briefs-chinabrf.html', 'snippet': 'He Depu, a prominent Chinese democracy advocate who had been jailed for eight years, was beaten by police officers on Monday, just after he was released from jail, according to a report by Human Rights in China.', 'lead_paragraph': ' He Depu, a prominent Chinese democracy advocate who had been jailed for eight years, was beaten by police officers on Monday, just after he was released from jail, according to a report by Human Rights in China. The report, which cited a witness, said that Mr. He had been beaten when he resisted being shoved into a police vehicle. He was given rules to abide by in the next two years, the report said, including not criticizing the government. Mr. He took part in the 1989 movement that ended in the Tiananmen Square massacre and helped form the now-banned China Democracy Party in 1998. After his release on Monday, Mr. He told a friend about being tortured while in prison, the report said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Dissident Is Reported Beaten', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Dissident Is Reported Beaten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights in China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/14366540-b350-56fe-8f53-6b2a90027094', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14366540-b350-56fe-8f53-6b2a90027094'}, {'abstract': 'We must do something or other to avoid the fate that maybe happened somewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/25/the-ryan-response/', 'snippet': 'We must do something or other to avoid the fate that maybe happened somewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': '… was as bad as you might expect. Lots of breast-beating about deficits; you’d never know that no leading Republican, Ryan very much included, has offered a serious proposal to cut the deficit. Some cooked statistics about federal spending. And then there was this curious assertion:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ryan Response', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:51:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7693ee10-6c99-5cad-b3cd-74220a4defdb', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7693ee10-6c99-5cad-b3cd-74220a4defdb'}, {'abstract': 'Flights get canceled. Passengers get bumped. But there are steps you can take to minimize the damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/travel/30prac-flightrights.html', 'snippet': 'Flights get canceled. Passengers get bumped. But there are steps you can take to minimize the damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS thousands of passengers who were caught up in the latest bout of snowstorms along the East Coast can attest, when weather disrupts the system, travelers are basically on their own. Just getting someone on the phone to confirm a new flight was a major headache for travelers who had been stranded for days in cities up and down the East Coast during the holidays.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla