te of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T03:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53f0cc85-12b2-55b8-a0a8-28dddd39b5e5', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53f0cc85-12b2-55b8-a0a8-28dddd39b5e5'}, {'abstract': 'Ed Stelmach said on Tuesday that he would step down as the premier of Alberta, blaming “U.S.-style, negative-attack politics” for his decision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/world/americas/26briefs-Canadabrf.html', 'snippet': 'Ed Stelmach said on Tuesday that he would step down as the premier of Alberta, blaming “U.S.-style, negative-attack politics” for his decision.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ed Stelmach said on Tuesday that he would step down as the premier of Alberta, blaming “U.S.-style, negative-attack politics” for his decision. His party is expected to name a successor soon after he makes a formal announcement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Alberta’s Premier to Resign', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Alberta’s Premier to Resign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T04:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk'