7ed262-fcb6-5d51-8615-325fcddd1a94'}, {'abstract': 'The disappearance of birds that evolved with an ecosystem over thousands of years could have a cascade of consequences, a scientist warns.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/q-and-a-imperiled-birds-on-a-warming-planet/', 'snippet': 'The disappearance of birds that evolved with an ecosystem over thousands of years could have a cascade of consequences, a scientist warns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days ago I wrote about the risk of mass extinctions from impending climate change over the next century, especially among animals that live high on mountains or in the tropics. They will have difficulty moving themselves to cooler climates, either because they cannot move up in altitude or because the distance from the tropics to a cooler habitat is simply farther than they can travel. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Imperiled Birds on a Warming Planet', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T12:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/611039b5-960c-54ad-8a17-8ae0da4eed5a', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/611039b5-960c-54ad-8a17-8ae0da4eed5a'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets appeared to win the battle of words with New England before their upset victory in the divisional round, and