cker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T14:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8ec2425-a32e-5826-b168-b1944bcf4e7e', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8ec2425-a32e-5826-b168-b1944bcf4e7e'}, {'abstract': 'In a comic interview on “The Colbert Report,” Amy Chua tried to argue that her book “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother” was a memoir, not a how-to guide on parenting.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/tiger-mother-in-stephen-colberts-den/', 'snippet': 'In a comic interview on “The Colbert Report,” Amy Chua tried to argue that her book “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother” was a memoir, not a how-to guide on parenting.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tiger Mother’ in Stephen Colbert’s Den', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T14:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE ITZKOFF', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ITZKOFF', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/694f3db9-2271-51ed-8a16-cd293368798a', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/694f3db9-2271-51ed-8a16-cd293368798a'}, {'abstract': 'In a comic interview on “The Colbert Report,” Amy Chua tried to argue that her book “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother” was a memoir, not a how-to guide on parenting.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/tiger-mother-in-stephen-colberts-den/', 'snippet': 'In a comic interview on “The Colbert Report,” Amy Chua tried to argue that her book “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother” was a memoir, not a how-to guide on parenting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only a matter of time before Amy Chua, the author of “Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother” and proponent of a much discussed method of child rearing that emphasizes hard work, limits social interaction and includes the occasional threat to burn a stuffed animal, made her way onto “The Colbert Report.” On Tuesday’s broadcast the host, Stephen Colbert, recapped for his audience the controversy that has swirled around Ms. Chua’s book and offered some advice to viewers who might be the children of tiger mothers. (“Get back to that Mendelssohn concerto before she drowns your bunny!”) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tiger Mother’ in Stephen Colbert’s Den', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chua, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T14:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/74277d57-b4dd-5753-a9d6-7d266242a2ea', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74277d57-b4dd-5753-a9d6-7d266242a2ea'}, {'abstract': 'The plane maker predicted its earnings would fall below analysts’ expectations, partly from delays to the 787 Dreamliner program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/business/27boeing.html', 'snippet': 'The plane maker predicted its earnings would fall below analysts’ expectations, partly from delays to the 787 Dreamliner program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boeing predicted that its profit in 2011 would fall below analysts’ estimates, mainly because of higher pension expenses and delays in finishing the 787 Dreamliner, setting off a 3 percent decline in its share price.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Boeing/Boeing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Boeing/Boeing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Boeing/Boeing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Profit Slips as Boeing Delivers Fewer Planes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Forecasts a Hit to Profit, but Production Is Expected to Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T14:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a346c08b-312c-5f47-b067-a0e6e0f72b8d', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a346c08b-312c-5f47-b067-a0e6e0f72b8d'}, {'abstract': 'TPC is out to get you.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/separated-at-birth/', 'snippet': 'TPC is out to get you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hmm. One of my commenters claims that Representative Ryan is a dead ringer for the evil representative of The Phone Company from The President’s Analyst (one of my favorite good-bad movies too). [“It explains your utter lack of hostility. You can vent your aggressive feelings by actually killing people! It’s a sensational solution to the hostility problem. “]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Separated at Birth?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T14:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8b4b3f7-b52b-5aa2-9b7a-a2c34858b310', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8b4b3f7-b52b-5aa2-9b7a-a2c34858b310'}, {'abstract': 'The Financial Services Authority fined Barclays Capital £1.12 million for failing to separate client funds held in money market accounts from its own funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/barclays-fined-by-regulators/', 'snippet': 'The Financial Services Authority fined Barclays Capital £1.12 million for failing to separate client funds held in money market accounts from its own funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Financial Services Authority, the British securities regulator, said on Wednesday that it had fined Barclays Capital £1.12 million for failing to put a fence around clients’ funds held in money market accounts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headli