o': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Andrew Ross', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McGraw-Hill Cos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wipro Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T15:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf3571a-a73d-5e6a-83ca-3243da945f62', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf3571a-a73d-5e6a-83ca-3243da945f62'}, {'abstract': 'The borough president, Helen M. Marshall, said in her State of the Borough address that over all, Queens was weathering the storm of the weak economy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/in-queens-a-lament-that-the-borough-is-shortchanged/', 'snippet': 'The borough president, Helen M. Marshall, said in her State of the Borough address that over all, Queens was weathering the storm of the weak economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The performance featured a number from the hit musical “Grease,” a salute to the Mets, depressing crime statistics and a rousing tribute to a 95-year-old former salesman who orchestrated the largest air rescue of American soldiers behind enemy lines in World War II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Queens, a Lament That the Borough Is Shortchanged', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Helen M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T15:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/55da5991-331b-5071-859b-d2104ab9a7ad', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55da5991-331b-5071-859b-d2104ab9a7ad'}, {'abstract': 'Filmmakers, artists and publicists might answer that an Oscar is priceless in terms of reputation. But studio heads, agents and producers would prefer to put a very specific figure on it.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/the-value-of-the-oscar-bump/', 'snippet': 'Filmmakers, artists and publicists might answer that an Oscar is priceless in terms of reputation. But studio heads, agents and producers would prefer to put a very specific figure on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Just how much is an Oscar nomination worth? Filmmakers, artists and publicists might answer that it’s priceless in terms of reputation. But studio heads, agents and producers would prefer to put a very specific figure on it. The research firm IBISWorld crunched the numbers and found that “the average best Picture Oscar winners over the last four years saw a bump of 22.2 percent (or $20.3 million) in box office revenue after they were named a nominee and an additional 15.3 percent (or $14.0 million) following their win at the award show,” according to data the firm put out. (Simon Beaufoy was right: a nomination is more significant, financially, than a win.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Value of the Oscar Bump', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaufoy, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T15:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3175dcb2-4448-5f0e-94cd-d0a0ca665a77', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3175dcb2-4448-5f0e-94cd-d0a0ca665a77'}, {'abstract': 'The president speaks about tuition tax credits, student loans, the need for new teachers and the critical role of community colleges.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/obama-2/', 'snippet': 'The president speaks about tuition tax credits, student loans, the need for new teachers and the critical role of community colleges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his State of the Union address, President Obama occasionally adopted the tone of national guidance counselor in advocating for high school and college students and their families.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President as College Counselor', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T15:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a31605f7-fa02-593c-a327-cd405e5802db', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a31605f7-fa02-593c-a327-cd405e5802db'}, {'abstract': '“We got on and it really started smoking,” one passenger said. “We were just sitting ducks.” Then the rescue boat came.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/ferry-boat-on-fire-in-hudson-police-say/', 'snippet': '“We got on and it really started smoking,” one passenger said. “We were just sitting ducks.” Then the rescue boat came.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:31 p.m. A Hudson River ferryboat that helped rescue passengers from a ditched jetliner needed some rescuing itself on Wednesday when it began smoldering shortly after leaving the dock at Edgewater, N.J.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Passengers Pulled to Safety From Smoldering Hudson Ferry', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edgewater (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T15:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c7841a-6eed-5fd