abstract': 'A state of the union speech whose power was constructed of small elements.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/language-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'A state of the union speech whose power was constructed of small elements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s state of the union speech was eloquently prosaic. The rhetoric did not soar; and the speech’s force was carried by short, repeated phrases that served to tie together themes and exhortations. “Win the future” served both as an organizing device and a call to arms. But the arms were, in the grand scheme of things, small — high-speed railways, more teachers, a better and faster Internet. These are not inconsiderable goals, but they don’t have the ring of “bringing peace to the Middle East,” a hope not even mentioned. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Language of the Union', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T17:43:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b94d8089-04d5-5b59-8da6-1c0fc7e357b2', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b94d8089-04d5-5b59-8da6-1c0fc7e357b2'}, {'abstract': 'Michigan State hockey coach Rick Comley has decided to retire at the end of the season. His replacement could come from the pro, college or Team USA development ranks.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/michigan-states-comley-surprises-with-retirement-announcement/', 'snippet': 'Michigan State hockey coach Rick Comley has decided to retire at the end of the season. His replacement could come from the pro, college or Team USA development ranks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A change is coming to one of the storied programs in men’s college hockey, and the ripple effect could be felt up to the pro level.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan State’s Comley Surprises with Retirement Announcement', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T17:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2acc0290-186e-5e1f-95b2-5b6102a2a16c', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2acc0290-186e-5e1f-95b2-5b6102a2a16c'}, {'abstract': 'Spas at huge winter resorts are nothing new. But don’t be surprised if the next time you walk into the one at Stowe Mountain Resort in Vermont, you see a youngster getting a massage.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/at-resorts-spas-just-for-the-kids/', 'snippet': 'Spas at huge winter resorts are nothing new. But don’t be surprised if the next time you walk into the one at Stowe Mountain Resort in Vermont, you see a youngster getting a massage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spas at huge winter resorts are nothing new. But don’t be surprised if the next time you walk into the one at Stowe Mountain Resort in Vermont, you see a youngster getting a massage. In late December, Stowe (802-253-3560; stowemountainlodge.com) opened the Chillax KidSpa, a relaxation room for children inside the 21,000-square-foot (adult) spa. Children of any age are allowed treatments at the spa proper, when accompanied by an adult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Resorts, Spas Just for the Kids', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T17:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Vatner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vatner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9b0a846-0d53-5519-a6d8-7812de60e338', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9b0a846-0d53-5519-a6d8-7812de60e338'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to the State of the Union address.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/l27obama.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to the State of the Union address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/opinion/27letters/27letters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/opinion/27letters/27letters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/opinion/27letters/27letters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s ‘Win the Future’ Challenge', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s ‘Win the Future’ Challenge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T17:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/23e3f0f5-6754-5e68-876e-346a2258513d', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23e3f0f5-6754-5e68-876e-346a2258513d'}, {'abstract': 'Why have all recent presidents only accomplished a political agenda that belonged to the other side?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/too-moderate-or-too-modest/', 'snippet': 'Why have all recent presidents only accomplished a political agenda that belonged to the other side?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David, every year we get all worked up about the State of the Union speech. When it finally happens I’m always disappointed, bored, underwhelmed. Then the pollsters announce that the public loved it. So obviously it’s me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Moderate or Too Modest?', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'va