hootings, an official close to the investigation said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/us/27giffords.html', 'snippet': 'The death penalty and solitary confinement were other topics of interest in the hours before the Tucson shootings, an official close to the investigation said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON \x97 Jared L. Loughner, the man accused of opening fire outside a Tucson supermarket on Jan. 8 in what the authorities consider an attempted assassination of Representative Gabrielle Giffords, researched famous assassins, the death penalty and solitary confinement on the Internet before the shootings, an official close to the investigation said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Charged in Tucson Shootings Had Researched Assassins, Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Charged in Tucson Shootings Had Researched Assassins, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T18:11:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein and Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of