e/a5e805e2-be49-58be-bd5d-8de9f6d106ed'}, {'abstract': 'They take the top spot on the Billboard album chart.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/check-your-calendar-decemberists-reign-in-january/', 'snippet': 'They take the top spot on the Billboard album chart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least three camps will be very happy that the Decemberists, the indie-folk band from Portland, Ore., known for its high-concept songs and S.A.T.-level vocabulary, has reached No. 1 on the latest Billboard album chart: the band and its record company, its fans and the hand-wringers and observers of the music industry who have recently seen two historic lows in a key sales metric.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Check Your Calendar: Decemberists Reign in January', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allman, Gregg', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mars, Bruno', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Decemberists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen SoundScan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/feb486a3-8345-541a-bd5c-08cd76a7c9ef', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feb486a3-8345-541a-bd5c-08cd76a7c9ef'}, {'abstract': 'Is Julian Assange, the WikiLeaks founder, a puppet master of the news media? He would like you to think so. But The Times’s dealings with him reveal a different story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Wikileaks-t.html', 'snippet': 'Is Julian Assange, the WikiLeaks founder, a puppet master of the news media? He would like you to think so. But The Times’s dealings with him reveal a different story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past June, Alan Rusbridger, the editor of The Guardian, phoned me and asked, mysteriously, whether I had any idea how to arrange a secure communication. Not really, I confessed. The Times doesn’t have encrypted phone lines, or a Cone of Silence. Well then, he said, he would try to speak circumspectly. In a roundabout way, he laid out an unusual proposition: an organization called WikiLeaks, a secretive cadre of antisecrecy vigilantes, had come into possession of a substantial amount of classified United States government communications. WikiLeaks’s leader, Julian Assange, an eccentric former computer hacker of Australian birth and no fixed residence, offered The Guardian half a million military dispatches from the battlefields of Afghanistan and Iraq. There might be more after that, including an immense bundle of confidential diplomatic cables. The Guardian suggested — to increase the impact as well as to share the labor of handling such a trove — that The New York Times be invited to share this exclusive bounty. The source agreed. Was I interested?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/magazine/assange-337/assange-337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/magazine/assange-337/assange-337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/magazine/assange-337/assange-337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With Assange and the WikiLeaks Secrets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE \nBOY \nWHO \nKICKED \nTHE \nHORNET’S \nNEST ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Der Spiegel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cffea54-b28a-580d-8290-e1c930c361bb', 'word_count': 7982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cffea54-b28a-580d-8290-e1c930c361bb'}, {'abstract': 'the Polish-American virtuoso pianist', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0128.html', 'snippet': 'the Polish-American virtuoso pianist', 'lead_paragraph': ' Arthur Rubinstein, one of the greatest pianists of the century, died quietly in his sleep at his home in Geneva yesterday. He was 95 years old.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arthur Rubinstein Dies in Geneva at 95', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96acf6a2-609f-56d9-813f-8ebb163af302', 'word_count': 3502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96acf6a2-609f-56d9-813f-8ebb163af302'}, {'abstract': "one of America's foremost composers of music for the theatre and screen", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0127.html', 'snippet': "one of America's foremost composers of music for the theatre and screen", 'lead_paragraph': "Jerome Kern, the composer, died yesterday at 1:10 P.M. of a cerebral hemorrhage in Doctors Hospital. His age was 60. At the bedside were his wife, Eva Leale Kern; his daughter, Elizabeth Kern, former wife of Artie Shaw, the bandleader, and Oscar Hammerstein 2d, producer and song writer, who was closely associated with Mr. Kern in his career. Shortly after Mr. Kern's death Irving Berlin called at the hospital. ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jerome Kern Dies; Noted Composer, 60', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e