story in 1947 by becoming the first black baseball player in the major leagues', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/0131.html', 'snippet': 'who made history in 1947 by becoming the first black baseball player in the major leagues', 'lead_paragraph': ' Jackie Robinson, who made history in 1947 by becoming the first black baseball player in the major leagues, suffered a heart attack in his home in Stamford, Conn., yesterday morning and died at Stamford Hospital at 7:10 A.M. He was 53 years old. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jackie Robinson, First Black in Major Leagues, Dies', 'kicker': 'OBITUARY', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE ANDERSON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ANDERSON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f38f6fe-d2e6-576a-93c3-d64bc1238649', 'word_count': 2862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f38f6fe-d2e6-576a-93c3-d64bc1238649'}, {'abstract': 'The study confirmed that the 25 schools proposed for closing are among the lowest performing in the city. But it also found they are not universally the worst.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/schools-chosen-to-close-have-toughest-demographics/', 'snippet': 'The study confirmed that the 25 schools proposed for closing are among the lowest performing in the city. But it also found they are not universally the worst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 14 high schools that the city is proposing to close for poor performance have more homeless students, more special education students, and double the number of over-age students than the average city high school, and their share of such students has expanded in recent years, according to a new report from the city’s Independent Budget Office released on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Closing Schools Have Most Challenging Demographics', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4cae77-84bc-54b5-9b0b-d3b70b956723', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4cae77-84bc-54b5-9b0b-d3b70b956723'}, {'abstract': 'Indian executives at Davos take pride in the things that set their country apart from China: democracy, a reliable legal framework, widespread English and a famed information technology sector.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/can-india-leapfrog-china/', 'snippet': 'Indian executives at Davos take pride in the things that set their country apart from China: democracy, a reliable legal framework, widespread English and a famed information technology sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — India is trying hard not to be forgotten at the World Economic Forum amid the China-focus. The country has brought the single biggest delegation to Davos and ads for its “Inclusive Growth” slogan could be seen 