d screenplay, and not for best original screenplay?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Category Confusion, Cleared Up', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinfeld, Hailee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:23:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a41fd51-5e5b-5641-bb3c-24427ca39840', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a41fd51-5e5b-5641-bb3c-24427ca39840'}, {'abstract': 'The police searched a car abandoned after an accident in Manhattan and found a man injured with what were apparently knife cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/after-hit-run-man-is-found-stuffed-in-car-trunk/', 'snippet': 'The police searched a car abandoned after an accident in Manhattan and found a man injured with what were apparently knife cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hit-and-run accident in Upper Manhattan led police officers to an injured man tied up and stuffed in the trunk of a car, the police said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hit-Run, Man Is Found Stuffed in Car Trunk', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hit-and-Run Drivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':