gypt has not focused on Israel, it could have a momentous impact on the future of the country’s oldest and most important Middle East relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM \x97 After the Tunisian revolution and the emergence of a Hezbollah-backed government in Lebanon, Israelis are confronting another jolt to the system as mass protests rock Egypt, the partner in Israel’s oldest and most important Middle East relationship.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warily Eyeing Egypt, Israelis Feel Like Spectators', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Regional Unrest, Israel Is a Spectator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eran, Oded', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T19:36:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0c42153-83be-5810-8fe9-d3c1e72c0943', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0c42153-83be-5810-8fe9-d3c1e72c0943'}, {'abstract': 'At a round-table session in The Hague, environmental groups and business officials accused Shell of understating its responsibility for oil spills in the Niger Delta region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/science/earth/