he right thing, Gil Meche told the Kansas City Royals he did not want any of the $12 million due him in 2011 and retired from baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/sports/baseball/27meche.html', 'snippet': 'Saying he wanted to do the right thing, Gil Meche told the Kansas City Royals he did not want any of the $12 million due him in 2011 and retired from baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guaranteed contract is a fundamental principle of Major League Baseball, as much a part of the game as balls, strikes and outs. No matter how a player performs, or how his body holds up, he must be paid in full. Only in rare cases — an injury sustained off the field, gross personal misconduct — does a player forfeit his paycheck.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/27meche1/27meche1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/27meche1/27meche1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/27meche1/27meche1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/27meche1/27meche1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/27meche1/27meche1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitcher Spurns $12 Million, to Keep Self-Respect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pitcher Spurns $12 Million, to Keep Self-Respect', 'name': None, 'se