d': 'nyt://article/3f54ffa0-6090-5896-bed1-473886056fe5', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f54ffa0-6090-5896-bed1-473886056fe5'}, {'abstract': 'Diane von Furstenberg tells W.W.D. about her skiing accident.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/quote-unquote-black-and-blue-is-the-new-black/', 'snippet': 'Diane von Furstenberg tells W.W.D. about her skiing accident.', 'lead_paragraph': '–Diane von Furstenberg tells W.W.D. about the skiing accident that left her with a broken nose. At least she doesn’t look like Mike Tyson’s opponent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quote Unquote | Black and Blue is the New Black', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:03:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Leon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/51066206-6761-5378-aea4-bddea2e45114', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51066206-6761-5378-aea4-bddea2e45114'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Lee Myers, The Times’s outgoing Baghdad bureau chief, is taking readers’ questions on the state of politics, the withdrawal of U.S. troops and the mood on the ground in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/ask-baghdad-bureau-reader-q-a/', 'snippet': 'Steven Lee Myers, The Times’s outgoing Baghdad bureau chief, is taking readers’ questions on the state of politics, the withdrawal of U.S. troops and the mood on the ground in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Lee Myers, The Times’s Baghdad bureau chief, is leaving his post after two years. He is taking questions from readers, looking at the changes he has seen in Iraq and weighing in on the scheduled December 2011 deadline for the withdrawal of American troops, the fragility of the Iraqi coalition government and the future role of key players like Moktada al-Sadr. He also addresses the mood on the ground among an Iraqi populace disenchanted with its own political leaders, witnessing political turmoil in the region around them. Here, he and Alissa J. Rubin, the Kabul bureau chief, discuss President Obama’s State of the Union address, as seen from Baghdad and Kabul. Post questions for Mr. Myers in the comment section below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask Baghdad Bureau: Reader Q. and A.', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers and Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/57fddcbc-2873-537b-b2e9-45e4b8e4e800', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57fddcbc-2873-537b-b2e9-45e4b8e4e800'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters in Egypt oppose President Mubarak, an American ally for three decades; President Medvedev of Russia makes a quick trip to Davos after the suicide bombing; and the costume designers behind "Black Swan."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/continuous/1248069590417/timescast-january-26-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters in Egypt oppose President Mubarak, an American ally for three decades; President Medvedev of Russia makes a quick trip to Davos after the suicide bombing; and the costume designers behind "Black Swan."', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protesters in Egypt oppose President Mubarak, an American ally for three decades; President Medvedev of Russia makes a quick trip to Davos after the suicide bombing; and the costume designers behind "Black Swan."', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/continuous/11101_1_tc-012611_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/26/continuous/11101_1_tc-012611_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | January 26, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Black Swan (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costume Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/635ed871-ac5d-59d6-89b7-22365d1d4c8f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/635ed871-ac5d-59d6-89b7-22365d1d4c8f'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to new services that store data in the cloud, yet another stage of storage evolution has been reached: the celestial hard drive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/technology/personaltech/27basics.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to new services that store data in the cloud, yet another stage of storage evolution has been reached: the celestial hard drive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the old days of computing, you could carry only as many files as you had floppy disks. Then came hard drives and thumb drives, allowing those so inclined to carry entire digital encyclopedias in their pockets. Finally, thanks to new services that store data in the cloud, yet another stage of storage evolution (maybe the final one) has been reached: the celestial hard drive, a storage medium that exists solely in the electronic ether.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/BASICS/BASICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 955, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/BASICS/BASICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/business/BASICS/BASICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Your Files, Lots of Room In the Cloud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Your Files,