Budget Office, Douglas W. Elmendorf, has been appointed to a full four-year term by the House speaker, John A. Boehner of Ohio, and the Senate president pro tempore, Daniel K. Inouye of Hawaii, officials announced on Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'C.B.O. Director Appointed for Full Term', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:46:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herszenhorn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e110f8a5-5d08-5f73-b80c-ee75f9415738', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e110f8a5-5d08-5f73-b80c-ee75f9415738'}, {'abstract': 'From his first haute couture collections, in the mid-’90s, Jean Paul Gaultier has given a name to each outfit, usually indicating the mood we might expect.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/jean-paul-gaultier-black-magic/', 'snippet': 'From his first haute couture collections, in the mid-’90s, Jean Paul Gaultier has given a name to each outfit, usually indicating the mood we might expect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From his first haute couture collections, in the mid-’90s, Jean Paul Gaultier has given a name to each outfit, usually indicating the mood we might expect. Today, when I looked at his run-of-show and saw names like Le Chat Noir, Punk Is Not Dead and Moulin Rouge, naturally I figured we were in for a punk moment with nicer fishnets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jean Paul Gaultier: Black Magic', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:46:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2535e5-e659-52c2-b188-4ba8368ca441', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2535e5-e659-52c2-b188-4ba8368ca441'}, {'abstract': 'Levels found in the gulf in September — some five months after the oil spill — were extremely low, however, and past studies suggest that such concentrations do not pose a significant threat to sea life.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/oil-dispersants-lingered-in-deep-ocean-scientists-say/', 'snippet': 'Levels found in the gulf in September — some five months after the oil spill — were extremely low, however, and past studies suggest that such concentrations do not pose a significant threat to sea life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A crucial component of the chemical dispersant applied to oil gushing from BP’s blown-out well in the Gulf of Mexico last year did not break down as fast as scientists initially expected and probably remains at detectable levels in the deep ocean, scientists said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Dispersants Lingered in Deep Ocean, Scientists Say', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 