340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034ad24d-d7f1-59b4-af68-5067e29f1de9'}, {'abstract': 'Units created to care for the wounded after the Walter Reed Army Medical Center scandal struggle with staffing, training and too many medications, the Army inspector general said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/us/27warrior.html', 'snippet': 'Units created to care for the wounded after the Walter Reed Army Medical Center scandal struggle with staffing, training and too many medications, the Army inspector general said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Army units created to provide special care for wounded soldiers after the Walter Reed Army Medical Center scandal continue to struggle with short staffing, inadequate training and an overabundance of prescription medications, a report by the Army inspector general’s office said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Army Trauma Unit’s Woes Detailed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Army Trauma Unit’s Woes Detailed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reed, Walter, Army Medical Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T21:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35f05512-5162-5c01-b7e4-2059b600da23', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35f05512-5162-5c01-b7e4-2059b600da23'}, {'abstract': '“Could you suggest some middle-priced cruise lines that don’t cost an arm and a leg but manage to provide high-end dining and service?”', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/qa-a-mid-priced-cruise-with-high-end-service/', 'snippet': '“Could you suggest some middle-priced cruise lines that don’t cost an arm and a leg but manage to provide high-end dining and service?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cruising has always seemed fascinating to us because of the elegant meals and treatment advertised by the “top” cruise lines. However, we are daunted by the prices charged by these top-of-the-line carriers and would prefer something a little less expensive. Our problem is that the less expensive cruise lines seem to feature huge size, very active sports programs and dance-all-night activities. In other words, they are not so elegant. Could you suggest some middle-priced cruise lines that don’t cost an arm and a leg but manage to provide high-end dining and service? We are willing to go anywhere: Caribbean, Mediterranean, Asia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: A Mid-Priced Cruise With High-End Service', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T22:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rusha Haljuci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haljuci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/322b1507-b970-5455-bdc9-fe8903c520be', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/322b1507-b970-5455-bdc9-fe8903c520be'}, {'abstract': 'An unscientific study of Internet calling apps — all available for Android phones and iPhones — discovers strengths and weaknesses in the likes of Google Voice and Fring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/technology/personaltech/27pogue.html', 'snippet': 'An unscientific study of Internet calling apps — all available for Android phones and iPhones — discovers strengths and weaknesses in the likes of Google Voice and Fring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s e-mail bag brought a note that echoes the sentiments of many others:', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/06/01/technology/Pogue-190-for-Email/Pogue-190-for-Email-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/06/01/technology/Pogue-190-for-Email/Pogue-190-for-Email-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ins and Outs of Calling via the Net', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ins and Outs Of Calling Via the Net', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T22:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6994ee40-ca34-5586-93f7-737b7ec64813', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6994ee40-ca34-5586-93f7-737b7ec64813'}, {'abstract': 'It was a school project, and a quiet moment, that taught the 21-year-old freelance photographer Diana Markosian what to look for.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/stay-one-minute-longer-to-get-the-picture/', 'snippet': 'It was a school project, and a quiet moment, that taught the 21-year-old freelance photographer Diana Markosian what to look for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diana Markosian was born in Moscow and lived there until she was 9. She graduated from the University of Oregon and was a freelance journalist in China and Russia. In 2009, at the Columbia Journalism School, a professor introduced her to photography. Her pictures have since appeared in The Guardian and Vanity Fair and on Reuters. Now 21, she is back in Moscow. Her conversation with Kerri MacDonald for Turning Point has been condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stay One Minute Longer to Get the Picture', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T22:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f7fde8b-1719-5c46-b17d-d113c780ba27', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f7fde8b-1719-5c46-b17d-d113c780ba27'}, {'abstract': 'This was one of the most imaginative, uplifting Gaultier performances we’ve been treated to in a while.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/27/fashion/20110127-gaultier.html', 'snippet': 'This was one of the most imaginative, uplifting Gaultier performances we’ve been treated to in a while.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was one of the most imaginative, uplifting Gaultier performances we’ve been treated to in a while.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/fashion/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/fashion/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/fashion/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR/20110127-gaultier-slide-Z6UR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Haute Couture: Jean Paul Gaultier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T22:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d469dbf0-115d-5c26-bd5c-7f62b4acd36d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d469dbf0-115d-5c26-bd5c-7f62b4acd36d'}, {'abstract': 'Do the the Academy Awards help to perpetuate the growing irrelevance of world cinema in American movie culture?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/movies/awardsseason/30scott.html', 'snippet': 'Do the the Academy Awards help to perpetuate the growing irrelevance of world cinema in American movie culture?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the few surprises at the Golden Globes two weeks ago \x97 you’ll be forgiven if you’ve already forgotten about that odd little broadcast \x97 was the award given to “Carlos,” the French director Olivier Assayas’s five-hour-plus reconstruction of the life and career of the notorious terrorist of the 1970s and ’80s Carlos the Jackal. The award represented a high point of cosmopolitanism at a predictably parochial event: 11 languages spoken on screen; dozens of locations across Europe and the Middle East; a polyglot cast led by a Venezuelan star, Édgar Ramírez, who has the potential to become an international sex symbol. What more could you want from a foreign film?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/SCOTT-span/SCOTT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/SCOTT-span/SCOTT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/SCOTT-span/SCOTT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/SCOTT-span/SCOTT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/SCOTT-span/SCOTT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Golden Age of Foreign Films, Mostly Unseen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cinema Purgatorio', 'name': None, '