ividuals regarded as terrorist threats who cannot readily be brought to trial, usually because of concern that relevant evidence would compromise intelligence sources.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Proposes Easing Detentions in Terror Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain Proposes Easing Detentions in Terror Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-26T22:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd53ecc-f316-5f95-9f4e-06ac28fea87f', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd53ecc-f316-5f95-9f4e-06ac28fea87f'}, {'abstract': 'The architect and author of “Bohemian Modern” shopped for wall coverings with warm colors and bold patterns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/01/27/garden/20110127-shopping.html', 'snippet': 'The architect and author of “Bohemian Modern” shopped for wall coverings with warm colors and bold patterns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architect and author of “Bohemian Modern” shopped for wall coverings with warm colors and bold patterns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for Wall Coverings With Barbara Bestor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo':