 Texas financier R. Allen Stanford was incompetent to stand trial at this time on charges that he ran a $7 billion Ponzi scheme.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanford Ruled Incompetent to Stand Trial', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi Schemes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanford, Robert Allen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford Financial Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T00:45:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5901edb-17d6-54a4-b83b-6c714fae94ad', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5901edb-17d6-54a4-b83b-6c714fae94ad'}, {'abstract': 'Li Na plays top-seeded Caroline Wozniacki in the first women’s semifinal in Melbourne.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/semifinals-preview-li-vs-wozniacki/', 'snippet': 'Li Na plays top-seeded Caroline Wozniacki in the first women’s semifinal in Melbourne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Na plays top-seeded Caroline Wozniacki in the first women’s semifinal. The two played in the Round of 16 at the Australian Open last year, with Li Na winning convincingly by outhitting Wozniacki. She dominated Wozniacki from the first point, playing with sustained aggression and controlling court positioning throughout her straight-set victory. In that match, Wozniacki came up with a meager three winners, while Li Na struck 21 outright winners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Semifinal Preview: Li vs. Wozniacki', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T00:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f32c82a-aa00-5ddf-a85c-601c6ce05269', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f32c82a-aa00-5ddf-a85c-601c6ce05269'}, {'abstract': 'The News of the World tabloid said it found evidence linking the editor, Ian Edmondson, to allegations that the newspaper illegally intercepted celebrities’ telephone messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/europe/27hacking.html', 'snippet': 'The News of the World tabloid said it found evidence linking the editor, Ian Edmondson, to allegations that the newspaper illegally intercepted celebrities’ telephone messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON \x97 The News of the World tabloid said on Wednesday that it had dismissed its assistant editor for news, Ian Edmondson, after finding “material evidence” linking him to allegations that the newspaper illegally intercepted celebrities’ telephone messages. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Tabloid Dismisses Editor Over Hacking Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Editor\nIs Dismissed\nIn Scandal\nOver Hacking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'},