, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e0a22cb4-596f-5582-aac9-9f1e5b8c1a46', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e0a22cb4-596f-5582-aac9-9f1e5b8c1a46'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans on the government panel investigating the financial crisis said the inquiry had too domestic a focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/business/economy/27inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans on the government panel investigating the financial crisis said the inquiry had too domestic a focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 The government commission’s account of what caused the 2008 financial crisis offers a broad indictment of regulatory weakness, Wall Street avarice and corporate incompetence. But that narrative is competing with alternative views by the Republicans on the panel, who released their dissenting reports on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Inquiry/Inquiry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissenters Fault Report on Crisis in Finance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dissenters Fault Report On Crisis In Finance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T01:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f19f7018-d589-57ab-8d01-7e196834f38a', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19f7018-d589-57ab-8d01-7e196834f38a'}, {'abstract': 'The Kellogg Company is doing something that goes against the grain: selling cereal to American adults solely on the claim of being tasty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/business/media/27adco.html', 'snippet': 'The Kellogg Company is doing something that goes against the grain: selling cereal to American adults solely on the claim of being tasty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT sets adult cereal apart from most other foods is that, oddly, it is rarely advertised primarily on the promise of tasting good. Special K, for example, is marketed as a dieting aid for women who eat it throughout the day, while Wheaties promises to fuel athletic performance and Fiber One promotes the digestive benefits of a high-fiber diet. Although popular adult cereals make secondary claims about being toothsome, of course, the primary pitch is for healthfulness.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did We Mention That It Tastes Good?', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Did We Mention That It Tastes Good?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kellogg Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cereals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T01:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bfdc333-0eb7-5438-83c5-b83e4a91a762', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bfdc333-0eb7-5438-83c5-b83e4a91a762'}, {'abstract': 'NBC Universal’s chief executive will try to revive the NBC lineup and end the public discord that was often more interesting than the network’s shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/business/media/27nbc.html', 'snippet': 'NBC Universal’s chief executive will try to revive the NBC lineup and end the public discord that was often more interesting than the network’s shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, from Studio 6B in Rockefeller Center, home of “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon,” the NBC anchor Brian Williams will officially introduce the network’s newest boss, Stephen B. Burke, in a closed-circuit presentation to the entire company.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/27NBC/27NBC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/27NBC/27NBC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/business/27NBC/27NBC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Less Drama at NBC', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Less Drama at NBC', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T01:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a887bae-6aa9-5bce-91fd-e305df325165', 'word_count': 1540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a887bae-6aa9-5bce-91fd-e305df325165'}, {'abstract': 'A day after winning their respective quarterfinal matches, Kim Clijsters faces Vera Zvonareva in the Australian Open semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/semifinals-preview-clijsters-vs-zvonareva/', 'snippet': 'A day after winning their respective quarterfinal matches, Kim Clijsters faces Vera Zvonareva in the Australian Open semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after winning their quarterfinal matches, Kim Clijsters faces Vera Zvonareva in the Australian Open semifinals on Thursday. Clijsters trounced Zvonareva in the United States Open final last September, in a match that clearly showed Zvonareva had rattled nerves on the big stage. The Russian tried to outhit Clijsters in that match, and never really put Clijsters under any pressure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Semifinal Preview: Clijsters vs. Zvonareva', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T01:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80f4a73-af48-5acd-8f33-ffe367c74059', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80f4a73-af48-5acd-8f33-ffe367c74059'}, {'abstract': 'Even as their leaders insist on the need for military cuts, divisions have opened among Republicans about how to chop Pentagon spending that comes to more than a half trillion dollars a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/us/politics/27pentagon.html', 'snippet': 'Even as their leaders insist on the need for military cuts, divisions have opened among Republicans about how to chop Pentagon spending that comes to more than a half trillion dollars a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — To hear the Republican leadership tell it, the once-sacred Pentagon budget, protected by the party for generations, is suddenly on the table. But a closer look shows that even as Speaker John A. Boehner and Representative Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, insist on the need for military cuts, divisions have opened among Republicans about whether, and how much, to chop Pentagon spending that comes to more than a half trillion dollars a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/us/jp-PENTAGON-1/jp-PENTAGON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/27/us/jp-PENTAGON-1/jp-PENTAGON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/us/jp-PENTAGON-1/jp-PENTAGON-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/us/jp-PENTAGON-1/jp-PENTAGON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/us/jp-PENTAGON-1/jp-PENTAGON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Splits Over Plans to Cut Defense Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Is Split As It Weighs Military Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'majo