st be published in the state’s register, which will make them effective. Ms. Martinez had forbidden the register from publishing the rules. “No one is above the law,” the state’s chief justice, Charles W. Daniels, said as he announced the decision. The dairy industry had opposed a rule by the New Mexico Water Quality Commission requiring that all manure lagoons incorporate a synthetic liner to keep contaminants from leaching into the groundwater. Officials of the state’s Environment Department have estimated that two-thirds of such ponds have contaminated groundwater beneath them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Mexico: Court Overrules Governor on Pollutants', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTHWEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Mexico: Court Overrules Governor on Pollutants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Susana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/adca4aa7-6bf3-58f4-9898-8e9d9b80830a', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adca4aa7-6bf3-58f4-9898-8e9d9b80830a'}, {'abstract': 'Deutsche Bank foreclosed on the home of Sgt. James B. Hurley and his wife in violation of a law intended to protect service members from such actions while they are overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/business/27foreclose.html', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Bank foreclosed on the home of Sgt. James B. Hurley and his wife in violation of a law intended to protect service members from such actions while they are overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Sgt. James B. Hurley was away at war, he lost a heartbreaking battle at home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/FORECLOSE/FORECLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/27/business/FORECLOSE/FORECLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/FORECLOSE/FORECLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/business/FORECLOSE/FORECLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/business/FORECLOSE/FORECLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reservist in a New War, Against Foreclosure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Reservist in a New War, Against Foreclosure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diana B. Henriques', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c0f37f3-dc12-51ff-9b23-ed1c4b9541a7', 'word_count': 1544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c0f37f3-dc12-51ff-9b23-ed1c4b9541a7'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court in Richmond, Va., announced Wednesday that it would expedite its consideration of a lower court ruling against a key provision of the Obama health care act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/health/policy/27brfs-QUICKRULINGP_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court in Richmond, Va., announced Wednesday that it would expedite its consideration of a lower court ruling against a key provision of the Obama health care act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court in Richmond, Va., announced Wednesday that it would expedite its consideration of a lower court ruling against a key provision of the Obama health care act. The Court of Appeals for the Fourth Circuit said it would hear arguments between May 10 and May 13 in the Obama administration’s appeal of a ruling last month by Judge Howard E. Hudson of Federal District Court in Richmond. Judge Hudson ruled that Congress had exceeded the boundaries of the Commerce Clause of the Constitution by requiring citizens to obtain commercial insurance. He allowed the law to remain in effect pending appeals, which are likely to end at the Supreme Court. Two other federal judges have upheld the insurance requirement, while a fourth judge, in Florida, is expected to rule soon. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: Quick Ruling Promised on Challenge to Health Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia: Quick Ruling Promised On Challenge to Health Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interstate Commerce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e8e5335-2466-57b3-a4c8-eb1452f06712', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e8e5335-2466-57b3-a4c8-eb1452f06712'}, {'abstract': 'The World Economic Forum conference in Davos, Switzerland, is well known for its confusing profusion of discussions and events. Here to help is DealBook’s handy slide-show guide to the highlights of Day 1.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/highlights-of-davos-day-1/', 'snippet': 'The World Economic Forum conference in Davos, Switzerland, is well known for its confusing profusion of discussions and events. Here to help is DealBook’s handy slide-show guide to the highlights of Day 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Economic Forum is well known for its profusion of discussions and events — so much so that it is overwhelming and confusing to observers. Here to help is DealBook’s handy slide-show guide to the highlights of Davos, Day 1. Click through and explore — without the headaches of information overload.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights of Davos, Day 1', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tzyh Ng', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tzyh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ng', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8484b211-7275-530d-bdba-f680b667793b', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8484b211-7275-530d-bdba-f680b667793b'}, {'abstract': 'Rodney Alcala, a serial murderer who is on death row in California, was charged with killing two women in the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/nyregion/27unsolved.html', 'snippet': 'Rodney Alcala, a serial murderer who is on death row in California, was charged with killing two women in the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One victim, Cornelia Michel Crilley, was a Trans World Airlines flight attendant who was raped and strangled in her Upper East Side apartment in 1971; the other, Ellen Jane Hover, an aspiring orchestra conductor who disappeared one summer day in 1977 — and whose remains were found nearly a year later on the Rockefeller estate in Westchester County.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/nyregion/27unsolved_337/27unsolved_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/nyregion/27unsolved_337/27unsolved_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Decades, Charges in 2 Manhattan Murders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Decades, Charges In 2 Manhattan Murders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcab601c-d3d7-5759-b5b7-55eee5b4b280', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcab601c-d3d7-5759-b5b7-55eee5b4b280'}, {'abstract': 'The Illinois Supreme Court has said it will consider Rahm Emanuel’s case as he tries to remain on the mayoral ballot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/us/27chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The Illinois Supreme Court has said it will consider Rahm Emanuel’s case as he tries to remain on the mayoral ballot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO \x97 The candidates for mayor, scores of election workers, and, perhaps most of all, this city’s confused voters received no new clarity on Wednesday on whether Rahm Emanuel would be permitted to run for mayor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Candidates, and Chicago, Await Ruling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Candidates, And Chicago, Await Ruling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06db4734-b4b4-5c04-9a82-a4dee53787ed', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06db4734-b4b4-5c04-9a82-a4dee53787ed'}, {'abstract': 'At a fund-raiser, the general manager spoke of Andy Pettitte, the Red Sox and Derek Jeter.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/26/cashman-pours-drinks-and-talks-yankees/', 'snippet': 'At a fund-raiser, the general manager spoke of Andy Pettitte, the Red Sox and Derek Jeter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yankees General Manager Brian Cashman donned his spiked hair/bandana hairpiece and assumed his celebrity bartender persona — Hard Cash — at Foley’s Pub and Restaurant on Wednesday to pour drinks and help raise money to fight cancer (his father-in-law died of the disease). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cashman Pours Drinks and Talks Yankees', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T02:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aefdab86-bc9e-50cc-b781-3ab455f78d14', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aefdab86-bc9e-50cc-b781-3ab455f78d14'}, {'abstract': 'Hosni Mubarak’s traditional opponents have been displaced by the leaderless tens of thousands of young Egyptians who turned out this week to demand an end to his 30-year rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/27opposition.html', 'snippet': 'Hosni Mubarak’s traditional opponents have been displaced by the leaderless tens of thousands of young Egyptians who turned out this week to demand an end to his 30-year rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, Egypt’s authoritarian president, Hosni Mubarak, played a clever game with his political opponents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/world/middleeast/20100126-slide-PEVT/20100126-slide-PEVT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/26/world/middleeast/20100126-slide-PEVT/20100126-slide-PEVT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thum