y tense and applause sparing, John Boehner was restless in the speaker’s chair during President Obama’s State of the Union address. A few minutes after it was over, Mr. Boehner made his impatience explicit with a statement accusing Mr. Obama of having “accelerated the job-destroying spending spree in Washington.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Realism Without the Bitterness', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Realism Without the Bitterness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f93c886-30e4-5efd-a2b7-d9004321727f', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f93c886-30e4-5efd-a2b7-d9004321727f'}, {'abstract': 'We sympathize with the anger that is drawing tens of thousands of Egyptians to demonstrate in the streets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/27thu2.html', 'snippet': 'We sympathize with the anger that is drawing tens of thousands of Egyptians to demonstrate in the streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We sympathize with the frustration and anger that is drawing tens of thousands of Egyptians into the streets of Cairo and other cities this week, the country’s largest demonstrations in years. Citizens of one of the Arab world’s great nations, they struggle with poverty \x97 40 percent live on less than $2 a day \x97 rising food prices, unemployment and political repression. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Mubarak Is Put on Notice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Mubarak Is Put on Notice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfcccac5-ad44-5dbc-bd9d-cc5931f05e50', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfcccac5-ad44-5dbc-bd9d-cc5931f05e50'}, {'abstract': 'A new brand of crazy in the land has politicians scrambling to introduce guns into every conceivable part of American life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/27collins.html', 'snippet': 'A new brand of crazy in the land has politicians scrambling to introduce guns into every conceivable part of American life.', 'lead_paragraph': ' This week in Washington, Senator Frank Lautenberg of New Jersey introduced three very modest gun regulation bills, including one making it more difficult to sell guns to people on the terror watch list.', 'print_section': 