ng influence and power in Albany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/lweb27albany.html', 'snippet': 'Letter to the editor regarding influence and power in Albany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Influence in Albany', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Influence in Albany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANY (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d849d581-a9ad-56b6-9b44-7dd465b07ebf', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d849d581-a9ad-56b6-9b44-7dd465b07ebf'}, {'abstract': 'A court ruling that upheld a college admissions plan that considers race should give confidence to all universities about seeking diversity and merit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/27thu3.html', 'snippet': 'A court ruling that upheld a college admissions plan that considers race should give confidence to all universities about seeking diversity and merit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifteen years ago, the United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit flouted Supreme Court law when it struck down affirmative action at the University of Texas Law School. Last week, in an act of redemption, the appellate court upheld an admissions plan for undergraduates at the University of Texas at Austin that takes race into account to encourage diversity. The plan was adopted after the Supreme Court again approved affirmative action in higher education in 2003. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Nation, Indivisible', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Nation, Indivisible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Equal Educational Opportunities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/105c0f73-86eb-563e-8887-7c9e6239ed50', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/105c0f73-86eb-563e-8887-7c9e6239ed50'}, {'abstract': 'Most big banks appeared to be profitable in 2010. But even standout results were underwhelming on closer inspection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/opinion/27thu1.html', 'snippet': 'Most big banks appeared to be profitable in 2010. But even standout results were underwhelming on closer inspection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the exception of Bank of America, the big banks were profitable in 2010, according to year-end reports filed earlier this month. But even standout results \x97 like JPMorgan Chase’s profit surge or Citigroup’s first full-year profit since the financial crisis \x97 were underwhelming on closer inspection. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Was It a Good Year?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Was It a Good Year?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/617c6488-6874-52e5-a72c-63855d30ca1e', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/617c6488-6874-52e5-a72c-63855d30ca1e'}, {'abstract': 'The most popular fast food in Berlin, currywurst, a greasy pile of pork sausage smothered in ketchup and sprinkled with curry powder, embodies the city’s contradictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/europe/27berlin.html', 'snippet': 'The most popular fast food in Berlin, currywurst, a greasy pile of pork sausage smothered in ketchup and sprinkled with curry powder, embodies the city’s contradictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — There is no shortage of contradictions when it comes to this city. Like the rest of Germany, Berlin demands conformity to certain rules (think twice about crossing against the light), but leaves moral judgments up to the individual (no problem with nude bathing in public parks or gambling in storefront casinos).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/world/27BERLIN/27BERLIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/27/world/27BERLIN/27BERLIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/world/27BERLIN/27BERLIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/world/27BERLIN/27BERLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/world/27BERLIN/27BERLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'National Dish Comes Wrapped in Foreign Flavoring', 'kicker': 'Berlin Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Favorite Dish Laden With Fat and Contradiction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curry (Cuisine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Slackman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slackman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6f76af-bf83-5fa3-a461-c89897d7a203', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6f76af-bf83-5fa3-a461-c89897d7a203'}, {'abstract': 'After a year in which he did not win a tournament, Tiger Woods will open his season in the familiar surroundings of Torrey Pines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/sports/golf/27tiger.html', 'snippet': 'After a year in which he did not win a tournament, Tiger Woods will open his season in the familiar surroundings of Torrey Pines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Tiger Woods returned to familiarity on Wednesday, to the fairways and greens of Torrey Pines Golf Course, comfortable confines that are etched in his mind like the layout of his childhood home some 90 miles north in Cypress.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/TIGERfloater/TIGERfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/TIGERfloater/TIGERfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/sports/TIGERfloater/TIGERfloater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 878, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woods Says He’s Ready to Return to Tour, and to Winning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woods Says He’s Ready to Return to Tour, and to Winning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Torrey Pines Golf Course', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88cbf2ba-1a06-5796-8a82-d72af1688359', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88cbf2ba-1a06-5796-8a82-d72af1688359'}, {'abstract': 'Four Palestinians were charged on Wednesday with the murder of an American tourist, Kristine Luken, who was killed in a forest outside Jerusalem in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/27briefs-Israel.html', 'snippet': 'Four Palestinians were charged on Wednesday with the murder of an American tourist, Kristine Luken, who was killed in a forest outside Jerusalem in December.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Four Palestinians were charged on Wednesday with the murder of an American tourist, Kristine Luken, who was killed in a forest outside Jerusalem in December. Ms. Luken, an evangelical Christian in her mid-40s, had been hiking with a friend who was also stabbed, but survived. Micky Rosenfeld, a police spokesman, said that the attackers came from the West Bank, and that they were suspected of at least one other murder. One of the group said that the attacks began as revenge for the killing of a senior Hamas official in a Dubai hotel room a year ago, Mr. Rosenfeld said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: 4 Palestinians Charged in Killing of U.S. Woman', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: 4 Palestinians Charged in Killing of U.S. Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:53:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8b02283-6dce-550a-a820-07c831d3d95b', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8b02283-6dce-550a-a820-07c831d3d95b'}, {'abstract': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev dismissed a federal transit police official, seeking to shake up the security apparatus for failing to stop the suicide bombing at an airport on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/27webbriefs-Russiatransit.html', 'snippet': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev dismissed a federal transit police official, seeking to shake up the security apparatus for failing to stop the suicide bombing at an airport on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Dmitri A. Medvedev on Wednesday dismissed the federal transit police official in charge of the Moscow region, seeking to shake up the security apparatus for failing to stop the suicide bombing at the capital’s busiest international airport on Monday. “I believe that in general, transport security \x97 and not just because of the terrorist act that occurred \x97 is unsatisfactory,” Mr. Medvedev said. He did not directly criticize any of his own top security aides, instead continuing to focus blame on the lower ranks. Police officials in charge of security at the airport itself were also dismissed. Investigators continued to search for the organizers of the bombing, which killed at least 35 people and wounded scores of others. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Transit Police Official Fired in Wake of Bombing', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Transit Police Official Fired in Wake of Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T03:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford J. Levy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Levy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4fa69c-ca13-5785-856e-e3da380e12fb', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4fa69c-ca13-5785-856e-e3da380e12fb'}, {'abstract': 'An explosion at a coal mine in northeastern Colombia killed as many as 20 miners and left six injured, according to a statement from the Colombian Institute of Geology and Mining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/world/americas/27webbriefs-Columbia.html', 'snippet': 'An explosion at a coal mine in northeastern Colombia killed as many as 20 miners and left six injured, according to a statement from the Colombian Institute of Geology and Mining.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An explosion at a coal mine in northeastern Colombia killed as many as 20 miners and left six injured, according to a statement from the Colombian Institute of Geology and Mining. The disaster was caused by the release of methane gas that led to a blast and a cave-in. Dozens of people were killed in similar accidents last year in Colombia, South America’s largest coal producer. More than 30 miners died at the same mine, called La Preciosa, in 2007. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colombia: Coal Mine Explosion Kills as Many as 20', 'kicker': 'WORLD BRIEFING | THE A