neral public. Lande gained his experience as a former scout and front-office executive. Before joining The Sporting News, he spent three years as a college scout for the Cleveland Browns. The Footballguys.com staff writer and Rookie Scouting Portfolio author Matt Waldman sat down with Lande after Day 3 of Senior Bowl practices to discuss the craft of talent evaluation and what he has observed with this class of players in Mobile, Ala. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With N.F.L. Talent Evaluator Russ Lande', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T11:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Waldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3a72bc8-2f13-52b4-957a-0177734b1410', 'word_count': 1890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3a72bc8-2f13-52b4-957a-0177734b1410'}, {'abstract': 'The “Ancient Czech Legends” exhibition at the National Museum in Prague is a child-friendly show that explores vampires, knights and wild boars.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/exploring-ancient-czech-legends-in-prague/', 'snippet': 'The “Ancient Czech Legends” exhibition at the National Museum in Prague is a child-friendly show that explores vampires, knights and wild boars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interactive exhibitions for children are a rarity in Prague, so it was with great relish that a group of boys and girls took a recent run around the National Museum with a taxidermic boar on their backs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Ancient Czech Legends in Prague', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T11:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dinah Spritzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dinah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spritzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c135fe1d-cac9-5c4c-86d2-1889a5b42f31', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c135fe1d-cac9-5c4c-86d2-1889a5b42f31'}, {'abstract': 'David Kato, the activist, was one of the most visible defenders of gay rights in a country where leaders have proposed executing gay people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/africa/28uganda.html', 'snippet': 'David Kato, the activist, was one of the most visible defenders of gay rights in a country where leaders have proposed executing gay people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya \x97 David Kato knew he was a marked man.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/world/africa/28uganda-2/28uganda-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/world/africa/28uganda-2/28uganda-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'