uch, instead of making yourself sick, you risk making your customers sick of you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I sat around with six important people in my business and discussed our marketing plan for 2011. We determined that we need to get more e-mail addresses from our customers so that we can send them promotions more efficiently. We want to avoid the printing and postage costs of direct mail promotions, which will be good for us, for the customers and for the environment. Sorry, printers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Often Can You Send E-Mail Promotions?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T12:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ffece0-0a9b-5218-9e4d-e3e5a93408ab', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ffece0-0a9b-5218-9e4d-e3e5a93408ab'}, {'abstract': 'Here are the players we believe notably increased or decreased their standing among talent evaluators for the N.F.L. draft.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/senior-bowl-day-3-risers-fallers-and-steady-as-they-go/', 'snippet': 'Here are the players we believe notably increased or decreased their standing among talent evaluators for the N.F.L. draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cecil Lammey is a senior staff writer for Footballguys.com and the NFL Insider for the Front Range Sports Network. Matt Waldman