ectric bring to the table?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/is-a-multinational-c-e-o-the-best-jobs-czar/', 'snippet': 'Multinationals have a bad record of job growth in the United States. Given his company’s views on corporate tax policy and job creation, what will Jeffrey Immelt of General Electric bring to the table?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of Jeffrey Immelt‘s ascent to the chairmanship of President Obama‘s jobs council, some commentators have questioned whether the leader of General Electric, a company that has sharply reduced its United States payrolls over the years, is the best person to be orchestrating a jobs revival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Multinational C.E.O. the Best Jobs Czar?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outsourcing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Immelt, Jeffrey R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/08602c95-c36c-5715-89ba-04e067a22c46', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08602c95-c36c-5715-89ba-04e067a22c46'}, {'abstract': 'The wave of protests against autocratic governments in the Arab world has now spread to Yemen. Video of a large demonstration in the capital, Sana, has been posted online by Al Jazeera.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/video-of-protests-in-yemen/', 'snippet': 'The wave of protests against autocratic governments in the Arab world has now spread to Yemen. Video of a large demonstration in the capital, Sana, has been posted online by Al Jazeera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 2:53 p.m. As my colleagues Nada Bakri and David Goodman report, the wave of protests against autocratic governments in the Arab world has now spread to Yemen, where thousands of people took to the streets of the capital Sana on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Protests in Yemen', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f158db46-0616-5557-a3d5-c9a18d8dda93', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f158db46-0616-5557-a3d5-c9a18d8dda93'}, {'abstract': 'New charges for a serial killer already on death row in California; what is thundersnow;  a possible overhaul for the city’s airports and more in Morning Buzz.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/morning-buzz-3/', 'snippet': 'New charges for a serial killer already on death row in California; what is thundersnow;  a possible overhaul for the city’s airports and more in Morning Buzz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No school for the city’s students, but commuters should check transportation advisories before heading out the door.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dating Game’ Killer Charged With Two Murders From the 1970s', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ac2f4f3-6bb8-57fb-8ba1-a2ee9762c8e7', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ac2f4f3-6bb8-57fb-8ba1-a2ee9762c8e7'}, {'abstract': 'Industry news this week spanned nearly 130 years, with a notable anniversary for Mercedes-Benz and a potential tax rebate for electric-vehicle shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/wheelies-ghosts-of-industrys-past-present-and-future-edition/', 'snippet': 'Industry news this week spanned nearly 130 years, with a notable anniversary for Mercedes-Benz and a potential tax rebate for electric-vehicle shoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: Ghosts of Industry’s Past, Present and Future Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daimler-Benz AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZAP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33c539d-e2ab-5c7d-ad19-ec569435e7ca', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33c539d-e2ab-5c7d-ad19-ec569435e7ca'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Jackson stepped in last year to direct the “Hobbit” films, then fought a pitched battle against labor unions in New Zealand and Australia that were seeking to ban the project.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/another-delay-for-the-hobbit-as-jackson-recovers-from-ulcer-surgery/', 'snippet': 'Peter Jackson stepped in last year to direct the “Hobbit” films, then fought a pitched battle against labor unions in New Zealand and Australia that were seeking to ban the project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’d recently taken on the weighty assignment of directing two movies adapted from J. R. R. Tolkien‘s “Hobbit,” then defended that project during a potentially catastrophic labor crisis, you might be under some stress, too. So have sympathy for Peter Jackson, who will likely take some time off from that mammoth fantasy franchise after undergoing surgery for a perforated ulcer. Melissa Booth, a publicist for Mr. Jackson, told Agence France-Presse that the filmmaker had been experiencing stomach pains and on Wednesday night was admitted to Wellington Hospital in New Zealand, where doctors gave him the diagnosis and operated on him. Mr. Jackson, the Academy Award-winning director of the “Lord of the Rings” movies, stepped in last year to direct the “Hobbit” films after Guillermo del Toro withdrew, then fought a pitched battle against labor unions in New Zealand and Australia over hiring practices, with Mr. Jackson warning he could move the films out of New Zealand if the unions did not back down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Delay for ‘The Hobbit’ as Jackson Recovers From Ulcer Surgery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c5eefe-2f3a-5ce5-9f62-d7134d5fc360', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c5eefe-2f3a-5ce5-9f62-d7134d5fc360'}, {'abstract': 'We all cobble together an internal account of our lives; in that, Dad was entirely typical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/books/excerpt-my-father-at-100.html', 'snippet': 'We all cobble together an internal account of our lives; in that, Dad was entirely typical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduction', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Father at 100’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By RON REAGAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'REAGAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/31709e7c-6013-5091-ad36-19e94cea08d3', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31709e7c-6013-5091-ad36-19e94cea08d3'}, {'abstract': '“My Father at 100,” a deeply felt memoir by Ron Reagan, underscores the bafflement Ronald Reagan’s own children often felt about their father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/books/28book.html', 'snippet': '“My Father at 100,” a deeply felt memoir by Ron Reagan, underscores the bafflement Ronald Reagan’s own children often felt about their father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronald Reagan, the politician, has been enshrined as a heroic visionary by the right, celebrated for ending the cold war and reducing the size of government, and invoked as a touchstone for all things conservative. At the same time, he’s been caricatured by the left as the dunderheaded godfather of a red-state America, promoting lower taxes for the rich, higher deficits and a more fragile social safety net. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28BOOK-1/JP-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28BOOK-1/JP-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28BOOK-1/JP-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ronald Reagan as Dad, a Sunny Stranger', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ronald Reagan as Dad, A Sunny Stranger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Prescott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d8ee6bd-5da1-514c-940e-8551410df851', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d8ee6bd-5da1-514c-940e-8551410df851'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney said the president was “cavalier” about the country’s economic problems and “doesn’t know what to do.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/romney-calls-obama-sad-and-cavalier/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney said the president was “cavalier” about the country’s economic problems and “doesn’t know what to do.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watch the latest video at video.foxnews.com', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Calls Obama ‘Cavalier’ on Lost Jobs', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:22:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_n