27/amazonian-giant-comes-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Sustainable paiche, one of the world’s largest fish, is on the menu at Sushi Samba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the oldest, largest freshwater fish in the world — which breathes air and can spring out of the water — has landed in New York restaurants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazonian Giant Comes to New York', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d11cbf6-ea4c-5972-88c6-f708d1298049', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d11cbf6-ea4c-5972-88c6-f708d1298049'}, {'abstract': 'The not-so-commanding heights.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/not-in-davos/', 'snippet': 'The not-so-commanding heights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year at this time the great and the good — and a lot of bankers, too — gather in Davos for the World Economic Forum. I do it on rare occasions, but mostly not; I was supposed to be at the MIT 150th Anniversary conference, but Amtrak let me down, and I’m about to straggle back to New Jersey from New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not In Davos', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c769e2cc-de4d-548f-a493-a7e60c91e836', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c769e2cc-de4d-548f-a493-a7e60c91e836'}, {'abstract': 'The Nelson Mandela Foundation said that the former South African leader is hospitalized but “is in no danger and is in good spirits.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/africa/28safrica.html', 'snippet': 'The Nelson Mandela Foundation said that the former South African leader is hospitalized but “is in no danger and is in good spirits.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG \x97 Nelson Mandela, the beloved but increasingly frail hero of South African democracy, remained hospitalized for a second day here on Thursday for what his foundation called “routine tests.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speculation Over Mandela’s Hospitalization', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mandela’s Hospital Stay Stirs Speculation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuma, Jacob G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madikizela-Mandela, Winnie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:49:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia W. Dugger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dugger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cdf8002-81f1-59fe-8fc3-8f1b2616c497', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cdf8002-81f1-59fe-8fc3-8f1b2616c497'}, {'abstract': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy of France warned anyone betting against the euro to watch out, while several corporate chiefs argued that without the single currency Europe would be in much worse shape right now.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/defending-the-euro-at-davos/', 'snippet': 'President Nicolas Sarkozy of France warned anyone betting against the euro to watch out, while several corporate chiefs argued that without the single currency Europe would be in much worse shape right now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — There is no shortage of euro skepticism at the World Economic Forum this year, but the beleaguered single currency had its defenders as well on Thursday, ranging from President Nicolas Sarkozy of France to Jamie Dimon, chief executive of JPMorgan Chase.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending the Euro at Davos', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T14:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b14963c0-aeb6-5523-9b71-843dddfee4c4', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b14963c0-aeb6-5523-9b71-843dddfee4c4'}, {'abstract': 'Term in China for cramped and expensive housing. (Also translated as “narrow dwellings.”)', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/snail-houses/', 'snippet': 'Term in China for cramped and expensive housing. (Also translated as “narrow dwellings.”)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Term in China for cramped housing. (Also translated as “narrow dwellings.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snail Houses', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/40456c5f-903b-5dcc-8efd-c4b563634820', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40456c5f-903b-5dcc-8efd-c4b563634820'}, {'abstract': 'Our favorites from the biannual trade show Capsule, which features ready-to-wear looks inspired from the men’s shows in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/a-capsule-summary/', 'snippet': 'Our favorites from the biannual trade show Capsule, which features ready-to-wear looks inspired from the men’s shows in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While dispatches were pouring in from the men’s shows in Europe announcing fur and color as big trends for fall, we perused the racks at the biannual trade show Capsule here in New York for a taste of what to expect in stores. There are some crossovers (hunting gear, Fair Isle, an aristocratic influence, among them), but for the most part, designers favored a pared-down aesthetic punctuated with rich knits. Here, our favorites, in an interactive display.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Capsule Summary', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc592d8f-1219-57ce-9f90-23c42cda1992', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc592d8f-1219-57ce-9f90-23c42cda1992'}, {'abstract': 'For many customers, roller rinks are like opening a dusty photo album from the attic and welcoming back a flood of memories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/nyregion/28roller.html', 'snippet': 'For many customers, roller rinks are like opening a dusty photo album from the attic and welcoming back a flood of memories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STATEN ISLAND had been without a roller rink for 22 years when Joe Costa opened RollerJam USA in Tottenville in 2007. He said he was simply trying to meet demand, but he also found that for many of his customers, it was as if he had opened a dusty photo album from the attic, welcoming back a flood of memories.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/ROLLER/ROLLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/ROLLER/ROLLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/ROLLER/ROLLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/ROLLER/ROLLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/ROLLER/ROLLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bit of the Disco Era Has Rolled Back Into Town', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bit of the Disco Era Has Rolled Back Into Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roller Skating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b26e73bf-be71-525a-b257-c88cc5872e69', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26e73bf-be71-525a-b257-c88cc5872e69'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Bettany now says he wishes he hadn’t turned down the role that went to Colin Firth, while Harvey Weinstein regrets all the swearing.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/a-few-regrets-for-kings-speech/', 'snippet': 'Paul Bettany now says he wishes he hadn’t turned down the role that went to Colin Firth, while Harvey Weinstein regrets all the swearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The Bagger is back in the warm, smoggy embrace of the city of angels, to report all your awards news without the distraction of earnest first-time filmmakers or hot tubs in the snow. Here’s some of the latest:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Few Regrets for ‘King’s Speech’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettany, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Firth, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/982a4e2e-da6e-55a8-ae08-59e9126d3ad0', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/982a4e2e-da6e-55a8-ae08-59e9126d3ad0'}, {'abstract': 'This week we pair the poem “Picasso” with an obituary of the artist Corneille.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/poetry-pairing-jan-27-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week we pair the poem “Picasso” with an obituary of the artist Corneille.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | Jan. 27, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c282177-b891-5eb4-bfab-5ef2d8c0712a', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c282177-b891-5eb4-bfab-5ef2d8c0712a'}, {'abstract': 'The author’s fondness for Burger King, Tim Henman and the Three Tenors are among the personal details revealed in letters recently made public by the University of East Anglia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/ketchup-in-the-rye-j-d-salingers-favorite-hamburger-revealed/', 'snippet': 'The author’s fondness for Burger King, Tim Henman and the Three Tenors are among the personal details revealed in letters recently made public by the University of East Anglia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How’s this for a fast food slogan: “Have It Your Way, Even if You’re the Reclusive Author of What Some Would Argue Is the Greatest Novel of the 20th Century.” It might not fit on a Burger King wrapper, but the Home of the Whopper can now also bill itself as the sometime home of J. D. Salinger, who expressed his preference for that hamburger chain in letters that were recently made public by the University of East Anglia in Britain, The Guardian reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ketchup on the Rye: J. D. Salinger’s Favorite Hamburger Revealed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salinger, J D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T15:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/27961325-aff0-58dd-b5dc-4dfa72ff344c', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27961325-aff0-58dd-b5dc-4dfa72ff344c'}, {'abstract': 'If successful, an offering would make Prada the only European luxury group and the only Italian company to list in Hong Kong.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/prada-plans-i-p-o-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'If successful, an offering would make Prada the only European luxury group and the only Italian company to list in Hong Kong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prada, the Italian fashion group, will go ahead with plans for an initial public offering in Hong Kong, the company said on Thursday, hoping that an outreach to investors that has been delayed for almost a decade will finally succeed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prada Plans I.P.O. in Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value