ine corporate tax system.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/winners-and-losers-under-the-u-s-corporate-tax-code/', 'snippet': 'A look at which industries and companies fare best under the nation’s byzantine corporate tax system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague Binyamin Appelbaum has an article today on the challenges of reforming the corporate tax code, which currently presents a wide disparity in its treatment of different industries and individual companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winners and Losers Under the U.S. Corporate Tax Code', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Martin A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4686312-8549-5105-97a6-b712ae7fa0d6', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4686312-8549-5105-97a6-b712ae7fa0d6'}, {'abstract': 'The return of Wanda Jackson, the Queen of Rockabilly; also, Ben Ratliff breaks down the latest album by Destroyer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/popcast-the-return-of-wanda-jackson-and-a-new-destroyer-album/', 'snippet': 'The return of Wanda Jackson, the Queen of Rockabilly; also, Ben Ratliff breaks down the latest album by Destroyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week on Popcast, The Times’s weekly music podcast, Melena Ryzik discusses her Arts & Leisure profile of Wanda Jackson, the 73-year-old Queen of Rockabilly. Ms. Jackson started her career alongside her onetime boyfriend Elvis Presley, became a born-again Christian and now — still growling and swiveling her hips onstage — has a new album produced by Jack White that she hopes will introduce her to a new audience. “You can’t hardly name anything that I haven’t experienced somewhere along the way,” she told Ms.\xa0 Ryzik in her interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: The Return of Wanda Jackson and a New Destroyer Album', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Wanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Destroyer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a96b1ad-f05b-5841-981e-01e7d0ab2909', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a96b1ad-f05b-5841-981e-01e7d0ab2909'}, {'abstract': 'The return of Wanda Jackson, the Queen of Rockabilly; also, Ben Ratliff breaks down the latest album by Destroyer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/popcast-the-return-of-wanda-jackson-and-a-new-destroyer-album/', 'snippet': 'The return of Wanda Jackson, the Queen of Rockabilly; also, Ben Ratliff breaks down the latest album by Destroyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week on Popcast, The Times’s weekly music podcast, Melena Ryzik discusses her Arts & Leisure profile of Wanda Jackson, the 73-year-old Queen of Rockabilly. Ms. Jackson started her career alongside her onetime boyfriend Elvis Presley, became a born-again Christian and now — still growling and swiveling her hips onstage — has a new album produced by Jack White that she hopes will introduce her to a new audience. “You can’t hardly name anything that I haven’t experienced somewhere along the way,” she told Ms.\xa0 Ryzik in her interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: The Return of Wanda Jackson and a New Destroyer Album', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b9d619e-51f3-5e84-98f4-d37c0787ed56', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b9d619e-51f3-5e84-98f4-d37c0787ed56'}, {'abstract': 'Chang Ping, a prominent newspaper columnist who challenged government censors by writing about corruption and political reform, was fired by his publisher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/asia/28china.html', 'snippet': 'Chang Ping, a prominent newspaper columnist who challenged government censors by writing about corruption and political reform, was fired by his publisher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI \x97 A prominent newspaper columnist who challenged government censors by writing about corruption and political reform was dismissed Thursday by the Southern Daily Group, publisher of some of the country’s best-known newspapers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Journalist Who Defied the Censors and Wrote About Corruption Is Fired', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Journalist Who Defied the Censors and Wrote About Corruption Is Fired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freed