 YouTube part of the State of the Union tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Add one more to the list of State of the Union traditions — YouTube.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'YouTube: A State of the Union Tradition', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verne G. Kopytoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8c2db1-60a9-55da-b4be-0c1406520105', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8c2db1-60a9-55da-b4be-0c1406520105'}, {'abstract': 'An Ohio mother says she was trying to keep her children safe. The school district says she broke the law.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/jailed-for-choosing-a-better-school/', 'snippet': 'An Ohio mother says she was trying to keep her children safe. The school district says she broke the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kelley Williams-Bolar got out of jail yesterday, having served 9 days of her 10-day sentence. Now she faces two years of probation and 80 hours of community service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jailed for Choosing a Better School?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/295bb78c-be1d-5d22-8910-dc28204b9a42', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/295bb78c-be1d-5d22-8910-dc28204b9a42'}, {'abstract': 'Poppa Neutrino, whose life was chronicled by a New Yorker writer, founded his own church and crossed the Atlantic on a raft made from scrap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/us/28neutrino.html', 'snippet': 'Poppa Neutrino, whose life was chronicled by a New Yorker writer, founded his own church and crossed the Atlantic on a raft made from scrap.', 'lead_paragraph': ' David Pearlman, an itinerant philosopher, adventurer and environmentalist widely known as Poppa Neutrino, who founded his own church, crossed the Atlantic on a raft made from scrap and invented a theoretically unstoppable football strategy, died on Sunday in New Orleans. He was 77.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/nyregion/28neutrino/28neutrino-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/nyregion/28neutrino/28neutrino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/nyregion/28neutrino/28neutrino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poppa Neutrino, Trans-Atlantic Adventurer, Dies at 77', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poppa Neutrino, 77, ‘the Happiest Man in the World’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flying Neutrinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearlman, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T16:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/576f9155-7392-5d90-99cc-a07de6ca86b5', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/576f9155-7392-5d90-99cc-a07de6ca86b5'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not a normal year when neither Roger Federer nor Rafael Nadal has advanced to a Grand Slam final.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/sports/tennis/28leading.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not a normal year when neither Roger Federer nor Rafael Nadal has advanced to a Grand Slam final.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took mere seconds after the final point of Roger Federer’s loss in the Australian Open semifinals Thursday for the idea to grab hold that an era had ended. No, Federer didn’t announce his retirement after the match, but his defeat, coming only a day after Rafael Nadal was bounced from the tournament, seemed ominous. After all, having Federer or Nadal in a Grand Slam final was always so dependable. They were like the furniture. It’s never normal when you wake up to find your couch missing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Power Shift in Men’s Tennis?', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power Shift in Men’s Tennis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba8bde3-41c7-5e40-b388-697ab204466c', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba8bde3-41c7-5e40-b388-697ab204466c'}, {'abstract': 'A 16-year-old high school student came forward to explain how a grand piano wound up in Biscayne Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/us/28piano.html', 'snippet': 'A 16-year-old high school student came forward to explain how a grand piano wound up in Biscayne Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI SHORES, Fla. — The marine patrol officers and fish and wildlife agents made an onshore visit Thursday to the home of one Nick Harrington, 16, to deliver an ultimatum: Remove the grand piano from Biscayne Bay within 24 hours or face felony charges, a $5,000 fine or, perhaps, worse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/