emy Awards, but in all the Oscar fanfare you might have missed an equally rarefied award: the Razzies, (dis)honoring the worst films and performances of the year. Leading the pack for the Feb. 26 awards show is M. Night Shyamalan’s “The Last Airbender,” which earned worst director, worst picture, worst remake, worst screenplay, worst screen couple/ensemble (the entire cast) and a brand-new category, worst eye-gouging misuse of 3-D. The rest of the worst films were: “The Twilight Saga: Eclipse;” the parody “Vampires Suck;” “Sex and the City 2” (alas, not a parody); and “The Bounty Hunter.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Worst of Them All', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Raspberry Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Liza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shyamalan, M Night', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/206acf63-a579-5e6c-b2ad-7dc5c9f800ce', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206acf63-a579-5e6c-b2ad-7dc5c9f800ce'}, {'abstract': 'Former Prime Minister Ehud Olmert of Israel says Mahmoud Abbas’s hesitation, his own legal troubles and the war in Gaza scotched a potential deal in late 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/middleeast/28mideast.html', 'snippet': 'Former Prime Minister Ehud Olmert of Israel says Mahmoud Abbas’s hesitation, his own legal troubles and the war in Gaza scotched a potential deal in late 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Ehud Olmert, the former prime minister of Israel, says in new memoirs that he and Mahmoud Abbas, the Palestinian president, were very close to a peace deal two years ago, but Mr. Abbas’s hesitation, Mr. Olmert’s own legal troubles and the Israeli war in Gaza caused their talks to end. Shortly afterward, a right-wing Israeli government came to power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28MIDEAST/28MIDEAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28MIDEAST/28MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28MIDEAST/28MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Olmert Memoir Cites Near Deal for Mideast Peace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olmert Says He and Abbas Were Near Deal in ’08', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olmert, Ehud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c735ecc-31ee-5a45-83dd-d5ce9059c2dc', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c735ecc-31ee-5a45-83dd-d5ce9059c2dc'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Federer did not play poorly on Thursday, but unlike Novak Djokovic, he did not reserve his best for the critical phases, and that pattern repeated itself in every set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/sports/tennis/28tennis.html', 'snippet': 'Roger Federer did not play poorly on Thursday, but unlike Novak Djokovic, he did not reserve his best for the critical phases, and that pattern repeated itself in every set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia \x97 In professional tennis, which bristles with entourages and agendas, postmatch consensus can be as elusive as a great drop shot. But when the men’s semifinal between Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic finished Thursday night, there was no debate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/sports/28djokovic-inline1/28djokovic-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/sports/28djokovic-inline1/28djokovic-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/sports/28djokovic-inline1/28djokovic-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic in Top Form Ousting Federer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Djokovic, at His Best, Is Too Good for Federer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20bc99bb-9866-5a70-aa60-0aeb65bc37dd', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20bc99bb-9866-5a70-aa60-0aeb65bc37dd'}, {'abstract': 'A federal directive emphasizes that the public has a right to photograph the exteriors of federal buildings from the public way.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/photographing-a-federal-building-from-a-public-space-youre-not-breaking-any-laws/', 'snippet': 'A federal directive emphasizes that the public has a right to photograph the exteriors of federal buildings from the public way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most street photographers — amateur and professional — have probably had the run-in at least once: they’re taking pictures of building exteriors from a public way and someone wearing a uniform comes up and tells them to stop. (“Can I help you?” are among the more chilling words a photographer can hear these days.) After Antonio Musumeci was arrested for doing just that, the New York Civil Liberties Union filed a lawsuit. The case was settled in October when the government agreed that the public had a right to photograph the exteriors of federal buildings from public spaces. Now, the civil liberties union has received a copy of the federal directive that puts this finding in force and has shared it with the public. Having a print-out in hand may save you some hassle the next time you’re taking pictures. The full story is on Lens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing a Federal Building From a Public Space? You’re Not Breaking Any Laws', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musumeci, Antonio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/557a12fe-bb1d-5860-817d-ddb127b5fa52', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/557a12fe-bb1d-5860-817d-ddb127b5fa52'}, {'abstract': 'What’s the best egg-and-cheese-on-an-everything-bagel sandwich in New York City? That question, and others, answered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/dining/28mrcritic.html', 'snippet': 'What’s the best egg-and-cheese-on-an-everything-bagel sandwich in New York City? That question, and others, answered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mail brought a devilish question about breakfast bagels, while someone wanted to know where to get a drink and a bite after seeing “The Merchant of Venice” on Broadway. I tried to answer these queries and more. As always, you can send questions about where to go or what to eat in New York to dinejournal@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/dining/28mrcritic-span/28mrcritic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/dining/28mrcritic-span/28mrcritic-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/dining/28mrcritic-span/28mrcritic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/dining/28mrcritic-span/28mrcritic-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egg and Cheese on a Bagel: The Quest for the Best', 'kicker': 'Hey, Mr. Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egg and Cheese on a Bagel: The Quest for the Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/230af939-7265-560b-bd84-eabfd0f4a597', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230af939-7265-560b-bd84-eabfd0f4a597'}, {'abstract': 'Some eerie parallels between President Obama’s State of the Union speech and some  statements by Herbert Hoover, who presided during the early years of the Great Depression.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/herbert-obama/', 'snippet': 'Some eerie parallels between President Obama’s State of the Union speech and some  statements by Herbert Hoover, who presided during the early years of the Great Depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David A. Rosenberg, the chief economist and strategist at Gluskin Sheff, noticed some eerie parallels between President Obama’s State of the Union speech and some statements by Herbert Hoover, who presided during the early years of the Great Depression. From Mr. Rosenberg’s client note today:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Herbert Obama?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoover, Herbert Clark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26ad214-9176-57ae-a99f-f2da12ae321d', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26ad214-9176-57ae-a99f-f2da12ae321d'}, {'abstract': 'One of New York’s newest coffee bars, located on Washington Street, is also one of the city’s most striking.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/ristretto-first-look-at-the-kava-cafe/', 'snippet': 'One of New York’s newest coffee bars, located on Washington Street, is also one of the city’s most striking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kava Cafe opened earlier this month on a quiet stretch of Washington Street one block south of the High Line, where the Meatpacking District fades into the West Village. It’s not just one of New York’s newest coffee bars, it’s one of the city’s most striking. 803 Washington Street; (212) 255-7495; kavanyc.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | First Look at the Kava Cafe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb3c6454-6e24-5be2-8f0c-f38f21f8ac35', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb3c6454-6e24-5be2-8f0c-f38f21f8ac35'}, {'abstract': 'Holders of American Express’ Centurion card, commonly known as the black card, can now negotiate car prices online and earn perks from manufacturers like Tesla Motors and Jaguar.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/for-luxury-car-customers-an-amex-card-that-drives-a-hard-bargain/', 'snippet': 'Holders of American Express’ Centurion card, commonly known as the black card, can now negotiate car prices online and earn perks from manufacturers like Tesla Motors and Jaguar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From our colleagues at Bucks:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Luxury Car Customers, an AmEx Card That Drives a Hard Bargain', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/74487e57-4187-5180-b25d-ec4f008c6904', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74487e57-4187-5180-b25d-ec4f008c6904'}, {'abstract': 'Jerry Seinfeld, who directed Mr. Quinn in “Colin Quinn Long Story Short,” will also direct the tapings of that show, which HBO plans to broadcast in April.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/colin-quinns-broadway-show-will-become-an-hbo-special/', 'snippet': 'Jerry Seinfeld, who directed Mr. Quinn in “Colin Quinn Long Story Short,” will also direct the tapings of that show, which HBO plans to broadcast in April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If this was how Colin Quinn and Jerry Seinfeld planned to get themselves back on television, they certainly picked a roundabout way of doing it: “Colin Quinn Long Story Short,” Mr. Quinn’s one-man show about the ascent and decline of civilization, which is also Mr. Seinfeld’s Broadway directorial debut, will be taped by HBO to be shown as a special in April, the cable network announced on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colin Quinn’s Broadway Show Will Become an HBO Special', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe8f0fc1-208b-51bc-9ae5-550487d50412', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe8f0fc1-208b-51bc-9ae5-550487d50412'}, {'abstract': '“This thing is not on a collision course with anything,” a spokesman said. “You could walk faster alongside it.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/walk-away-barge-loose-on-hudson-river/', 'snippet': '“This thing is not on a collision course with anything,” a spokesman said. “You could walk faster alongside it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update, 12:59 p.m. | The city can rest easy: a barge floating free down the Hudson from Tarrytown has been stopped. “As of 12:30, the barge is corralled,” said Charles Rowe, a spokesman for the Coast Guard. The barge had traveled only about a mile south of the Tappan Zee Bridge. “The tug got it under control and is taking back to its original mooring.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walk-Away Barge Is ‘Corralled’ on Hudson River', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tappan Zee Bridge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T17:37:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d8938a-5ea8-5b37-99d5-67b1e47ff1be', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d8938a-5ea8-5b37-99d5-67b1e47ff1be'}, {'abstract': 'The carmaker based its decision on improved cash reserves and a desire to avoid more debt. The request had been pending in order to revamp factories and produce more fuel-efficient vehicles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/business/28auto.html', 'snippet