mes.com/2011/01/27/gran-turismo-5-awaits-new-challengers/', 'snippet': 'Our resident gaming expert delivers his third and final assessment of the popular Playstation 3 racing-simulator game, which will soon face competition from new titles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After its much-anticipated — and delayed — arrival, “Gran Turismo 5,” the racing simulation series for the Sony PlayStation 3, hit the streets in late November. Over the last couple of months, Sam Schembari — our resident racing game aficionado, and a son of James Schembari, an editor for the Automobiles section — has been unraveling the layers of the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Gran Turismo 5’ Awaits New Challengers', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation 3 (Video Game System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/76468ada-81f0-5150-b000-7761cd1f4f92', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76468ada-81f0-5150-b000-7761cd1f4f92'}, {'abstract': 'Photo of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/photo-of-the-week-78/', 'snippet': 'Photo of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A vegetable seller walks in the Brahmaputra River in Guwahati, India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo of the Week', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2150c85-e895-51ab-a164-1f2db33db226', 'word_count': 11, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2150c85-e895-51ab-a164-1f2db33db226'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Barber, who was praised for the Off Broadway production “From Up Here,” will be joined by  Maxwell Caulfield and Lois Robbins.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/in-cactus-flower-revival-jenni-barber-gets-the-role-that-made-goldie-hawn-famous/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Barber, who was praised for the Off Broadway production “From Up Here,” will be joined by  Maxwell Caulfield and Lois Robbins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casting is complete for the first major New York revival of “Cactus Flower,” the Abe Burrows romantic farce that had 1,234 performances on Broadway from 1965 to 1968 and netted Goldie Hawn a career-making Best Supporting Actress Oscar for the 1969 film version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘Cactus Flower’ Revival, Jenni Barber Gets the Role That Made Goldie Hawn a Movie Star', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff4b7fee-f50b-5186-ba72-8d53444f25af', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff4b7fee-f50b-5186-ba72-8d53444f25af'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Porter, professor at Harvard Business School, speaks to DealBook’s Andrew Ross Sorkin at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/does-the-u-s-have-a-competitiveness-problem/', 'snippet': 'Michael Porter, professor at Harvard Business School, speaks to DealBook’s Andrew Ross Sorkin at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interview with DealBook’s Andrew Ross Sorkin at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, Michael Porter, professor at Harvard Business School, offers insight on how to make the United States more competitive. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the U.S. Can Compete Better', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porter, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Andrew Ross', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard Business School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/06e8423d-4523-5cf2-b771-dd618096ef1e', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06e8423d-4523-5cf2-b771-dd618096ef1e'}, {'abstract': 'Some tips for keeping thieves away from your home when you’re out of town.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/tricks-to-keep-thieves-away-from-your-home/', 'snippet': 'Some tips for keeping thieves away from your home when you’re out of town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you don’t have a burglar alarm, or even if you do, you may set your lights to timers to make it appear that someone is home as a way to help keep thieves at bay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tricks to Keep Thieves Away From Your Home', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d651ad6-f830-5d90-ba74-3fe065a08ae7', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d651ad6-f830-5d90-ba74-3fe065a08ae7'}, {'abstract': '“Krugman was somewhat disingenuous in his praise of the flexibility of a national currency in his examination of the problems facing some of the Eurozone economies.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-EUROTRASHED_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“Krugman was somewhat disingenuous in his praise of the flexibility of a national currency in his examination of the problems facing some of the Eurozone economies.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I read with great interest Paul Krugman’s review of the issues facing the euro. What he failed to point out, however, was that many of the policies that got Europe and its currency into so much trouble are in the process of being repeated by the Obama administration — deficit spending on runaway government expenditures, unaffordable social programs, unfunded public pension funds, among others. Shouldn’t Europe’s problems be a siren call for the United States to return to a policy of living within its means and of individual responsibility?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Eurotrashed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTERS; Eurotrashed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/033c2d4d-3e08-57d8-b8b5-3d2e67832eeb', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/033c2d4d-3e08-57d8-b8b5-3d2e67832eeb'}, {'abstract': '“A very informative piece, but with one tantalizing fact omitted: in what language do they converse?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-HOWDEEPISTHE_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“A very informative piece, but with one tantalizing fact omitted: in what language do they converse?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Erlanger’s article told us how the sparks fly between Nicolas Sarkozy and Angela Merkel as each tries to press his or her vision of Europe’s future on the other. Pictures of the two leaders show them apparently bickering in an alleyway and strolling amicably at the Deauville waterside. A very informative piece, but with one tantalizing fact omitted: in what language do they converse?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter: How Deep Is Their Love?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTER; How Deep Is Their Love?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/734861aa-21ec-51b5-9e93-669d37e50bad', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/734861aa-21ec-51b5-9e93-669d37e50bad'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo appointed an ally from the business world to lead the state’s primary economic development agency.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/new-leader-for-state-development-agency/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo appointed an ally from the business world to lead the state’s primary economic development agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo appointed one of the state’s top business lobbyists on Thursday as chief executive of the Empire State Development Corporation, the quasi-independent agency that traditionally leads New York’s economic development efforts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leader for State Development Agency', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Kenneth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Save New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empire State Development Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c79359cd-8936-50c4-a12b-d095d25d9eb0', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c79359cd-8936-50c4-a12b-d095d25d9eb0'}, {'abstract': '“Warner’s commentary prompted the same question as Amy Chua’s essay in The Wall Street Journal did: Where’s Dad? Parenting is a team sport.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-NOMOREMRSNIC_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“Warner’s commentary prompted the same question as Amy Chua’s essay in The Wall Street Journal did: Where’s Dad? Parenting is a team sport.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to Judith Warner’s question, “Is the iron hand of Chinese parenting the future for Americans raising their kids?” my answer is a resounding no — it shouldn’t be. Perhaps I’m biased, being a Chinese-American daughter myself, but doesn’t that give me a voice on this issue?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: No More Mrs. Nice Mom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTERS; No More Mrs. Nice Mom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chua, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e18c2da1-3cab-5a86-88f0-b1617ae5945a', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e18c2da1-3cab-5a86-88f0-b1617ae5945a'}, {'abstract': '“We are fed the messages that all this new technology is providing us with freedom, when in reality we are becoming continually dependent on the very thing that promises liberation.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-WATCHMEREADM_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“We are fed the messages that all this new technology is providing us with freedom, when in reality we are becoming continually dependent on the very thing that promises liberation.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virginia Heffernan’s Medium column misses the mark. Do we really need a break from the “hard mental labor” of reading books? Does my affinity to books without the bells and whistles of insta-scenes and audible voices make me a television-hater? Surely our imaginations don’t need a break when our attention spans are shrinking by the moment in this fast-paced world of Internet, e-mail, texts, Twitter and the rest. Apparently the Vook is distinctive from an “overdesigned book” or the Web because when you read/watch/listen to the Vook, you are uninterrupted by the constant flow of “gaudy video, graphics, music, clocks.” Fair enough, but wouldn’t a real book be the true antidote?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter: Watch Me, Read Me', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watch Me, Read Me', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de1d7f6-6209-5a95-bfdf-313b8f1ca862', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de1d7f6-6209-5a95-bfdf-313b8f1ca862'}, {'abstract': '“As the world’s population increases, the need for planting perennial nut and fruit crops becomes more obvious.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-NUTWORTH_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“As the world’s population increases, the need for planting perennial nut and fruit crops becomes more obvious.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christine Muhlke’s Food column on hazelnut farming can be a lesson for thousands of people who own a bit of land and are not afraid of hard work. While it is rare to find those who can make their livelihood exclusively from growing nuts, it is common to find those who have planted a few trees in their backyards, on school campuses or as a fence row to their properties who delight in the food they have grown with their own hands. As the world’s population increases, the need for planting perennial nut and fruit crops becomes more obvious.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter: Nut Worth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTER; Nut Worth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/908f376e-3185-56ef-9e68-06c5b14fe8f2', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/908f376e-3185-56ef-9e68-06c5b14fe8f2'}, {'abstract': '“Reading Caitlin Shetterly’s Lives column, my reaction was one of deep sorrow.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-THECRAZYLADY_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“Reading Caitlin Shetterly’s Lives column, my reaction was one of deep sorrow.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading Caitlin Shetterly’s Lives column, my reaction was one of deep sorrow. My story, fortunately, has a happy ending. When my younger sister went out to California in the 1970s to live and work, she had a secretarial job and an apartment and was, for the most part, self-sufficient. Then slowly things started to go awry. She lost her job and became unrealistic in her approach to her life and her day-to-day living. She stopped answering her phone and never left her apartment until she was evicted. When she came to live with my husband and me, it was four years before we could get her all the necessary help she needed. She is now 66 years old, content and happily settled in a wonderful home facility not far from us with a caring staff. How very sad that the deeply troubled lady upstairs from Shetterly wouldn’t or couldn’t allow someone in her life to help her.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: The Crazy Lady Upstairs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTERS; The Crazy Lady Upstairs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e11328b2-eb65-58ca-8fec-03c558d50ea2', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e11328b2-eb65-58ca-8fec-03c558d50ea2'}, {'abstract': '“The richness of narratives in physical form has been going through a vanishing act for some time.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/magazine/30Letters-t-THINGSTODOIN_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': '“The richness of narratives in physical form has been going through a vanishing act for some time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The richness of narratives in physical form has been going through a vanishing act for some time. The scarcity of instant outlets of expression like Twitter, Facebook, text messages and even regular e-mail perhaps allowed room for greater introspection and reflection to the pre-Internet generation to a degree that makes my generation, the so-called millennials, seem shallow. But the banality and ubiquity of tweets, posts and online communication gives back our humanity, wrapped in humility. It’s still precious. Rob Walker’s article (Jan. 9) reminded me that our digital preserves/selves need more care and thought than I imagined.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter: Things to Do in Cyberspace When You’re Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LETTER; Things To Do In Cyberspace When You’re Dead ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/64d00349-f7e5-5aea-bb20-f22e6e9d92dc', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64d00349-f7e5-5aea-bb20-f22e6e9d92dc'}, {'abstract': 'One year to the day after Steve Jobs unveiled the iPad, the News Corporation says it is ready to unveil its iPad newspaper, The Daily.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/news-corporation-to-release-the-daily-next-week/', 'snippet': 'One year to the day after Steve Jobs unveiled the iPad, the News Corporation says it is ready to unveil its iPad newspaper, The Daily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One year to the day after Steve Jobs unveiled the iPad, the News Corporation said it was ready to unveil its iPad newspaper, The Daily.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corporation to Release The Daily Next Week', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf712e8-62ea-5b76-8a5a-cd7dda1c6d25', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf712e8-62ea-5b76-8a5a-cd7dda1c6d25'}, {'abstract': 'The government’s hiring of Perella Weinberg, a boutique investment bank, comes as Ally prepares to go public later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/treasury-hires-perella-weinberg-to-advise-on-ally-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'The government’s hiring of Perella Weinberg, a boutique investment bank, comes as Ally prepares to go public later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury Department has hired Perella Weinberg Partners to advise the government on Ally Financial’s impending initial public offering, according to a contract posted online on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Hires Perella Weinberg to Advise on Ally I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ally Financial Inc.', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Perella Weinberg Partners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62a21ea-111b-5be8-b00e-5f2178a31a0e', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62a21ea-111b-5be8-b00e-5f2178a31a0e'}, {'abstract': 'The disparities among major industries in their effective tax rates may have much to do with the life cycle of companies, an N.Y.U. professor says.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/corporate-taxes-more-winners-and-losers/', 'snippet': 'The disparities among major industries in their effective tax rates may have much to do with the life cycle of companies, an N.Y.U. professor says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a wide variation among industries in the share of income paid in federal taxes, as I noted in an article this morning about the president’s call for an overhaul of the corporate tax code. The article includes a few examples, but the longer list of industries and effective tax rates also makes for fascinating reading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Taxes: More Winners and Losers', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/558d7a84-9e78-5cac-a3e2-666567bd827a', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/558d7a84-9e78-5cac-a3e2-666567bd827a'}, {'abstract': 'An agreement to curtail anonymous blocks and other parliamentary tactics averts a politically charged showdown.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/deal-reached-in-senate-to-limit-blocking-tactics/', 'snippet': 'An agreement to curtail anonymous blocks and other parliamentary tactics averts a politically charged showdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate leadership agreed on Thursday to temper some of the procedural tactics that have tied up the chamber for the past two years, and to institute other changes intended to ease gridlock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Reaches Deal to Limit Blocking Tactics', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a137ca3-954e-5756-8249-dd816a45950c', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a137ca3-954e-5756-8249-dd816a45950c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ozawa’s doctors believe he will not have recovered enough for concerts that were scheduled on April 1 and 2.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/ozawa-cancels-carnegie-hall-dates-after-back-surgery/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ozawa’s doctors believe he will not have recovered enough for concerts that were scheduled on April 1 and 2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seiji Ozawa, whose health problems have forced him to cut back on performing for the last year, is canceling his spring appearances at Carnegie Hall. Mr. Ozawa’s doctors believe he will not have recovered enough from recent back surgery to repair herniated discs, Carnegie said. The concerts were scheduled for April 1 and 2. Mr. Ozawa was to have conducted his youth orchestra, the Seiji Ozawa Ongaku-juku, as part of Carnegie’s JapanNYC festival, of which he is the artistic director. The hall said ticket holders would be reimbursed for the canceled concerts. Mr. Ozawa scaled down his appearances with the Saito Kinen Orchestra during the festival’s December portion because of his ailments, which included esophageal cancer and chronic back problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ozawa Cancels Carnegie Hall Dates After Back Surgery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ozawa, Seiji', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6196231-f5c5-5d59-969e-4195231ca860', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6196231-f5c5-5d59-969e-4195231ca860'}, {'abstract': 'Koch Industries wants to unmask the anonymous pranksters who issued a phony press release suggesting that the company, which supports global-warming skeptics, had had a change of heart.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/koch-industries-unamused-by-climate-spoof/', 'snippet': 'Koch Industries wants to unmask the anonymous pranksters who issued a phony press release suggesting that the company, which supports global-warming skeptics, had had a change of heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the sometimes bizarre front lines of the climate-change culture wars: It seems the brothers Koch, proprietors of the giant, Kansas-based industrial conglomerate and well-heeled supporters of Tea Party causes, have now set their sights on a group of anonymous pranksters who spoofed a Koch Industries press release last month — one that suggested the brothers were having a change of heart on climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Koch Industries Unamused by Climate Spoof', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impersonations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch Industries Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Citizen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T18:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Zeller Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeller', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/60e9d3bf-54f4-56a7-92c5-3ad7f0574089', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60e9d3bf-54f4-56a7-92c5-3ad7f0574089'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ general manager has never been shy about expressing himself. What has struck people has been his willingness to be so strident lately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/sports/baseball/28araton.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ general manager has never been shy about expressing himself. What has struck people has been his willingness to be so strident lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the better part of a memorable decade, Brian Cashman was the stealth operator in an organization fronted by a sainted manager and a combustible owner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/sports/28araton1/28araton1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/sports/28araton1/28araton1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 