cker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franzen, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f4652bb-cc77-52b4-b3ed-0f904495fb7f', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f4652bb-cc77-52b4-b3ed-0f904495fb7f'}, {'abstract': 'Kendrick Perkins is a difference-maker for the Celtics, even if box score statistics — and even adjusted plus-minus — don’t show it.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/celtics-perkins-the-some-stats-all-star/', 'snippet': 'Kendrick Perkins is a difference-maker for the Celtics, even if box score statistics — and even adjusted plus-minus — don’t show it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a seminal piece here at The Times, the esteemed Michael Lewis once dubbed Shane Battier -– a defensive specialist and limited offensive wing player for the Houston Rockets -– as the “No-Stats All-Star.” In a way, the distinction was fitting; the traditional box score has never been kind to Battier, due to his lack of impressive point totals, superhuman rebounding performances, or gaudy assist numbers. Even on the defensive end, Battier’s style is more conducive to contested shots than outright steals or blocks, leaving little statistical trace of his on-court impact in the box score.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celtics’ Perkins, the Some-Stats All-Star', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perkins, Kendrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d04219c0-340b-5f01-a1fc-1c72fc6b3cae', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d04219c0-340b-5f01-a1fc-1c72fc6b3cae'}, {'abstract': 'Two first-person accounts offer insight into what goes on beneath the surface in the minds of those transfixed by body image concerns, ”fat phobia” and excessive worries about weight and shape.', 'web_url': 'https://consults.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/insiders-guides-to-overcoming-anorexia-and-bulimia/', 'snippet': 'Two first-person accounts offer insight into what goes on beneath the surface in the minds of those transfixed by body image concerns, ”fat phobia” and excessive worries about weight and shape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading is an inestimable resource in just about any undertaking, especially so when one discovers a work that performs a real service and is written with passion, accuracy and pragmatism. Such is the case with two unflinching personal narratives on eating disorders, Portia de Rossi’s “Unbearable Lightness: A Story of Loss and Gain” and the 25th anniversary edition of “Bulimia: A Guide to Recovery,” by Lindsey Hall and Leigh Cohn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insiders’ Guides to Overcoming Eating Disorders', 'kicker': 'Consults', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Rossi, Portia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Unbearable Lightness: A Story of Loss and Gain (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn J. Zerbe, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Zerbe', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a528969-76c0-5337-abd0-61b1c850c18b', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a528969-76c0-5337-abd0-61b1c850c18b'}, {'abstract': 'There are indeed apps that let you make free WiFi calls to any domestic phone number from your cellphone — if you can live with a stack of footnotes.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/appendix-apps-for-free-calls-to-regular-phones/', 'snippet': 'There are indeed apps that let you make free WiFi calls to any domestic phone number from your cellphone — if you can live with a stack of footnotes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my Times column today, I tackled the complex and rapidly shifting topic of free Internet phone calls. I pointed out that these so-called VOIP apps (for ‘voice over Internet Protocol’) generally offer poor sound quality, audio delays and longer connection times — but they can save you a ton of money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appendix: Apps for Free Calls to Regular Phones', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internet Telephony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fe32da-a8a9-54cb-aa75-3d8b228b6b46', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fe32da-a8a9-54cb-aa75-3d8b228b6b46'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Yemen, Egypt and New York', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/27/blogs/20110127POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Yemen, Egypt and New York', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Yemen, Egypt and New York', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/blogs/20110127POD-slide-1H8A/20110127POD-slide-1H8A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/blogs/20110127POD-slide-1H8A/20110127POD-slide-1H8A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/blogs/20110127POD-slide-1H8A/20110127POD-slide-1H8A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Yemen and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/eb789117-ad2e-5674-b277-cf019750883a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/eb789117-ad2e-5674-b277-cf019750883a'}, {'abstract': 'In the 576-page report released on Thursday by the Financial Crisis Inquiry Committee, there’s not a hero to be found.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/everyone-was-to-blame-crisis-commission-finds/', 'snippet': 'In the 576-page report released on Thursday by the Financial Crisis Inquiry Committee, there’s not a hero to be found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blow-by-blow chronicle of the Wall Street recklessness that led to the financial crisis is reminiscent of a legendary house party. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Was to Blame, Crisis Commission Finds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa38bf7e-566f-5555-b045-1b181868d662', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa38bf7e-566f-5555-b045-1b181868d662'}, {'abstract': 'Lesson Plan | Preparing and interviewing subjects for written profiles, using New York Times features as models.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/putting-personality-on-paper-writing-about-people-using-times-models/', 'snippet': 'Lesson Plan | Preparing and interviewing subjects for written profiles, using New York Times features as models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | How does a writer get beyond basic facts and events to write about people in a captivating yet concise way? What elements and details make for an interesting profile? This lesson offers some examples of ways you can use The New York Times as a model for writing about people. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Personality on Paper: Writing About People Using Times Models', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annissa Hambouz and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hambouz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e45cc012-6b17-5135-b575-c7eba29ef041', 'word_count': 1797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e45cc012-6b17-5135-b575-c7eba29ef041'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: Commuters exiting the Staten Island Ferry Terminal.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/staten-island-ferry-terminal-802-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: Commuters exiting the Staten Island Ferry Terminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commuters exiting the Staten Island Ferry Terminal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staten Island Ferry Terminal, 8:02 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/66c2fada-e246-5cc8-9508-7edda320a560', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66c2fada-e246-5cc8-9508-7edda320a560'}, {'abstract': 'Some of our favorite quotations from political figures over the past 48 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/notable-quotes-from-obama-palin-bachmann-and-reid/', 'snippet': 'Some of our favorite quotations from political figures over the past 48 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The past couple of days have been full of noteworthy comments from political figures. Here are some of our favorites:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notable Quotes From Obama, Palin, Bachmann and Reid', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c8d0cb5-2e9f-5b3b-b455-26ac01071970', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c8d0cb5-2e9f-5b3b-b455-26ac01071970'}, {'abstract': 'A father and son, and two teams, and a long history with the New York City Police Department.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/in-a-fathers-footsteps-into-the-police-force-and-on-the-track/', 'snippet': 'A father and son, and two teams, and a long history with the New York City Police Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derek Powers will not be passing the baton to his son Erek on Friday. He already passed his shield to him years ago — the same badge Derek’s grandfather wore a half-century ago in the New York Police Department.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Father’s Footsteps, Into the Police Force and on the Track', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0727be5f-76b3-536a-9164-aa55445134d4', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0727be5f-76b3-536a-9164-aa55445134d4'}, {'abstract': 'Weeks ago, a committee of the Joint Meeting Parties, an umbrella group of Yemen’s opposition parties that helped organize Thursday’s protests, settled on an escalating scale of protest colors.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/yemens-opposition-goes-to-code-pink/', 'snippet': 'Weeks ago, a committee of the Joint Meeting Parties, an umbrella group of Yemen’s opposition parties that helped organize Thursday’s protests, settled on an escalating scale of protest colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The protesters who filled the streets of Sana, the Yemeni capital, on Thursday demanding the resignation of the country’s authoritarian leader claimed inspiration from similar large antigovernment protests that have rattled Egypt and toppled the government in Tunisia this month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen’s Opposition Goes to Code Pink', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67e4906-f21c-5b5c-8bda-75164371db9c', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67e4906-f21c-5b5c-8bda-75164371db9c'}, {'abstract': 'There is a way, a very simple way, to get chicken with a crisp skin and a moist interior. It requires, oddly, doing a little bit less.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/getting-chicken-crisp-outside-moist-inside/', 'snippet': 'There is a way, a very simple way, to get chicken with a crisp skin and a moist interior. It requires, oddly, doing a little bit less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When eating in a restaurant, I try to learn things that I can apply to my home cooking. What I mostly learn, of course, is how much better the professionals are, but still …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Chicken Crisp Outside, Moist Inside', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5a49093-3829-5e78-b05a-af36257d1137', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5a49093-3829-5e78-b05a-af36257d1137'}, {'abstract': 'If the stone tools found in the United Arab Emirates were made by modern humans, then modern humans got out of Africa much earlier than believed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/science/28africa.html', 'snippet': 'If the stone tools found in the United Arab Emirates were made by modern humans, then modern humans got out of Africa much earlier than believed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cache of stone tools found on the east coast of the Arabian Peninsula has reopened the critical question of when and how modern humans escaped from their ancestral homeland in eastern Africa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/science/28africa1/28africa1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 666, 'subType