e of corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman, in his first official press conference, announced on Thursday that he would bulk up his office’s unit that takes on Medicaid fraud and create a new group to tackle fraud in other areas, like taxes, pensions and government contracts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attorney General to Bolster Anti-Fraud Efforts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T19:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/303b408f-963c-5d5a-ae27-4bc7aca7ac9b', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/303b408f-963c-5d5a-ae27-4bc7aca7ac9b'}, {'abstract': 'Taiwan’s Next Media Animation comments on MTV’s plans to bring Snooki, the Situation and company to Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/they-came-they-saw-they-smushed-a-vision-of-jersey-shore-in-italy/', 'snippet': 'Taiwan’s Next Media Animation comments on MTV’s plans to bring Snooki, the Situation and company to Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Next Media Animation, the Taiwanese company that delights us with its off-kilter, computer-rendered interpretations of American popular culture, turns its attention to the recent news that the “Jersey Shore” cast will be headed to Italy, and the resulting video (which we were pointed to by the good folks at Gothamist) is, to coin a phrase, a blast in a glass. Whoever digitally reproduced the Sistine Chapel so that it could be defaced in animation by what appears to be a “Jersey Shore” cast member (Pauly D? Vinny?) is clearly the Michelangelo of this nascent art form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Came, They Saw, They Smushed: A Vision of ‘Jersey Shore’ in Italy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T20:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/93443a5e-baed-5df1-934f-9fd730b3c090', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93443a5e-baed-5df1-934f-9fd730b3c090'}, {'abstract': 'The former president discussed topics including the Middle East, American politics and the Neanderthal genome project.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/globe-trotter-clinton-makes-davos-stop/', 'snippet': 'The former president discussed topics including the Middle East, American politics and the Neanderthal genome project.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Globe-Trotter Clinton Makes Davos Stop', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T20:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}