ission lambastes an alphabet soup of federal regulatory agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/harsh-words-for-regulators-in-crisis-commission-report/', 'snippet': 'In its exhaustive report released on Thursday, the Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission lambastes an alphabet soup of federal regulatory agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Congressional commission’s scathing account of the financial crisis casts regulators in a rather unflattering light, as the sheriff who didn’t stop Wall Street from becoming the Wild West.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harsh Words for Regulators in Crisis Commission Report', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenspan, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Henry M Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T20:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d351eb01-ac7c-5ed9-aa13-b55294be0474', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d351eb01-ac7c-5ed9-aa13-b55294be0474'}, {'abstract': 'Mice with an inactivated paternal version of the Grb10 gene engaged in more social grooming, nibbled off more fur and whiskers of other mice, and were less likely to back down in a confrontation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/science/01obgene.html', 'snippet': 'Mice with an inactivated paternal version of the Grb10 gene engaged in more social grooming, nibbled off more fur and whiskers of other mice, and were less likely to back down in a confrontation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some genes, either the father’s version or the mother’s version is active, but not both. Which version of the gene works is determined before conception, as the sperm and egg are developing, in a process called imprinting. By mimicking that process in the lab, and turning off a gene in mice, scientists have produced a change in social dominance behavior. In laboratory tests, mice with the paternal version of the gene known as Grb10 inactivated were more aggressive in their behavior, according to new research in the journal Nature. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01obgene1/01obgene1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 905, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01obgene1/01obgene1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01obgene1/01obgene1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Altering a Mouse Gene Turns Up Aggression, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 