kesman for Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr., will replace Robert Gibbs as the White House press secretary.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:19 p.m. | Updated Jay Carney, the spokesman for Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr., will replace Robert Gibbs as the White House press secretary, the White House announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jay Carney to Become White House Press Secretary', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T21:13:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7468252-d986-5c03-b151-12e8a1d27d14', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7468252-d986-5c03-b151-12e8a1d27d14'}, {'abstract': 'Borrowers may not realize that some of the fees are negotiable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/realestate/30mort.html', 'snippet': 'Borrowers may not realize that some of the fees are negotiable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BORROWERS have some weapons for keeping closing costs down, the result of recent guidelines requiring lenders to disclose certain fees, but perhaps the most underutilized consumer tool simply involves old-fashioned haggling. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/30mort-graphic/30mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/30mort-graphic/30mort-gra