bject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Windsor Terrace (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T21:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3c7d213f-493c-5a7c-a183-2cc9df44e4de', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3c7d213f-493c-5a7c-a183-2cc9df44e4de'}, {'abstract': 'Rob Carlo wanted a condo near his new bar in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Among his must-haves were a view and a roof deck for entertaining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/realestate/30hunt.html', 'snippet': 'Rob Carlo wanted a condo near his new bar in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Among his must-haves were a view and a roof deck for entertaining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the summer of 2009, Rob Carlo and some partners opened a bar called Lucky Dog, on Bedford Avenue in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Mr. Carlo was also an owner of the East Village Tavern in Greenwich Village, but he took to Williamsburg in a way he hadn’t to the Village. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/hunt4/hunt4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/hunt4/hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/hunt4/hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Because Summer Is for Barbecues', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Because Summer Is for Bar