ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3470cb76-593a-5535-be51-eaa544645754', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3470cb76-593a-5535-be51-eaa544645754'}, {'abstract': 'With average pay at a 10-year low, Long Islanders are anxious about how they can maintain their lifestyle, a new report finds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/realestate/30lizo.html', 'snippet': 'With average pay at a 10-year low, Long Islanders are anxious about how they can maintain their lifestyle, a new report finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Garden City', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Addressing the Issue of Home Affordability', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Tracks Increasing Anxiety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcelle S. Fischler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcelle', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fischler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f45dfeaa-620b-5527-b755-a9993158685c', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f45dfeaa-620b-5527-b755-a9993158685c'}, {'abstract': 'HarperCollins will publish a young-adult book that was originally submitted on Inkpop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/books/28arts-WEBBOOKMOVES_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'HarperCollins will publish a young-adult book that was originally submitted on Inkpop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HarperCollins will publish a young-adult book that was originally submitted on Inkpop, its Web site for teenage writing. The book, a debut novel by Leigh Fallon, a South African living in Ireland, is scheduled for release in the fall, the publisher said on Thursday. Ms. Fallon first contacted literary agents about her novel, “The Carrier of the Mark,” a paranormal romance, but was unsuccessful in getting it published. She submitted it on Inkpop in December 2009, and it was quickly voted one of the top five manuscripts on the site. HarperCollins followed up a few months later with an offer of a book contract \x97 its first for a work published on the site. Susan Katz, the president and publisher of HarperCollins Children’s Books, called the novel “an outstanding project.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Web Book Moves to Print', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Web Book Moves to Print', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f705053f-3d9c-5168-8af6-508f2237270e', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f705053f-3d9c-5168-8af6-508f2237270e'}, {'abstract': 'In late 2009, after inventory swelled precipitously in New Jersey, the “hot” lists stopped coming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/realestate/30njzo.html', 'snippet': 'In late 2009, after inventory swelled precipitously in New Jersey, the “hot” lists stopped coming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REMEMBER when brokers used to say the sales pace in a particular town, neighborhood or ZIP code had turned white-hot or was sizzling?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 