blissed out, a bit nervous, possibly on the edge of tears. She is talking about her still-unfinished debut collection, which will premiere under the name Giulietta on February 14 as part of New York Fashion Week. She has invited The Moment into her design studio on Grand Street in SoHo, when the conversation suddenly shifts from classic Italian films to a much more personal place. “I don’t think I’ve experienced such happiness since I was a five-year-old girl in Italy,” she says about her clothes, welling up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giulietta of the Spirits', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/909efe85-db1d-5835-9d74-813ccdfd76ab', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/909efe85-db1d-5835-9d74-813ccdfd76ab'}, {'abstract': '“Kaboom,” written and directed by Gregg Araki, follows libidinous college students as they look into strange doings on and off campus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom.html', 'snippet': '“Kaboom,” written and directed by Gregg Araki, follows libidinous college students as they look into strange doings on and off campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smith, the bisexual Southern California college student whose misadventures \x97 some possibly in his own head, many in other people’s beds \x97 are at the center of “Kaboom,” is a cinema studies major. This fact in itself may not be enough to establish him as an alter ego for the director, Gregg Araki, but it does allow Mr. Araki to offer some hints about what he is up to in this chaotic, trifling, oddly likable film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom-span/28kaboom-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom-span/28kaboom-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom-span/28kaboom-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom-span/28kaboom-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/movies/28kaboom-span/28kaboom-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End of the World? Maybe. First, Sex.', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Kaboom'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End of the World? Maybe. First, Sex.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARAKI, GREGG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dekker, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarey, Leo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Haley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c46490e-8be9-5242-af6b-aaf4a22cb4a3', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c46490e-8be9-5242-af6b-aaf4a22cb4a3'}, {'abstract': 'Australia, a relative newcomer to the Asian confederation, faces Japan in Saturday’s final of the Asian Cup in Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/asian-cup-redemption-for-australia/', 'snippet': 'Australia, a relative newcomer to the Asian confederation, faces Japan in Saturday’s final of the Asian Cup in Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — Australia Day was special this year because the Socceroos have made it to the championship game of the Asian Cup, after trouncing Uzbekistan, 6-0. Australia will play Japan for the title on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Cup: Redemption for Australia?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osieck, Holger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doha (Qatar)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Behrooz Afrakhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Behrooz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afrakhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/df51293c-1570-59f3-95c2-916d9aa0aa4a', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df51293c-1570-59f3-95c2-916d9aa0aa4a'}, {'abstract': 'Museums in Pittsburgh and Milwaukee (the closest to Green Bay) have made a bet on next Sunday’s big game.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/27/wagering-art-loans-on-the-superbowl/', 'snippet': 'Museums in Pittsburgh and Milwaukee (the closest to Green Bay) have made a bet on next Sunday’s big game.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Impressionism and the Super Bowl might seem like strange bedfellows, but they will be getting a little bro time together this year in the spirit of the game. Continuing an art tradition that began last year, the Carnegie Museum of Art in Pittsburgh and the Milwaukee Art Museum (the closest museum to Green Bay, Wisc., home of the Packers), have agreed to make a gridiron bet. If Green Bay wins, the Carnegie will send Pierre Renoir’s “Bathers with a Crab” from the 1890s to Milwaukee as a temporary loan. If the Steelers win, the Carnegie’s patrons will get a brief visit from a Gustave Caillebotte, another water-focused scene titled “Boating on the Yerres” from 1877.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wagering Art Loans on the Superbowl', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/273a0eae-90a7-5f72-84c4-a13bca65ac09', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273a0eae-90a7-5f72-84c4-a13bca65ac09'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew Lopez makes his New York debut as a playwright with “The Whipping Man,” about a Jewish Confederate soldier and two former slaves at the end of the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/theater/28lopez.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew Lopez makes his New York debut as a playwright with “The Whipping Man,” about a Jewish Confederate soldier and two former slaves at the end of the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MATTHEW LOPEZ is ready for the question but continues to refine the answer. How did he, a self-described “foxhole Episcopalian” from the Florida Panhandle, the son of a Puerto Rican father and a Polish-Russian mother, come to write a play about a Jewish Confederate soldier and two former slaves raised as Jews who, in the charred wreck of a Virginia home after the Civil War, celebrate Passover together? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28LOPEZ-span/JP-LOPEZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28LOPEZ-span/JP-LOPEZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28LOPEZ-span/JP-LOPEZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing the Play His Curiosity Led Him To', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writing the Play His Curiosity Led Him To', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theater Club', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'na