ecovery from a series of dire illnesses — pneumonia, leading to chronic fatigue syndrome and an infection that spread from her lungs to her heart — and of her new Deutsche Grammophon recording, “Reflections”: a mixed bag of orchestral, vocal and chamber works by Robert and Clara Schumann and their prodigious protégé Brahms.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28HELENE/JP-HELENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28HELENE/JP-HELENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/arts/28HELENE/JP-HELENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recording as a Road to Recovery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recording As a Road To Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Grammophon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimaud, Helene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wolf Conservation Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-27T22:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/934cf441-1d6f-545e-a0b9-a98c221734fa', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934cf441-1d6f-545e-a0b9-a98c221734fa'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on social etiquette about invitees who do not respond promptly, and other issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/fashion/30Social.html', 'snippet': 'Advice on social etiquette about invitees who do not respond promptly, and other issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I hosted a dinner-dance for my husband’s 40th birthday. With two weeks to go, I’d heard from all 80 invitees, except one couple. A few days before the party, I ran into the wife. “Meant to call,” she said. “We can’t make it.” I was taken aback, but thanked her. Then the husband showed up to the seated dinner. I created a place, and the party went swimmingly, but I continue to be stunned. Thoughts? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/10/22/fashion/socialqs/socialqs-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/10/22/fashion/socialqs/socialqs-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/10/22/fashion/socialqs/socialqs-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2009/10/22/fashion/socialqs/socialqs-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/10/22/fashion/socialqs/socialqs-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'h