s in Gander, Newfoundland, were evacuated and controllers in Ronkonkoma, N.Y., and overseas assumed responsibility for dozens of trans-Atlantic flights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/us/28flights.html', 'snippet': 'Air traffic controllers in Gander, Newfoundland, were evacuated and controllers in Ronkonkoma, N.Y., and overseas assumed responsibility for dozens of trans-Atlantic flights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fire at an air traffic control center in Newfoundland forced air traffic controllers in New York and Portugal to handle dozens of additional airliners over the Atlantic on Thursday morning. Many planes had to be detoured hundreds of miles, to their destinations in the United States, the Caribbean or South America, according to air traffic officials. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire in Newfoundland Diverts Atlantic Flights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fire in Newfoundland Diverts Atlantic Flights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newfoundland (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nav Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T00:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e81b86b2-82b9-531d-8cbe-723431d0e7d2', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e81b86b2-82b9-531d-8cbe-723431d0e7d2'}, {'abstract': 'These writings, nearly all previously uncollected, offer a faithful representation of Irving Kristol’s ideas and evolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t.html', 'snippet': 'These writings, nearly all previously uncollected, offer a faithful representation of Irving Kristol’s ideas and evolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Irving Kristol, who died in 2009, is sometimes called the “godfather” or even “father” of neoconservatism, and the patriarchal honorific, like a well-worn hat, sits comfortably atop “The Neoconservative Persuasion: Selected Essays, 1942-2009.” The book is strictly a family enterprise. It has been lovingly edited by Kristol’s widow, the historian Gertrude Himmelfarb, and carries a prefatory funeral eulogy by their sorrowful son, the Republican journalist William Kristol. Even the selection of essays reflects a uniquely familial degree of intimacy.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t_CA0/Berman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t_CA0/Berman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t_CA0/Berman-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t_CA0/Berman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Berman-t_CA0/Berman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Irving Kristol’s Brute Reason', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brute Reason', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Himmelfarb, Gertrude', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristol, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristol, Irving', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T00:45:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Berman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7067de28-e4d8-5fb6-baec-91730b35c47e', 'word_count': 2850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7067de28-e4d8-5fb6-baec-91730b35c47e'}, {'abstract': 'To the uninitiated eye, the Maidan is just a park. To Kolkata, it is a place to recharge the soul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/asia/28india.html', 'snippet': 'To the uninitiated eye, the Maidan is just a park. To Kolkata, it is a place to recharge the soul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOLKATA, India \x97 It is not precisely clear when, how or by whom it was decided that goats could graze in the heart of the Old City here. One local historian traces the decision back nearly three centuries, to the early days of the British East India Company. A different explanation says the goats were liberated to graze when India was liberated from Britain in 1947.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28INDIA2/28INDIA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28INDIA2/28INDIA2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/world/28INDIA2/28INDIA2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In City’s Teeming Heart, a Place to Gaze and Graze', 'kicker': 'Kolkata Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a City’s Teeming Heart, A Place to Gaze and Graze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Calcutta (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T00:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c8fd936-c1d3-546d-a686-009e41619904', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c8fd936-c1d3-546d-a686-009e41619904'}, {'abstract': 'Mohamed ElBaradei, the Nobel laureate who has become a leading opponent of President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt, returned to Cairo in an attempt to galvanize youth-led street protests that extended into a third day across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/20110128_EGYPT.html', 'snippet': 'Mohamed ElBaradei, the Nobel laureate who has become a leading opponent of President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt, returned to Cairo in an attempt to galvanize youth-led street protests that extended into a third day across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mohamed ElBaradei, the Nobel laureate who has become a leading opponent of President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt, returned to Cairo in an attempt to galvanize youth-led street protests that extended into a third day across the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/27/world/middleeast/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR/20110128_EGYPT-slide-NNYR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Third Day of Protests in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T00:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organiza