hometown after more than a decade away, Martavius Jones began spending his evenings at school board meetings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/us/Memphis-1/Memphis-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/us/Memphis-1/Memphis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/28/us/Memphis-1/Memphis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memphis to Vote on Transferring School System to County', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Memphis to Vote on Transferring School System to County', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Memphis (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T02:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5c7e271-1a54-5b68-8a00-4859d784d156', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5c7e271-1a54-5b68-8a00-4859d784d156'}, {'abstract': 'We hope Lebanon’s next prime minister, Najib Mikati, can find ways to put his country’s interests over Hezbollah’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/opinion/28fri2.html', 'snippet': 'We hope Lebanon’s next prime minister, Najib Mikati, can find ways to put his country’s interests over Hezbollah’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lebanon’s next prime minister, Najib Mikati, owes his job to Hezbollah. That is regrettable and dangerous. It will heighten Lebanon’s divisions, antagonize Western donors (including the United States) and complicate the work of the international tribunal set up to try the killers of Rafik Hariri, a former prime minister. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Mikati’s Choice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Mikati’s Choice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mikati, Najib', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Saad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T02:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/169f6ef2-e2e1-5da1-8fd7-f7a4d2fe21db', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/169f6ef2-e2e1-5da1-8fd7-f7a4d2fe21db'}, {'abstract': 'President René Préval and his party, bowing to pressure from regional leaders, are encouraging their candidate, Jude Célestin, to drop out of the runoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/world/americas/28haiti.html', 'snippet': 'President René Préval and his party, bowing to pressure from regional leaders, are encouraging their candidate, Jude Célestin, to drop out of the runoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti \x97 President René Préval and his party, bowing to pressure from regional leaders, including the United States, have begun to encourage their candidate for the coming presidential runoff to drop out, according to party officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti’s President Urges His Candidate to Drop Out, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti’s President Urges His Candidate to Drop Out, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Celestin, Jude', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preval, Rene', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T02:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginger Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca57311-57e0-5775-88cf-3da9d2524a3c', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca57311-57e0-5775-88cf-3da9d2524a3c'}, {'abstract': 'A shortage of the drug used in executions has widened the gap between the reality of carrying out capital punishment and its support in American law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/opinion/28fri3.html', 'snippet': 'A shortage of the drug used in executions has widened the gap between the reality of carrying out capital punishment and its support in American law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capital punishment means lethal injection. The administration of a barbiturate as part of a fatal dose of drugs is meant to render a convict unconscious before other drugs stop his or her breathing and heart so the execution can somehow be construed by a judge as being neither cruel nor unusual.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lethal Injection and the F.D.A.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lethal Injection and the F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T02:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1756d5c4-ea46-51e8-8049-97d363ab713e', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1756d5c4-ea46-51e8-8049-97d363ab713e'}, {'abstract': 'The defense secretary says the Pentagon hopes to revise training and regulations “sooner rather than later.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/us/politics/28military.html', 'snippet': 'The defense secretary says the Pentagon hopes to revise training and regulations “sooner rather than later.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA \x97 Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said that the military could be ready this year to carry out the repeal of a ban on gay men and lesbians serving openly in the armed forces, and that he has accelerated efforts to revise training and regulations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gates Says New Military Policy on Gays Can Start Soon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gates Says New Military Policy on Gays Can Start Soon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T02:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker and Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad66b752-9a85-5719-9e55-bf40143eb6f0', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad66b752-9a85-5719-9e55-bf40143eb6f0'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/nyregion/28lottery.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 27, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', '