rge part by Hescos: the dirt-filled, wire-mesh containers that form the protective outer walls of most American bases in Iraq and Afghanistan. The Year at War series offers p...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The geographic world of every deployed soldier or Marine is defined in large part by Hescos: the dirt-filled, wire-mesh containers that form the protective outer walls of most American bases in Iraq and Afghanistan. To say one is going “outside the wire” means leaving the confines of the Hesco barriers topped with concertina wire that mark the end of a combat outpost and the beginning of the world beyond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year at War: Panoramic Views From Kunduz', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kunduz (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/716bb7da-5de5-5694-965c-56c07d78e71e', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/716bb7da-5de5-5694-965c-56c07d78e71e'}, {'abstract': 'As Davos heads into the weekend, the social aspects are being emphasized, highlighting the gathering’s contradictions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/davos-roundup-parties-shoes-and-serious-stuff/', 'snippet': 'As Davos heads into the weekend, the social aspects are being emphas