desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9fd25b5-352b-510f-b455-fb43b7a8024a', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9fd25b5-352b-510f-b455-fb43b7a8024a'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following protests across Egypt, as demonstrators demanding an end to the autocratic rule of President Hosni Mubarak took to the streets following the end of Friday Prayers.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/latest-updates-on-protests-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following protests across Egypt, as demonstrators demanding an end to the autocratic rule of President Hosni Mubarak took to the streets following the end of Friday Prayers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede followed protests across Egypt of Friday, as demonstrators demanding an end to the autocratic rule of President Hosni Mubarak took to the streets following the end of Friday Prayers. For a summary of the latest events, see the main news article on this site with reports from my colleagues inside Egypt. Readers who are in Egypt and want to share information with us can write in the comment thread below or send photographs to pix@nyt.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on Friday’s Protests in Egypt', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T12:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a29f83-244a-5472-bdd5-f8d8f51cfbd7', 'word_count': 6845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a29f83-244a-5472-bdd5-f8d8f51cfbd7'}, {'abstract': 'The Illinois Supreme Court ruled that Rahm Emanuel can run for mayor in Chicago, but what effect will the saga in the courts have on voters’ views of him?', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/will-court-battle-hurt-emanuel-with-chicago-voters/', 'snippet': 'The Illinois Supreme Court ruled that Rahm Emanuel can run for mayor in Chicago, but what effect will the saga in the courts have on voters’ views of him?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — With an Illinois Supreme Court ruling in his favor and a phone call from President Obama (presumably congratulatory), Rahm Emanuel declared the back-and-forth battle over his qualifications to be mayor of this city over. But as Chicago awoke to a newly clear ballot picture, a question remained: For the candidates, what will be the fallout from this peculiar chapter, one in which, in a dizzying week, Mr. Emanuel was ordered off the ballot, then back on again?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Court Battle Hurt Emanuel With Chicago Voters?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T12:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/053e9d10-2611-5a1e-957e-1628d40fc32f', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/053e9d10-2611-5a1e-957e-1628d40fc32f'}, {'abstract': 'Getting information on a file by clicking “Properties.”', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/tip-of-the-week-a-files-properties/', 'snippet': 'Getting information on a file by clicking “Properties.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Windows, right-clicking on a file or folder and choosing the Properties item from the pop-up menu opens the item’s Properties box, which can tell you all sorts of helpful information about the file, like when it was created or how much hard drive space it is currently taking up. If you do not want to deal with menus, there is another way to get to the Properties box right from the keyboard. Just click on the file or folder to select it and press the Alt + Enter keys on the keyboard to pop open the same box.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: A File’s Properties', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T12:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6aa8c8d-3cc9-56b1-bab2-bfe7b5e4ead0', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6aa8c8d-3cc9-56b1-bab2-bfe7b5e4ead0'}, {'abstract': 'The British prime minister declared Britain “open again for business” and urged his European peers to take steps to “unleash enterprise.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/cameron-joins-innovation-bandwagon-at-davos/', 'snippet': 'The British prime minister declared Britain “open again for business” and urged his European peers to take steps to “unleash enterprise.”', 'lead_para