gue’s hockey operations staff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blake Joins Shanahan in N.H.L. Front Office', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blake, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanahan, Brendan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T14:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff4ed0ae-d30c-5baa-976a-bcf1f18e25bc', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff4ed0ae-d30c-5baa-976a-bcf1f18e25bc'}, {'abstract': 'Carlton Cuse, one of the two show runners of “Lost,” found that completing that series left him, and everyone else, wondering what he would do next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/arts/television/30lost.html', 'snippet': 'Carlton Cuse, one of the two show runners of “Lost,” found that completing that series left him, and everyone else, wondering what he would do next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST summer I went hiking with my teenage daughter in the Swiss Alps. On the first day we left the small village of Wengen and climbed above the timberline to a mountain outpost, Kleine Scheidegg, where we stopped to catch our breath. As I was drinking some water and taking in the awesome panorama, I noticed a hiker approaching. He was bearded and sunburned, wearing a kerosene-stained Swiss mountaineering pack and using trekking poles. I thought he was going to warn us of some danger. Instead he walked up to me and in German-accented English asked, “Are you Carlton Cuse, from ‘Lost’?” Startled, I answered, “Yes.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/LOST/LOST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/LOST/LOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/LOST/LOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So ‘Lost’ Is Over: Now What’s to Be Found?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So ‘Lost’ Is Over: Now What’s To Be Found?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T14:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlton Cuse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cuse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0418491-1442-5c4d-af64-237f5cabce59', 'word_count': 1881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0418491-1442-5c4d-af64-237f5cabce59'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of cultural events this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/arts/30weekaheadweb.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of cultural events this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page':