eb_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/couture-scorecard-jean-paul-gaultier-wins/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scorecard knows this has been a fashion week that saw couturiers anguished by the question of whether those who do made-to-measure extravagance can continue to maintain their cultural relevance, in ways that don’t involve flashbulb-friendly sparkle. Leave it to fashion’s perennial enfant terrible Jean Paul Gaultier to pastiche a very classically post-war run of show on the closing day with — astonishingly elegant — numbered placard carrying faux-hawked Crazy Horse dancers. That sent out a resounding\xa0rallying cry: “Yes We Can-Can.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Couture Scorecard | Jean Paul Gaultier Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f0f66f7-fe11-502e-bbb9-5d38e2c590cc', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f0f66f7-fe11-502e-bbb9-5d38e2c590cc'}, {'abstract': 'To balance a drop in items sold for big renovations, the company is trying to get women, 50 percent of its customers, excited about more modest makeovers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/business/29home.html', 'snippet': 'To balance a drop in items sold for big renovations, the company is trying to get women, 50 percent of its customers, excited about more modest makeovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring, Home Depot hopes to turn a woman’s fancy toward redecoratin