ical island. I’d never been to a tropical island because I never wanted to go. I never wanted to go because the prospect of lounging around on a beach while being waited on by foreign poor people with dark skin made me feel uncomfortably rich and white — and American. As the son of communist parents, one Iranian and one Jewish American, who taught me to eschew most forms of pleasure and all forms of imperialist ostentation, I told my wife when we married that she had a long and torturous battle ahead of her with trying to get me to go. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/magazine/30lives/30lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/magazine/30lives/30lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/magazine/30lives/30lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Commie-Pinko in Cancún', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A COMMIE-PINKO IN CANCÚN', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By SAID SAYRAFIEZADEH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Said', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SAYRAFIEZADEH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/718f836d-d4b5-5334-acd1-a173008a1188', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718f836d-d4b5-5334-acd1-a173008a1188'}, {'abstract': 'The Washington Capitals signed Alexander Semin to another one-year contract extension.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/capitals-sign-semin-to-one-year-deal/', 'snippet': 'The Washington Capitals signed Alexander Semin to another one-year contract extension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON–Alex Ovechkin may get most of the attention, but the Washington Capitals also have another Russian Alex on whom they are counting to revive their offense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capitals Sign Semin to One-Year Deal', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9be478ac-ac00-552b-8cbb-922fbede6b99', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9be478ac-ac00-552b-8cbb-922fbede6b99'}, {'abstract': '“The little brother Ali was little enough but you didn’t know what he would come up with, and they laughed when he told what his teacher had said, that we are all nomads.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/excerpt-night-soul-and-other-stories.html', 'snippet': '“The little brother Ali was little enough but you didn’t know what he would come up with, and they laughed when he told what his teacher had said, that we are all nomads.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'No Man’s Land', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Night Soul and Other Stories’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeb07420-653c-5388-bee9-b091fb2147af', 'word_count': 3067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeb07420-653c-5388-bee9-b091fb2147af'}, {'abstract': 'These clever and oblique short stories, written over three decades, highlight the breadth and diversity of Joseph McElroy’s vision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/Burn-t.html', 'snippet': 'These clever and oblique short stories, written over three decades, highlight the breadth and diversity of Joseph McElroy’s vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a problem with the way Joseph McElroy’s fiction reaches the contemporary reader. While McElroy comes packaged as a postmodern novelist, the reader who picks up one of his books looking for the superficial imprint of his contemporaries — black humor? joke names? — will be confused by the classification. Although his work certainly feeds off late-20th-century energies, McElroy’s cosmopolitan, erudite fiction needs to be received on a wider bandwidth that also registers signals from other disciplines and earlier literature. The sudden shifts between his paragraphs, for instance, recall Braque and Picasso’s collage techniques, while many of his thematic obsessions overlap with those of modernists like Woolf, Bergson and Nietzsche. Reading “Night Soul” — a collection of 12 clever and oblique short stories — is, in fact, a little like being a member of Marlow’s audience in “Heart of Darkness.” We listen in a foggy void, and try to puzzle out the significance of a narrator’s inconclusive experiences. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Burn-t_CA0/Burn-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Topological Fiction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Topological Fiction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McElroy, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:44:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Burn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17e14398-0371-5d58-80fe-0c6b27414af7', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17e14398-0371-5d58-80fe-0c6b27414af7'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Clijsters and Li Na play for the women’s singles title in Melbourne Saturday evening in a battle of aggressive baseliners. The two play remarkably similar games, with flat, bruising groundstrokes off of both sides.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/womens-finals-preview-li-vs-clijsters/', 'snippet': 'Kim Clijsters and Li Na play for the women’s singles title in Melbourne Saturday evening in a battle of aggressive baseliners. The two play remarkably similar games, with flat, bruising groundstrokes off of both sides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kim Clijsters and Li Na play for the women’s singles title in Melbourne Saturday evening in a battle of aggressive baseliners. The two play remarkably similar games, with flat, bruising groundstrokes off of both sides. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s Finals Preview: Li vs. Clijsters', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/74dc0a94-c852-599c-9403-6e0ef19c728d', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74dc0a94-c852-599c-9403-6e0ef19c728d'}, {'abstract': 'A homey village at the heart of a sprawling town offers a wide assortment of homes, from Victorians to small ranches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/realestate/30living.html', 'snippet': 'A homey village at the heart of a sprawling town offers a wide assortment of homes, from Victorians to small ranches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER three years living with her parents in Garden City, Carla Loeven and her husband, Rich, felt they had saved enough money to go house shopping. What they found close to home was too expensive, especially with the high property taxes. In Franklin Square, where Mr. Loeven grew up, the yards were too small for the price. While they loved Huntington and Centerport, they found that their $375,000 would go a lot further 15 minutes away in the village of Farmingdale, at the eastern edge of Nassau County.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/LIVING/LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/LIVING/LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 240}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/LIVING/LIVING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/LIVING/LIVING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/realestate/LIVING/LIVING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For First-Time Buyers Drawn to Yesteryear', 'kicker': 'Living In | Farmingdale Village, L.I.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attention, First-Time Buyers Drawn to Yesteryear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Farmingdale (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcelle S. Fischler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcelle', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fischler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d1ae3bb-c9b7-5399-b29e-3a8dda49c2e6', 'word_count': 1472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d1ae3bb-c9b7-5399-b29e-3a8dda49c2e6'}, {'abstract': 'I admit I didn’t grasp the point of all the drum-beating this week in Women’s Wear Daily. But this morning all was illuminated when I went to wwd.com and saw the headline “Michelle Obama Puts Kara Ross on World Stage.”', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/witch-hunt/', 'snippet': 'I admit I didn’t grasp the point of all the drum-beating this week in Women’s Wear Daily. But this morning all was illuminated when I went to wwd.com and saw the headline “Michelle Obama Puts Kara Ross on World Stage.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'O.K., I’m a little slow; I admit I didn’t grasp the point of all the drum-beating this week in Women’s Wear Daily. I’ve been in Paris covering shows. But this morning all was illuminated when I went to wwd.com and saw the headline “Michelle Obama Puts Kara Ross on World Stage.” The article stated that Ms. Ross, a jewelry designer, had been “called up to the major leagues” by the “prime placement” of earrings on Mrs. Obama, most recently at the State of the Union speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'About That McQueen Dress', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7cd604c-74e4-5ad0-a98c-ee8129afe6bf', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7cd604c-74e4-5ad0-a98c-ee8129afe6bf'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Whitaker, the NBC Washington Bureau chief and former editor of Newsweek magazine, has been hired by CNN as its executive vice president and managing editor.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/mark-whitaker-to-leave-nbc-news-for-cnn/', 'snippet': 'Mark Whitaker, the NBC Washington Bureau chief and former editor of Newsweek magazine, has been hired by CNN as its executive vice president and managing editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another sign of its often-stated commitment to hard-news journalism, CNN announced Friday that it had hired Mark Whitaker, the NBC Washington Bureau chief and former editor of Newsweek magazine, to a newly created position of executive vice president and managing editor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Whitaker to Leave NBC News for CNN', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitaker, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cable News Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newsweek', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T16:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54fc5b67-6282-58cf-9141-287f3a8d8fe0', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54fc5b67-6282-58cf-9141-287f3a8d8fe0'}, {'abstract': 'H. G. Adler, a death-camp survivor who pioneered Holocaust studies, wrote the first draft of this thinly disguised bildungsroman in 1948.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/Shulevitz-t.html', 'snippet': 'H. G. Adler, a death-camp survivor who pioneered Holocaust studies, wrote the first draft of this thinly disguised bildungsroman in 1948.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every so often, a book shocks you into realizing just how much effort and sheer luck was required to get it into your hands. “Panorama” was the first novel written by H. G. Adler, a \xadGerman-speaking Jewish intellectual from Prague who survived a labor camp in Bohemia, Theresienstadt, Auschwitz and a particularly hellish underground slave-labor camp called Langenstein, near Buchenwald. Adler wrote the first draft in less than two weeks in 1948, three years after he had walked back to Prague from Langenstein and a few weeks after he had fled Prague just before the Communist coup. He wound up in England, but couldn’t find anyone willing to publish the book until 1968, 20 years and two drafts later. The book is coming out in English for the first time only now.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Shulevitz-t_CA0/Shulevitz-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 759, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Shulevitz-t_CA0/Shulevitz-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/Shulevitz-t_CA0/Shulevitz-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vanished World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vanished World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adler, H G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filkins, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Shulevitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shulevitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e265f1a-d2ca-5e39-9592-f70e5fb82df1', 'word_count': 1827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e265f1a-d2ca-5e39-9592-f70e5fb82df1'}, {'abstract': 'Before Hyundai stuffed the new Sonata, it built a great shell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/30/automobiles/autoreviews/20110130-hyundai.html', 'snippet': 'Before Hyundai stuffed the new Sonata, it built a great shell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Hyundai stuffed the new Sonata, it built a great shell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/automobiles/autoreviews/20110130-hyundai-slide-WD8Q/20110130-hyundai-slide-WD8Q-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/automobiles/autoreviews/20110130-hyundai-slide-WD8Q/2