ization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3edeb81-c87e-575c-a8db-14a588901d3e', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3edeb81-c87e-575c-a8db-14a588901d3e'}, {'abstract': 'The work of the fantasy novelist Robert Jordan gets a graphic novel adaptation in “New Spring,” part of the author’s “Wheel of Time” series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/graphic-books-best-sellers-an-adaptation-of-robert-jordans-new-spring/', 'snippet': 'The work of the fantasy novelist Robert Jordan gets a graphic novel adaptation in “New Spring,” part of the author’s “Wheel of Time” series.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The work of the fantasy novelist Robert Jordan gets a graphic novel adaptation in “New Spring,” part of the author’s “Wheel of Time” series. The graphic novel is at No. 2 on our soft cover list this week. Robert Jordan was a pseudonym used by James Oliver Rigney Jr., who died in 2007. In his obituary, Margalit Fox wrote that the “Wheel of Time” series was known for its “epic sweep, intricate plotting and large cast of complex characters.” And that the series focused on “Rand al’Thor, a humble messianic figure who must stave off the forces of evil that threaten to overtake the faraway land in which he lives. Along the way, there are perils and portents, fair maidens, fantastical deeds and the like.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: An Adaptation of Robert Jordan’s ‘New Spring’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8134578-b5d5-58b5-8921-609028074d0f', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8134578-b5d5-58b5-8921-609028074d0f'}, {'abstract': 'From photographic collages to the latest smartphone apps, visitors to London can now find all manner of maps of the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/london-underground-map-it-your-way/', 'snippet': 'From photographic collages to the latest smartphone apps, visitors to London can now find all manner of maps of the city.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#795", 592, 490, true, chameleonData); ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Underground | Map It Your Way', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias Redstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Redstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/458597aa-1e2f-5c54-9d64-58cb6915f8ca', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/458597aa-1e2f-5c54-9d64-58cb6915f8ca'}, {'abstract': '“Anna Karenina,” Manchester United and Nero are all grist for this analysis of global inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/Rampell-t.html', 'snippet': '“Anna Karenina,” Manchester United and Nero are all grist for this analysis of global inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who needs to keep up with the Joneses? What people really care about is keeping up with the Rockefellers. That’s the main theme of “The Haves and the Have-Nots,” an eclectic book on inequality that attempts to document the long history of coveting by the poor, and the grim consequences of that coveting.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/30rampell/30rampell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/30rampell/30rampell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/30rampell/30rampell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thy Neighbor’s Wealth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thy Neighbor’s Wealth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:31:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60578da0-37c0-538e-9592-913e4e14b98c', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60578da0-37c0-538e-9592-913e4e14b98c'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed regulations would phase out the most polluting oils, No. 6 and No. 4, yielding health and environmental benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/new-york-floats-rules-for-cleaner-heating-oil/', 'snippet': 'Proposed regulations would phase out the most polluting oils, No. 6 and No. 4, yielding health and environmental benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buildings in New York City would burn cleaner heating oil and emit far less pollution under proposed rules announced on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Floats Rules for Cleaner Heating Oil', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea30a2a8-add6-5f46-b8a7-22c66bb282b6', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea30a2a8-add6-5f46-b8a7-22c66bb282b6'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt has cut off nearly all Internet traffic into and out of the country and disrupted cellphone service as it struggles to contain protests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/technology/internet/29cutoff.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt has cut off nearly all Internet traffic into and out of the country and disrupted cellphone service as it struggles to contain protests.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Autocratic governments often limit phone and Internet access in tense times. But the Internet has never faced anything like what happened in Egypt on Friday, when the government of a country with 80 million people and a modernizing economy cut off nearly all access to the network and shut down cellphone service.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/28/technology/20110129_CUTOFF_INLINE/20110129_CUTOFF_INLINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Cuts Off Most Internet and Cell Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Halts Most Internet and Cell Service, and Scale of Shutdown Surprises Experts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Internet', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Richtel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richtel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8a7764e-8713-5188-8238-9c60aecbc2f0', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8a7764e-8713-5188-8238-9c60aecbc2f0'}, {'abstract': 'In Courthouse Confidential, a national fraternity that is already in an internal fight over leadership now is fighting over a move to disband the organization.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/a-fraternitys-fight-could-lead-to-its-end/', 'snippet': 'In Courthouse Confidential, a national fraternity that is already in an internal fight over leadership now is fighting over a move to disband the organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A century-old fraternity locked in a legal battle over the actions of its national executives filed for Chapter 7 bankruptcy this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fraternity’s Fight Could Lead to Its End', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T17:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/edd6c1bc-a800-553e-9e1c-19e3c1888430', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edd6c1bc-a800-553e-9e1c-19e3c1888430'}, {'abstract': 'A study of the global economy marks the passing of the “Age of Optimism.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/books/review/Malcomson-t.html', 'snippet': 'A study of the global economy marks the passing of the “Age of Optimism.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gideon Rachman’s \xad“Zero-Sum Future” is slightly misnamed. Rachman, the chief foreign affairs columnist for The Financial Times, seems to believe that this future — an Age of Anxiety — is already here.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/books/review/30malcomson/30malcomson