, 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dd77abf-8fcd-526b-9ef9-8dde219778d1', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dd77abf-8fcd-526b-9ef9-8dde219778d1'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptians have demonstrated over the years about low wages, poverty and the election process, but never in such a widespread fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/middleeast/29mubarak.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptians have demonstrated over the years about low wages, poverty and the election process, but never in such a widespread fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Standing before a joint session of Parliament in 2006, President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt told lawmakers what most in attendance had already assumed: He planned to stay in power until the day he died.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptians’ Fury Has Smoldered Beneath the Surface for Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Compact Between Egypt And Its Leader Erodes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T18:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Slackman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slackman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89ecccb8-5cdc-50a4-a2bc-e3bd3e79e196', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89ecccb8-5cdc-50a4-a2bc-e3bd3e79e196'}, {'abstract': 'Hitting coach Kevin Long and Derek Jeter began working last September on refining his swing and this week they picked up where they left off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/sports/baseball/29jeter.html', 'snippet': 'Hitting coach Kevin Long and Derek Jeter began working last September on refining his swing and this week they picked up where they left off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. \x97 Kevin Long needed a place to demonstrate Derek Jeter’s retooled hitting mechanics, so the bar area of a Bonefish Grill on Thursday night had to suffice. Long nudged aside a coffee table, assumed the hitting position \x97 legs flexed, body squared, arms bent and out front \x97 and moved his front foot up and down. As he pretended to swing a bat, a waitress bumped into him. Long, so engrossed in his explanation, did not seem to notice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/29jeter1/29jeter1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/29jeter1/29jeter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/29jeter1/29jeter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Increase Production, Jeter Tries Subtracting a Step', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Increase Production, Jeter Tries Subtracting a Step', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Long, Kevin (1966- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T18:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7eb40f3-b8f4-5da4-8c00-13a44baf8378', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7eb40f3-b8f4-5da4-8c00-13a44baf8378'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. staff recommended that stock brokers be required to act in their clients’ best interest, a win for investors. But it’s likely to be a while before any new rules take effect.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/s-e-c-staff-to-brokers-clients-should-come-first/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. staff recommended that stock brokers be required to act in their clients’ best interest, a win for investors. But it’s likely to be a while before any new rules take effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The intense debate over whether brokers should be required to put their customers’ interests before their own is far from over, but it’s moving in the right direction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Staff to Brokers: Clients Should Come First', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'n