4, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964acfa5-edeb-543c-a0e8-f623766b4bfa'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/weekend-fare-28/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kings County Distillery in Williamsburg, 35 Meadow Street (Bogart Street), bottles its moonshine in clear flasks with white labels adorned with typewriter fonts. On Saturday, watch this small producer make its unaged corn whiskey from 1 to 6 p.m. Admission is free and tastings are $3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T21:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/31e6c882-552b-5518-9336-3346e6ee1524', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31e6c882-552b-5518-9336-3346e6ee1524'}, {'abstract': 'Credit rating agencies’ concerns over the tumult in the Middle East focused on how much governments there might step up spending to calm public ire, but others called the timing of the agencies’ warnings “ill-advised.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/middleeast/29egypt-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Credit rating agencies’ concerns over the tumult in the Middle East focused on how much governments there might step up spending to calm public ire, but others called the timing of the agencies’ warnings “ill-advised.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland \x97 As the turmoil gripping much of the Arab world reached a critical pitch in Egypt on Friday, the possible economic fallout was on the minds of credit ratings agencies monitoring the situation from thousands of miles away, and they did not like what they saw. But the warnings they issued are themselves raising eyebrows. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unrest Worries Credit Raters. So Does Calming It.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unrest Worries Credit Raters. So Does Calming It.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Kenneth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Corp", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T21:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc51819e-b1a1-5c12-a691-72c5312f740a', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc51819e-b1a1-5c12-a691-72c5312f740a'}, {'abstract': 'With the indie mystery “Cold Weather,” the director Aaron Katz, shooting in his hometown, Portland, Ore., explores character within the parameters of noir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/movies/30katz.html', 'snippet': 'With the indie mystery “Cold Weather,” the director Aaron Katz, shooting in his hometown, Portland, Ore., explores character within the parameters of noir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLD WEATHER,” the third feature by the young filmmaker Aaron Katz, begins in the modestly introspective vein of many a low-budget American indie. On an indefinite break from college, Doug has returned home to Portland, Ore., where he’s staying with his sister, Gail. The film appears poised to explore their shared history and private uncertainty, the simultaneous distance and closeness that sometimes defines adult sibling dynamics.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/KATZ-span/KATZ-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/KATZ-span/KATZ-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/KATZ-span/KATZ-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/KATZ-span/KATZ-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/KATZ-span/KATZ-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indie Gumshoe in Oregon’s Gloom', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Indie Gumshoe in Oregon’s Gloom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Aaron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'ran