rch', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6feb3de7-8a36-50c6-a762-b41a5adc3140', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6feb3de7-8a36-50c6-a762-b41a5adc3140'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/01/30/arts/design/20110130-WIC-SS.html', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/design/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/design/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/arts/design/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3/20110130-WIC-SS-slide-N8E3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Culture Pictures, Jan. 28', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T22:32:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cba9a1b9-bbb5-5e30-b960-a8e4db448849', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cba9a1b9-bbb5-5e30-b960-a8e4db448849'}, {'abstract': 'What started out in a Seattle barbershop has become a bona fide scene, one whose aesthetics and business model are redefining the overlapping worlds of drinking, dining, sleeping and shopping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/fashion/30ACE.html', 'snippet': 'What started out in a Seattle barbershop has become a bona fide scene, one whose aesthetics and business model are redefining the overlapping worlds of drinking, dining, sleeping and shopping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALK into the Ace Hotel, on the corner of Broadway and 29th Street, at any given time, and here is what you may find: The band Jác might be playing in one corner of the vast lobby, their horn-and-accordion tunes bouncing off the century-old mosaic floor, the dark wood paneling, the 17 1/2-foot white columns. In one of the red-suede sofa nooks, under a huge American flag bought at the Brimfield Antique Show, a motley crew of friends from Washington — a women’s-wear designer, a tour guide, a defense contractor — might be striking up a conversation with the British pop-soul singer Edei. In the middle of the lobby, the long library-style black tables have been colonized by MacBooks.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/fashion/ALEX1/ALEX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/fashion/ALEX1/ALEX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/fashion/ALEX1/ALEX1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cre