-concerns-about-hormone-therapy/', 'snippet': 'A huge study in Britain suggests that the women thought to be at the lowest risk from hormones may actually be at the highest risk, at least when it comes to breast cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times reports on Friday that a large of study of women in the United Kingdom has found that those who used hormone replacement therapy at menopause suffered an elevated risk of breast cancer, compared with women who used hormones only in the years following menopause.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Concerns About Hormone Therapy', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menopause', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T22:42:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/236b1f66-0b17-5343-9919-457c0e04ed00', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/236b1f66-0b17-5343-9919-457c0e04ed00'}, {'abstract': 'Intel will spend $100 million on a half-dozen or more collaborative research projects with scientists from many universities.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/intel-spreads-its-university-research-bets/', 'snippet': 'Intel will spend $100 million on a half-dozen or more collaborative research projects with scientists from many universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Computing in general is increasingly applying the old engineering dictum, divide and conquer. Look at the engines behind cloud computing — vast, distributed armies of server computers. Even at the chip level, the wave of the recent past and the future is, as they say in the industry, multicore — microprocessors with multiple data-processing cores, for lower-power consumption and better performance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intel Spreads Its University Research Bets', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T22:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5812ffea-5f94-5a44-85eb-7f0e11907545', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5812ffea-5f94-5a44-85eb-7f0e11907545'}, {'abstract': 'Clarinda Mac Low and Jordana Che Toback perform at Dance New Amsterdam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/arts/dance/29splice.html', 'snippet': 'Clarinda Mac Low and Jordana Che Toback perform at Dance New Amsterdam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attending a show at Dance New Amsterdam has become a little like stepping back in time. For Splice, two choreographers share a program in a series that brings to mind Dance Theater Workshop’s former Split Stream series with one uncomfortable difference. Splice also requires participants to collaborate on a piece, and Clarinda Mac Low and Jordana Che Toback, performing on Thursday night, don’t exactly brim over with artistic simpatico. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/SPLICE/SPLICE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dinosaurs, Politicians, Oil and Water', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dinosaurs, Politicians, Oil and Water', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T22:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f12a40e9-eb4e-5d0b-ad54-0f5180a7fcc4', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f12a40e9-eb4e-5d0b-ad54-0f5180a7fcc4'}, {'abstract': 'The chief of staff of Egypt’s armed forces, Lt. Gen. Sami Hafez Enan, was due to meet Monday with Adm. Mike Mullen, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/middleeast/29military-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The chief of staff of Egypt’s armed forces, Lt. Gen. Sami Hafez Enan, was due to meet Monday with Adm. Mike Mullen, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senior Egyptian military commanders cut short a visit to the Pentagon on Friday and were headed back home Friday, American military officials said, as the Egyptian Army was deployed on the streets of Cairo and other cities to back up state security forces who had confronted mass protests around the country throughout the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Military Chiefs Cut Pentagon Visit Short', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egyptian Military Chiefs Cut Pentagon Visit Short', 'name': None, '