snippet': '“Snow Falling on Cedars,” a play adapted by Kevin McKeon from the novel by David Guterson, is at Hartford Stage.', 'lead_paragraph': ' There are grounds for believing that David Guterson’s popular 1994 novel, “Snow Falling on Cedars,” could make good theater. Set in 1954, in a Puget Sound community divided among fishermen and farmers, whites and Japanese, it is at once a courtroom drama, a mystery, a love story and, in flashbacks, a social history freighted with the angry residue of World War II and the Japanese internment camps. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30THEA1CO/30THEA1CO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30THEA1CO/30THEA1CO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30THEA1CO/30THEA1CO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Town Divided by the Residue of War', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Town Divided By the Residue of War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guterson, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hartford Stage Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-28T23:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'las