ns of thousands of protesters on the streets of Egypt pressing for an end to President Hosni Mubarak’s 30-year rule.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/protesters-in-new-york-area-take-aim-at-u-s-position-on-egypt/', 'snippet': 'About 100 men, women and children gathered in Jersey City to support the tens of thousands of protesters on the streets of Egypt pressing for an end to President Hosni Mubarak’s 30-year rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERSEY CITY — Waving Egyptian flags, chanting slogans in English and Arabic and setting fire to a photo of President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt, about 100 men, women and children gathered Friday afternoon here in Journal Square to support the tens of thousands of protesters on the streets of Egypt pressing for an end to Mr. Mubarak’s 30-year rule.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters in New York Area Take Aim at U.S. Position on Egypt', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Speri and Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Speri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/357567aa-e129-523a-8e52-973a389e8181', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/357567aa-e129-523a-8e52-973a389e8181'}, {'abstract': 'At Le Poisson Rouge on Thursday, the Metropolis Ensemble presented a program devoted to works in which acoustics and electronics shared roughly equal status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/arts/music/29metropolis.html', 'snippet': 'At Le Poisson Rouge on Thursday, the Metropolis Ensemble presented a program devoted to works in which acoustics and electronics shared roughly equal status.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The mixing of acoustic instruments and electronic sounds was not always as easy and natural as it can seem nowadays. Certainly, adventurous composers were drawn to the limitless palette of sounds made possible by recording technology and computers. But not until digital sampling and the versatile laptop computer arrived did it become relatively easy to exploit all the unusual timbres and unnatural juxtapositions promised by electronics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/Metropolis/Metropolis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/Metropolis/Metropolis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/Metropolis/Metropolis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night of Acoustic and Electronic Exploits', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Night of Acoustic and Electronic Exploits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolis Ensemble', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f43d701f-01c8-5778-a4db-c3a128f2ec9c', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f43d701f-01c8-5778-a4db-c3a128f2ec9c'}, {'abstract': 'Slide Show: Subjects include rebel yoga, winter weather, and a funeral for a guardian angel.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/the-week-in-pictures-for-jan-28/', 'snippet': 'Slide Show: Subjects include rebel yoga, winter weather, and a funeral for a guardian angel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include rebel yoga, winter weather, and a funeral for a guardian angel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for Jan. 28', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e60df74-1ccb-5b90-bc31-b20916dbf9c3', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e60df74-1ccb-5b90-bc31-b20916dbf9c3'}, {'abstract': 'Simplicity and a slow tempo characterized Rebecca Martin’s intimate approach to her repertory at the Cornelia Street Café on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/arts/music/29cornelia.html', 'snippet': 'Simplicity and a slow tempo characterized Rebecca Martin’s intimate approach to her repertory at the Cornelia Street Café on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As jazz singers go, Rebecca Martin exudes the plainest sort of poise, almost radical in its utter lack of flash. When she wasn’t cradling an acoustic guitar on Thursday night at the Cornelia Street Café, she held her arms clasped behind her back, as if to make sure they wouldn’t be a distraction. She sang quietly, favoring slow tempos. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/CORNELIA/CORNELIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/CORNELIA/CORNELIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/arts/CORNELIA/CORNELIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Vocals Illuminate Emotions Underneath', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Vocals Illuminate Emotions Underneath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Rebecca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a397bbfe-3ebc-558e-a999-c25ccc826bb7', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a397bbfe-3ebc-558e-a999-c25ccc826bb7'}, {'abstract': 'NEC, the Japanese computer company, hosts an annual international bridge tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/crosswords/bridge/29card.html', 'snippet': 'NEC, the Japanese computer company, hosts an annual international bridge tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEC, the Japanese computer company, hosts an annual international bridge tournament. This year’s will take place in Yokohama City from Feb. 8 to 13. Play can be followed at Bridge Base Online. The diagramed deal was interesting in the tournament’s 2007 final, in which Ton Bakkeren, Huub Bertens, Leon Jacobs and Maarten Schollaardt from the Netherlands, defeated Cezary Balicki and Adam Zmudzinski, from Poland, and Alexander Dubinin and Andrei Gromov, from Russia. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Play Was Found From a Pause in the Bidding', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning Play Was Found From a Pause In the Bidding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c3e8e70-3248-5c74-ad15-ee5c9113ecb6', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c3e8e70-3248-5c74-ad15-ee5c9