of Art in Huntington through March 27.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an old cartoon I saw many years ago, a wealthy-looking codger gleefully defaces a series of old portraits as two museum guards look on with dismay. The caption says something like, “There’s not a thing we can do \x97 this is the Brown Collection, and that’s Mr. Brown.”', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ART1LI/30ART1LI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ART1LI/30ART1LI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ART1LI/30ART1LI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ART1LI/30ART1LI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ART1LI/30ART1LI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In This Show, Art Imitates Art', 'kicker': 'Art Review | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In This Show, Art Imitates Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T00:26:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/074e38db-eec3-5577-b948-c4096d7e5ae8', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074e38db-eec3-5577-b948-c4096d7e5ae8'}, {'abstract': 'A police confrontation is the latest turn in Mohamed ElBaradei’s unexpected second career in Egypt’s politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/middleeast/29elbaradei.html', 'snippet': 'A police confrontation is the latest turn in Mohamed ElBaradei’s unexpected second career in Egypt’s politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO \x97 Mohamed ElBaradei, an Egyptian who won a Nobel Peace Prize for his work to promote nuclear nonproliferation, never made a very likely revolutionary leader. But there he was Friday, in a soft leather jacket and clip-on sunglasses, standing toe-to-toe with a line of hundreds of riot police several blocks long.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/world/29ELBARADEI/29ELBARADEI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/world/29ELBARADEI/29ELBARADEI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/world/29ELBARADEI/29ELBARADEI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nobelist Has an Unfamiliar Role in Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Protests, a Nobelist Has an Unfamiliar Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '