tract': 'With the ballot war finally settled, Rahm Emanuel and the other candidates for Chicago mayor resumed arguing about policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/us/politics/29chicago.html', 'snippet': 'With the ballot war finally settled, Rahm Emanuel and the other candidates for Chicago mayor resumed arguing about policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO \x97 The candidates for mayor of Chicago were back on the campaign trail on Friday, arguing about tax policy, a day after the Illinois Supreme Court ruled that Rahm Emanuel, the former White House chief of staff, could be included on the ballot. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/us/29chicago1_span/29chicago-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/29/us/29chicago1_span/29chicago-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/us/29chicago1_span/29chicago-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 525, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/us/29chicago1_span/29chicago-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/us/29chicago1_span/29chicago-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emanuel, Back in the Race, Is Also Back on the Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emanuel, Back in the Race, Is Also Back on the Trail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chico, Gery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Richard M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By EMMA GRAVES FITZSIMMONS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'Graves', 'lastname': 'FITZSIMMONS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/266991e6-4f0b-508b-885d-9c142eb1f519', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/266991e6-4f0b-508b-885d-9c142eb1f519'}, {'abstract': 'For young people, learning the social norms of the office is crucial for survival in the new economy.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/28/beyond-the-business-suit/', 'snippet': 'For young people, learning the social norms of the office is crucial for survival in the new economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, I wrote about Year Up, an organization that is unusually successful at preparing young adults from disadvantaged backgrounds for jobs in big companies like banks, investment houses, health care providers and technology firms. What became clear to me while researching the story was that workforce development no longer means giving people job skills; it means giving them the ability to navigate a career in a professional environment. This isn’t knowledge you’re born with. You pick it up from family and friends and, if you’re lucky, from mentors. Oddly, for something so important, it receives little emphasis in schools and colleges; many job training programs gloss over it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond the Business Suit', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Year Up', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb00dee-8541-518a-b055-3754561c57e3', 'word_count': 1402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb00dee-8541-518a-b055-3754561c57e3'}, {'abstract': 'Alberto Contador said that he would not stand for any punishment for failing a drug test last summer and that he was upset that cycling officials accepted his defense yet still wanted to bar him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/sports/cycling/29cycling.html', 'snippet': 'Alberto Contador said that he would not stand for any punishment for failing a drug test last summer and that he was upset that cycling officials accepted his defense yet still wanted to bar him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alberto Contador, the Tour de France champion from Spain, said Friday that he would challenge any punishment \x97 including being stripped of his Tour title \x97 for failing a drug test last summer. He continued to say that he was not at fault for ingesting the banned substance and said he intended to appeal the one-year suspension.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/y-cycling/y-cycling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 951, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/y-cycling/y-cycling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/y-cycling/y-cycling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contador Questions Process and Says He’ll Appeal Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contador Questions Process and Says He’ll Appeal Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contador, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Testing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Cycling Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68013c56-cf2a-58b0-8770-1138f21656e7', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68013c56-cf2a-58b0-8770-1138f21656e7'}, {'abstract': 'A British study of more than a million women indicates that those at the highest risk took hormones before or soon after menopause began.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/health/29hormone.html', 'snippet': 'A British study of more than a million women indicates that those at the highest risk took hormones before or soon after menopause began.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing evidence about the risks of breast cancer and other serious illnesses posed by hormone therapy for menopause has led many women to give up the drugs, and many doctors to stop recommending them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earlier Hormone Therapy Elevates Risk of Breast Cancer, Researchers Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Earlier Hormone Therapy Elevates Risk of Breast Cancer, Researchers Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menopause', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breasts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7e65572-4c06-563d-ae9d-3bfbbbe69fe7', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7e65572-4c06-563d-ae9d-3bfbbbe69fe7'}, {'abstract': 'New York City is one of the hardest places in the world to legally buy a gun. But there are places to find one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/nyregion/30critic.html', 'snippet': 'New York City is one of the hardest places in the world to legally buy a gun. But there are places to find one.', 'lead_paragraph': ' You don’t find a lot of retail businesses that officially turn away buyers. But when I visited the John Jovino Gun Shop, the city’s oldest, the mildest inquiry elicited a swift and gruff response. Show me your police identification, I was told, or goodbye. The store does not sell to civilians. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30CRITIC/30CRITIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30CRITIC/30CRITIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30CRITIC/30CRITIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30CRITIC/30CRITIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30CRITIC/30CRITIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Permit? No Touching the Pistols', 'kicker': 'City Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Permit? No Touc