one, 'print_headline': 'Agencies in Cost-Cutting California Told Not to Buy New Cars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:11:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850eb9c1-18f1-5663-826d-d1830f875bd2', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850eb9c1-18f1-5663-826d-d1830f875bd2'}, {'abstract': 'For the Tony Award-winning actress, Sunday is a day to sleep in, read scripts and enjoy the pace of a slowed-down city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/nyregion/30routine.html', 'snippet': 'For the Tony Award-winning actress, Sunday is a day to sleep in, read scripts and enjoy the pace of a slowed-down city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since receiving her big break (and bagging the first of her two Tony Awards) in “The Real Thing,” in 1984, Christine Baranski has carved a career across theater, film and television. Ms. Baranski is currently taking a dramatic turn as a partner in the Chicago law firm at the center of “The Good Wife” on CBS. She lives with her husband, the actor and writer Matthew Cowles, in Washington, Conn., where they raised their daughters, Lily and Isabel. While working in New York, Ms. Baranski, 58, stays in their Upper East Side apartment. DAVID ROONEY ON THE TOWN Happily, now after years of commuting to L.A. and trying to do the whole bicoastal thing, “The Good Wife” shoots in Greenpoint, Brooklyn. Our kids are grown up and in graduate school, so I have this life where I can enjoy the city and not worry about racing home to Connecticut.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-SPAN/30ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-SPAN/30ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-SPAN/30ROUTINE-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-SPAN/30ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-SPAN/30ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leisurely Day to Learn Her Lines', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Leisurely Day to Learn Her Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baranski, Christine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8118b03-0c20-5be5-8886-f0f8b0e5a125', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8118b03-0c20-5be5-8886-f0f8b0e5a125'}, {'abstract': 'Drilling into the Greenland icecap, Mr. Dansgaard was able to analyze ancient bubbles of trapped oxygen and gauge temperature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/europe/29dansgaard.html', 'snippet': 'Drilling into the Greenland icecap, Mr. Dansgaard was able to analyze ancient bubbles of trapped oxygen and gauge temperature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is said that every breath we take contains molecules breathed by Socrates, Jesus and Abraham Lincoln \x97 a notable exception being the ancient air that the Danish geophysicist Willi Dansgaard and his colleagues found trapped deep in the ice of Greenland.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/world/DANSGAARD-obit/DANSGAARD-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/world/DANSGAARD-obit/DANSGAARD-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/world/DANSGAARD-obit/DANSGAARD-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Willi Dansgaard Dies at 88; Read Climates in Old Ice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Willi Dansgaard, 88, Dies; Read Climates in Old Ice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:18:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b3bc23f-5e55-5d88-a125-572c36b3622a', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b3bc23f-5e55-5d88-a125-572c36b3622a'}, {'abstract': 'The proposal has been met with resistance from some New York lawmakers who are trying to save hundreds of state jobs in their districts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/nyregion/29prisons.html', 'snippet': 'The proposal has been met with resistance from some New York lawmakers who are trying to save hundreds of state jobs in their districts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY \x97 Nearly a month ago, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo made a call to close some prisons an emotional capstone of his first annual address to the Legislature, vowing, to sustained applause from fellow Democrats, that underused prisons would no longer be “an employment program” for upstate New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Republicans Resist Closing Prisons, Cuomo Is Said to Scale Back Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Republicans Resist Closing Prisons, Cuomo Is Said to Scale Back Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim and Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e440349-2b5c-5eaa-a616-3726ddaedc59', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e440349-2b5c-5eaa-a616-3726ddaedc59'}, {'abstract': 'Reports on diversification of the New York police force, the rivalry between passenger van companies, a woman’s mysterious death and reverse migration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/nyregion/30world.html', 'snippet': 'Reports on diversification of the New York police force, the rivalry between passenger van companies, a woman’s mysterious death and reverse migration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURING the past month, a newspaper aimed at the city’s South Asian population reported on the diversification of the New York police force, a Chinese-language paper explored the heated rivalry among passenger van companies, a Pakistani paper publicized the mysterious death of a woman, and a Korean paper wrote about the reverse migration to South Korea. KIRK SEMPLE', 'print_section': 'MB',