'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/europe/29briefs-France.html', 'snippet': 'The constitutional council upheld longstanding legislation on Friday that effectively bans marriage for same-sex couples.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The constitutional council upheld longstanding legislation on Friday that effectively bans marriage for same-sex couples. The council ruled that civil code references to marriage as a union between a man and woman were not contrary to the Constitution, and said the legislature could change the law if it saw fit. “The principle of equality prohibits neither that the legislature regulate differing situations in differing manners, nor that it depart from equality for reasons of general interest,” the decision said. Gay couples in France are allowed civil unions, which advocates say do not afford the same rights as marriage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Gay Marriage Ban Upheld', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Gay Marriage Ban Upheld', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T01:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', '