www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/africa/29briefs-Rwanda.html', 'snippet': 'Three people were killed in a grenade attack in the capital, Kigali, on Friday night, witnesses said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Three people were killed in a grenade attack in the capital, Kigali, on Friday night, witnesses said. Witnesses said a man riding a motorcycle tossed the grenade into a crowd and sped off. More than 25 people were wounded. Three suspects have been arrested. Violent crime is rare in Rwanda, though politics are getting turbulent. The government has blamed previous grenade attacks on rebel groups. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rwanda: Grenade Attack in Capital', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rwanda: Grenade Attack in Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:02:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6702bb19-003c-5d91-9451-a8539cc7926f', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6702bb19-003c-5d91-9451-a8539cc7926f'}, {'abstract': 'The disgraced financier Bernard Madoff remains a not-silent and not-invisible emotional partner for the woeful Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/sports/baseball/29vecsey.html', 'snippet': 