id': 'nyt://article/5e5aa368-7de0-5b3d-831a-35b9697b35d4', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e5aa368-7de0-5b3d-831a-35b9697b35d4'}, {'abstract': 'Protests begun over the disputed 2009 elections flared into violence last week after the deputy prime minister was implicated in a corruption scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/europe/29briefs-Albania.html', 'snippet': 'Protests begun over the disputed 2009 elections flared into violence last week after the deputy prime minister was implicated in a corruption scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Tens of thousands of antigovernment protesters marched down Tirana’s main street on Friday, despite appeals from Western officials to reduce the political tension. The demonstration commemorated the deaths of three protesters killed by National Guard officers last week. Protests begun over the disputed 2009 elections flared into violence last week after the deputy prime minister was implicated in a corruption scandal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albania: Tens of Thousands Protest', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Albania: Tens of Thousands Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANIA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Brunwasser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brunwasser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b4a5356-5c25-5864-86ca-e6e923773230', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b4a5356-5c25-5864-86ca-e6e923773230'}, {'abstract': 'For New York City residents living beyond Manhattan, the recent snowstorms mean more than delays in getting to work; vacation days spent shoveling are another concern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/nyregion/29snow.html', 'snippet': 'For New York City residents living beyond Manhattan, the recent snowstorms mean more than delays in getting to work; vacation days spent shoveling are another concern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leo Martinez spent a backache-inducing 40 minutes on Thursday clearing 19 inches of snow from the roof and windows of his S.U.V., in the winter wonderland that was East Tremont in the Bronx. It was hard work, but it was costing him, too: He had to pay the two men helping him dig out his car $10 each. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Bad Is the Snow? Depends Where You Live', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Bad Is the Snow? Depends Where You Live', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aba93684-f12e-5312-b832-ad3e59bd4783', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aba93684-f12e-5312-b832-ad3e59bd4783'}, {'abstract': 'The Vietnamese ambassador to China, told Chinese reporters on Thursday that China and Vietnam would hold a new round of talks on their territorial dispute in the South China Sea this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/asia/29webbrfs.html', 'snippet': 'The Vietnamese ambassador to China, told Chinese reporters on Thursday that China and Vietnam would hold a new round of talks on their territorial dispute in the South China Sea this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nguyen Van Tho, the Vietnamese ambassador to China, told Chinese reporters on Thursday that China and Vietnam would hold a new round of talks on their territorial dispute in the South China Sea this year, Chinese news organizations reported Friday. He declined to name a specific date, but said, “I am optimistic about this issue,” the reports said. Both countries and other Asian nations claim parts of the South China Sea, which has potentially large oil and natural gas deposits. The territorial dispute is one of the thorniest diplomatic issues between China and Vietnam. They also take different approaches to trying to resolve the dispute: Vietnam prefers multilateral negotiations, with all the countries at the table, while China prefers bilateral talks. Last July, the United States surprised China when it said it had “national interests” in the area and wanted China to abide by a declaration of conduct that China had reached in 2002 with other Asian nations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China and Vietnam to Talk on Sea Dispute', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e9f761-08e5-5a90-b802-ea8051de4274', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e9f761-08e5-5a90-b802-ea8051de4274'}, {'abstract': 'It is difficult to predict what role the military might play in quelling protests or easing President Hosni Mubarak from power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/world/middleeast/29forces.html', 'snippet': 'It is difficult to predict what role the military might play in quelling protests or easing President Hosni Mubarak from power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as armored military vehicles deployed around important Egyptian government institutions on Friday for the first time in decades, it remained difficult to predict what role the armed forces might play in either quelling the disturbances or easing President Hosni Mubarak from power. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Military Is Seen as Pivotal in Next Step', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Respected Military Is Seen as Pivotal in What Happens Next', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/885a5b7a-1b6d-55c7-afb7-1909a3b3e425', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/885a5b7a-1b6d-55c7-afb7-1909a3b3e425'}, {'abstract': 'Homosexuals living in the nation illegally and seeking protection against being deported to less tolerant societies may risk being viewed as not openly gay enough to qualify.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/nyregion/29asylum.html', 'snippet': 'Homosexuals living in the nation illegally and seeking protection against being deported to less tolerant societies may risk being viewed as not openly gay enough to qualify.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Romulo Castro considered attending his asylum interview in Rosedale, Queens, dressed as Fidela Castro, a towering drag queen in six-inch stilettos, a bright green poodle skirt and a mane of strawberry blond hair. In the end, Mr. Castro, 34, opted for what he described as understatement: pink eye shadow, a bright pink V-neck shirt and intermittent outbursts of tears. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/ASYLUM/ASYLUM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/ASYLUM/ASYLUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/nyregion/ASYLUM/ASYLUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gays Seeking Asylum in U.S. Encounter a New Hurdle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gays Seeking Asylum in U.S. Encounter A New Hurdle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens Pride House', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizenship and Immigration Services (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2e674f-2ef1-5fa1-92e4-10be2a16ce35', 'word_count': 1396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2e674f-2ef1-5fa1-92e4-10be2a16ce35'}, {'abstract': 'As N.F.L. linemen grow ever larger — from one 300-pound player in 1970 to 532 in 2010 — studies question the players’ health risks and find conflicting answers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/sports/football/29weight.html', 'snippet': 'As N.F.L. linemen grow ever larger — from one 300-pound player in 1970 to 532 in 2010 — studies question the players’ health risks and find conflicting answers.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When B. J. Raji nimbly intercepted a pass and shimmied in the end zone last Sunday, helping to put Green Bay into the Super Bowl, the feat was remarkable given that Raji is a nose tackle and, at 337 pounds, is thought to be the largest player to score a postseason touchdown in N.F.L. history.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/WEIGHTsilo/WEIGHTsilo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/WEIGHTsilo/WEIGHTsilo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/29/sports/WEIGHTsilo/WEIGHTsilo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Linemen Tip the Scales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SUPERBOWL XLV; TIPPING THE SCALES OVER', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raji, B J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T02:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d64b013-7b90-57d5-8c44-c30d9d17044b', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d64b013-7b90-57d5-8c44-c30d9d17044b'}, {'abstract': 'The percentage of workers who car-pool has dropped by almost half since 1980, according to data from the Census Bureau, confounding efforts by urban planners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/us/29carpool.html', 'snippet': 'The percentage of workers who car-pool has dropped by almost half since 1980, according to data from the Census Bureau, confounding efforts by urban planners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOODBRIDGE, Va. \x97 Remember the 1970s? Watergate, disco, oil embargoes and, of course, car-pooling. Many big companies organized group rides for th