ble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gretzky, Somehow, Is Out of Hockey', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gretzky, Wayne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T20:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein and Stu Hackel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hackel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/51505a43-6401-5646-8b19-5dda47dd8f3b', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51505a43-6401-5646-8b19-5dda47dd8f3b'}, {'abstract': 'A driver of a Lexus who the police said drove away after striking a food deliveryman was arrested a few blocks away.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/hit-and-run-driver-injures-cyclist-near-times-square/', 'snippet': 'A driver of a Lexus who the police said drove away after striking a food deliveryman was arrested a few blocks away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A food deliveryman was seriously injured by a hit-and-run driver who struck his bicycle from behind near Times Square about 10:15 p.m. Friday, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hit-and-Run Driver Injures Cyclist Near Times Square', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T20:56:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ae44f3d-3c70-5ce1-b082-c684bda3861d', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ae44f3d-3c70-5ce1-b082-c684bda3861d'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Sharp is a Twitter “ambassador” of sorts, whose job is to help government make better use of the service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/us/politics/30twitter.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Sharp is a Twitter “ambassador” of sorts, whose job is to help government make better use of the service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Adam Sharp fits in well in the Beltway political scene where he used to work \x97 first in the office of Senator Mary L. Landrieu, and then as the executive producer for digital services at C-Span. But his new job, as Twitter’s Washington liaison, requires a slightly different skill set.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter, as a Helpmate, Goes to Capitol Hill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twitter’s Man on Capitol Hill Is an Evangelist Whose Message is the Medium', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T21:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab11b067-f620-58bb-9815-f794b046caf0', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab11b067-f620-58bb-9815-f794b046caf0'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed rules being considered by the governing body for amateur hockey in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/29/usa-hockeys-proposed-rule-changes-for-body-checking-head-shots-and-fighting/', 'snippet': 'Proposed rules being considered by the governing body for amateur hockey in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Below, the full set of rule changes proposed at USA Hockey’s Winter Meeting last weekend in Colorado Springs. The proposals seek to raise the minimum age for body checking in boys hockey from 11-12 to 13-14, make all contact to the head-and-neck area illegal at all age levels and, in those classifications in which fighting does not result in immediate expulsion, provide for extra penalties when one player tears off an his own helmet or an opponent’s helmet during a fight. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'USA Hockey’s Proposed Rule Changes for Body-Checking, Head Shots and Fighting', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Hockey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-29T21:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/83506452-8b8f-539a-8efd-1ce51c9ff2f0', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83506452-8b8f