'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af65999-c794-585c-b9ca-0011f9cc0d47', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af65999-c794-585c-b9ca-0011f9cc0d47'}, {'abstract': 'The McMurdo Marathon brings together a small field of runners on a course at the bottom of the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/sports/30antarctica.html', 'snippet': 'The McMurdo Marathon brings together a small field of runners on a course at the bottom of the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McMURDO STATION, Antarctica \x97 A hulking orange all-terrain bus emblazoned with the words Ivan the Terra Bus rumbled to the starting line of the 13th annual McMurdo Marathon, and 17 runners and 6 skiers stepped onto the ice shelf. On this Sunday morning, Jan. 16, the temperature was a balmy 28 degrees, with a nearly cloudless sky and a strong sun. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/antarctica2/antarctica2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/antarctica2/antarctica2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/antarctica2/antarctica2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/antarctica2/antarctica2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/antarctica2/antarctica2-thumbStandard