 were even a few singalongs of the Egyptian national anthem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Protests Extend to Streets of New York', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T00:54:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a070705a-936c-52aa-84a9-ea3f9ab3862a', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a070705a-936c-52aa-84a9-ea3f9ab3862a'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said concern about a potential power vacuum drove President Obama’s decision not to call for Mr. Mubarak’s resignation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/world/middleeast/30diplo.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said concern about a potential power vacuum drove President Obama’s decision not to call for Mr. Mubarak’s resignation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 President Obama’s decision to stop short, at least for now, of calling for Hosni Mubarak’s resignation was driven by the administration’s concern that it could lose all leverage over the Egyptian president, and because it feared creating a power vacuum inside the country, according to administration officials involved in the debate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama