e the team’s general manager, Sandy Alderson now seems uniquely qualified to help the Mets with their on and off field problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/sports/baseball/30alderson.html', 'snippet': 'Considered by some as overqualified to be the team’s general manager, Sandy Alderson now seems uniquely qualified to help the Mets with their on and off field problems.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When Sandy Alderson was hired by the Mets in October to be their new general manager, some wondered if he was overqualified for the job. He had already been the chief executive of the San Diego Padres, an executive vice president of Major League Baseball, and, most recently, Commissioner Bud Selig’s point man in baseball’s efforts to attack the issues plaguing the development of teenage prospects in the Dominican Republic. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/sub-mets/sub-mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/sub-mets/sub-mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/30/sports/sub-mets/sub-mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alderson Is Perfectly Suited to Steer the Mets', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alderson Is Perfectly Suited to Steer the Mets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDERSON, SANDY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'