lpture', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T11:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b90c420e-3eed-5c44-b563-9b761bf994a5', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b90c420e-3eed-5c44-b563-9b761bf994a5'}, {'abstract': 'In a commanding performance, Novak Djokovic outplayed Andy Murray, 6-4, 6-2, 6-3, to capture the Australian Open championship.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/djokovic-wins-second-australian-open-title/', 'snippet': 'In a commanding performance, Novak Djokovic outplayed Andy Murray, 6-4, 6-2, 6-3, to capture the Australian Open championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back and forth, the two punched and counterpunched like heavyweights. If the Australian Open men’s singles final between No. 3 Novak Djokovic and No. 5 Andy Murray resembled a grueling boxing match, each lightning-quick jab met with an exquisite parry, it was also a master chess duel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic Wins Second Australian Open Title', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 