44-d1f6bf2a7a08', 'word_count': 3408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2647ddd-8f96-5483-a644-d1f6bf2a7a08'}, {'abstract': 'Novak Djokovic won his second Australian Open title by defeating Andy Murray, his boyhood friend, 6-4, 6-2, 6-3, on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/sports/tennis/31tennis.html', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic won his second Australian Open title by defeating Andy Murray, his boyhood friend, 6-4, 6-2, 6-3, on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — Into the stands went the shirt. Into the stands went the shoes. Into the chair plopped Novak Djokovic, looking weary — very weary — yet fulfilled.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/31tennis_final1/31tennis_final1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/31tennis_final1/31tennis_final1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/31tennis_final1/31tennis_final1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer and Nadal ... and Djokovic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federer And Nadal ... and Djokovic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T12:39:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0acd8e63-6ece-58e5-8c6c-253d2525c663', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0acd8e63-6ece-58e5-8c6c-253d2525c663'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following the continuing protests in Egypt on Sunday, as demonstrators press their demand for an end to the autocratic rule of President Hosni Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/latest-updates-on-day-6-of-egypt-protests/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following the continuing protests in Egypt on Sunday, as demonstrators press their demand for an end to the autocratic rule of President Hosni Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede is following the continuing street protests in Egypt on Sunday. For a summary of the latest events, see the main news article by my colleagues in Egypt. There is a stream of Twitter updates by bloggers and journalists we’re following to the right. Updates below mix alerts on breaking news with reports from other Web sites and eyewitness accounts, video and photographs posted on social networks. Readers who want to share information with us can write in the comment thread below or send photographs or video from Egypt to pix@nyt.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on Day 6 of Egypt Protests', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T15:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ed89649-ab82-5ada-ae7b-58c9234646b7', 'word_count': 3853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ed89649-ab82-5ada-ae7b-58c9234646b7'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton urged Egyptians to take up a national dialogue that would lead to free and fair elections this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/world/middleeast/31clinton.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton urged Egyptians to take up a national dialogue that would lead to free and fair elections this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON \x97 Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Sunday urged Egyptians to take up a national dialogue that would lead to free and fair elections this fall and, while not explicitly distancing the United States from the embattled President Hosni Mubarak, said that the United States stood “ready to help with the kind of transition that will lead to greater political and economic freedom.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Urges Egyptian Dialogue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Urges Egyptian Dialogue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T15:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c354dd0-8552-5b1e-847c-239e9e775b77', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c354dd0-8552-5b1e-847c-239e9e775b77'}, {'abstract': 'During a six-hour ceremony, Tom Hooper took best director honors for “The King’s Speech,” scrambling the race in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/an-upset-for-kings-speech-at-directors-guild-awards/', 'snippet': 'During a six-hour ceremony, Tom Hooper took best director honors for “The King’s Speech,” scrambling the race in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— Tom Hooper, the director of “The King’s Speech,” picked up the top prize at the Directors Guild of America awards on Saturday night, a surprise victory that scrambled the prognostications of the Oscar experts. The win came at the expense of another front-runner, David Fincher, the director of “The Social Network,” and followed a similar upset at the Producers Guild of America awards when the British period drama took the top honor. (David O. Russell (“The Fighter”), Darren Aronofsky (“Black Swan”) and Christopher Nolan (“Inception”) were the other nominees last night.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Upset for ‘King’s Speech’ at Directors Guild Awards', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Directors Guild of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T15:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/575cf34d-db89-5dc4-9cca-edbfa7027349', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/575cf34d-db89-5dc4-9cca-edbfa7027349'}, {'abstract': 'The three leaders appealed for free elections, but fell short of calling for the resignation of President Hosni Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/world/europe/31europe.html', 'snippet': 'The three leaders appealed for free elections, but fell short of calling for the resignation of President Hosni Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN \x97 With the European Union yet to form a common response to the mass demonstrations in the Arab world, leaders of three of its diplomatic heavyweights appealed for free and fair elections in Egypt over the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Key European Leaders Urge Restraint in Cairo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Key Europeans Urge Restraint in Cairo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T16:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Dempsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dempsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33cae4f0-ff5b-5e6b-a7c1-187edbf85754', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33cae4f0-ff5b-5e6b-a7c1-187edbf85754'}, {'abstract': 'In “Alan Lomax: The Man Who Recorded the World,” John Szwed, a biographer of Miles Davis and Sun Ra, covers the life of a tireless music folklorist and anthologist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/books/31book.html', 'snippet': 'In “Alan Lomax: The Man Who Recorded the World,” John Szwed, a biographer of Miles Davis and Sun Ra, covers the life of a tireless music folklorist and anthologist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1961, as a young graduate student at an ethnomusicologists’ meeting, John Szwed caught the eye of the master: Alan Lomax, the man whose tremendous body of work allowed previously unheard folk recordings to become universally well known. Seemingly apropos of nothing, Lomax remarked “Pygmies are a baseline culture.” Then he went on his way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 947, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Singing the Perfectionist-Folkie Blues', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singing the Perfectionist-Folkie Blues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lomax, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Szwed, John F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0957cc4-956a-5a48-a9dc-127df5a5a6bf', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0957cc4-956a-5a48-a9dc-127df5a5a6bf'}, {'abstract': 'Where the big price hikes are.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/this-age-of-rubber/', 'snippet': 'Where the big price hikes are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest IMF World Economic Outlook update has, as usual, a lot of useful information. I was especially struck by the chart on commodity prices, which highlights something I only sort of appreciated before: the big runup this year has been neither in food nor in energy, but rather in agricultural raw materials:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Age of Rubber', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfe3a099-585f-5b12-a49c-7569c5a9f902', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfe3a099-585f-5b12-a49c-7569c5a9f902'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Geiss helped “Sesame Street” win 22 daytime Emmy Awards and invented several Muppets characters, including Abby Cadabby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/arts/television/31geiss.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Geiss helped “Sesame Street” win 22 daytime Emmy Awards and invented several Muppets characters, including Abby Cadabby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tony Geiss, who entertained generations of children by putting words in the mouths of Big Bird, Kermit the Frog, Elmo and other characters on “Sesame Street,” helping the show win 22 daytime Emmys for scriptwriting and songwriting, died on Jan. 21 in Valhalla, N.Y. He was 86 and lived in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/31geiss_1/31geiss_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/31geiss_1/31geiss_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/31geiss_1/31geiss_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Geiss, Writer for ‘Sesame Street,’ Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tony Geiss, 86, Scriptwriter for ‘Sesame Street’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sesame Workshop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Television Workshop", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cd0aec1-1b5f-5219-9c55-749fd951bc49', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cd0aec1-1b5f-5219-9c55-749fd951bc49'}, {'abstract': 'The future isn’t what it used to be.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/the-kitchen-test/', 'snippet': 'The future isn’t what it used to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyler Cowen argues that technological change since the early 1960s hasn’t been as transformative for ordinary peoples’ lives as the change that went before. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kitchen Test', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:29:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4716f518-d5b2-5aa6-b463-ae92a17c1f14', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4716f518-d5b2-5aa6-b463-ae92a17c1f14'}, {'abstract': 'Japan is once again the champion of the continent after defeating Australia to win the Asian Cup in Qatar.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/the-final-the-asian-game-comes-of-age/', 'snippet': 'Japan is once again the champion of the continent after defeating Australia to win the Asian Cup in Qatar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — The Asian Cup final Saturday night between Australia and Japan was tied 0-0 after 90 minutes of regulation play and the first 15 minutes of extra time at Khalifa Stadium in Doha. Then Tadanari Lee came on as a substitute for the Blue Samurai, and within three minutes drove an airborne volley from Yuto Nagatomo past Mark Schwarzer into the back of the Socceroos’ net. The Aussies had a final chance to tie the game in the 119th minute when David Carney had a free kick on goal deflected, securing the 1-0 victory for Japan. Keisuke Honda was named the tournament’s most valuable player. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Final: The Asian Game Comes of Age', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghotbi, Afshin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doha (Qatar)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Behrooz Afrakhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Behrooz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afrakhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e847fa22-0d17-56bc-9cdb-08c4c91ddab1', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e847fa22-0d17-56bc-9cdb-08c4c91ddab1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Patterson and his wife at the time, Phyllis, are widely credited with having created the first modern Renaissance fair, begun in Southern California in 1963.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/us/31patterson.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Patterson and his wife at the time, Phyllis, are widely credited with having created the first modern Renaissance fair, begun in Southern California in 1963.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Patterson, who nearly half a century ago helped found the country’s first Renaissance fair, which inspired a thriving nationwide industry of jousters and jesters, hawking street vendors and brave men in doublets and tights, died on Jan. 15 in Sausalito, Calif. He was 80. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/us/31patterson/31patterson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/01/31/us/31patterson/31patterson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/us/31patterson/31patterson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/us/31patterson/31patterson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/us/31patterson/31patterson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ron Patterson, Renaissance (Fair) Man, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ron Patterson, Renaissance (Fair) Man\nAnd Fan of the 16th Century, Dies at 80', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:40:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/548aca32-1b52-5fa1-9f6d-888bb726c729', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/548aca32-1b52-5fa1-9f6d-888bb726c729'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cavill, a British actor whose credits include “Stardust” and “Immortals,” continues the tradition of having relative unknowns play the Man of Steel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/henry-cavill-is-cast-as-superman-in-new-movie/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cavill, a British actor whose credits include “Stardust” and “Immortals,” continues the tradition of having relative unknowns play the Man of Steel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mythology of comic books, Superman is the survivor of a dying alien planet who is sent to earth to become its protector. For his new Superman movie, the director Zack Snyder did not have to search quite as far to cast his title character, but in the tradition of previous installments of the franchise, he has settled on a relative unknown to take up the mantle of the Man of Steel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Henry Cavill is Cast as Superman in New Movie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavill, Henry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Zack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T17:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb723303-472a-545d-8b0d-dac1ba04676e', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb723303-472a-545d-8b0d-dac1ba04676e'}, {'abstract': 'Top Israeli offi