the published papers of Washington, Jefferson, John Adams, James Madison, Alexander Hamilton and Benjamin Franklin on a free Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/a-digital-future-for-the-founding-fathers/', 'snippet': 'The University of Virginia Press is in the process of putting the published papers of Washington, Jefferson, John Adams, James Madison, Alexander Hamilton and Benjamin Franklin on a free Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justice Antonin Scalia of the Supreme Court visited the Capitol last week to lecture representatives about the Constitution, at the invitation of Representative Michele Bachmann, the Minnesota Republican and Tea Party leader. Some people may be interested in seeing what the founders themselves had to say, and thanks to digital technology, an increasing number of original documents can be found online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Digital Future for the Founding Fathers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Historical Publications and Records Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T19:38:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'ty