b_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/sports/ncaabasketball/31stjohns.html', 'snippet': 'The Red Storm, which had lost 5 of 6 coming into Sunday, led by double digits for much of the game and handily defeated the Blue Devils.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jogging onto the Madison Square Garden floor on Sunday afternoon, the Duke Blue Devils were greeted by the St. John’s student rooting section with the inhospitable chant of “overrated.” By late in the second half of a nonconference shocker, what had sounded like the overstatement of deluded youth resonated more as reasonable assertion, if not point of fact.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/YSTJOHNS/YSTJOHNS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/YSTJOHNS/YSTJOHNS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/sports/YSTJOHNS/YSTJOHNS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'St. John’s Stuns Duke From Start to Finish', 'kicker': "St. John's 93, Duke 78", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'St. John’s Stuns Duke From Start To Finish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T22:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62817abc-1d37-5c51-bf6e-5b2f006d197e', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62817abc-1d37-5c51-bf6e-5b2f006d197e'}, {'abstract': 'A Juilliard Focus! Festival concert celebrating the Polish composer Witold Lutoslawski used chance music to vivid effect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/arts/music/31focus.html', 'snippet': 'A Juilliard Focus! Festival concert celebrating the Polish composer Witold Lutoslawski used chance music to vivid effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most classical works written after the Baroque era little is left to chance, with the composer specifying notes, tempos, dynamics and phrasing. In aleatoric, or chance, music, on the other hand, some elements of the score are more spontaneous.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/FOCUS/FOCUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 764, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Composer Who Rolled the Dice', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Composer Who Rolled The Dice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lutoslawski, Witold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milarsky, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T22:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e35a9e43-af38-57e5-9895-6975f35e1a4c', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e35a9e43-af38-57e5-9895-6975f35e1a4c'}, {'abstract': 'Layard Thompson performed his dance solo “Spellin’ Flashhhh Lightsssss,” full of grimaces and nonsense syllables, at the FLICfest in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/arts/dance/31flicfest.html', 'snippet': 'Layard Thompson performed his dance solo “Spellin’ Flashhhh Lightsssss,” full of grimaces and nonsense syllables, at the FLICfest in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Irondale Center is a gorgeous place to take in a performance. For the past two weekends this former Sunday school in the Lafayette Avenue Presbyterian Church in Fort Greene, Brooklyn, has been home to FLICfest (Feature-Length Independent Choreography), a new festival of dance created by Jeramy Zimmerman. But on Friday night the generous, romantically dilapidated room was thrown into darkness when the Bessie Award-winning Layard Thompson performed his solo “Spellin’ Flashhhh Lightsssss.” As the title \x97 typical of Mr. Thompson’s eccentric spelling \x97 indicates, flashlights, wielded by Mr. Thompson, provided most of the illumination. They cast jagged beams or big, eyelike circles on the green, peeling walls and warm wood floor, serving as a counterpoint to the night sky, rimmed by the large, graceful windows along the balcony.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/FLICFEST/FLICFEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 572, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/FLICFEST/FLICFEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/arts/FLICFEST/FLICFEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Otherworldly Wildness This Way Comes', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Otherworldly Wildness This Way Comes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Layard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T22:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e02d4067-9eb1-5e30-aabf-fe2dd8c7016e', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e02d4067-9eb1-5e30-aabf-fe2dd8c7016e'}, {'abstract': 'Rebeca Tomás and her dancers brought out the festive side of flamenco at Theater 80 St. Marks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/arts/dance/31tomas.html', 'snippet': 'Rebeca Tomás and her dancers brought out the festive side of flamenco at Theater 80 St. Marks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebeca Tomás has the kind of ingénue appeal that brings out the joyful and festive side of flamenco. In other words, if you like your flamenco infused with tragedy, look elsewhere: her soulfulness, at best, is forcefully fresh and poetically tender. On Friday night she returned to Theater 80 St. Marks, a scrappy, intimate space that retains a quirky element of the East Village \x97 the curtain was delayed as an usher went on a spider hunt \x97 with her group of dancers and excellent musicians, led by Pedro Cortés. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flamenco With Soulfulness and a Burst of Springtime', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flamenco With Soulfulness and a Burst of Springtime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamenco (Dance)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomas, Rebeca', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T22:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba864c2c-8191-544a-a0e5-9d9775c0db74', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba864c2c-8191-544a-a0e5-9d9775c0db74'}, {'abstract': 'From the District 3 Winter Regional, a look at the trap pass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/crosswords/bridge/31card.html', 'snippet': 'From the District 3 Winter Regional, a look at the trap pass.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Look at the South hand in the diagramed deal. You are vulnerable against nonvulnerable opponents. East opens two spades, a weak two-bid. What would you do?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Weak Two-Bid, to Lurk or to Jump In?', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Weak Two-Bid, to Lurk or to Jump In?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'nam