N.F.L. in 2007.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Future Arrives at Rutgers, Again', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-30T22:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristian R. Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristian', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/901fec22-e961-5d35-844e-9d16b99d4f1c', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/901fec22-e961-5d35-844e-9d16b99d4f1c'}, {'abstract': 'Inflation is starting to slow China’s export machine as buyers from Western companies balk at higher prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/business/global/31trade.html', 'snippet': 'Inflation is starting to slow China’s export machine as buyers from Western companies balk at higher prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG \x97 Inflation is starting to slow China’s mighty export machine, as buyers from Western multinational companies balk at higher prices and have cut back their planned spring shipments across the Pacific. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/business/trade/trade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation in China May Limit U.S. Trade Deficit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inflation in China May Limit U.S. Trade Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject'