xpected hopefuls, including the best actor nod for Colin Firth.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/30/kings-speech-gets-another-push/', 'snippet': 'There were no surprises in the movie categories at the Screen Actors Guild awards, which on Sunday night bestowed prizes on all the expected hopefuls, including the best actor nod for Colin Firth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— There were no surprises in the movie categories at the Screen Actors Guild awards, which on Sunday night bestowed prizes on all the expected hopefuls: Melissa Leo and Christian Bale as best supporting actors in “The Fighter;” Natalie Portman as best actress for “Black Swan;” and Colin Firth as best actor for “The King’s Speech.” That movie also picked up the group’s version of best picture, the best ensemble prize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘King’s Speech’ Gets Another Push', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bale, Christian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Firth, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leo, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Natalie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T03:27:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c8ede3b-a289-52d0-93cf-fae90b9c90dd', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c8ede3b-a289-52d0-93cf-fae90b9c90dd'}, {'abstract': 'The lack of attention on a big tobacco lawsuit 