, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb32a9c7-cc05-5118-ad0b-f380e8592887'}, {'abstract': 'Off the Rails: Let’s try that again. The Metropolitan Transportation Authority outlines its goals for the year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/m-t-a-puts-new-aspirations-under-an-old-title/', 'snippet': 'Off the Rails: Let’s try that again. The Metropolitan Transportation Authority outlines its goals for the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago — before the fare increases, prior to the service cuts, back when the W and V trains still rumbled on their now-silenced routes beneath the city — the Metropolitan Transportation Authority published a glossy manifesto outlining its aims and aspirations for 2010. The pamphlet, a brisk 24-page primer, was christened after the agency’s newly adopted ethos: “Making Every Dollar Count.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.T.A. Puts New Aspirations Under an Old Title', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walder, Jay H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T14:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da6bc03-2a36-5631-a9b8-788e2e354bb2', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da6bc03-2a36-5631-a9b8-788e2e354bb2'}, {'abstract': '