 smart electricity meters and other consumer-focused items from Monday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/monday-reading-new-payment-models-for-realtors/', 'snippet': 'Agents taking less than a 6 percent commission, a backlash against smart electricity meters and other consumer-focused items from Monday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: New Payment Models for Realtors', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T15:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saranow Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Saranow', 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfaec87c-e9dc-59c9-b7a1-64f6871ca66c', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfaec87c-e9dc-59c9-b7a1-64f6871ca66c'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared their favorite things. All who participated will receive “brown paper packages tied up with strings”; the following will have them delivered by “wild geese that fly with the moon on their wings.”', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/bright-leaves-in-autumn-and-cats-that-are-purring/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared their favorite things. All who participated will receive “brown paper packages tied up with strings”; the following will have them delivered by “wild geese that fly with the moon on their wings...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously shared their favorite things.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bright Leaves in Autumn and Cats that Are Purring', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T15:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/03af1420-eb08-5cc8-ac5d-e6fb8bee0ccd', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03af1420-eb08-5cc8-ac5d-e6fb8bee0ccd'}, {'abstract': 'The latest episode of this HBO series demonstrated the contradiction between a man’s vision of himself as a do-good reformer and the reality of him has an insensitive lughead.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/big-love-watch-two-faces-of-bill-henrickson/', 'snippet': 'The latest episode of this HBO series demonstrated the contradiction between a man’s vision of himself as a do-good reformer and the reality of him has an insensitive lughead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So now we know just what kind of a sexist pig Bill Henrickson really is. He is the kind who buys the youngest of his three wives a bathroom scale for Christmas right after she has given birth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Big Love’ Watch: Two Faces of Bill Henrickson', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paxton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T15:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aae32f4-b8fb-5dbc-9889-b387eb5a9d64', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aae32f4-b8fb-5dbc-9889-b387eb5a9d64'}, {'abstract': 'The president of the Managed Funds Association said his organization contacted the S.E.C. a few weeks ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/hedge-fund-group-seeks-guidance-on-expert-networks/', 'snippet': 'The president of the Managed Funds Association said his organization contacted the S.E.C. a few weeks ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALM BEACH, Fla. — The country’s largest hedge fund lobbying group has asked the Securities and Exchange Commission for guidance on using “expert networks,” a business that has been under scrutiny after a series of arrests linked to an investigation of insider trading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Group Seeks Guidance on Expert Networks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T15:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/87430576-4af2-5739-931e-47d15825b5f8', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87430576-4af2-5739-931e-47d15825b5f8'}, {'abstract': 'Intel said that 5 percent of the Series 6, or Cougar Point, chipset, which recently started shipping, might fail over the next three to five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/technology/01chip.html', 'snippet': 'Intel said that 5 percent of the Series 6, or Cougar Point, chipset, which recently started shipping, might fail over the next three to five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO \x97 Intel said on Monday it had stopped shipping a new chipset after discovering a design flaw that might cause 5 percent of the chips to fail over the next three to five years. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intel, Finding a Chip Flaw, Expects to Lose $1 Billion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intel, Finding a Chip Flaw, Expects to Lose $1 Billion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T15:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verne G. Kopytoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/406cb81e-c6fb-5a91-8a49-33baf08a75a3', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406cb81e-c6fb-5a91-8a49-33baf08a75a3'}, {'abstract': 'Describe your first apartment in New York City, in all its fabulousness or lack thereof.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/appraisal-sidebar/', 'snippet': 'Describe your first apartment in New York City, in all its fabulousness or lack thereof.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What do you remember about your first New York apartment? Was it a mouse-infested closet? A flat with a fake dividing wall? Perhaps it was a fabulous space with persnickety roommates. This week’s Appraisal features a fiction author’s real-life reminiscences about her first apartment, where her roommates included so many mice that she learned to make plans, lots of plans, so that she was never home. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us About Your First New York Apartment', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPRAISALS AND VALUATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:09:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4286bf7a-ea3a-5d54-89e7-2e0a7d4eb237', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4286bf7a-ea3a-5d54-89e7-2e0a7d4eb237'}, {'abstract': 'Jill Kargman, in a chapter of “Sometimes I Feel Like a Nut,” recalls the charms of living in a rodent-ridden Upper East Side apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/nyregion/01appraisal.html', 'snippet': 'Jill Kargman, in a chapter of “Sometimes I Feel Like a Nut,” recalls the charms of living in a rodent-ridden Upper East Side apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Some girls chart the chapters of their lives by jobs or guys or haircuts; I do it by real estate.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i