, travel agencies and other businesses have been surprised by the demand for their services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/sports/football/01fans.html', 'snippet': 'Ticket brokers, travel agencies and other businesses have been surprised by the demand for their services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just moments after the Green Bay Packers beat the Chicago Bears for the N.F.C. championship, Tony Hoes ran for the phone to call Titletown Tickets, a tour operator. After waiting nervously on hold, Hoes plunked down $10,000 for two trip packages to suburban Dallas so he and his wife can see the Packers play in the Super Bowl for the first time in 13 years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/sports/cty-fans-1/cty-fans-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/02/01/sports/cty-fans-1/cty-fans-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/sports/cty-fans-1/cty-fans-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/sports/cty-fans-1/cty-fans-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/sports/cty-fans-1/cty-fans-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rabid Fans Put Dallas on Itinerary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rabid Fans Put Dallas on Their Itinerary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f302c751-aaef-51f6-8344-f175d94fffab', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f302c751-aaef-51f6-8344-f175d94fffab'}, {'abstract': 'Hamas and the Palestinian Authority have kept silent, fearing that unrest could spread to their areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/world/middleeast/01palestinians.html', 'snippet': 'Hamas and the Palestinian Authority have kept silent, fearing that unrest could spread to their areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA \x97The Hamas rulers of Gaza and the rival Palestinian Authority leadership of the West Bank rarely see eye-to-eye on anything. But with mass protests rocking Egypt, across Gaza’s southern border, the Palestinian adversaries have united in maintaining a cautious silence, hedging their bets given the unpredictability of the outcome and clearly concerned about a possible spread of popular unrest to their areas. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Adversaries Unite, for Now, on Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinian Adversaries Are United in Cautious Quiet Over the Unrest in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram and Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7cabd4e-18a0-5eb0-8629-dec91130ef6e', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7cabd4e-18a0-5eb0-8629-dec91130ef6e'}, {'abstract': 'The latest federal nutrition guidelines reiterate much from previous years, but this time, they also suggest just consuming less.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/business/01food.html', 'snippet': 'The latest federal nutrition guidelines reiterate much from previous years, but this time, they also suggest just consuming less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the nation’s obesity crisis continues unabated, federal regulators on Monday issued their bluntest nutrition advice to date: drink water instead of sugary drinks like soda, fill your plate with fruits and vegetables and cut down on processed foods filled with sodium, fat or sugar.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/business/01food-span/01food-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/02/01/business/01food-span/01food-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/business/01food-span/01food-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/business/01food-span/01food-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/business/01food-span/01food-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Government’s Dietary Advice: Eat Less', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Guidelines Praised for Urging Less Food and Soda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57427dc7-3b86-5261-b301-09884c73a059', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57427dc7-3b86-5261-b301-09884c73a059'}, {'abstract': 'Focusing on what the Dow did yesterday, or last month (or what it will do next month) will probably lead you astray when managing your money.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/the-case-for-ignoring-the-stock-market/', 'snippet': 'Focusing on what the Dow did yesterday, or last month (or what it will do next month) will probably lead you astray when managing your money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog, and other drawings are available on his personal Web site, BehaviorGap.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for Ignoring the Stock Market', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc450462-caa1-5c4c-9e1c-9debde278deb', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc450462-caa1-5c4c-9e1c-9debde278deb'}, {'abstract': 'A dispatch from the former Playland Arcade in Coney Island, at a moment when more of Coney’s venerable remaining institutions are being shut down.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/in-the-ruins-of-playland-artifacts-of-better-days/', 'snippet': 'A dispatch from the former Playland Arcade in Coney Island, at a moment when more of Coney’s venerable remaining institutions are being shut down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nathan Kensinger, photo-chronicler extraordinaire of the city’s abandoned spaces, returns this morning with a lavishly illustrated dispatch from the Playland Arcade in Coney Island, which flourished, to varying degrees, from 1935 until 1982. It comes at a moment in Coney’s history when several of its more venerable remaining institutions are getting the boot, when, Mr. Kensinger writes, “Cha Cha’s and Ruby’s have served their last drinks and have, in turn, been served with eviction papers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Ruins of Playland, Artifacts of Better Days', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:42:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/074b93ea-9793-5ada-ae2f-85543e350594', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074b93ea-9793-5ada-ae2f-85543e350594'}, {'abstract': 'There is safety in numbers in Cairo, but Ed Ou is trying, when he can, to break away from the photo pack.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/getting-into-cairos-byways/', 'snippet': 'There is safety in numbers in Cairo, but Ed Ou is trying, when he can, to break away from the photo pack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Ou was an intern at The Times (“A Dozen Promising Photographers“) and is now a freelancer, represented by Reportage by Getty Images, shooting for The Times in Egypt. He has photographed in the Middle East, Africa and the former Soviet republics. James Estrin spoke with him by phone early Sunday morning and early Monday morning, Cairo time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Into Cairo’s Byways', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/00078971-aada-5445-a8be-7b52e7a8336d', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00078971-aada-5445-a8be-7b52e7a8336d'}, {'abstract': 'Numberplay takes a break this week but will resume next Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/no-numberplay-this-week/', 'snippet': 'Numberplay takes a break this week but will resume next Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pradeep is taking a break this week, but Gary will provide math puzzles next Monday, as usual.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Numberplay This Week', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:52:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ee03314-ef03-5cd8-bb7b-50d285a9fa74', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ee03314-ef03-5cd8-bb7b-50d285a9fa74'}, {'abstract': 'BP’s partners in Russia, who have filed an injunction seeking to stop a BP deal with Rosneft, are now trying to withhold dividend payments from their Russian joint venture, TNK-BP.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/russian-investors-move-to-block-bp-dividend/', 'snippet': 'BP’s partners in Russia, who have filed an injunction seeking to stop a BP deal with Rosneft, are now trying to withhold dividend payments from their Russian joint venture, TNK-BP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — BP suggested over the weekend that the latest dispute with its powerful Russian partners, who are looking to derail BP’s deal with the state-run oil company Rosneft, might be swiftly resolved in an arbitration process, rather than in court. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Partners Move to Block TNK-BP Payout', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosneft', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TNK-BP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/806e45fc-eed4-58c1-b9f1-615e1afbaae9', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806e45fc-eed4-58c1-b9f1-615e1afbaae9'}, {'abstract': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/what-were-reading-108/', 'snippet': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An aggregation of links by the reporters and editors of Diner’s Journal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ff4b276-ec6c-5360-b466-cb6e588b34ab', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ff4b276-ec6c-5360-b466-cb6e588b34ab'}, {'abstract': 'A big-ticket trinket to tempt the discerning gentleman can be found right off of Old Bond Street.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/go-for-broke-van-cleef-arpels-cuff-links/', 'snippet': 'A big-ticket trinket to tempt the discerning gentleman can be found right off of Old Bond Street.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Downton Abbey,” the English high-society drama on PBS, has more than one chap channeling his inner lord of the manor. They would do well to turn to Sandra Cronan. Among the fanciful estate gems at her charming boutique on Albermarle Street, just a stone’s (or in this case, diamond’s) throw from Old Bond Street, is this handsome pair of Van Cleef & Arpels 18-karat yellow gold cuff links with interchangeable bars of tiger’s eye and lapis lazuli from the 1950s. With big-ticket trinkets like this to tempt the discerning gentleman, no wonder so many lost their estates. About $4,773. At Sandra Cronan, 011-44-207-491-4851.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Go for Broke | Van Cleef & Arpels Cuff Links', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/657fd519-0ce6-514c-b7db-8cceaf9238d4', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/657fd519-0ce6-514c-b7db-8cceaf9238d4'}, {'abstract': 'Does an academic study really suggest that women should do more around the house than men?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/equality-isnt-always-easy/', 'snippet': 'Does an academic study really suggest that women should do more around the house than men?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news out of Ohio State University last week seems to contradict everything “forward thinking parents” believe. In a study published in the journal Developmental Psychology, researchers reported that couples who share caregiving are more likely to experience “conflict” than couples where the wife does more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Equality Isn’t Always Easy', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/befe3f06-404f-5e63-934a-a7c677d8fedc', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/befe3f06-404f-5e63-934a-a7c677d8fedc'}, {'abstract': 'The confidential finding was in response to a longstanding complaint by the European Union over United States support of Boeing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/business/01wto.html', 'snippet': 'The confidential finding was in response to a longstanding complaint by the European Union over United States support of Boeing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS \x97 A panel at the World Trade Organization ruled on Monday that Boeing had received up to $5 billion in improper subsidies for its 787 Dreamliner and other jets, giving it an unfair advantage against its European rival, Airbus, European officials said. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'W.T.O. Is Said to Affirm That Boeing Got Improper Subsidies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trade Organization Ruling Is Said to Affirm That Boeing Received Improper Subsidies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T16:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark and Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37a35fef-892b-593a-bb3e-b6e7fded46aa', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37a35fef-892b-593a-bb3e-b6e7fded46aa'}, {'abstract': 'I finally make it to Cairo. Here’s the scoop.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/im-in-cairo-finally/', 'snippet': 'I finally make it to Cairo. Here’s the scoop.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:05 p.m. | Updated with a segment of Times Cast featuring Nick in Cairo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report From Cairo', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:04:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b2b6d6b-434e-5354-9081-cef6052e955d', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b2b6d6b-434e-5354-9081-cef6052e955d'}, {'abstract': 'We’ll continue to update this post, which provides a variety of ways to address the breaking news about Egypt in the classroom.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/ways-to-teach-the-unrest-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'We’ll continue to update this post, which provides a variety of ways to address the breaking news about Egypt in the classroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egypt, the most populous country in the Arab world, erupted in mass protests in January 2011, as the revolution in Tunisia seemed to inflame decades worth of smoldering grievances against the heavy-handed rule of President Hosni Mubarak. After 18 days of angry protests, Mr. Mubarak resigned and turned over all power to the military on Feb. 11, 2011, ending his 30 years of autocratic rule and bowing to a historic popular uprising that has transformed politics in Egypt and around the Arab world. The announcement, delivered during evening prayers in Cairo, set off a frenzy of celebration, with protesters shouting “Egypt is free!” The popular protest, peaceful and resilient despite numerous effort by Mr. Mubarak’s legendary security apparatus to suppress it, ultimately deposed an ally of the United States who has been instrumental in implementing American policy in the region for decades.–Overview from the Times Topics page on Egypt, updated Feb. 11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ways to Teach About the Unrest in Egypt', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten, Sarah Kavanagh and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/92351c07-e23d-5175-9a34-c86fe9735494', 'word_count': 3567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92351c07-e23d-5175-9a34-c86fe9735494'}, {'abstract': 'The condition can cause sudden power loss and, in some cases, fire, according to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/ignition-coil-problem-identified-on-nearly-500000-vw-passats/', 'snippet': '