: 'Charlotte Bartholomew joined Allen & Gerritsen, Watertown, Mass., in a new post, multimedia designer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlotte Bartholomew joined Allen & Gerritsen, Watertown, Mass., in a new post, multimedia designer. She had been a presentation specialist at Hill, Holliday, Connors, Cosmopulos, Boston, part of the Interpublic Group of Companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/691a5dfd-a36e-56e5-9fe9-e70627279ee3', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/691a5dfd-a36e-56e5-9fe9-e70627279ee3'}, {'abstract': 'Women who do end up gaining weight, experts say, may simply be misperceiving normal weight gain over time as an unwanted side effect of contraceptives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/health/01really.html', 'snippet': 'Women who do end up gaining weight, experts say, may simply be misperceiving normal weight gain over time as an unwanted side effect of contraceptives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Claim: Contraceptives Can Make You Gain Weight', 'kicker': 'Really?', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE CLAIM: Contraceptives Can Make You Gain Weight.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:21:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae36430-6d91-5e42-aa7d-2ca325cd0887', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae36430-6d91-5e42-aa7d-2ca325cd0887'}, {'abstract': 'Dallas Mavericks star Dirk Nowitzki doesn’t want to be idle during an N.B.A. lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/nowitzki-mulls-lockout-options/', 'snippet': 'Dallas Mavericks star Dirk Nowitzki doesn’t want to be idle during an N.B.A. lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More N.B.A. players are starting to\xa0look abroad for playing opportunities, exploring options for next season if there is a lockout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nowitzki Mulls Lockout Options', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:27:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/94a8cf7e-ed8a-5f3f-a248-0276c510f3b0', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94a8cf7e-ed8a-5f3f-a248-0276c510f3b0'}, {'abstract': 'Helena Bonham Carter gave an intensely honest speech at the Directors Guild awards, saying she initially turned down the role and calling Tom Hooper bonkers.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/the-queen-mom-who-almost-wasnt/', 'snippet': 'Helena Bonham Carter gave an intensely honest speech at the Directors Guild awards, saying she initially turned down the role and calling Tom Hooper bonkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The Bagger spent the weekend at various award shows, convening with celebrities and other beautiful people, commiserating about having to be at awards shows. Tough gig, we know. But before we get to the scene on the dance floor with Justin Timberlake and Amanda Seyfried at a Dewar’s-fueled Screen Actors Guild after-party, let us catch you up on the nontelevised happenings at the Directors Guild awards. The group allows all its best feature film nominees to give a speech before the winner is revealed, which is part of why the event — dinner and the ceremony — was nearly six hours long. (See, it is worth commiserating.) But there were moments of mirth, like Colin Firth and Helena Bonham Carter’s introduction of Tom Hooper, the director of “The King’s Speech” (and the evening’s ultimate winner). Mr. Firth talked about being nervous performing in front of Mr. Hooper, who kept looking down at his shoes; when he finally looked up, Mr. Firth said he knew he’d nailed the part. Ms. Bonham Carter was even more honest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Queen Mom Who Almost Wasn’t', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonham Carter, Helena', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Firth, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Directors Guild of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:28:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f8c62bc-bd7f-593a-9d76-4dc397af4be3', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f8c62bc-bd7f-593a-9d76-4dc397af4be3'}, {'abstract': 'C.J. Chivers offers a fresh look at some of the Taliban’s weapons as a means to understanding more fully how the Taliban fights.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/taliban-gun-lockers-the-rifles-of-rural-ghazni-province/', 'snippet': 'C.J. Chivers offers a fresh look at some of the Taliban’s weapons as a means to understanding more fully how the Taliban fights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORWARD OPERATING BASE ANDAR, Afghanistan — This month Tyler Hicks and I have been working alongside the soldiers of Task Force Iron, an infantry battalion from the 101st Airborne Division that soon will complete a one-year tour in Afghanistan. We’re busy editing photographs and wrapping up reporting on some of the operations we observed alongside American soldiers and Afghan police and intelligence officers, and will have at least two stories for the newspaper soon. As we work, we want to pause to share a fresh look at some of the Taliban’s weapons, based on the battalion’s recent captures from slain Taliban fighters or caches, as a means to understanding more fully how the Taliban fights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Gun Lockers: The Rifles of Rural Ghazni Province', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:37:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc6a598d-2f26-56b0-b093-e6a38011be14', 'word_count': 1984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc6a598d-2f26-56b0-b093-e6a38011be14'}, {'abstract': 'Many women swear that they gain weight after starting birth control pills or other hormonal contraceptives, but scientists say the pill isn’t to blame for putting on extra pounds.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/dont-blame-weight-gain-on-the-pill/', 'snippet': 'Many women swear that they gain weight after starting birth control pills or other hormonal contraceptives, but scientists say the pill isn’t to blame for putting on extra pounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many women swear that they gain weight after starting birth control pills or other hormonal contraceptives, but scientists say the pill isn’t to blame for those extra pounds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Blame the Pill for Weight Gain', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T17:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/83c323c5-3e8d-5ac5-827f-78181c4f7c20', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83c323c5-3e8d-5ac5-827f-78181c4f7c20'}, {'abstract': 'In light of the unrest roiling Egypt, here’s a roundup of readings on the economic consequences, and roots, of the crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/economics-roundup-on-the-egyptian-crisis/', 'snippet': 'In light of the unrest roiling Egypt, here’s a roundup of readings on the economic consequences, and roots, of the crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In light of the unrest roiling Egypt, here’s a roundup of readings on the economic consequences, and roots, of the crisis:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'mai