'“The Extinction Method” takes the place of “Carl’s Sister,” a new play by Alfred Uhry (“Driving Miss Daisy”) based on the book “Apples and Oranges” by Marie Brenner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manhattan Theater Club has added “The Extinction Method,” a new play by Daniel Goldfarb about two couples who live in adjacent Brooklyn apartments, to its season. Sam Buntrock, who received a Tony nomination for his revival of “Sunday in the Park With George,” will direct the production, which begins previews on May 10 and opens on May 25 at New York City Center – Stage I. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manhattan Theater Club Adds ‘Extinction,’ Postpones ‘Carl’s Sister’ This Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T18:47:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d32451a1-2000-5936-8f7b-84b472e73169', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d32451a1-2000-5936-8f7b-84b472e73169'}, {'abstract': 'Unless questions about King George VI’s anti-Nazi stance or the vagaries of Hollywood math derail it, “The King’s Speech” is in line for a best picture Oscar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/movies/awardsseason/01smear.html', 'snippet': 'Unless questions about King George VI’s anti-Nazi stance or the vagaries of Hollywood math derail it, “The King’s Speech” is in line for a best picture Oscar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It is the king’s to lose.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty