ng light fixtures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest school building in New York City where the federal Environmental Protection Agency has tested for leaks of PCB’s from light fixtures found elevated levels of the chemical in all seven samples taken.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Present! Roll Call Continues for PCB Leaks', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PCB (Polychlorinated Biphenyls)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'EAST NEW YORK (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T18:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e358d59-eacc-584a-bf22-bae07a5651a3', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e358d59-eacc-584a-bf22-bae07a5651a3'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s office released several videos detailing the city’s undercover investigation into the ease with which one can buy guns at a gun show in Arizona.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/hear-no-evil-suspect-no-evil-at-an-arizona-gun-show/', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s office released several videos detailing the city’s undercover investigation into the ease with which one can buy guns at a gun show in Arizona.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg‘s office released several videos this morning detailing the city’s recent undercover investigation into the ease with which one can buy guns at a gun show in Arizona — even if you tell the seller you probably wouldn’t pass a background check, and even in the wake of the Jan. 9 Tucson shootings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hear No Evil, Suspect No Evil at an Arizona Gun Show', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T18:57:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/de14ee2c-87a1-583e-9e68-403ce37b114c', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de14ee2c-87a1-583e-9e68-403ce37b114c'}, {'abstract': 'Winter vegetables are perfect for bubbly, comforting gratins and other baked casseroles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/health/nutrition/31recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Winter vegetables are perfect for bubbly, comforting gratins and other baked casseroles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cold-weather and winter vegetables lend themselves to comforting, bubbly baked dishes \x97 and I don’t mean the casseroles conjured up from cream soups tossed with overcooked meats and canned vegetables. Some of my favorite winter casseroles are gratins, which are baked until the edges and top brown. (The browned part, including the bits you like to scrape off the sides of the dish, are the gratinée. Grater mean "to scrape" in French.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi