d Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T18:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/e531fa10-5372-5657-b2fc-6be7e115bc49', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e531fa10-5372-5657-b2fc-6be7e115bc49'}, {'abstract': 'The theory that American anxiety about China’s increasing power might evolve into animosity and aggression.(After Thucydides’s account of the causes of the Peloponnesian war.)', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/the-thucydides-trap/', 'snippet': 'The theory that American anxiety about China’s increasing power might evolve into animosity and aggression.(After Thucydides’s account of the causes of the Peloponnesian war.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theory that American anxiety about China’s increasing power might evolve into animosity and aggression.(After Thucydides’s account of the causes of the Peloponnesian war.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Thucydides Trap', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2f0bef-0a5f-59e9-b885-c1cfaf959958', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2f0bef-0a5f-59e9-b885-c1cfaf959958'}, {'abstract': 'A new book by Kate Betts meditates on the meaning and importance of style for women of power.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/michelle-obama-first-lady-of-fashion/', 'snippet': 'A new book by Kate Betts meditates on the meaning and importance of style for women of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is she or isn’t she? A closet clotheshorse (despite her staff’s reluctance to discuss the matter), enamored of Jimmy Choo kitten heels and Azzedine Alaïa belts? Or is she a woman of great natural style, only one of the expressions of which is to be found in her collection of colorful cardigans and her passion for prints? Do we pay attention to her wardrobe as a way of understanding the larger arc of her character? Or are her clothes no more than a manifestation of a carefully constructed image, an attempt to put across a persona of individualism and confidence?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama, First Lady of Fashion', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daphne Merkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daphne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Merkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b6b79a1-1bf6-5002-8dfb-dd95f7654b9c', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b6b79a1-1bf6-5002-8dfb-dd95f7654b9c'}, {'abstract': '“I Think I Love You,” by Allison Pearson, channels an insecure 13-year-old with a crush on David Cassidy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/books/01book.html', 'snippet': '“I Think I Love You,” by Allison Pearson, channels an insecure 13-year-old with a crush on David Cassidy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as Allison Pearson’s 2002 best seller, “I Don’t Know How She Does It,” proved she had perfect pitch for channeling a stressed-out working mom in hedge-fund-crazy London, so her new novel, “I Think I Love You,” shows she has the same gift for channeling an insecure 13-year-old in 1974 with a mad crush on the pop star David Cassidy. You know, David Cassidy of “The Partridge Family” \x97 he with the Bambi eyes and feathered mop top, who was the love object of millions of young girls in that era of bell-bottom pants, platform shoes and Mary Quant eye shadow. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soft Lyrics Set in Motion a Mad Crush', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girlish Crush Has Lasting Implications', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearson, Allison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5177070-da8b-550a-9088-1cd05aad03d3', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5177070-da8b-550a-9088-1cd05aad03d3'}, {'abstract': 'The National Republican Trust, which supported Scott Brown’s 2009 bid for the Senate, says it will work to defeat him in the Massachusetts Republican primary next year.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/republican-group-plans-to-challenge-scott-brown/', 'snippet': 'The National Republican Trust, which supported Scott Brown’s 2009 bid for the Senate, says it will work to defeat him in the Massachusetts Republican primary next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Scott Brown was surging toward victory in the United States Senate race in Massachusetts in 2009, he earned the support — and money — of the National Republican Trust.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Group Plans to Challenge Scott Brown', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1019b0a3-7567-57c4-9dd4-a3856c6b8b83', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1019b0a3-7567-57c4-9dd4-a3856c6b8b83'}, {'abstract': 'The snow that many people curse is providing strong business for those who see opportunities in a foreboding forecast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall.html', 'snippet': 'The snow that many people curse is providing strong business for those who see opportunities in a foreboding forecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The line for Louis Migliore between moonlighter and entrepreneur this winter measures nearly five feet deep.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall/01windfall-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall/01windfall-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall/01windfall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall/01windfall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/nyregion/01windfall/01windfall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whether Plowing or Serving Hot Chocolate, Some Find a Payday in the Snow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whether Plowing or Serving Hot Chocolate, Some Find a Payday in the Snow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:06:58+0000', 'document_ty