e/387d5820-67f1-5c64-a2b8-b59eab3b445e'}, {'abstract': 'Coachella is sod out while some single-day tickets for All Tomorrow’s Parties are still available, but going fast.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/two-pop-festivals-are-already-hits-with-ticket-buyers/', 'snippet': 'Coachella is sod out while some single-day tickets for All Tomorrow’s Parties are still available, but going fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new year has barely begun, but two big-event music festivals are already hits. Last week the Coachella Valley Music & Arts Festival  in Indio, Calif., with Arcade Fire, Kanye West, Kings of Leon and the Strokes, sold out less than a week after going on sale. And by Monday all of the three-day passes for I’ll Be Your Mirror, the new event in Asbury Park, N.J., presented by the people behind the All Tomorrow’s Parties concerts, had sold out, three days after they went on sale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Pop Festivals Are Already Hits With Ticket Buyers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "All Tomorrow's Parties (Music Festival)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T19:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/60126ec2-abdc-5ad2-a5f0-e95effaf681d', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60126ec2-abdc-5ad2-a5f0-e95effaf681d'}, {'abstract': 'Coachella is sod out while some single-day tickets for All Tomorrow’s Parties are still available, but going fast.'