, 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/now-booking-one-fine-stay/', 'snippet': 'A London Web site has emerged that reflects a new trend in travel: luxury rentals-by-owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those of us with grand travel dreams have recurring travel nightmares as well — one of mine is of wheeling my suitcase through the endless corridors of a throbbing nightclub, unable to find my room. This dream tends to occur when I’ve been staying at too many boutique hotels, and leaves me longing for an alternative that’s as stylish, but more homey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | One Fine Stay', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T20:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Stivers-Isakova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stivers-Isakova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c1e6cd-1645-5ba8-83d2-2c2ea54ef630', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c1e6cd-1645-5ba8-83d2-2c2ea54ef630'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Huntsman, the ambassador to China, has told the White House that he plans to leave his post in the next few months, stoking speculation about his presidential ambitions.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/huntsman-to-step-down-fueling-speculation-about-presidential-bid/', 'snippet': 'Jon Huntsman, the ambassador to China, has told the White House that he plans to leave his post in the next few months, stoking speculation about his presidential ambitions.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': '6:11 p.m. | Updated Jon Huntsman, the United States ambassador to China, has informed the White House that he plans to step down in the next few months, further stoking speculation about his presidential ambitions.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huntsman to Step Down, Fueling Speculation About Presidential Bid', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T20:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/61b3d4d5-1a9d-58c4-a4a8-891a1e8576eb', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61b3d4d5-1a9d-58c4-a4a8-891a1e8576eb'}, {'abstract': 'A buildup in stocks related to rising oil imports derived from Canadian oil sands has helped make crude significantly cheaper in the United States than it is in Europe or Asia.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/in-an-oil-price-gap-the-scent-of-tar-sands/', 'snippet': 'A buildup in stocks related to rising oil imports derived from Canadian oil sands has helped make crude significantly cheaper in the United States than it is in Europe or Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you haven’t noticed, oil prices in the United States differ from those in the rest of the world. Usually the variance is just a few dollars, but over the last few weeks the difference between West Texas Intermediate prices and Brent crude, which is sourced in Europe’s North Sea, has widened to about $10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Oil Price Gap, the Scent of Tar Sands', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Sea', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T20:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a6261f-f559-5fcf-8a98-1874e6df9477', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a6261f-f559-5fcf-8a98-1874e6df9477'}, {'abstract': 'A study says H.I.V.-positive breast-feeding women are less likely to infect their newborns if they start taking antiretroviral triple therapy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/health/01global.html', 'snippet': 'A study says H.I.V.-positive breast-feeding women are less likely to infect their newborns if they start taking antiretroviral triple therapy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breast-feeding m