ir new racing cars a day before the first test of the new year begins in Valencia, Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, this is a big week. The first tests of the new year begin in Valencia, Spain, on Tuesday, and four teams unveiled their 2011 model racing cars on Monday. Ferrari beat the others to the punch by introducing its new model last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Cars Unveiled for Formula One Season', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T20:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f77ea17e-6b23-51c9-91e1-d113ac57d4fb', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f77ea17e-6b23-51c9-91e1-d113ac57d4fb'}, {'abstract': 'As the uprising in Egypt approaches the one-week mark, some of the big network anchors are joining their reporters to broadcast from the scene.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/with-egypt-in-crisis-anchors-head-to-cairo/', 'snippet': 'As the uprising in Egypt approaches the one-week mark, some of the big network anchors are joining their reporters to broadcast from the scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the uprising in Egypt approaches the one-week mark, television networks based in the United States continue to send reporters to the region. Now it appears some of the big network anchors are arriving there, as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Egypt in Crisis, Anchors Head to Cairo', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMANPOUR, CHRISTIANE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Anderson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couric, Katie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T21:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea832d64-6bdd-54e8-aa9d-1a6fb72bf52d', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea832d64-6bdd-54e8-aa9d-1a6fb72bf52d'}, {'abstract': 'The traditional first stop after the SAG Awards is the People magazine afterparty, which had the feel of a high-gloss reunion.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/scenes-from-an-afterparty/', 'snippet': 'The traditional first stop after the SAG Awards is the People magazine afterparty, which had the feel of a high-gloss reunion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES— The reputation of the Screen Actors Guild parties is that they’re loose and uninhibited affairs, actors having been known to enjoy a celebration or several hundred after the SAG Awards. The traditional first stop is the People magazine afterparty, held in a tent adjacent to the Shrine Auditorium, where the award ceremony takes place. With the mix of TV and movie stars, it had the feel of a high-gloss reunion, with both a band and a D.J., and buffets for starving performers, who mostly went around congratulating each other and admitting their fandom. (It is the season of back-patting, after all.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From an Afterparty', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARONOFSKY, DARREN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenberg, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T21:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae9b76f7-40c7-55a7-91c0-bff07fc7e4f7', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae9b76f7-40c7-55a7-91c0-bff07fc7e4f7'}, {'abstract': 'After returning from weeks in Costa Rica, a college professor has to contend with a car buried by snow.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/cold-realit/', 'snippet': 'After returning from weeks in Costa Rica, a college professor has to contend with a car buried by snow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monica Ferrell was in stockings, a skirt and heels. And she was clawing, helplessly, at the dirty, sandy, icy snow that clung to her Saab 9-3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Tropical Vacation to Cold Reality', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T21:23:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2884a8cc-b184-5a99-8563-ab5791c6a0ff', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2884a8cc-b184-5a99-8563-ab5791c6a0ff'}, {'abstract': 'At One Medical Group, which charges a fee of $150 to $200 a year, same-day appointments are routine, doctors welcome e-mail communication and see at most 16 patients a day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/health/01medical.html', 'snippet': 'At One Medical Group, which charges a fee of $150 to $200 a year, same-day appointments are routine, doctors welcome e-mail communication and see at most 16 patients a day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO \x97 When Jennifer Contreras went to see her new physician, she had hardly arrived in the waiting room before she was called in \x97 by the doctor herself.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01medi/01medi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01medi/01medi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/science/01medi/01medi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Concierge Medical Care With a Smaller Price Tag', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concierge Medical Care With a Smaller Price Tag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subjec