 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Fourth of July to Israel', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Hot Dogs and Grill, The Fourth of July Arrives in Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hot Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T22:44:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Last', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Last', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0983a0ad-89d6-5007-9fcd-c533d8da77c5', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0983a0ad-89d6-5007-9fcd-c533d8da77c5'}, {'abstract': 'Coverage of the N.F.L. Pro Bowl lifted Fox to No. 1 in the ratings on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/arts/television/01arts-PROBOWLLIFTS_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Coverage of the N.F.L. Pro Bowl lifted Fox to No. 1 in the ratings on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coverage of the N.F.L. Pro Bowl lifted Fox to No. 1 in the ratings on Sunday evening, while CBS finished close behind with strong ratings for its made-for-television movie “The Lost Valentine.” According to Nielsen’s estimates, 14.5 million viewers tuned to CBS for the film, outperforming its competitors from 9 to 11 p.m. and delivering the largest audience for a “Hallmark Hall of Fame” broadcast in four years. Earlier, CBS drew 10.1 million viewers for “60 Minutes,” featuring an interview with Julian Assange of WikiLeaks, and 8.1 million for a repeat of “Undercover Boss.” Fox was somewhat more consistent, averaging 12.4 million viewers for its football coverage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pro Bowl Lifts Fox', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pro Bowl Lifts Fox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T22:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c6edc6-c8d8-5360-abe2-d45ab2522b39', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c6edc6-c8d8-5360-abe2-d45ab2522b39'}, {'abstract': 'Reporters Anthony Shadid, Liam Stack and Stephen Farrell report on the state of unrest around Cairo.  ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/1248069601739/cairo-protests-day-7.html', 'snippet': 'Reporters Anthony Shadid, Liam Stack and Stephen Farrell report on the state of unrest around Cairo.  ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporters Anthony Shadid, Liam Stack and Stephen Farrell report on the state of unrest around Cairo.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/01/31/world/middleeast/11165_1_cairoprotests_75x75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/01/31/world/middleeast/11165_1_cairoprotests_75x75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cairo Protests: Day 7 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T22:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Brent McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/32014e8f-8161-58a7-8488-41bce68f86cf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/32014e8f-8161-58a7-8488-41bce68f86cf'}, {'abstract': 'With tons of snow sitting on top of buildings and a heavy mix of snow and freezing rain expected overnight, officials are warning of the danger of roof collapses.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/01/31/shovel-that-roof-before-something-bad-happens/', 'snippet': 'With tons of snow sitting on top of buildings and a heavy mix of snow and freezing rain expected overnight, officials are warning of the danger of roof collapses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Weather Service and the city are urging property owners and builders to clear rooftops, awnings and overhangs of snow ASAP, to avoid potential collapses when an ice storm is expected to hit New York early Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shovel That Roof, Before Something Bad Happens', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T22:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6f12a7-1798-5446-8a55-854515c5c32e', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6f12a7-1798-5446-8a55-854515c5c32e'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,453 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/us/01list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,453 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,453 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T22:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad94674a-4c9e-5ffe-afde-c27a7ef6db04', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad94674a-4c9e-5ffe-afde-c27a7ef6db04'}, {'abstract': 'New CDs by Ricky Martin, MEN and Lori McKenna', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/arts/music/01choice.html', 'snippet': 'New CDs by Ricky Martin, MEN and Lori McKenna', 'lead_paragraph': 'The back story is upfront on Ricky Martin’s “Música + Alma + Sexo” (“Music + Soul + Sex”), his first studio album since 2005 and his first since he announced last year on his Web site that he is “proud to say that I am a fortunate homosexual man.” On this album his usual exhortations to seize life’s pleasures mingle with coming-out manifestos, and he smiles through them all.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/CHOICE/CHOICE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/CHOICE/CHOICE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/01/arts/CHOICE/CHOICE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ricky Martin, Now as Himself', 'kicker': 'Critics’ Choice: New Cds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ricky Martin, Now as Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKenna, Lori (1968- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T23:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles, Ben Ratliff and Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e46b77e9-4de3-5162-81ee-b7626c283b0f', 'word_count': 1270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e46b77e9-4de3-5162-81ee-b7626c283b0f'}, {'abstract': 'Major oil companies are spending billions on projects now, and investors could reap some of the benefits in several years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/02/01/business/01views.html', 'snippet': 'Major oil companies are spending billions on projects now, and investors could reap some of the benefits in several years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major oil firms have become big spenders. Together, the top three American giants say they plan capital spending this year of about $60 billion, well above the year of peak crude prices in 2008, despite showing only tepid cash flow growth. At first blush, this looks like desperation, as Western oil companies increasingly struggle to replace crude reserves. But patient investors will find higher returns are on the way.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/01/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Likely Upswing in the Oil Patch', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patience Pays\nIn the Oil Patch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Default Swaps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-01-31T23:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Swann and Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier':